":"A_kwHOB96YWc4ABU2s","owner":{"login":"coderabbitai","id":132028505,"node_id":"O_kgDOB96YWQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/132028505?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai","html_url":"https://github.com/coderabbitai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/received_events","type":"Organization","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"name":"coderabbitai","description":"# Transforming Code Reviews with AI\r\n\r\n## Features\r\n\r\n**Automated Reviews**: Continuous reviews of the pull requests including incremental commits. \r\n\r\n**Summarization**: Generates high-level summary and a technical walkthrough of the PR changes. \r\n\r\n**Line-by-line review**: Provides line-by-line suggestions committable with one click.\r\n\r\n**Codebase verification**:  Verifies the impact on the overall codebase and identifies missing changes.\r\n\r\n**Insights into your code**:  Ask any questions on your codebase within the pull request \r\n\r\n**Chat about your code** : Chat with the bot around your code. The more you chat, the smarter it gets.\r\n\r\n**Issue Validation**:  Validates the PR against the linked issues and identifies other related issues \r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n","external_url":"https://coderabbit.ai?utm_source=cr_app&utm_medium=github","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/coderabbitai","created_at":"2023-06-14T15:47:27Z","updated_at":"2026-03-14T07:58:44Z","permissions":{"actions":"read","checks":"write","contents":"write","discussions":"read","issues":"write","members":"read","metadata":"read","pull_requests":"write","statuses":"write"},"events":["issues","issue_comment","label","organization","pull_request","pull_request_review","pull_request_review_comment","pull_request_review_thread","release","repository"]}},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/issues/comments/3805509333","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/322#issuecomment-3805509333","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/issues/322","id":3805509333,"node_id":"IC_kwDOPaLyBs7i03bV","user":{"login":"Artifizer","id":192502778,"node_id":"U_kgDOC3lb-g","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/192502778?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer","html_url":"https://github.com/Artifizer","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-01-27T14:23:40Z","updated_at":"2026-01-27T15:23:09Z","body":"Topics to discuss:\r\n\r\n## 1. Audit and metrics are missing\r\n\r\n2. Upstream configuration:\r\na. should be identified as GTS well known ID or UUID?\r\nb. Can't see if upstream is defined per tenant\r\nc. can single upstream support multiple protocols? e.g. completions - sync API call vs streaming\r\nd. any response caching?\r\n\r\n## 2. Routes\r\na. should be also per-tenant?\r\nb. enable/disable?\r\nc. initially I had some per-route strategy - sticky session, round robin\r\n\r\n## 3. What about client-control retry?\r\n\r\nPR220 defines explicit caller-controlled retry:\r\n- `RetryIntent` with `max_attempts`, `retry_on[]`, `scope`, `backoff`, `budget`\r\n- Scopes: `same_link | different_link | reroute`\r\n- **OAGW never performs implicit retries**\r\n- Streaming requests are never retried\r\n- `Retry-After` always propagates from downstream\r\n\r\n## 4. I believe some error definition is incomplete\r\n- can't see 'RouteNotFound'\r\n- can't see 'IdleTimeout'\r\n\r\n## 5. What about OAGW defaults in config?\r\n\r\n- token_cache_max_capacity: 10,000\r\n- token_cache_max_ttl_sec: 3600\r\n- default_connection_timeout_ms: 5,000\r\n- default_request_timeout_ms: 30,000\r\n- default_idle_timeout_ms: 60,000\r\n- default_rate_limit_per_min: 1,000\r\n- circuit_breaker_threshold: 5\r\n- audit_guarantee: BestEffort\r\n\r\n## 6. What about delivery phases? The requirements doesn't have versions but this is critical for the users to understand when to expect what and here we could expect some debates\r\n\r\n## 7. Need to ensure credential binding happens on tenant level (or route level), e.g. different tenants may bring their own API keys, or use default provided by the parent tenant\r\n\r\n## 8. Need more info about exact roles to be checked\r\n\r\n## 9. How to distinguish upstream error/body vs OAGW error/body?","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/issues/comments/3805509333/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/issues/comments/3807795669","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cybe