rences around the same text\nwith concrete acceptance criteria and success metrics (retain X days,\nsearchable/immutable logs, export endpoint, encryption-at-rest, role-based\naccess, and evidence of delivery guarantees) so readers can validate compliance\nand testing.\n- Around line 95-102: Update the \"Upstream Management\" and \"Route Management\"\nsections to explicitly state resource scoping, identifier format, and\ncross-tenant visibility: specify whether upstreams and routes are tenant-scoped\nor global (e.g., add a \"scope\" field with allowed values \"tenant\" or \"global\"),\ndefine the canonical ID format (e.g., UUIDv4 or GTS well-known ID) and\nuniqueness guarantees, document ownership and RBAC constraints (who can\nread/modify global vs tenant resources), and list visibility rules for\ncross-tenant references (whether tenants can reference global upstreams or only\ntheir own), and include schema examples/fields (e.g., scope, id, ownerTenantId,\nvisibility) so both sections and the related later block are unambiguous.\n- Around line 352-365: Update the \"Error Codes\" section to add a distinct\nIdleTimeout row (HTTP 504? or a new specific code you choose) alongside the\nexisting Timeout entry and explicitly annotate which error codes are generated\nby the OAGW gateway versus those forwarded from upstream services; modify the\ntable or add a short explanatory column/footnote indicating \"Source: OAGW\" or\n\"Source: Upstream\" for each entry (e.g., mark IdleTimeout and CircuitBreakerOpen\nas OAGW-generated, and DownstreamError as upstream), and ensure the prose\nexplains that upstream error bodies are preserved/propagated while gateway\nerrors use the documented canonical bodies.\n- Around line 103-108: In the \"Request Proxying\" section add a clear\nclient-controlled retry contract by introducing a RetryIntent schema (name it\nRetryIntent) that documents fields: max_attempts (integer), retry_on (enum of\nretryable conditions), scope (per-request or per-connection), backoff (type and\nparameters e.g., type, base_delay, max_delay), and budget (overall allowed retry\ncost); explicitly state that OAGW performs no automatic retries and clients must\nsupply RetryIntent to request retries; declare that streaming requests (any\nrequest using transfer-encoding: chunked or long-lived streaming endpoints) are\nnever retried by OAGW; and specify that if an upstream responds with\nRetry-After, OAGW will propagate the Retry-After header unchanged to the client\n(and include a brief note on how Retry-After interacts with\nmax_attempts/backoff).\n- Around line 1-3: Add a short \"Compliance\" section to PRD: Outbound API Gateway\n(OAGW) that either (a) links to a formal change-proposal file (e.g.,\nopenspec/changes/add-oagw/proposal.md) and summarizes why the change is needed,\nwhat will change, and the impacted specs/code, or (b) states that the capability\nwas pre-approved and includes the approval reference; ensure the PRD references\nopenspec/AGENTS.md for the formal change-proposal requirement and include the\nexact proposal path or approval ID for traceability.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment by CodeRabbit for review status -->","state":"COMMENTED","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/322#pullrequestreview-3764488127","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/322","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","_links":{"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/322#pullrequestreview-3764488127"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/322"}},"submitted_at":"2026-02-06T18:06:21Z","commit_id":"14ef3e26e3d0660cccbe8f7e8463d5fa3254c0e3"}]},{"source_pr_number":321,"source_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/321","source_state":"closed","source_author":"github-actions[bot]","target_issue_number":null,"title":"[PR #321] chore: release","status":"exported","mir