DOPaLyBs7ih6t3","user":{"login":"coderabbitai[bot]","id":136622811,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOCCSy2w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/347564?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/coderabbitai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-01-26T16:37:25Z","updated_at":"2026-01-27T02:05:18Z","body":"<!-- This is an auto-generated comment: summarize by coderabbit.ai -->\n<!-- walkthrough_start -->\n\n<details>\n<summary>📝 Walkthrough</summary>\n\n## Walkthrough\n\nAdds standardized package metadata (readme, categories, keywords, repository, publish) to many Cargo.toml files, creates or updates README.md files across libs and modules, replaces branding references from HyperSpot to CyberFabric in docs, and changes several GitHub Actions workflows to manual/PR-dispatch triggers.\n\n## Changes\n\n| Cohort / File(s) | Summary |\n|---|---|\n| **Library crates (manifests & docs)** <br> `libs/modkit*/*`, `libs/modkit-auth/*`, `libs/modkit-db*/*`, `libs/modkit-errors*/*`, `libs/modkit-macros/*`, `libs/modkit-node-info/*`, `libs/modkit-odata*/*`, `libs/modkit-sdk/*`, `libs/modkit-security/*`, `libs/modkit-transport-grpc/*`, `libs/modkit-utils/*`, `libs/system-sdks/*` | Added `readme = \"README.md\"` and `categories` (and in some crates `keywords`/`publish`/`repository`) to Cargo.toml; added or updated crate README.md files. `libs/modkit-macros/README.md` was substantially restructured. |\n| **System modules (manifests & docs)** <br> `modules/system/...` (e.g. `api_gateway`, `grpc_hub`, `module_orchestrator`, `nodes_registry`, `tenant_resolver`, `types_registry`) | Added workspace/repository/readme/keywords/categories metadata to Cargo.toml; created or edited README.md files with module overviews and config. Several READMEs had Architecture sections removed or branding updated. |\n| **Simple User Settings module & SDK** <br> `modules/simple_user_settings/*` | Added package metadata (`publish`, `repository.workspace`, `readme`, `keywords`, `categories`) to Cargo.toml files; added README.md for module and SDK; updated openspec/project docs to CyberFabric. |\n| **System SDKs & sub-crates** <br> `libs/system-sdks/sdks/directory/*`, `modules/system/nodes_registry/nodes_registry-sdk/*`, `modules/system/types_registry/types_registry-sdk/*` | Added `readme`, `keywords`, and `categories` metadata; added README.md files describing SDKs and re-exports. |\n| **Tenant resolver plugins & gateways** <br> `modules/system/tenant_resolver/*`, `.../plugins/*` | Added repository/readme/keywords/categories metadata; removed cross-reference lines from some plugin READMEs; updated tenant_resolver README content and public API docs phrasing. |\n| **Workflows** <br> `.github/workflows/adr-lint.yml`, `.github/workflows/ci.yml`, `.github/workflows/scorecard.yml` | Replaced push-based triggers with `workflow_dispatch`/kept PR triggers; removed branch push triggers and some path filters; added `if` label-skip condition to adr-lint job. |\n| **Branding & minor docs** <br> `docs/*`, `guidelines/*`, `dylint_lints/*`, `examples/*`, many `modules/*/README.md` | Replaced \"HyperSpot\" with \"CyberFabric\" across docs; minor editorial changes and removal of some Architecture sections. |\n\n## Estimated code review effort\n\n🎯 2 (Simple) | ⏱️ ~10 minutes\n\n## Possibly related PRs\n\n- hypernetix/hyperspot#223 — Adds/updates simple-user-settings module, SDK, and related manifests (overlaps module-level artifacts).\n- hypernetix/hyperspot#308 — Similar manifest metadata edits across crates (readme/categories/workspace fields).\n- hypernetix/hyperspot#314 — Modifies types_registry and simple_user_settings manifests and workspace entries (overlapping paths).\n\n## Suggested reviewers\n\n- Bechma\n- Artifizer\n\n## Poem\n\n> 🐰 I hopped through TOMLs, left READMEs bright,  \n> Swapped names and tidied each metadata site.  \n> From HyperSpot shadows to CyberFabric light,  \n> Crates now labeled, docs neat and right.  \n> A rabbit’s small chorus — repo looks just right! ✨\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- walkthrough_end -->\n\n\n<!-- pre_merge_checks_walkthrough_start -->\n\n<details>\n<summary>🚥 Pre-merge checks | ✅ 3</summary>\n\n<details>\n<summary>✅ Passed checks (3 passed)</summary>\n\n|     Check name     | Status   | Explanation                                                                                                                             |\n| :----------------: | :------- | :-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n|  Description Check | ✅ Passed | Check skipped - CodeRabbit’s high-level summary is enabled.                                                                             |\n|     Title check    | ✅ Passed | The title accurately summarizes the main changes: adding module descriptions, README files, and crate metadata across multiple modules. |\n| Docstring Coverage | ✅ Passed | No functions found in the changed files to evaluate docstring coverage. Skipping docstring coverage check.                              |\n\n</details>\n\n<sub>✏️ Tip: You can configure your own custom pre-merge checks in the settings.</sub>\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- pre_merge_checks_walkthrough_end -->\n\n<!-- tips_start -->\n\n---\n\n\n\n<sub>Comment `@coderabbitai help` to get the list of available commands and usage tips.</sub>\n\n<!-- tips_end -->\n\n<!-- internal state start -->\n\n\n<!--  -->\n\n<!-- internal state end -->","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/issues/comments/3800542071/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":{"id":347564,"client_id":"Iv1.6aaafe4fe882736b","slug":"coderabbitai","node_id":"A_kwHOB96YWc4ABU2s","owner":{"login":"coderabbitai","id":132028505,"node_id":"O_kgDOB96YWQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/132028505?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai","html_url":"https://github.com/coderabbitai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/received_events","type":"Organization","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"name":"coderabbitai","description":"# Transforming Code Reviews with AI\r\n\r\n## Features\r\n\r\n**Automated Reviews**: Continuous reviews of the pull requests including incremental commits. \r\n\r\n**Summarization**: Generates high-level summary and a technical walkthrough of the PR changes. \