cho \"=== Searching for simple_user_settings SDK directories ===\"\nfd -t d 'simple.*user.*settings' modules/ 2>/dev/null | head -20\n\necho \"=== Checking Cargo.toml content ===\"\ncat modules/system/types_registry/types_registry/Cargo.toml | grep -A2 -B2 \"types-registry\"\n```\n\nRepository: hypernetix/hyperspot\n\nLength of output: 1417\n\n---\n\n\n\n</details>\n\n**Inconsistent naming convention: `types_registry-sdk` uses hyphen while similar modules use underscores.**\n\nThe actual directory `types_registry-sdk` uses a hyphen before `sdk`, whereas `simple_user_settings_sdk` uses fully snake_case. For consistency across the workspace, consider renaming the directory to `types_registry_sdk` (all underscores) and update the Cargo.toml path accordingly.\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nIn `@modules/system/types_registry/types_registry/Cargo.toml` at line 18, The\nCargo.toml dependency entry uses a mismatched directory naming convention:\nchange the path for types-registry-sdk in Cargo.toml so it points to a renamed\ndirectory using snake_case (types_registry_sdk) to match other modules; update\nthe dependency line referencing types-registry-sdk / package\n\"cf-types-registry-sdk\" to use path \"../types_registry_sdk\" and rename the\nactual folder from types_registry-sdk to types_registry_sdk to keep naming\nconsistent across the workspace.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- fingerprinting:phantom:poseidon:ocelot -->\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated reply by CodeRabbit -->","created_at":"2026-01-26T13:17:40Z","updated_at":"2026-01-26T20:17:04Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/314#discussion_r2727572693","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/314","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2727572693"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/314#discussion_r2727572693"},"pull_request":{"hr