BOT_kgDOCCSy2w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/347564?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/coderabbitai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"`@Artifizer`, thank you for the clarification! You're absolutely right—I misunderstood the naming convention. The pattern `module_name-suffix` (snake_case module name with hyphenated suffix) is consistent throughout the codebase, as seen with `tenant_resolver-sdk` and `types_registry-sdk`. My suggestion was incorrect. The current implementation is correct according to your agreed-upon convention.\n\n---\n\n<details>\n<summary>✏️ Learnings added</summary>\n\n```\nLearnt from: Artifizer\nRepo: hypernetix/hyperspot PR: 314\nFile: modules/system/tenant_resolver/tenant_resolver-gw/Cargo.toml:18-18\nTimestamp: 2026-01-26T20:17:35.744Z\nLearning: In the hypernetix/hyperspot repository, the naming convention for module paths and directory names is: `module_name-suffix` where `module_name` uses snake_case and suffixes (like `-sdk`, `-gw`) are separated by hyphens. For example: `types_registry-sdk`, `tenant_resolver-sdk`, `simple_user_settings_sdk`.\n```\n\n> Note: Learnings are effective only in the context of similar code segments. To apply general coding guidelines, please configure [review instructions](https://docs.coderabbit.ai/guides/review-instructions). You can manage existing learnings in the [app](https://app.coderabbit.ai/learnings).\n\n</details>\n\n\n\n---\n\n<details>\n<summary>🧠 Learnings used</summary>\n\n```\nLearnt from: CR\nRepo: hypernetix/hyperspot PR: 0\nFile: dylint_lints/AGENTS.md:0-0\nTimestamp: 2026-01-14T17:18:31.912Z\nLearning: Applies to dylint_lints/**/Cargo.toml : In `Cargo.toml` for lint crates, reference common workspace dependencies (`clippy_utils`, `dylint_linting`, `lint_utils`) using `.workspace = true` to avoid duplication\n```\n\n---\n\n```\nLearnt from: CR\nRepo: hypernetix/hyperspot PR: 0\nFile: dylint_lints/AGENTS.md:0-0\nTimestamp: 2026-01-14T17:18:31.912Z\nLearning: Applies to dylint_lints/**/Cargo.toml : Register new lint crates by adding them to the `members` list in the workspace root `Cargo.toml`\n```\n\n</details>\n\n\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated reply by CodeRabbit -->","created_at":"2026-01-26T20:17:52Z","updated_at":"2026-01-26T20:17:52Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/314#discussion_r2729107550","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/314","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2729107550"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/314#discussion_r2729107550"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/314"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2729107550/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":18,"original_line":18,"side":"RIGHT","in_reply_to_id":2727572689,"author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","original_position":5,"position":5,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2729108163","pull_request_review_id":3707829144,"id":2729108163,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs6iquLD","diff_hunk":"@@ -15,7 +15,7 @@ doctest = false\n \n [dependencies]\n # SDK - public API, models, and errors\n-types-registry-sdk = { package = \"cf-types-registry-sdk\", version = \"0.1.0\", path = \"../types-registry-sdk\" }\n+types-registry-sdk = { package = \"cf-types-registry-sdk\", version = \"0.1.0\", path = \"../types_registry-sdk\" }","path":"modules/system/types_registry/types_registry/Cargo.toml","commit_id":"a74cb06a65cf7b83d5f293524c5efe43871f47c0","original_commit_id":"a74cb06a65cf7b83d5f293524c5efe43871f47c0","user":{"login":"coderabbitai[bot]","id":136622811,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOCCSy2w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/347564?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/coderabbitai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"<details>\n<summary>🧩 Analysis chain</summary>\n\n🏁 Script executed:\n```\n#!/bin/bash\n# Check actual directory structure for both modules to verify naming convention\necho \"=== Directory structure for types_registry ===\"\nfd -t d -d 1 . modules/system/types_registry 2>/dev/null\n\necho -e \"\\n=== Directory structure for simple_user_settings ===\"\nfd -t d -d 1 . modules/simple_user_settings 2>/dev/null\n\necho -e \"\\n=== Verify naming in workspace root Cargo.toml ===\"\ngrep -E \"(types_registry|simple_user_settings)\" Cargo.toml\n```\n\nLength of output: 796\n\n---\n\n\n\n</details>\n\n`@Artifizer`, thank you for clarifying the naming convention! You're absolutely right that `types_registry-sdk` follows the agreed pattern.\n\nHowever, I notice that `simple_user_settings_sdk` in this PR doesn't follow the same convention. According to the \"module_name-suffix\" pattern, it should be `simple_user_settings-sdk` (with a hyphen) rather than `simple_user_settings_sdk` (with an underscore).\n\n**Current state in this PR:**\n- ✅ `types_registry-sdk` (correct: snake_case + hyphen + suffix)\n- ❌ `simple_user_settings_sdk` (incorrect: should be `simple_user_settings-sdk`)\n\nWould you like to update `simple_user_settings_sdk` to `simple_user_settings-sdk` to maintain consistency across the workspace?\n\n---\n\n<details>\n<summary>✏️ Learnings added</summary>\n\n```\nLearnt from: Artifizer\nRepo: hypernetix/hyperspot PR: 314\nFile: modules/system/types_registry/types_registry/Cargo.toml:18-18\nTimestamp: 2026-01-26T20:17:53.124Z\nLearning: In Rust workspace modules, the naming convention follows \"module_name-suffix\" pattern where module_name uses snake_case and suffix (like \"sdk\", \"gw\") is separated by a hyphen. Example: types_registry-sdk, simple_user_settings-sdk.\n```\n\n> Note: Learnings are effective only in the context of similar code segments. To apply general coding guidelines, please configure [review instructions](https://docs.coderabbit.ai/guides/review-instructions). You can manage existing learnings in the [app](https://app.coderabbit.ai/learnings).\n\n</details>\n\n\n\n---\n\n<details>\n<summary>🧠 Learnings used</summary>\n\n```\nLearnt from: CR\nRepo: hypernetix/hyperspot PR: 0\nFile: dylint_lints/AGENTS.md:0-0\nTimestamp: 2026-01-14T17:18:31.912Z\nLearning: Applies to dylint_lints/**/Cargo.toml : In `Cargo.toml` for lint crates, reference common workspace dependencies (`clippy_utils`, `dylint_linting`, `lint_utils`) using `.workspace = true` to avoid duplication\n```\n\n---\n\n```\nLearnt from: CR\nRepo: hypernetix/hyperspot PR: 0\nFile: dylint_lints/AGENTS.md:0-0\nTimestamp: 2026-01-14T17:18:31.912Z\nLearning: Applies to dylint_lints/**/Cargo.toml : Register new lint crates by adding them to the `members` list in the workspace root `Cargo.toml`\n```\n\n</details>\n\n\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated reply by CodeRabbit -->","created_at":"2026-01-26T20:18:03Z","updated_at":"2026-01-26T20:18:03Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/314#discussion_r2729108163","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/314","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2729108163"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/314#discussion_r2729108163"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/314"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2729108163/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":18,"original_line":18,"side":"RIGHT","in_reply_to_id":2727572693,"author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","original_position":5,"position":5,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2729108348","pull_request_review_id":3707829421,"id":2729108348,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs6iquN8","diff_hunk":"@@ -15,7 +15,7 @@ workspace = true\n [dependencies]\n # Local dependencies\n tenant-resolver-sdk = { package = \"cf-tenant-resolver-sdk\", version = \"0.1.0\", path = \"../../tenant_resolver-sdk\" }\n-types-registry-sdk = { package = \"cf-types-registry-sdk\", version = \"0.1.0\", path = \"../../../types-registry/types-registry-sdk\" }\n+types-registry-sdk = { package = \"cf-types-registry-sdk\", version = \"0.1.0\", path = \"../../../types_registry/types_registry-sdk\" }","path":"modules/system/tenant_resolver/plugins/static_tr_plugin/Cargo.toml","commit_id":"a74cb06a65cf7b83d5f293524c5efe43871f47c0","original_commit_id":"a74cb06a65cf7b83d5f293524c5efe43871f47c0","user":{"login":"coderabbitai[bot]","id":136622811,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOCCSy2w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/347564?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/coderabbitai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"`@Artifizer`, thank you for the clarification! I understand the convention is `module_name` + `-<suffix>` (hyphen before suffix), which makes `types_registry-sdk` correct for this file.\n\nHowever, I noticed an inconsistency within this PR:\n- ✅ `types_registry/types_registry-sdk` (uses hyphen)\n- ❌ `simple_user_settings/simple_user_settings_sdk` (uses underscore)\n\nBased on the convention you described, should `simple_user_settings_sdk` be renamed to `simple_user_settings-sdk` for consistency?\n\n\n\n<!-- <review_comment_addressed> -->\n\n---\n\n<details>\n<summary>✏️ Learnings added</summary>\n\n```\nLearnt from: Artifizer\nRepo: hypernetix/hyperspot PR: 314\nFile: modules/system/tenant_resolver/plugins/static_tr_plugin/Cargo.toml:18-18\nTimestamp: 2026-01-26T20:17:54.827Z\nLearning: In the hyperspot repository, the naming convention for SDK subdirectories is \"module_name\" + \"-<suffix>\" (e.g., types_registry-sdk, not types_registry_sdk). Module directories use snake_case, but suffixes like \"-sdk\" use a hyphen separator.\n```\n\n> Note: Learnings are effective only in the context of similar code segments. To apply general coding guidelines, please configure [review instructions](https://docs.coderabbit.ai/guides/review-instructions). You can manage existing learnings in the [app](https://app.coderabbit.ai/learnings).\n\n</details>\n\n\n\n---\n\n<details>\n<summary>🧠 Learnings used</summary>\n\n```\nLearnt from: CR\nRepo: hypernetix/hyperspot PR: 0\nFile: dylint_lints/AGENTS.md:0-0\nTimestamp: 2026-01-14T17:18:31.912Z\nLearning: Applies to dylint_lints/**/Cargo.toml : In `Cargo.toml` for lint crates, reference common workspace dependencies (`clippy_utils`, `dylint_linting`, `lint_utils`) using `.workspace = true` to avoid duplication\n```\n\n---\n\n```\nLearnt from: CR\nRepo: hypernetix/hyperspot PR: 0\nFile: dylint_lints/AGENTS.md:0-0\nTimestamp: 2026-01-14T17:18:31.912Z\nLearning: Applies to dylint_lints/**/Cargo.toml : Register new lint crates by adding them to the `members` list in the workspace root `Cargo.toml`\n```\n\n</details>\n\n\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated reply by CodeRabbit -->","created_at":"2026-01-26T20:18:09Z","updated_at":"2026-01-26T20:18:09Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/314#discussion_r2729108348","p