ough</summary>\n\n## Walkthrough\n\nReplaced git-sourced gts/gts-macros with version literals in Cargo manifests and standardized in-memory SQLite DSNs in several tests, including adding TempDir-based DSN construction for the shared-memory SQLite test.\n\n## Changes\n\n| Cohort / File(s) | Summary |\n|---|---|\n| **Workspace Cargo manifests** <br> `Cargo.toml`, `dylint_lints/Cargo.toml` | Replaced git-based dependencies for `gts` and `gts-macros` with explicit version strings (top-level `Cargo.toml`: `\"0.1\"`; `dylint_lints/Cargo.toml`: `\"0.1.0\"`) |\n| **Advisory locks tests** <br> `libs/modkit-db/src/advisory_locks.rs` | Updated test DSNs from `sqlite:file:memdbX?mode=memory&cache=shared` to `sqlite::memory:` across multiple tests (no logic changes) |\n| **Shared-memory SQLite test** <br> `libs/modkit-db/tests/sqlite/sqlite_tests.rs` | Replaced hardcoded DSN with TempDir-derived path and `sqlite://{memdb_path}?mode=memory&cache=shared`; removed redundant TempDir and narrowed `manager.get(\"test_module\").await` scope |\n\n## Estimated code review effort\n\n🎯 2 (Simple) | ⏱️ ~10 minutes\n\n## Poem\n\n> 🐰 I tweaked the crates with a careful hop,  \n> swapped branches for versions—no more Git crop.  \n> I tucked a memdb in a TempDir bed,  \n> let SQLite share its memory thread.  \n> A tiny hop, and tests nod ahead.\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- walkthrough_end -->\n\n\n<!-- pre_merge_checks_walkthrough_start -->\n\n<details>\n<summary>🚥 Pre-merge checks | ✅ 3</summary>\n\n<details>\n<summary>✅ Passed checks (3 passed)</summary>\n\n|     Check name     | Status   | Explanation                                                                                                                        |\n| :----------------: | :------- | :--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n|  Description Check | ✅ Passed | Check skipped - CodeRabbit’s high-level summary is enabled.                                                                        |\n| Docstring Coverage | ✅ Passed | Docstring coverage is 100.00% which is sufficient. The required threshold is 80.00%.                                               |\n|     Title check    | ✅ Passed | The title accurately summarizes both main changes: switching gts dependencies from git to crates.io and updating SQLite test DSNs. |\n\n</details>\n\n<sub>✏️ Tip: You can configure your own custom pre-merge checks in the settings.</sub>\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- pre_merge_checks_walkthrough_end -->\n\n<!-- finishing_touch_checkbox_start -->\n\n<details>\n<summary>✨ Finishing touches</summary>\n\n- [ ] <!-- {\"checkboxId\": \"7962f53c-55bc-4827-bfbf-6a18da830691\"} --> 📝 Generate docstrings\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- finishing_touch_checkbox_end -->\n\n<!-- tips_start -->\n\n---\n\n\n\n<sub>Comment `@coderabbitai help` to get the list of available commands and usage tips.</sub>\n\n<!-- tips_end -->\n\n<!-- internal state start -->\n\n\n<!--  -->\n\n<!-- internal state end -->","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/issues/comments/3796848566/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":{"id":347564,"client_id":"Iv1.6aaafe4fe882736b","slug":"coderabbitai","node_id":"A_kwHOB96YWc4ABU2s","owner":{"login":"coderabbitai","id":132028505,"node_id":"O_kgDOB96YWQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/132028505?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai","html_url":"https://github.com/coderabbitai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.gi