`\n\nRepository: hypernetix/hyperspot\n\nLength of output: 141\n\n---\n\n🏁 Script executed:\n\n```shell\n# Check git history to see what the previous dependency specification was\ngit log --oneline -n 20 -- Cargo.toml | head -20\n```\n\nRepository: hypernetix/hyperspot\n\nLength of output: 194\n\n---\n\n🏁 Script executed:\n\n```shell\n# Look at the current Cargo.toml to understand the full context\nsed -n '420,440p' Cargo.toml\n```\n\nRepository: hypernetix/hyperspot\n\nLength of output: 223\n\n---\n\n🏁 Script executed:\n\n```shell\n# Get the previous version of Cargo.toml before the switch to crates.io\ngit show HEAD~1:Cargo.toml | sed -n '420,440p'\n```\n\nRepository: hypernetix/hyperspot\n\nLength of output: 100\n\n---\n\n🏁 Script executed:\n\n```shell\n# Search for any references to v0.7.7 or gts in git history\ngit log --all --grep=\"gts\" --oneline | head -10\n```\n\nRepository: hypernetix/hyperspot\n\nLength of output: 762\n\n---\n\n🏁 Script executed:\n\n```shell\n# Check if there's any tag or reference to v0.7.7\ngit tag | grep -i \"v0.7.7\\|gts\"\n```\n\nRepository: hypernetix/hyperspot\n\nLength of output: 46\n\n---\n\n🏁 Script executed:\n\n```shell\n# Check the commit that switched to crates.io for any documentation or tests verifying compatibility\ngit show 4fd8304 --stat\n```\n\nRepository: hypernetix/hyperspot\n\nLength of output: 50376\n\n---\n\n🏁 Script executed:\n\n```shell\n# Search for any migration notes or comments about the gts-rust to gts transition\ngit log --all --oneline -S \"gts\" | head -15\n```\n\nRepository: hypernetix/hyperspot\n\nLength of output: 150\n\n---\n\n🏁 Script executed:\n\n```shell\n# Check if there are any tests or examples that might indicate API compatibility\nrg -t toml \"git.*gts\" --no-heading\n```\n\nRepository: hypernetix/hyperspot\n\nLength of output: 564\n\n---\n\n\n\n</details>\n\n**Verify API compatibility and resolve inconsistent dependencies for gts migration.**\n\nThe switch from `gts-rust` v0.7.7 to `gts` 0.1.0 represents a significant change: both a package rename and major version downgrade. The new crates.io versions lack documentation, making it impossible to confirm API parity.\n\nAdditionally, `dylint_lints/Cargo.toml` still references the old git source (`gts-rust` v0.7.7), creating an inconsistency. Ensure the migration is complete across all workspace members and that dependencies resolve correctly without version conflicts.\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nIn `@Cargo.toml` around lines 429 - 430, The workspace migration replaced gts-rust\nv0.7.7 with gts = \"0.1\" and gts-macros = \"0.1\" but left inconsistent references\n(e.g., dylint_lints/Cargo.toml still points to gts-rust), so verify API\ncompatibility and make dependency declarations consistent across the workspace:\ninspect public APIs used from gts-rust in your codebase (functions/types/macros\nreferenced), update call sites to match the new gts/gts-macros APIs or revert to\nthe compatible crate, update every Cargo.toml that still references gts-rust\n(including dylint_lints) to the chosen crate/version, run cargo update and cargo\nbuild to detect version conflicts, and if the new crate lacks parity pin the\ncorrect git/rev or restore gts-rust v0.7.7 to avoid breaking changes.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- fingerprinting:phantom:poseidon:eagle -->\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment by CodeRabbit -->","created_at":"2026-01-25T16:45:49Z","updated_at":"2026-01-25T16:45:51Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/307#discussion_r2725713735","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/307","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2725713735"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/307#discussion_r2725713735"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/307"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://a