o}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-01-23T22:34:42Z","updated_at":"2026-01-23T22:47:13Z","body":"<!-- This is an auto-generated comment: summarize by coderabbit.ai -->\n<!-- walkthrough_start -->\n\n<details>\n<summary>📝 Walkthrough</summary>\n\n## Walkthrough\n\nAdds automatic labeling of release PRs in the CI workflow, changes release workflow triggers/conditions to require the `release-plz` label or manual dispatch for publishing, updates changelog formatting and docs, and disables semver checks by default in `release-plz.toml` for initial bootstrap.\n\n## Changes\n\n| Cohort / File(s) | Summary |\n|---|---|\n| **Release Workflow** <br> `\\.github/workflows/release-plz.yml` | Adds `pull_request` trigger (closed PRs to `main`), new \"Label release PR\" step that queries open PRs targeting `main` whose `headRefName` starts with `release-plz-` or whose author is `release-plz`, and applies the `release-plz` label. Revises release job to publish only on manual `workflow_dispatch` (mode=`release`) or when a merged PR on `main` has the `release-plz` label. Comments added clarifying labeling and publishing criteria. |\n| **Repository config** <br> `release-plz.toml` | Sets default `semver_check = false` with explanatory note about bootstrap noise and re-enabling after first successful publish. |\n| **Documentation** <br> `docs/releasing.md` | Documents new automatic labeling behavior and that the release job runs only after a labeled PR is merged; adds bootstrap note about crates.io rate limiting (HTTP 429) and idempotent re-runs. |\n| **Changelog** <br> `CHANGELOG.md` | Rewrote header to Keep a Changelog style, added links to semantic versioning guidance, inserted an \"Unreleased\" section (Added/Changed/Fixed), noted that release-plz updates the file, and preserved `0.1.0` entry. |\n\n## Sequence Diagram(s)\n\n```mermaid\nsequenceDiagram\n    participant PR as Release PR\n    participant GH_WF as GitHub Actions Workflow\n    participant GH_API as GitHub API\n    participant Release as Release Job\n\n    PR->>GH_WF: merged to main (pull_request.closed)\n    activate GH_WF\n    GH_WF->>GH_API: query open PRs targeting main (headRefName starts with \"release-plz-\" OR author=\"release-plz\")\n    GH_API-->>GH_WF: return matching PRs\n    GH_WF->>GH_API: add label \"release-plz\" to matching PR(s)\n    GH_API-->>GH_WF: label applied\n    alt merged PR has \"release-plz\" label or manual dispatch (mode=release)\n        GH_WF->>Release: invoke release job\n        activate Release\n        Release->>Release: publish artifacts to registry\n        deactivate Release\n    end\n    deactivate GH_WF\n```\n\n## Estimated code review effort\n\n🎯 3 (Moderate) | ⏱️ ~22 minutes\n\n## Poem\n\n> 🐰 *I hopped through workflows late at night,*  \n> *Labeled PRs with gentle bite,*  \n> *A bootstrap pause, then crates take flight,*  \n> *Changelogs tidy, everything right!* ✨\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- walkthrough_end -->\n\n\n<!-- pre_merge_checks_walkthrough_start -->\n\n<details>\n<summary>🚥 Pre-merge checks | ✅ 3</summary>\n\n<details>\n<summary>✅ Passed checks (3 passed)</summary>\n\n|     Check name     | Status   | Explanation                                                                                                               |\n| :----------------: | :------- | :------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ |\n|  Description Check | ✅ Passed | Check skipped - CodeRabbit’s high-level summary is enabled.                                                               |\n|     Title check    | ✅ Passed | The title accurately summarizes the main changes: auto-labeling release PRs and gating publish to merged release-plz PRs. |\n| Docstring Coverage | ✅ Passed | No functions found in the changed files to evaluate docstring coverage. Skipping docstring coverage check.                |\n\n</details>\n\n<sub>✏️ Tip: You can configure your own custom pre-merge checks in the settings.</sub>\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- pre_merge_checks_walkthrough_end -->\n\n<!-- tips_start -->\n\n---\n\n\n\n<sub>Comment `@coderabbitai help` to get the list of available commands and usage tips.</sub>\n\n<!-- tips_end -->\n\n<!-- internal state start -->\n\n\n<!--  -->\n\n<!-- internal state end -->","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/issues/comments/3792871921/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":{"id":347564,"client_id":"Iv1.6aaafe4fe882736b","slug":"coderabbitai","node_id":"A_kwHOB96YWc4ABU2s","owner":{"login":"coderabbitai","id":132028505,"node_id":"O_kgDOB96YWQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/132028505?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai","html_url":"https://github.com/coderabbitai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/received_events","type":"Organization","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"name":"coderabbitai","description":"# Transforming Code Reviews with AI\r\n\r\n## Features\r\n\r\n**Automated Reviews**: Continuous reviews of the pull requests including incremental commits. \r\n\r\n**Summarization**: Generates high-level summary and a technical walkthrough of the PR changes. \r\n\r\n**Line-by-line review**: Provides line-by-line suggestions committable with one click.\r\n\r\n**Codebase verification**:  Verifies the impact on the overall codebase and identifies missing changes.\r\n\r\n**Insights into your code**:  Ask any questions on your codebase within the pull request \r\n\r\n**Chat about your code** : Chat with the bot around your code. The more you chat, the smarter it gets.\r\n\r\n**Issue Validation**:  Validates the PR against the linked issues and identifies other related issues \r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n","external_url":"https://coderabbit.ai?utm_source=cr_app&utm_medium=github","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/coderabbitai","created_at":"2023-06-14T15:47:27Z","updated_at":"2026-03-14T07:58:44Z","permissions":{"actions":"read","checks":"write","contents":"write","discussions":"read","issues":"write","members":"read","metadata":"read","pull_requests":"write","statuses":"write"},"events":["issues","issue_comment","label","organization","pull_request","pull_request_review","pull_request_review_comment","pull_request_review_thread","release","repository"]}},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/issues/comments/3792876217","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/304#issuecomment-3792876217","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/issues/304","id":3792876217,"node_id":"IC_kwDOPaLyBs7iErK5","user":{"login":"mergify[bot]","id":37929162,"node_id":"MDM6Qm90Mzc5MjkxNjI=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/10562?v=4","gravatar_id":"","ur