/api.github.com/users/Bechma/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bechma/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bechma/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bechma/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bechma/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"are we going to publish this one also?","created_at":"2026-01-23T13:56:28Z","updated_at":"2026-01-23T13:58:04Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/303#discussion_r2721299201","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/303","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2721299201"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/303#discussion_r2721299201"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/303"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2721299201/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":4,"original_line":4,"side":"LEFT","author_association":"MEMBER","original_position":4,"position":4,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2721315136","pull_request_review_id":3697634974,"id":2721315136,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs6iM_lA","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,81 @@\n+name: Release (release-plz)\n+\n+on:\n+  push:\n+    branches:\n+      - main\n+  workflow_dispatch:\n+    inputs:\n+      mode:\n+        description: \"Which release-plz command to run\"\n+        required: true\n+        default: \"release\"\n+        type: choice\n+        options:\n+          - release\n+          - release-pr\n+\n+concurrency:\n+  group: release-plz-${{ github.workflow }}-${{ github.ref }}\n+  cancel-in-progress: false\n+\n+jobs:\n+  release-pr:\n+    name: Create release PR\n+    runs-on: ubuntu-latest\n+    if: ${{ github.event_name == 'push' || github.event.inputs.mode == 'release-pr' }}\n+    permissions:\n+      contents: write\n+      pull-requests: write\n+    steps:\n+      - name: Checkout\n+        uses: actions/checkout@34e114876b0b11c390a56381ad16ebd13914f8d5 # v4.3.1\n+        with:\n+          fetch-depth: 0\n+          persist-credentials: false\n+\n+      - name: Install Rust toolchain\n+        uses: dtolnay/rust-toolchain@4be9e76fd7c4901c61fb841f559994984270fce7 # stable\n+\n+      - name: release-plz release-pr\n+        uses: release-plz/action@v0.5\n+        with:","path":".github/workflows/release-plz.yml","commit_id":"d24898483e891dd23eac658c2e2d21a92634cbac","original_commit_id":"76e998087fa6cfc7abfef3b99ce42d6c55b410f2","user":{"login":"coderabbitai[bot]","id":136622811,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOCCSy2w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/347564?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/coderabbitai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"_⚠️ Potential issue_ | _🟠 Major_\n\n<details>\n<summary>🧩 Analysis chain</summary>\n\n🌐 Web query:\n\n`release-plz/action GitHub pinning commit SHA best practices`\n\n💡 Result:\n\n## Best practices: pinning `release-plz/action` (and other GitHub Actions) to commit SHAs\n\n1. **Prefer full (40-char) commit SHA pins for third‑party actions** (most tamper-resistant / immutable reference). GitHub explicitly recommends pinning to a full-length commit SHA. [1]\n\n2. **Avoid floating tags like `@v0.5` for security-sensitive workflows.** `release-plz`’s docs note that `release-plz/action@v0.5` is a moving tag (tracks latest `0.5.x`), which is convenient but increases supply-chain risk. They recommend pinning to a specific commit hash instead. [2]\n\n3. **Pin to the SHA corresponding to a release tag, and record the human version in a comment** (so it’s auditable and tools can propose updates more easily). Example pattern: `action@<sha> # vX.Y.Z`. [3]\n\n4. **Automate updates (don’t “set and forget”).** Use Dependabot (GitHub-native) or a pinning/updater tool so you still get security fixes while keeping immutability. GitHub’s guidance is to pin, then update deliberately. [1]\n\n5. **Enforce SHA pinning centrally where possible.** GitHub Actions policies can require SHA pinning; GitHub also added explicit “enforce SHA pinning” support in Actions policy controls (Aug 15, 2025). [4]\n\n### Example: pin `release-plz/action` to a commit SHA\n```yaml\n- name: Run release-plz\n  uses: release-plz/action@63ab0c2746bedc448370bad4b0b3d536458398b0 # v0.5.x (replace with exact release)\n```\n(Use the SHA for the specific release you intend to trust; `release-plz` documents this approach and uses it themselves in practice.) [2]\n\n**Sources:** GitHub Actions security guidance [1], release-plz security docs [2], GitHub Well-Architected Actions security recommendation [3], GitHub Changelog on SHA-pinning enforcement [4].\n\n---\n\n🌐 Web query:\n\n`release-plz/action v0.5 commit SHA releases`\n\n💡 Result:\n\n- `release-plz/action@v0.5` is a **moving tag** that always points to the latest **0.5.x** release of the action (so the underlying commit SHA can change whenever a new 0.5.x is published). [1]  \n- The Release-plz docs show an example of pinning the action by commit SHA: `63ab0c2746bedc448370bad4b0b3d536458398b0`. [1]  \n- To see the **full list of action releases** (and pick a specific 0.5.x), the docs recommend checking the **previous GitHub Action releases** for `release-plz/action`. [2]\n\n**Sources:**  \n[1] Release-plz docs – Security (GitHub Action pinning / `v0.5` behavior) ([release-plz.dev](https://release-plz.dev/docs/github/security?utm_source=openai))  \n[2] Release-plz docs – Troubleshooting (check previous GitHub Action releases) ([release-plz.dev](https://release-plz.dev/docs/troubleshooting?utm_source=openai))\n\nCitations:\n\n- 1: https://release-plz.dev/docs/github/security?utm_source=openai\n- 2: https://release-plz.dev/docs/troubleshooting?utm_source=openai\n\n---\n\n🌐 Web query:\n\n`GitHub Actions pinning to commit SHA best practices security`\n\n💡 Result:\n\n## GitHub Actions security best practices for pinning to commit SHAs\n\n- **Pin third‑party actions (and reusable workflows) to a *full‑length* commit SHA** (not a branch or tag) to get an immutable reference and reduce supply‑chain risk from retagging or compromised upstream releases. Verify the SHA is from the *official* upstream repo (not a fork). [1][2]  \n  - Example: `uses: actions/checkout@692973e3d937129bcbf40652eb9f2f61becf3332 # v4.1.7` [2]\n\n- **Prefer SHAs that correspond to a tagged release**, and **leave a comment with the release version** (helps humans track updates; many teams standardize this). [2]\n\n- **Audit the action’s code (and behavior) before pinning**, especially anything that touches secrets, networking, or PR-provided inputs. [1]\n\n- **Watch out for “unpinnable” behavior even when pinned**: some actions remain effectively mutable because they pull code at runtime, reference unpinned container images, or otherwise depend on mutable external artifacts. Review for these patterns and avoid them when possible. [2][4]\n\n- **Use GitHub policy controls to enforce SHA pinning** (org/enterprise governance): GitHub’s allowed-actions policy can be configured to require SHA pinning, and can also explicitly block specific actions/versions. [3]\n\n- **Plan for updates intentionally**: pinning improves integrity but increases maintenance—set an owner/process to regularly bump SHAs after review/testing. (Also note: GitHub docs mention Dependabot limitations/behavior around alerts and SHA-pinning.) [1]\n\n**Sources:** GitHub Docs security hardening guidance [1], GitHub Well‑Architected Actions security recommendations [2], GitHub Changelog on SHA‑pinning enforcement/blocking policies [3], and research on “unpinnable” actions risks [4].\n\n---\n\n🏁 Script executed:\n\n```shell\ncat -n .github/workflows/release-plz.yml\n```\n\nRepository: hypernetix/hyperspot\n\nLength of output: 2953\n\n---\n\n\n\n</details>\n\n**Pin `release-plz/action` to a commit SHA.**\n\nLines 41 and 75 use a mutable tag (`v0.5`). All other actions in this workflow are already pinned to commit SHAs; pinning `release-plz/action` aligns with that pattern and reduces supply-chain risk. The release-plz project documentation explicitly recommends SHA pinning.\n\n<details>\n<summary>🔒 Proposed change</summary>\n\n```diff\n      - name: release-plz release-pr\n-       uses: release-plz/action@v0.5\n+       uses: release-plz/action@<commit-sha> # v0.5.x\n        with:\n          command: release-pr\n...\n      - name: release-plz release\n-       uses: release-plz/action@v0.5\n+       uses: release-plz/action@<commit-sha> # v0.5.x\n        with:\n          command: release\n```\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nIn @.github/workflows/release-plz.yml around lines 40 - 42, The workflow uses a\nmutable tag for the release step (\"release-plz release-pr\") referencing\nrelease-plz/action@v0.5; replace the tag with the specific commit SHA\nrecommended by release-plz (pin the action to a commit) so the step uses\nrelease-plz/action@<COMMIT_SHA> instead of `@v0.5`—update both occurrences if\npresent to match other actions' SHA pinning and keep the step name \"release-plz\nrelease-pr\" unchanged.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- fingerprinting:phantom:poseidon:eagle -->\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment by CodeRabbit -->\n\n✅ Addressed in commit 7ed8e12","created_at":"2026-01-23T14:00:29Z","updated_at":"2026-01-23T16:42:03Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/303#discussion_r2721315136","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/303","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2721315136"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/303#discussion_r2721315136"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/303"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2721315136/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":40,"original_start_line":40,"start_side":"RIGHT","line":42,"original_line":42,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","original_position":42,"position":42,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2721315148","pull_request_review_id":3697634974,"id":2721315148,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs6iM_lM","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,70 @@\n+## Releasing (automated)\n+\n+This repository uses **release-plz** to automate:\n+- version bumps\n+- changelog updates\n+- crates.io publishing\n+- GitHub releases\n+\n+### How the flow works\n+\n+- **On every push to `main`** the workflow runs `release-plz release-pr`.\n+- If there are releasable changes, release-plz opens a **Release PR** updating:\n+  - crate versions (per-crate, based on each crate’s `Cargo.toml`)\n+  - the root [`CHANGELOG.md`](../CHANGELOG.md)\n+- **After the Release PR is merged**, the workflow runs `release-plz release` which:\n+  - publishes crates to crates.io (only crates that are publishable and have a new version)\n+  - creates GitHub Releases\n+\n+Workflows:\n+- Root workspace: [`.github/workflows/release-plz.yml`](../.github/workflows/release-plz.yml)\n+\n+### What gets published\n+\n+Publishing is controlled by Cargo manifests:\n+- crates with `publish = false` are **never published**\n+- crates without `publish = false` are **publishable** (subject to crates.io rules)\n+\n+This repo is configured so that:\n+- `apps/**` and `examples/**` are **not** publishable (we set `publish = false`)\n+- `libs/**` and `modules/**` are publishable as intended\n+\n+### Versioning policy (as implemented)\n+\n+- **Framework (`libs/cf-modkit*`)**: share a single version via `version.workspace = true` and the root workspace version (`Cargo.toml` → `[workspace.package] version`).","path":"docs/releasing.md","commit_id":"76e998087fa6cfc7abfef3b99ce42d6c55b410f2","original_commit_id":"76e998087fa6cfc7abfef3b99ce42d6c55b410f2","user":{"login":"coderabbitai[bot]","id":136622811,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOCCSy2w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/347564?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/coderabbitai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"_⚠️ Potential issue_ | _🟡 Minor_\n\n**Clarify path vs package name in versioning policy.**\n\nThe text references `libs/cf-modkit*` but the actual directory paths are `libs/modkit-*` (without the `cf-` prefix). The `cf-` prefix applies to the package names in `Cargo.toml`, not the filesystem paths. Consider updating to avoid confusion:\n\n\n<details>\n<summary>Suggested fix</summary>\n\n```diff\n-- **Framework (`libs/cf-modkit*`)**: share a single version via `version.workspace = true` and the root workspace version (`Cargo.toml` → `[workspace.package] version`).\n++ **Framework (`libs/modkit-*` crates, published as `cf-modkit-*`)**: share a single version via `version.workspace = true` and the root workspace version (`Cargo.toml` → `[workspace.package] version`).\n```\n</details>\n\n<!-- suggestion_start -->\n\n<details>\n<summary>📝 Committable suggestion</summary>\n\n> ‼️ **IMPORTANT**\n> Carefully review the code before committing. Ensure that it accurately replaces the highlighted code, contains no missing lines, and has no issues with indentation. Thoroughly test & benchmark the code to ensure it meets the requirements.\n\n```suggestion\n- **Framework (`libs/modkit-*` crates, published as `cf-modkit-*`)**: share a single version via `version.workspace = true` and the root workspace version (`Cargo.toml` → `[workspace.package] version`).\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- suggestion_end -->\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nIn `@docs/releasing.md` at line 34, Update the wording to distinguish filesystem\npaths from package names: change the reference from \"libs/cf-modkit*\" to\n\"libs/modkit-*\" (filesystem directories) and note that the \"cf-\" prefix is used\nin Cargo package names in Cargo.toml (e.g., package.name = \"cf-modkit-*\"); keep\nthe guidance that these crates share a single version via version.workspace =\ntrue and the root [workspace.package] version in Cargo.toml.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- fingerprinting:phantom:poseidon:ocelot -->\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment by CodeRabbit -->\n\n✅ Addressed in commit 7ed8e12","created_at":"2026-01-23T14:00:29Z","updated_at":"2026-01-23T16:42:02Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/303#discussion_r2721315148","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/303","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2721315148"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/303#discussion_r2721315148"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/303"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2721315148/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":null,"original_line":34,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","original_position":34,"position":1,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2721315159","pull_request_review_id":3697634974,"id":2721315159,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs6iM_lX","diff_hunk":"@@ -1,5 +1,5 @@\n [package]\n-name = \"nodes_registry-sdk\"\n+name = \"cf-nodes_registry-sdk\"","path":"modules/system/nodes_registry/nodes_registry-sdk/Cargo.toml","commit_id":"7ed8e12ee7d348d122e710eb0a701d0b2642ec5f","original_commit_id":"76e998087fa6cfc7abfef3b99ce42d6c55b410f2","user":{"login":"coderabbitai[bot]","id":136622811,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOCCSy2w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/347564?v=4