</summary>\n\n## Walkthrough\n\nAdds end-to-end fuzzing: local tooling and Makefile targets, three libFuzzer fuzz targets, ClusterFuzzLite CI workflow and build config, containerized build script, workspace and gitignore updates, and documentation for running fuzzing locally and in CI.\n\n## Changes\n\n| Cohort / File(s) | Summary |\n|---|---|\n| **CI Workflow** <br> `\\.github/workflows/clusterfuzzlite.yml` | New GitHub Actions workflow to trigger ClusterFuzzLite fuzzing on PRs and manual dispatch (address sanitizer, 600s runs, SARIF enabled, crash artifact upload). |\n| **ClusterFuzzLite Build** <br> `\\.clusterfuzzlite/Dockerfile`, `\\.clusterfuzzlite/build.sh`, `\\.clusterfuzzlite/project.yaml` | Container build, build script and project config to compile fuzz binaries with nightly Rust and copy outputs for ClusterFuzzLite. |\n| **Fuzz Targets** <br> `fuzz/fuzz_targets/fuzz_odata_cursor.rs`, `fuzz/fuzz_targets/fuzz_odata_filter.rs`, `fuzz/fuzz_targets/fuzz_odata_orderby.rs` | Three libFuzzer harnesses added; each caps input size and invokes existing OData parsing/decoding code paths. |\n| **Fuzz Package & Toolchain** <br> `fuzz/Cargo.toml`, `fuzz/rust-toolchain.toml`, `fuzz/.gitignore` | New fuzz crate metadata, nightly toolchain config (rust-src), and fuzz-specific .gitignore entries. |\n| **Dev Tooling & Scripts** <br> `Makefile`, `scripts/ci.py` | New Makefile targets (`fuzz-install`, `fuzz-build`, `fuzz-list`, `fuzz-run`, `fuzz`, `fuzz-clean`, `fuzz-corpus`) and CLI subcommands in `scripts/ci.py` to build/list/run/clean fuzz targets; enforce nightly toolchain and cargo-fuzz checks. |\n| **Docs & Project Config** <br> `README.md`, `CONTRIBUTING.md`, `fuzz/README.md`, `\\.gitignore`, `Cargo.toml` | Added fuzzing docs and CONTRIBUTING section, updated global and fuzz .gitignore rules, excluded `fuzz` from workspace in `Cargo.toml`. |\n\n## Sequence Diagram(s)\n\n```mermaid\nsequenceDiagram\n  autonumber\n  participant Dev as Developer (PR)\n  participant GH as GitHub Actions\n  participant CFLT as ClusterFuzzLite Runner\n  participant Docker as Docker Build\n  participant Fuzz as Fuzz Binaries\n\n  Dev->>GH: Push PR / workflow_dispatch\n  GH->>CFLT: Start ClusterFuzzLite job (address sanitizer)\n  CFLT->>Docker: Build container using .clusterfuzzlite/Dockerfile\n  Docker->>CFLT: Deliver container with nightly Rust and build.sh\n  CFLT->>CFLT: Run build.sh (cargo fuzz build -O)\n  CFLT->>Fuzz: Produce fuzz binaries and copy to $OUT\n  CFLT->>GH: Upload SARIF + fuzz crash artifacts on failures\n  GH->>Dev: Report status and provide artifact links\n```\n\n## Estimated code review effort\n\n🎯 3 (Moderate) | ⏱️ ~22 minutes\n\n## Possibly related issues\n\n- **#269** — Implements CI fuzzing and Makefile/CLI integration requested to enable fuzzing in CI.  \n- **#349** — Matches ClusterFuzzLite and cargo-fuzz integration (same feature area and files).\n\n## Suggested labels\n\n`easy`\n\n## Suggested reviewers\n\n- Bechma  \n- Artifizer  \n- MikeFalcon77\n\n## Poem\n\n> 🐇  \n> I nibble bytes in moonlit code,  \n> I hop through inputs, light and broad,  \n> Cursor, Filter, OrderBy—peek!  \n> I chase the crash until it squeaks,  \n> Bugs flee — the builds wake up and cheer! 🎉\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- walkthrough_end -->\n\n\n<!-- pre_merge_checks_walkthrough_start -->\n\n<details>\n<summary>🚥 Pre-merge checks | ✅ 4 | ❌ 1</summary>\n\n<details>\n<summary>❌ Failed checks (1 inconclusive)</summary>\n\n|         Check name         | Status         | Explanation                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                     | Resolution                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                             |\n| :------------------------: | :------------- | :-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | :--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| Out of Scope Changes check | ❓ Inconclusive | The PR includes eight fuzz targets as stated in objectives, but the GitHub Actions workflow and summary mention only three HIGH-priority targets while the Cargo.toml shows only two targets enabled (fuzz_odata_cursor and fuzz_odata_orderby) with fuzz_odata_filter disabled due to a discovered parser bug. | Clarify whether all eight fuzz targets mentioned in PR objectives should be included or if this PR intentionally includes only the subset with fuzz_odata_filter removed pending separate issue; verify alignment between stated objectives and actual implementation. |\n\n</details>\n<details>\n<summary>✅ Passed checks (4 passed)</summary>\n\n|      Check name     | Status   | Explanation                                                                                                                                                                                                                                    |\n| :-----------------: | :------- | :--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n|  Description Check  | ✅ Passed | Check skipped - CodeRabbit’s high-level summary is enabled.                                                                                                                                                                                    |\n|     Title check     | ✅ Passed | The PR title 'feat(fuzz): integrate ClusterFuzzLite continuous fuzzing' accurately and concisely describes the main change: adding ClusterFuzzLite continuous fuzzing infrastructure.                                                          |\n| Linked Issues check | ✅ Passed | The PR successfully addresses all coding requirements from issue `#269`: integrates ClusterFuzzLite for CI fuzzing, adds cargo-fuzz infrastructure, exposes developer Makefile targets (fuzz-build, fuzz-list, fuzz), and updates documentation. |\n|  Docstring Coverage | ✅ Passed | Docstring coverage is 100.00% which is sufficient. The required threshold is 80.00%.                                                                                                                                                           |\n\n</details>\n\n<sub>✏️ Tip: You can configure your own custom pre-merge checks in the settings.</sub>\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- pre_merge_checks_walkthrough_end -->\n\n<!-- finishing_touch_checkbox_start -->\n\n<details>\n<summary>✨ Finishing touches</summary>\n\n- [ ] <!-- {\"checkboxId\": \"7962f53c-55bc-4827-bfbf-6a18da830691\"} --> 📝 Generate docstrings\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- finishing_touch_checkbox_end -->\n\n<!-- tips_start -->\n\n---\n\nThanks for using [CodeRabbit](https://coderabbit.ai?utm_source=oss&utm_medium=github&utm_campaign=hypernetix/hyperspot&utm_content=301)! It's free for OSS, and your support helps us grow. If you like it, consider giving us a shout-out.\n\n<details>\n<summary>❤️ Share</summary>\n\n- [X](https://twitter.com/intent/tweet?text=I%20just%20used%20%40coderabbitai%20for%20my%20code%20review%2C%20and%20it%27s%20fantastic%21%20It%27s%20free%20for%20OSS%20and%20offers%20a%20free%20trial%20for%20the%20proprietary%20code.%20Check%20it%20out%3A&url=https%3A//coderabbit.ai)\n- [Mastodon](https://mastodon.social/share?text=I%20just%20used%20%40coderabbitai%20for%20my%20code%20review%2C%20and%20it%27s%20fantastic%21%20It%27s%20free%20for%20OSS%20and%20offers%20a%20free%20trial%20for%20the%20proprietary%20code.%20Check%20it%20out%3A%20https%3A%2F%2Fcoderabbit.ai)\n- [Reddit](https://www.reddit.com/submit?title=Great%20tool%20for%20code%20review%20-%20CodeRabbit&text=I%20just%20used%20CodeRabbit%20for%20my%20code%20review%2C%20and%20it%27s%20fantastic%21%20It%27s%20free%20for%20OSS%20and%20offers%20a%20free%20trial%20for%20proprietary%20code.%20Check%20it%20out%3A%20https%3A//coderabbit.ai)\n- [LinkedIn](https://www.linkedin.com/sharing/share-offsite/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fcoderabbit.ai&mini=true&title=Great%20tool%20for%20code%20review%20-%20CodeRabbit&summary=I%20just%20used%20CodeRabbit%20for%20my%20code%20review%2C%20and%20it%27s%20fantastic%21%20It%27s%20free%20for%20OSS%20and%20offers%20a%20free%20trial%20for%20proprietary%20code)\n\n</details>\n\n<sub>Comment `@coderabbitai help` to get the list of available commands and usage tips.</sub>\n\n<!-- tips_end -->\n\n<!-- internal state start -->\n\n\n<!--  -->\n\n<!-- internal state end -->","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/issues/comments/3789909130/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":{"id":347564,"client_id":"Iv1.6aaafe4fe882736b","slug":"coderabbitai","node_id":"A_kwHOB96YWc4ABU2s","owner":{"login":"coderabbitai","id":132028505,"node_id":"O_kgDOB96YWQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/132028505?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai","html_url":"https://github.com/coderabbitai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/received_events","type":"Organization","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"name":"coderabbitai","description":"# Transforming Code Reviews with AI\r\n\r\n## Features\r\n\r\n**Automated Reviews**: Continuous reviews of the pull requests including incremental commits. \r\n\r\n**Summarization**: Generates high-level summary and a technical walkthrough of the PR changes. \r\n\r\n**Line-by-line review**: Provides line-by-line suggestions committable with one click.\r\n\r\n**Codebase verification**:  Verifies the impact on the overall codebase and identifies missing changes.\r\n\r\n**Insights into your code**:  Ask any questions on your codebase within the pull request \r\n\r\n**Chat about your code** : Chat with the bot around your code. The more you chat, the smarter it gets.\r\n\r\n**Issue Validation**:  Validates the PR against the linked issues and identifies other related issues \r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n","external_url":"https://coderabbit.ai?utm_source=cr_app&utm_medium=github","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/coderabbitai","created_at":"2023-06-14T15:47:27Z","updated_at":"2026-03-14T07:58:44Z","permissions":{"actions":"read","checks":"write","contents":"write","discussions":"read","issues":"write","members":"read","metadata":"read","pull_requests":"write","statuses":"write"},"events":["issues","issue_comment","label","organization","pull_request","pull_request_review","pull_request_review_comment","pull_request_review_thread","release","repository"]}},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/issues/comments/3789912216","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/301#issuecomment-3789912216","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/issues/301","id":3789912216,"node_id":"IC_kwDOPaLyBs7h5XiY","user":{"login":"mergify[bot]","id":37929162,"node_id":"MDM6Qm90Mzc5MjkxNjI=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/10562?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mergify%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/mergify","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mergify%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mergify%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mergify%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mergify%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mergify%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mergify%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mergify%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mergify%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mergify%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-01-23T11:57:23Z","updated_at":"2026-01-28T18:26:07Z","body":"<!--MERGIFY-CI-INSIGHTS-REPORT-->\n# 🧪 CI Insights\n\nHere's what we observed from your CI run for 9ef05615.\n\n## 🟢 All jobs passed!\n\nBut CI Insights is watching 👀","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/issues/comments/3789912216/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":{"id":10562,"client_id":"Iv1.d035f68f69425dc1","slug":"mergify","node_id":"MDM6QXBwMTA1NjI=","owner":{"login":"Mergifyio","id":37838584,"node_id":"MDEyOk9yZ2FuaXphdGlvbjM3ODM4NTg0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/37838584?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mergifyio","html_url":"https://github.com/Mergifyio","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mergifyio/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mergifyio/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mergifyio/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mergifyio/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mergifyio/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mergifyio/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mergifyio/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mergifyio/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mergifyio/received_events","type":"Organization","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"name":"Mergify","description":"Pull requests automation service.","external_url":"https://mergify.com","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/mergify","created_at":"2018-03-30T10:19:51Z","updated_at":"2026-03-02T11:02:56Z","permissions":{"actions":"write","administration":"read","checks":"write","contents":"write","deployments":"write","emails":"read","issues":"write","members":"read","merge_queues":"read","metadata":"read","pages":"write","pull_requests":"write","statuses":"read","workflows":"write"},"events":["branch_protection_configuration","branch_protection_rule","check_run","check_suite","deployment_status","issue_comment","member","membership","merge_group","organization","pull_request","pull_request_review","pull_request_review_comment","pull_request_review_thread","push","repository","repository_ruleset","status","team","team_add","workflow_job","workflow_run"]}},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/issues/comments/3800289044","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/301#issuecomment-3800289044","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/issues/301","id":3800289044,"node_id":"IC_kwDOPaLyBs7ig88U","user":{"login":"KvizadSaderah","id":14391797,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE0MzkxNzk3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/14391797?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/KvizadSaderah","html_url":"https://github.com/KvizadSaderah","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KvizadSaderah/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KvizadSaderah/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KvizadSaderah/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KvizadSaderah/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KvizadSaderah/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KvizadSaderah/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KvizadSaderah/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KvizadSaderah/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KvizadSaderah/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-01-26T15:46:01Z","updated_at":"2026-01-26T15:46:01Z","body":"Hi @Bechma, the fuzzing is working and found an issue: `fuzz_odata_filter` triggers an OOM crash on inputs under 1KB. This appears to be a real bug in `parse_filter_string` (possibly exponential memory growth on certain patterns).\n\nHow would you like to proceed?\n1. Remove `fuzz_odata_filter` from this PR and file a separate issue for the bug\n2. Keep it and fix the parser first\n3. Other suggestion?\n\nThe other two targets (`fuzz_odata_cursor`, `fuzz_odata_orderby`) pass without issues.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/issues/comments/3800289044/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/issues/comments/3800598582","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/301#issuecomment-3800598582","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/issues/301","id":3800598582,"node_id":"IC_kwDOPaLyBs7iiIg2","user":{"login":"Bechma","id":19294519,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5Mjk0NTE5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19294519?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bechma","html_url":"https://github.com/Bechma","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bechma/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bechma/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bechma/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bechma/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bechma/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bechma/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bechma/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bechma/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bechma/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-01-26T16:49:08Z","updated_at":"2026-01-26T16:49:08Z","body":"> Hi @Bechma, the fuzzing is working and found an issue: `fuzz_odata_filter` triggers an OOM crash on inputs under 1KB. This appears to be a real bug in `parse_filter_string` (possibly exponential memory growth on certain patterns).\r\n> \r\n> How would you like to proceed?\r\n> \r\n> 1. Remove `fuzz_odata_filter` from this PR and file a separate issue for the bug\r\n> 2. Keep it and fix the parser first\r\n> 3. Other suggestion?\r\n> \r\n> The other two targets (`fuzz_odata_cursor`, `fuzz_odata_orderby`) pass without issues.\r\n\r\nI think the github worker ran out of memory, try to run it locally to see whether it crashes also in your local. If it does, try to increase the memory to 4GB, and if still does it... Let's see.\r\nOn a side note, remove the .gitkeep from the non-used folders","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/issues/comments/3800598582/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/issues/comments/3801581981","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/301#issuecomment-3801581981","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/issues/301","id":3801581981,"node_id":"IC_kwDOPaLyBs7il4md","user":{"login":"Artifizer","id":192502778,"node_id":"U_kgDOC3lb-g","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/192502778?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer","html_url":"https://github.com/Artifizer","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-01-26T20:20:40Z","updated_at":"2026-01-26T20:20:40Z","body":"> > Hi @Bechma, the fuzzing is working and found an issue: `fuzz_odata_filter` triggers an OOM crash on inputs under 1KB. This appears to be a real bug in `parse_filter_string` (possibly exponential memory growth on certain patterns).\r\n> > How would you like to proceed?\r\n> > \r\n> > 1. Remove `fuzz_odata_filter` from this PR and file a separate issue for the bug\r\n> > 2. Keep it and fix the parser first\r\n> > 3. Other suggestion?\r\n> > \r\n> > The other two targets (`fuzz_odata_cursor`, `fuzz_odata_orderby`) pass without issues.\r\n> \r\n> I think the github worker ran out of memory, try to run it locally to see whether it crashes also in your local. If it does, try to increase the memory to 4GB, and if still does it... Let's see. On a side note, remove the .gitkeep from the non-used folders\r\n\r\n@KvizadSaderah, can we check why so much memory is required in CI and try to minimize it?","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/issues/comments/3801581981/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/issues/comments/3804718858","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/301#issuecomment-3804718858","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/issues/301","id":3804718858,"node_id":"IC_kwDOPaLyBs7ix2cK","user":{"login":"KvizadSaderah","id":14391797,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE0MzkxNzk3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/14391797?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/KvizadSaderah","html_url":"https://github.com/KvizadSaderah","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KvizadSaderah/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KvizadSaderah/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KvizadSaderah/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KvizadSaderah/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KvizadSaderah/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KvizadSaderah/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KvizadSaderah/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KvizadSaderah/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KvizadSaderah/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-01-27T11:45:07Z","updated_at":"2026-01-27T11:45:07Z","body":"@Artifizer, I investigated the memory issue. Here's what I found:\n\n**Root cause:** The fuzzer discovered a bug in `parse_filter_string` — nested parentheses like `((((EAEAEAE(((EAEA((AE(((EAEAEEE` cause **exponential time complexity** (22+ seconds to process a single 32-byte input).\n\nThis is not a CI configuration issue — it's a real parser bug (catastrophic backtracking). The OOM happens because:\n1. Fuzzer finds such pathological inputs\n2. Parser hangs for 22+ seconds per input\n3. Memory accumulates during these hangs → OOM\n\n**Options:**\n1. Remove `fuzz_odata_filter` from this PR and file a separate issue for the parser bug\n2. Fix the parser first, then re-enable fuzzing\n\nThe other two targets (`fuzz_odata_cursor`, `fuzz_odata_orderby`) pass without issues.\n\nWhat would you prefer?","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/issues/comments/3804718858/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/issues/comments/3807795833","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/301#issuecomment-3807795833","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/issues/301","id":3807795833,"node_id":"IC_kwDOPaLyBs7i9lp5","user":{"login":"github-actions[bot]","id":41898282,"node_id":"MDM6Qm90NDE4OTgyODI=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/15368?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/github-actions","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-a