:"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/14391797?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/KvizadSaderah","html_url":"https://github.com/KvizadSaderah","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KvizadSaderah/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KvizadSaderah/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KvizadSaderah/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KvizadSaderah/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KvizadSaderah/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KvizadSaderah/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KvizadSaderah/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KvizadSaderah/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KvizadSaderah/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-01-28T10:01:17Z","updated_at":"2026-01-28T10:01:17Z","body":"Hi @Bechma,\n\nI ran the fuzzer locally as you suggested.\n\n**Findings:**\n- Input: `((((EAEAEAE(((EAEA((AE(((EAEAEEE` (32 bytes)\n- Processing time: **16 seconds**\n- Memory: up to **1.1 GB**\n\n**Root cause:** Exponential time complexity in `parse_filter_string` on nested parentheses. Even with 4GB it would eventually OOM with longer fuzzing runs.\n\n**Done:**\n- ✅ Removed `.gitkeep` from unused folders\n\n**Question:** How to proceed with `fuzz_odata_filter`?\n1. Remove it from this PR and create separate issue for the parser bug\n2. Other suggestion?\n\n`fuzz_odata_cursor` and `fuzz_odata_orderby` work fine.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/issues/comments/3810252979/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/issues/comments/3812696395","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/301#issuecomment-3812696395","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/issues/301","id":3812696395,"node_id":"IC_kwDOPaLyBs7jQSFL","user":{"login":"MikeFalcon77","id":3686170,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM2ODYxNzA=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3686170?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/MikeFalcon77","html_url":"https://github.com/MikeFalcon77","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MikeFalcon77/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MikeFalcon77/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MikeFalcon77/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MikeFalcon77/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MikeFalcon77/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MikeFalcon77/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MikeFalcon77/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MikeFalcon77/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MikeFalcon77/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-01-28T17:19:39Z","updated_at":"2026-01-28T17:19:39Z","body":"> @Artifizer, I investigated the memory issue. Here's what I found:\r\n> \r\n> **Root cause:** The fuzzer discovered a bug in `parse_filter_string` — nested parentheses like `((((EAEAEAE(((EAEA((AE(((EAEAEEE` cause **exponential time complexity** (22+ seconds to process a single 32-byte input).\r\n> \r\n> This is not a CI configuration issue — it's a real parser bug (catastrophic backtracking). The OOM happens because:\r\n> \r\n> 1. Fuzzer finds such pathological inputs\r\n> 2. Parser hangs for 22+ seconds per input\r\n> 3. Memory accumulates during these hangs → OOM\r\n> \r\n> **Options:**\r\n> \r\n> 1. Remove `fuzz_odata_filter` from this PR and file a separate issue for the parser bug\r\n> 2. Fix the parser first, then re-enable fuzzing\r\n> \r\n> The other two targets (`fuzz_odata_cursor`, `fuzz_odata_orderby`) pass without issues.\r\n> \r\n> What would you prefer?\r\n\r\nIt's good catch","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/issues/comments/3812696395/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null}],"source_review_comments":[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2720993460","pull_request_review_id":3697252215,"id":2720993460,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs6iLxC0","diff_hunk":"@@ -335,5 +385,5 @@ build:\n \tcargo +stable build --release\n \n # Run all necessary quality checks and tests and then build the release binary\n-all: build check test-sqlite e2e-local\n+all: build check test-sqlite e2e-local fuzz","path":"Makefile","commit_id":"cee3e428503fbbe141f4486655e121cfff0ebb53","original_commit_id":"99828b719472e23ec408b20448f5cf8bef29b404","user":{"login":"graphite-app[bot]","id":96075541,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOBbn_FQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/158384?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/graphite-app%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/graphite-app","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/graphite-app%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/graphite-app%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/graphite-app%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/graphite-app%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/graphite-app%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/graphite-app%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/graphite-app%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/graphite-app%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/graphite-app%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Adding `fuzz` to the `all` target will cause every `make all` invocation to run fuzzing for 30 seconds on each of the 8 targets (total ~4 minutes). This significantly slows down local development workflows where `all` is typically used for standard build/test cycles.\n\nFuzzing is resource-intensive and should be opt-in rather than part of the default pipeline. Consider removing `fuzz` from the `all` target:\n\n```makefile\nall: build check test-sqlite e2e-local\n```\n\nDevelopers can explicitly run `make fuzz` when needed, and CI will handle continuous fuzzing via the GitHub Actions workflow.\n```suggestion\nall: build check test-sqlite e2e-local\n```\n  \n\n*Spotted by [Graphite Agent](https://app.graphite.com/diamond/?org=hypernetix&ref=ai-review-comment)*<i class='graphite__hidden'><br /><br /><a href=\"https://app.graphite.com/github/pr/hypernetix/hyperspot/301?chatWithGeneratedComment=edd1dd55-2e5d-4e28-99c0-8b61c9db402b\"><picture><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\" srcset=\"https://static.graphite.dev/github-diamond-fix-in-graphite-dark.svg\"><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\" srcset=\"https://static.graphite.dev/github-diamond-fix-in-graphite-light.svg\"><img alt=\"Fix in Graphite\" src=\"https://static.graphite.dev/github-diamond-fix-in-graphite-dark.svg\"></picture></a></i><i class='graphite__hidden'><br /><br />Is this helpful? React 👍 or 👎 to let us know.</i>","created_at":"2026-01-23T12:23:54Z","updated_at":"2026-01-23T12:23:56Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/301#discussion_r2720993460","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/301","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2720993460"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/301#discussion_r2720993460"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/301"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2720993460/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":null,"original_line":388,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","original_position":62,"position":1,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2721003912","pull_request_review_id":3697263519,"id":2721003912,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs6iLzmI","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,5 @@\n+target/\n+artifacts/\n+corpus/*/\n+!corpus/*/.gitkeep\n+Cargo.lock","path":"fuzz/.gitignore","commit_id":"99828b719472e23ec408b20448f5cf8bef29b404","original_commit_id":"99828b719472e23ec408b20448f5cf8bef29b404","user":{"login":"coderabbitai[bot]","id":136622811,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOCCSy2w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/347564?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/coderabbitai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"_⚠️ Potential issue_ | _🟡 Minor_\n\n**`Cargo.lock` should be tracked, not ignored.**\n\nThis line ignores `Cargo.lock`, but for binary/application crates (which fuzz targets are), `Cargo.lock` should be committed to ensure reproducible builds. This is especially important for fuzzing to reproduce crashes reliably.\n\n\n<details>\n<summary>Proposed fix</summary>\n\nEither remove this line entirely, or if other gitignore rules higher up ignore it, negate it:\n\n```diff\n-Cargo.lock\n+!Cargo.lock\n```\n</details>\n\n<!-- suggestion_start -->\n\n<details>\n<summary>📝 Committable suggestion</summary>\n\n> ‼️ **IMPORTANT**\n> Carefully review the code before committing. Ensure that it accurately replaces the highlighted code, contains no missing lines, and has no issues with indentation. Thoroughly test & benchmark the code to ensure it meets the requirements.\n\n```suggestion\n!Cargo.lock\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- suggestion_end -->\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nIn `@fuzz/.gitignore` at line 5, Remove the rule that ignores Cargo.lock from the\nfuzz .gitignore: either delete the \"Cargo.lock\" entry or negate it so Cargo.lock\nis tracked (e.g., remove the line containing Cargo.lock or add a negation to\nensure Cargo.lock is committed) to ensure reproducible builds for the fuzz\ntargets; update the .gitignore entry referencing \"Cargo.lock\" and then commit\nthe tracked Cargo.lock file.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- fingerprinting:phantom:poseidon:ocelot -->\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment by CodeRabbit -->","created_at":"2026-01-23T12:27:25Z","updated_at":"2026-01-23T12:27:26Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/301#discussion_r2721003912","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/301","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2721003912"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/