ted:\n\n```shell\n# Search for all FileParserBackend implementations\nrg \"impl FileParserBackend\" --type rust -A 2\n```\n\nRepository: hypernetix/hyperspot\n\nLength of output: 1567\n\n---\n\n🏁 Script executed:\n\n```shell\n# Check the root workspace Cargo.toml for tl dependency\ncat Cargo.toml | head -200\n```\n\nRepository: hypernetix/hyperspot\n\nLength of output: 6214\n\n---\n\n🏁 Script executed:\n\n```shell\n# Look specifically in fuzz directory for any Cargo configuration\nls -la fuzz/\n```\n\nRepository: hypernetix/hyperspot\n\nLength of output: 422\n\n---\n\n🏁 Script executed:\n\n```shell\n# Check fuzz Cargo.toml completely\ncat -n fuzz/Cargo.toml\n```\n\nRepository: hypernetix/hyperspot\n\nLength of output: 1887\n\n---\n\n🏁 Script executed:\n\n```shell\n# Search for tl crate in all Cargo.toml files\nrg \"^\\[.*tl\" fuzz/ -A 5\n```\n\nRepository: hypernetix/hyperspot\n\nLength of output: 46\n\n---\n\n🏁 Script executed:\n\n```shell\n# Look for tl crate dependency definition anywhere\nrg '\"tl\"' --type toml\n```\n\nRepository: hypernetix/hyperspot\n\nLength of output: 104\n\n---\n\n🏁 Script executed:\n\n```shell\n# Let me check what tl crate is by searching online documentation or checking if it's a path dependency\nrg \"tl.*=\" fuzz/ --type toml -A 2 -B 2\n```\n\nRepository: hypernetix/hyperspot\n\nLength of output: 207\n\n---\n\n🏁 Script executed:\n\n```shell\n# Check git dependencies or path dependencies in fuzz/Cargo.toml\ncat fuzz/Cargo.toml | grep -E \"path|git|version\"\n```\n\nRepository: hypernetix/hyperspot\n\nLength of output: 645\n\n---\n\n🏁 Script executed:\n\n```shell\n# Now let's look at what tl crate is - check Cargo.lock for the crate info\nrg -A 10 'name = \"tl\"' Cargo.lock | head -20\n```\n\nRepository: hypernetix/hyperspot\n\nLength of output: 443\n\n---\n\n🏁 Script executed:\n\n```shell\n# Let's also check the fuzz_html_parser to understand the pattern\ncat -n fuzz/fuzz_targets/fuzz_html_parser.rs\n```\n\nRepository: hypernetix/hyperspot\n\nLength of output: 364\n\n---\n\n🏁 Script executed:\n\n```shell\n# And check if there's a separate markdown parser fuzz target that should exist\nls -la fuzz/fuzz_targets/\n```\n\nRepository: hypernetix/hyperspot\n\nLength of output: 724\n\n---\n\n🏁 Script executed:\n\n```shell\n# Search for what markdown parsing should actually use in production\nrg \"markdown|Markdown\" modules/file_parser/src --type rust -B 2 -A 2 | head -60\n```\n\nRepository: hypernetix/hyperspot\n\nLength of output: 3637\n\n---\n\n🏁 Script executed:\n\n```shell\n# Check if markdown is in any supported extensions\nrg \"supported_extensions\" modules/file_parser/src/infra/parsers --type rust -A 2\n```\n\nRepository: hypernetix/hyperspot\n\nLength of output: 1608\n\n---\n\n🏁 Script executed:\n\n```shell\n# Check the service to see what file types are registered\ncat -n modules/file_parser/src/domain/service.rs | grep -A 50 \"fn new\"\n```\n\nRepository: hypernetix/hyperspot\n\nLength of output: 2149\n\n---\n\n🏁 Script executed:\n\n```shell\n# Look at PlainTextParser implementation\ncat -n modules/file_parser/src/infra/parsers/plain_text.rs\n```\n\nRepository: hypernetix/hyperspot\n\nLength of output: 3399\n\n---\n\n\n\n</details>\n\n**Fix fuzz_markdown_parser to test the actual production parsing path.**\n\nThe fuzz target currently uses `tl::parse` (an HTML parser) to test markdown, but production parses markdown files using `PlainTextParser`, which treats them as plain text. Replace the `tl::parse` call with `file_parser::PlainTextParser` to match the production code path, or clarify the harness intent.\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nIn `@fuzz/fuzz_targets/fuzz_markdown_parser.rs` around lines 6 - 10, The fuzz\ntarget is invoking the HTML parser (tl::parse) instead of the production\nplaintext path; update the closure used by fuzz_target to instantiate and invoke\nfile_parser::PlainTextParser on the UTF-8 input (matching the production parsing\nflow) instead of calling tl::parse and remove/replace any tl::ParserOptions\nusage; locate the fuzz_target closure and the call site that currently\nreferences tl::parse and switch it to the PlainTextParser constructor and its\nparse method so the harness exercises the same code path as production.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- fingerprinting:phantom:poseidon:eagle -->\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment by CodeRabbit -->","created_at":"2026-01-23T12:27:25Z","updated_at":"2026-01-23T12:27:26Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/301#discussion_r2721003923","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/301","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2721003923"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/301#discussion_r2721003923"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/301"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2721003923/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":6,"start_side":"RIGHT","line":null,"original_line":10,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","original_position":10,"position":1,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2721099649","pull_request_review_id":3697364498,"id":2721099649,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs6iMK-B","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,58 @@\n+name: ClusterFuzzLite PR Fuzzing\n+\n+on:\n+  pull_request:\n+    branches: [ main, develop ]\n+    paths-ignore:\n+      - '**/*.md'\n+      - 'docs/**'\n+  workflow_dispatch:\n+\n+permissions:\n+  contents: read\n+  security-events: write\n+\n+concurrency:\n+  group: ${{ github.workflow }}-${{ matrix.sanitizer }}-${{ github.ref }}\n+  cancel-in-progress: true","path":".github/workflows/clusterfuzzlite.yml","commit_id":"a2d6e1f2bb744176c3d7eb0f085c217e647bdba4","original_commit_id":"a2d6e1f2bb744176c3d7eb0f085c217e647bdba4","user":{"login":"coderabbitai[bot]","id":136622811,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOCCSy2w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/347564?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/coderabbitai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"_⚠️ Potential issue_ | _🟠 Major_\n\n<details>\n<summary>🧩 Analysis chain</summary>\n\n🏁 Script executed:\n\n```shell\ncd /tmp && find . -name \"clusterfuzzlite.yml\" -o -name \"*.yml\" | head -20\n```\n\nRepository: hypernetix/hyperspot\n\nLength of output: 46\n\n---\n\n🏁 Script executed:\n\n```shell\ngit ls-files | grep -i \"clusterfuzzlite.yml\"\n```\n\nRepository: hypernetix/hyperspot\n\nLength of output: 101\n\n---\n\n🏁 Script executed:\n\n```shell\nfind . -type f -name \"clusterfuzzlite.yml\" 2>/dev/null\n```\n\nRepository: hypernetix/hyperspot\n\nLength of output: 103\n\n---\n\n🏁 Script executed:\n\n```shell\ncat .github/workflows/clusterfuzzlite.yml | head -50\n```\n\nRepository: hypernetix/hyperspot\n\nLength of output: 1228\n\n---\n\n🌐 Web query:\n\n`GitHub Actions concurrency context matrix available at workflow level`\n\n💡 Result:\n\nNo—`matrix` is **not available** in the **workflow-level** `concurrency` key.\n\nAt the workflow level, `concurrency` expressions can only use these contexts: **`github`, `inputs`, `vars`**. ([docs.github.com](https://docs.github.com/en/actions/learn-github-actions/contexts?utm_source=openai))\n\nIf you need matrix-specific concurrency (e.g., one lock per `matrix.os`), you must set **job-level** concurrency (`jobs.<job_id>.concurrency`), where **`matrix` is allowed**. ([docs.github.com](https://docs.github.com/en/actions/learn-github-actions/contexts?utm_source=openai))\n\nCitations:\n\n- 1: https://docs.github.com/en/actions/learn-github-actions/contexts?utm_source=openai\n- 2: https://docs.github.com/en/actions/learn-github-actions/contexts?utm_source=openai\n\n---\n\n🌐 Web query:\n\n`GitHub Actions concurrency group scope context availability job vs workflow`\n\n💡 Result:\n\n- **Scope of a concurrency group:** A `concurrency.group` name is effectively **repository-scoped**—i.e., any **workflow runs and/or jobs in the same repository** that resolve to the same group string will contend with each other (can queue/cancel each other), even if they’re in different workflows. To avoid cross-workflow interference, include something like `${{ github.workflow }}` in the group name. [1] [2] [3]\n\n- **Workflow-level vs job-level concurrency (what gets “locked”):**\n  - **Workflow-level `concurrency`:** limits **entire workflow runs** (the whole run is the unit being serialized/canceled). [1] [2]\n  - **Job-level `jobs.<job_id>.concurrency`:** limits **that specific job** (across runs, and potentially across workflows if the group matches). Other jobs in the same workflow can still run concurrently unless they also have concurrency set. [2] [3]\n\n- **Context availability in `group` expressions (what you can reference):**\n  - **Workflow-level `concurrency`:** only `github`, `inputs`, `vars`. [4]\n  - **Job-level `jobs.<job_id>.concurrency`:** `github`, `needs`, `strategy`, `matrix`, `inputs`, `vars`. [3] [4]\n\n- **Behavior details (applies to both levels):** At most **one running and one pending** item per group; when a new one is queued, any existing **pending** in the same group is canceled, and with `cancel-in-progress: true` you can also cancel what’s currently running. [2] [3]\n\n**Sources:**  \n[1] GitHub Docs — Workflow syntax (`concurrency` examples incl. `github.workflow`) https://docs.github.com/en/actions/writing-workflows/workflow-syntax-for-github-actions  \n[2] GitHub Docs — Workflow concurrency how-to https://docs.github.com/en/actions/how-tos/write-workflows/choose-when-workflows-run/control-workflow-concurrency  \n[3] GitHub Docs — Workflow syntax (`jobs.<job_id>.concurrency`, allowed contexts) https://docs.github.com/en/actions/reference/workflow-syntax-for-github-actions  \n[4] GitHub Docs — Context availability table (workflow `concurrency` vs job concurrency) https://docs.github.com/en/actions/learn-github-actions/contexts\n\n---\n\n\n\n</details>\n\n**Fix concurrency context: `matrix` isn't available at workflow scope.**\n\nThe workflow defines `concurrency` at the top level with `${{ matrix.sanitizer }}`, but `matrix` context is only available at job scope. This will fail to resolve. Move `concurrency` under the job or remove `matrix` from the group.\n\n<details>\n<summary>🔧 Proposed fix (move concurrency to the job)</summary>\n\n```diff\n-concurrency:\n-  group: ${{ github.workflow }}-${{ matrix.sanitizer }}-${{ github.ref }}\n-  cancel-in-progress: true\n-\n jobs:\n   PR:\n+    concurrency:\n+      group: ${{ github.workflow }}-${{ matrix.sanitizer }}-${{ github.ref }}\n+      cancel-in-progress: true\n     runs-on: ubuntu-latest\n```\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>🧰 Tools</summary>\n\n<details>\n<summary>🪛 actionlint (1.7.10)</summary>\n\n16-16: context \"matrix\" is not allowed here. available contexts are \"github\", \"inputs\", \"vars\". see https://docs.github.com/en/actions/learn-github-actions/contexts#context-availability for more details\n\n(expression)\n\n---\n\n16-16: property \"sanitizer\" is not defined in object type {}\n\n(expression)\n\n</details>\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nIn @.github/workflows/clusterfuzzlite.yml around lines 15 - 17, The top-level\nconcurrency block uses `${{ matrix.sanitizer }}` which is invalid because the\nmatrix context is only available at the job scope; update the workflow by moving\nthe concurrency block into the job that uses `matrix` (e.g., under the job that\nreferences `matrix.sanitizer`) or remove `matrix.sanitizer` from the `group`\nvalue and use only available contexts like `${{ github.workflow }}-${{\ngithub.ref }}`; adjust the `concurrency` key (and its\n`group`/`cancel-in-progress`) accordingly so it lives where `matrix` is defined\nor no longer references `matrix.sanitizer`.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- fingerprinting:phantom:poseidon:eagle -->\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment by CodeRabbit -->\n\n✅ Addressed in commit c19efb1","created_at":"2026-01-23T12:58:23Z","updated_at":"2026-01-23T13:01:23Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/301#discussion_r2721099649","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/301","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2721099649"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/301#discussion_r2721099649"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/301"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2721099649/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":15,"start_side":"RIGHT","line":null,"original_line":17,"side":"RIGHT","author_assoc