gestion\ncorpus/**\n!corpus/**/\n!corpus/**/.gitkeep\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- suggestion_end -->\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nIn `@fuzz/.gitignore` around lines 3 - 4, The .gitignore currently uses the\npattern \"corpus/*/\" which ignores the corpus subdirectories themselves and\nprevents the negation \"!corpus/*/.gitkeep\" from re-including placeholder files;\nupdate the ignore patterns so directories are not implicitly excluded—for\nexample replace the directory-only pattern with a recursive pattern like\n\"corpus/**\" (or change the negation to \"!corpus/**/.gitkeep\") so that .gitkeep\nfiles inside corpus subfolders remain tracked; modify the patterns referencing\n\"corpus/*/\" and \"!corpus/*/.gitkeep\" accordingly.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- fingerprinting:phantom:poseidon:eagle -->\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment by CodeRabbit -->\n\n✅ Addressed in commit 640687a","created_at":"2026-01-23T13:07:33Z","updated_at":"2026-01-23T14:54:40Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/301#discussion_r2721127897","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/301","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2721127897"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/301#discussion_r2721127897"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/301"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2721127897/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":3,"start_side":"RIGHT","line":null,"original_line":4,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","original_position":4,"position":1,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2721127901","pull_request_review_id":3697395667,"id":2721127901,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs6iMR3d","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,70 @@\n+[package]\n+name = \"hyperspot-fuzz\"\n+version = \"0.0.0\"\n+publish = false\n+edition = \"2021\"\n+\n+[package.metadata]\n+cargo-fuzz = true","path":"fuzz/Cargo.toml","commit_id":"9ef0561564fdd44fddb3844c7c2f21201ac52940","original_commit_id":"c19efb130a70a7c1b79e931123b402a7c70bf05c","user":{"login":"coderabbitai[bot]","id":136622811,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOCCSy2w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/347564?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/coderabbitai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"_⚠️ Potential issue_ | _🟡 Minor_\n\n<details>\n<summary>🧩 Analysis chain</summary>\n\n🏁 Script executed:\n\n```shell\n# Check fuzz/Cargo.toml edition\necho \"=== fuzz/Cargo.toml ===\"\nhead -10 fuzz/Cargo.toml\n\n# Check root Cargo.toml edition\necho \"=== Root Cargo.toml ===\"\nhead -10 Cargo.toml\n```\n\nRepository: hypernetix/hyperspot\n\nLength of output: 487\n\n---\n\n🌐 Web query:\n\n`cargo-fuzz Rust edition 2024 compatibility requirements`\n\n💡 Result:\n\n**cargo-fuzz + Rust “edition = 2024” compatibility (practical requirements)**\n\n- **Rust toolchain must support the 2024 edition:** Rust **1.85.0** is the stable release that **stabilized Rust 2024** (Feb 20, 2025). So you need **rustc ≥ 1.85** (stable/beta/nightly) to compile crates set to `edition = \"2024\"`. [1]\n- **cargo-fuzz generally requires a nightly toolchain (still true in current docs):** cargo-fuzz uses unstable `-Z` flags for sanitizer integration, so you typically run it with **`cargo +nightly fuzz ...`** / install nightly via rustup. [2]\n- **Platform/LLVM requirements come from libFuzzer + sanitizers:**\n  - libFuzzer needs **LLVM sanitizer support** and a **C++11 compiler**. [2]\n  - The Rust Fuzz Book notes this works on **x86_64 Linux**, **x86_64 macOS**, **Apple-silicon macOS**, and **Windows (MSVC ASan)**. [2]\n  - (Note: the cargo-fuzz README still claims “Unix-like only (not Windows)”, so for Windows you should follow the Book and expect some toolchain/ASan caveats.) [3][2]\n\n**Bottom line:** if your project is `edition = \"2024\"`, use a **recent nightly (≥ 1.85-era or newer)** and cargo-fuzz should work without any special “edition 2024” knobs beyond that. [1][2]\n\n**Sources:** [1] Rust 1.85.0 announcement (stabilizes Rust 2024) • [2] Rust Fuzz Book “Setup / Requirements” • [3] cargo-fuzz README (nightly + platform note)\n\n---\n\n\n\n</details>\n\n**Update fuzz/Cargo.toml to use `edition = \"2024\"` to match the root workspace.**\n\nThe fuzz workspace currently uses `edition = \"2021\"` while the root workspace specifies `edition = \"2024\"`. cargo-fuzz has no compatibility issues with edition 2024, and the project's minimum rust-version (1.92.0) well exceeds the version that stabilized edition 2024 (1.85.0). Align the fuzz workspace with the root workspace edition for consistency.\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nIn `@fuzz/Cargo.toml` around lines 1 - 8, Update the fuzz workspace Cargo.toml to\nmatch the root workspace edition by changing the package edition field in the\n[package] section (edition = \"2021\") to edition = \"2024\"; edit the edition key\nin the fuzz/Cargo.toml so the package's edition aligns with the root workspace.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- fingerprinting:phantom:medusa:ocelot -->\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment by CodeRabbit -->\n\n✅ Addressed in commit 9c15c15","created_at":"2026-01-23T13:07:33Z","updated_at":"2026-01-23T15:54:06Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/301#discussion_r2721127901","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/301","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2721127901"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/301#discussion_r2721127901"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/301"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2721127901/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":1,"original_start_line":1,"start_side":"RIGHT","line":8,"original_line":8,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","original_position":8,"position":8,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2722106870","pull_request_review_id":3698632307,"id":2722106870,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs6iQA32","diff_hunk":"@@ -307,6 +307,56 @@ coverage-e2e-local: check-prereq-e2e-local\n \t@command -v cargo-llvm-cov >/dev/null || (echo \"Installing cargo-llvm-cov...\" && cargo install cargo-llvm-cov)\n \tpython3 scripts/coverage.py e2e-local\n \n+# -------- Fuzzing --------\n+\n+.PHONY: fuzz fuzz-build fuzz-list fuzz-run fuzz-clean fuzz-corpus\n+\n+## Install cargo-fuzz (required for fuzzing)\n+fuzz-install:\n+\t@command -v cargo-fuzz >/dev/null || \\\n+\t\t(echo \"Installing cargo-fuzz...\" && cargo install cargo-fuzz)\n+\n+## Build all fuzz targets\n+fuzz-build: fuzz-install\n+\tcd fuzz && cargo +nightly fuzz build\n+\n+## List all available fuzz targets\n+fuzz-list: fuzz-install\n+\tcd fuzz && cargo +nightly fuzz list\n+\n+## Run a specific fuzz target (use FUZZ_TARGET=name)\n+## Example: make fuzz-run FUZZ_TARGET=fuzz_odata_filter FUZZ_SECONDS=60\n+fuzz-run: fuzz-install\n+\t@if [ -z \"$(FUZZ_TARGET)\" ]; then \\\n+\t\techo \"ERROR: FUZZ_TARGET is required. Example: make fuzz-run FUZZ_TARGET=fuzz_odata_filter\"; \\\n+\t\texit 1; \\\n+\tfi\n+\tcd fuzz && cargo +nightly fuzz run $(FUZZ_TARGET) -- -max_total_time=$(or $(FUZZ_SECONDS),60)\n+\n+## Run all fuzz targets for a short time (smoke test)\n+fuzz: fuzz-build\n+\t@echo \"Running all fuzz targets for 30 seconds each...\"\n+\t@cd fuzz && \\\n+\tfor target in $$(cargo +nightly fuzz list); do \\\n+\t\techo \"=== Fuzzing $$target ===\"; \\\n+\t\tcargo +nightly fuzz run $$target -- -max_total_time=30 || true; \\\n+\tdone\n+\t@echo \"Fuzzing complete. Check fuzz/artifacts/ for crashes.\"","path":"Makefile","commit_id":"cee3e428503fbbe141f4486655e121cfff0ebb53","original_commit_id":"cee3e428503fbbe141f4486655e121cfff0ebb53","user":{"login":"coderabbitai[bot]","id":136622811,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOCCSy2w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/347564?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/coderabbitai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"_⚠️ Potential issue_ | _🟠 Major_\n\n**Smoke test silently ignores crashes due to `|| true`.**\n\nThe `|| true` on line 342 causes the fuzz target to succeed even when crashes are found. This defeats the purpose of a smoke test since failures are silently ignored and `make fuzz` will always report success.\n\n\n\n<details>\n<summary>Suggested fix to fail on any crash</summary>\n\n```diff\n fuzz: fuzz-build\n \t`@echo` \"Running all fuzz targets for 30 seconds each...\"\n \t`@cd` fuzz && \\\n+\tFAILED=0; \\\n \tfor target in $$(cargo +nightly fuzz list); do \\\n \t\techo \"=== Fuzzing $$target ===\"; \\\n-\t\tcargo +nightly fuzz run $$target -- -max_total_time=30 || true; \\\n+\t\tcargo +nightly fuzz run $$target -- -max_total_time=30 || FAILED=1; \\\n+\tdone; \\\n+\tif [ $$FAILED -ne 0 ]; then \\\n+\t\techo \"Fuzzing found crashes. Check fuzz/artifacts/ for details.\"; \\\n+\t\texit 1; \\\n+\tfi\n-\tdone\n \t`@echo` \"Fuzzing complete. Check fuzz/artifacts/ for crashes.\"\n```\n</details>\n\n<!-- suggestion_start -->\n\n<details>\n<summary>📝 Committable suggestion</summary>\n\n> ‼️ **IMPORTANT**\n> Carefully review the code before committing. Ensure that it accurately replaces the highlighted code, contains no missing lines, and has no issues with indentation. Thoroughly test & benchmark the code to ensure it meets the requirements.\n\n```suggestion\nfuzz: fuzz-build\n\t`@echo` \"Running all fuzz targets for 30 seconds each...\"\n\t`@cd` fuzz && \\\n\tFAILED=0; \\\n\tfor target in $$(cargo +nightly fuzz list); do \\\n\t\techo \"=== Fuzzing $$target ===\"; \\\n\t\tcargo +nightly fuzz run $$target -- -max_total_time=30 || FAILED=1; \\\n\tdone; \\\n\tif [ $$FAILED -ne 0 ]; then \\\n\t\techo \"Fuzzing found crashes. Check fuzz/artifacts/ for details.\"; \\\n\t\texit 1; \\\n\tfi\n\t`@echo` \"Fuzzing complete. Check fuzz/artifacts/ for crashes.\"\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- suggestion_end -->\n\n<details>\n<summary>🧰 Tools</summary>\n\n<details>\n<summary>🪛 checkmake (0.2.2)</summary>\n\n[warning] 337-337: Target body for \"fuzz\" exceeds allowed length of 5 (7).\n\n(maxbodylength)\n\n</details>\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nIn `@Makefile` around lines 337 - 344, The fuzz Makefile rule currently masks\ncrashes because the loop runs each cargo +nightly fuzz run $$target with \"||\ntrue\", making the recipe always succeed; update the fuzz target loop in the\nMakefile (the fuzz: fuzz-build recipe) to remove \"|| true\" and instead propagate\nany non-zero exit code (e.g., run cargo +nightly fuzz run $$target --\n-max_total_time=30 and if it fails immediately exit with that status or set -e\nso the recipe fails on first crash), ensuring the make target fails when any\nfuzz target crashes and surfaces the error.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- fingerprinting:phantom:poseidon:ocelot -->\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment by CodeRabbit -->\n\n✅ Addressed in commit 1ac3081","created_at":"2026-01-23T17:05:20Z","updated_at":"2026-01-23T17:32:42Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/301#discussion_r2722106870","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/301","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2722106870"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/301#discussion_r2722106870"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/301"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2722106870/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_sta