scripts/ci.py\n```\n\nRepository: hypernetix/hyperspot\n\nLength of output: 2819\n\n---\n\n🏁 Script executed:\n\n```shell\n# Also check if there are any nightly preflight checks added anywhere else in those functions\nsed -n '509,650p' scripts/ci.py | grep -E \"def cmd_fuzz|rustup|nightly|ensure\"\n```\n\nRepository: hypernetix/hyperspot\n\nLength of output: 706\n\n---\n\n\n\n</details>\n\n**Add explicit nightly toolchain preflight check before cargo-fuzz operations.**\n\nThe current check for `cargo +nightly fuzz --version` conflates two distinct issues: missing nightly toolchain and missing cargo-fuzz. When nightly is absent, the command fails silently and the code attempts to install cargo-fuzz, which either fails or succeeds but doesn't resolve the actual problem. A dedicated nightly check provides clearer guidance and prevents the confusing install attempt.\n\n<details>\n<summary>🛠️ Suggested preflight helper</summary>\n\n```diff\n def ensure_tool(binary, install_hint=None):\n     result = run_cmd_allow_fail([binary, \"--version\"])\n     if result.returncode != 0:\n         msg = f\"{binary} is not installed\"\n         if install_hint:\n             msg += f\". Install with: {install_hint}\"\n         print(msg)\n         sys.exit(1)\n\n+def ensure_nightly_toolchain():\n+    ensure_tool(\"rustup\", \"https://rustup.rs\")\n+    result = run_cmd_allow_fail([\"rustup\", \"run\", \"nightly\", \"rustc\", \"--version\"])\n+    if result.returncode != 0:\n+        print(\n+            \"ERROR: Rust nightly toolchain not installed. \"\n+            \"Install with: rustup toolchain install nightly\"\n+        )\n+        sys.exit(1)\n\n def cmd_fuzz_build(_args):\n     step(\"Building fuzz targets\")\n+    ensure_nightly_toolchain()\n     fuzz_dir = os.path.join(PROJECT_ROOT, \"fuzz\")\n\n def cmd_fuzz_list(_args):\n     step(\"Listing fuzz targets\")\n+    ensure_nightly_toolchain()\n     fuzz_dir = os.path.join(PROJECT_ROOT, \"fuzz\")\n\n def cmd_fuzz_run(args):\n     step(f\"Running fuzz target: {args.target}\")\n+    ensure_nightly_toolchain()\n     fuzz_dir = os.path.join(PROJECT_ROOT, \"fuzz\")\n```\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nIn `@scripts/ci.py` around lines 509 - 520, The cmd_fuzz_build flow currently\nconflates missing nightly toolchain and missing cargo-fuzz; add an explicit\nnightly preflight: use run_cmd_allow_fail to run a rustup toolchain query (e.g.,\n[\"rustup\", \"toolchain\", \"list\"] or [\"rustup\", \"show\", \"active-toolchain\"]) and\ncheck the output for \"nightly\" before attempting any cargo +nightly commands in\ncmd_fuzz_build; if nightly is not present, print a clear instruction to install\nit (e.g., \"rustup toolchain install nightly\") and exit/abort the build step so\nwe don't try to install cargo-fuzz against the wrong toolchain; only after\nconfirming nightly exists, perform the existing cargo-fuzz --version check\n(using run_cmd_allow_fail) and install cargo-fuzz with run_cmd([\"cargo\",\n\"install\", \"cargo-fuzz\"]) if missing, then run the build in fuzz_dir.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- fingerprinting:phantom:poseidon:eagle -->\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment by CodeRabbit -->\n\n✅ Addressed in commit eac0659","created_at":"2026-01-26T12:24:41Z","updated_at":"2026-01-26T15:28:07Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/301#discussion_r2727407965","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/301","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2727407965"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/301#discussion_r2727407965"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/301"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2727407965/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocke