 section is numbered \"2.4\" (line 100), but the existing \"Sign Your Commits (DCO)\" section is also numbered \"2.4\" (line 137). One of these should be renumbered to maintain proper document structure.\n> \n> \n> <details>\n> <summary>Suggested fix</summary>\n> \n> Renumber the sections starting from the new fuzzing section:\n> - Line 100: `### 2.4. Run Fuzzing Tests (Recommended)` (keep as-is)\n> - Line 137: `### 2.5. Sign Your Commits (DCO)` (was 2.4)\n> - Line 157: `### 2.6. Commit Changes` (was 2.5)\n> - Line 215: `### 2.7. Push and Create PR` (was 2.6)\n> - Line 261: `### 2.8 Review Process` (was 2.7)\n> \n> </details>\n> \n> </blockquote></details>\n> \n> </blockquote></details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Fix all issues with AI agents</summary>\n\n```\nIn `@fuzz/.gitignore`:\n- Line 5: Remove the rule that ignores Cargo.lock from the fuzz .gitignore:\neither delete the \"Cargo.lock\" entry or negate it so Cargo.lock is tracked\n(e.g., remove the line containing Cargo.lock or add a negation to ensure\nCargo.lock is committed) to ensure reproducible builds for the fuzz targets;\nupdate the .gitignore entry referencing \"Cargo.lock\" and then commit the tracked\nCargo.lock file.\n\nIn `@fuzz/fuzz_targets/fuzz_markdown_parser.rs`:\n- Around line 6-10: The fuzz target is invoking the HTML parser (tl::parse)\ninstead of the production plaintext path; update the closure used by fuzz_target\nto instantiate and invoke file_parser::PlainTextParser on the UTF-8 input\n(matching the production parsing flow) instead of calling tl::parse and\nremove/replace any tl::ParserOptions usage; locate the fuzz_target closure and\nthe call site that currently references tl::parse and switch it to the\nPlainTextParser constructor and its parse method so the harness exercises the\nsame code path as production.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>🧹 Nitpick comments (4)</summary><blockquote>\n\n<details>\n<summary>scripts/ci.py (2)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`524-527`: **Add cargo-fuzz installation check for consistency.**\n\n`cmd_fuzz_list` doesn't verify `cargo-fuzz` is installed, unlike `cmd_fuzz_build` and `cmd_fuzz_run`. If a user runs `fuzz-list` first, they'll get a confusing error.\n\n\n<details>\n<summary>Suggested fix</summary>\n\n```diff\n def cmd_fuzz_list(_args):\n     step(\"Listing fuzz targets\")\n     fuzz_dir = os.path.join(PROJECT_ROOT, \"fuzz\")\n+\n+    # Check if cargo-fuzz is installed\n+    result = run_cmd_allow_fail([\"cargo\", \"+nightly\", \"fuzz\", \"--version\"])\n+    if result.returncode != 0:\n+        print(\"Installing cargo-fuzz...\")\n+        run_cmd([\"cargo\", \"install\", \"cargo-fuzz\"])\n+\n     run_cmd([\"cargo\", \"+nightly\", \"fuzz\", \"list\"], cwd=fuzz_dir)\n```\n\n</details>\n\n---\n\n`367-367`: **Consider using list unpacking for clarity.**\n\nPer Ruff RUF005, list unpacking is more idiomatic than concatenation.\n\n\n<details>\n<summary>Suggested fix</summary>\n\n```diff\n-    pytest_cmd = pytest_base_cmd + [\"testing/e2e\", \"-vv\"]\n+    pytest_cmd = [*pytest_base_cmd, \"testing/e2e\", \"-vv\"]\n```\n\n</details>\n\n</blockquote></details>\n<details>\n<summary>fuzz/README.md (1)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`124-129`: **Consider using `+nightly` flag instead of setting global default.**\n\nSetting `rustup default nightly` changes the global default toolchain, which may affect other projects. A safer approach is to use `cargo +nightly fuzz` or set up a `rust-toolchain.toml` in the fuzz directory.\n\n\n<details>\n<summary>Proposed documentation update</summary>\n\n```diff\n ### Nightly toolchain issues\n \n ```bash\n rustup install nightly\n-rustup default nightly\n+# Use +nightly flag with cargo-fuzz commands:\n+cargo +nightly fuzz run fuzz_odata_filter\n+\n+# Or create fuzz/rust-toolchain.toml with:\n+# [toolchain]\n+# channel = \"nightly\"\n ```\n```\n</details>\n\n</blockquote></details>\n<details>\n<summary>.github/workflows/clusterfuzzlite.yml (1)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`63-65`: **Pin cargo-fuzz to a known-good version for CI stability.**\n\nInstalling the latest each run can introduce unexpected breakages; consider pinning a version used locally.  \n \n\n<details>\n<summary>♻️ Proposed change (pin version)</summary>\n\n```diff\n env:\n   CARGO_TERM_COLOR: always\n   RUST_BACKTRACE: full\n+  CARGO_FUZZ_VERSION: \"x.y.z\" # set to a known-good version\n@@\n       - name: Install cargo-fuzz\n-        run: cargo +nightly install cargo-fuzz\n+        run: cargo +nightly install cargo-fuzz --version ${{ env.CARGO_FUZZ_VERSION }}\n```\n</details>\n\n</blockquote></details>\n\n</blockquote></details>\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment by CodeRabbit for review status -->","state":"COMMENTED","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/301#pullrequestreview-3697263519","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/301","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","_links":{"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/301#pullrequestreview-3697263519"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/301"}},"submitted_at":"2026-01-23T12:27:26Z","commit_id":"99828b719472e23ec408b20448f5cf8bef29b404"},{"id":3697364498,"node_id":"PRR_kwDOPaLyBs7cYU4S","user":{"login":"coderabbitai[bot]","id":136622811,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOCCSy2w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/347564?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/coderabbitai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"**Actionable comments posted: 1**\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Fix all issues with AI agents</summary>\n\n```\nIn @.github/workflows/clusterfuzzlite.yml:\n- Around line 15-17: The top-level concurrency block uses `${{ matrix.sanitizer\n}}` which is invalid because the matrix context is only available at the job\nscope; update the workflow by moving the concurrency block into the job that\nuses `matrix` (e.g., under the job that references `matrix.sanitizer`) or remove\n`matrix.sanitizer` from the `group` value and use only available contexts like\n`${{ github.workflow }}-${{ github.ref }}`; adjust the `concurrency` key (and\nits `group`/`cancel-in-progress`) accordingly so it lives where `matrix` is\ndefined or no longer references `matrix.sanitizer`.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>♻️ Duplicate comments (1)</summary><blockquote>\n\n<details>\n<summary>Makefile (1)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`388-388`: **Including `fuzz` in `all` adds ~4 minutes to every build.**\n\nRunning fuzzing smoke tests (30s × 8 targets) on every `make all` invocation significantly impacts local development velocity. Fuzzing is resource-intensive and better suited as an explicit opt-in or CI-only operation.\n\n\n\n<details>\n<summary>Suggested fix</summary>\n\n```diff\n-all: build check test-sqlite e2e-local fuzz\n+all: build check test-sqlite e2e-local\n```\n\nDevelopers can run `make fuzz` explicitly, and CI handles continuous fuzzing via the ClusterFuzzLite workflow.\n</details>\n\n</blockquote></details>\n\n</blockquote></details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>🧹 Nitpick comments (1)</summary><blockquote>\n\n<details>\n<summary>scripts/ci.py (1)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`367-367`: **Consider list unpacking for cleaner syntax.**\n\nStatic analysis suggests using list unpacking instead of concatenation.\n\n\n\n<details>\n<summary>Suggested fix</summary>\n\n```diff\n-    pytest_cmd = pytest_base_cmd + [\"testing/e2e\", \"-vv\"]\n+    pytest_cmd = [*pytest_base_cmd, \"testing/e2e\", \"-vv\"]\n```\n</details>\n\n</blockquote></details>\n\n</blockquote></details>\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment by CodeRabbit for review status -->","state":"COMMENTED","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/301#pullrequestreview-3697364498","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/301","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","_links":{"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/301#pullrequestreview-3697364498"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/301"}},"submitted_at":"2026-01-23T12:58:24Z","commit_id":"a2d6e1f2bb744176c3d7eb0f085c217e647bdba4"},{"id":3697395667,"node_id":"PRR_kwDOPaLyBs7cYcfT","user":{"login":"coderabbitai[bot]","id":136622811,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOCCSy2w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/347564?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/coderabbitai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/c