ng into standard workflows. However, as noted in a previous review, this adds ~30s × 8 targets to every `make all` invocation.\n\nConsider whether this tradeoff is acceptable for your team's workflow, or if a separate `make ci-full` target (including fuzzing) would better serve both quick iteration and comprehensive checks.\n\n</blockquote></details>\n\n</blockquote></details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>🧹 Nitpick comments (2)</summary><blockquote>\n\n<details>\n<summary>scripts/ci.py (1)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`509-534`: **Consider extracting cargo-fuzz installation check to a helper.**\n\nThe cargo-fuzz installation check is duplicated across `cmd_fuzz_build`, `cmd_fuzz_list`, `cmd_fuzz_run`, and `cmd_fuzz`. This could be extracted to a helper function:\n\n```python\ndef ensure_cargo_fuzz():\n    result = run_cmd_allow_fail([\"cargo\", \"+nightly\", \"fuzz\", \"--version\"])\n    if result.returncode != 0:\n        print(\"Installing cargo-fuzz...\")\n        run_cmd([\"cargo\", \"install\", \"cargo-fuzz\"])\n```\n\nThis is a minor improvement that can be deferred.\n\n</blockquote></details>\n<details>\n<summary>fuzz/README.md (1)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`15-33`: **Add explicit nightly toolchain usage in Quick Start.**  \nYou mention nightly in prerequisites/troubleshooting, but the Quick Start commands don’t show `+nightly`. Consider adding it to avoid confusion.  \n\n<details>\n<summary>✏️ Suggested doc tweak</summary>\n\n```diff\n-# Build all fuzz targets\n-make fuzz-build\n+# Build all fuzz targets (requires nightly)\n+make fuzz-build\n+\n+# Or run cargo-fuzz explicitly with nightly\n+# cargo +nightly fuzz run fuzz_odata_filter\n```\n</details>\n\n</blockquote></details>\n\n</blockquote></details>\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment by CodeRabbit for review status -->","state":"COMMENTED","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/301#pullrequestreview-3697395667","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-ru