":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"**Actionable comments posted: 2**\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Fix all issues with AI agents</summary>\n\n```\nIn `@scripts/ci.py`:\n- Around line 547-551: The fuzz_seconds assignment needs validation so passing 0\nor negative seconds doesn't produce invalid fuzz args; update the logic around\nfuzz_seconds (used to build fuzz_cmd) to validate args.seconds: if args.seconds\nis None use the existing default (60), otherwise coerce to an int and if <= 0\neither raise a clear error or clamp to a minimum (e.g., 1) and log/warn; then\nuse that validated fuzz_seconds when constructing fuzz_cmd to ensure\n\"-max_total_time\" is always a positive value.\n- Around line 509-520: The cmd_fuzz_build flow currently conflates missing\nnightly toolchain and missing cargo-fuzz; add an explicit nightly preflight: use\nrun_cmd_allow_fail to run a rustup toolchain query (e.g., [\"rustup\",\n\"toolchain\", \"list\"] or [\"rustup\", \"show\", \"active-toolchain\"]) and check the\noutput for \"nightly\" before attempting any cargo +nightly commands in\ncmd_fuzz_build; if nightly is not present, print a clear instruction to install\nit (e.g., \"rustup toolchain install nightly\") and exit/abort the build step so\nwe don't try to install cargo-fuzz against the wrong toolchain; only after\nconfirming nightly exists, perform the existing cargo-fuzz --version check\n(using run_cmd_allow_fail) and install cargo-fuzz with run_cmd([\"cargo\",\n\"install\", \"cargo-fuzz\"]) if missing, then run the build in fuzz_dir.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment by CodeRabbit for review status -->","state":"COMMENTED","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/301#pullrequestreview-3705805533","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/301","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","_links":{"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/301#pullrequestreview-3705805533"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/301"}},"submitted_at":"2026-01-26T12:24:42Z","commit_id":"d882f161185dc52f0478308b057991d31ad2ca99"},{"id":3706608366,"node_id":"PRR_kwDOPaLyBs7c7lru","user":{"login":"coderabbitai[bot]","id":136622811,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOCCSy2w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/347564?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/coderabbitai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"**Actionable comments posted: 1**\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Fix all issues with AI agents</summary>\n\n```\nIn `@scripts/ci.py`:\n- Around line 590-602: The smoke_time calculation in cmd_fuzz (smoke_time =\nargs.seconds or 30) can accept negative values because cmd_fuzz lacks the\npositive-seconds validation present in cmd_fuzz_run; update cmd_fuzz to validate\nargs.seconds is None or a positive integer (e.g., if args.seconds is not None\nand args.seconds <= 0: raise/exit with an error), then set smoke_time using the\nvalidated value (smoke_time = args.seconds if args.seconds is not None else 30)\nso negative values cannot produce invalid fuzz arguments.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment by CodeRabbit for review status -->","state":"COMMENTED","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/301#pullrequestreview-3706608366","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/301","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","_links":{"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/301#pullrequestreview-3706608366"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/301"}},"submitted_at":"2026-01-26T15:31:25Z","commit_id":"eac065952000074e1b64ba216b257e5922b1a5e8"},{"id":3711368711,"node_id":"PRR_kwDOPaLyBs7dNv4H","user":{"login":"coderabbitai[bot]","id":136622811,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOCCSy2w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/347564?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/coderabbitai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"**Actionable comments posted: 4**\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Fix all issues with AI agents</summary>\n\n```\nIn `@fuzz/fuzz_targets/fuzz_odata_filter.rs`:\n- Around line 6-15: Add a complexity guard to the fuzz harness around\nparse_filter_string to avoid expensive pathological inputs: in the fuzz_target\nbefore invoking parse_filter_string either perform a cheap pre-parse\nnesting/depth check or parse into an AST and immediately call node_count() and\nreturn if it exceeds a safe threshold (e.g. 1000). Locate the call to\nparse_filter_string in the fuzz_target and add the guard so deeply-nested inputs\nare skipped (use parse result + node_count() or a pre-parse depth heuristic)\nrather than allowing the parser to consume excessive resources.\n\nIn `@libs/modkit-macros/src/domain_model.rs`:\n- Around line 16-76: The test found two issues: the field-assertion const block\nreferences generic type parameters out of scope and the generated impl of\nDomainSafe lacks required trait bounds on type parameters. Fix\nexpand_domain_model by (1) attaching the struct's generics to the validation\nfunctions/const block so type params are in scope (use the existing\nimpl_generics when declaring fn __validate_domain_model_fields and the const\nblock, e.g., fn __validate_domain_model_fields#impl_generics() {\n__assert_field_is_domain_safe::<#field_types>(); }) and (2) require each generic\ntype parameter to implement ::modkit::domain::DomainSafe by extending\nimpl_generics/where_clause for the impl of ::modkit::domain::DomainSafe for\n`#name` (so impl `#impl_generics` becomes impl `#impl_generics` where <generic\nparams>: ::modkit::domain::DomainSafe). Ensure you update the generated\nfield_assertions and the impl for ::modkit::domain::DomainSafe accordingly.\n\nIn `@scripts/ci.py`:\n- Around line 520-526: In ensure_cargo_fuzz(), the installation currently uses\nthe default toolchain; change the install invocation to run under nightly so\ncargo-fuzz is installed into the nightly toolchain: replace the\nrun_cmd([\"cargo\", \"install\", \"cargo-fuzz\"]) call with run_cmd([\"cargo\",\n\"+nightly\", \"install\", \"cargo-fuzz\"]) so that ensure_cargo_fuzz() consistently\nchecks and installs cargo-fuzz for the nightly toolchain.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>🧹 Nitpick comments (5)</summary><blockquote>\n\n<details>\n<summary>.clusterfuzzlite/build.sh (2)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`15-15`: **Quote the variable to handle paths with spaces.**\n\nWhile unlikely in CI environments, quoting `$SRC` is defensive and follows shell best practices.\n\n\n<details>\n<summary>🔧 Suggested fix</summary>\n\n```diff\n-cd $SRC/hyperspot\n+cd \"$SRC/hyperspot\"\n```\n</details>\n\n---\n\n`21-27`: **Hardcoded architecture may limit portability.**\n\nThe path `x86_64-unknown-linux-gnu` assumes x86_64 Linux. If ClusterFuzzLite ever runs on ARM runners, this would need adjustment. Consider using `rustc -vV | grep host` to detect the target triple dynamically.\n\n\n<details>\n<summary>🔧 Suggested alternative</summary>\n\n```diff\n-FUZZ_TARGET_OUTPUT_DIR=fuzz/target/x86_64-unknown-linux-gnu/release\n+# Detect host target triple dynamically\n+HOST_TARGET=$(rustc -vV | grep '^host:' | cut -d' ' -f2)\n+FUZZ_TARGET_OUTPUT_DIR=\"fuzz/target/${HOST_TARGET}/release\"\n```\n</details>\n\n</blockquote></details>\n<details>\n<summary>scripts/ci.py (1)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`578-589`: **Handle potential empty or None stdout.**\n\nIf `cargo fuzz list` fails in an unexpected way, `result.stdout` could be `None` or empty, causing `strip()` or `split()` to fail.\n\n\n<details>\n<summary>🔧 Suggested defensive handling</summary>\n\n```diff\n     result = subprocess.run(\n         [\"cargo\", \"+nightly\", \"fuzz\", \"list\"],\n         cwd=fuzz_dir,\n         capture_output=True,\n         text=True\n     )\n\n     if result.returncode != 0:\n         print(\"Failed to list fuzz targets\")\n         sys.exit(1)\n\n-    targets = result.stdout.strip().split('\\n')\n+    targets = (result.stdout or \"\").strip().split('\\n')\n     smoke_time = args.seconds or 30\n```\n</details>\n\n</blockquote></details>\n<details>\n<summary>Makefile (1)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`342-355`: **Consider delegating the smoke-test loop to a helper script to satisfy checkmake’s maxbodylength warning.**\n\nThis target exceeds the recommended recipe length; moving the loop to `scripts/ci.py` (or a small shell script) keeps the Makefile terse without changing behavior.\n\n</blockquote></details>\n<details>\n<summary>modules/simple_user_settings/simple_user_settings/src/domain/repo.rs (1)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`7-11`: **Unconventional but valid compile-time enforcement pattern.**\n\nUsing a where clause on a trait with concrete types (not generic parameters) is an unusual pattern. This effectively creates a compile-time assertion that `SimpleUserSettings` and `SimpleUserSettingsPatch` implement `DomainModel` whenever this trait is referenced.\n\nThis approach achieves the domain-layer enforcement goal, but consider whether a simpler alternative might be clearer—such as adding `#[domain_model]` directly to the `SimpleUserSettings` and `SimpleUserSettingsPatch` types themselves (if not already done) and removing this where clause, or adding a brief comment explaining this enforcement pattern for future maintainers.\n\n</blockquote></details>\n\n</blockquote></details>\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment by CodeRabbit for review status -->","state":"COMMENTED","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/301#pullrequestreview-3711368711","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/301","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","_links":{"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/301#pullrequestreview-3711368711"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/301"}},"submitted_at":"2026-01-27T14:00:01Z","commit_id":"24a5734aa20105673196c4904f52a84341199147"},{"id":3718129428,"node_id":"PRR_kwDOPaLyBs7dnicU","user":{"login":"coderabbitai[bot]","id":136622811,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOCCSy2w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/347564?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/coderabbitai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"**Actionable comments posted: 1**\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Fix all issues with AI agents</summary>\n\n```\nIn `@CONTRIBUTING.md`:\n- Around line 100-120: The example in CONTRIBUTING.md shows the disabled fuzz\ntarget fuzz_odata_filter which will confuse contributors; update the example\ncommand to use an enabled target such as fuzz_odata_cursor or fuzz_odata_orderby\n(e.g., replace occurrences of fuzz_odata_filter in the \"Target specific\ncomponent\" example) and add a short parenthetical note indicating that\nfuzz_odata_filter is currently disabled due to a parser bug to prevent future\nconfusion.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>🧹 Nitpick comments (1)</summary><blockquote>\n\n<details>\n<summary>Makefile (1)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`321-327`: **Minor inconsistency with `scripts/ci.py` for cargo-fuzz installation.**\n\nThe Makefile installs cargo-fuzz to the default toolchain (`cargo install cargo-fuzz`), while `scripts/ci.py` uses `cargo +nightly install cargo-fuzz`. Both work since cargo-fuzz is invoked with `+nightly`, but for consistency consider:\n\n```diff\n fuzz-install:\n \t`@command` -v cargo-fuzz >/dev/null || \\\n-\t\t(echo \"Installing cargo-fuzz...\" && cargo install cargo-fuzz)\n+\t\t(echo \"Installing cargo-fuzz...\" && cargo +nightly install cargo-fuzz)\n```\n\nThis is non-blocking since the current setup functions correctly.\n\n</blockquote></details>\n\n</blockquote></details>\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment by CodeRabbit for review status -->","state":"COMMENTED","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/301#pullrequestreview-3718129428","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/301","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","_links":{"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/301#pullrequestreview-3718129428"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/301"}},"submitted_at":"2026-01-28T17:49:39Z","commit_id":"9ef0561564fdd44fddb3844c7c2f21201ac52940"}]},{"source_pr_number":300,"source_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/300","source_state":"closed","source_author":"bit8shift","target_issue_number":null,"title":"[PR #300] fix: prevent unsafe PID conversion in process termination","status":"exported","mirrored_at":null,"comments_status":"none","comments_mirrored":0,"pr_head_ref":"fix/prevent-unsafe-PID-conversation-in-process-termination","pr_head_sha":"b77db7b705b8c641894aa3ffd5bde0c6f3e6f0f1","pr_base_ref":"main","pr_head_owner":"bit8shift","pr_from_fork":1,"source_data":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/300","id":3202841326,"node_id":"PR_kwDOPaLyBs6-53ru","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/300","diff_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/300.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/300.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/issues/300","number":300,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"fix: prevent unsafe PID conversion in process termination","user":{"login":"bit8shift","id":253408973,"node_id":"U_kgDODxq2zQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/253408973?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/bit8shift","html_url":"https://github.com/bit8shift","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bit8shift/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bit8shift/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bit8shift/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bit8shift/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bit8shift/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bit8shift/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bit8shift/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bit8shift/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bit8shift/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Closes #234 \r\n\r\n## Summary\r\n\r\nThis PR fixes a dangerous PID conversion bug in Unix process termination logic.\r\n\r\n## Problem\r\n\r\nOn Unix systems, converting a `u32` PID to `i32` using `unwrap_or(0)` could silently default to PID `0`.  \r\nSending a signal to PID `0` targets **all processes in the current process group**, which could unintentionally terminate unrelated processes during shutdown.\r\n\r\n## Changes\r\n\r\n- Replace `unwrap_or(0)` with explicit `let-else` conversion handling\r\n- Log a warning when a PID exceeds `i32::MAX`\r\n- Return `false` instead of signaling when conversion fails\r\n- Improve documentation of failure modes and platform-specific behavior\r\n- **Add tests covering PID conversion failure and termination edge cases**\r\n\r\n## Behavior Change\r\n\r\n- **Before:** Failed PID conversion could signal the entire process group\r\n- **After:** Failed PID conversion logs a warning and no signal is sent\r\n\r\nThis makes shutdown behaviour safer and more predictable.\r\n\r\n\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai -->\n## Summary by CodeRabbit\n\n* **Bug Fixes**\n  * Improved child process termination with stricter PID validation and handling; added debug logging when a termination signal is not sent\n  * Unix path: better handling of large/invalid PIDs and signal delivery reporting\n  * Windows path: explicit non-graceful termination behavior (no reliable graceful termination)\n* **Documentation**\n  * Expanded docs describing termination behavior on Unix and Windows\n* **Tests**\n  * Added tests covering termination behavior and edge cases\n\n<sub>✏️ Tip: You can customize this high-level summary in your review settings.</sub>\n<!-- end of auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai -->","created_at":"2026-01-23T10:50:10Z","updated_at":"2026-01-26T08:17:14Z","closed_at":"2026-01-26T08:16:54Z","merged_at":"2026-01-26T08:16:54Z","merge_commit_sha":"0058ea6b050cb76085f9223eced24e0bb92d1b4d","assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[],"requested_teams":[],"labels":[],"milestone":null,"draft":false,"commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/300/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/300/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/issues/300/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/statuses/b77db7b705b8c641894aa3ffd5bde0c6f3e6f0f1","head":{"label":"bit8shift:fix/prevent-unsafe-PID-conversation-in-process-termination","ref":"fix/prevent-unsafe-PID-conversation-in-process-termination","sha":"b77db7b705b8c641894aa3ffd5bde0c6f3e6f0f1","user":{"login":"bit8shift","id":253408973,"node_id":"U_kgDODxq2zQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/253408973?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/bit8shift","html_url":"https://github.com/bit8shift","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bit8shift/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bit8shift/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bit8shift/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bit8shift/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bit8shift/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bit8shift/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bit8shift/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bit8shift/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bit8shift/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"repo":{"id":1130083757,"node_id":"R_kgDOQ1u1rQ","name":"cyberfabric-core","full_name":"bit8shift/cyberfabric-core","private":false,"owner":{"login":"bit8shift","id":253408973,"node_id":"U_kgDODxq2zQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/253408973?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/bit8shift","html_url":"https://github.com/bit8shift","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bit8shift/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bit8shift/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bit8shift/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bit8shift/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bit8shift/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bit8shift/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bit8shift/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bit8shift/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bit8shift/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"html_url":"https://github.com/bit8shift/cyberfabric-core","description":"All-in-one open-source services development platform with integrated LLMs manager, chat,