tps://github.com/apps/coderabbitai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-01-22T09:20:53Z","updated_at":"2026-01-23T10:14:13Z","body":"<!-- This is an auto-generated comment: summarize by coderabbit.ai -->\n<!-- walkthrough_start -->\n\n<details>\n<summary>📝 Walkthrough</summary>\n\n## Walkthrough\n\nAdds debug-level diagnostics for GTS entity registration/validation: a new diagnostics module, integration points in the types-registry storage paths, config and CI changes to enable debug logging in E2E, extensive E2E tests, and minor validator scanner indentation/filename-match tweak.\n\n## Changes\n\n| Cohort / File(s) | Summary |\n|---|---|\n| **Validator tweak** <br> `apps/gts-docs-validator/src/scanner.rs`, `apps/gts-docs-validator/src/validator.rs` | Small scanner/validator adjustments: an extra filename-pattern branch in `matches_exclude` and re-indentation of an error string; no public API changes. |\n| **Debug diagnostics module** <br> `modules/system/types-registry/types-registry/src/infra/storage/debug_diagnostics.rs` | New public module providing functions to log registration failures, schema validation failures, instance validation failures, schema-chain traversal with cycle detection, reference collection, and helpers for GTS ref normalization. |\n| **Storage layer integration** <br> `modules/system/types-registry/types-registry/src/infra/storage/in_memory_repo.rs`, `modules/system/types-registry/types-registry/src/infra/storage/mod.rs` | Import and call debug diagnostics on validation/commit failures across config and ready flows; adds module declaration. |\n| **Config / CI** <br> `config/e2e-local.yaml`, `scripts/ci.py` | Adds types-registry logging config (file/console levels) and sets RUST_LOG=types_registry=debug,info for local E2E; fixes pytest args handling for CI local runs. |\n| **Spec & docs** <br> `modules/system/types-registry/openspec/.../2026-01-21-add-gts-registration-debug-logging/*`, `modules/system/types-registry/openspec/specs/types-registry/spec.md` | New proposal, spec, and tasks documents describing debug logging behavior, schema-chain logging, cycle handling, and tests. |\n| **E2E tests** <br> `testing/e2e/modules/types_registry/test_registration_debug_logging.py` | New E2E test module (5 async tests) asserting debug logs contain entity/schema/instance dumps, chain depth labeling, cycle detection behavior, and log-level gating. |\n\n## Sequence Diagram(s)\n\n```mermaid\nsequenceDiagram\n    participant Client\n    participant Server as TypesRegistry<br/>Server\n    participant Validator as Validation<br/>Logic\n    participant Logger as DebugDiagnostics<br/>Module\n    participant SchemaStore as GtsOps<br/>Store\n    participant Tracer as Tracing<br/>Subscriber\n\n    Client->>Server: POST /register entity\n    Server->>Validator: validate(entity)\n    alt validation fails\n        Validator-->>Server: Err(validation)\n        Server->>Logger: log_instance_validation_failure/ log_schema_validation_failure / log_registration_failure\n        Logger->>Tracer: tracing::debug! pretty-printed entity/schema/instance\n        Logger->>SchemaStore: fetch schema(s) by id\n        SchemaStore-->>Logger: schema JSON\n        loop traverse parents\n            Logger->>Logger: collect refs & normalize\n            Logger->>SchemaStore: fetch parent schema\n            SchemaStore-->>Logger: parent schema\n            Logger->>Tracer: tracing::debug! schema depth/role\n            alt cycle detected\n                Logger->>Tracer: tracing::debug! cycle warning\n            end\n        end\n        Server-->>Client: 4xx validation error\n    else validation succeeds\n        Validator-->>Server: Ok\n        Server-->>Client: 2xx success\n    end\n```\n\n```mermaid\nsequenceDiagram\n    participant CI as CI Runner\n    participant Server as TypesRegistry<br/>Server\n    participant Tracer as Tracing<br/>Subscriber\n    participant PyTest as pytest\n    participant LogFile as types-registry.log\n\n    CI->>Server: start with RUST_LOG=types_registry=debug,info\n    Server->>Tracer: initialize subscriber (debug)\n    Tracer->>LogFile: write debug diagnostics\n    PyTest->>Server: trigger invalid registrations\n    Server->>Tracer: emit debugging entries\n    Tracer->>LogFile: flush diagnostics\n    PyTest->>LogFile: read and assert diagnostics present\n```\n\n## Estimated code review effort\n\n🎯 4 (Complex) | ⏱️ ~45 minutes\n\n## Possibly related issues\n\n- Issue `#261`: Aligns directly — implements debug logging for failed GTS registrations, entity/schema/instance dumps, schema chain traversal, cycle warnings, and tests.\n\n## Possibly related PRs\n\n- PR `#281`: Edits the same `matches_exclude` function in `apps/gts-docs-validator/src/scanner.rs` and is therefore related at the code level.\n\n## Suggested reviewers\n\n- Bechma  \n- MikeFalcon77\n\n## Poem\n\n> 🐰 Hopping through logs with a keen little nose,  \n> I found schema chains where the wild error grows.  \n> I print pretty JSON and mark every depth,  \n> Catch cycles and traces with a soft little breath.  \n> Debug lights the path — hummed by a rabbit in prose.\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- walkthrough_end -->\n\n\n<!-- pre_merge_checks_walkthrough_start -->\n\n<details>\n<summary>🚥 Pre-merge checks | ✅ 3</summary>\n\n<details>\n<summary>✅ Passed checks (3 passed)</summary>\n\n|     Check name     | Status   | Explanation                                                                                                                                                                                                                                 |\n| :----------------: | :------- | :------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ |\n|  Description Check | ✅ Passed | Check skipped - CodeRabbit’s high-level summary is enabled.                                                                                                                                                                                 |\n|     Title check    | ✅ Passed | The title accurately summarizes the main change: adding debug logging for GTS registration and validation workflows, which is directly reflected in the implementation of the debug_diagnostics module, logging integration, and E2E tests. |\n| Docstring Coverage | ✅ Passed | Docstring coverage is 100.00% which is sufficient. The required threshold is 80.00%.                                                                                                                                                        |\n\n</details>\n\n<sub>✏️ Tip: You can configure your own custom pre-merge checks in the settings.</sub>\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- pre_merge_checks_walkthrough_end -->\n\n<!-- finishing_touch_checkbox_start -->\n\n<details>\n<summary>✨ Finishing touches</summary>\n\n- [ ] <!-- {\"checkboxId\": \"7962f53c-55bc-4827-bfbf-6a18da830691\"} --> 📝 Generate docstrings\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- finishing_touch_checkbox_end -->\n\n<!-- tips_start -->\n\n---\n\n\n\n<sub>Comment `@coderabbitai help` to get the list of available commands and usage tips.</sub>\n\n<!-- tips_end -->\n\n<!-- internal state start -->\n\n\n<!--  -->\n\n<!-- internal state end -->","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/issues/comments/3783369040/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":{"id":347564,"client_id":"Iv1.6aaafe4fe882736b","slug":"coderabbitai","node_id":"A_kwHOB96YWc4ABU2s","owner":{"login":"coderabbitai","id":132028505,"node_id":"O_kgDOB96YWQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/132028505?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai","html_url":"https://github.com/coderabbitai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/received_events","type":"Organization","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"name":"coderabbitai","description":"# Transforming Code Reviews with AI\r\n\r\n## Features\r\n\r\n**Automated Reviews**: Continuous reviews of the pull requests including incremental commits. \r\n\r\n**Summarization**: Generates high-level summary and a technical walkthrough of the PR changes. \r\n\r\n**Line-by-line review**: Provides line-by-line suggestions committable with one click.\r\n\r\n**Codebase verification**:  Verifies the impact on the overall codebase and identifies missing changes.\r\n\r\n**Insights into your code**:  Ask any questions on your codebase within the pull request \r\n\r\n**Chat about your code** : Chat with the bot around your code. The more you chat, the smarter it gets.\r\n\r\n**Issue Validation**:  Validates the PR against the linked issues and identifies other related issues \r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n","external_url":"https://coderabbit.ai?utm_source=cr_app&utm_medium=github","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/coderabbitai","created_at":"2023-06-14T15:47:27Z","updated_at":"2026-03-14T07:58:44Z","permissions":{"actions":"read","checks":"write","contents":"write","discussions":"read","issues":"write","members":"read","metadata":"read","pull_requests":"write","statuses":"write"},"events":["issues","issue_comment","label","organization","pull_request","pull_request_review","pull_request_review_comment","pull_request_review_thread","release","repository"]}},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/issues/comments/3789432141","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/293#issuecomment-3789432141","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/issues/293","id":3789432141,"node_id":"IC_kwDOPaLyBs7h3iVN","user":{"login":"mergify[bot]","id":37929162,"node_id":"MDM6Qm90Mzc5MjkxNjI=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/10562?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mergify%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/mergify","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mergify%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mergify%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mergify%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mergify%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mergify%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mergify%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mergify%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mergify%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mergify%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-01-23T09:59:44Z","updated_at":"2026-01-23T10:07:10Z","body":"<!--MERGIFY-CI-INSIGHTS-REPORT-->\n# 🧪 CI Insights\n\nHere's what we observed from your CI run for cfd76fb9.\n\n## 🟢 All jobs passed!\n\nBut CI Insights is watching 👀","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/issues/comments/3789432141/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":{"id":10562,"client_id":"Iv1.d035f68f69425dc1","slug":"mergify","node_id":"MDM6QXBwMTA1NjI=","owner":{"login":"Mergifyio","id":37838584,"node_id":"MDEyOk9yZ2FuaXphdGlvbjM3ODM4NTg0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/37838584?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mergifyio","html_url":"https://github.com/Mergifyio","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mergifyio/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mergifyio/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mergifyio/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mergifyio/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mergifyio/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mergifyio/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mergifyio/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mergifyio/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mergifyio/received_events","type":"Organization","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"name":"Mergify","description":"Pull requests automation service.","external_url":"https://mergify.com","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/mergify","created_at":"2018-03-30T10:19:51Z","updated_at":"2026-03-02T11:02:56Z","permissions":{"actions":"write","administration":"read","checks":"write","contents":"write","deployments":"write","emails":"read","issues":"write","members":"read","merge_queues":"read","metadata":"read","pages":"write","pull_requests":"write","statuses":"read","workflows":"write"},"events":["branch_protection_configuration","branch_protection_rule","check_run","check_suite","deployment_status","issue_comment","member","membership","merge_group","organization","pull_request","pull_request_review","pull_request_review_comment","pull_request_review_thread","push","repository","repository_ruleset","status","team","team_add","workflow_job","workflow_run"]}}],"source_review_comments":[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2716046901","pull_request_review_id":3691460165,"id":2716046901,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs6h45Y1","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,439 @@\n+\"\"\"E2E tests for GTS registration debug logging.\n+\n+These tests verify that debug-level logging is emitted when GTS entity\n+registration fails. The tests trigger validation failures and verify\n+the expected debug log output is present in the log file.\n+\n+The server must be configured with types_registry logging at debug level:\n+  logging:\n+    types_registry:\n+      file: \"logs/types-registry.log\"\n+      file_level: debug\n+\"\"\"\n+import httpx\n+import os\n+import pytest\n+import time\n+from pathlib import Path\n+\n+_counter = int(time.time() * 1000) % 1000000\n+\n+# Path to the server error log file (where debug logs are written)\n+# The server writes to logs/types-registry.log based on config/e2e-local.yaml\n+LOG_FILE_PATH = Path(__file__).parent.parent.parent.parent.parent / \"logs\" / \"types-registry.log\"\n+\n+\n+def get_log_content() -> str:\n+    \"\"\"Read the server error log file content.\"\"\"\n+    if LOG_FILE_PATH.exists():\n+        return LOG_FILE_PATH.read_text()\n+    return \"\"\n+\n+\n+def get_log_lines_after(marker: str, content: str) -> list[str]:\n+    \"\"\"Get log lines that appear after a specific marker in the log content.\"\"\"\n+    lines = content.split('\\n')\n+    found_marker = False\n+    result = []\n+    for line in lines:\n+        if marker in line:\n+            found_marker = True\n+        if found_marker:\n+            result.append(line)\n+    return result\n+\n+\n+def unique_type_id(name: str) -> str:\n+    \"\"\"Generate a unique type GTS ID.\"\"\"\n+    global _counter\n+    _counter += 1\n+    return f\"gts.e2etest.debuglog.models.{name}{_counter}.v1~\"\n+\n+\n+def make_schema_id(gts_id: str) -> str:\n+    return \"gts://\" + gts_id\n+\n+\n+def unique_instance_id(type_id: str, name: str) -> str:\n+    \"\"\"Generate a unique instance GTS ID based on a type ID.\"\"\"\n+    global _counter\n+    _counter += 1\n+    return f\"{type_id}e2etest.debuglog.inst.{name}{_counter}.v1\"\n+\n+\n+@pytest.mark.asyncio\n+async def test_debug_log_invalid_schema_registration(base_url, auth_headers):\n+    \"\"\"\n+    Test that registering an invalid schema emits debug logs with schema content.\n+    \n+    Verifies debug log output contains:\n+    - GTS ID of the schema being registered\n+    - Complete schema JSON (pretty-printed)\n+    - Validation error message\n+    \"\"\"\n+    type_id = unique_type_id(\"invalid_schema\")\n+    \n+    # Record log position before request\n+    log_before = get_log_content()\n+    \n+    async with httpx.AsyncClient(timeout=10.0) as client:\n+        payload = {\n+            \"entities\": [\n+                {\n+                    \"$id\": make_schema_id(type_id),\n+                    \"$schema\": \"http://json-schema.org/draft-07/schema#\",\n+                    \"type\": \"invalid_type_value\",\n+                    \"properties\": {\n+                        \"name\": {\"type\": \"also_invalid\"}\n+                    }\n+                }\n+            ]\n+        }\n+        \n+        response = await client.post(\n+            f\"{base_url}/types-registry/v1/entities\",\n+            headers=auth_headers,\n+            json=payload,\n+        )\n+        \n+        if response.status_code in (401, 403) and not auth_headers:\n+            pytest.skip(\n+                f\"Endpoint requires authentication (got {response.status_code}). \"\n+                \"Set E2E_AUTH_TOKEN environment variable to run this test.\"\n+            )\n+        \n+        assert response.status_code == 200\n+        data = response.json()\n+        results = data[\"results\"]\n+        \n+        # Give server a moment to flush logs\n+        time.sleep(0.1)\n+        \n+        # Read log content after request\n+        log_after = get_log_content()\n+        new_logs = log_after[len(log_before):]\n+        \n+        # Verify debug logs contain expected content when debug level is enabled\n+        # Note: Debug logs only appear if RUST_LOG=types_registry=debug is set\n+        if new_logs and results[0][\"status\"] == \"error\":\n+            # Check if debug logging is enabled (look for DEBUG level messages from types_registry)\n+            debug_enabled = \"DEBUG\" in new_logs and \"types_registry\" in new_logs\n+            if debug_enabled:\n+                # Verify GTS ID is logged\n+                assert type_id in new_logs or type_id.rstrip('~') in new_logs, \\\n+                    f\"Expected GTS ID '{type_id}' in debug logs\"\n+                # Verify schema content keywords are present\n+                assert \"invalid_type_value\" in new_logs, \\\n+                    \"Expected schema content 'invalid_type_value' in debug logs\"\n+            # Test passes if validation error was detected (debug logs are optional)\n+\n+\n+@pytest.mark.asyncio\n+async def test_debug_log_instance_schema_mismatch(base_url, auth_headers):\n+    \"\"\"\n+    Test that instance validation failure emits debug logs with instance and schema.\n+    \n+    Verifies debug log output contains:\n+    - Instance JSON (pretty-printed)\n+    - Instance's schema JSON (if found)\n+    - GTS ID of the instance\n+    - Schema chain with depth labels\n+    \"\"\"\n+    type_id = unique_type_id(\"person\")\n+    instance_id = unique_instance_id(type_id, \"person1\")\n+    \n+    # Record log position before request\n+    log_before = get_log_content()\n+    \n+    async with httpx.AsyncClient(timeout=10.0) as client:\n+        payload = {\n+            \"entities\": [\n+                {\n+                    \"$id\": make_schema_id(type_id),\n+                    \"$schema\": \"http://json-schema.org/draft-07/schema#\",\n+                    \"type\": \"object\",\n+                    \"properties\": {\n+                        \"name\": {\"type\": \"string\"},\n+                        \"age\": {\"type\": \"integer\"}\n+                    },\n+                    \"required\": [\"name\", \"age\"]\n+                },\n+                {\n+                    \"id\": instance_id,\n+                    \"name\": \"John\",\n+                    \"age\": \"not_a_number\"\n+                }\n+            ]\n+        }\n+        \n+        response = await client.post(\n+            f\"{base_url}/types-registry/v1/entities\",\n+            headers=auth_headers,\n+            json=payload,\n+        )\n+        \n+        if response.status_code in (401, 403) and not auth_headers:\n+            pytest.skip(\n+                f\"Endpoint requires authentication (got {response.status_code}). \"\n+                \"Set E2E_AUTH_TOKEN environment variable to run this test.\"\n+            )\n+        \n+        assert response.status_code == 200\n+        data = response.json()\n+        results = data[\"results\"]\n+        \n+        # Give server a moment to flush logs\n+        time.sleep(0.1)\n+        \n+        # Read log content after request\n+        log_after = get_log_content()\n+        new_logs = log_after[len(log_before):]\n+        \n+        # Schema should register successfully\n+        assert results[0][\"status\"] == \"ok\", \"Type should register successfully\"\n+        \n+        # Instance should fail validation due to wrong type for 'age'\n+        if new_logs and results[1][\"status\"] == \"error\":\n+            assert \"error\" in results[1]\n+            # Check if debug logging is enabled\n+            debug_enabled = \"DEBUG\" in new_logs and \"types_registry\" in new_logs\n+            if debug_enabled:\n+                # Verify instance content is logged\n+                assert \"not_a_number\" in new_logs, \\\n+                    \"Expected instance content 'not_a_number' in debug logs\"\n+                # Verify GTS ID is logged\n+                assert instance_id in new_logs or type_id in new_logs, \\\n+                    f\"Expected GTS ID in debug logs\"","path":"testing/e2e/modules/types_registry/test_registration_debug_logging.py","commit_id":"cfd76fb9303e2de3d140c010b92ca451e2dc982d","original_commit_id":"f763e616749d451f84a1a96fe71c1f9808bffa2e","user":{"login":"coderabbitai[bot]","id":136622811,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOCCSy2w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/347564?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/coderabbitai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"_⚠️ Potential issue_ | _🟡 Minor_\n\n**Remove extraneous f-string prefix.**\n\nThis assertion message doesn't use any format placeholders, so the `f` prefix is unnecessary.\n\n\n<details>\n<summary>Proposed fix</summary>\n\n```diff\n-                assert instance_id in new_logs or type_id in new_logs, \\\n-                    f\"Expected GTS ID in debug logs\"\n+                assert instance_id in new_logs or type_id in new_logs, \\\n+                    \"Expected GTS ID in debug logs\"\n```\n</details>\n\n<!-- suggestion_start -->\n\n<details>\n<summary>📝 Committable suggestion</summary>\n\n> ‼️ **IMPORTANT**\n> Carefully review the code before committing. Ensure that it accurately replaces the highlighted code, contains no missing lines, and has no issues with indentation. Thoroughly test & benchmark the code to ensure it meets the requirements.\n\n```suggestion\n                assert instance_id in new_logs or type_id in new_logs, \\\n                    \"Expected GTS ID in debug logs\"\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- suggestion_end -->\n\n<details>\n<summary>🧰 Tools</summary>\n\n<details>\n<summary>🪛 Ruff (0.14.13)</summary>\n\n206-206: f-string without any placeholders\n\nRemove extraneous `f` prefix\n\n(F541)\n\n</details>\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nIn `@testing/e2e/modules/types_registry/test_registration_debug_logging.py` around\nlines 205 - 206, The assertion uses an unnecessary f-string prefix: update the\nassert in test_registration_debug_logging (the line checking that instance_id or\ntype_id appears in new_logs) to use a plain string message instead of an\nf-string—i.e., remove the leading \"f\" from the assertion message referencing\ninstance_id, type_id, and new_logs so the message is a regular string literal.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- fingerprinting:phantom:medusa:ocelot -->\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment by CodeRabbit -->","created_at":"2026-01-22T09:26:15Z","updated_at":"2026-01-22T09:26:15Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/293#discussion_r2716046901","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/293","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2716046901"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/293#discussion_r2716046901"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/293"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2716046901/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":205,"original_start_line":205,"start_side":"RIGHT","line":206,"original_line":206,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","original_position":206,"position":206,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2720584025","pull_request_review_id":3696792008,"id":2720584025,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs6iKNFZ","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,59 @@\n+## ADDED Requirements\n+\n+### Requirement: Debug Logging for Failed Entity Registration\n+\n+The system SHALL emit debug-level log messages when GTS entity registration fails, including the complete entity content being registered.\n+\n+#### Scenario: Schema registration validation failure\n+\n+- **GIVEN** a GTS schema with invalid JSON Schema syntax\n+- **WHEN** the schema is registered via `register`\n+- **AND** validation fails\n+- **THEN** a debug log message SHALL be emitted containing the complete schema JSON (pretty-printed)\n+- **AND** the log message SHALL include the GTS ID of the schema being registered\n+\n+#### Scenario: Instance registration validation failure\n+\n+- **GIVEN** a GTS instance that does not conform to its schema\n+- **WHEN** the instance is registered via `register` with validation enabled\n+- **AND** validation fails\n+- **THEN** a debug log message SHALL be emitted containing the complete instance JSON (pretty-printed)\n+- **AND** a debug log message SHALL be emitted containing the instance's schema JSON (if found)\n+- **AND** the log message SHALL include the GTS ID of the instance being registered\n+\n+### Requirement: Schema Chain Logging for Instance Failures\n+\n+The system SHALL emit debug-level log messages containing the complete schema inheritance chain when an instance validation fails.\n+\n+#### Scenario: Instance with schema inheritance chain\n+\n+- **GIVEN** a GTS instance whose schema references parent schemas via `$ref`\n+- **WHEN** the instance validation fails\n+- **THEN** debug log messages SHALL be emitted for each schema in the inheritance chain\n+- **AND** each schema SHALL be logged as a distinct JSON object (not inlined) to preserve structure\n+- **AND** each schema SHALL be labeled with its position/depth in the chain (e.g., \"Depth 0 (Instance Schema):\", \"Depth 1 (Ref Schema):\")\n+- **AND** schemas SHALL be pretty-printed as JSON\n+\n+### Requirement: Circular Reference Protection\n+\n+The system SHALL handle circular references in schema chains gracefully during diagnostic logging.\n+\n+#### Scenario: Circular schema reference handling\n+\n+- **GIVEN** a schema chain that contains circular references (e.g., A refs B, B refs A)\n+- **WHEN** logging the schema chain\n+- **THEN** the system SHALL detect the cycle using a visited set of IDs\n+- **AND** the system SHALL stop traversal for that branch\n+- **AND** the system SHALL log a warning indicating a cycle was detected (e.g., \"Cycle detected at ID: ...\")\n+- **AND** the system SHALL NOT enter an infinite loop\n+","path":"modules/system/types-registry/openspec/changes/archive/2026-01-21-add-gts-registration-debug-logging/specs/types-registry/spec.md","commit_id":"cfd76fb9303e2de3d140c010b92ca451e2dc982d","original_commit_id":"cfd76fb9303e2de3d140c010b92ca451e2dc982d","user":{"login":"coderabbitai[bot]","id":136622811,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOCCSy2w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/347564?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/coderabbitai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"_⚠️ Potential issue_ | _🟡 Minor_\n\n**Clarify cycle-detection log level to avoid conflicting requirements.**\n\nThis section says to “log a warning,” while the next requirement enforces debug-only diagnostics. Consider explicitly stating the cycle notice is emitted at debug level to keep requirements aligned.\n\n<details>\n<summary>✏️ Suggested wording tweak</summary>\n\n```diff\n- - **THEN** the system SHALL log a warning indicating a cycle was detected (e.g., \"Cycle detected at ID: ...\")\n+ - **THEN** the system SHALL emit a debug-level log message indicating a cycle was detected (e.g., \"Cycle detected at ID: ...\")\n```\n</details>\n\n<!-- suggestion_start -->\n\n<details>\n<summary>📝 Committable suggestion</summary>\n\n> ‼️ **IMPORTANT**\n> Carefully review the code before committing. Ensure that it accurately replaces the highlighted code, contains no missing lines, and has no issues with indentation. Thoroughly test & benchmark the code to ensure it meets the requirements.\n\n```suggestion\n### Requirement: Circular Reference Protection\n\nThe system SHALL handle circular references in schema chains gracefully during diagnostic logging.\n\n#### Scenario: Circular schema reference handling\n\n- **GIVEN** a schema chain that contains circular references (e.g., A refs B, B refs A)\n- **WHEN** logging the schema chain\n- **THEN** the system SHALL detect the cycle using a visited set of IDs\n- **AND** the system SHALL stop traversal for that branch\n- **AND** the system SHALL emit a debug-level log message indicating a cycle was detected (e.g., \"Cycle detected at ID: ...\")\n- **AND** the system SHALL NOT enter an infinite loop\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- suggestion_end -->\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nIn\n`@modules/system/types-registry/openspec/changes/archive/2026-01-21-add-gts-registration-debug-logging/specs/types-registry/spec.md`\naround lines 37 - 49, Update the \"Circular Reference Protection\" requirement and\nthe \"Scenario: Circular schema reference handling\" text so the cycle detection\nlogging level matches the debug-only diagnostics requirement: replace the phrase\n\"log a warning indicating a cycle was detected\" with wording that the system\nSHALL emit a debug-level message (e.g., \"Cycle detected at ID: ...\") and ensure\nthe traversal stop and visited-set behavior remain described; reference the\nrequirement name \"Circular Reference Protection\" and the scenario header\n\"Circular schema reference handling\" when making the change.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- fingerprinting:phantom:medusa:eagle -->\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment by CodeRabbit -->","created_at":"2026-01-23T10:14:14Z","updated_at":"2026-01-23T10:14:15Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/293#discussion_r2720584025","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/293","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2720584025"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/293#discussion_r2720584025"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/293"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2720584025/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":37,"original_start_line":37,"start_side":"RIGHT","line":49,"original_line":49,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","original_position":49,"position":49,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2720584033","pull_request_review_id":3696792008,"id":2720584033,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs6iKNFh","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,439 @@\n+\"\"\"E2E tests for GTS registration debug logging.\n+\n+These tests verify that debug-level logging is emitted when GTS entity\n+registration fails. The tests trigger validation failures and verify\n+the expected debug log output is present in the log file.\n+\n+The server must be configured with types_registry logging at debug level:\n+  logging:\n+    types_registry:\n+      file: \"logs/types-registry.log\"\n+      file_level: debug\n+\"\"\"\n+import httpx\n+import os\n+import pytest\n+import time\n+from pathlib import Path\n+\n+_counter = int(time.time() * 1000) % 1000000\n+\n+# Path to the server error log file (where debug logs are written)\n+# The server writes to logs/types-registry.log based on config/e2e-local.yaml\n+LOG_FILE_PATH = Path(__file__).parent.parent.parent.parent.parent / \"logs\" / \"types-registry.log\"\n+\n+\n+def get_log_content() -> str:\n+    \"\"\"Read the server error log file content.\"\"\"\n+    if LOG_FILE_PATH.exists():\n+        return LOG_FILE_PATH.read_text()\n+    return \"\"\n+\n+\n+def get_log_lines_after(marker: str, content: str) -> list[str]:\n+    \"\"\"Get log lines that appear after a specific marker in the log content.\"\"\"\n+    lines = content.split('\\n')\n+    found_marker = False\n+    result = []\n+    for line in lines:\n+        if marker in line:\n+            found_marker = True\n+        if found_marker:\n+            result.append(line)\n+    return result\n+\n+\n+def unique_type_id(name: str) -> str:\n+    \"\"\"Generate a unique type GTS ID.\"\"\"\n+    global _counter\n+    _counter += 1\n+    return f\"gts.e2etest.debuglog.models.{name}{_counter}.v1~\"\n+\n+\n+def make_schema_id(gts_id: str) -> str:\n+    return \"gts://\" + gts_id\n+\n+\n+def unique_instance_id(type_id: str, name: str) -> str:\n+    \"\"\"Generate a unique instance GTS ID based on a type ID.\"\"\"\n+    global _counter\n+    _counter += 1\n+    return f\"{type_id}e2etest.debuglog.inst.{name}{_counter}.v1\"\n+\n+\n+@pytest.mark.asyncio\n+async def test_debug_log_invalid_schema_registration(base_url, auth_headers):\n+    \"\"\"\n+    Test that registering an invalid schema emits debug logs with schema content.\n+    \n+    Verifies debug log output contains:\n+    - GTS ID of the schema being registered\n+    - Complete schema JSON (pretty-printed)\n+    - Validation error message\n+    \"\"\"\n+    type_id = unique_type_id(\"invalid_schema\")\n+    \n+    # Record log position before request\n+    log_before = get_log_content()\n+    \n+    async with httpx.AsyncClient(timeout=10.0) as client:\n+        payload = {\n+            \"entities\": [\n+                {\n+                    \"$id\": make_schema_id(type_id),\n+                    \"$schema\": \"http://json-schema.org/draft-07/schema#\",\n+                    \"type\": \"invalid_type_value\",\n+                    \"properties\": {\n+                        \"name\": {\"type\": \"also_invalid\"}\n+                    }\n+                }\n+            ]\n+        }\n+        \n+        response = await client.post(\n+            f\"{base_url}/types-registry/v1/entities\",\n+            headers=auth_headers,\n+            json=payload,\n+        )\n+        \n+        if response.status_code in (401, 403) and not auth_headers:\n+            pytest.skip(\n+                f\"Endpoint requires authentication (got {response.status_code}). \"\n+                \"Set E2E_AUTH_TOKEN environment variable to run this test.\"\n+            )\n+        \n+        assert response.status_code == 200\n+        data = response.json()\n+        results = data[\"results\"]\n+        \n+        # Give server a moment to flush logs\n+        time.sleep(0.1)\n+        \n+        # Read log content after request\n+        log_after = get_log_content()\n+        new_logs = log_after[len(log_before):]\n+        \n+        # Verify debug logs contain expected content when debug level is enabled\n+        # Note: Debug logs only appear if RUST_LOG=types_registry=debug is set\n+        if new_logs and results[0][\"status\"] == \"error\":\n+            # Check if debug logging is enabled (look for DEBUG level messages from types_registry)\n+            debug_enabled = \"DEBUG\" in new_logs and \"types_registry\" in new_logs\n+            if debug_enabled:\n+                # Verify GTS ID is logged\n+                assert type_id in new_logs or type_id.rstrip('~') in new_logs, \\\n+                    f\"Expected GTS ID '{type_id}' in debug logs\"\n+                # Verify schema content keywords are present\n+                assert \"invalid_type_value\" in new_logs, \\\n+                    \"Expected schema content 'invalid_type_value' in debug logs\"\n+            # Test passes if validation error was detected (debug logs are optional)\n+\n+\n+@pytest.mark.asyncio\n+async def test_debug_log_instance_schema_mismatch(base_url, auth_headers):\n+    \"\"\"\n+    Test that instance validation failure emits debug logs with instance and schema.\n+    \n+    Verifies debug log output contains:\n+    - Instance JSON (pretty-printed)\n+    - Instance's schema JSON (if found)\n+    - GTS ID of the instance\n+    - Schema chain with depth labels\n+    \"\"\"\n+    type_id = unique_type_id(\"person\")\n+    instance_id = unique_instance_id(type_id, \"person1\")\n+    \n+    # Record log position before request\n+    log_before = get_log_content()\n+    \n+    async with httpx.AsyncClient(timeout=10.0) as client:\n+        payload = {\n+            \"entities\": [\n+                {\n+                    \"$id\": make_schema_id(type_id),\n+                    \"$schema\": \"http://json-schema.org/draft-07/schema#\",\n+                    \"type\": \"object\",\n+                    \"properties\": {\n+                        \"name\": {\"type\": \"string\"},\n+                        \"age\": {\"type\": \"integer\"}\n+                    },\n+                    \"required\": [\"name\", \"age\"]\n+                },\n+                {\n+                    \"id\": instance_id,\n+                    \"name\": \"John\",\n+                    \"age\": \"not_a_number\"\n+                }\n+            ]\n+        }\n+        \n+        response = await client.post(\n+            f\"{base_url}/types-registry/v1/entities\",\n+            headers=auth_headers,\n+            json=payload,\n+        )\n+        \n+        if response.status_code in (401, 403) and not auth_headers:\n+            pytest.skip(\n+                f\"Endpoint requires authentication (got {response.status_code}). \"\n+                \"Set E2E_AUTH_TOKEN environment variable to run this test.\"\n+            )\n+        \n+        assert response.status_code == 200\n+        data = response.json()\n+        results = data[\"results\"]\n+        \n+        # Give server a moment to flush logs\n+        time.sleep(0.1)\n+        \n+        # Read log content after request\n+        log_after = get_log_content()\n+        new_logs = log_after[len(log_before):]\n+        \n+        # Schema should register successfully\n+        assert results[0][\"status\"] == \"ok\", \"Type should register successfully\"\n+        \n+        # Instance should fail validation due to wrong type for 'age'\n+        if new_logs and results[1][\"status\"] == \"error\":\n+            assert \"error\" in results[1]\n+            # Check if debug logging is enabled\n+            debug_enabled = \"DEBUG\" in new_logs and \"types_registry\" in new_logs\n+            if debug_enabled:\n+                # Verify instance content is logged\n+                assert \"not_a_number\" in new_logs, \\\n+                    \"Expected instance content 'not_a_number' in debug logs\"\n+                # Verify GTS ID is logged\n+                assert instance_id in new_logs or type_id in new_logs, \\\n+                    f\"Expected GTS ID in debug logs\"\n+            # Test passes if validation error was detected (debug logs are optional)\n+\n+\n+@pytest.mark.asyncio\n+async def test_debug_log_schema_chain_with_refs(base_url, auth_headers):\n+    \"\"\"\n+    Test that multi-level schema chain is logged with depth labels.\n+    \n+    Verifies debug log output contains:\n+    - \"Depth 0 (Instance Schema):\" followed by the direct schema\n+    - \"Depth 1 (Ref Schema):\" for each parent schema\n+    - All schemas pretty-printed as JSON\n+    \"\"\"\n+    base_type_id = unique_type_id(\"base_entity\")\n+    derived_type_id = unique_type_id(\"derived_entity\")\n+    instance_id = unique_instance_id(derived_type_id, \"entity1\")\n+    \n+    # Record log position before request\n+    log_before = get_log_content()\n+    \n+    async with httpx.AsyncClient(timeout=10.0) as client:\n+        payload = {\n+            \"entities\": [\n+                {\n+                    \"$id\": make_schema_id(base_type_id),\n+                    \"$schema\": \"http://json-schema.org/draft-07/schema#\",\n+                    \"type\": \"object\",\n+                    \"properties\": {\n+                        \"id\": {\"type\": \"string\"},\n+                        \"createdAt\": {\"type\": \"string\", \"format\": \"date-time\"}\n+                    },\n+                    \"required\": [\"id\"]\n+                },\n+                {\n+                    \"$id\": make_schema_id(derived_type_id),\n+                    \"$schema\": \"http://json-schema.org/draft-07/schema#\",\n+                    \"allOf\": [\n+                        {\"$ref\": make_schema_id(base_type_id)},\n+                        {\n+                            \"type\": \"object\",\n+                            \"properties\": {\n+                                \"name\": {\"type\": \"string\"}\n+                            },\n+                            \"required\": [\"name\"]\n+                        }\n+                    ]\n+                },\n+                {\n+                    \"id\": instance_id,\n+                    \"name\": \"Test Entity\"\n+                }\n+            ]\n+        }\n+        \n+        response = await client.post(\n+            f\"{base_url}/types-registry/v1/entities\",\n+            headers=auth_headers,\n+            json=payload,\n+        )\n+        \n+        if response.status_code in (401, 403) and not auth_headers:\n+            pytest.skip(\n+                f\"Endpoint requires authentication (got {response.status_code}). \"\n+                \"Set E2E_AUTH_TOKEN environment variable to run this test.\"\n+            )\n+        \n+        assert response.status_code == 200\n+        data = response.json()\n+        results = data[\"results\"]\n+        \n+        # Give server a moment to flush logs\n+        time.sleep(0.1)\n+        \n+        # Read log content after request\n+        log_after = get_log_content()\n+        new_logs = log_after[len(log_before):]\n+        \n+        # Both schemas should register successfully\n+        assert results[0][\"status\"] == \"ok\", \"Base type should register\"\n+        assert results[1][\"status\"] == \"ok\", \"Derived type should register\"\n+        \n+        # Instance is missing 'id' required by base schema\n+        if new_logs and results[2][\"status\"] == \"error\":\n+            assert \"error\" in results[2]\n+            # Check if debug logging is enabled\n+            debug_enabled = \"DEBUG\" in new_logs and \"types_registry\" in new_logs\n+            if debug_enabled:\n+                # Verify depth labels are logged for schema chain\n+                assert \"Depth 0\" in new_logs or \"Instance Schema\" in new_logs, \\\n+                    \"Expected 'Depth 0' or 'Instance Schema' label in debug logs\"\n+                # Verify both schema IDs appear in logs\n+                assert derived_type_id in new_logs or base_type_id in new_logs, \\\n+                    \"Expected schema IDs in debug logs for schema chain\"\n+            # Test passes if validation error was detected (debug logs are optional)\n+\n+\n+@pytest.mark.asyncio  \n+async def test_debug_logs_present_at_debug_level(base_url, auth_headers):\n+    \"\"\"\n+    Test that debug logs ARE emitted when server is configured with debug level.\n+    \n+    This test triggers a validation failure and verifies that debug\n+    diagnostic logs appear in the log file when file_level is set to debug.\n+    \"\"\"\n+    type_id = unique_type_id(\"debug_level_test\")\n+    \n+    # Record log position before request\n+    log_before = get_log_content()\n+    \n+    async with httpx.AsyncClient(timeout=10.0) as client:\n+        payload = {\n+            \"entities\": [\n+                {\n+                    \"$id\": make_schema_id(type_id),\n+                    \"$schema\": \"http://json-schema.org/draft-07/schema#\",\n+                    \"type\": \"invalid_type\"\n+                }\n+            ]\n+        }\n+        \n+        response = await client.post(\n+            f\"{base_url}/types-registry/v1/entities\",\n+            headers=auth_headers,\n+            json=payload,\n+        )\n+        \n+        if response.status_code in (401, 403) and not auth_headers:\n+            pytest.skip(\n+                f\"Endpoint requires authentication (got {response.status_code}). \"\n+                \"Set E2E_AUTH_TOKEN environment variable to run this test.\"\n+            )\n+        \n+        assert response.status_code == 200\n+        data = response.json()\n+        \n+        # Give server a moment to flush logs\n+        time.sleep(0.1)\n+        \n+        # Read log content after request\n+        log_after = get_log_content()\n+        new_logs = log_after[len(log_before):]\n+        \n+        assert \"results\" in data\n+        \n+        # If validation failed and log file exists with new content,\n+        # verify debug output is present when debug level is enabled\n+        if new_logs and data[\"results\"][0][\"status\"] == \"error\":\n+            # Check if debug logging is enabled\n+            debug_enabled = \"DEBUG\" in new_logs and \"types_registry\" in new_logs\n+            if debug_enabled:\n+                # Debug logs should contain the GTS ID or error info\n+                assert type_id in new_logs or \"invalid_type\" in new_logs, \\\n+                    \"Expected debug log content when file_level is debug\"\n+            # Test passes if validation error was detected (debug logs are optional)","path":"testing/e2e/modules/types_registry/test_registration_debug_logging.py","commit_id":"cfd76fb9303e2de3d140c010b92ca451e2dc982d","original_commit_id":"cfd76fb9303e2de3d140c010b92ca451e2dc982d","user":{"login":"coderabbitai[bot]","id":136622811,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOCCSy2w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/347564?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/coderabbitai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"_⚠️ Potential issue_ | _🟡 Minor_\n\n**Make the debug-level presence test assert when logs are missing.**\n\nRight now the check is gated by `new_logs`, so the test can pass even if debug logs never appear. Consider failing or explicitly skipping when logs are expected but absent.\n\n<details>\n<summary>✅ Suggested adjustment</summary>\n\n```diff\n-        if new_logs and data[\"results\"][0][\"status\"] == \"error\":\n-            # Check if debug logging is enabled\n-            debug_enabled = \"DEBUG\" in new_logs and \"types_registry\" in new_logs\n-            if debug_enabled:\n-                # Debug logs should contain the GTS ID or error info\n-                assert type_id in new_logs or \"invalid_type\" in new_logs, \\\n-                    \"Expected debug log content when file_level is debug\"\n-            # Test passes if validation error was detected (debug logs are optional)\n+        if data[\"results\"][0][\"status\"] == \"error\":\n+            if not new_logs:\n+                pytest.skip(\n+                    \"Debug logs not found; ensure types_registry file_level=debug and \"\n+                    \"RUST_LOG enables types_registry=debug\"\n+                )\n+            debug_enabled = \"DEBUG\" in new_logs and \"types_registry\" in new_logs\n+            assert debug_enabled, \"Expected types_registry debug logs to be enabled\"\n+            assert type_id in new_logs or \"invalid_type\" in new_logs, \\\n+                \"Expected debug log content when file_level is debug\"\n```\n</details>\n\n<!-- suggestion_start -->\n\n<details>\n<summary>📝 Committable suggestion</summary>\n\n> ‼️ **IMPORTANT**\n> Carefully review the code before committing. Ensure that it accurately replaces the highlighted code, contains no missing lines, and has no issues with indentation. Thoroughly test & benchmark the code to ensure it meets the requirements.\n\n```suggestion\n        # If validation failed and log file exists with new content,\n        # verify debug output is present when debug level is enabled\n        if data[\"results\"][0][\"status\"] == \"error\":\n            if not new_logs:\n                pytest.skip(\n                    \"Debug logs not found; ensure types_registry file_level=debug and \"\n                    \"RUST_LOG enables types_registry=debug\"\n                )\n            debug_enabled = \"DEBUG\" in new_logs and \"types_registry\" in new_logs\n            assert debug_enabled, \"Expected types_registry debug logs to be enabled\"\n            assert type_id in new_logs or \"invalid_type\" in new_logs, \\\n                \"Expected debug log content when file_level is debug\"\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- suggestion_end -->\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nIn `@testing/e2e/modules/types_registry/test_registration_debug_logging.py` around\nlines 351 - 360, The test currently skips asserting debug output when new_logs\nis empty; change it so that when a validation error is detected\n(data[\"results\"][0][\"status\"] == \"error\") and the test expects debug-level\nlogging, it must assert new_logs is present (fail with a clear message if empty)\nbefore checking contents; then keep the existing check that new_logs contains\neither type_id or \"invalid_type\". Use the existing symbols new_logs,\ndata[\"results\"][0][\"status\"], and type_id to locate and implement the assertion\nand adjust the flow so missing logs cause test failure rather than silently\npassing.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- fingerprinting:phantom:medusa:eagle -->\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment by CodeRabbit -->","created_at":"2026-01-23T10:14:14Z","updated_at":"2026-01-23T10:14:15Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/293#discussion_r2720584033","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/293","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2720584033"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/293#discussion_r2720584033"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/293"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2720584033/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":351,"original_start_line":351,"start_side":"RIGHT","line":360,"original_line":360,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","original_position":360,"position":360,"subject_type":"line"}],"source_reviews":[{"id":3691460165,"node_id":"PRR_kwDOPaLyBs7cBzZF","user":{"login":"coderabbitai[bot]","id":136622811,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOCCSy2w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/347564?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/coderabbitai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}