/modules/types_registry/test_registration_debug_logging.py (1)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`205-206`: **Remove extraneous f-string prefix (already noted).**\n\n<details>\n<summary>🧹 Suggested cleanup</summary>\n\n```diff\n-                assert instance_id in new_logs or type_id in new_logs, \\\n-                    f\"Expected GTS ID in debug logs\"\n+                assert instance_id in new_logs or type_id in new_logs, \\\n+                    \"Expected GTS ID in debug logs\"\n```\n</details>\n\n</blockquote></details>\n\n</blockquote></details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>🧹 Nitpick comments (2)</summary><blockquote>\n\n<details>\n<summary>apps/gts-docs-validator/src/scanner.rs (1)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`35-49`: **Remove the duplicate `file_name` match.**\n\nLines 38-41 already check `file_name`; the added block (Line 45-49) repeats the same condition, adding noise and extra work. If you intended to match any path component, consider iterating components instead.\n\n\n\n<details>\n<summary>♻️ Suggested cleanup</summary>\n\n```diff\n-        // Also try matching just the file/dir name\n-        if let Some(name) = path.file_name()\n-            && pattern.matches(&name.to_string_lossy())\n-        {\n-            return true;\n-        }\n```\n</details>\n\n</blockquote></details>\n<details>\n<summary>scripts/ci.py (1)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`332-343`: **Preserve existing `RUST_LOG` when enabling `types_registry` debug.**\n\nOverwriting can drop user-set filters (e.g., `sqlx=debug`). Consider appending the module filter when `RUST_LOG` is already set.\n\n<details>\n<summary>♻️ Suggested change</summary>\n\n```diff\n                 # Set RUST_LOG to enable debug logging for types_registry module\n                 server_env = os.environ.copy()\n-                server_env[\"RUST_LOG\"] = \"types_registry=debug,info\"\n+                existing_rust_log = server_env.get(\"RUST_LOG\")\n+                if existing_rust_log:\n+                    if \"types_registry=debug\" not in existing_rust_log:\n+                        server_env[\"RUST_LOG\"] = f\"{existing_rust_log},types_registry=debug\"\n+                else:\n+                    server_env[\"RUST_LOG\"] = \"types_registry=debug,info\"\n```\n</details>\n\n</blockquote></details>\n\n</blockquote></details>\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment by CodeRabbit for review status -->","state":"COMMENTED","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/293#pullrequestreview-3696792008","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/293","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","_links":{"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/293#pullrequestreview-3696792008"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/293"}},"submitted_at":"2026-01-23T10:14:15Z","commit_id":"cfd76fb9303e2de3d140c010b92ca451e2dc982d"}]},{"source_pr_number":292,"source_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/292","source_state":"closed","source_author":"QuietSyscall","target_issue_number":null,"title":"[PR #292] tech(parsing): replace serde_yaml with serde_saphyr","status":"exported","mirrored_at":null,"comments_status":"none","comments_mirrored":0,"pr_head_ref":"yaml","pr_head_sha":"61d5845dce87794b4f7a227fac59bc9f0df7bdee","pr_base_ref":"main","pr_head_owner":"QuietSyscall","pr_from_fork":1,"source_data":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/292","id":3195776886,"node_id":"PR_kwDOPaLyBs6-e692","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/292","diff_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/292.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/292.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/issues/292","number":292,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"tech(parsing): replace serde_yaml with serde_saphyr","user":{"login":"QuietSyscall","id":248649801,"node_i