ted_at":"2026-01-21T15:51:44Z","body":"<!-- This is an auto-generated comment: summarize by coderabbit.ai -->\n<!-- walkthrough_start -->\n\n<details>\n<summary>📝 Walkthrough</summary>\n\n## Walkthrough\n\nThe pull request migrates YAML serialization dependencies across the codebase from the unmaintained serde_yaml to serde-saphyr. This includes removing serde_yaml from multiple Cargo.toml files, updating code to use serde_saphyr APIs, and introducing a new DEPENDENCIES.md guideline document explaining the migration rationale and usage patterns.\n\n## Changes\n\n| Cohort / File(s) | Summary |\n|---|---|\n| **Dependency Migration** <br> `Cargo.toml`, `libs/modkit/Cargo.toml`, `apps/hyperspot-server/Cargo.toml` | Removed serde_yaml dependency from main Cargo.toml and modkit workspace dependencies; replaced serde_yaml with serde-saphyr in hyperspot-server dev-dependencies. Bootstrap feature in modkit no longer includes serde_yaml. |\n| **Code Updates** <br> `libs/modkit/src/bootstrap/config/dump.rs`, `apps/hyperspot-server/tests/cli_smoke_tests.rs` | Updated YAML serialization/deserialization calls from serde_yaml to serde_saphyr; test now uses HashMap<String, serde_json::Value> instead of serde_yaml::Value for parsing. |\n| **Documentation** <br> `guidelines/DEPENDENCIES.md`, `guidelines/README.md`, `AGENTS.md` | Added new DEPENDENCIES.md guideline detailing preferred libraries (mandating serde-saphyr over serde_yaml); updated README.md and AGENTS.md to reference the new guidelines file. |\n\n## Estimated code review effort\n\n🎯 3 (Moderate) | ⏱️ ~20 minutes\n\n## Poem\n\n> 🐰 *A hop and a skip from YAML old,*  \n> *We've swapped out the rust—or so we're told,*  \n> *To saphyr streams, more fresh and new,*  \n> *Dependencies replaced, the code shines true!* ✨\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- walkthrough_end -->\n\n\n<!-- pre_merge_checks_walkthrough_start -->\n\n<details>\n<summary>🚥 Pre-merge checks | ✅ 3</summary>\n\n<details>\n<summary>✅ Passed checks (3 passed)</summary>\n\n|     Check name     | Status   | Explanation                                                                                                                                                                                       |\n| :----------------: | :------- | :------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ |\n|  Description Check | ✅ Passed | Check skipped - CodeRabbit’s high-level summary is enabled.                                                                                                                                       |\n|     Title check    | ✅ Passed | The pull request title accurately summarizes the main change: replacing the serde_yaml dependency with serde_saphyr across multiple files including Cargo.toml, tests, and configuration modules. |\n| Docstring Coverage | ✅ Passed | Docstring coverage is 100.00% which is sufficient. The required threshold is 80.00%.                                                                                                              |\n\n</details>\n\n<sub>✏️ Tip: You can configure your own custom pre-merge checks in the settings.</sub>\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- pre_merge_checks_walkthrough_end -->\n\n<!-- finishing_touch_checkbox_start -->\n\n<details>\n<summary>✨ Finishing touches</summary>\n\n- [ ] <!-- {\"checkboxId\": \"7962f53c-55bc-4827-bfbf-6a18da830691\"} --> 📝 Generate docstrings\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- finishing_touch_checkbox_end -->\n\n<!-- tips_start -->\n\n---\n\n\n\n<sub>Comment `@coderabbitai help` to get the list of available commands and usage tips.</sub>\n\n<!-- tips_end -->\n\n<!-- internal state start -->\n\n\n<!--  -->\n\n<!-- internal state end -->","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/issues/comments/3779025353/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"c