api.github.com/users/MikeFalcon77/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MikeFalcon77/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-02-23T15:56:40Z","updated_at":"2026-02-23T15:56:40Z","body":"Probably not for PR creatore but common issue:\r\n\r\nThese changes introduce for every module now has 20+ lines per error type:\r\n\r\n#[struct_to_gts_schema(\r\n    dir_path = \"schemas\",\r\n    schema_id = \"gts.cf.core.errors.err.v1~cf.file_parser.errors.file_not_found.v1~\",\r\n    description = \"File not found\",\r\n    properties = \"path\",\r\n    base = BaseErrorV1,\r\n)]\r\n#[derive(Debug)]\r\npub struct FileNotFoundV1 {\r\n    pub path: String,\r\n}\r\n\r\nimpl GtsError for FileNotFoundV1 {\r\n    const STATUS: u16 = 404;\r\n    const TITLE: &'static str = \"File Not Found\";\r\n}\r\n\r\nThis is ~15 lines per error, repeated 40+ times (in this PR). The old macro-based approach had its own problems, but this is a LOT of boilerplate. A #[derive(GtsError)] macro that reads STATUS and TITLE from attributes would cut this in half:\r\n\r\n#[derive(Debug, GtsError)]\r\n#[gts_error(status = 404, title = \"File Not Found\")]\r\n#[struct_to_gts_schema(...)]\r\npub struct FileNotFoundV1 {\r\n    pub path: String,\r\n}\r\n\r\n@Artifizer  please take a look","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/issues/comments/3945656070/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/issues/comments/3950149413","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/290#issuecomment-3950149413","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/issues/290","id":3950149413,"node_id":"IC_kwDOPaLyBs7rcn8l","user":{"login":"github-actions[bot]","id":41898282,"node_id":"MDM