IBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/issues/comments/4016534537/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":{"id":15368,"client_id":"Iv1.05c79e9ad1f6bdfa","slug":"github-actions","node_id":"MDM6QXBwMTUzNjg=","owner":{"login":"github","id":9919,"node_id":"MDEyOk9yZ2FuaXphdGlvbjk5MTk=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/9919?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/github","html_url":"https://github.com/github","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github/received_events","type":"Organization","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"name":"GitHub Actions","description":"Automate your workflow from idea to production","external_url":"https://help.github.com/en/actions","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/github-actions","created_at":"2018-07-30T09:30:17Z","updated_at":"2026-05-05T14:51:38Z","permissions":{"actions":"write","administration":"read","artifact_metadata":"write","attestations":"write","checks":"write","code_quality":"write","contents":"write","copilot_requests":"write","deployments":"write","discussions":"write","issues":"write","merge_queues":"write","metadata":"read","models":"read","packages":"write","pages":"write","pull_requests":"write","repository_hooks":"write","repository_projects":"write","security_events":"write","statuses":"write","vulnerability_alerts":"read"},"events":["branch_protection_rule","check_run","check_suite","create","delete","deployment","deployment_status","discussion","discussion_comment","fork","gollum","issues","issue_comment","label","merge_group","milestone","page_build","public","pull_request","pull_request_review","pull_request_review_comment","push","registry_package","release","repository","repository_dispatch","status","watch","workflow_dispatch","workflow_run"]}}],"source_review_comments":[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2711942476","pull_request_review_id":3686469565,"id":2711942476,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs6hpPVM","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,417 @@\n+# GTS Error System Documentation\n+\n+This document describes how errors are defined, structured, transformed, and used in the Hyperspot/gts-rust project.\n+\n+## Overview\n+\n+The error system follows **RFC 9457 Problem Details for HTTP APIs** and uses a **GTS (Global Type System)** format for error codes. The system provides:\n+\n+- **Compile-time validated** error catalogs via JSON files\n+- **Type-safe** error code enums generated by proc-macros\n+- **Layered error transformation** from domain → API → HTTP response\n+- **Consistent error format** across all modules\n+\n+## Architecture\n+\n+```\n+┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n+│                           Error Flow                                     │\n+├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n+│                                                                          │\n+│  gts/errors.json  ──────►  declare_errors! macro  ──────►  ErrorCode    │\n+│  (Source of Truth)         (Compile-time)                  (Enum)       │\n+│                                                                          │\n+│  DomainError  ──────►  ErrorCode::xxx().with_context()  ──────►  Problem│\n+│  (Business Logic)      (Mapping Layer)                        (RFC 9457)│\n+│                                                                          │\n+│  Problem  ──────►  IntoResponse (Axum)  ──────►  HTTP Response          │\n+│  (Data)            (Framework Integration)       (JSON + Headers)       │\n+│                                                                          │\n+└─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘\n+```\n+\n+## Components\n+\n+### 1. Error Catalog JSON (`gts/errors.json`)\n+\n+The source of truth for error definitions. Located in each module's `gts/` directory.\n+\n+**File Location Pattern:** `<module>/gts/errors.json`\n+\n+**Schema:**\n+```json\n+[\n+  {\n+    \"status\": 404,\n+    \"title\": \"User Not Found\",\n+    \"code\": \"gts.hx.core.errors.err.v1~hx.example1.user.not_found.v1\",\n+    \"type\": \"https://errors.example.com/...\",  // optional\n+    \"alias\": \"user_not_found\"                   // optional\n+  }\n+]\n+```\n+\n+**Fields:**\n+| Field | Required | Description |\n+|-------|----------|-------------|\n+| `status` | Yes | HTTP status code (100-599) |\n+| `title` | Yes | Human-readable error title |\n+| `code` | Yes | GTS-formatted error code |\n+| `type` | No | URI for error documentation |\n+| `alias` | No | Short name override for generated accessor |\n+\n+### 2. GTS Code Format\n+\n+GTS codes follow a strict format for global type identification:\n+\n+```\n+gts.vendor.package.namespace.type.version~chain1~chain2~...~instanceGTX\n+```\n+\n+**Structure:**\n+- **Prefix:** Always starts with `gts.`\n+- **Chain separator:** `~` separates GTX segments\n+- **Segment separator:** `.` separates parts within a GTX\n+- **Final GTX:** Must have at least 5 segments: `vendor.package.namespace.type.version`\n+- **Version:** Must end with `vN` or `vN.M` format\n+\n+**Example Breakdown:**\n+```\n+gts.hx.core.errors.err.v1~hx.example1.user.not_found.v1\n+│   │  │    │      │   │  │  │        │    │         │\n+│   │  │    │      │   │  │  │        │    │         └─ version\n+│   │  │    │      │   │  │  │        │    └─ type (not_found)\n+│   │  │    │      │   │  │  │        └─ namespace (user)\n+│   │  │    │      │   │  │  └─ package (example1)\n+│   │  │    │      │   │  └─ vendor (hx)\n+│   │  │    │      │   └─ version\n+│   │  │    │      └─ type (err)\n+│   │  │    └─ namespace (errors)\n+│   │  └─ package (core)\n+│   └─ vendor (hx)\n+└─ prefix\n+```\n+\n+**Validation Rules:**\n+1. Must start with `gts.`\n+2. All segments must be lowercase alphanumeric or underscore\n+3. No empty segments allowed\n+4. Final GTX must have ≥5 segments after vendor","path":"docs/GTS_ERRORS.md","commit_id":"5bdb0f43b25858af78999718f7247813802b9634","original_commit_id":"5bdb0f43b25858af78999718f7247813802b9634","user":{"login":"graphite-app[bot]","id":96075541,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOBbn_FQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/158384?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/graphite-app%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/graphite-app","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/graphite-app%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/graphite-app%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/graphite-app%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/graphite-app%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/graphite-app%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/graphite-app%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/graphite-app%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/graphite-app%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/graphite-app%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"**Contradictory validation rules for GTX segments**\n\nLine 74 states: \"Must have at least 5 segments: `vendor.package.namespace.type.version`\" (5 segments total)\n\nLine 99 states: \"Final GTX must have ≥5 segments after vendor\" (≥6 segments total)\n\nThese rules are mathematically inconsistent. Based on the example at line 80 (`hx.example1.user.not_found.v1` = 5 total segments), the correct rule should be:\n\n```\n4. Final GTX must have ≥5 segments total (vendor.package.namespace.type.version)\n```\n\nOr alternatively:\n\n```\n4. Final GTX must have ≥4 segments after vendor\n```\n\nImplementing validation based on \"≥5 segments after vendor\" would incorrectly reject valid GTS IDs shown throughout the documentation.\n\n*Spotted by [Graphite Agent](https://app.graphite.com/diamond/?org=hypernetix&ref=ai-review-comment)*<i class='graphite__hidden'><br /><br /><a href=\"https://app.graphite.com/github/pr/hypernetix/hyperspot/290?chatWithGeneratedComment=072f3f84-3aaa-47d7-af7e-eaac34838f15\"><picture><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\" srcset=\"https://static.graphite.dev/github-diamond-fix-in-graphite-dark.svg\"><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\" srcset=\"https://static.graphite.dev/github-diamond-fix-in-graphite-light.svg\"><img alt=\"Fix in Graphite\" src=\"https://static.graphite.dev/github-diamond-fix-in-graphite-dark.svg\"></picture></a></i><i class='graphite__hidden'><br /><br />Is this helpful? React 👍 or 👎 to let us know.</i>","created_at":"2026-01-21T10:29:49Z","updated_at":"2026-01-21T10:29:53Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/290#discussion_r2711942476","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/290","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2711942476"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/290#discussion_r2711942476"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/290"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2711942476/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":0,"-1":1,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":74,"start_side":"RIGHT","line":null,"original_line":99,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","original_position":99,"position":1,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2711942595","pull_request_review_id":3686469565,"id":2711942595,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs6hpPXD","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,1574 @@\n+# Unified Error System - Intention Document\n+\n+This document defines the architecture, rules, and implementation plan for a unified error handling system across the Hyperspot project. All REST API errors MUST have a GTS identifier, trace ID, and be registered in the types registry.\n+\n+## Table of Contents\n+\n+1. [Executive Summary](#executive-summary)\n+2. [Industry Research](#industry-research)\n+3. [Current State Analysis](#current-state-analysis)\n+4. [Requirements](#requirements)\n+5. [Implementation Rules](#implementation-rules)\n+6. [Migration Plan](#migration-plan)\n+7. [Examples](#examples)\n+8. [HTTP Headers](#http-headers)\n+9. [Security Considerations](#security-considerations)\n+10. [Appendix A: Error Category Definitions](#appendix-a-error-category-definitions)\n+11. [Appendix B: Retryable Error Guidelines](#appendix-b-retryable-error-guidelines)\n+12. [GTS System Errors Catalog](#gts-system-errors-catalog)\n+13. [References](#references)\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Executive Summary\n+\n+### Problem Statement\n+\n+The current error handling across Hyperspot modules is inconsistent:\n+- Some modules use `declare_errors!` macro with JSON catalogs\n+- Others define errors inline without GTS codes\n+- Errors are not registered in the types registry\n+- No standardized metadata/context fields\n+- Inconsistent trace ID propagation\n+\n+### Goals\n+\n+1. **Every REST API error** MUST have a valid GTS identifier\n+2. **Every error response** MUST include a trace ID for debugging\n+3. **All error types** MUST be registered in the types registry\n+4. **Consistent error schema** across all modules following RFC 9457\n+5. **Machine-readable error codes** for programmatic handling\n+6. **Error stack propagation** for nested service calls\n+\n+### Non-Goals\n+\n+- Changing internal domain error types (only API-facing errors)\n+- Modifying logging infrastructure\n+- Changing HTTP status code semantics\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Industry Research\n+\n+### How Major Tech Companies Handle Errors\n+\n+| Company | Standard | Key Features |\n+|---------|----------|--------------|\n+| **Google** | AIP-193 + gRPC Status | `reason` (UPPER_SNAKE_CASE), `domain` (service name), `metadata` (key-value context), `ErrorInfo`, `LocalizedMessage`, `Help` links |\n+| **Amazon AWS** | Custom JSON | `errorType`, `httpStatus`, `requestId`, `message`, custom error object serialization |\n+| **Twitter/X** | JSON with `errors` array | `code` (CAPS_CASE), `message`, `parameter`, `details`, `value` |\n+| **RFC 9457** | Problem Details | `type` (URI), `title`, `status`, `detail`, `instance`, extension members |\n+\n+### Key Patterns Identified\n+\n+1. **Machine-readable identifiers** - Unique codes for programmatic handling (Google's `reason`, Twitter's `code`)\n+2. **Domain/namespace separation** - Identify error source (Google's `domain`, our GTS vendor.package)\n+3. **Structured metadata** - Key-value context without parsing messages (Google's `ErrorInfo.metadata`)\n+4. **Trace/Request IDs** - Correlation for debugging (AWS `requestId`, our `trace_id`)\n+5. **Documentation links** - URIs to error documentation (RFC 9457 `type`, Google's `Help`)\n+6. **Error categorization** - System vs User-defined, Retryable vs Non-retryable\n+\n+### Google AIP-193 ErrorInfo Structure (Reference)\n+\n+```json\n+{\n+  \"error\": {\n+    \"code\": 429,\n+    \"message\": \"The zone 'us-east1-a' does not have enough resources...\",\n+    \"status\": \"RESOURCE_EXHAUSTED\",\n+    \"details\": [\n+      {\n+        \"@type\": \"type.googleapis.com/google.rpc.ErrorInfo\",\n+        \"reason\": \"RESOURCE_AVAILABILITY\",\n+        \"domain\": \"compute.googleapis.com\",\n+        \"metadata\": {\n+          \"zone\": \"us-east1-a\",\n+          \"vmType\": \"e2-medium\"\n+        }\n+      }\n+    ]\n+  }\n+}\n+```\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Current State Analysis\n+\n+### Existing Infrastructure\n+\n+1. **`Problem` struct** (`libs/modkit-errors/src/problem.rs`) - RFC 9457 compliant\n+   - Fields: `type_url`, `title`, `status`, `detail`, `instance`, `code`, `trace_id`, `errors`\n+   - Implements `IntoResponse` for Axum with automatic trace ID enrichment\n+\n+2. **`struct_to_gts_schema` macro** (`modules/types-registry/gts-rust/gts-macros/src/lib.rs`)\n+   - Attribute macro for explicit struct definitions with GTS IDs visible in code\n+   - Generates constants: `GTS_SCHEMA_ID`, `GTS_SCHEMA_JSON`, etc.\n+   - **This pattern will be adapted for error definitions**\n+\n+3. **`declare_errors!` macro** (`libs/modkit-errors-macro/src/lib.rs`) - **TO BE DEPRECATED**\n+   - Generates type-safe error enums from JSON catalogs\n+   - Problem: GTS IDs hidden in external JSON files, not visible to LLMs\n+   - Used by: `users_info` example, `modkit-odata`\n+\n+### Gaps Identified\n+\n+| Gap | Current State | Required State |\n+|-----|---------------|----------------|\n+| **Hidden GTS IDs** | JSON-based `declare_errors!` | Explicit `#[gts_error]` structs with visible GTS IDs |\n+| **Inconsistent definitions** | Some modules use inline errors | All modules use `#[gts_error]` structs |\n+| **No types registry** | Errors not registered | All errors registered as GTS types |\n+| **Missing metadata** | No structured context | Struct fields → `metadata` map |\n+| **Partial trace IDs** | Only in `IntoResponse` | Mandatory in all error responses |\n+| **No error categories** | Flat error codes | System/Operational/Client categories |\n+| **No error stack** | Single error | Upstream error chain propagation |\n+\n+### Current Module Migration Status\n+\n+| Module | Location | Status | Issues |\n+|--------|----------|--------|--------|\n+| **file_parser** | `modules/file_parser/` | 🔴 Not migrated | No GTS IDs, inline `Problem::new()` |\n+| **types-registry** | `modules/system/types-registry/` | 🟡 Partial | Has codes but not GTS format (e.g., `TYPES_REGISTRY_NOT_FOUND`) |\n+| **nodes_registry** | `modules/system/nodes_registry/` | 🔴 Not migrated | Non-GTS codes (e.g., `NODES_NOT_FOUND`) |\n+| **api_gateway** | `modules/system/api_gateway/` | 🔴 Not migrated | No Problem struct, simple error codes |\n+| **tenant_resolver** | `modules/system/tenant_resolver/` | 🔴 Not migrated | No GTS IDs |\n+| **simple-user-settings** | `modules/simple-user-settings/` | 🟡 Partial | Uses `declare_errors!` with old chain format |\n+| **modkit-auth** | `libs/modkit-auth/` | 🔴 Not migrated | No GTS IDs, custom `IntoResponse` |\n+| **modkit-odata** | `libs/modkit-odata/` | 🟡 Partial | Uses `declare_errors!` with old chain format |\n+| **users_info** (example) | `examples/modkit/users_info/` | 🟡 Partial | Uses `declare_errors!` with old chain format |\n+\n+#### Legend\n+- 🟢 **Migrated** - Uses `#[gts_error]` structs with proper base types\n+- 🟡 **Partial** - Has GTS IDs but uses deprecated `declare_errors!` or old format\n+- 🔴 **Not migrated** - No GTS IDs or non-GTS format codes\n+\n+#### GTS ID Format Note\n+\n+**Old chain format** (used by `declare_errors!`):\n+```\n+gts.hx.core.errors.err.v1~hx.module.error_name.v1\n+```\n+\n+**New format** (with `base` field):\n+```\n+gts.hx.module.namespace.error_name.v1~\n+```\n+The `base` field in `#[gts_error]` replaces the chain suffix, making inheritance explicit in code.\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Requirements\n+\n+### R1: Error Schema Requirements\n+\n+Every error returned from REST API MUST conform to the unified schema:\n+\n+```rust\n+pub struct Problem {\n+    // =========================================================================\n+    // REQUIRED FIELDS - Core error identification\n+    // =========================================================================\n+    \n+    /// URI reference identifying the problem type (GTS-based)\n+    /// Example: \"https://docs.hyperspot.com/errors/types_registry_entity_not_found_v1\"\n+    #[serde(rename = \"type\")]\n+    pub type_url: String,\n+    \n+    /// Human-readable summary of the problem type (static per error type)\n+    pub title: String,\n+    \n+    /// GTS error code (machine-readable identifier)\n+    pub code: String,\n+    \n+    /// Trace ID for request correlation\n+    pub trace_id: String,\n+    \n+    // =========================================================================\n+    // CONTEXTUAL FIELDS - Optional based on error context\n+    // =========================================================================\n+    \n+    /// HTTP status code. Optional because:\n+    /// - gRPC errors use different status codes\n+    /// - Internal/domain errors may not have HTTP context\n+    /// - Event-driven systems have no request/response\n+    /// When serializing for HTTP response, this is populated from error definition.\n+    #[serde(skip_serializing_if = \"Option::is_none\")]\n+    pub status: Option<u16>,\n+    \n+    /// Human-readable explanation specific to this occurrence.\n+    /// Optional - title may be sufficient for simple errors.\n+    #[serde(skip_serializing_if = \"Option::is_none\")]\n+    pub detail: Option<String>,\n+    \n+    /// Error category for client handling.\n+    /// Optional - can be inferred from base type hierarchy.\n+    #[serde(skip_serializing_if = \"Option::is_none\")]\n+    pub category: Option<ErrorCategory>,\n+    \n+    /// Whether client can retry this request.\n+    /// Optional - can be inferred from base type; not relevant for all contexts.\n+    #[serde(skip_serializing_if = \"Option::is_none\")]\n+    pub retryable: Option<bool>,\n+    \n+    /// URI identifying this specific occurrence (auto-populated from request path)\n+    #[serde(skip_serializing_if = \"Option::is_none\")]\n+    pub instance: Option<String>,\n+    \n+    /// Structured metadata (key-value context)\n+    #[serde(skip_serializing_if = \"Option::is_none\")]\n+    pub metadata: Option<HashMap<String, String>>,\n+    \n+    /// Validation errors for 4xx responses\n+    #[serde(skip_serializing_if = \"Option::is_none\")]\n+    pub errors: Option<Vec<ValidationViolation>>,\n+    \n+    /// Upstream error chain (when error_stack enabled)\n+    #[serde(skip_serializing_if = \"Option::is_none\")]\n+    pub upstream_errors: Option<Vec<UpstreamError>>,\n+}\n+\n+pub enum ErrorCategory {\n+    /// Platform-level execution errors (panics, OOM, internal bugs)\n+    System,\n+    /// Infrastructure/operational issues (DB unavailable, service down, rate limits)\n+    Operational,\n+    /// Client input/request errors (validation, not found, unauthorized)\n+    Client,\n+}\n+```\n+\n+#### Field Requirements Summary\n+\n+| Field | Required | Reason |\n+|-------|----------|--------|\n+| `type_url` | ✅ Yes | RFC 9457 requires problem type URI |\n+| `title` | ✅ Yes | Human-readable error name (static per type) |\n+| `code` | ✅ Yes | GTS identifier for machine processing |\n+| `trace_id` | ✅ Yes | Request correlation for debugging |\n+| `status` | ❌ No | Only relevant for HTTP; gRPC/events/domain errors don't need it |\n+| `detail` | ❌ No | Instance-specific message; title may suffice |\n+| `category` | ❌ No | Inherited from base type hierarchy |\n+| `retryable` | ❌ No | Inherited from base type; not relevant for all contexts |\n+| `instance` | ❌ No | Auto-populated from request path when applicable |\n+| `metadata` | ❌ No | Additional context key-value pairs |\n+| `errors` | ❌ No | Validation violations for 4xx errors |\n+| `upstream_errors` | ❌ No | Error chain from upstream services |\n+\n+**Note:** When converting to HTTP response, `status` is populated from the error definition. When the error is used in non-HTTP contexts (gRPC, domain logic, events), `status` remains `None`.\n+\n+### R2: GTS Identifier and Base Type Requirements\n+\n+Every error MUST have a valid GTS identifier and specify its base type using the `base` field.\n+\n+#### GTS ID Format\n+\n+```\n+gts.<vendor>.<package>.<namespace>.<type>.v<version>~\n+```\n+\n+**Examples:**\n+- `gts.hx.types_registry.entity.not_found.v1~` - Types registry not found error\n+- `gts.hx.file_parser.validation.invalid_format.v1~` - File parser validation error\n+- `gts.hx.system.runtime.timeout.v1~` - System timeout error\n+\n+#### Base Type Chaining\n+\n+Errors form an inheritance chain using the `base` field. The `base` field references another error struct type (not a string literal), similar to how `struct_to_gts_schema` works.\n+\n+The root base error type is:\n+\n+```rust\n+/// Root error type for all GTS errors.\n+#[gts_error(\n+    gts_id = \"gts.hx.core.errors.err.v1~\",\n+    base = true,  // Marks this as a root base type (no parent)\n+    title = \"Error\",\n+    // Optional attributes with defaults for inheritance:\n+    status = 500,        // Default HTTP status (optional, inherited by children)\n+    category = \"System\", // Default category (optional, inherited by children)\n+    retryable = false    // Default retryable (optional, inherited by children)\n+)]\n+pub struct BaseError;\n+```\n+\n+All module-specific errors MUST reference their base type as a struct (extending the appropriate logical/system error):\n+\n+```rust\n+use modkit_errors::system::logical::NotFoundError;\n+\n+/// Entity was not found in the types registry.\n+/// Note: status, category, retryable are inherited from NotFoundError if not specified.\n+#[gts_error(\n+    gts_id = \"gts.hx.types_registry.entity.not_found.v1~\",\n+    base = NotFoundError,  // Extends logical.not_found, not BaseError\n+    title = \"Entity Not Found\",\n+    // These are optional - inherited from base if omitted:\n+    // status = 404,      // Inherited from NotFoundError\n+    // category = \"Client\", // Inherited from NotFoundError  \n+    // retryable = false,   // Inherited from NotFoundError\n+)]\n+pub struct EntityNotFoundError {\n+    pub gts_id: String,\n+}\n+```\n+\n+#### Multi-Level Inheritance\n+\n+Errors can form deeper inheritance chains:\n+\n+```rust\n+/// Logical not found error (platform-level).\n+#[gts_error(\n+    gts_id = \"gts.hx.system.logical.not_found.v1~\",\n+    base = BaseError,  // Platform errors extend BaseError\n+    status = 404,\n+    title = \"Not Found\",\n+    category = \"Client\",\n+    retryable = false\n+)]\n+pub struct NotFoundError;\n+\n+/// Types registry entity not found (module-level).\n+#[gts_error(\n+    gts_id = \"gts.hx.types_registry.entity.not_found.v1~\",\n+    base = NotFoundError,  // Module errors extend logical errors\n+    status = 404,\n+    title = \"Entity Not Found\",\n+    category = \"Client\",\n+    retryable = false\n+)]\n+pub struct EntityNotFoundError {\n+    pub gts_id: String,\n+}\n+```\n+\n+#### Inheritance Hierarchy\n+\n+```\n+BaseError (gts.hx.core.errors.err.v1~)                              [base = true]\n+├── Transport Errors (hx.system.transport.*)                        [base = BaseError]\n+├── Runtime Errors (hx.system.runtime.*)                            [base = BaseError]\n+│   └── hx.types_registry.system.internal.v1~                       [base = runtime.internal]\n+├── HTTP Errors (hx.system.http.*)                                  [base = BaseError]\n+│   └── hx.auth.token_expired.v1~                                   [base = http.unauthorized]\n+├── gRPC Errors (hx.system.grpc.*)                                  [base = BaseError]\n+└── Logical Errors (hx.system.logical.*)                            [base = BaseError]\n+    ├── logical.not_found.v1~                                       [base = BaseError]\n+    │   ├── hx.types_registry.entity.not_found.v1~                  [base = logical.not_found]\n+    │   └── hx.db.entity.not_found.v1~                              [base = logical.not_found]\n+    ├── logical.already_exists.v1~                                  [base = BaseError]\n+    │   └── hx.types_registry.entity.already_exists.v1~             [base = logical.already_exists]\n+    └── logical.validation_failed.v1~                               [base = BaseError]\n+        └── hx.file_parser.validation.invalid_format.v1~            [base = logical.validation_failed]\n+```\n+\n+### R3: Trace ID Requirements\n+\n+- Every error response MUST include a non-empty `trace_id`\n+- Trace ID MUST be propagated from incoming request headers or generated\n+- Trace ID MUST be logged with the error for correlation\n+\n+### R4: Types Registry Integration\n+\n+- All error types MUST be registered in the types registry at startup\n+- Error schema MUST extend base error type: `gts.hx.core.errors.err.v1`\n+- Registration MUST include: code, title, status, category, retryable flag\n+\n+### R5: Standardized System Error Types\n+\n+See [GTS System Errors Catalog](#gts-system-errors-catalog) for the complete list of all system errors.\n+\n+### R6: Error Stack Propagation\n+\n+When a function calls another service/function that returns an error:\n+- The error SHOULD be wrapped with context\n+- `upstream_errors` array SHOULD contain the chain of errors\n+- Each upstream error includes: `code`, `title`, `detail`, `source`\n+- Propagation controlled by `error_stack` configuration flag\n+\n+---\n+\n+## GTS Error Code Format\n+\n+### Structure\n+\n+```\n+gts.<vendor>.<package>.<namespace>.<type>.<version>~<chain>\n+```\n+\n+### Components\n+\n+| Component | Description | Example |\n+|-----------|-------------|---------|\n+| `gts` | Global Type System prefix | `gts` |\n+| `vendor` | Organization identifier | `hx` (Hyperspot) |\n+| `package` | Module/service name | `types_registry`, `file_parser` |\n+| `namespace` | Error category | `entity`, `validation`, `runtime` |\n+| `type` | Specific error type | `not_found`, `invalid_format` |\n+| `version` | Schema version | `v1`, `v1.0` |\n+| `~chain` | Base type chain | `~hx.core.errors.err.v1` |\n+\n+### Validation Rules\n+\n+1. MUST start with `gts.`\n+2. All segments MUST be lowercase alphanumeric or underscore\n+3. No empty segments allowed\n+4. Final segment MUST be version format (`vN` or `vN.M`)\n+5. MUST chain from base error type\n+\n+### Short Name Derivation\n+\n+Short accessor names derived from final GTX segment:\n+```\n+gts.hx.core.errors.err.v1~hx.types_registry.entity.not_found.v1\n+                         └─────────────────────────────────────┘\n+                                          ↓\n+                         types_registry_entity_not_found_v1()\n+```\n+","path":"intended_design/UNIFIED_ERROR_SYSTEM.md","commit_id":"5bdb0f43b25858af78999718f7247813802b9634","original_commit_id":"5bdb0f43b25858af78999718f7247813802b9634","user":{"login":"graphite-app[bot]","id":96075541,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOBbn_FQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/158384?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/graphite-app%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/graphite-app","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/graphite-app%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/graphite-app%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/graphite-app%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/graphite-app%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/graphite-app%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/graphite-app%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/graphite-app%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/graphite-app%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/graphite-app%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"**GTS Error Code Format section describes deprecated format**\n\nThis section documents the old chain format with `~<chain>` suffix (line 409), but the document established at lines 152-156 that the new format uses `~` terminator with separate `base` field instead:\n\n- Old: `gts.hx.core.errors.err.v1~hx.module.error_name.v1`\n- New: `gts.hx.module.namespace.error_name.v1~` with `base = NotFoundError`\n\nThe section should clarify this is the old format and reference the new format documented in R2 (lines 260-363). The table at line 409 showing `~chain` as a component contradicts all examples in the document that use trailing `~` without chain data.\n\nImplementing validation based on this format would reject the new format used throughout all code examples.\n```suggestion\n\n## GTS Error Code Format\n\n### Current Format (R2)\n\n```\ngts.<vendor>.<package>.<namespace>.<type>.<version>~\n```\n\nWith a separate `base` field to indicate inheritance.\n\nFor details on the current format, see the [R2 Error Format](#r2-error-format) section.\n\n### Legacy Format (Pre-R2)\n\nThe following format is deprecated and included for historical reference only:\n\n```\ngts.<vendor>.<package>.<namespace>.<type>.<version>~<chain>\n```\n\n#### Components (Legacy)\n\n| Component | Description | Example |\n|-----------|-------------|---------|\n| `gts` | Global Type System prefix | `gts` |\n| `vendor` | Organization identifier | `hx` (Hyperspot) |\n| `package` | Module/service name | `types_registry`, `file_parser` |\n| `namespace` | Error category | `entity`, `validation`, `runtime` |\n| `type` | Specific error type | `not_found`, `invalid_format` |\n| `version` | Schema version | `v1`, `v1.0` |\n| `~chain` | Base type chain | `~hx.core.errors.err.v1` |\n\n#### Validation Rules (Legacy)\n\n1. MUST start with `gts.`\n2. All segments MUST be lowercase alphanumeric or underscore\n3. No empty segments allowed\n4. Final segment MUST be version format (`vN` or `vN.M`)\n5. MUST chain from base error type\n\n#### Short Name Derivation (Legacy)\n\nShort accessor names derived from final GTX segment:\n```\ngts.hx.core.errors.err.v1~hx.types_registry.entity.not_found.v1\n                         └─────────────────────────────────────┘\n                                          ↓\n                         types_registry_entity_not_found_v1()\n```\n\n```\n  \n\n*Spotted by [Graphite Agent](https://app.graphite.com/diamond/?org=hypernetix&ref=ai-review-comment)*<i class='graphite__hidden'><br /><br /><a href=\"https://app.graphite.com/github/pr/hypernetix/hyperspot/290?chatWithGeneratedComment=9ff3c92e-84ee-421c-bafa-9d2f56321f41\"><picture><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\" srcset=\"https://static.graphite.dev/github-diamond-fix-in-graphite-dark.svg\"><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\" srcset=\"https://static.graphite.dev/github-diamond-fix-in-graphite-light.svg\"><img alt=\"Fix in Graphite\" src=\"https://static.graphite.dev/github-diamond-fix-in-graphite-dark.svg\"></picture></a></i><i class='graphite__hidden'><br /><br />Is this helpful? React 👍 or 👎 to let us know.</i>","created_at":"2026-01-21T10:29:51Z","updated_at":"2026-01-21T10:29:53Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/290#discussion_r2711942595","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/290","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2711942595"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/290#discussion_r2711942595"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/290"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2711942595/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":391,"start_side":"RIGHT","line":null,"original_line":428,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","original_position":428,"position":1,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2711945708","pull_request_review_id":3686473187,"id":2711945708,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs6hpQHs","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,417 @@\n+# GTS Error System Documentation\n+\n+This document describes how errors are defined, structured, transformed, and used in the Hyperspot/gts-rust project.\n+\n+## Overview\n+\n+The error system follows **RFC 9457 Problem Details for HTTP APIs** and uses a **GTS (Global Type System)** format for error codes. The system provides:\n+\n+- **Compile-time validated** error catalogs via JSON files\n+- **Type-safe** error code enums generated by proc-macros\n+- **Layered error transformation** from domain → API → HTTP response\n+- **Consistent error format** across all modules\n+","path":"docs/GTS_ERRORS.md","commit_id":"5bdb0f43b25858af78999718f7247813802b9634","original_commit_id":"5bdb0f43b25858af78999718f7247813802b9634","user":{"login":"coderabbitai[bot]","id":136622811,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOCCSy2w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/347564?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/coderabbitai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"_🛠️ Refactor suggestion_ | _🟠 Major_\n\n**Add cross-reference to the unified error system design.**\n\nThis document describes the current GTS error system using `declare_errors!` and JSON catalogs. However, `intended_design/UNIFIED_ERROR_SYSTEM.md` indicates that this approach will be deprecated in favor of `#[gts_error]` structs with explicit base types (UNIFIED_ERROR_SYSTEM.md line 109).\n\nConsider adding a prominent notice at the top of this document to:\n1. Clarify that this describes the current/legacy implementation\n2. Reference the unified error system design document\n3. Indicate whether new modules should use this approach or wait for the new system\n\nWithout this context, developers may not realize there's a migration planned and could build new modules using an approach that will soon be deprecated.\n\n\n<details>\n<summary>📝 Suggested addition</summary>\n\n```diff\n # GTS Error System Documentation\n+\n+> **⚠️ Migration Notice:** This document describes the current error system implementation.\n+> A unified error system is being designed to replace this approach. See\n+> [`intended_design/UNIFIED_ERROR_SYSTEM.md`](../intended_design/UNIFIED_ERROR_SYSTEM.md)\n+> for the future architecture using `#[gts_error]` structs.\n \n This document describes how errors are defined, structured, transformed, and used in the Hyperspot/gts-rust project.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- suggestion_start -->\n\n<details>\n<summary>📝 Committable suggestion</summary>\n\n> ‼️ **IMPORTANT**\n> Carefully review the code before committing. Ensure that it accurately replaces the highlighted code, contains no missing lines, and has no issues with indentation. Thoroughly test & benchmark the code to ensure it meets the requirements.\n\n```suggestion\n# GTS Error System Documentation\n\n> **⚠️ Migration Notice:** This document describes the current error system implementation.\n> A unified error system is being designed to replace this approach. See\n> [`intended_design/UNIFIED_ERROR_SYSTEM.md`](../intended_design/UNIFIED_ERROR_SYSTEM.md)\n> for the future architecture using `#[gts_error]` structs.\n\nThis document describes how errors are defined, structured, transformed, and used in the Hyperspot/gts-rust project.\n\n## Overview\n\nThe error system follows **RFC 9457 Problem Details for HTTP APIs** and uses a **GTS (Global Type System)** format for error codes. The system provides:\n\n- **Compile-time validated** error catalogs via JSON files\n- **Type-safe** error code enums generated by proc-macros\n- **Layered error transformation** from domain → API → HTTP response\n- **Consistent error format** across all modules\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- suggestion_end -->\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nIn `@docs/GTS_ERRORS.md` around lines 1 - 13, Add a prominent notice at the top of\nthis document clarifying that the page describes the current/legacy GTS error\nsystem (the declare_errors! + JSON catalog approach) and link to the unified\nerror system design (UNIFIED_ERROR_SYSTEM.md) which introduces the new\n#[gts_error] struct-based errors; explicitly state whether new modules should\nadopt the legacy pattern or wait for migration, and reference the section in\nUNIFIED_ERROR_SYSTEM.md that explains the deprecation/migration plan so readers\ncan find details about the new base-type approach.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- fingerprinting:phantom:triton:puma -->\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment by CodeRabbit -->","created_at":"2026-01-21T10:30:42Z","updated_at":"2026-01-21T10:30:43Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/290#discussion_r2711945708","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/290","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2711945708"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/290#discussion_r2711945708"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/290"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2711945708/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":1,"start_side":"RIGHT","line":null,"original_line":13,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","original_position":13,"position":1,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2720785173","pull_request_review_id":3697012913,"id":2720785173,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs6iK-MV","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,417 @@\n+# GTS Error System Documentation\n+\n+This document describes how errors are defined, structured, transformed, and used in the Hyperspot/gts-rust project.\n+\n+## Overview\n+\n+The error system follows **RFC 9457 Problem Details for HTTP APIs** and uses a **GTS (Global Type System)** format for error codes. The system provides:\n+\n+- **Compile-time validated** error catalogs via JSON files\n+- **Type-safe** error code enums generated by proc-macros\n+- **Layered error transformation** from domain → API → HTTP response\n+- **Consistent error format** across all modules\n+\n+## Architecture\n+\n+```\n+┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n+│                           Error Flow                                     │\n+├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n+│                                                                          │\n+│  gts/errors.json  ──────►  declare_errors! macro  ──────►  ErrorCode    │\n+│  (Source of Truth)         (Compile-time)                  (Enum)       │\n+│                                                                          │\n+│  DomainError  ──────►  ErrorCode::xxx().with_context()  ──────►  Problem│\n+│  (Business Logic)      (Mapping Layer)                        (RFC 9457)│\n+│                                                                          │\n+│  Problem  ──────►  IntoResponse (Axum)  ──────►  HTTP Response          │","path":"docs/GTS_ERRORS.md","commit_id":"5bdb0f43b25858af78999718f7247813802b9634","original_commit_id":"5bdb0f43b25858af78999718f7247813802b9634","user":{"login":"Bechma","id":19294519,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5Mjk0NTE5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19294519?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bechma","html_url":"https://github.com/Bechma","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bechma/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bechma/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bechma/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bechma/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bechma/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bechma/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bechma/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bechma/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bechma/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"So if an issue happens in infra while processing a request through a request it will be:\r\nProblem(ErrorCode::(gts_errorXXX)().with_context()\r\nIs that correct?\r\n\r\nIf a problem happens in a background, in which format that error is logged? How do we store that error in the db?","created_at":"2026-01-23T11:13:59Z","updated_at":"2026-01-23T13:02:20Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/290#discussion_r2720785173","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/290","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2720785173"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/290#discussion_r2720785173"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/290"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2720785173/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":null,"original_line":27,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"MEMBER","original_position":27,"position":1,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2720808711","pull_request_review_id":3697012913,"id":2720808711,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs6iLD8H","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,417 @@\n+# GTS Error System Documentation\n+\n+This document describes how errors are defined, structured, transformed, and used in the Hyperspot/gts-rust project.\n+\n+## Overview\n+\n+The error system follows **RFC 9457 Problem Details for HTTP APIs** and uses a **GTS (Global Type System)** format for error codes. The system provides:\n+\n+- **Compile-time validated** error catalogs via JSON files\n+- **Type-safe** error code enums generated by proc-macros\n+- **Layered error transformation** from domain → API → HTTP response\n+- **Consistent error format** across all modules\n+\n+## Architecture\n+\n+```\n+┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n+│                           Error Flow                                     │\n+├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n+│                                                                          │\n+│  gts/errors.json  ──────►  declare_errors! macro  ──────►  ErrorCode    │\n+│  (Source of Truth)         (Compile-time)                  (Enum)       │\n+│                                                                          │\n+│  DomainError  ──────►  ErrorCode::xxx().with_context()  ──────►  Problem│\n+│  (Business Logic)      (Mapping Layer)                        (RFC 9457)│\n+│                                                                          │\n+│  Problem  ──────►  IntoResponse (Axum)  ──────►  HTTP Response          │\n+│  (Data)            (Framework Integration)       (JSON + Headers)       │\n+│                                                                          │\n+└─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘\n+```\n+\n+## Components\n+\n+### 1. Error Catalog JSON (`gts/errors.json`)\n+\n+The source of truth for error definitions. Located in each module's `gts/` directory.\n+\n+**File Location Pattern:** `<module>/gts/errors.json`\n+\n+**Schema:**\n+```json\n+[\n+  {\n+    \"status\": 404,\n+    \"title\": \"User Not Found\",\n+    \"code\": \"gts.hx.core.errors.err.v1~hx.example1.user.not_found.v1\",\n+    \"type\": \"https://errors.example.com/...\",  // optional\n+    \"alias\": \"user_not_found\"                   // optional\n+  }\n+]\n+```\n+\n+**Fields:**\n+| Field | Required | Description |\n+|-------|----------|-------------|\n+| `status` | Yes | HTTP status code (100-599) |\n+| `title` | Yes | Human-readable error title |\n+| `code` | Yes | GTS-formatted error code |\n+| `type` | No | URI for error documentation |\n+| `alias` | No | Short name override for generated accessor |\n+\n+### 2. GTS Code Format\n+\n+GTS codes follow a strict format for global type identification:\n+\n+```\n+gts.vendor.package.namespace.type.version~chain1~chain2~...~instanceGTX\n+```\n+\n+**Structure:**\n+- **Prefix:** Always starts with `gts.`\n+- **Chain separator:** `~` separates GTX segments\n+- **Segment separator:** `.` separates parts within a GTX\n+- **Final GTX:** Must have at least 5 segments: `vendor.package.namespace.type.version`\n+- **Version:** Must end with `vN` or `vN.M` format\n+\n+**Example Breakdown:**\n+```\n+gts.hx.core.errors.err.v1~hx.example1.user.not_found.v1\n+│   │  │    │      │   │  │  │        │    │         │\n+│   │  │    │      │   │  │  │        │    │         └─ version\n+│   │  │    │      │   │  │  │        │    └─ type (not_found)\n+│   │  │    │      │   │  │  │        └─ namespace (user)\n+│   │  │    │      │   │  │  └─ package (example1)\n+│   │  │    │      │   │  └─ vendor (hx)\n+│   │  │    │      │   └─ version\n+│   │  │    │      └─ type (err)\n+│   │  │    └─ namespace (errors)\n+│   │  └─ package (core)\n+│   └─ vendor (hx)\n+└─ prefix\n+```\n+\n+**Validation Rules:**\n+1. Must start with `gts.`\n+2. All segments must be lowercase alphanumeric or underscore\n+3. No empty segments allowed\n+4. Final GTX must have ≥5 segments after vendor","path":"docs/GTS_ERRORS.md","commit_id":"5bdb0f43b25858af78999718f7247813802b9634","original_commit_id":"5bdb0f43b25858af78999718f7247813802b9634","user":{"login":"Bechma","id":19294519,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5Mjk0NTE5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19294519?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bechma","html_url":"https://github.com/Bechma","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bechma/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bechma/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bechma/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bechma/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bechma/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bechma/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bechma/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bechma/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bechma/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"I read it 3 times and I still don't understand the point made there","created_at":"2026-01-23T11:21:55Z","updated_at":"2026-01-23T13:02:20Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/290#discussion_r2720808711","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/290","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2720808711"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/290#discussion_r2720808711"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/290"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2720808711/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":74,"start_side":"RIGHT","line":null,"original_line":99,"side":"RIGHT","in_reply_to_id":2711942476,"author_association":"MEMBER","original_position":99,"position":1,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2720838362","pull_request_review_id":3697012913,"id":2720838362,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs6iLLLa","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,417 @@\n+# GTS Error System Documentation\n+\n+This document describes how errors are defined, structured, transformed, and used in the Hyperspot/gts-rust project.\n+\n+## Overview\n+\n+The error system follows **RFC 9457 Problem Details for HTTP APIs** and uses a **GTS (Global Type System)** format for error codes. The system provides:\n+\n+- **Compile-time validated** error catalogs via JSON files\n+- **Type-safe** error code enums generated by proc-macros\n+- **Layered error transformation** from domain → API → HTTP response\n+- **Consistent error format** across all modules\n+\n+## Architecture\n+\n+```\n+┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n+│                           Error Flow                                     │\n+├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n+│                                                                          │\n+│  gts/errors.json  ──────►  declare_errors! macro  ──────►  ErrorCode    │\n+│  (Source of Truth)         (Compile-time)                  (Enum)       │\n+│                                                                          │\n+│  DomainError  ──────►  ErrorCode::xxx().with_context()  ──────►  Problem│\n+│  (Business Logic)      (Mapping Layer)                        (RFC 9457)│\n+│                                                                          │\n+│  Problem  ──────►  IntoResponse (Axum)  ──────►  HTTP Response          │\n+│  (Data)            (Framework Integration)       (JSON + Headers)       │\n+│                                                                          │\n+└─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘\n+```\n+\n+## Components\n+\n+### 1. Error Catalog JSON (`gts/errors.json`)\n+\n+The source of truth for error definitions. Located in each module's `gts/` directory.\n+\n+**File Location Pattern:** `<module>/gts/errors.json`\n+\n+**Schema:**\n+```json\n+[\n+  {\n+    \"status\": 404,\n+    \"title\": \"User Not Found\",\n+    \"code\": \"gts.hx.core.errors.err.v1~hx.example1.user.not_found.v1\",\n+    \"type\": \"https://errors.example.com/...\",  // optional\n+    \"alias\": \"user_not_found\"                   // optional\n+  }\n+]\n+```\n+\n+**Fields:**\n+| Field | Required | Description |\n+|-------|----------|-------------|\n+| `status` | Yes | HTTP status code (100-599) |\n+| `title` | Yes | Human-readable error title |\n+| `code` | Yes | GTS-formatted error code |\n+| `type` | No | URI for error documentation |\n+| `alias` | No | Short name override for generated accessor |\n+\n+### 2. GTS Code Format\n+\n+GTS codes follow a strict format for global type identification:\n+\n+```\n+gts.vendor.package.namespace.type.version~chain1~chain2~...~instanceGTX\n+```\n+\n+**Structure:**\n+- **Prefix:** Always starts with `gts.`\n+- **Chain separator:** `~` separates GTX segments\n+- **Segment separator:** `.` separates parts within a GTX\n+- **Final GTX:** Must have at least 5 segments: `vendor.package.namespace.type.version`\n+- **Version:** Must end with `vN` or `vN.M` format\n+\n+**Example Breakdown:**\n+```\n+gts.hx.core.errors.err.v1~hx.example1.user.not_found.v1\n+│   │  │    │      │   │  │  │        │    │         │\n+│   │  │    │      │   │  │  │        │    │         └─ version\n+│   │  │    │      │   │  │  │        │    └─ type (not_found)\n+│   │  │    │      │   │  │  │        └─ namespace (user)\n+│   │  │    │      │   │  │  └─ package (example1)\n+│   │  │    │      │   │  └─ vendor (hx)\n+│   │  │    │      │   └─ version\n+│   │  │    │      └─ type (err)\n+│   │  │    └─ namespace (errors)\n+│   │  └─ package (core)\n+│   └─ vendor (hx)\n+└─ prefix\n+```\n+\n+**Validation Rules:**\n+1. Must start with `gts.`\n+2. All segments must be lowercase alphanumeric or underscore\n+3. No empty segments allowed\n+4. Final GTX must have ≥5 segments after vendor\n+5. Must end with valid version format (`v1`, `v1.2`, etc.)\n+\n+### 3. Proc-Macro: `declare_errors!`\n+\n+Generates type-safe error code enums from JSON at compile time.\n+\n+**Location:** `libs/modkit-errors-macro/src/lib.rs`\n+\n+**Usage:**\n+```rust\n+use modkit_errors_macro::declare_errors;\n+\n+declare_errors! {\n+    path = \"gts/errors.json\",\n+    namespace = \"errors\",\n+    vis = \"pub\"\n+}\n+```\n+\n+**Parameters:**\n+| Parameter | Required | Description |\n+|-----------|----------|-------------|\n+| `path` | Yes | Path to JSON file relative to `CARGO_MANIFEST_DIR` |\n+| `namespace` | Yes | Module name for generated code |\n+| `vis` | No | Visibility (`\"pub\"` or private) |\n+\n+**Generated Code:**\n+```rust\n+// Enum with all error codes\n+#[derive(Debug, Clone, Copy, PartialEq, Eq, Hash)]\n+pub enum ErrorCode {\n+    gts_hx_core_errors_err_v1_hx_example1_user_not_found_v1,\n+    // ...\n+}\n+\n+impl ErrorCode {\n+    // Get HTTP status\n+    pub const fn status(&self) -> u16 { ... }\n+    \n+    // Get full error definition\n+    pub const fn def(&self) -> ErrDef { ... }\n+    \n+    // Convert to Problem with detail\n+    pub fn as_problem(&self, detail: impl Into<String>) -> Problem { ... }\n+    \n+    // Create Problem with context (instance + trace_id)\n+    pub fn with_context(\n+        &self,\n+        detail: impl Into<String>,\n+        instance: &str,\n+        trace_id: Option<String>,\n+    ) -> Problem { ... }\n+    \n+    // Short accessor (derived from GTS or alias)\n+    pub const fn example1_user_not_found_v1() -> Self { ... }\n+}\n+\n+// Compile-time validated macro\n+macro_rules! problem_from_catalog { ... }\n+macro_rules! response_from_catalog { ... }\n+```\n+\n+### 4. Core Types\n+\n+#### `ErrDef` (Error Definition)\n+**Location:** `libs/modkit-errors/src/catalog.rs`\n+\n+```rust\n+pub struct ErrDef {\n+    pub status: u16,\n+    pub title: &'static str,\n+    pub code: &'static str,\n+    pub type_url: &'static str,\n+}\n+\n+impl ErrDef {\n+    pub fn as_problem(&self, detail: impl Into<String>) -> Problem { ... }\n+}\n+```\n+\n+#### `Problem` (RFC 9457)\n+**Location:** `libs/modkit-errors/src/problem.rs`\n+\n+```rust\n+pub struct Problem {\n+    pub type_url: String,      // URI reference for problem type\n+    pub title: String,         // Human-readable summary\n+    pub status: StatusCode,    // HTTP status code\n+    pub detail: String,        // Specific occurrence explanation\n+    pub instance: String,      // URI for this occurrence\n+    pub code: String,          // Machine-readable error code\n+    pub trace_id: Option<String>,\n+    pub errors: Option<Vec<ValidationViolation>>,\n+}\n+```\n+\n+**Builder Pattern:**\n+```rust\n+Problem::new(StatusCode::NOT_FOUND, \"Not Found\", \"User not found\")","path":"docs/GTS_ERRORS.md","commit_id":"5bdb0f43b25858af78999718f7247813802b9634","original_commit_id":"5bdb0f43b25858af78999718f7247813802b9634","user":{"login":"Bechma","id":19294519,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5Mjk0NTE5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19294519?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bechma","html_url":"https://github.com/Bechma","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bechma/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bechma/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bechma/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bechma/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bechma/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bechma/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bechma/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bechma/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bechma/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"this makes no sense, if we are using a builder pattern, why we have all members public?","created_at":"2026-01-23T11:31:57Z","updated_at":"2026-01-23T13:02:20Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/290#discussion_r2720838362","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/290","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2720838362"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/290#discussion_r2720838362"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/290"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2720838362/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":null,"original_line":198,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"MEMBER","original_position":198,"position":1,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2720840144","pull_request_review_id":3697012913,"id":2720840144,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs6iLLnQ","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,417 @@\n+# GTS Error System Documentation\n+\n+This document describes how errors are defined, structured, transformed, and used in the Hyperspot/gts-rust project.\n+\n+## Overview\n+\n+The error system follows **RFC 9457 Problem Details for HTTP APIs** and uses a **GTS (Global Type System)** format for error codes. The system provides:\n+\n+- **Compile-time validated** error catalogs via JSON files\n+- **Type-safe** error code enums generated by proc-macros\n+- **Layered error transformation** from domain → API → HTTP response\n+- **Consistent error format** across all modules\n+\n+## Architecture\n+\n+```\n+┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n+│                           Error Flow                                     │\n+├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n+│                                                                          │\n+│  gts/errors.json  ──────►  declare_errors! macro  ──────►  ErrorCode    │\n+│  (Source of Truth)         (Compile-time)                  (Enum)       │\n+│                                                                          │\n+│  DomainError  ──────►  ErrorCode::xxx().with_context()  ──────►  Problem│\n+│  (Business Logic)      (Mapping Layer)                        (RFC 9457)│\n+│                                                                          │\n+│  Problem  ──────►  IntoResponse (Axum)  ──────►  HTTP Response          │\n+│  (Data)            (Framework Integration)       (JSON + Headers)       │\n+│                                                                          │\n+└─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘\n+```\n+\n+## Components\n+\n+### 1. Error Catalog JSON (`gts/errors.json`)\n+\n+The source of truth for error definitions. Located in each module's `gts/` directory.\n+\n+**File Location Pattern:** `<module>/gts/errors.json`\n+\n+**Schema:**\n+```json\n+[\n+  {\n+    \"status\": 404,\n+    \"title\": \"User Not Found\",\n+    \"code\": \"gts.hx.core.errors.err.v1~hx.example1.user.not_found.v1\",\n+    \"type\": \"https://errors.example.com/...\",  // optional\n+    \"alias\": \"user_not_found\"                   // optional\n+  }\n+]\n+```\n+\n+**Fields:**\n+| Field | Required | Description |\n+|-------|----------|-------------|\n+| `status` | Yes | HTTP status code (100-599) |\n+| `title` | Yes | Human-readable error title |\n+| `code` | Yes | GTS-formatted error code |\n+| `type` | No | URI for error documentation |\n+| `alias` | No | Short name override for generated accessor |\n+\n+### 2. GTS Code Format\n+\n+GTS codes follow a strict format for global type identification:\n+\n+```\n+gts.vendor.package.namespace.type.version~chain1~chain2~...~instanceGTX\n+```\n+\n+**Structure:**\n+- **Prefix:** Always starts with `gts.`\n+- **Chain separator:** `~` separates GTX segments\n+- **Segment separator:** `.` separates parts within a GTX\n+- **Final GTX:** Must have at least 5 segments: `vendor.package.namespace.type.version`\n+- **Version:** Must end with `vN` or `vN.M` format\n+\n+**Example Breakdown:**\n+```\n+gts.hx.core.errors.err.v1~hx.example1.user.not_found.v1\n+│   │  │    │      │   │  │  │        │    │         │\n+│   │  │    │      │   │  │  │        │    │         └─ version\n+│   │  │    │      │   │  │  │        │    └─ type (not_found)\n+│   │  │    │      │   │  │  │        └─ namespace (user)\n+│   │  │    │      │   │  │  └─ package (example1)\n+│   │  │    │      │   │  └─ vendor (hx)\n+│   │  │    │      │   └─ version\n+│   │  │    │      └─ type (err)\n+│   │  │    └─ namespace (errors)\n+│   │  └─ package (core)\n+│   └─ vendor (hx)\n+└─ prefix\n+```\n+\n+**Validation Rules:**\n+1. Must start with `gts.`\n+2. All segments must be lowercase alphanumeric or underscore\n+3. No empty segments allowed\n+4. Final GTX must have ≥5 segments after vendor\n+5. Must end with valid version format (`v1`, `v1.2`, etc.)\n+\n+### 3. Proc-Macro: `declare_errors!`\n+\n+Generates type-safe error code enums from JSON at compile time.\n+\n+**Location:** `libs/modkit-errors-macro/src/lib.rs`\n+\n+**Usage:**\n+```rust\n+use modkit_errors_macro::declare_errors;\n+\n+declare_errors! {\n+    path = \"gts/errors.json\",\n+    namespace = \"errors\",\n+    vis = \"pub\"\n+}\n+```\n+\n+**Parameters:**\n+| Parameter | Required | Description |\n+|-----------|----------|-------------|\n+| `path` | Yes | Path to JSON file relative to `CARGO_MANIFEST_DIR` |\n+| `namespace` | Yes | Module name for generated code |\n+| `vis` | No | Visibility (`\"pub\"` or private) |\n+\n+**Generated Code:**\n+```rust\n+// Enum with all error codes\n+#[derive(Debug, Clone, Copy, PartialEq, Eq, Hash)]\n+pub enum ErrorCode {\n+    gts_hx_core_errors_err_v1_hx_example1_user_not_found_v1,\n+    // ...\n+}\n+\n+impl ErrorCode {\n+    // Get HTTP status\n+    pub const fn status(&self) -> u16 { ... }\n+    \n+    // Get full error definition\n+    pub const fn def(&self) -> ErrDef { ... }\n+    \n+    // Convert to Problem with detail\n+    pub fn as_problem(&self, detail: impl Into<String>) -> Problem { ... }\n+    \n+    // Create Problem with context (instance + trace_id)\n+    pub fn with_context(\n+        &self,\n+        detail: impl Into<String>,\n+        instance: &str,\n+        trace_id: Option<String>,\n+    ) -> Problem { ... }\n+    \n+    // Short accessor (derived from GTS or alias)\n+    pub const fn example1_user_not_found_v1() -> Self { ... }\n+}\n+\n+// Compile-time validated macro\n+macro_rules! problem_from_catalog { ... }\n+macro_rules! response_from_catalog { ... }\n+```\n+\n+### 4. Core Types\n+\n+#### `ErrDef` (Error Definition)\n+**Location:** `libs/modkit-errors/src/catalog.rs`\n+\n+```rust\n+pub struct ErrDef {\n+    pub status: u16,\n+    pub title: &'static str,\n+    pub code: &'static str,\n+    pub type_url: &'static str,\n+}\n+\n+impl ErrDef {\n+    pub fn as_problem(&self, detail: impl Into<String>) -> Problem { ... }\n+}\n+```\n+\n+#### `Problem` (RFC 9457)\n+**Location:** `libs/modkit-errors/src/problem.rs`\n+\n+```rust\n+pub struct Problem {\n+    pub type_url: String,      // URI reference for problem type\n+    pub title: String,         // Human-readable summary\n+    pub status: StatusCode,    // HTTP status code\n+    pub detail: String,        // Specific occurrence explanation\n+    pub instance: String,      // URI for this occurrence\n+    pub code: String,          // Machine-readable error code\n+    pub trace_id: Option<String>,\n+    pub errors: Option<Vec<ValidationViolation>>,\n+}\n+```\n+\n+**Builder Pattern:**\n+```rust\n+Problem::new(StatusCode::NOT_FOUND, \"Not Found\", \"User not found\")\n+    .with_code(\"gts.hx....\")\n+    .with_type(\"https://...\")\n+    .with_instance(\"/api/users/123\")\n+    .with_trace_id(\"req-456\")\n+    .with_errors(vec![...])\n+```\n+\n+## Error Flow by Layer\n+\n+### Layer 1: Domain Errors\n+\n+Domain errors represent business logic failures. They are internal and don't contain HTTP-specific information.\n+\n+**Location:** `<module>/src/domain/error.rs`\n+\n+```rust\n+#[derive(Error, Debug)]","path":"docs/GTS_ERRORS.md","commit_id":"5bdb0f43b25858af78999718f7247813802b9634","original_commit_id":"5bdb0f43b25858af78999718f7247813802b9634","user":{"login":"Bechma","id":19294519,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5Mjk0NTE5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19294519?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bechma","html_url":"https://github.com/Bechma","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bechma/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bechma/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bechma/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bechma/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bechma/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bechma/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bechma/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bechma/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bechma/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"full path to `thiserror::Error` to be more clear","created_at":"2026-01-23T11:32:31Z","updated_at":"2026-01-23T13:02:20Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/290#discussion_r2720840144","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/290","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2720840144"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/290#discussion_r2720840144"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/290"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2720840144/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":null,"original_line":215,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"MEMBER","original_position":215,"position":1,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2720841138","pull_request_review_id":3697012913,"id":2720841138,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs6iLL2y","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,417 @@\n+# GTS Error System Documentation\n+\n+This document describes how errors are defined, structured, transformed, and used in the Hyperspot/gts-rust project.\n+\n+## Overview\n+\n+The error system follows **RFC 9457 Problem Details for HTTP APIs** and uses a **GTS (Global Type System)** format for error codes. The system provides:\n+\n+- **Compile-time validated** error catalogs via JSON files\n+- **Type-safe** error code enums generated by proc-macros\n+- **Layered error transformation** from domain → API → HTTP response\n+- **Consistent error format** across all modules\n+\n+## Architecture\n+\n+```\n+┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n+│                           Error Flow                                     │\n+├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n+│                                                                          │\n+│  gts/errors.json  ──────►  declare_errors! macro  ──────►  ErrorCode    │\n+│  (Source of Truth)         (Compile-time)                  (Enum)       │\n+│                                                                          │\n+│  DomainError  ──────►  ErrorCode::xxx().with_context()  ──────►  Problem│\n+│  (Business Logic)      (Mapping Layer)                        (RFC 9457)│\n+│                                                                          │\n+│  Problem  ──────►  IntoResponse (Axum)  ──────►  HTTP Response          │\n+│  (Data)            (Framework Integration)       (JSON + Headers)       │\n+│                                                                          │\n+└─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘\n+```\n+\n+## Components\n+\n+### 1. Error Catalog JSON (`gts/errors.json`)\n+\n+The source of truth for error definitions. Located in each module's `gts/` directory.\n+\n+**File Location Pattern:** `<module>/gts/errors.json`\n+\n+**Schema:**\n+```json\n+[\n+  {\n+    \"status\": 404,\n+    \"title\": \"User Not Found\",\n+    \"code\": \"gts.hx.core.errors.err.v1~hx.example1.user.not_found.v1\",\n+    \"type\": \"https://errors.example.com/...\",  // optional\n+    \"alias\": \"user_not_found\"                   // optional\n+  }\n+]\n+```\n+\n+**Fields:**\n+| Field | Required | Description |\n+|-------|----------|-------------|\n+| `status` | Yes | HTTP status code (100-599) |\n+| `title` | Yes | Human-readable error title |\n+| `code` | Yes | GTS-formatted error code |\n+| `type` | No | URI for error documentation |\n+| `alias` | No | Short name override for generated accessor |\n+\n+### 2. GTS Code Format\n+\n+GTS codes follow a strict format for global type identification:\n+\n+```\n+gts.vendor.package.namespace.type.version~chain1~chain2~...~instanceGTX\n+```\n+\n+**Structure:**\n+- **Prefix:** Always starts with `gts.`\n+- **Chain separator:** `~` separates GTX segments\n+- **Segment separator:** `.` separates parts within a GTX\n+- **Final GTX:** Must have at least 5 segments: `vendor.package.namespace.type.version`\n+- **Version:** Must end with `vN` or `vN.M` format\n+\n+**Example Breakdown:**\n+```\n+gts.hx.core.errors.err.v1~hx.example1.user.not_found.v1\n+│   │  │    │      │   │  │  │        │    │         │\n+│   │  │    │      │   │  │  │        │    │         └─ version\n+│   │  │    │      │   │  │  │        │    └─ type (not_found)\n+│   │  │    │      │   │  │  │        └─ namespace (user)\n+│   │  │    │      │   │  │  └─ package (example1)\n+│   │  │    │      │   │  └─ vendor (hx)\n+│   │  │    │      │   └─ version\n+│   │  │    │      └─ type (err)\n+│   │  │    └─ namespace (errors)\n+│   │  └─ package (core)\n+│   └─ vendor (hx)\n+└─ prefix\n+```\n+\n+**Validation Rules:**\n+1. Must start with `gts.`\n+2. All segments must be lowercase alphanumeric or underscore\n+3. No empty segments allowed\n+4. Final GTX must have ≥5 segments after vendor\n+5. Must end with valid version format (`v1`, `v1.2`, etc.)\n+\n+### 3. Proc-Macro: `declare_errors!`\n+\n+Generates type-safe error code enums from JSON at compile time.\n+\n+**Location:** `libs/modkit-errors-macro/src/lib.rs`\n+\n+**Usage:**\n+```rust\n+use modkit_errors_macro::declare_errors;\n+\n+declare_errors! {\n+    path = \"gts/errors.json\",\n+    namespace = \"errors\",\n+    vis = \"pub\"\n+}\n+```\n+\n+**Parameters:**\n+| Parameter | Required | Description |\n+|-----------|----------|-------------|\n+| `path` | Yes | Path to JSON file relative to `CARGO_MANIFEST_DIR` |\n+| `namespace` | Yes | Module name for generated code |\n+| `vis` | No | Visibility (`\"pub\"` or private) |\n+\n+**Generated Code:**\n+```rust\n+// Enum with all error codes\n+#[derive(Debug, Clone, Copy, PartialEq, Eq, Hash)]\n+pub enum ErrorCode {\n+    gts_hx_core_errors_err_v1_hx_example1_user_not_found_v1,\n+    // ...\n+}\n+\n+impl ErrorCode {\n+    // Get HTTP status\n+    pub const fn status(&self) -> u16 { ... }\n+    \n+    // Get full error definition\n+    pub const fn def(&self) -> ErrDef { ... }\n+    \n+    // Convert to Problem with detail\n+    pub fn as_problem(&self, detail: impl Into<String>) -> Problem { ... }\n+    \n+    // Create Problem with context (instance + trace_id)\n+    pub fn with_context(\n+        &self,\n+        detail: impl Into<String>,\n+        instance: &str,\n+        trace_id: Option<String>,\n+    ) -> Problem { ... }\n+    \n+    // Short accessor (derived from GTS or alias)\n+    pub const fn example1_user_not_found_v1() -> Self { ... }\n+}\n+\n+// Compile-time validated macro\n+macro_rules! problem_from_catalog { ... }\n+macro_rules! response_from_catalog { ... }\n+```\n+\n+### 4. Core Types\n+\n+#### `ErrDef` (Error Definition)\n+**Location:** `libs/modkit-errors/src/catalog.rs`\n+\n+```rust\n+pub struct ErrDef {\n+    pub status: u16,\n+    pub title: &'static str,\n+    pub code: &'static str,\n+    pub type_url: &'static str,\n+}\n+\n+impl ErrDef {\n+    pub fn as_problem(&self, detail: impl Into<String>) -> Problem { ... }\n+}\n+```\n+\n+#### `Problem` (RFC 9457)\n+**Location:** `libs/modkit-errors/src/problem.rs`\n+\n+```rust\n+pub struct Problem {\n+    pub type_url: String,      // URI reference for problem type\n+    pub title: String,         // Human-readable summary\n+    pub status: StatusCode,    // HTTP status code\n+    pub detail: String,        // Specific occurrence explanation\n+    pub instance: String,      // URI for this occurrence\n+    pub code: String,          // Machine-readable error code\n+    pub trace_id: Option<String>,\n+    pub errors: Option<Vec<ValidationViolation>>,\n+}\n+```\n+\n+**Builder Pattern:**\n+```rust\n+Problem::new(StatusCode::NOT_FOUND, \"Not Found\", \"User not found\")\n+    .with_code(\"gts.hx....\")\n+    .with_type(\"https://...\")\n+    .with_instance(\"/api/users/123\")\n+    .with_trace_id(\"req-456\")\n+    .with_errors(vec![...])\n+```\n+\n+## Error Flow by Layer\n+\n+### Layer 1: Domain Errors\n+\n+Domain errors represent business logic failures. They are internal and don't contain HTTP-specific information.\n+\n+**Location:** `<module>/src/domain/error.rs`\n+\n+```rust\n+#[derive(Error, Debug)]\n+pub enum DomainError {\n+    #[error(\"User not found: {id}\")]\n+    UserNotFound { id: Uuid },\n+    \n+    #[error(\"Email '{email}' already exists\")]\n+    EmailAlreadyExists { email: String },\n+    \n+    #[error(\"Database error: {message}\")]\n+    Database { message: String },\n+    // ...\n+}\n+```\n+\n+### Layer 2: SDK Errors (Public API)\n+\n+SDK errors are exposed to other modules via the client trait. They are simplified and safe to expose.\n+\n+**Location:** `<module>-sdk/src/errors.rs`\n+\n+```rust\n+#[derive(Error, Debug, Clone)]","path":"docs/GTS_ERRORS.md","commit_id":"5bdb0f43b25858af78999718f7247813802b9634","original_commit_id":"5bdb0f43b25858af78999718f7247813802b9634","user":{"login":"Bechma","id":19294519,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5Mjk0NTE5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19294519?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bechma","html_url":"https://github.com/Bechma","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bechma/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bechma/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bechma/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bechma/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bechma/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bechma/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bechma/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bechma/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bechma/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"full path to `thiserror::Error` to be more clear","created_at":"2026-01-23T11:32:51Z","updated_at":"2026-01-23T13:02:20Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/290#discussion_r2720841138","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/290","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2720841138"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/290#discussion_r2720841138"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/290"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2720841138/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":null,"original_line":236,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"MEMBER","original_position":236,"position":1,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2720920191","pull_request_review_id":3697012913,"id":2720920191,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs6iLfJ_","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,417 @@\n+# GTS Error System Documentation\n+\n+This document describes how errors are defined, structured, transformed, and used in the Hyperspot/gts-rust project.\n+\n+## Overview\n+\n+The error system follows **RFC 9457 Problem Details for HTTP APIs** and uses a **GTS (Global Type System)** format for error codes. The system provides:\n+\n+- **Compile-time validated** error catalogs via JSON files\n+- **Type-safe** error code enums generated by proc-macros\n+- **Layered error transformation** from domain → API → HTTP response\n+- **Consistent error format** across all modules\n+\n+## Architecture\n+\n+```\n+┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n+│                           Error Flow                                     │\n+├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n+│                                                                          │\n+│  gts/errors.json  ──────►  declare_errors! macro  ──────►  ErrorCode    │\n+│  (Source of Truth)         (Compile-time)                  (Enum)       │\n+│                                                                          │\n+│  DomainError  ──────►  ErrorCode::xxx().with_context()  ──────►  Problem│\n+│  (Business Logic)      (Mapping Layer)                        (RFC 9457)│\n+│                                                                          │\n+│  Problem  ──────►  IntoResponse (Axum)  ──────►  HTTP Response          │\n+│  (Data)            (Framework Integration)       (JSON + Headers)       │\n+│                                                                          │\n+└─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘\n+```\n+\n+## Components\n+\n+### 1. Error Catalog JSON (`gts/errors.json`)\n+\n+The source of truth for error definitions. Located in each module's `gts/` directory.\n+\n+**File Location Pattern:** `<module>/gts/errors.json`\n+\n+**Schema:**\n+```json\n+[\n+  {\n+    \"status\": 404,\n+    \"title\": \"User Not Found\",\n+    \"code\": \"gts.hx.core.errors.err.v1~hx.example1.user.not_found.v1\",\n+    \"type\": \"https://errors.example.com/...\",  // optional\n+    \"alias\": \"user_not_found\"                   // optional\n+  }\n+]\n+```\n+\n+**Fields:**\n+| Field | Required | Description |\n+|-------|----------|-------------|\n+| `status` | Yes | HTTP status code (100-599) |\n+| `title` | Yes | Human-readable error title |\n+| `code` | Yes | GTS-formatted error code |\n+| `type` | No | URI for error documentation |\n+| `alias` | No | Short name override for generated accessor |\n+\n+### 2. GTS Code Format\n+\n+GTS codes follow a strict format for global type identification:\n+\n+```\n+gts.vendor.package.namespace.type.version~chain1~chain2~...~instanceGTX\n+```\n+\n+**Structure:**\n+- **Prefix:** Always starts with `gts.`\n+- **Chain separator:** `~` separates GTX segments\n+- **Segment separator:** `.` separates parts within a GTX\n+- **Final GTX:** Must have at least 5 segments: `vendor.package.namespace.type.version`\n+- **Version:** Must end with `vN` or `vN.M` format\n+\n+**Example Breakdown:**\n+```\n+gts.hx.core.errors.err.v1~hx.example1.user.not_found.v1\n+│   │  │    │      │   │  │  │        │    │         │\n+│   │  │    │      │   │  │  │        │    │         └─ version\n+│   │  │    │      │   │  │  │        │    └─ type (not_found)\n+│   │  │    │      │   │  │  │        └─ namespace (user)\n+│   │  │    │      │   │  │  └─ package (example1)\n+│   │  │    │      │   │  └─ vendor (hx)\n+│   │  │    │      │   └─ version\n+│   │  │    │      └─ type (err)\n+│   │  │    └─ namespace (errors)\n+│   │  └─ package (core)\n+│   └─ vendor (hx)\n+└─ prefix\n+```\n+\n+**Validation Rules:**\n+1. Must start with `gts.`\n+2. All segments must be lowercase alphanumeric or underscore\n+3. No empty segments allowed\n+4. Final GTX must have ≥5 segments after vendor\n+5. Must end with valid version format (`v1`, `v1.2`, etc.)\n+\n+### 3. Proc-Macro: `declare_errors!`\n+\n+Generates type-safe error code enums from JSON at compile time.\n+\n+**Location:** `libs/modkit-errors-macro/src/lib.rs`\n+\n+**Usage:**\n+```rust\n+use modkit_errors_macro::declare_errors;\n+\n+declare_errors! {\n+    path = \"gts/errors.json\",\n+    namespace = \"errors\",\n+    vis = \"pub\"\n+}\n+```\n+\n+**Parameters:**\n+| Parameter | Required | Description |\n+|-----------|----------|-------------|\n+| `path` | Yes | Path to JSON file relative to `CARGO_MANIFEST_DIR` |\n+| `namespace` | Yes | Module name for generated code |\n+| `vis` | No | Visibility (`\"pub\"` or private) |\n+\n+**Generated Code:**\n+```rust\n+// Enum with all error codes\n+#[derive(Debug, Clone, Copy, PartialEq, Eq, Hash)]\n+pub enum ErrorCode {\n+    gts_hx_core_errors_err_v1_hx_example1_user_not_found_v1,\n+    // ...\n+}\n+\n+impl ErrorCode {\n+    // Get HTTP status\n+    pub const fn status(&self) -> u16 { ... }\n+    \n+    // Get full error definition\n+    pub const fn def(&self) -> ErrDef { ... }\n+    \n+    // Convert to Problem with detail\n+    pub fn as_problem(&self, detail: impl Into<String>) -> Problem { ... }\n+    \n+    // Create Problem with context (instance + trace_id)\n+    pub fn with_context(\n+        &self,\n+        detail: impl Into<String>,\n+        instance: &str,\n+        trace_id: Option<String>,\n+    ) -> Problem { ... }\n+    \n+    // Short accessor (derived from GTS or alias)\n+    pub const fn example1_user_not_found_v1() -> Self { ... }\n+}\n+\n+// Compile-time validated macro\n+macro_rules! problem_from_catalog { ... }\n+macro_rules! response_from_catalog { ... }\n+```\n+\n+### 4. Core Types\n+\n+#### `ErrDef` (Error Definition)\n+**Location:** `libs/modkit-errors/src/catalog.rs`\n+\n+```rust\n+pub struct ErrDef {\n+    pub status: u16,\n+    pub title: &'static str,\n+    pub code: &'static str,\n+    pub type_url: &'static str,\n+}\n+\n+impl ErrDef {\n+    pub fn as_problem(&self, detail: impl Into<String>) -> Problem { ... }\n+}\n+```\n+\n+#### `Problem` (RFC 9457)\n+**Location:** `libs/modkit-errors/src/problem.rs`\n+\n+```rust\n+pub struct Problem {\n+    pub type_url: String,      // URI reference for problem type\n+    pub title: String,         // Human-readable summary\n+    pub status: StatusCode,    // HTTP status code\n+    pub detail: String,        // Specific occurrence explanation\n+    pub instance: String,      // URI for this occurrence\n+    pub code: String,          // Machine-readable error code\n+    pub trace_id: Option<String>,\n+    pub errors: Option<Vec<ValidationViolation>>,\n+}\n+```\n+\n+**Builder Pattern:**\n+```rust\n+Problem::new(StatusCode::NOT_FOUND, \"Not Found\", \"User not found\")\n+    .with_code(\"gts.hx....\")\n+    .with_type(\"https://...\")\n+    .with_instance(\"/api/users/123\")\n+    .with_trace_id(\"req-456\")\n+    .with_errors(vec![...])\n+```\n+\n+## Error Flow by Layer\n+\n+### Layer 1: Domain Errors\n+\n+Domain errors represent business logic failures. They are internal and don't contain HTTP-specific information.\n+\n+**Location:** `<module>/src/domain/error.rs`\n+\n+```rust\n+#[derive(Error, Debug)]\n+pub enum DomainError {\n+    #[error(\"User not found: {id}\")]\n+    UserNotFound { id: Uuid },\n+    \n+    #[error(\"Email '{email}' already exists\")]\n+    EmailAlreadyExists { email: String },\n+    \n+    #[error(\"Database error: {message}\")]\n+    Database { message: String },\n+    // ...\n+}\n+```\n+\n+### Layer 2: SDK Errors (Public API)\n+\n+SDK errors are exposed to other modules via the client trait. They are simplified and safe to expose.\n+\n+**Location:** `<module>-sdk/src/errors.rs`\n+\n+```rust\n+#[derive(Error, Debug, Clone)]\n+pub enum UsersInfoError {\n+    #[error(\"Resource not found: {id}\")]\n+    NotFound { id: Uuid },\n+    \n+    #[error(\"Validation error: {message}\")]\n+    Validation { message: String },\n+    \n+    #[error(\"Internal error\")]\n+    Internal,\n+}\n+```\n+\n+### Layer 3: API Error Mapping\n+\n+The API layer maps domain errors to RFC 9457 Problems using the error catalog.\n+\n+**Location:** `<module>/src/api/rest/error.rs`\n+\n+```rust\n+use crate::errors::ErrorCode;\n+\n+pub fn domain_error_to_problem(e: &DomainError, instance: &str) -> Problem {\n+    let trace_id = tracing::Span::current()\n+        .id()\n+        .map(|id| id.into_u64().to_string());\n+\n+    match &e {\n+        DomainError::UserNotFound { id } => {\n+            ErrorCode::example1_user_not_found_v1().with_context(\n+                format!(\"User with id {id} was not found\"),\n+                instance,\n+                trace_id,\n+            )\n+        }\n+        DomainError::Database { .. } => {\n+            tracing::error!(error = ?e, \"Database error occurred\");\n+            ErrorCode::example1_user_internal_database_v1().with_context(\n+                \"An internal database error occurred\",\n+                instance,\n+                trace_id,\n+            )\n+        }\n+        // ...\n+    }\n+}\n+```\n+\n+### Layer 4: HTTP Response\n+\n+`Problem` implements `IntoResponse` for Axum, automatically:\n+- Setting the correct HTTP status code\n+- Setting `Content-Type: application/problem+json`\n+- Enriching with trace ID from current span if not set\n+\n+```rust\n+// In handler\n+async fn get_user(...) -> Result<Json<User>, Problem> {\n+    let user = service.get_user(id).await","path":"docs/GTS_ERRORS.md","commit_id":"5bdb0f43b25858af78999718f7247813802b9634","original_commit_id":"5bdb0f43b25858af78999718f7247813802b9634","user":{"login":"Bechma","id":19294519,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5Mjk0NTE5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19294519?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bechma","html_url":"https://github.com/Bechma","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bechma/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bechma/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bechma/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bechma/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bechma/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bechma/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bechma/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bechma/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bechma/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":".map(Json)","created_at":"2026-01-23T11:59:00Z","updated_at":"2026-01-23T13:02:20Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/290#discussion_r2720920191","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/290","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2720920191"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/290#discussion_r2720920191"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/290"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2720920191/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":null,"original_line":294,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"MEMBER","original_position":294,"position":1,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2720921701","pull_request_review_id":3697012913,"id":2720921701,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs6iLfhl","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,417 @@\n+# GTS Error System Documentation\n+\n+This document describes how errors are defined, structured, transformed, and used in the Hyperspot/gts-rust project.\n+\n+## Overview\n+\n+The error system follows **RFC 9457 Problem Details for HTTP APIs** and uses a **GTS (Global Type System)** format for error codes. The system provides:\n+\n+- **Compile-time validated** error catalogs via JSON files\n+- **Type-safe** error code enums generated by proc-macros\n+- **Layered error transformation** from domain → API → HTTP response\n+- **Consistent error format** across all modules\n+\n+## Architecture\n+\n+```\n+┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n+│                           Error Flow                                     │\n+├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n+│                                                                          │\n+│  gts/errors.json  ──────►  declare_errors! macro  ──────►  ErrorCode    │\n+│  (Source of Truth)         (Compile-time)                  (Enum)       │\n+│                                                                          │\n+│  DomainError  ──────►  ErrorCode::xxx().with_context()  ──────►  Problem│\n+│  (Business Logic)      (Mapping Layer)                        (RFC 9457)│\n+│                                                                          │\n+│  Problem  ──────►  IntoResponse (Axum)  ──────►  HTTP Response          │\n+│  (Data)            (Framework Integration)       (JSON + Headers)       │\n+│                                                                          │\n+└─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘\n+```\n+\n+## Components\n+\n+### 1. Error Catalog JSON (`gts/errors.json`)\n+\n+The source of truth for error definitions. Located in each module's `gts/` directory.\n+\n+**File Location Pattern:** `<module>/gts/errors.json`\n+\n+**Schema:**\n+```json\n+[\n+  {\n+    \"status\": 404,\n+    \"title\": \"User Not Found\",\n+    \"code\": \"gts.hx.core.errors.err.v1~hx.example1.user.not_found.v1\",\n+    \"type\": \"https://errors.example.com/...\",  // optional\n+    \"alias\": \"user_not_found\"                   // optional\n+  }\n+]\n+```\n+\n+**Fields:**\n+| Field | Required | Description |\n+|-------|----------|-------------|\n+| `status` | Yes | HTTP status code (100-599) |\n+| `title` | Yes | Human-readable error title |\n+| `code` | Yes | GTS-formatted error code |\n+| `type` | No | URI for error documentation |\n+| `alias` | No | Short name override for generated accessor |\n+\n+### 2. GTS Code Format\n+\n+GTS codes follow a strict format for global type identification:\n+\n+```\n+gts.vendor.package.namespace.type.version~chain1~chain2~...~instanceGTX\n+```\n+\n+**Structure:**\n+- **Prefix:** Always starts with `gts.`\n+- **Chain separator:** `~` separates GTX segments\n+- **Segment separator:** `.` separates parts within a GTX\n+- **Final GTX:** Must have at least 5 segments: `vendor.package.namespace.type.version`\n+- **Version:** Must end with `vN` or `vN.M` format\n+\n+**Example Breakdown:**\n+```\n+gts.hx.core.errors.err.v1~hx.example1.user.not_found.v1\n+│   │  │    │      │   │  │  │        │    │         │\n+│   │  │    │      │   │  │  │        │    │         └─ version\n+│   │  │    │      │   │  │  │        │    └─ type (not_found)\n+│   │  │    │      │   │  │  │        └─ namespace (user)\n+│   │  │    │      │   │  │  └─ package (example1)\n+│   │  │    │      │   │  └─ vendor (hx)\n+│   │  │    │      │   └─ version\n+│   │  │    │      └─ type (err)\n+│   │  │    └─ namespace (errors)\n+│   │  └─ package (core)\n+│   └─ vendor (hx)\n+└─ prefix\n+```\n+\n+**Validation Rules:**\n+1. Must start with `gts.`\n+2. All segments must be lowercase alphanumeric or underscore\n+3. No empty segments allowed\n+4. Final GTX must have ≥5 segments after vendor\n+5. Must end with valid version format (`v1`, `v1.2`, etc.)\n+\n+### 3. Proc-Macro: `declare_errors!`\n+\n+Generates type-safe error code enums from JSON at compile time.\n+\n+**Location:** `libs/modkit-errors-macro/src/lib.rs`\n+\n+**Usage:**\n+```rust\n+use modkit_errors_macro::declare_errors;\n+\n+declare_errors! {\n+    path = \"gts/errors.json\",\n+    namespace = \"errors\",\n+    vis = \"pub\"\n+}\n+```\n+\n+**Parameters:**\n+| Parameter | Required | Description |\n+|-----------|----------|-------------|\n+| `path` | Yes | Path to JSON file relative to `CARGO_MANIFEST_DIR` |\n+| `namespace` | Yes | Module name for generated code |\n+| `vis` | No | Visibility (`\"pub\"` or private) |\n+\n+**Generated Code:**\n+```rust\n+// Enum with all error codes\n+#[derive(Debug, Clone, Copy, PartialEq, Eq, Hash)]\n+pub enum ErrorCode {\n+    gts_hx_core_errors_err_v1_hx_example1_user_not_found_v1,\n+    // ...\n+}\n+\n+impl ErrorCode {\n+    // Get HTTP status\n+    pub const fn status(&self) -> u16 { ... }\n+    \n+    // Get full error definition\n+    pub const fn def(&self) -> ErrDef { ... }\n+    \n+    // Convert to Problem with detail\n+    pub fn as_problem(&self, detail: impl Into<String>) -> Problem { ... }\n+    \n+    // Create Problem with context (instance + trace_id)\n+    pub fn with_context(\n+        &self,\n+        detail: impl Into<String>,\n+        instance: &str,\n+        trace_id: Option<String>,\n+    ) -> Problem { ... }\n+    \n+    // Short accessor (derived from GTS or alias)\n+    pub const fn example1_user_not_found_v1() -> Self { ... }\n+}\n+\n+// Compile-time validated macro\n+macro_rules! problem_from_catalog { ... }\n+macro_rules! response_from_catalog { ... }\n+```\n+\n+### 4. Core Types\n+\n+#### `ErrDef` (Error Definition)\n+**Location:** `libs/modkit-errors/src/catalog.rs`\n+\n+```rust\n+pub struct ErrDef {\n+    pub status: u16,\n+    pub title: &'static str,\n+    pub code: &'static str,\n+    pub type_url: &'static str,\n+}\n+\n+impl ErrDef {\n+    pub fn as_problem(&self, detail: impl Into<String>) -> Problem { ... }\n+}\n+```\n+\n+#### `Problem` (RFC 9457)\n+**Location:** `libs/modkit-errors/src/problem.rs`\n+\n+```rust\n+pub struct Problem {\n+    pub type_url: String,      // URI reference for problem type\n+    pub title: String,         // Human-readable summary\n+    pub status: StatusCode,    // HTTP status code\n+    pub detail: String,        // Specific occurrence explanation\n+    pub instance: String,      // URI for this occurrence\n+    pub code: String,          // Machine-readable error code\n+    pub trace_id: Option<String>,\n+    pub errors: Option<Vec<ValidationViolation>>,\n+}\n+```\n+\n+**Builder Pattern:**\n+```rust\n+Problem::new(StatusCode::NOT_FOUND, \"Not Found\", \"User not found\")\n+    .with_code(\"gts.hx....\")\n+    .with_type(\"https://...\")\n+    .with_instance(\"/api/users/123\")\n+    .with_trace_id(\"req-456\")\n+    .with_errors(vec![...])\n+```\n+\n+## Error Flow by Layer\n+\n+### Layer 1: Domain Errors\n+\n+Domain errors represent business logic failures. They are internal and don't contain HTTP-specific information.\n+\n+**Location:** `<module>/src/domain/error.rs`\n+\n+```rust\n+#[derive(Error, Debug)]\n+pub enum DomainError {\n+    #[error(\"User not found: {id}\")]\n+    UserNotFound { id: Uuid },\n+    \n+    #[error(\"Email '{email}' already exists\")]\n+    EmailAlreadyExists { email: String },\n+    \n+    #[error(\"Database error: {message}\")]\n+    Database { message: String },\n+    // ...\n+}\n+```\n+\n+### Layer 2: SDK Errors (Public API)\n+\n+SDK errors are exposed to other modules via the client trait. They are simplified and safe to expose.\n+\n+**Location:** `<module>-sdk/src/errors.rs`\n+\n+```rust\n+#[derive(Error, Debug, Clone)]\n+pub enum UsersInfoError {\n+    #[error(\"Resource not found: {id}\")]\n+    NotFound { id: Uuid },\n+    \n+    #[error(\"Validation error: {message}\")]\n+    Validation { message: String },\n+    \n+    #[error(\"Internal error\")]\n+    Internal,\n+}\n+```\n+\n+### Layer 3: API Error Mapping\n+\n+The API layer maps domain errors to RFC 9457 Problems using the error catalog.\n+\n+**Location:** `<module>/src/api/rest/error.rs`\n+\n+```rust\n+use crate::errors::ErrorCode;\n+\n+pub fn domain_error_to_problem(e: &DomainError, instance: &str) -> Problem {\n+    let trace_id = tracing::Span::current()\n+        .id()\n+        .map(|id| id.into_u64().to_string());\n+\n+    match &e {\n+        DomainError::UserNotFound { id } => {\n+            ErrorCode::example1_user_not_found_v1().with_context(\n+                format!(\"User with id {id} was not found\"),\n+                instance,\n+                trace_id,\n+            )\n+        }\n+        DomainError::Database { .. } => {\n+            tracing::error!(error = ?e, \"Database error occurred\");\n+            ErrorCode::example1_user_internal_database_v1().with_context(\n+                \"An internal database error occurred\",\n+                instance,\n+                trace_id,\n+            )\n+        }\n+        // ...\n+    }\n+}\n+```\n+\n+### Layer 4: HTTP Response\n+\n+`Problem` implements `IntoResponse` for Axum, automatically:\n+- Setting the correct HTTP status code\n+- Setting `Content-Type: application/problem+json`\n+- Enriching with trace ID from current span if not set\n+\n+```rust\n+// In handler\n+async fn get_user(...) -> Result<Json<User>, Problem> {\n+    let user = service.get_user(id).await\n+        .map_err(|e| domain_error_to_problem(&e, &path))?;\n+    Ok(Json(user))\n+}\n+```\n+\n+## Creating a New Error Catalog\n+\n+### Step 1: Create `gts/errors.json`\n+\n+```json\n+[\n+  {\n+    \"status\": 404,\n+    \"title\": \"Resource Not Found\",\n+    \"code\": \"gts.hx.core.errors.err.v1~hx.mymodule.resource.not_found.v1\"\n+  },\n+  {\n+    \"status\": 422,\n+    \"title\": \"Validation Error\",\n+    \"code\": \"gts.hx.core.errors.err.v1~hx.mymodule.validation.invalid_input.v1\"\n+  }\n+]\n+```\n+\n+### Step 2: Create `src/errors.rs`\n+\n+```rust\n+use modkit_errors_macro::declare_errors;\n+\n+declare_errors! {\n+    path = \"gts/errors.json\",\n+    namespace = \"errors\",\n+    vis = \"pub\"\n+}\n+```\n+\n+### Step 3: Add to `Cargo.toml`\n+\n+```toml\n+[dependencies]\n+modkit-errors-macro = { path = \"../../libs/modkit-errors-macro\" }","path":"docs/GTS_ERRORS.md","commit_id":"5bdb0f43b25858af78999718f7247813802b9634","original_commit_id":"5bdb0f43b25858af78999718f7247813802b9634","user":{"login":"Bechma","id":19294519,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5Mjk0NTE5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19294519?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bechma","html_url":"https://github.com/Bechma","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bechma/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bechma/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bechma/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bechma/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bechma/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bechma/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bechma/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bechma/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bechma/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"workspace = true\r\n\r\nWe stop using the path reference","created_at":"2026-01-23T11:59:32Z","updated_at":"2026-01-23T13:02:20Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/290#discussion_r2720921701","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/290","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2720921701"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/290#discussion_r2720921701"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/290"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2720921701/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":null,"original_line":335,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"MEMBER","original_position":335,"position":1,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2720926697","pull_request_review_id":3697012913,"id":2720926697,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs6iLgvp","diff_hunk":"","path":"intended_design/UNIFIED_ERROR_SYSTEM.md","commit_id":"a14d31841e0d559695e4ab49973b4f815551ccf3","original_commit_id":"5bdb0f43b25858af78999718f7247813802b9634","user":{"login":"Bechma","id":19294519,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5Mjk0NTE5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19294519?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bechma","html_url":"https://github.com/Bechma","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bechma/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bechma/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bechma/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bechma/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bechma/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bechma/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bechma/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bechma/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bechma/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Completely misc neatpick: intended_design -> proposed_rfc ?","created_at":"2026-01-23T12:01:18Z","updated_at":"2026-01-23T13:02:20Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/290#discussion_r2720926697","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/290","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2720926697"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/290#discussion_r2720926697"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/290"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2720926697/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":1,"original_line":1,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"MEMBER","original_position":1,"position":1,"subject_type":"file"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2731391069","pull_request_review_id":3710446544,"id":2731391069,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs6izbhd","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,417 @@\n+# GTS Error System Documentation\n+\n+This document describes how errors are defined, structured, transformed, and used in the Hyperspot/gts-rust project.\n+\n+## Overview\n+\n+The error system follows **RFC 9457 Problem Details for HTTP APIs** and uses a **GTS (Global Type System)** format for error codes. The system provides:\n+\n+- **Compile-time validated** error catalogs via JSON files\n+- **Type-safe** error code enums generated by proc-macros\n+- **Layered error transformation** from domain → API → HTTP response\n+- **Consistent error format** across all modules\n+\n+## Architecture\n+\n+```\n+┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n+│                           Error Flow                                     │\n+├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n+│                                                                          │\n+│  gts/errors.json  ──────►  declare_errors! macro  ──────►  ErrorCode    │\n+│  (Source of Truth)         (Compile-time)                  (Enum)       │\n+│                                                                          │\n+│  DomainError  ──────►  ErrorCode::xxx().with_context()  ──────►  Problem│\n+│  (Business Logic)      (Mapping Layer)                        (RFC 9457)│\n+│                                                                          │\n+│  Problem  ──────►  IntoResponse (Axum)  ──────►  HTTP Response          │\n+│  (Data)            (Framework Integration)       (JSON + Headers)       │\n+│                                                                          │\n+└─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘\n+```\n+\n+## Components\n+\n+### 1. Error Catalog JSON (`gts/errors.json`)\n+\n+The source of truth for error definitions. Located in each module's `gts/` directory.\n+\n+**File Location Pattern:** `<module>/gts/errors.json`\n+\n+**Schema:**\n+```json\n+[\n+  {\n+    \"status\": 404,\n+    \"title\": \"User Not Found\",\n+    \"code\": \"gts.hx.core.errors.err.v1~hx.example1.user.not_found.v1\",\n+    \"type\": \"https://errors.example.com/...\",  // optional\n+    \"alias\": \"user_not_found\"                   // optional\n+  }\n+]\n+```\n+\n+**Fields:**\n+| Field | Required | Description |\n+|-------|----------|-------------|\n+| `status` | Yes | HTTP status code (100-599) |\n+| `title` | Yes | Human-readable error title |\n+| `code` | Yes | GTS-formatted error code |\n+| `type` | No | URI for error documentation |\n+| `alias` | No | Short name override for generated accessor |\n+\n+### 2. GTS Code Format\n+\n+GTS codes follow a strict format for global type identification:\n+\n+```\n+gts.vendor.package.namespace.type.version~chain1~chain2~...~instanceGTX\n+```\n+\n+**Structure:**\n+- **Prefix:** Always starts with `gts.`\n+- **Chain separator:** `~` separates GTX segments\n+- **Segment separator:** `.` separates parts within a GTX\n+- **Final GTX:** Must have at least 5 segments: `vendor.package.namespace.type.version`\n+- **Version:** Must end with `vN` or `vN.M` format\n+\n+**Example Breakdown:**\n+```\n+gts.hx.core.errors.err.v1~hx.example1.user.not_found.v1","path":"docs/GTS_ERRORS.md","commit_id":"5bdb0f43b25858af78999718f7247813802b9634","original_commit_id":"5bdb0f43b25858af78999718f7247813802b9634","user":{"login":"Artifizer","id":192502778,"node_id":"U_kgDOC3lb-g","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/192502778?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer","html_url":"https://github.com/Artifizer","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"must be 'cf', not 'hx'","created_at":"2026-01-27T10:44:35Z","updated_at":"2026-01-30T21:23:01Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/290#discussion_r2731391069","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/290","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2731391069"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/290#discussion_r2731391069"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/290"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2731391069/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":null,"original_line":80,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"MEMBER","original_position":80,"position":1,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2731402842","pull_request_review_id":3710446544,"id":2731402842,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs6izeZa","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,417 @@\n+# GTS Error System Documentation\n+\n+This document describes how errors are defined, structured, transformed, and used in the Hyperspot/gts-rust project.\n+\n+## Overview\n+\n+The error system follows **RFC 9457 Problem Details for HTTP APIs** and uses a **GTS (Global Type System)** format for error codes. The system provides:\n+\n+- **Compile-time validated** error catalogs via JSON files\n+- **Type-safe** error code enums generated by proc-macros\n+- **Layered error transformation** from domain → API → HTTP response\n+- **Consistent error format** across all modules\n+\n+## Architecture\n+\n+```\n+┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n+│                           Error Flow                                     │\n+├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n+│                                                                          │\n+│  gts/errors.json  ──────►  declare_errors! macro  ──────►  ErrorCode    │\n+│  (Source of Truth)         (Compile-time)                  (Enum)       │\n+│                                                                          │\n+│  DomainError  ──────►  ErrorCode::xxx().with_context()  ──────►  Problem│\n+│  (Business Logic)      (Mapping Layer)                        (RFC 9457)│\n+│                                                                          │\n+│  Problem  ──────►  IntoResponse (Axum)  ──────►  HTTP Response          │\n+│  (Data)            (Framework Integration)       (JSON + Headers)       │\n+│                                                                          │\n+└─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘\n+```\n+\n+## Components\n+\n+### 1. Error Catalog JSON (`gts/errors.json`)\n+\n+The source of truth for error definitions. Located in each module's `gts/` directory.\n+\n+**File Location Pattern:** `<module>/gts/errors.json`\n+\n+**Schema:**\n+```json\n+[\n+  {\n+    \"status\": 404,\n+    \"title\": \"User Not Found\",\n+    \"code\": \"gts.hx.core.errors.err.v1~hx.example1.user.not_found.v1\",\n+    \"type\": \"https://errors.example.com/...\",  // optional\n+    \"alias\": \"user_not_found\"                   // optional\n+  }\n+]\n+```\n+\n+**Fields:**\n+| Field | Required | Description |\n+|-------|----------|-------------|\n+| `status` | Yes | HTTP status code (100-599) |\n+| `title` | Yes | Human-readable error title |\n+| `code` | Yes | GTS-formatted error code |\n+| `type` | No | URI for error documentation |\n+| `alias` | No | Short name override for generated accessor |\n+\n+### 2. GTS Code Format\n+\n+GTS codes follow a strict format for global type identification:\n+\n+```\n+gts.vendor.package.namespace.type.version~chain1~chain2~...~instanceGTX\n+```\n+\n+**Structure:**\n+- **Prefix:** Always starts with `gts.`\n+- **Chain separator:** `~` separates GTX segments\n+- **Segment separator:** `.` separates parts within a GTX\n+- **Final GTX:** Must have at least 5 segments: `vendor.package.namespace.type.version`\n+- **Version:** Must end with `vN` or `vN.M` format\n+\n+**Example Breakdown:**\n+```\n+gts.hx.core.errors.err.v1~hx.example1.user.not_found.v1\n+│   │  │    │      │   │  │  │        │    │         │\n+│   │  │    │      │   │  │  │        │    │         └─ version\n+│   │  │    │      │   │  │  │        │    └─ type (not_found)\n+│   │  │    │      │   │  │  │        └─ namespace (user)\n+│   │  │    │      │   │  │  └─ package (example1)\n+│   │  │    │      │   │  └─ vendor (hx)\n+│   │  │    │      │   └─ version\n+│   │  │    │      └─ type (err)\n+│   │  │    └─ namespace (errors)\n+│   │  └─ package (core)\n+│   └─ vendor (hx)\n+└─ prefix\n+```\n+\n+**Validation Rules:**\n+1. Must start with `gts.`\n+2. All segments must be lowercase alphanumeric or underscore\n+3. No empty segments allowed\n+4. Final GTX must have ≥5 segments after vendor","path":"docs/GTS_ERRORS.md","commit_id":"5bdb0f43b25858af78999718f7247813802b9634","original_commit_id":"5bdb0f43b25858af78999718f7247813802b9634","user":{"login":"Artifizer","id":192502778,"node_id":"U_kgDOC3lb-g","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/192502778?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer","html_url":"https://github.com/Artifizer","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"@alizid10 , I would just refer here to GTS spec w/o own description of segments and such","created_at":"2026-01-27T10:47:19Z","updated_at":"2026-01-30T21:23:01Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/290#discussion_r2731402842","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/290","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2731402842"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/290#discussion_r2731402842"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/290"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2731402842/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":74,"start_side":"RIGHT","line":null,"original_line":99,"side":"RIGHT","in_reply_to_id":2711942476,"author_association":"MEMBER","original_position":99,"position":1,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2731520996","pull_request_review_id":3710597227,"id":2731520996,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs6iz7Pk","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,417 @@\n+# GTS Error System Documentation\n+\n+This document describes how errors are defined, structured, transformed, and used in the Hyperspot/gts-rust project.\n+\n+## Overview\n+\n+The error system follows **RFC 9457 Problem Details for HTTP APIs** and uses a **GTS (Global Type System)** format for error codes. The system provides:\n+\n+- **Compile-time validated** error catalogs via JSON files\n+- **Type-safe** error code enums generated by proc-macros\n+- **Layered error transformation** from domain → API → HTTP response\n+- **Consistent error format** across all modules\n+\n+## Architecture\n+\n+```\n+┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n+│                           Error Flow                                     │\n+├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n+│                                                                          │\n+│  gts/errors.json  ──────►  declare_errors! macro  ──────►  ErrorCode    │\n+│  (Source of Truth)         (Compile-time)                  (Enum)       │\n+│                                                                          │\n+│  DomainError  ──────►  ErrorCode::xxx().with_context()  ──────►  Problem│\n+│  (Business Logic)      (Mapping Layer)                        (RFC 9457)│\n+│                                                                          │\n+│  Problem  ──────►  IntoResponse (Axum)  ──────►  HTTP Response          │\n+│  (Data)            (Framework Integration)       (JSON + Headers)       │\n+│                                                                          │\n+└─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘\n+```\n+\n+## Components\n+\n+### 1. Error Catalog JSON (`gts/errors.json`)\n+\n+The source of truth for error definitions. Located in each module's `gts/` directory.\n+\n+**File Location Pattern:** `<module>/gts/errors.json`\n+\n+**Schema:**\n+```json\n+[\n+  {\n+    \"status\": 404,\n+    \"title\": \"User Not Found\",\n+    \"code\": \"gts.hx.core.errors.err.v1~hx.example1.user.not_found.v1\",\n+    \"type\": \"https://errors.example.com/...\",  // optional\n+    \"alias\": \"user_not_found\"                   // optional\n+  }\n+]\n+```\n+\n+**Fields:**\n+| Field | Required | Description |\n+|-------|----------|-------------|\n+| `status` | Yes | HTTP status code (100-599) |\n+| `title` | Yes | Human-readable error title |\n+| `code` | Yes | GTS-formatted error code |\n+| `type` | No | URI for error documentation |\n+| `alias` | No | Short name override for generated accessor |\n+\n+### 2. GTS Code Format\n+\n+GTS codes follow a strict format for global type identification:\n+\n+```\n+gts.vendor.package.namespace.type.version~chain1~chain2~...~instanceGTX\n+```\n+\n+**Structure:**\n+- **Prefix:** Always starts with `gts.`\n+- **Chain separator:** `~` separates GTX segments\n+- **Segment separator:** `.` separates parts within a GTX\n+- **Final GTX:** Must have at least 5 segments: `vendor.package.namespace.type.version`","path":"docs/GTS_ERRORS.md","commit_id":"5bdb0f43b25858af78999718f7247813802b9634","original_commit_id":"5bdb0f43b25858af78999718f7247813802b9634","user":{"login":"devjow","id":239822647,"node_id":"U_kgDODktnNw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/239822647?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/devjow","html_url":"https://github.com/devjow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/devjow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/devjow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/devjow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/devjow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/devjow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/devjow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/devjow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/devjow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/devjow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"i see the term `GTX` but GTS has no such term that's meant to be smth like \"extension\", they're defined as types (schema, instance) and can be chained (inheritance). @Artifizer should we keep it?","created_at":"2026-01-27T11:19:21Z","updated_at":"2026-01-27T11:19:22Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/290#discussion_r2731520996","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/290","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2731520996"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/290#discussion_r2731520996"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/290"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2731520996/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":null,"original_line":75,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"MEMBER","original_position":75,"position":1,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2731757110","pull_request_review_id":3710883713,"id":2731757110,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs6i0042","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,1574 @@\n+# Unified Error System - Intention Document\n+\n+This document defines the architecture, rules, and implementation plan for a unified error handling system across the Hyperspot project. All REST API errors MUST have a GTS identifier, trace ID, and be registered in the types registry.\n+\n+## Table of Contents\n+\n+1. [Executive Summary](#executive-summary)\n+2. [Industry Research](#industry-research)\n+3. [Current State Analysis](#current-state-analysis)\n+4. [Requirements](#requirements)\n+5. [Implementation Rules](#implementation-rules)\n+6. [Migration Plan](#migration-plan)\n+7. [Examples](#examples)\n+8. [HTTP Headers](#http-headers)\n+9. [Security Considerations](#security-considerations)\n+10. [Appendix A: Error Category Definitions](#appendix-a-error-category-definitions)\n+11. [Appendix B: Retryable Error Guidelines](#appendix-b-retryable-error-guidelines)\n+12. [GTS System Errors Catalog](#gts-system-errors-catalog)\n+13. [References](#references)\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Executive Summary\n+\n+### Problem Statement\n+\n+The current error handling across Hyperspot modules is inconsistent:\n+- Some modules use `declare_errors!` macro with JSON catalogs\n+- Others define errors inline without GTS codes\n+- Errors are not registered in the types registry\n+- No standardized metadata/context fields\n+- Inconsistent trace ID propagation\n+\n+### Goals\n+\n+1. **Every REST API error** MUST have a valid GTS identifier\n+2. **Every error response** MUST include a trace ID for debugging\n+3. **All error types** MUST be registered in the types registry\n+4. **Consistent error schema** across all modules following RFC 9457\n+5. **Machine-readable error codes** for programmatic handling\n+6. **Error stack propagation** for nested service calls\n+\n+### Non-Goals\n+\n+- Changing internal domain error types (only API-facing errors)\n+- Modifying logging infrastructure\n+- Changing HTTP status code semantics\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Industry Research\n+\n+### How Major Tech Companies Handle Errors\n+\n+| Company | Standard | Key Features |\n+|---------|----------|--------------|\n+| **Google** | AIP-193 + gRPC Status | `reason` (UPPER_SNAKE_CASE), `domain` (service name), `metadata` (key-value context), `ErrorInfo`, `LocalizedMessage`, `Help` links |\n+| **Amazon AWS** | Custom JSON | `errorType`, `httpStatus`, `requestId`, `message`, custom error object serialization |\n+| **Twitter/X** | JSON with `errors` array | `code` (CAPS_CASE), `message`, `parameter`, `details`, `value` |\n+| **RFC 9457** | Problem Details | `type` (URI), `title`, `status`, `detail`, `instance`, extension members |\n+\n+### Key Patterns Identified\n+\n+1. **Machine-readable identifiers** - Unique codes for programmatic handling (Google's `reason`, Twitter's `code`)\n+2. **Domain/namespace separation** - Identify error source (Google's `domain`, our GTS vendor.package)\n+3. **Structured metadata** - Key-value context without parsing messages (Google's `ErrorInfo.metadata`)\n+4. **Trace/Request IDs** - Correlation for debugging (AWS `requestId`, our `trace_id`)\n+5. **Documentation links** - URIs to error documentation (RFC 9457 `type`, Google's `Help`)\n+6. **Error categorization** - System vs User-defined, Retryable vs Non-retryable\n+\n+### Google AIP-193 ErrorInfo Structure (Reference)\n+\n+```json\n+{\n+  \"error\": {\n+    \"code\": 429,\n+    \"message\": \"The zone 'us-east1-a' does not have enough resources...\",\n+    \"status\": \"RESOURCE_EXHAUSTED\",\n+    \"details\": [\n+      {\n+        \"@type\": \"type.googleapis.com/google.rpc.ErrorInfo\",\n+        \"reason\": \"RESOURCE_AVAILABILITY\",\n+        \"domain\": \"compute.googleapis.com\",\n+        \"metadata\": {\n+          \"zone\": \"us-east1-a\",\n+          \"vmType\": \"e2-medium\"\n+        }\n+      }\n+    ]\n+  }\n+}\n+```\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Current State Analysis\n+\n+### Existing Infrastructure\n+\n+1. **`Problem` struct** (`libs/modkit-errors/src/problem.rs`) - RFC 9457 compliant\n+   - Fields: `type_url`, `title`, `status`, `detail`, `instance`, `code`, `trace_id`, `errors`\n+   - Implements `IntoResponse` for Axum with automatic trace ID enrichment\n+\n+2. **`struct_to_gts_schema` macro** (`modules/types-registry/gts-rust/gts-macros/src/lib.rs`)\n+   - Attribute macro for explicit struct definitions with GTS IDs visible in code\n+   - Generates constants: `GTS_SCHEMA_ID`, `GTS_SCHEMA_JSON`, etc.\n+   - **This pattern will be adapted for error definitions**\n+\n+3. **`declare_errors!` macro** (`libs/modkit-errors-macro/src/lib.rs`) - **TO BE DEPRECATED**\n+   - Generates type-safe error enums from JSON catalogs\n+   - Problem: GTS IDs hidden in external JSON files, not visible to LLMs\n+   - Used by: `users_info` example, `modkit-odata`\n+\n+### Gaps Identified\n+\n+| Gap | Current State | Required State |\n+|-----|---------------|----------------|\n+| **Hidden GTS IDs** | JSON-based `declare_errors!` | Explicit `#[gts_error]` structs with visible GTS IDs |\n+| **Inconsistent definitions** | Some modules use inline errors | All modules use `#[gts_error]` structs |\n+| **No types registry** | Errors not registered | All errors registered as GTS types |\n+| **Missing metadata** | No structured context | Struct fields → `metadata` map |\n+| **Partial trace IDs** | Only in `IntoResponse` | Mandatory in all error responses |\n+| **No error categories** | Flat error codes | System/Operational/Client categories |\n+| **No error stack** | Single error | Upstream error chain propagation |\n+\n+### Current Module Migration Status\n+\n+| Module | Location | Status | Issues |\n+|--------|----------|--------|--------|\n+| **file_parser** | `modules/file_parser/` | 🔴 Not migrated | No GTS IDs, inline `Problem::new()` |\n+| **types-registry** | `modules/system/types-registry/` | 🟡 Partial | Has codes but not GTS format (e.g., `TYPES_REGISTRY_NOT_FOUND`) |\n+| **nodes_registry** | `modules/system/nodes_registry/` | 🔴 Not migrated | Non-GTS codes (e.g., `NODES_NOT_FOUND`) |\n+| **api_gateway** | `modules/system/api_gateway/` | 🔴 Not migrated | No Problem struct, simple error codes |\n+| **tenant_resolver** | `modules/system/tenant_resolver/` | 🔴 Not migrated | No GTS IDs |\n+| **simple-user-settings** | `modules/simple-user-settings/` | 🟡 Partial | Uses `declare_errors!` with old chain format |\n+| **modkit-auth** | `libs/modkit-auth/` | 🔴 Not migrated | No GTS IDs, custom `IntoResponse` |\n+| **modkit-odata** | `libs/modkit-odata/` | 🟡 Partial | Uses `declare_errors!` with old chain format |\n+| **users_info** (example) | `examples/modkit/users_info/` | 🟡 Partial | Uses `declare_errors!` with old chain format |\n+\n+#### Legend\n+- 🟢 **Migrated** - Uses `#[gts_error]` structs with proper base types\n+- 🟡 **Partial** - Has GTS IDs but uses deprecated `declare_errors!` or old format\n+- 🔴 **Not migrated** - No GTS IDs or non-GTS format codes\n+\n+#### GTS ID Format Note\n+\n+**Old chain format** (used by `declare_errors!`):\n+```\n+gts.hx.core.errors.err.v1~hx.module.error_name.v1\n+```\n+\n+**New format** (with `base` field):\n+```\n+gts.hx.module.namespace.error_name.v1~\n+```\n+The `base` field in `#[gts_error]` replaces the chain suffix, making inheritance explicit in code.\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Requirements\n+\n+### R1: Error Schema Requirements\n+\n+Every error returned from REST API MUST conform to the unified schema:\n+\n+```rust\n+pub struct Problem {\n+    // =========================================================================\n+    // REQUIRED FIELDS - Core error identification\n+    // =========================================================================\n+    \n+    /// URI reference identifying the problem type (GTS-based)\n+    /// Example: \"https://docs.hyperspot.com/errors/types_registry_entity_not_found_v1\"\n+    #[serde(rename = \"type\")]\n+    pub type_url: String,\n+    \n+    /// Human-readable summary of the problem type (static per error type)\n+    pub title: String,\n+    \n+    /// GTS error code (machine-readable identifier)\n+    pub code: String,\n+    \n+    /// Trace ID for request correlation\n+    pub trace_id: String,\n+    \n+    // =========================================================================\n+    // CONTEXTUAL FIELDS - Optional based on error context\n+    // =========================================================================\n+    \n+    /// HTTP status code. Optional because:\n+    /// - gRPC errors use different status codes\n+    /// - Internal/domain errors may not have HTTP context\n+    /// - Event-driven systems have no request/response\n+    /// When serializing for HTTP response, this is populated from error definition.\n+    #[serde(skip_serializing_if = \"Option::is_none\")]\n+    pub status: Option<u16>,\n+    \n+    /// Human-readable explanation specific to this occurrence.\n+    /// Optional - title may be sufficient for simple errors.\n+    #[serde(skip_serializing_if = \"Option::is_none\")]\n+    pub detail: Option<String>,\n+    \n+    /// Error category for client handling.\n+    /// Optional - can be inferred from base type hierarchy.\n+    #[serde(skip_serializing_if = \"Option::is_none\")]\n+    pub category: Option<ErrorCategory>,\n+    \n+    /// Whether client can retry this request.\n+    /// Optional - can be inferred from base type; not relevant for all contexts.\n+    #[serde(skip_serializing_if = \"Option::is_none\")]\n+    pub retryable: Option<bool>,\n+    \n+    /// URI identifying this specific occurrence (auto-populated from request path)\n+    #[serde(skip_serializing_if = \"Option::is_none\")]\n+    pub instance: Option<String>,\n+    \n+    /// Structured metadata (key-value context)\n+    #[serde(skip_serializing_if = \"Option::is_none\")]\n+    pub metadata: Option<HashMap<String, String>>,\n+    \n+    /// Validation errors for 4xx responses\n+    #[serde(skip_serializing_if = \"Option::is_none\")]\n+    pub errors: Option<Vec<ValidationViolation>>,\n+    \n+    /// Upstream error chain (when error_stack enabled)\n+    #[serde(skip_serializing_if = \"Option::is_none\")]\n+    pub upstream_errors: Option<Vec<UpstreamError>>,\n+}\n+\n+pub enum ErrorCategory {\n+    /// Platform-level execution errors (panics, OOM, internal bugs)\n+    System,\n+    /// Infrastructure/operational issues (DB unavailable, service down, rate limits)\n+    Operational,\n+    /// Client input/request errors (validation, not found, unauthorized)\n+    Client,\n+}\n+```\n+\n+#### Field Requirements Summary\n+\n+| Field | Required | Reason |\n+|-------|----------|--------|\n+| `type_url` | ✅ Yes | RFC 9457 requires problem type URI |\n+| `title` | ✅ Yes | Human-readable error name (static per type) |\n+| `code` | ✅ Yes | GTS identifier for machine processing |\n+| `trace_id` | ✅ Yes | Request correlation for debugging |\n+| `status` | ❌ No | Only relevant for HTTP; gRPC/events/domain errors don't need it |\n+| `detail` | ❌ No | Instance-specific message; title may suffice |\n+| `category` | ❌ No | Inherited from base type hierarchy |\n+| `retryable` | ❌ No | Inherited from base type; not relevant for all contexts |\n+| `instance` | ❌ No | Auto-populated from request path when applicable |\n+| `metadata` | ❌ No | Additional context key-value pairs |\n+| `errors` | ❌ No | Validation violations for 4xx errors |\n+| `upstream_errors` | ❌ No | Error chain from upstream services |\n+\n+**Note:** When converting to HTTP response, `status` is populated from the error definition. When the error is used in non-HTTP contexts (gRPC, domain logic, events), `status` remains `None`.\n+\n+### R2: GTS Identifier and Base Type Requirements\n+\n+Every error MUST have a valid GTS identifier and specify its base type using the `base` field.\n+\n+#### GTS ID Format\n+\n+```\n+gts.<vendor>.<package>.<namespace>.<type>.v<version>~\n+```\n+\n+**Examples:**\n+- `gts.hx.types_registry.entity.not_found.v1~` - Types registry not found error\n+- `gts.hx.file_parser.validation.invalid_format.v1~` - File parser validation error\n+- `gts.hx.system.runtime.timeout.v1~` - System timeout error\n+\n+#### Base Type Chaining\n+\n+Errors form an inheritance chain using the `base` field. The `base` field references another error struct type (not a string literal), similar to how `struct_to_gts_schema` works.\n+\n+The root base error type is:\n+\n+```rust\n+/// Root error type for all GTS errors.\n+#[gts_error(\n+    gts_id = \"gts.hx.core.errors.err.v1~\",\n+    base = true,  // Marks this as a root base type (no parent)\n+    title = \"Error\",\n+    // Optional attributes with defaults for inheritance:\n+    status = 500,        // Default HTTP status (optional, inherited by children)\n+    category = \"System\", // Default category (optional, inherited by children)\n+    retryable = false    // Default retryable (optional, inherited by children)\n+)]\n+pub struct BaseError;\n+```\n+\n+All module-specific errors MUST reference their base type as a struct (extending the appropriate logical/system error):\n+\n+```rust\n+use modkit_errors::system::logical::NotFoundError;\n+\n+/// Entity was not found in the types registry.\n+/// Note: status, category, retryable are inherited from NotFoundError if not specified.\n+#[gts_error(\n+    gts_id = \"gts.hx.types_registry.entity.not_found.v1~\",\n+    base = NotFoundError,  // Extends logical.not_found, not BaseError\n+    title = \"Entity Not Found\",\n+    // These are optional - inherited from base if omitted:\n+    // status = 404,      // Inherited from NotFoundError\n+    // category = \"Client\", // Inherited from NotFoundError  \n+    // retryable = false,   // Inherited from NotFoundError\n+)]\n+pub struct EntityNotFoundError {\n+    pub gts_id: String,\n+}\n+```\n+\n+#### Multi-Level Inheritance\n+\n+Errors can form deeper inheritance chains:\n+\n+```rust\n+/// Logical not found error (platform-level).\n+#[gts_error(\n+    gts_id = \"gts.hx.system.logical.not_found.v1~\",\n+    base = BaseError,  // Platform errors extend BaseError\n+    status = 404,\n+    title = \"Not Found\",\n+    category = \"Client\",\n+    retryable = false\n+)]\n+pub struct NotFoundError;\n+\n+/// Types registry entity not found (module-level).\n+#[gts_error(\n+    gts_id = \"gts.hx.types_registry.entity.not_found.v1~\",\n+    base = NotFoundError,  // Module errors extend logical errors\n+    status = 404,\n+    title = \"Entity Not Found\",\n+    category = \"Client\",\n+    retryable = false\n+)]\n+pub struct EntityNotFoundError {\n+    pub gts_id: String,\n+}\n+```\n+\n+#### Inheritance Hierarchy\n+\n+```\n+BaseError (gts.hx.core.errors.err.v1~)                              [base = true]\n+├── Transport Errors (hx.system.transport.*)                        [base = BaseError]\n+├── Runtime Errors (hx.system.runtime.*)                            [base = BaseError]\n+│   └── hx.types_registry.system.internal.v1~                       [base = runtime.internal]\n+├── HTTP Errors (hx.system.http.*)                                  [base = BaseError]\n+│   └── hx.auth.token_expired.v1~                                   [base = http.unauthorized]\n+├── gRPC Errors (hx.system.grpc.*)                                  [base = BaseError]\n+└── Logical Errors (hx.system.logical.*)                            [base = BaseError]\n+    ├── logical.not_found.v1~                                       [base = BaseError]\n+    │   ├── hx.types_registry.entity.not_found.v1~                  [base = logical.not_found]\n+    │   └── hx.db.entity.not_found.v1~                              [base = logical.not_found]\n+    ├── logical.already_exists.v1~                                  [base = BaseError]\n+    │   └── hx.types_registry.entity.already_exists.v1~             [base = logical.already_exists]\n+    └── logical.validation_failed.v1~                               [base = BaseError]\n+        └── hx.file_parser.validation.invalid_format.v1~            [base = logical.validation_failed]\n+```\n+\n+### R3: Trace ID Requirements\n+\n+- Every error response MUST include a non-empty `trace_id`\n+- Trace ID MUST be propagated from incoming request headers or generated\n+- Trace ID MUST be logged with the error for correlation\n+\n+### R4: Types Registry Integration\n+\n+- All error types MUST be registered in the types registry at startup\n+- Error schema MUST extend base error type: `gts.hx.core.errors.err.v1`\n+- Registration MUST include: code, title, status, category, retryable flag\n+\n+### R5: Standardized System Error Types\n+\n+See [GTS System Errors Catalog](#gts-system-errors-catalog) for the complete list of all system errors.\n+\n+### R6: Error Stack Propagation\n+\n+When a function calls another service/function that returns an error:\n+- The error SHOULD be wrapped with context\n+- `upstream_errors` array SHOULD contain the chain of errors\n+- Each upstream error includes: `code`, `title`, `detail`, `source`\n+- Propagation controlled by `error_stack` configuration flag\n+\n+---\n+\n+## GTS Error Code Format\n+\n+### Structure\n+\n+```\n+gts.<vendor>.<package>.<namespace>.<type>.<version>~<chain>\n+```\n+\n+### Components\n+\n+| Component | Description | Example |\n+|-----------|-------------|---------|\n+| `gts` | Global Type System prefix | `gts` |\n+| `vendor` | Organization identifier | `hx` (Hyperspot) |\n+| `package` | Module/service name | `types_registry`, `file_parser` |\n+| `namespace` | Error category | `entity`, `validation`, `runtime` |\n+| `type` | Specific error type | `not_found`, `invalid_format` |\n+| `version` | Schema version | `v1`, `v1.0` |\n+| `~chain` | Base type chain | `~hx.core.errors.err.v1` |\n+\n+### Validation Rules\n+\n+1. MUST start with `gts.`\n+2. All segments MUST be lowercase alphanumeric or underscore\n+3. No empty segments allowed\n+4. Final segment MUST be version format (`vN` or `vN.M`)\n+5. MUST chain from base error type\n+\n+### Short Name Derivation\n+\n+Short accessor names derived from final GTX segment:\n+```\n+gts.hx.core.errors.err.v1~hx.types_registry.entity.not_found.v1\n+                         └─────────────────────────────────────┘\n+                                          ↓\n+                         types_registry_entity_not_found_v1()\n+```\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Types Registry Integration\n+\n+### Error Type Schema\n+\n+```json\n+{\n+  \"gts_id\": \"gts.hx.types_registry.entity.not_found.v1~\",\n+  \"kind\": \"error\",\n+  \"schema\": {\n+    \"type\": \"object\",\n+    \"extends\": \"gts.hx.system.logical.not_found.v1~\",\n+    \"properties\": {\n+      \"status\": { \"const\": 404 },\n+      \"title\": { \"const\": \"Entity Not Found\" },\n+      \"category\": { \"const\": \"Client\" },\n+      \"retryable\": { \"const\": false }\n+    }\n+  },\n+  \"metadata\": {\n+    \"module\": \"types-registry\",\n+    \"documentation_url\": \"https://docs.hyperspot.com/errors/types_registry_entity_not_found_v1\"\n+  }\n+}\n+```\n+\n+### Registration Flow\n+\n+1. Module defines errors as explicit structs with `#[gts_error]` attribute in `src/errors.rs`\n+2. Each struct generates `ERROR_DEF` constant with GTS metadata\n+3. Module implements `all_error_definitions()` function returning all error definitions\n+4. At module startup (`on_ready`), errors are registered with types registry:\n+   ```rust\n+   impl Module for MyModule {\n+       async fn on_ready(&self, ctx: &ModuleContext) -> Result<()> {\n+           // Register all error types with types registry\n+           let errors = crate::errors::all_error_definitions();\n+           ctx.types_registry().register_errors(errors).await?;\n+           Ok(())\n+       }\n+   }\n+   ```\n+5. Types registry validates GTS format and schema compliance\n+6. Errors become discoverable via types registry API\n+\n+### API for Error Discovery\n+\n+```http\n+GET /api/types-registry/v1/types?kind=error&module=types-registry\n+\n+Response:\n+{\n+  \"items\": [\n+    {\n+      \"gts_id\": \"gts.hx.core.errors.err.v1~hx.types_registry.entity.not_found.v1\",\n+      \"status\": 404,\n+      \"title\": \"Entity Not Found\",\n+      \"category\": \"Client\",\n+      \"retryable\": false,\n+      \"documentation_url\": \"...\"\n+    }\n+  ]\n+}\n+```\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Implementation Rules\n+\n+### Rule 1: All Errors MUST Use Explicit Struct Definitions with `#[gts_error]`\n+\n+Errors are defined as explicit structs with the `#[gts_error]` attribute macro. This approach:\n+- Makes GTS IDs visible directly in code (better for LLM code generation)\n+- Provides compile-time validation\n+- Generates `Problem` conversion automatically\n+- Enables types registry integration\n+\n+```rust\n+// ✅ CORRECT - Explicit struct definition with visible GTS ID and base type reference\n+use modkit_errors::gts_error;\n+\n+// First, import the appropriate base error types from system errors\n+use modkit_errors::system::logical::{NotFoundError, AlreadyExistsError, ValidationFailedError};\n+\n+/// Entity was not found in the types registry.\n+#[gts_error(\n+    gts_id = \"gts.hx.types_registry.entity.not_found.v1~\",\n+    base = NotFoundError,  // Extends logical.not_found, not BaseError\n+    status = 404,\n+    title = \"Entity Not Found\",\n+    category = \"Client\",\n+    retryable = false\n+)]\n+pub struct EntityNotFoundError {\n+    /// The GTS ID that was not found\n+    pub gts_id: String,\n+}\n+\n+/// Entity already exists in the registry.\n+#[gts_error(\n+    gts_id = \"gts.hx.types_registry.entity.already_exists.v1~\",\n+    base = AlreadyExistsError,  // Extends logical.already_exists\n+    status = 409,\n+    title = \"Entity Already Exists\",\n+    category = \"Client\",\n+    retryable = false\n+)]\n+pub struct EntityAlreadyExistsError {\n+    /// The GTS ID that already exists\n+    pub gts_id: String,\n+}\n+\n+/// Invalid GTS ID format.\n+#[gts_error(\n+    gts_id = \"gts.hx.types_registry.validation.invalid_gts_id.v1~\",\n+    base = ValidationFailedError,  // Extends logical.validation_failed\n+    status = 400,\n+    title = \"Invalid GTS ID\",\n+    category = \"Client\",\n+    retryable = false\n+)]\n+pub struct InvalidGtsIdError {\n+    /// Description of the validation error\n+    pub message: String,\n+}\n+\n+// ❌ WRONG - Inline error definitions without GTS ID\n+impl From<DomainError> for Problem {\n+    fn from(e: DomainError) -> Self {\n+        Problem::new(StatusCode::NOT_FOUND, \"Not Found\", \"...\")\n+            .with_code(\"SOME_CODE\") // Not GTS format!\n+    }\n+}\n+\n+// ❌ WRONG - JSON-based declaration (GTS ID hidden in external file)\n+declare_errors! {\n+    path = \"gts/errors.json\",\n+    namespace = \"errors\",\n+    vis = \"pub\"\n+}\n+```\n+\n+### Rule 2: Error Struct Field Conventions\n+\n+Error structs contain context fields that become `metadata` in the Problem response:\n+\n+```rust\n+use modkit_errors::system::logical::ValidationFailedError as LogicalValidationFailed;\n+\n+/// Request validation failed (module-specific).\n+#[gts_error(\n+    gts_id = \"gts.hx.types_registry.validation.failed.v1~\",\n+    base = LogicalValidationFailed,  // Extends logical.validation_failed\n+    status = 422,\n+    title = \"Validation Failed\",\n+    category = \"Client\",\n+    retryable = false\n+)]\n+pub struct ValidationFailedError {\n+    /// Human-readable error message\n+    pub message: String,\n+    /// Field that failed validation (optional)\n+    #[gts_error(skip_metadata)]  // Don't include in metadata\n+    pub violations: Vec<ValidationViolation>,\n+}\n+```\n+\n+### Rule 3: Error Mapping Pattern\n+\n+```rust\n+use crate::errors::{EntityNotFoundError, EntityAlreadyExistsError, InvalidGtsIdError};\n+\n+pub fn domain_error_to_problem(e: &DomainError) -> Problem {\n+    match e {\n+        DomainError::NotFound { id } => {\n+            // into_problem() auto-populates trace_id from current tracing span\n+            EntityNotFoundError { gts_id: id.clone() }\n+                .into_problem()\n+                .with_detail(format!(\"Entity with GTS ID '{}' was not found\", id))\n+        }\n+        DomainError::AlreadyExists { id } => {\n+            EntityAlreadyExistsError { gts_id: id.clone() }\n+                .into_problem()\n+                .with_detail(format!(\"Entity with GTS ID '{}' already exists\", id))\n+        }\n+        DomainError::InvalidGtsId(msg) => {\n+            InvalidGtsIdError { message: msg.clone() }\n+                .into_problem()\n+        }\n+        // ...\n+    }\n+}\n+```\n+\n+### Rule 4: Trace ID Auto-Population\n+\n+Trace ID is **mandatory** in all error responses but **optional** in `into_problem()`. If not provided, it's auto-populated from the current tracing span.\n+\n+```rust\n+// Default: trace_id auto-populated from current tracing span\n+let problem = EntityNotFoundError { gts_id: id.clone() }\n+    .into_problem()  // trace_id extracted from tracing::Span::current()\n+    .with_detail(\"Entity not found\");\n+\n+// Override: explicitly pass trace_id if needed\n+let problem = EntityNotFoundError { gts_id: id.clone() }\n+    .into_problem()\n+    .with_trace_id(&custom_trace_id)  // Override auto-populated value\n+    .with_detail(\"Entity not found\");\n+```\n+\n+### Rule 5: Instance Auto-Population\n+\n+The `instance` field is **optional** and **auto-populated** from the request path in the Axum `IntoResponse` implementation. You don't need to pass it manually.\n+\n+```rust\n+// In Axum IntoResponse implementation\n+impl IntoResponse for Problem {\n+    fn into_response(self) -> Response {\n+        // Auto-populate instance from request URI if not set\n+        let problem = if self.instance.is_none() {\n+            // Instance is populated from request extensions or current URI\n+            if let Some(uri) = REQUEST_URI.try_with(|u| u.clone()).ok() {\n+                self.with_instance(uri.path())\n+            } else {\n+                self\n+            }\n+        } else {\n+            self\n+        };\n+        // ... rest of response building\n+    }\n+}\n+```\n+\n+If you need to override the instance manually, use `with_instance()`:\n+\n+```rust\n+let problem = EntityNotFoundError { gts_id: id.clone() }\n+    .into_problem()\n+    .with_instance(\"/custom/path\");  // Optional override\n+```\n+\n+### Rule 6: Error Registration at Startup\n+\n+Error definitions are **auto-collected** at compile time using the `#[gts_error]` macro with `linkme`. No manual registration list needed.\n+\n+#### How `linkme` Works\n+\n+The [`linkme`](https://docs.rs/linkme) crate provides **distributed slices** - a way to collect static items from across the crate into a single slice at link time.\n+\n+**Step 1: Define the collection point** (in `src/errors.rs`):\n+```rust\n+use linkme::distributed_slice;\n+\n+/// This is the \"collection point\" - an empty slice that will be filled at link time.\n+/// The linker will gather all items marked with #[distributed_slice(ERROR_DEFINITIONS)]\n+/// and place them contiguously in this slice.\n+#[distributed_slice]\n+pub static ERROR_DEFINITIONS: [&'static GtsErrorDefStatic];\n+```\n+\n+**Step 2: Each `#[gts_error]` macro generates a contributor**:\n+```rust\n+// When you write:\n+#[gts_error(\n+    gts_id = \"gts.hx.types_registry.entity.not_found.v1~\",\n+    base = NotFoundError,  // Extends logical.not_found\n+    status = 404,\n+    ...\n+)]\n+pub struct EntityNotFoundError { ... }\n+\n+// The macro generates (among other things):\n+impl EntityNotFoundError {\n+    pub const ERROR_DEF: GtsErrorDefStatic = GtsErrorDefStatic { ... };\n+}\n+\n+// AND this linkme contributor:\n+#[linkme::distributed_slice(crate::errors::ERROR_DEFINITIONS)]\n+#[linkme(crate = linkme)]\n+static __ENTITY_NOT_FOUND_ERROR_DEF: &'static GtsErrorDefStatic = &EntityNotFoundError::ERROR_DEF;\n+```\n+\n+**Step 3: At link time, the linker collects all contributors**:\n+```\n+┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n+│                    Link-Time Collection                          │\n+├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n+│                                                                  │\n+│  EntityNotFoundError::ERROR_DEF ──────┐                         │\n+│  EntityAlreadyExistsError::ERROR_DEF ─┼──► ERROR_DEFINITIONS[]  │\n+│  InvalidGtsIdError::ERROR_DEF ────────┤    (contiguous slice)   │\n+│  ValidationFailedError::ERROR_DEF ────┤                         │\n+│  ServiceNotReadyError::ERROR_DEF ─────┤                         │\n+│  InternalError::ERROR_DEF ────────────┘                         │\n+│                                                                  │\n+│  The linker places all #[distributed_slice(ERROR_DEFINITIONS)]  │\n+│  items into a contiguous memory section, making them accessible │\n+│  as a single &[&'static GtsErrorDefStatic] slice at runtime.    │\n+│                                                                  │\n+└─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘\n+```\n+\n+**Step 4: Access at runtime**:\n+```rust\n+pub fn all_error_definitions() -> &'static [&'static GtsErrorDefStatic] {\n+    &ERROR_DEFINITIONS  // Returns slice with ALL error defs, auto-collected\n+}\n+```\n+\n+#### Why This Works\n+\n+- **Linker magic**: `linkme` uses platform-specific linker sections (`.init_array` on Linux, `__DATA,__mod_init_func` on macOS) to collect items\n+- **Zero runtime cost**: Collection happens at link time, not runtime\n+- **Compile-time guarantee**: If you use `#[gts_error]`, it's automatically in the slice\n+- **No manual list**: Impossible to forget an error - the macro handles registration\n+\n+#### Module Startup\n+\n+```rust\n+impl Module for MyModule {\n+    async fn on_ready(&self, ctx: &ModuleContext) -> Result<()> {\n+        // All errors are auto-collected - no way to forget one!\n+        let errors = crate::errors::all_error_definitions();\n+        ctx.types_registry().register_errors(errors).await?;\n+        Ok(())\n+    }\n+}\n+```\n+\n+### Rule 7: Metadata for Dynamic Context\n+\n+```rust\n+// ✅ CORRECT - Use metadata for dynamic values\n+ValidationFailedError { message: \"Validation failed\".to_string(), violations: vec![] }\n+    .into_problem()  // trace_id auto-populated from tracing span\n+    .with_metadata([\n+        (\"field\", \"email\"),\n+        (\"constraint\", \"must be valid email format\"),\n+        (\"provided_value\", \"[REDACTED]\"), // Never expose sensitive data\n+    ])\n+\n+// ❌ WRONG - Parsing dynamic values from detail string\n+ValidationFailedError { \n+    message: \"Field 'email' failed constraint 'must be valid email'\".to_string(),\n+    violations: vec![] \n+}\n+    .into_problem()\n+```\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Migration Plan\n+\n+### Phase 1: Create `#[gts_error]` Macro\n+\n+1. Create new proc-macro crate `libs/modkit-errors-macro-v2/` with `#[gts_error]` attribute macro\n+2. Implement macro to generate:\n+   - `GTS_ID`, `STATUS`, `TITLE`, `CATEGORY`, `RETRYABLE` constants\n+   - `ERROR_DEF` static for registration\n+   - `into_problem()` method\n+   - `to_metadata()` for struct fields → HashMap conversion\n+   - `Display` and `Error` trait implementations\n+3. Add compile-time GTS format validation\n+4. Add field attribute `#[gts_error(skip_metadata)]` and `#[gts_error(as_errors)]`\n+\n+### Phase 2: Extend Problem Struct\n+\n+1. Extend `Problem` struct with new fields:\n+   - `category: ErrorCategory`\n+   - `retryable: bool`\n+   - `metadata: Option<HashMap<String, String>>`\n+   - `upstream_errors: Option<Vec<UpstreamError>>`\n+   - Make `trace_id` non-optional (String instead of Option<String>)\n+2. Add builder methods: `with_category()`, `with_retryable()`, `with_metadata()`\n+3. Update `IntoResponse` implementation\n+\n+### Phase 3: Types Registry Integration\n+\n+1. Define `GtsErrorDef` trait and `GtsErrorDefStatic` struct\n+2. Add error registration API to types registry\n+3. Implement `register_errors()` method in module context\n+4. Add error discovery endpoint: `GET /api/types-registry/v1/types?kind=error`\n+\n+### Phase 4: Module Migration\n+\n+Migrate modules to explicit struct-based errors:\n+1. `types-registry` - Create `src/errors.rs` with `#[gts_error]` structs\n+2. `file_parser` - Create `src/errors.rs` with `#[gts_error]` structs\n+3. `nodes_registry` - Create `src/errors.rs` with `#[gts_error]` structs\n+4. `api_gateway` - Create `src/errors.rs` with `#[gts_error]` structs\n+\n+### Phase 5: System Errors Library\n+\n+1. Create `libs/modkit-errors/src/system_errors.rs` with common errors:\n+   - `InternalServerError`, `ServiceUnavailableError`, `GatewayTimeoutError`\n+   - `UnauthorizedError`, `ForbiddenError`, `NotFoundError`\n+   - `BadRequestError`, `ValidationFailedError`, `ConflictError`\n+   - `RateLimitedError`\n+2. Export from `modkit::errors::system` for all modules to use\n+3. Register system errors at platform startup\n+\n+### Phase 6: Deprecate `declare_errors!`\n+\n+1. Mark `declare_errors!` macro as deprecated\n+2. Update `GTS_ERRORS.md` documentation\n+3. Add migration guide from JSON-based to struct-based errors\n+4. Remove JSON error catalogs from migrated modules\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Examples\n+\n+### Example 1: Complete Error Response\n+\n+```json\n+{\n+  \"type\": \"https://docs.hyperspot.com/errors/types_registry_entity_not_found_v1\",\n+  \"title\": \"Entity Not Found\",\n+  \"status\": 404,\n+  \"detail\": \"Entity with GTS ID 'gts.hx.example.test.v1' was not found in the registry\",\n+  \"instance\": \"/api/types-registry/v1/types/gts.hx.example.test.v1\",\n+  \"code\": \"gts.hx.core.errors.err.v1~hx.types_registry.entity.not_found.v1\",\n+  \"trace_id\": \"abc123-def456-ghi789\",\n+  \"category\": \"Client\",\n+  \"retryable\": false,\n+  \"metadata\": {\n+    \"gts_id\": \"gts.hx.example.test.v1\",\n+    \"searched_at\": \"2026-01-19T13:30:00Z\"\n+  }\n+}\n+```\n+\n+### Example 2: Validation Error with Multiple Violations\n+\n+```json\n+{\n+  \"type\": \"https://docs.hyperspot.com/errors/validation_failed_v1\",\n+  \"title\": \"Validation Failed\",\n+  \"status\": 422,\n+  \"detail\": \"Request validation failed with 2 errors\",\n+  \"instance\": \"/api/users/v1/users\",\n+  \"code\": \"gts.hx.core.errors.err.v1~hx.system.validation_failed.v1\",\n+  \"trace_id\": \"req-12345\",\n+  \"category\": \"Client\",\n+  \"retryable\": false,\n+  \"errors\": [\n+    {\n+      \"field\": \"email\",\n+      \"message\": \"Must be a valid email address\",\n+      \"code\": \"INVALID_EMAIL_FORMAT\"\n+    },\n+    {\n+      \"field\": \"age\",\n+      \"message\": \"Must be at least 18\",\n+      \"code\": \"MIN_VALUE_VIOLATION\"\n+    }\n+  ]\n+}\n+```\n+\n+### Example 3: Error with Upstream Chain\n+\n+```json\n+{\n+  \"type\": \"https://docs.hyperspot.com/errors/upstream_error_v1\",\n+  \"title\": \"Upstream Service Error\",\n+  \"status\": 502,\n+  \"detail\": \"Failed to fetch user data from identity service\",\n+  \"instance\": \"/api/users/v1/users/123/profile\",\n+  \"code\": \"gts.hx.core.errors.err.v1~hx.users.upstream.identity_failed.v1\",\n+  \"trace_id\": \"trace-abc-123\",\n+  \"category\": \"System\",\n+  \"retryable\": true,\n+  \"upstream_errors\": [\n+    {\n+      \"code\": \"gts.hx.core.errors.err.v1~hx.identity.user.not_found.v1\",\n+      \"title\": \"User Not Found\",\n+      \"detail\": \"User 123 not found in identity service\",\n+      \"source\": \"identity-service\"\n+    }\n+  ]\n+}\n+```\n+\n+### Example 4: Complete Error Module Definition","path":"intended_design/UNIFIED_ERROR_SYSTEM.md","commit_id":"5bdb0f43b25858af78999718f7247813802b9634","original_commit_id":"5bdb0f43b25858af78999718f7247813802b9634","user":{"login":"devjow","id":239822647,"node_id":"U_kgDODktnNw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/239822647?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/devjow","html_url":"https://github.com/devjow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/devjow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/devjow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/devjow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/devjow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/devjow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/devjow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/devjow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/devjow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/devjow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"the `/src/error.rs` violates separation of concerns because the error definition knows about HTTP status codes, which is the responsibility of `/src/api/rest/error.rs`. what if someone integrates with gRPC, which uses different status codes? the error would need to change even though the business meaning didn't","created_at":"2026-01-27T12:21:45Z","updated_at":"2026-01-27T12:21:45Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/290#discussion_r2731757110","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/290","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2731757110"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/290#discussion_r2731757110"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/290"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2731757110/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":null,"original_line":916,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"MEMBER","original_position":916,"position":1,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2735807271","pull_request_review_id":3715718572,"id":2735807271,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs6jERsn","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,1574 @@\n+# Unified Error System - Intention Document\n+\n+This document defines the architecture, rules, and implementation plan for a unified error handling system across the Hyperspot project. All REST API errors MUST have a GTS identifier, trace ID, and be registered in the types registry.\n+\n+## Table of Contents\n+\n+1. [Executive Summary](#executive-summary)\n+2. [Industry Research](#industry-research)\n+3. [Current State Analysis](#current-state-analysis)\n+4. [Requirements](#requirements)\n+5. [Implementation Rules](#implementation-rules)\n+6. [Migration Plan](#migration-plan)\n+7. [Examples](#examples)\n+8. [HTTP Headers](#http-headers)\n+9. [Security Considerations](#security-considerations)\n+10. [Appendix A: Error Category Definitions](#appendix-a-error-category-definitions)\n+11. [Appendix B: Retryable Error Guidelines](#appendix-b-retryable-error-guidelines)\n+12. [GTS System Errors Catalog](#gts-system-errors-catalog)\n+13. [References](#references)\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Executive Summary\n+\n+### Problem Statement\n+\n+The current error handling across Hyperspot modules is inconsistent:\n+- Some modules use `declare_errors!` macro with JSON catalogs\n+- Others define errors inline without GTS codes\n+- Errors are not registered in the types registry\n+- No standardized metadata/context fields\n+- Inconsistent trace ID propagation\n+\n+### Goals\n+\n+1. **Every REST API error** MUST have a valid GTS identifier\n+2. **Every error response** MUST include a trace ID for debugging\n+3. **All error types** MUST be registered in the types registry\n+4. **Consistent error schema** across all modules following RFC 9457\n+5. **Machine-readable error codes** for programmatic handling\n+6. **Error stack propagation** for nested service calls\n+\n+### Non-Goals\n+\n+- Changing internal domain error types (only API-facing errors)\n+- Modifying logging infrastructure\n+- Changing HTTP status code semantics\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Industry Research\n+\n+### How Major Tech Companies Handle Errors\n+\n+| Company | Standard | Key Features |\n+|---------|----------|--------------|\n+| **Google** | AIP-193 + gRPC Status | `reason` (UPPER_SNAKE_CASE), `domain` (service name), `metadata` (key-value context), `ErrorInfo`, `LocalizedMessage`, `Help` links |\n+| **Amazon AWS** | Custom JSON | `errorType`, `httpStatus`, `requestId`, `message`, custom error object serialization |\n+| **Twitter/X** | JSON with `errors` array | `code` (CAPS_CASE), `message`, `parameter`, `details`, `value` |\n+| **RFC 9457** | Problem Details | `type` (URI), `title`, `status`, `detail`, `instance`, extension members |\n+\n+### Key Patterns Identified\n+\n+1. **Machine-readable identifiers** - Unique codes for programmatic handling (Google's `reason`, Twitter's `code`)\n+2. **Domain/namespace separation** - Identify error source (Google's `domain`, our GTS vendor.package)\n+3. **Structured metadata** - Key-value context without parsing messages (Google's `ErrorInfo.metadata`)\n+4. **Trace/Request IDs** - Correlation for debugging (AWS `requestId`, our `trace_id`)\n+5. **Documentation links** - URIs to error documentation (RFC 9457 `type`, Google's `Help`)\n+6. **Error categorization** - System vs User-defined, Retryable vs Non-retryable\n+\n+### Google AIP-193 ErrorInfo Structure (Reference)\n+\n+```json\n+{\n+  \"error\": {\n+    \"code\": 429,\n+    \"message\": \"The zone 'us-east1-a' does not have enough resources...\",\n+    \"status\": \"RESOURCE_EXHAUSTED\",\n+    \"details\": [\n+      {\n+        \"@type\": \"type.googleapis.com/google.rpc.ErrorInfo\",\n+        \"reason\": \"RESOURCE_AVAILABILITY\",\n+        \"domain\": \"compute.googleapis.com\",\n+        \"metadata\": {\n+          \"zone\": \"us-east1-a\",\n+          \"vmType\": \"e2-medium\"\n+        }\n+      }\n+    ]\n+  }\n+}\n+```\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Current State Analysis\n+\n+### Existing Infrastructure\n+\n+1. **`Problem` struct** (`libs/modkit-errors/src/problem.rs`) - RFC 9457 compliant\n+   - Fields: `type_url`, `title`, `status`, `detail`, `instance`, `code`, `trace_id`, `errors`\n+   - Implements `IntoResponse` for Axum with automatic trace ID enrichment\n+\n+2. **`struct_to_gts_schema` macro** (`modules/types-registry/gts-rust/gts-macros/src/lib.rs`)\n+   - Attribute macro for explicit struct definitions with GTS IDs visible in code\n+   - Generates constants: `GTS_SCHEMA_ID`, `GTS_SCHEMA_JSON`, etc.\n+   - **This pattern will be adapted for error definitions**\n+\n+3. **`declare_errors!` macro** (`libs/modkit-errors-macro/src/lib.rs`) - **TO BE DEPRECATED**\n+   - Generates type-safe error enums from JSON catalogs\n+   - Problem: GTS IDs hidden in external JSON files, not visible to LLMs\n+   - Used by: `users_info` example, `modkit-odata`\n+\n+### Gaps Identified\n+\n+| Gap | Current State | Required State |\n+|-----|---------------|----------------|\n+| **Hidden GTS IDs** | JSON-based `declare_errors!` | Explicit `#[gts_error]` structs with visible GTS IDs |\n+| **Inconsistent definitions** | Some modules use inline errors | All modules use `#[gts_error]` structs |\n+| **No types registry** | Errors not registered | All errors registered as GTS types |\n+| **Missing metadata** | No structured context | Struct fields → `metadata` map |\n+| **Partial trace IDs** | Only in `IntoResponse` | Mandatory in all error responses |\n+| **No error categories** | Flat error codes | System/Operational/Client categories |\n+| **No error stack** | Single error | Upstream error chain propagation |\n+\n+### Current Module Migration Status\n+\n+| Module | Location | Status | Issues |\n+|--------|----------|--------|--------|\n+| **file_parser** | `modules/file_parser/` | 🔴 Not migrated | No GTS IDs, inline `Problem::new()` |\n+| **types-registry** | `modules/system/types-registry/` | 🟡 Partial | Has codes but not GTS format (e.g., `TYPES_REGISTRY_NOT_FOUND`) |\n+| **nodes_registry** | `modules/system/nodes_registry/` | 🔴 Not migrated | Non-GTS codes (e.g., `NODES_NOT_FOUND`) |\n+| **api_gateway** | `modules/system/api_gateway/` | 🔴 Not migrated | No Problem struct, simple error codes |\n+| **tenant_resolver** | `modules/system/tenant_resolver/` | 🔴 Not migrated | No GTS IDs |\n+| **simple-user-settings** | `modules/simple-user-settings/` | 🟡 Partial | Uses `declare_errors!` with old chain format |\n+| **modkit-auth** | `libs/modkit-auth/` | 🔴 Not migrated | No GTS IDs, custom `IntoResponse` |\n+| **modkit-odata** | `libs/modkit-odata/` | 🟡 Partial | Uses `declare_errors!` with old chain format |\n+| **users_info** (example) | `examples/modkit/users_info/` | 🟡 Partial | Uses `declare_errors!` with old chain format |\n+\n+#### Legend\n+- 🟢 **Migrated** - Uses `#[gts_error]` structs with proper base types\n+- 🟡 **Partial** - Has GTS IDs but uses deprecated `declare_errors!` or old format\n+- 🔴 **Not migrated** - No GTS IDs or non-GTS format codes\n+\n+#### GTS ID Format Note\n+\n+**Old chain format** (used by `declare_errors!`):\n+```\n+gts.hx.core.errors.err.v1~hx.module.error_name.v1\n+```\n+\n+**New format** (with `base` field):\n+```\n+gts.hx.module.namespace.error_name.v1~","path":"intended_design/UNIFIED_ERROR_SYSTEM.md","commit_id":"5bdb0f43b25858af78999718f7247813802b9634","original_commit_id":"5bdb0f43b25858af78999718f7247813802b9634","user":{"login":"MikeFalcon77","id":3686170,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM2ODYxNzA=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3686170?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/MikeFalcon77","html_url":"https://github.com/MikeFalcon77","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MikeFalcon77/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MikeFalcon77/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MikeFalcon77/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MikeFalcon77/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MikeFalcon77/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MikeFalcon77/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MikeFalcon77/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MikeFalcon77/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MikeFalcon77/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"*.hx.* should be *.cf.* now","created_at":"2026-01-28T09:53:51Z","updated_at":"2026-01-28T12:02:23Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/290#discussion_r2735807271","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/290","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2735807271"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/290#discussion_r2735807271"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/290"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2735807271/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":null,"original_line":154,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"MEMBER","original_position":154,"position":1,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2736265169","pull_request_review_id":3715718572,"id":2736265169,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs6jGBfR","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,1574 @@\n+# Unified Error System - Intention Document\n+\n+This document defines the architecture, rules, and implementation plan for a unified error handling system across the Hyperspot project. All REST API errors MUST have a GTS identifier, trace ID, and be registered in the types registry.\n+\n+## Table of Contents\n+\n+1. [Executive Summary](#executive-summary)\n+2. [Industry Research](#industry-research)\n+3. [Current State Analysis](#current-state-analysis)\n+4. [Requirements](#requirements)\n+5. [Implementation Rules](#implementation-rules)\n+6. [Migration Plan](#migration-plan)\n+7. [Examples](#examples)\n+8. [HTTP Headers](#http-headers)\n+9. [Security Considerations](#security-considerations)\n+10. [Appendix A: Error Category Definitions](#appendix-a-error-category-definitions)\n+11. [Appendix B: Retryable Error Guidelines](#appendix-b-retryable-error-guidelines)\n+12. [GTS System Errors Catalog](#gts-system-errors-catalog)\n+13. [References](#references)\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Executive Summary\n+\n+### Problem Statement\n+\n+The current error handling across Hyperspot modules is inconsistent:\n+- Some modules use `declare_errors!` macro with JSON catalogs\n+- Others define errors inline without GTS codes\n+- Errors are not registered in the types registry\n+- No standardized metadata/context fields\n+- Inconsistent trace ID propagation\n+\n+### Goals\n+\n+1. **Every REST API error** MUST have a valid GTS identifier\n+2. **Every error response** MUST include a trace ID for debugging\n+3. **All error types** MUST be registered in the types registry\n+4. **Consistent error schema** across all modules following RFC 9457\n+5. **Machine-readable error codes** for programmatic handling\n+6. **Error stack propagation** for nested service calls\n+\n+### Non-Goals\n+\n+- Changing internal domain error types (only API-facing errors)\n+- Modifying logging infrastructure\n+- Changing HTTP status code semantics\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Industry Research\n+\n+### How Major Tech Companies Handle Errors\n+\n+| Company | Standard | Key Features |\n+|---------|----------|--------------|\n+| **Google** | AIP-193 + gRPC Status | `reason` (UPPER_SNAKE_CASE), `domain` (service name), `metadata` (key-value context), `ErrorInfo`, `LocalizedMessage`, `Help` links |\n+| **Amazon AWS** | Custom JSON | `errorType`, `httpStatus`, `requestId`, `message`, custom error object serialization |\n+| **Twitter/X** | JSON with `errors` array | `code` (CAPS_CASE), `message`, `parameter`, `details`, `value` |\n+| **RFC 9457** | Problem Details | `type` (URI), `title`, `status`, `detail`, `instance`, extension members |\n+\n+### Key Patterns Identified\n+\n+1. **Machine-readable identifiers** - Unique codes for programmatic handling (Google's `reason`, Twitter's `code`)\n+2. **Domain/namespace separation** - Identify error source (Google's `domain`, our GTS vendor.package)\n+3. **Structured metadata** - Key-value context without parsing messages (Google's `ErrorInfo.metadata`)\n+4. **Trace/Request IDs** - Correlation for debugging (AWS `requestId`, our `trace_id`)\n+5. **Documentation links** - URIs to error documentation (RFC 9457 `type`, Google's `Help`)\n+6. **Error categorization** - System vs User-defined, Retryable vs Non-retryable\n+\n+### Google AIP-193 ErrorInfo Structure (Reference)\n+\n+```json\n+{\n+  \"error\": {\n+    \"code\": 429,\n+    \"message\": \"The zone 'us-east1-a' does not have enough resources...\",\n+    \"status\": \"RESOURCE_EXHAUSTED\",\n+    \"details\": [\n+      {\n+        \"@type\": \"type.googleapis.com/google.rpc.ErrorInfo\",\n+        \"reason\": \"RESOURCE_AVAILABILITY\",\n+        \"domain\": \"compute.googleapis.com\",\n+        \"metadata\": {\n+          \"zone\": \"us-east1-a\",\n+          \"vmType\": \"e2-medium\"\n+        }\n+      }\n+    ]\n+  }\n+}\n+```\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Current State Analysis\n+\n+### Existing Infrastructure\n+\n+1. **`Problem` struct** (`libs/modkit-errors/src/problem.rs`) - RFC 9457 compliant\n+   - Fields: `type_url`, `title`, `status`, `detail`, `instance`, `code`, `trace_id`, `errors`\n+   - Implements `IntoResponse` for Axum with automatic trace ID enrichment\n+\n+2. **`struct_to_gts_schema` macro** (`modules/types-registry/gts-rust/gts-macros/src/lib.rs`)\n+   - Attribute macro for explicit struct definitions with GTS IDs visible in code\n+   - Generates constants: `GTS_SCHEMA_ID`, `GTS_SCHEMA_JSON`, etc.\n+   - **This pattern will be adapted for error definitions**\n+\n+3. **`declare_errors!` macro** (`libs/modkit-errors-macro/src/lib.rs`) - **TO BE DEPRECATED**\n+   - Generates type-safe error enums from JSON catalogs\n+   - Problem: GTS IDs hidden in external JSON files, not visible to LLMs\n+   - Used by: `users_info` example, `modkit-odata`\n+\n+### Gaps Identified\n+\n+| Gap | Current State | Required State |\n+|-----|---------------|----------------|\n+| **Hidden GTS IDs** | JSON-based `declare_errors!` | Explicit `#[gts_error]` structs with visible GTS IDs |\n+| **Inconsistent definitions** | Some modules use inline errors | All modules use `#[gts_error]` structs |\n+| **No types registry** | Errors not registered | All errors registered as GTS types |\n+| **Missing metadata** | No structured context | Struct fields → `metadata` map |\n+| **Partial trace IDs** | Only in `IntoResponse` | Mandatory in all error responses |\n+| **No error categories** | Flat error codes | System/Operational/Client categories |\n+| **No error stack** | Single error | Upstream error chain propagation |\n+\n+### Current Module Migration Status\n+\n+| Module | Location | Status | Issues |\n+|--------|----------|--------|--------|\n+| **file_parser** | `modules/file_parser/` | 🔴 Not migrated | No GTS IDs, inline `Problem::new()` |\n+| **types-registry** | `modules/system/types-registry/` | 🟡 Partial | Has codes but not GTS format (e.g., `TYPES_REGISTRY_NOT_FOUND`) |\n+| **nodes_registry** | `modules/system/nodes_registry/` | 🔴 Not migrated | Non-GTS codes (e.g., `NODES_NOT_FOUND`) |\n+| **api_gateway** | `modules/system/api_gateway/` | 🔴 Not migrated | No Problem struct, simple error codes |\n+| **tenant_resolver** | `modules/system/tenant_resolver/` | 🔴 Not migrated | No GTS IDs |\n+| **simple-user-settings** | `modules/simple-user-settings/` | 🟡 Partial | Uses `declare_errors!` with old chain format |\n+| **modkit-auth** | `libs/modkit-auth/` | 🔴 Not migrated | No GTS IDs, custom `IntoResponse` |\n+| **modkit-odata** | `libs/modkit-odata/` | 🟡 Partial | Uses `declare_errors!` with old chain format |\n+| **users_info** (example) | `examples/modkit/users_info/` | 🟡 Partial | Uses `declare_errors!` with old chain format |\n+\n+#### Legend\n+- 🟢 **Migrated** - Uses `#[gts_error]` structs with proper base types\n+- 🟡 **Partial** - Has GTS IDs but uses deprecated `declare_errors!` or old format\n+- 🔴 **Not migrated** - No GTS IDs or non-GTS format codes\n+\n+#### GTS ID Format Note\n+\n+**Old chain format** (used by `declare_errors!`):\n+```\n+gts.hx.core.errors.err.v1~hx.module.error_name.v1\n+```\n+\n+**New format** (with `base` field):\n+```\n+gts.hx.module.namespace.error_name.v1~\n+```\n+The `base` field in `#[gts_error]` replaces the chain suffix, making inheritance explicit in code.\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Requirements\n+\n+### R1: Error Schema Requirements\n+\n+Every error returned from REST API MUST conform to the unified schema:\n+\n+```rust\n+pub struct Problem {\n+    // =========================================================================\n+    // REQUIRED FIELDS - Core error identification\n+    // =========================================================================\n+    \n+    /// URI reference identifying the problem type (GTS-based)\n+    /// Example: \"https://docs.hyperspot.com/errors/types_registry_entity_not_found_v1\"\n+    #[serde(rename = \"type\")]\n+    pub type_url: String,\n+    \n+    /// Human-readable summary of the problem type (static per error type)\n+    pub title: String,\n+    \n+    /// GTS error code (machine-readable identifier)\n+    pub code: String,\n+    \n+    /// Trace ID for request correlation\n+    pub trace_id: String,\n+    \n+    // =========================================================================\n+    // CONTEXTUAL FIELDS - Optional based on error context\n+    // =========================================================================\n+    \n+    /// HTTP status code. Optional because:\n+    /// - gRPC errors use different status codes\n+    /// - Internal/domain errors may not have HTTP context\n+    /// - Event-driven systems have no request/response\n+    /// When serializing for HTTP response, this is populated from error definition.\n+    #[serde(skip_serializing_if = \"Option::is_none\")]\n+    pub status: Option<u16>,\n+    \n+    /// Human-readable explanation specific to this occurrence.\n+    /// Optional - title may be sufficient for simple errors.\n+    #[serde(skip_serializing_if = \"Option::is_none\")]\n+    pub detail: Option<String>,\n+    \n+    /// Error category for client handling.\n+    /// Optional - can be inferred from base type hierarchy.\n+    #[serde(skip_serializing_if = \"Option::is_none\")]\n+    pub category: Option<ErrorCategory>,\n+    \n+    /// Whether client can retry this request.\n+    /// Optional - can be inferred from base type; not relevant for all contexts.\n+    #[serde(skip_serializing_if = \"Option::is_none\")]\n+    pub retryable: Option<bool>,\n+    \n+    /// URI identifying this specific occurrence (auto-populated from request path)\n+    #[serde(skip_serializing_if = \"Option::is_none\")]\n+    pub instance: Option<String>,\n+    \n+    /// Structured metadata (key-value context)\n+    #[serde(skip_serializing_if = \"Option::is_none\")]\n+    pub metadata: Option<HashMap<String, String>>,\n+    \n+    /// Validation errors for 4xx responses\n+    #[serde(skip_serializing_if = \"Option::is_none\")]\n+    pub errors: Option<Vec<ValidationViolation>>,\n+    \n+    /// Upstream error chain (when error_stack enabled)\n+    #[serde(skip_serializing_if = \"Option::is_none\")]\n+    pub upstream_errors: Option<Vec<UpstreamError>>,\n+}\n+\n+pub enum ErrorCategory {\n+    /// Platform-level execution errors (panics, OOM, internal bugs)\n+    System,\n+    /// Infrastructure/operational issues (DB unavailable, service down, rate limits)\n+    Operational,\n+    /// Client input/request errors (validation, not found, unauthorized)\n+    Client,\n+}\n+```\n+\n+#### Field Requirements Summary\n+\n+| Field | Required | Reason |\n+|-------|----------|--------|\n+| `type_url` | ✅ Yes | RFC 9457 requires problem type URI |\n+| `title` | ✅ Yes | Human-readable error name (static per type) |\n+| `code` | ✅ Yes | GTS identifier for machine processing |\n+| `trace_id` | ✅ Yes | Request correlation for debugging |\n+| `status` | ❌ No | Only relevant for HTTP; gRPC/events/domain errors don't need it |\n+| `detail` | ❌ No | Instance-specific message; title may suffice |\n+| `category` | ❌ No | Inherited from base type hierarchy |\n+| `retryable` | ❌ No | Inherited from base type; not relevant for all contexts |\n+| `instance` | ❌ No | Auto-populated from request path when applicable |\n+| `metadata` | ❌ No | Additional context key-value pairs |\n+| `errors` | ❌ No | Validation violations for 4xx errors |\n+| `upstream_errors` | ❌ No | Error chain from upstream services |\n+\n+**Note:** When converting to HTTP response, `status` is populated from the error definition. When the error is used in non-HTTP contexts (gRPC, domain logic, events), `status` remains `None`.\n+\n+### R2: GTS Identifier and Base Type Requirements\n+\n+Every error MUST have a valid GTS identifier and specify its base type using the `base` field.\n+\n+#### GTS ID Format\n+\n+```\n+gts.<vendor>.<package>.<namespace>.<type>.v<version>~\n+```\n+\n+**Examples:**\n+- `gts.hx.types_registry.entity.not_found.v1~` - Types registry not found error\n+- `gts.hx.file_parser.validation.invalid_format.v1~` - File parser validation error\n+- `gts.hx.system.runtime.timeout.v1~` - System timeout error\n+\n+#### Base Type Chaining\n+\n+Errors form an inheritance chain using the `base` field. The `base` field references another error struct type (not a string literal), similar to how `struct_to_gts_schema` works.\n+\n+The root base error type is:\n+\n+```rust\n+/// Root error type for all GTS errors.\n+#[gts_error(\n+    gts_id = \"gts.hx.core.errors.err.v1~\",\n+    base = true,  // Marks this as a root base type (no parent)\n+    title = \"Error\",\n+    // Optional attributes with defaults for inheritance:\n+    status = 500,        // Default HTTP status (optional, inherited by children)\n+    category = \"System\", // Default category (optional, inherited by children)\n+    retryable = false    // Default retryable (optional, inherited by children)\n+)]\n+pub struct BaseError;\n+```\n+\n+All module-specific errors MUST reference their base type as a struct (extending the appropriate logical/system error):\n+\n+```rust\n+use modkit_errors::system::logical::NotFoundError;\n+\n+/// Entity was not found in the types registry.\n+/// Note: status, category, retryable are inherited from NotFoundError if not specified.\n+#[gts_error(\n+    gts_id = \"gts.hx.types_registry.entity.not_found.v1~\",\n+    base = NotFoundError,  // Extends logical.not_found, not BaseError\n+    title = \"Entity Not Found\",\n+    // These are optional - inherited from base if omitted:\n+    // status = 404,      // Inherited from NotFoundError\n+    // category = \"Client\", // Inherited from NotFoundError  \n+    // retryable = false,   // Inherited from NotFoundError\n+)]\n+pub struct EntityNotFoundError {\n+    pub gts_id: String,\n+}\n+```\n+\n+#### Multi-Level Inheritance\n+\n+Errors can form deeper inheritance chains:\n+\n+```rust\n+/// Logical not found error (platform-level).\n+#[gts_error(\n+    gts_id = \"gts.hx.system.logical.not_found.v1~\",\n+    base = BaseError,  // Platform errors extend BaseError\n+    status = 404,\n+    title = \"Not Found\",\n+    category = \"Client\",\n+    retryable = false\n+)]\n+pub struct NotFoundError;\n+\n+/// Types registry entity not found (module-level).\n+#[gts_error(\n+    gts_id = \"gts.hx.types_registry.entity.not_found.v1~\",\n+    base = NotFoundError,  // Module errors extend logical errors\n+    status = 404,\n+    title = \"Entity Not Found\",\n+    category = \"Client\",\n+    retryable = false\n+)]\n+pub struct EntityNotFoundError {\n+    pub gts_id: String,\n+}\n+```\n+\n+#### Inheritance Hierarchy\n+\n+```\n+BaseError (gts.hx.core.errors.err.v1~)                              [base = true]\n+├── Transport Errors (hx.system.transport.*)                        [base = BaseError]\n+├── Runtime Errors (hx.system.runtime.*)                            [base = BaseError]\n+│   └── hx.types_registry.system.internal.v1~                       [base = runtime.internal]\n+├── HTTP Errors (hx.system.http.*)                                  [base = BaseError]\n+│   └── hx.auth.token_expired.v1~                                   [base = http.unauthorized]\n+├── gRPC Errors (hx.system.grpc.*)                                  [base = BaseError]\n+└── Logical Errors (hx.system.logical.*)                            [base = BaseError]\n+    ├── logical.not_found.v1~                                       [base = BaseError]\n+    │   ├── hx.types_registry.entity.not_found.v1~                  [base = logical.not_found]\n+    │   └── hx.db.entity.not_found.v1~                              [base = logical.not_found]\n+    ├── logical.already_exists.v1~                                  [base = BaseError]\n+    │   └── hx.types_registry.entity.already_exists.v1~             [base = logical.already_exists]\n+    └── logical.validation_failed.v1~                               [base = BaseError]\n+        └── hx.file_parser.validation.invalid_format.v1~            [base = logical.validation_failed]\n+```\n+\n+### R3: Trace ID Requirements\n+\n+- Every error response MUST include a non-empty `trace_id`\n+- Trace ID MUST be propagated from incoming request headers or generated\n+- Trace ID MUST be logged with the error for correlation\n+\n+### R4: Types Registry Integration\n+\n+- All error types MUST be registered in the types registry at startup\n+- Error schema MUST extend base error type: `gts.hx.core.errors.err.v1`\n+- Registration MUST include: code, title, status, category, retryable flag\n+\n+### R5: Standardized System Error Types\n+\n+See [GTS System Errors Catalog](#gts-system-errors-catalog) for the complete list of all system errors.\n+\n+### R6: Error Stack Propagation\n+\n+When a function calls another service/function that returns an error:\n+- The error SHOULD be wrapped with context\n+- `upstream_errors` array SHOULD contain the chain of errors\n+- Each upstream error includes: `code`, `title`, `detail`, `source`\n+- Propagation controlled by `error_stack` configuration flag\n+\n+---\n+\n+## GTS Error Code Format\n+\n+### Structure\n+\n+```\n+gts.<vendor>.<package>.<namespace>.<type>.<version>~<chain>\n+```\n+\n+### Components\n+\n+| Component | Description | Example |\n+|-----------|-------------|---------|\n+| `gts` | Global Type System prefix | `gts` |\n+| `vendor` | Organization identifier | `hx` (Hyperspot) |\n+| `package` | Module/service name | `types_registry`, `file_parser` |\n+| `namespace` | Error category | `entity`, `validation`, `runtime` |\n+| `type` | Specific error type | `not_found`, `invalid_format` |\n+| `version` | Schema version | `v1`, `v1.0` |\n+| `~chain` | Base type chain | `~hx.core.errors.err.v1` |\n+\n+### Validation Rules\n+\n+1. MUST start with `gts.`\n+2. All segments MUST be lowercase alphanumeric or underscore\n+3. No empty segments allowed\n+4. Final segment MUST be version format (`vN` or `vN.M`)\n+5. MUST chain from base error type\n+\n+### Short Name Derivation\n+\n+Short accessor names derived from final GTX segment:\n+```\n+gts.hx.core.errors.err.v1~hx.types_registry.entity.not_found.v1\n+                         └─────────────────────────────────────┘\n+                                          ↓\n+                         types_registry_entity_not_found_v1()\n+```\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Types Registry Integration\n+\n+### Error Type Schema\n+\n+```json\n+{\n+  \"gts_id\": \"gts.hx.types_registry.entity.not_found.v1~\",\n+  \"kind\": \"error\",\n+  \"schema\": {\n+    \"type\": \"object\",\n+    \"extends\": \"gts.hx.system.logical.not_found.v1~\",\n+    \"properties\": {\n+      \"status\": { \"const\": 404 },\n+      \"title\": { \"const\": \"Entity Not Found\" },\n+      \"category\": { \"const\": \"Client\" },\n+      \"retryable\": { \"const\": false }\n+    }\n+  },\n+  \"metadata\": {\n+    \"module\": \"types-registry\",\n+    \"documentation_url\": \"https://docs.hyperspot.com/errors/types_registry_entity_not_found_v1\"\n+  }\n+}\n+```\n+\n+### Registration Flow\n+\n+1. Module defines errors as explicit structs with `#[gts_error]` attribute in `src/errors.rs`\n+2. Each struct generates `ERROR_DEF` constant with GTS metadata\n+3. Module implements `all_error_definitions()` function returning all error definitions\n+4. At module startup (`on_ready`), errors are registered with types registry:","path":"intended_design/UNIFIED_ERROR_SYSTEM.md","commit_id":"5bdb0f43b25858af78999718f7247813802b9634","original_commit_id":"5bdb0f43b25858af78999718f7247813802b9634","user":{"login":"MikeFalcon77","id":3686170,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM2ODYxNzA=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3686170?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/MikeFalcon77","html_url":"https://github.com/MikeFalcon77","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MikeFalcon77/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MikeFalcon77/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MikeFalcon77/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MikeFalcon77/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MikeFalcon77/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MikeFalcon77/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MikeFalcon77/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MikeFalcon77/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MikeFalcon77/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Please make this registration best-effort. If types-registry is unavailable, the service must still start and serve REST. Convert failures into warn! logs (or background retry), but do not fail the process start.\n\nI believe that avalability of type-registry shouldn't affect other modules core functionality like errors.\n\nAlso it's will be an issue with local developement.","created_at":"2026-01-28T11:46:46Z","updated_at":"2026-01-28T12:02:23Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/290#discussion_r2736265169","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/290","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2736265169"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/290#discussion_r2736265169"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/290"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2736265169/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":null,"original_line":461,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"MEMBER","original_position":461,"position":1,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2736273079","pull_request_review_id":3715718572,"id":2736273079,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs6jGDa3","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,1574 @@\n+# Unified Error System - Intention Document\n+\n+This document defines the architecture, rules, and implementation plan for a unified error handling system across the Hyperspot project. All REST API errors MUST have a GTS identifier, trace ID, and be registered in the types registry.\n+\n+## Table of Contents\n+\n+1. [Executive Summary](#executive-summary)\n+2. [Industry Research](#industry-research)\n+3. [Current State Analysis](#current-state-analysis)\n+4. [Requirements](#requirements)\n+5. [Implementation Rules](#implementation-rules)\n+6. [Migration Plan](#migration-plan)\n+7. [Examples](#examples)\n+8. [HTTP Headers](#http-headers)\n+9. [Security Considerations](#security-considerations)\n+10. [Appendix A: Error Category Definitions](#appendix-a-error-category-definitions)\n+11. [Appendix B: Retryable Error Guidelines](#appendix-b-retryable-error-guidelines)\n+12. [GTS System Errors Catalog](#gts-system-errors-catalog)\n+13. [References](#references)\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Executive Summary\n+\n+### Problem Statement\n+\n+The current error handling across Hyperspot modules is inconsistent:\n+- Some modules use `declare_errors!` macro with JSON catalogs\n+- Others define errors inline without GTS codes\n+- Errors are not registered in the types registry\n+- No standardized metadata/context fields\n+- Inconsistent trace ID propagation\n+\n+### Goals\n+\n+1. **Every REST API error** MUST have a valid GTS identifier\n+2. **Every error response** MUST include a trace ID for debugging\n+3. **All error types** MUST be registered in the types registry\n+4. **Consistent error schema** across all modules following RFC 9457\n+5. **Machine-readable error codes** for programmatic handling\n+6. **Error stack propagation** for nested service calls\n+\n+### Non-Goals\n+\n+- Changing internal domain error types (only API-facing errors)\n+- Modifying logging infrastructure\n+- Changing HTTP status code semantics\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Industry Research\n+\n+### How Major Tech Companies Handle Errors\n+\n+| Company | Standard | Key Features |\n+|---------|----------|--------------|\n+| **Google** | AIP-193 + gRPC Status | `reason` (UPPER_SNAKE_CASE), `domain` (service name), `metadata` (key-value context), `ErrorInfo`, `LocalizedMessage`, `Help` links |\n+| **Amazon AWS** | Custom JSON | `errorType`, `httpStatus`, `requestId`, `message`, custom error object serialization |\n+| **Twitter/X** | JSON with `errors` array | `code` (CAPS_CASE), `message`, `parameter`, `details`, `value` |\n+| **RFC 9457** | Problem Details | `type` (URI), `title`, `status`, `detail`, `instance`, extension members |\n+\n+### Key Patterns Identified\n+\n+1. **Machine-readable identifiers** - Unique codes for programmatic handling (Google's `reason`, Twitter's `code`)\n+2. **Domain/namespace separation** - Identify error source (Google's `domain`, our GTS vendor.package)\n+3. **Structured metadata** - Key-value context without parsing messages (Google's `ErrorInfo.metadata`)\n+4. **Trace/Request IDs** - Correlation for debugging (AWS `requestId`, our `trace_id`)\n+5. **Documentation links** - URIs to error documentation (RFC 9457 `type`, Google's `Help`)\n+6. **Error categorization** - System vs User-defined, Retryable vs Non-retryable\n+\n+### Google AIP-193 ErrorInfo Structure (Reference)\n+\n+```json\n+{\n+  \"error\": {\n+    \"code\": 429,\n+    \"message\": \"The zone 'us-east1-a' does not have enough resources...\",\n+    \"status\": \"RESOURCE_EXHAUSTED\",\n+    \"details\": [\n+      {\n+        \"@type\": \"type.googleapis.com/google.rpc.ErrorInfo\",\n+        \"reason\": \"RESOURCE_AVAILABILITY\",\n+        \"domain\": \"compute.googleapis.com\",\n+        \"metadata\": {\n+          \"zone\": \"us-east1-a\",\n+          \"vmType\": \"e2-medium\"\n+        }\n+      }\n+    ]\n+  }\n+}\n+```\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Current State Analysis\n+\n+### Existing Infrastructure\n+\n+1. **`Problem` struct** (`libs/modkit-errors/src/problem.rs`) - RFC 9457 compliant\n+   - Fields: `type_url`, `title`, `status`, `detail`, `instance`, `code`, `trace_id`, `errors`\n+   - Implements `IntoResponse` for Axum with automatic trace ID enrichment\n+\n+2. **`struct_to_gts_schema` macro** (`modules/types-registry/gts-rust/gts-macros/src/lib.rs`)\n+   - Attribute macro for explicit struct definitions with GTS IDs visible in code\n+   - Generates constants: `GTS_SCHEMA_ID`, `GTS_SCHEMA_JSON`, etc.\n+   - **This pattern will be adapted for error definitions**\n+\n+3. **`declare_errors!` macro** (`libs/modkit-errors-macro/src/lib.rs`) - **TO BE DEPRECATED**\n+   - Generates type-safe error enums from JSON catalogs\n+   - Problem: GTS IDs hidden in external JSON files, not visible to LLMs\n+   - Used by: `users_info` example, `modkit-odata`\n+\n+### Gaps Identified\n+\n+| Gap | Current State | Required State |\n+|-----|---------------|----------------|\n+| **Hidden GTS IDs** | JSON-based `declare_errors!` | Explicit `#[gts_error]` structs with visible GTS IDs |\n+| **Inconsistent definitions** | Some modules use inline errors | All modules use `#[gts_error]` structs |\n+| **No types registry** | Errors not registered | All errors registered as GTS types |\n+| **Missing metadata** | No structured context | Struct fields → `metadata` map |\n+| **Partial trace IDs** | Only in `IntoResponse` | Mandatory in all error responses |\n+| **No error categories** | Flat error codes | System/Operational/Client categories |\n+| **No error stack** | Single error | Upstream error chain propagation |\n+\n+### Current Module Migration Status\n+\n+| Module | Location | Status | Issues |\n+|--------|----------|--------|--------|\n+| **file_parser** | `modules/file_parser/` | 🔴 Not migrated | No GTS IDs, inline `Problem::new()` |\n+| **types-registry** | `modules/system/types-registry/` | 🟡 Partial | Has codes but not GTS format (e.g., `TYPES_REGISTRY_NOT_FOUND`) |\n+| **nodes_registry** | `modules/system/nodes_registry/` | 🔴 Not migrated | Non-GTS codes (e.g., `NODES_NOT_FOUND`) |\n+| **api_gateway** | `modules/system/api_gateway/` | 🔴 Not migrated | No Problem struct, simple error codes |\n+| **tenant_resolver** | `modules/system/tenant_resolver/` | 🔴 Not migrated | No GTS IDs |\n+| **simple-user-settings** | `modules/simple-user-settings/` | 🟡 Partial | Uses `declare_errors!` with old chain format |\n+| **modkit-auth** | `libs/modkit-auth/` | 🔴 Not migrated | No GTS IDs, custom `IntoResponse` |\n+| **modkit-odata** | `libs/modkit-odata/` | 🟡 Partial | Uses `declare_errors!` with old chain format |\n+| **users_info** (example) | `examples/modkit/users_info/` | 🟡 Partial | Uses `declare_errors!` with old chain format |\n+\n+#### Legend\n+- 🟢 **Migrated** - Uses `#[gts_error]` structs with proper base types\n+- 🟡 **Partial** - Has GTS IDs but uses deprecated `declare_errors!` or old format\n+- 🔴 **Not migrated** - No GTS IDs or non-GTS format codes\n+\n+#### GTS ID Format Note\n+\n+**Old chain format** (used by `declare_errors!`):\n+```\n+gts.hx.core.errors.err.v1~hx.module.error_name.v1\n+```\n+\n+**New format** (with `base` field):\n+```\n+gts.hx.module.namespace.error_name.v1~\n+```\n+The `base` field in `#[gts_error]` replaces the chain suffix, making inheritance explicit in code.\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Requirements\n+\n+### R1: Error Schema Requirements\n+\n+Every error returned from REST API MUST conform to the unified schema:\n+\n+```rust\n+pub struct Problem {\n+    // =========================================================================\n+    // REQUIRED FIELDS - Core error identification\n+    // =========================================================================\n+    \n+    /// URI reference identifying the problem type (GTS-based)\n+    /// Example: \"https://docs.hyperspot.com/errors/types_registry_entity_not_found_v1\"\n+    #[serde(rename = \"type\")]\n+    pub type_url: String,\n+    \n+    /// Human-readable summary of the problem type (static per error type)\n+    pub title: String,\n+    \n+    /// GTS error code (machine-readable identifier)\n+    pub code: String,\n+    \n+    /// Trace ID for request correlation\n+    pub trace_id: String,\n+    \n+    // =========================================================================\n+    // CONTEXTUAL FIELDS - Optional based on error context\n+    // =========================================================================\n+    \n+    /// HTTP status code. Optional because:\n+    /// - gRPC errors use different status codes\n+    /// - Internal/domain errors may not have HTTP context\n+    /// - Event-driven systems have no request/response\n+    /// When serializing for HTTP response, this is populated from error definition.\n+    #[serde(skip_serializing_if = \"Option::is_none\")]\n+    pub status: Option<u16>,\n+    \n+    /// Human-readable explanation specific to this occurrence.\n+    /// Optional - title may be sufficient for simple errors.\n+    #[serde(skip_serializing_if = \"Option::is_none\")]\n+    pub detail: Option<String>,\n+    \n+    /// Error category for client handling.\n+    /// Optional - can be inferred from base type hierarchy.\n+    #[serde(skip_serializing_if = \"Option::is_none\")]\n+    pub category: Option<ErrorCategory>,\n+    \n+    /// Whether client can retry this request.\n+    /// Optional - can be inferred from base type; not relevant for all contexts.\n+    #[serde(skip_serializing_if = \"Option::is_none\")]\n+    pub retryable: Option<bool>,\n+    \n+    /// URI identifying this specific occurrence (auto-populated from request path)\n+    #[serde(skip_serializing_if = \"Option::is_none\")]\n+    pub instance: Option<String>,\n+    \n+    /// Structured metadata (key-value context)\n+    #[serde(skip_serializing_if = \"Option::is_none\")]\n+    pub metadata: Option<HashMap<String, String>>,\n+    \n+    /// Validation errors for 4xx responses\n+    #[serde(skip_serializing_if = \"Option::is_none\")]\n+    pub errors: Option<Vec<ValidationViolation>>,\n+    \n+    /// Upstream error chain (when error_stack enabled)\n+    #[serde(skip_serializing_if = \"Option::is_none\")]\n+    pub upstream_errors: Option<Vec<UpstreamError>>,\n+}\n+\n+pub enum ErrorCategory {\n+    /// Platform-level execution errors (panics, OOM, internal bugs)\n+    System,\n+    /// Infrastructure/operational issues (DB unavailable, service down, rate limits)\n+    Operational,\n+    /// Client input/request errors (validation, not found, unauthorized)\n+    Client,\n+}\n+```\n+\n+#### Field Requirements Summary\n+\n+| Field | Required | Reason |\n+|-------|----------|--------|\n+| `type_url` | ✅ Yes | RFC 9457 requires problem type URI |\n+| `title` | ✅ Yes | Human-readable error name (static per type) |\n+| `code` | ✅ Yes | GTS identifier for machine processing |\n+| `trace_id` | ✅ Yes | Request correlation for debugging |","path":"intended_design/UNIFIED_ERROR_SYSTEM.md","commit_id":"5bdb0f43b25858af78999718f7247813802b9634","original_commit_id":"5bdb0f43b25858af78999718f7247813802b9634","user":{"login":"MikeFalcon77","id":3686170,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM2ODYxNzA=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3686170?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/MikeFalcon77","html_url":"https://github.com/MikeFalcon77","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MikeFalcon77/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MikeFalcon77/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MikeFalcon77/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MikeFalcon77/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MikeFalcon77/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MikeFalcon77/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MikeFalcon77/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MikeFalcon77/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MikeFalcon77/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"`trace_id` should remain optional (Option<String>). This trace_id may be absent in some code point but we shouldn't fail. \nPlease avoid emitting \"\" (empty string). Prefer None when unavailable (as it's implemented now)","created_at":"2026-01-28T11:49:01Z","updated_at":"2026-01-28T12:02:23Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/290#discussion_r2736273079","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/290","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2736273079"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/290#discussion_r2736273079"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/290"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2736273079/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":null,"original_line":247,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"MEMBER","original_position":247,"position":1,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2736278616","pull_request_review_id":3715718572,"id":2736278616,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs6jGExY","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,1574 @@\n+# Unified Error System - Intention Document\n+\n+This document defines the architecture, rules, and implementation plan for a unified error handling system across the Hyperspot project. All REST API errors MUST have a GTS identifier, trace ID, and be registered in the types registry.\n+\n+## Table of Contents\n+\n+1. [Executive Summary](#executive-summary)\n+2. [Industry Research](#industry-research)\n+3. [Current State Analysis](#current-state-analysis)\n+4. [Requirements](#requirements)\n+5. [Implementation Rules](#implementation-rules)\n+6. [Migration Plan](#migration-plan)\n+7. [Examples](#examples)\n+8. [HTTP Headers](#http-headers)\n+9. [Security Considerations](#security-considerations)\n+10. [Appendix A: Error Category Definitions](#appendix-a-error-category-definitions)\n+11. [Appendix B: Retryable Error Guidelines](#appendix-b-retryable-error-guidelines)\n+12. [GTS System Errors Catalog](#gts-system-errors-catalog)\n+13. [References](#references)\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Executive Summary\n+\n+### Problem Statement\n+\n+The current error handling across Hyperspot modules is inconsistent:\n+- Some modules use `declare_errors!` macro with JSON catalogs\n+- Others define errors inline without GTS codes\n+- Errors are not registered in the types registry\n+- No standardized metadata/context fields\n+- Inconsistent trace ID propagation\n+\n+### Goals\n+\n+1. **Every REST API error** MUST have a valid GTS identifier\n+2. **Every error response** MUST include a trace ID for debugging\n+3. **All error types** MUST be registered in the types registry\n+4. **Consistent error schema** across all modules following RFC 9457\n+5. **Machine-readable error codes** for programmatic handling\n+6. **Error stack propagation** for nested service calls\n+\n+### Non-Goals\n+\n+- Changing internal domain error types (only API-facing errors)\n+- Modifying logging infrastructure\n+- Changing HTTP status code semantics\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Industry Research\n+\n+### How Major Tech Companies Handle Errors\n+\n+| Company | Standard | Key Features |\n+|---------|----------|--------------|\n+| **Google** | AIP-193 + gRPC Status | `reason` (UPPER_SNAKE_CASE), `domain` (service name), `metadata` (key-value context), `ErrorInfo`, `LocalizedMessage`, `Help` links |\n+| **Amazon AWS** | Custom JSON | `errorType`, `httpStatus`, `requestId`, `message`, custom error object serialization |\n+| **Twitter/X** | JSON with `errors` array | `code` (CAPS_CASE), `message`, `parameter`, `details`, `value` |\n+| **RFC 9457** | Problem Details | `type` (URI), `title`, `status`, `detail`, `instance`, extension members |\n+\n+### Key Patterns Identified\n+\n+1. **Machine-readable identifiers** - Unique codes for programmatic handling (Google's `reason`, Twitter's `code`)\n+2. **Domain/namespace separation** - Identify error source (Google's `domain`, our GTS vendor.package)\n+3. **Structured metadata** - Key-value context without parsing messages (Google's `ErrorInfo.metadata`)\n+4. **Trace/Request IDs** - Correlation for debugging (AWS `requestId`, our `trace_id`)\n+5. **Documentation links** - URIs to error documentation (RFC 9457 `type`, Google's `Help`)\n+6. **Error categorization** - System vs User-defined, Retryable vs Non-retryable\n+\n+### Google AIP-193 ErrorInfo Structure (Reference)\n+\n+```json\n+{\n+  \"error\": {\n+    \"code\": 429,\n+    \"message\": \"The zone 'us-east1-a' does not have enough resources...\",\n+    \"status\": \"RESOURCE_EXHAUSTED\",\n+    \"details\": [\n+      {\n+        \"@type\": \"type.googleapis.com/google.rpc.ErrorInfo\",\n+        \"reason\": \"RESOURCE_AVAILABILITY\",\n+        \"domain\": \"compute.googleapis.com\",\n+        \"metadata\": {\n+          \"zone\": \"us-east1-a\",\n+          \"vmType\": \"e2-medium\"\n+        }\n+      }\n+    ]\n+  }\n+}\n+```\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Current State Analysis\n+\n+### Existing Infrastructure\n+\n+1. **`Problem` struct** (`libs/modkit-errors/src/problem.rs`) - RFC 9457 compliant\n+   - Fields: `type_url`, `title`, `status`, `detail`, `instance`, `code`, `trace_id`, `errors`\n+   - Implements `IntoResponse` for Axum with automatic trace ID enrichment\n+\n+2. **`struct_to_gts_schema` macro** (`modules/types-registry/gts-rust/gts-macros/src/lib.rs`)\n+   - Attribute macro for explicit struct definitions with GTS IDs visible in code\n+   - Generates constants: `GTS_SCHEMA_ID`, `GTS_SCHEMA_JSON`, etc.\n+   - **This pattern will be adapted for error definitions**\n+\n+3. **`declare_errors!` macro** (`libs/modkit-errors-macro/src/lib.rs`) - **TO BE DEPRECATED**\n+   - Generates type-safe error enums from JSON catalogs\n+   - Problem: GTS IDs hidden in external JSON files, not visible to LLMs\n+   - Used by: `users_info` example, `modkit-odata`\n+\n+### Gaps Identified\n+\n+| Gap | Current State | Required State |\n+|-----|---------------|----------------|\n+| **Hidden GTS IDs** | JSON-based `declare_errors!` | Explicit `#[gts_error]` structs with visible GTS IDs |\n+| **Inconsistent definitions** | Some modules use inline errors | All modules use `#[gts_error]` structs |\n+| **No types registry** | Errors not registered | All errors registered as GTS types |\n+| **Missing metadata** | No structured context | Struct fields → `metadata` map |\n+| **Partial trace IDs** | Only in `IntoResponse` | Mandatory in all error responses |\n+| **No error categories** | Flat error codes | System/Operational/Client categories |\n+| **No error stack** | Single error | Upstream error chain propagation |\n+\n+### Current Module Migration Status\n+\n+| Module | Location | Status | Issues |\n+|--------|----------|--------|--------|\n+| **file_parser** | `modules/file_parser/` | 🔴 Not migrated | No GTS IDs, inline `Problem::new()` |\n+| **types-registry** | `modules/system/types-registry/` | 🟡 Partial | Has codes but not GTS format (e.g., `TYPES_REGISTRY_NOT_FOUND`) |\n+| **nodes_registry** | `modules/system/nodes_registry/` | 🔴 Not migrated | Non-GTS codes (e.g., `NODES_NOT_FOUND`) |\n+| **api_gateway** | `modules/system/api_gateway/` | 🔴 Not migrated | No Problem struct, simple error codes |\n+| **tenant_resolver** | `modules/system/tenant_resolver/` | 🔴 Not migrated | No GTS IDs |\n+| **simple-user-settings** | `modules/simple-user-settings/` | 🟡 Partial | Uses `declare_errors!` with old chain format |\n+| **modkit-auth** | `libs/modkit-auth/` | 🔴 Not migrated | No GTS IDs, custom `IntoResponse` |\n+| **modkit-odata** | `libs/modkit-odata/` | 🟡 Partial | Uses `declare_errors!` with old chain format |\n+| **users_info** (example) | `examples/modkit/users_info/` | 🟡 Partial | Uses `declare_errors!` with old chain format |\n+\n+#### Legend\n+- 🟢 **Migrated** - Uses `#[gts_error]` structs with proper base types\n+- 🟡 **Partial** - Has GTS IDs but uses deprecated `declare_errors!` or old format\n+- 🔴 **Not migrated** - No GTS IDs or non-GTS format codes\n+\n+#### GTS ID Format Note\n+\n+**Old chain format** (used by `declare_errors!`):\n+```\n+gts.hx.core.errors.err.v1~hx.module.error_name.v1\n+```\n+\n+**New format** (with `base` field):\n+```\n+gts.hx.module.namespace.error_name.v1~\n+```\n+The `base` field in `#[gts_error]` replaces the chain suffix, making inheritance explicit in code.\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Requirements\n+\n+### R1: Error Schema Requirements\n+\n+Every error returned from REST API MUST conform to the unified schema:\n+\n+```rust\n+pub struct Problem {\n+    // =========================================================================\n+    // REQUIRED FIELDS - Core error identification\n+    // =========================================================================\n+    \n+    /// URI reference identifying the problem type (GTS-based)\n+    /// Example: \"https://docs.hyperspot.com/errors/types_registry_entity_not_found_v1\"\n+    #[serde(rename = \"type\")]\n+    pub type_url: String,\n+    \n+    /// Human-readable summary of the problem type (static per error type)\n+    pub title: String,\n+    \n+    /// GTS error code (machine-readable identifier)\n+    pub code: String,\n+    \n+    /// Trace ID for request correlation\n+    pub trace_id: String,\n+    \n+    // =========================================================================\n+    // CONTEXTUAL FIELDS - Optional based on error context\n+    // =========================================================================\n+    \n+    /// HTTP status code. Optional because:\n+    /// - gRPC errors use different status codes\n+    /// - Internal/domain errors may not have HTTP context\n+    /// - Event-driven systems have no request/response\n+    /// When serializing for HTTP response, this is populated from error definition.\n+    #[serde(skip_serializing_if = \"Option::is_none\")]\n+    pub status: Option<u16>,\n+    \n+    /// Human-readable explanation specific to this occurrence.\n+    /// Optional - title may be sufficient for simple errors.\n+    #[serde(skip_serializing_if = \"Option::is_none\")]\n+    pub detail: Option<String>,\n+    \n+    /// Error category for client handling.\n+    /// Optional - can be inferred from base type hierarchy.\n+    #[serde(skip_serializing_if = \"Option::is_none\")]\n+    pub category: Option<ErrorCategory>,\n+    \n+    /// Whether client can retry this request.\n+    /// Optional - can be inferred from base type; not relevant for all contexts.\n+    #[serde(skip_serializing_if = \"Option::is_none\")]\n+    pub retryable: Option<bool>,\n+    \n+    /// URI identifying this specific occurrence (auto-populated from request path)\n+    #[serde(skip_serializing_if = \"Option::is_none\")]\n+    pub instance: Option<String>,\n+    \n+    /// Structured metadata (key-value context)\n+    #[serde(skip_serializing_if = \"Option::is_none\")]\n+    pub metadata: Option<HashMap<String, String>>,\n+    \n+    /// Validation errors for 4xx responses\n+    #[serde(skip_serializing_if = \"Option::is_none\")]\n+    pub errors: Option<Vec<ValidationViolation>>,\n+    \n+    /// Upstream error chain (when error_stack enabled)\n+    #[serde(skip_serializing_if = \"Option::is_none\")]\n+    pub upstream_errors: Option<Vec<UpstreamError>>,\n+}\n+\n+pub enum ErrorCategory {\n+    /// Platform-level execution errors (panics, OOM, internal bugs)\n+    System,\n+    /// Infrastructure/operational issues (DB unavailable, service down, rate limits)\n+    Operational,\n+    /// Client input/request errors (validation, not found, unauthorized)\n+    Client,\n+}\n+```\n+\n+#### Field Requirements Summary\n+\n+| Field | Required | Reason |\n+|-------|----------|--------|\n+| `type_url` | ✅ Yes | RFC 9457 requires problem type URI |\n+| `title` | ✅ Yes | Human-readable error name (static per type) |\n+| `code` | ✅ Yes | GTS identifier for machine processing |\n+| `trace_id` | ✅ Yes | Request correlation for debugging |\n+| `status` | ❌ No | Only relevant for HTTP; gRPC/events/domain errors don't need it |\n+| `detail` | ❌ No | Instance-specific message; title may suffice |\n+| `category` | ❌ No | Inherited from base type hierarchy |\n+| `retryable` | ❌ No | Inherited from base type; not relevant for all contexts |\n+| `instance` | ❌ No | Auto-populated from request path when applicable |\n+| `metadata` | ❌ No | Additional context key-value pairs |\n+| `errors` | ❌ No | Validation violations for 4xx errors |\n+| `upstream_errors` | ❌ No | Error chain from upstream services |\n+\n+**Note:** When converting to HTTP response, `status` is populated from the error definition. When the error is used in non-HTTP contexts (gRPC, domain logic, events), `status` remains `None`.\n+\n+### R2: GTS Identifier and Base Type Requirements\n+\n+Every error MUST have a valid GTS identifier and specify its base type using the `base` field.\n+\n+#### GTS ID Format\n+\n+```\n+gts.<vendor>.<package>.<namespace>.<type>.v<version>~\n+```\n+\n+**Examples:**\n+- `gts.hx.types_registry.entity.not_found.v1~` - Types registry not found error\n+- `gts.hx.file_parser.validation.invalid_format.v1~` - File parser validation error\n+- `gts.hx.system.runtime.timeout.v1~` - System timeout error\n+\n+#### Base Type Chaining\n+\n+Errors form an inheritance chain using the `base` field. The `base` field references another error struct type (not a string literal), similar to how `struct_to_gts_schema` works.\n+\n+The root base error type is:\n+\n+```rust\n+/// Root error type for all GTS errors.\n+#[gts_error(\n+    gts_id = \"gts.hx.core.errors.err.v1~\",\n+    base = true,  // Marks this as a root base type (no parent)\n+    title = \"Error\",\n+    // Optional attributes with defaults for inheritance:\n+    status = 500,        // Default HTTP status (optional, inherited by children)\n+    category = \"System\", // Default category (optional, inherited by children)\n+    retryable = false    // Default retryable (optional, inherited by children)\n+)]\n+pub struct BaseError;\n+```\n+\n+All module-specific errors MUST reference their base type as a struct (extending the appropriate logical/system error):\n+\n+```rust\n+use modkit_errors::system::logical::NotFoundError;\n+\n+/// Entity was not found in the types registry.\n+/// Note: status, category, retryable are inherited from NotFoundError if not specified.\n+#[gts_error(\n+    gts_id = \"gts.hx.types_registry.entity.not_found.v1~\",\n+    base = NotFoundError,  // Extends logical.not_found, not BaseError\n+    title = \"Entity Not Found\",\n+    // These are optional - inherited from base if omitted:\n+    // status = 404,      // Inherited from NotFoundError\n+    // category = \"Client\", // Inherited from NotFoundError  \n+    // retryable = false,   // Inherited from NotFoundError\n+)]\n+pub struct EntityNotFoundError {\n+    pub gts_id: String,\n+}\n+```\n+\n+#### Multi-Level Inheritance\n+\n+Errors can form deeper inheritance chains:\n+\n+```rust\n+/// Logical not found error (platform-level).\n+#[gts_error(\n+    gts_id = \"gts.hx.system.logical.not_found.v1~\",\n+    base = BaseError,  // Platform errors extend BaseError\n+    status = 404,\n+    title = \"Not Found\",\n+    category = \"Client\",\n+    retryable = false\n+)]\n+pub struct NotFoundError;\n+\n+/// Types registry entity not found (module-level).\n+#[gts_error(\n+    gts_id = \"gts.hx.types_registry.entity.not_found.v1~\",\n+    base = NotFoundError,  // Module errors extend logical errors\n+    status = 404,\n+    title = \"Entity Not Found\",\n+    category = \"Client\",\n+    retryable = false\n+)]\n+pub struct EntityNotFoundError {\n+    pub gts_id: String,\n+}\n+```\n+\n+#### Inheritance Hierarchy\n+\n+```\n+BaseError (gts.hx.core.errors.err.v1~)                              [base = true]\n+├── Transport Errors (hx.system.transport.*)                        [base = BaseError]\n+├── Runtime Errors (hx.system.runtime.*)                            [base = BaseError]\n+│   └── hx.types_registry.system.internal.v1~                       [base = runtime.internal]\n+├── HTTP Errors (hx.system.http.*)                                  [base = BaseError]\n+│   └── hx.auth.token_expired.v1~                                   [base = http.unauthorized]\n+├── gRPC Errors (hx.system.grpc.*)                                  [base = BaseError]\n+└── Logical Errors (hx.system.logical.*)                            [base = BaseError]\n+    ├── logical.not_found.v1~                                       [base = BaseError]\n+    │   ├── hx.types_registry.entity.not_found.v1~                  [base = logical.not_found]\n+    │   └── hx.db.entity.not_found.v1~                              [base = logical.not_found]\n+    ├── logical.already_exists.v1~                                  [base = BaseError]\n+    │   └── hx.types_registry.entity.already_exists.v1~             [base = logical.already_exists]\n+    └── logical.validation_failed.v1~                               [base = BaseError]\n+        └── hx.file_parser.validation.invalid_format.v1~            [base = logical.validation_failed]\n+```\n+\n+### R3: Trace ID Requirements\n+\n+- Every error response MUST include a non-empty `trace_id`\n+- Trace ID MUST be propagated from incoming request headers or generated\n+- Trace ID MUST be logged with the error for correlation\n+\n+### R4: Types Registry Integration\n+\n+- All error types MUST be registered in the types registry at startup\n+- Error schema MUST extend base error type: `gts.hx.core.errors.err.v1`\n+- Registration MUST include: code, title, status, category, retryable flag\n+\n+### R5: Standardized System Error Types\n+\n+See [GTS System Errors Catalog](#gts-system-errors-catalog) for the complete list of all system errors.\n+\n+### R6: Error Stack Propagation\n+\n+When a function calls another service/function that returns an error:\n+- The error SHOULD be wrapped with context\n+- `upstream_errors` array SHOULD contain the chain of errors\n+- Each upstream error includes: `code`, `title`, `detail`, `source`\n+- Propagation controlled by `error_stack` configuration flag\n+\n+---\n+\n+## GTS Error Code Format\n+\n+### Structure\n+\n+```\n+gts.<vendor>.<package>.<namespace>.<type>.<version>~<chain>\n+```\n+\n+### Components\n+\n+| Component | Description | Example |\n+|-----------|-------------|---------|\n+| `gts` | Global Type System prefix | `gts` |\n+| `vendor` | Organization identifier | `hx` (Hyperspot) |\n+| `package` | Module/service name | `types_registry`, `file_parser` |\n+| `namespace` | Error category | `entity`, `validation`, `runtime` |\n+| `type` | Specific error type | `not_found`, `invalid_format` |\n+| `version` | Schema version | `v1`, `v1.0` |\n+| `~chain` | Base type chain | `~hx.core.errors.err.v1` |\n+\n+### Validation Rules\n+\n+1. MUST start with `gts.`\n+2. All segments MUST be lowercase alphanumeric or underscore\n+3. No empty segments allowed\n+4. Final segment MUST be version format (`vN` or `vN.M`)\n+5. MUST chain from base error type\n+\n+### Short Name Derivation\n+\n+Short accessor names derived from final GTX segment:\n+```\n+gts.hx.core.errors.err.v1~hx.types_registry.entity.not_found.v1\n+                         └─────────────────────────────────────┘\n+                                          ↓\n+                         types_registry_entity_not_found_v1()\n+```\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Types Registry Integration\n+\n+### Error Type Schema\n+\n+```json\n+{\n+  \"gts_id\": \"gts.hx.types_registry.entity.not_found.v1~\",\n+  \"kind\": \"error\",\n+  \"schema\": {\n+    \"type\": \"object\",\n+    \"extends\": \"gts.hx.system.logical.not_found.v1~\",\n+    \"properties\": {\n+      \"status\": { \"const\": 404 },\n+      \"title\": { \"const\": \"Entity Not Found\" },\n+      \"category\": { \"const\": \"Client\" },\n+      \"retryable\": { \"const\": false }\n+    }\n+  },\n+  \"metadata\": {\n+    \"module\": \"types-registry\",\n+    \"documentation_url\": \"https://docs.hyperspot.com/errors/types_registry_entity_not_found_v1\"\n+  }\n+}\n+```\n+\n+### Registration Flow\n+\n+1. Module defines errors as explicit structs with `#[gts_error]` attribute in `src/errors.rs`\n+2. Each struct generates `ERROR_DEF` constant with GTS metadata\n+3. Module implements `all_error_definitions()` function returning all error definitions\n+4. At module startup (`on_ready`), errors are registered with types registry:\n+   ```rust\n+   impl Module for MyModule {\n+       async fn on_ready(&self, ctx: &ModuleContext) -> Result<()> {\n+           // Register all error types with types registry\n+           let errors = crate::errors::all_error_definitions();\n+           ctx.types_registry().register_errors(errors).await?;\n+           Ok(())\n+       }\n+   }\n+   ```\n+5. Types registry validates GTS format and schema compliance\n+6. Errors become discoverable via types registry API\n+\n+### API for Error Discovery\n+\n+```http\n+GET /api/types-registry/v1/types?kind=error&module=types-registry\n+\n+Response:\n+{\n+  \"items\": [\n+    {\n+      \"gts_id\": \"gts.hx.core.errors.err.v1~hx.types_registry.entity.not_found.v1\",\n+      \"status\": 404,\n+      \"title\": \"Entity Not Found\",\n+      \"category\": \"Client\",\n+      \"retryable\": false,\n+      \"documentation_url\": \"...\"\n+    }\n+  ]\n+}\n+```\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Implementation Rules\n+\n+### Rule 1: All Errors MUST Use Explicit Struct Definitions with `#[gts_error]`\n+\n+Errors are defined as explicit structs with the `#[gts_error]` attribute macro. This approach:","path":"intended_design/UNIFIED_ERROR_SYSTEM.md","commit_id":"5bdb0f43b25858af78999718f7247813802b9634","original_commit_id":"5bdb0f43b25858af78999718f7247813802b9634","user":{"login":"MikeFalcon77","id":3686170,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM2ODYxNzA=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3686170?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/MikeFalcon77","html_url":"https://github.com/MikeFalcon77","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MikeFalcon77/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MikeFalcon77/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MikeFalcon77/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MikeFalcon77/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MikeFalcon77/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MikeFalcon77/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MikeFalcon77/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MikeFalcon77/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MikeFalcon77/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Please preserve a short, ergonomic identifier API (e.g. Errors::TYPES_REGISTRY_NOT_FOUND) so callers don’t have to construct full GTS strings. The “call site” DX should remain comparable to declare_errors!.","created_at":"2026-01-28T11:50:31Z","updated_at":"2026-01-28T12:02:23Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/290#discussion_r2736278616","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/290","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2736278616"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/290#discussion_r2736278616"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/290"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2736278616/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":null,"original_line":501,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"MEMBER","original_position":501,"position":1,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2736291564","pull_request_review_id":3715718572,"id":2736291564,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs6jGH7s","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,1574 @@\n+# Unified Error System - Intention Document\n+\n+This document defines the architecture, rules, and implementation plan for a unified error handling system across the Hyperspot project. All REST API errors MUST have a GTS identifier, trace ID, and be registered in the types registry.\n+\n+## Table of Contents\n+\n+1. [Executive Summary](#executive-summary)\n+2. [Industry Research](#industry-research)\n+3. [Current State Analysis](#current-state-analysis)\n+4. [Requirements](#requirements)\n+5. [Implementation Rules](#implementation-rules)\n+6. [Migration Plan](#migration-plan)\n+7. [Examples](#examples)\n+8. [HTTP Headers](#http-headers)\n+9. [Security Considerations](#security-considerations)\n+10. [Appendix A: Error Category Definitions](#appendix-a-error-category-definitions)\n+11. [Appendix B: Retryable Error Guidelines](#appendix-b-retryable-error-guidelines)\n+12. [GTS System Errors Catalog](#gts-system-errors-catalog)\n+13. [References](#references)\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Executive Summary\n+\n+### Problem Statement\n+\n+The current error handling across Hyperspot modules is inconsistent:\n+- Some modules use `declare_errors!` macro with JSON catalogs\n+- Others define errors inline without GTS codes\n+- Errors are not registered in the types registry\n+- No standardized metadata/context fields\n+- Inconsistent trace ID propagation\n+\n+### Goals\n+\n+1. **Every REST API error** MUST have a valid GTS identifier\n+2. **Every error response** MUST include a trace ID for debugging\n+3. **All error types** MUST be registered in the types registry\n+4. **Consistent error schema** across all modules following RFC 9457\n+5. **Machine-readable error codes** for programmatic handling\n+6. **Error stack propagation** for nested service calls\n+\n+### Non-Goals\n+\n+- Changing internal domain error types (only API-facing errors)\n+- Modifying logging infrastructure\n+- Changing HTTP status code semantics\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Industry Research\n+\n+### How Major Tech Companies Handle Errors\n+\n+| Company | Standard | Key Features |\n+|---------|----------|--------------|\n+| **Google** | AIP-193 + gRPC Status | `reason` (UPPER_SNAKE_CASE), `domain` (service name), `metadata` (key-value context), `ErrorInfo`, `LocalizedMessage`, `Help` links |\n+| **Amazon AWS** | Custom JSON | `errorType`, `httpStatus`, `requestId`, `message`, custom error object serialization |\n+| **Twitter/X** | JSON with `errors` array | `code` (CAPS_CASE), `message`, `parameter`, `details`, `value` |\n+| **RFC 9457** | Problem Details | `type` (URI), `title`, `status`, `detail`, `instance`, extension members |\n+\n+### Key Patterns Identified\n+\n+1. **Machine-readable identifiers** - Unique codes for programmatic handling (Google's `reason`, Twitter's `code`)\n+2. **Domain/namespace separation** - Identify error source (Google's `domain`, our GTS vendor.package)\n+3. **Structured metadata** - Key-value context without parsing messages (Google's `ErrorInfo.metadata`)\n+4. **Trace/Request IDs** - Correlation for debugging (AWS `requestId`, our `trace_id`)\n+5. **Documentation links** - URIs to error documentation (RFC 9457 `type`, Google's `Help`)\n+6. **Error categorization** - System vs User-defined, Retryable vs Non-retryable\n+\n+### Google AIP-193 ErrorInfo Structure (Reference)\n+\n+```json\n+{\n+  \"error\": {\n+    \"code\": 429,\n+    \"message\": \"The zone 'us-east1-a' does not have enough resources...\",\n+    \"status\": \"RESOURCE_EXHAUSTED\",\n+    \"details\": [\n+      {\n+        \"@type\": \"type.googleapis.com/google.rpc.ErrorInfo\",\n+        \"reason\": \"RESOURCE_AVAILABILITY\",\n+        \"domain\": \"compute.googleapis.com\",\n+        \"metadata\": {\n+          \"zone\": \"us-east1-a\",\n+          \"vmType\": \"e2-medium\"\n+        }\n+      }\n+    ]\n+  }\n+}\n+```\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Current State Analysis\n+\n+### Existing Infrastructure\n+\n+1. **`Problem` struct** (`libs/modkit-errors/src/problem.rs`) - RFC 9457 compliant\n+   - Fields: `type_url`, `title`, `status`, `detail`, `instance`, `code`, `trace_id`, `errors`\n+   - Implements `IntoResponse` for Axum with automatic trace ID enrichment\n+\n+2. **`struct_to_gts_schema` macro** (`modules/types-registry/gts-rust/gts-macros/src/lib.rs`)\n+   - Attribute macro for explicit struct definitions with GTS IDs visible in code\n+   - Generates constants: `GTS_SCHEMA_ID`, `GTS_SCHEMA_JSON`, etc.\n+   - **This pattern will be adapted for error definitions**\n+\n+3. **`declare_errors!` macro** (`libs/modkit-errors-macro/src/lib.rs`) - **TO BE DEPRECATED**\n+   - Generates type-safe error enums from JSON catalogs\n+   - Problem: GTS IDs hidden in external JSON files, not visible to LLMs\n+   - Used by: `users_info` example, `modkit-odata`\n+\n+### Gaps Identified\n+\n+| Gap | Current State | Required State |\n+|-----|---------------|----------------|\n+| **Hidden GTS IDs** | JSON-based `declare_errors!` | Explicit `#[gts_error]` structs with visible GTS IDs |\n+| **Inconsistent definitions** | Some modules use inline errors | All modules use `#[gts_error]` structs |\n+| **No types registry** | Errors not registered | All errors registered as GTS types |\n+| **Missing metadata** | No structured context | Struct fields → `metadata` map |\n+| **Partial trace IDs** | Only in `IntoResponse` | Mandatory in all error responses |\n+| **No error categories** | Flat error codes | System/Operational/Client categories |\n+| **No error stack** | Single error | Upstream error chain propagation |\n+\n+### Current Module Migration Status\n+\n+| Module | Location | Status | Issues |\n+|--------|----------|--------|--------|\n+| **file_parser** | `modules/file_parser/` | 🔴 Not migrated | No GTS IDs, inline `Problem::new()` |\n+| **types-registry** | `modules/system/types-registry/` | 🟡 Partial | Has codes but not GTS format (e.g., `TYPES_REGISTRY_NOT_FOUND`) |\n+| **nodes_registry** | `modules/system/nodes_registry/` | 🔴 Not migrated | Non-GTS codes (e.g., `NODES_NOT_FOUND`) |\n+| **api_gateway** | `modules/system/api_gateway/` | 🔴 Not migrated | No Problem struct, simple error codes |\n+| **tenant_resolver** | `modules/system/tenant_resolver/` | 🔴 Not migrated | No GTS IDs |\n+| **simple-user-settings** | `modules/simple-user-settings/` | 🟡 Partial | Uses `declare_errors!` with old chain format |\n+| **modkit-auth** | `libs/modkit-auth/` | 🔴 Not migrated | No GTS IDs, custom `IntoResponse` |\n+| **modkit-odata** | `libs/modkit-odata/` | 🟡 Partial | Uses `declare_errors!` with old chain format |\n+| **users_info** (example) | `examples/modkit/users_info/` | 🟡 Partial | Uses `declare_errors!` with old chain format |\n+\n+#### Legend\n+- 🟢 **Migrated** - Uses `#[gts_error]` structs with proper base types\n+- 🟡 **Partial** - Has GTS IDs but uses deprecated `declare_errors!` or old format\n+- 🔴 **Not migrated** - No GTS IDs or non-GTS format codes\n+\n+#### GTS ID Format Note\n+\n+**Old chain format** (used by `declare_errors!`):\n+```\n+gts.hx.core.errors.err.v1~hx.module.error_name.v1\n+```\n+\n+**New format** (with `base` field):\n+```\n+gts.hx.module.namespace.error_name.v1~\n+```\n+The `base` field in `#[gts_error]` replaces the chain suffix, making inheritance explicit in code.\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Requirements\n+\n+### R1: Error Schema Requirements\n+\n+Every error returned from REST API MUST conform to the unified schema:\n+\n+```rust\n+pub struct Problem {\n+    // =========================================================================\n+    // REQUIRED FIELDS - Core error identification\n+    // =========================================================================\n+    \n+    /// URI reference identifying the problem type (GTS-based)\n+    /// Example: \"https://docs.hyperspot.com/errors/types_registry_entity_not_found_v1\"\n+    #[serde(rename = \"type\")]\n+    pub type_url: String,\n+    \n+    /// Human-readable summary of the problem type (static per error type)\n+    pub title: String,\n+    \n+    /// GTS error code (machine-readable identifier)\n+    pub code: String,\n+    \n+    /// Trace ID for request correlation\n+    pub trace_id: String,\n+    \n+    // =========================================================================\n+    // CONTEXTUAL FIELDS - Optional based on error context\n+    // =========================================================================\n+    \n+    /// HTTP status code. Optional because:\n+    /// - gRPC errors use different status codes\n+    /// - Internal/domain errors may not have HTTP context\n+    /// - Event-driven systems have no request/response\n+    /// When serializing for HTTP response, this is populated from error definition.\n+    #[serde(skip_serializing_if = \"Option::is_none\")]\n+    pub status: Option<u16>,\n+    \n+    /// Human-readable explanation specific to this occurrence.\n+    /// Optional - title may be sufficient for simple errors.\n+    #[serde(skip_serializing_if = \"Option::is_none\")]\n+    pub detail: Option<String>,\n+    \n+    /// Error category for client handling.\n+    /// Optional - can be inferred from base type hierarchy.\n+    #[serde(skip_serializing_if = \"Option::is_none\")]\n+    pub category: Option<ErrorCategory>,\n+    \n+    /// Whether client can retry this request.\n+    /// Optional - can be inferred from base type; not relevant for all contexts.\n+    #[serde(skip_serializing_if = \"Option::is_none\")]\n+    pub retryable: Option<bool>,\n+    \n+    /// URI identifying this specific occurrence (auto-populated from request path)\n+    #[serde(skip_serializing_if = \"Option::is_none\")]\n+    pub instance: Option<String>,\n+    \n+    /// Structured metadata (key-value context)\n+    #[serde(skip_serializing_if = \"Option::is_none\")]\n+    pub metadata: Option<HashMap<String, String>>,\n+    \n+    /// Validation errors for 4xx responses\n+    #[serde(skip_serializing_if = \"Option::is_none\")]\n+    pub errors: Option<Vec<ValidationViolation>>,\n+    \n+    /// Upstream error chain (when error_stack enabled)\n+    #[serde(skip_serializing_if = \"Option::is_none\")]\n+    pub upstream_errors: Option<Vec<UpstreamError>>,\n+}\n+\n+pub enum ErrorCategory {\n+    /// Platform-level execution errors (panics, OOM, internal bugs)\n+    System,\n+    /// Infrastructure/operational issues (DB unavailable, service down, rate limits)\n+    Operational,\n+    /// Client input/request errors (validation, not found, unauthorized)\n+    Client,\n+}\n+```\n+\n+#### Field Requirements Summary\n+\n+| Field | Required | Reason |\n+|-------|----------|--------|\n+| `type_url` | ✅ Yes | RFC 9457 requires problem type URI |\n+| `title` | ✅ Yes | Human-readable error name (static per type) |\n+| `code` | ✅ Yes | GTS identifier for machine processing |\n+| `trace_id` | ✅ Yes | Request correlation for debugging |\n+| `status` | ❌ No | Only relevant for HTTP; gRPC/events/domain errors don't need it |\n+| `detail` | ❌ No | Instance-specific message; title may suffice |\n+| `category` | ❌ No | Inherited from base type hierarchy |\n+| `retryable` | ❌ No | Inherited from base type; not relevant for all contexts |\n+| `instance` | ❌ No | Auto-populated from request path when applicable |\n+| `metadata` | ❌ No | Additional context key-value pairs |\n+| `errors` | ❌ No | Validation violations for 4xx errors |\n+| `upstream_errors` | ❌ No | Error chain from upstream services |\n+\n+**Note:** When converting to HTTP response, `status` is populated from the error definition. When the error is used in non-HTTP contexts (gRPC, domain logic, events), `status` remains `None`.\n+\n+### R2: GTS Identifier and Base Type Requirements\n+\n+Every error MUST have a valid GTS identifier and specify its base type using the `base` field.\n+\n+#### GTS ID Format\n+\n+```\n+gts.<vendor>.<package>.<namespace>.<type>.v<version>~\n+```\n+\n+**Examples:**\n+- `gts.hx.types_registry.entity.not_found.v1~` - Types registry not found error\n+- `gts.hx.file_parser.validation.invalid_format.v1~` - File parser validation error\n+- `gts.hx.system.runtime.timeout.v1~` - System timeout error\n+\n+#### Base Type Chaining\n+\n+Errors form an inheritance chain using the `base` field. The `base` field references another error struct type (not a string literal), similar to how `struct_to_gts_schema` works.\n+\n+The root base error type is:\n+\n+```rust\n+/// Root error type for all GTS errors.\n+#[gts_error(\n+    gts_id = \"gts.hx.core.errors.err.v1~\",\n+    base = true,  // Marks this as a root base type (no parent)\n+    title = \"Error\",\n+    // Optional attributes with defaults for inheritance:\n+    status = 500,        // Default HTTP status (optional, inherited by children)\n+    category = \"System\", // Default category (optional, inherited by children)\n+    retryable = false    // Default retryable (optional, inherited by children)\n+)]\n+pub struct BaseError;\n+```\n+\n+All module-specific errors MUST reference their base type as a struct (extending the appropriate logical/system error):\n+\n+```rust\n+use modkit_errors::system::logical::NotFoundError;\n+\n+/// Entity was not found in the types registry.\n+/// Note: status, category, retryable are inherited from NotFoundError if not specified.\n+#[gts_error(\n+    gts_id = \"gts.hx.types_registry.entity.not_found.v1~\",\n+    base = NotFoundError,  // Extends logical.not_found, not BaseError\n+    title = \"Entity Not Found\",\n+    // These are optional - inherited from base if omitted:\n+    // status = 404,      // Inherited from NotFoundError\n+    // category = \"Client\", // Inherited from NotFoundError  \n+    // retryable = false,   // Inherited from NotFoundError\n+)]\n+pub struct EntityNotFoundError {\n+    pub gts_id: String,\n+}\n+```\n+\n+#### Multi-Level Inheritance\n+\n+Errors can form deeper inheritance chains:\n+\n+```rust\n+/// Logical not found error (platform-level).\n+#[gts_error(\n+    gts_id = \"gts.hx.system.logical.not_found.v1~\",\n+    base = BaseError,  // Platform errors extend BaseError\n+    status = 404,\n+    title = \"Not Found\",\n+    category = \"Client\",\n+    retryable = false\n+)]\n+pub struct NotFoundError;\n+\n+/// Types registry entity not found (module-level).\n+#[gts_error(\n+    gts_id = \"gts.hx.types_registry.entity.not_found.v1~\",\n+    base = NotFoundError,  // Module errors extend logical errors\n+    status = 404,\n+    title = \"Entity Not Found\",\n+    category = \"Client\",\n+    retryable = false\n+)]\n+pub struct EntityNotFoundError {\n+    pub gts_id: String,\n+}\n+```\n+\n+#### Inheritance Hierarchy\n+\n+```\n+BaseError (gts.hx.core.errors.err.v1~)                              [base = true]\n+├── Transport Errors (hx.system.transport.*)                        [base = BaseError]\n+├── Runtime Errors (hx.system.runtime.*)                            [base = BaseError]\n+│   └── hx.types_registry.system.internal.v1~                       [base = runtime.internal]\n+├── HTTP Errors (hx.system.http.*)                                  [base = BaseError]\n+│   └── hx.auth.token_expired.v1~                                   [base = http.unauthorized]\n+├── gRPC Errors (hx.system.grpc.*)                                  [base = BaseError]\n+└── Logical Errors (hx.system.logical.*)                            [base = BaseError]\n+    ├── logical.not_found.v1~                                       [base = BaseError]\n+    │   ├── hx.types_registry.entity.not_found.v1~                  [base = logical.not_found]\n+    │   └── hx.db.entity.not_found.v1~                              [base = logical.not_found]\n+    ├── logical.already_exists.v1~                                  [base = BaseError]\n+    │   └── hx.types_registry.entity.already_exists.v1~             [base = logical.already_exists]\n+    └── logical.validation_failed.v1~                               [base = BaseError]\n+        └── hx.file_parser.validation.invalid_format.v1~            [base = logical.validation_failed]\n+```\n+\n+### R3: Trace ID Requirements\n+\n+- Every error response MUST include a non-empty `trace_id`\n+- Trace ID MUST be propagated from incoming request headers or generated\n+- Trace ID MUST be logged with the error for correlation\n+\n+### R4: Types Registry Integration\n+\n+- All error types MUST be registered in the types registry at startup\n+- Error schema MUST extend base error type: `gts.hx.core.errors.err.v1`\n+- Registration MUST include: code, title, status, category, retryable flag\n+\n+### R5: Standardized System Error Types\n+\n+See [GTS System Errors Catalog](#gts-system-errors-catalog) for the complete list of all system errors.\n+\n+### R6: Error Stack Propagation\n+\n+When a function calls another service/function that returns an error:\n+- The error SHOULD be wrapped with context\n+- `upstream_errors` array SHOULD contain the chain of errors\n+- Each upstream error includes: `code`, `title`, `detail`, `source`\n+- Propagation controlled by `error_stack` configuration flag\n+\n+---\n+\n+## GTS Error Code Format\n+\n+### Structure\n+\n+```\n+gts.<vendor>.<package>.<namespace>.<type>.<version>~<chain>\n+```\n+\n+### Components\n+\n+| Component | Description | Example |\n+|-----------|-------------|---------|\n+| `gts` | Global Type System prefix | `gts` |\n+| `vendor` | Organization identifier | `hx` (Hyperspot) |\n+| `package` | Module/service name | `types_registry`, `file_parser` |\n+| `namespace` | Error category | `entity`, `validation`, `runtime` |\n+| `type` | Specific error type | `not_found`, `invalid_format` |\n+| `version` | Schema version | `v1`, `v1.0` |\n+| `~chain` | Base type chain | `~hx.core.errors.err.v1` |\n+\n+### Validation Rules\n+\n+1. MUST start with `gts.`\n+2. All segments MUST be lowercase alphanumeric or underscore\n+3. No empty segments allowed\n+4. Final segment MUST be version format (`vN` or `vN.M`)\n+5. MUST chain from base error type\n+\n+### Short Name Derivation\n+\n+Short accessor names derived from final GTX segment:\n+```\n+gts.hx.core.errors.err.v1~hx.types_registry.entity.not_found.v1\n+                         └─────────────────────────────────────┘\n+                                          ↓\n+                         types_registry_entity_not_found_v1()\n+```\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Types Registry Integration\n+\n+### Error Type Schema\n+\n+```json\n+{\n+  \"gts_id\": \"gts.hx.types_registry.entity.not_found.v1~\",\n+  \"kind\": \"error\",\n+  \"schema\": {\n+    \"type\": \"object\",\n+    \"extends\": \"gts.hx.system.logical.not_found.v1~\",\n+    \"properties\": {\n+      \"status\": { \"const\": 404 },\n+      \"title\": { \"const\": \"Entity Not Found\" },\n+      \"category\": { \"const\": \"Client\" },\n+      \"retryable\": { \"const\": false }\n+    }\n+  },\n+  \"metadata\": {\n+    \"module\": \"types-registry\",\n+    \"documentation_url\": \"https://docs.hyperspot.com/errors/types_registry_entity_not_found_v1\"\n+  }\n+}\n+```\n+\n+### Registration Flow\n+\n+1. Module defines errors as explicit structs with `#[gts_error]` attribute in `src/errors.rs`\n+2. Each struct generates `ERROR_DEF` constant with GTS metadata\n+3. Module implements `all_error_definitions()` function returning all error definitions\n+4. At module startup (`on_ready`), errors are registered with types registry:\n+   ```rust\n+   impl Module for MyModule {\n+       async fn on_ready(&self, ctx: &ModuleContext) -> Result<()> {\n+           // Register all error types with types registry\n+           let errors = crate::errors::all_error_definitions();\n+           ctx.types_registry().register_errors(errors).await?;\n+           Ok(())\n+       }\n+   }\n+   ```\n+5. Types registry validates GTS format and schema compliance\n+6. Errors become discoverable via types registry API\n+\n+### API for Error Discovery\n+\n+```http\n+GET /api/types-registry/v1/types?kind=error&module=types-registry\n+\n+Response:\n+{\n+  \"items\": [\n+    {\n+      \"gts_id\": \"gts.hx.core.errors.err.v1~hx.types_registry.entity.not_found.v1\",\n+      \"status\": 404,\n+      \"title\": \"Entity Not Found\",\n+      \"category\": \"Client\",\n+      \"retryable\": false,\n+      \"documentation_url\": \"...\"\n+    }\n+  ]\n+}\n+```\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Implementation Rules\n+\n+### Rule 1: All Errors MUST Use Explicit Struct Definitions with `#[gts_error]`\n+\n+Errors are defined as explicit structs with the `#[gts_error]` attribute macro. This approach:\n+- Makes GTS IDs visible directly in code (better for LLM code generation)\n+- Provides compile-time validation\n+- Generates `Problem` conversion automatically\n+- Enables types registry integration\n+\n+```rust\n+// ✅ CORRECT - Explicit struct definition with visible GTS ID and base type reference\n+use modkit_errors::gts_error;\n+\n+// First, import the appropriate base error types from system errors\n+use modkit_errors::system::logical::{NotFoundError, AlreadyExistsError, ValidationFailedError};\n+\n+/// Entity was not found in the types registry.\n+#[gts_error(\n+    gts_id = \"gts.hx.types_registry.entity.not_found.v1~\",\n+    base = NotFoundError,  // Extends logical.not_found, not BaseError\n+    status = 404,\n+    title = \"Entity Not Found\",\n+    category = \"Client\",\n+    retryable = false\n+)]\n+pub struct EntityNotFoundError {\n+    /// The GTS ID that was not found\n+    pub gts_id: String,\n+}\n+\n+/// Entity already exists in the registry.\n+#[gts_error(\n+    gts_id = \"gts.hx.types_registry.entity.already_exists.v1~\",\n+    base = AlreadyExistsError,  // Extends logical.already_exists\n+    status = 409,\n+    title = \"Entity Already Exists\",\n+    category = \"Client\",\n+    retryable = false\n+)]\n+pub struct EntityAlreadyExistsError {\n+    /// The GTS ID that already exists\n+    pub gts_id: String,\n+}\n+\n+/// Invalid GTS ID format.\n+#[gts_error(\n+    gts_id = \"gts.hx.types_registry.validation.invalid_gts_id.v1~\",\n+    base = ValidationFailedError,  // Extends logical.validation_failed\n+    status = 400,\n+    title = \"Invalid GTS ID\",\n+    category = \"Client\",\n+    retryable = false\n+)]\n+pub struct InvalidGtsIdError {\n+    /// Description of the validation error\n+    pub message: String,\n+}\n+\n+// ❌ WRONG - Inline error definitions without GTS ID\n+impl From<DomainError> for Problem {\n+    fn from(e: DomainError) -> Self {\n+        Problem::new(StatusCode::NOT_FOUND, \"Not Found\", \"...\")\n+            .with_code(\"SOME_CODE\") // Not GTS format!\n+    }\n+}\n+\n+// ❌ WRONG - JSON-based declaration (GTS ID hidden in external file)\n+declare_errors! {\n+    path = \"gts/errors.json\",\n+    namespace = \"errors\",\n+    vis = \"pub\"\n+}\n+```\n+\n+### Rule 2: Error Struct Field Conventions\n+\n+Error structs contain context fields that become `metadata` in the Problem response:\n+\n+```rust\n+use modkit_errors::system::logical::ValidationFailedError as LogicalValidationFailed;\n+\n+/// Request validation failed (module-specific).\n+#[gts_error(\n+    gts_id = \"gts.hx.types_registry.validation.failed.v1~\",\n+    base = LogicalValidationFailed,  // Extends logical.validation_failed\n+    status = 422,\n+    title = \"Validation Failed\",\n+    category = \"Client\",\n+    retryable = false\n+)]\n+pub struct ValidationFailedError {\n+    /// Human-readable error message\n+    pub message: String,\n+    /// Field that failed validation (optional)\n+    #[gts_error(skip_metadata)]  // Don't include in metadata\n+    pub violations: Vec<ValidationViolation>,\n+}\n+```\n+\n+### Rule 3: Error Mapping Pattern\n+\n+```rust\n+use crate::errors::{EntityNotFoundError, EntityAlreadyExistsError, InvalidGtsIdError};\n+\n+pub fn domain_error_to_problem(e: &DomainError) -> Problem {\n+    match e {\n+        DomainError::NotFound { id } => {\n+            // into_problem() auto-populates trace_id from current tracing span\n+            EntityNotFoundError { gts_id: id.clone() }\n+                .into_problem()\n+                .with_detail(format!(\"Entity with GTS ID '{}' was not found\", id))\n+        }\n+        DomainError::AlreadyExists { id } => {\n+            EntityAlreadyExistsError { gts_id: id.clone() }\n+                .into_problem()\n+                .with_detail(format!(\"Entity with GTS ID '{}' already exists\", id))\n+        }\n+        DomainError::InvalidGtsId(msg) => {\n+            InvalidGtsIdError { message: msg.clone() }\n+                .into_problem()\n+        }\n+        // ...\n+    }\n+}\n+```\n+\n+### Rule 4: Trace ID Auto-Population\n+\n+Trace ID is **mandatory** in all error responses but **optional** in `into_problem()`. If not provided, it's auto-populated from the current tracing span.\n+\n+```rust\n+// Default: trace_id auto-populated from current tracing span\n+let problem = EntityNotFoundError { gts_id: id.clone() }\n+    .into_problem()  // trace_id extracted from tracing::Span::current()\n+    .with_detail(\"Entity not found\");\n+\n+// Override: explicitly pass trace_id if needed\n+let problem = EntityNotFoundError { gts_id: id.clone() }\n+    .into_problem()\n+    .with_trace_id(&custom_trace_id)  // Override auto-populated value\n+    .with_detail(\"Entity not found\");\n+```\n+\n+### Rule 5: Instance Auto-Population\n+\n+The `instance` field is **optional** and **auto-populated** from the request path in the Axum `IntoResponse` implementation. You don't need to pass it manually.\n+\n+```rust\n+// In Axum IntoResponse implementation\n+impl IntoResponse for Problem {\n+    fn into_response(self) -> Response {\n+        // Auto-populate instance from request URI if not set\n+        let problem = if self.instance.is_none() {\n+            // Instance is populated from request extensions or current URI\n+            if let Some(uri) = REQUEST_URI.try_with(|u| u.clone()).ok() {\n+                self.with_instance(uri.path())\n+            } else {\n+                self\n+            }\n+        } else {\n+            self\n+        };\n+        // ... rest of response building\n+    }\n+}\n+```\n+\n+If you need to override the instance manually, use `with_instance()`:\n+\n+```rust\n+let problem = EntityNotFoundError { gts_id: id.clone() }\n+    .into_problem()\n+    .with_instance(\"/custom/path\");  // Optional override\n+```\n+\n+### Rule 6: Error Registration at Startup\n+\n+Error definitions are **auto-collected** at compile time using the `#[gts_error]` macro with `linkme`. No manual registration list needed.","path":"intended_design/UNIFIED_ERROR_SYSTEM.md","commit_id":"5bdb0f43b25858af78999718f7247813802b9634","original_commit_id":"5bdb0f43b25858af78999718f7247813802b9634","user":{"login":"MikeFalcon77","id":3686170,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM2ODYxNzA=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3686170?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/MikeFalcon77","html_url":"https://github.com/MikeFalcon77","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MikeFalcon77/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MikeFalcon77/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MikeFalcon77/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MikeFalcon77/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MikeFalcon77/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MikeFalcon77/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MikeFalcon77/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MikeFalcon77/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MikeFalcon77/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"I suggest keeping a manual explicit list of error definitions/entities for now. Auto-collection via inventory/linkme is vulnerable to dead-stripping and can be toolchain/linker sensitive. Explicit references are more reliable. Or implement linkme registration at he next phases.","created_at":"2026-01-28T11:54:20Z","updated_at":"2026-01-28T12:02:23Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/290#discussion_r2736291564","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/290","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2736291564"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/290#discussion_r2736291564"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/290"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2736291564/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":null,"original_line":675,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"MEMBER","original_position":675,"position":1,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2736298131","pull_request_review_id":3715718572,"id":2736298131,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs6jGJiT","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,1574 @@\n+# Unified Error System - Intention Document\n+\n+This document defines the architecture, rules, and implementation plan for a unified error handling system across the Hyperspot project. All REST API errors MUST have a GTS identifier, trace ID, and be registered in the types registry.\n+\n+## Table of Contents\n+\n+1. [Executive Summary](#executive-summary)\n+2. [Industry Research](#industry-research)\n+3. [Current State Analysis](#current-state-analysis)\n+4. [Requirements](#requirements)\n+5. [Implementation Rules](#implementation-rules)\n+6. [Migration Plan](#migration-plan)\n+7. [Examples](#examples)\n+8. [HTTP Headers](#http-headers)\n+9. [Security Considerations](#security-considerations)\n+10. [Appendix A: Error Category Definitions](#appendix-a-error-category-definitions)\n+11. [Appendix B: Retryable Error Guidelines](#appendix-b-retryable-error-guidelines)\n+12. [GTS System Errors Catalog](#gts-system-errors-catalog)\n+13. [References](#references)\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Executive Summary\n+\n+### Problem Statement\n+\n+The current error handling across Hyperspot modules is inconsistent:\n+- Some modules use `declare_errors!` macro with JSON catalogs\n+- Others define errors inline without GTS codes\n+- Errors are not registered in the types registry\n+- No standardized metadata/context fields\n+- Inconsistent trace ID propagation\n+\n+### Goals\n+\n+1. **Every REST API error** MUST have a valid GTS identifier\n+2. **Every error response** MUST include a trace ID for debugging\n+3. **All error types** MUST be registered in the types registry\n+4. **Consistent error schema** across all modules following RFC 9457\n+5. **Machine-readable error codes** for programmatic handling\n+6. **Error stack propagation** for nested service calls\n+\n+### Non-Goals\n+\n+- Changing internal domain error types (only API-facing errors)\n+- Modifying logging infrastructure\n+- Changing HTTP status code semantics\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Industry Research\n+\n+### How Major Tech Companies Handle Errors\n+\n+| Company | Standard | Key Features |\n+|---------|----------|--------------|\n+| **Google** | AIP-193 + gRPC Status | `reason` (UPPER_SNAKE_CASE), `domain` (service name), `metadata` (key-value context), `ErrorInfo`, `LocalizedMessage`, `Help` links |\n+| **Amazon AWS** | Custom JSON | `errorType`, `httpStatus`, `requestId`, `message`, custom error object serialization |\n+| **Twitter/X** | JSON with `errors` array | `code` (CAPS_CASE), `message`, `parameter`, `details`, `value` |\n+| **RFC 9457** | Problem Details | `type` (URI), `title`, `status`, `detail`, `instance`, extension members |\n+\n+### Key Patterns Identified\n+\n+1. **Machine-readable identifiers** - Unique codes for programmatic handling (Google's `reason`, Twitter's `code`)\n+2. **Domain/namespace separation** - Identify error source (Google's `domain`, our GTS vendor.package)\n+3. **Structured metadata** - Key-value context without parsing messages (Google's `ErrorInfo.metadata`)\n+4. **Trace/Request IDs** - Correlation for debugging (AWS `requestId`, our `trace_id`)\n+5. **Documentation links** - URIs to error documentation (RFC 9457 `type`, Google's `Help`)\n+6. **Error categorization** - System vs User-defined, Retryable vs Non-retryable\n+\n+### Google AIP-193 ErrorInfo Structure (Reference)\n+\n+```json\n+{\n+  \"error\": {\n+    \"code\": 429,\n+    \"message\": \"The zone 'us-east1-a' does not have enough resources...\",\n+    \"status\": \"RESOURCE_EXHAUSTED\",\n+    \"details\": [\n+      {\n+        \"@type\": \"type.googleapis.com/google.rpc.ErrorInfo\",\n+        \"reason\": \"RESOURCE_AVAILABILITY\",\n+        \"domain\": \"compute.googleapis.com\",\n+        \"metadata\": {\n+          \"zone\": \"us-east1-a\",\n+          \"vmType\": \"e2-medium\"\n+        }\n+      }\n+    ]\n+  }\n+}\n+```\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Current State Analysis\n+\n+### Existing Infrastructure\n+\n+1. **`Problem` struct** (`libs/modkit-errors/src/problem.rs`) - RFC 9457 compliant\n+   - Fields: `type_url`, `title`, `status`, `detail`, `instance`, `code`, `trace_id`, `errors`\n+   - Implements `IntoResponse` for Axum with automatic trace ID enrichment\n+\n+2. **`struct_to_gts_schema` macro** (`modules/types-registry/gts-rust/gts-macros/src/lib.rs`)\n+   - Attribute macro for explicit struct definitions with GTS IDs visible in code\n+   - Generates constants: `GTS_SCHEMA_ID`, `GTS_SCHEMA_JSON`, etc.\n+   - **This pattern will be adapted for error definitions**\n+\n+3. **`declare_errors!` macro** (`libs/modkit-errors-macro/src/lib.rs`) - **TO BE DEPRECATED**\n+   - Generates type-safe error enums from JSON catalogs\n+   - Problem: GTS IDs hidden in external JSON files, not visible to LLMs\n+   - Used by: `users_info` example, `modkit-odata`\n+\n+### Gaps Identified\n+\n+| Gap | Current State | Required State |\n+|-----|---------------|----------------|\n+| **Hidden GTS IDs** | JSON-based `declare_errors!` | Explicit `#[gts_error]` structs with visible GTS IDs |\n+| **Inconsistent definitions** | Some modules use inline errors | All modules use `#[gts_error]` structs |\n+| **No types registry** | Errors not registered | All errors registered as GTS types |\n+| **Missing metadata** | No structured context | Struct fields → `metadata` map |\n+| **Partial trace IDs** | Only in `IntoResponse` | Mandatory in all error responses |\n+| **No error categories** | Flat error codes | System/Operational/Client categories |\n+| **No error stack** | Single error | Upstream error chain propagation |\n+\n+### Current Module Migration Status\n+\n+| Module | Location | Status | Issues |\n+|--------|----------|--------|--------|\n+| **file_parser** | `modules/file_parser/` | 🔴 Not migrated | No GTS IDs, inline `Problem::new()` |\n+| **types-registry** | `modules/system/types-registry/` | 🟡 Partial | Has codes but not GTS format (e.g., `TYPES_REGISTRY_NOT_FOUND`) |\n+| **nodes_registry** | `modules/system/nodes_registry/` | 🔴 Not migrated | Non-GTS codes (e.g., `NODES_NOT_FOUND`) |\n+| **api_gateway** | `modules/system/api_gateway/` | 🔴 Not migrated | No Problem struct, simple error codes |\n+| **tenant_resolver** | `modules/system/tenant_resolver/` | 🔴 Not migrated | No GTS IDs |\n+| **simple-user-settings** | `modules/simple-user-settings/` | 🟡 Partial | Uses `declare_errors!` with old chain format |\n+| **modkit-auth** | `libs/modkit-auth/` | 🔴 Not migrated | No GTS IDs, custom `IntoResponse` |\n+| **modkit-odata** | `libs/modkit-odata/` | 🟡 Partial | Uses `declare_errors!` with old chain format |\n+| **users_info** (example) | `examples/modkit/users_info/` | 🟡 Partial | Uses `declare_errors!` with old chain format |\n+\n+#### Legend\n+- 🟢 **Migrated** - Uses `#[gts_error]` structs with proper base types\n+- 🟡 **Partial** - Has GTS IDs but uses deprecated `declare_errors!` or old format\n+- 🔴 **Not migrated** - No GTS IDs or non-GTS format codes\n+\n+#### GTS ID Format Note\n+\n+**Old chain format** (used by `declare_errors!`):\n+```\n+gts.hx.core.errors.err.v1~hx.module.error_name.v1\n+```\n+\n+**New format** (with `base` field):\n+```\n+gts.hx.module.namespace.error_name.v1~\n+```\n+The `base` field in `#[gts_error]` replaces the chain suffix, making inheritance explicit in code.\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Requirements\n+\n+### R1: Error Schema Requirements\n+\n+Every error returned from REST API MUST conform to the unified schema:\n+\n+```rust\n+pub struct Problem {\n+    // =========================================================================\n+    // REQUIRED FIELDS - Core error identification\n+    // =========================================================================\n+    \n+    /// URI reference identifying the problem type (GTS-based)\n+    /// Example: \"https://docs.hyperspot.com/errors/types_registry_entity_not_found_v1\"\n+    #[serde(rename = \"type\")]\n+    pub type_url: String,\n+    \n+    /// Human-readable summary of the problem type (static per error type)\n+    pub title: String,\n+    \n+    /// GTS error code (machine-readable identifier)\n+    pub code: String,\n+    \n+    /// Trace ID for request correlation\n+    pub trace_id: String,\n+    \n+    // =========================================================================\n+    // CONTEXTUAL FIELDS - Optional based on error context\n+    // =========================================================================\n+    \n+    /// HTTP status code. Optional because:\n+    /// - gRPC errors use different status codes\n+    /// - Internal/domain errors may not have HTTP context\n+    /// - Event-driven systems have no request/response\n+    /// When serializing for HTTP response, this is populated from error definition.\n+    #[serde(skip_serializing_if = \"Option::is_none\")]\n+    pub status: Option<u16>,\n+    \n+    /// Human-readable explanation specific to this occurrence.\n+    /// Optional - title may be sufficient for simple errors.\n+    #[serde(skip_serializing_if = \"Option::is_none\")]\n+    pub detail: Option<String>,\n+    \n+    /// Error category for client handling.\n+    /// Optional - can be inferred from base type hierarchy.\n+    #[serde(skip_serializing_if = \"Option::is_none\")]\n+    pub category: Option<ErrorCategory>,\n+    \n+    /// Whether client can retry this request.\n+    /// Optional - can be inferred from base type; not relevant for all contexts.\n+    #[serde(skip_serializing_if = \"Option::is_none\")]\n+    pub retryable: Option<bool>,\n+    \n+    /// URI identifying this specific occurrence (auto-populated from request path)\n+    #[serde(skip_serializing_if = \"Option::is_none\")]\n+    pub instance: Option<String>,\n+    \n+    /// Structured metadata (key-value context)\n+    #[serde(skip_serializing_if = \"Option::is_none\")]\n+    pub metadata: Option<HashMap<String, String>>,\n+    \n+    /// Validation errors for 4xx responses\n+    #[serde(skip_serializing_if = \"Option::is_none\")]\n+    pub errors: Option<Vec<ValidationViolation>>,\n+    \n+    /// Upstream error chain (when error_stack enabled)\n+    #[serde(skip_serializing_if = \"Option::is_none\")]\n+    pub upstream_errors: Option<Vec<UpstreamError>>,\n+}\n+\n+pub enum ErrorCategory {\n+    /// Platform-level execution errors (panics, OOM, internal bugs)\n+    System,\n+    /// Infrastructure/operational issues (DB unavailable, service down, rate limits)\n+    Operational,\n+    /// Client input/request errors (validation, not found, unauthorized)\n+    Client,\n+}\n+```\n+\n+#### Field Requirements Summary\n+\n+| Field | Required | Reason |\n+|-------|----------|--------|\n+| `type_url` | ✅ Yes | RFC 9457 requires problem type URI |\n+| `title` | ✅ Yes | Human-readable error name (static per type) |\n+| `code` | ✅ Yes | GTS identifier for machine processing |\n+| `trace_id` | ✅ Yes | Request correlation for debugging |\n+| `status` | ❌ No | Only relevant for HTTP; gRPC/events/domain errors don't need it |\n+| `detail` | ❌ No | Instance-specific message; title may suffice |\n+| `category` | ❌ No | Inherited from base type hierarchy |\n+| `retryable` | ❌ No | Inherited from base type; not relevant for all contexts |\n+| `instance` | ❌ No | Auto-populated from request path when applicable |\n+| `metadata` | ❌ No | Additional context key-value pairs |\n+| `errors` | ❌ No | Validation violations for 4xx errors |\n+| `upstream_errors` | ❌ No | Error chain from upstream services |\n+\n+**Note:** When converting to HTTP response, `status` is populated from the error definition. When the error is used in non-HTTP contexts (gRPC, domain logic, events), `status` remains `None`.\n+\n+### R2: GTS Identifier and Base Type Requirements\n+\n+Every error MUST have a valid GTS identifier and specify its base type using the `base` field.\n+\n+#### GTS ID Format\n+\n+```\n+gts.<vendor>.<package>.<namespace>.<type>.v<version>~\n+```\n+\n+**Examples:**\n+- `gts.hx.types_registry.entity.not_found.v1~` - Types registry not found error\n+- `gts.hx.file_parser.validation.invalid_format.v1~` - File parser validation error\n+- `gts.hx.system.runtime.timeout.v1~` - System timeout error\n+\n+#### Base Type Chaining\n+\n+Errors form an inheritance chain using the `base` field. The `base` field references another error struct type (not a string literal), similar to how `struct_to_gts_schema` works.\n+\n+The root base error type is:\n+\n+```rust\n+/// Root error type for all GTS errors.\n+#[gts_error(\n+    gts_id = \"gts.hx.core.errors.err.v1~\",\n+    base = true,  // Marks this as a root base type (no parent)\n+    title = \"Error\",\n+    // Optional attributes with defaults for inheritance:\n+    status = 500,        // Default HTTP status (optional, inherited by children)\n+    category = \"System\", // Default category (optional, inherited by children)\n+    retryable = false    // Default retryable (optional, inherited by children)\n+)]\n+pub struct BaseError;\n+```\n+\n+All module-specific errors MUST reference their base type as a struct (extending the appropriate logical/system error):\n+\n+```rust\n+use modkit_errors::system::logical::NotFoundError;\n+\n+/// Entity was not found in the types registry.\n+/// Note: status, category, retryable are inherited from NotFoundError if not specified.\n+#[gts_error(\n+    gts_id = \"gts.hx.types_registry.entity.not_found.v1~\",\n+    base = NotFoundError,  // Extends logical.not_found, not BaseError\n+    title = \"Entity Not Found\",\n+    // These are optional - inherited from base if omitted:\n+    // status = 404,      // Inherited from NotFoundError\n+    // category = \"Client\", // Inherited from NotFoundError  \n+    // retryable = false,   // Inherited from NotFoundError\n+)]\n+pub struct EntityNotFoundError {\n+    pub gts_id: String,\n+}\n+```\n+\n+#### Multi-Level Inheritance\n+\n+Errors can form deeper inheritance chains:\n+\n+```rust\n+/// Logical not found error (platform-level).\n+#[gts_error(\n+    gts_id = \"gts.hx.system.logical.not_found.v1~\",\n+    base = BaseError,  // Platform errors extend BaseError\n+    status = 404,\n+    title = \"Not Found\",\n+    category = \"Client\",\n+    retryable = false\n+)]\n+pub struct NotFoundError;\n+\n+/// Types registry entity not found (module-level).\n+#[gts_error(\n+    gts_id = \"gts.hx.types_registry.entity.not_found.v1~\",\n+    base = NotFoundError,  // Module errors extend logical errors\n+    status = 404,\n+    title = \"Entity Not Found\",\n+    category = \"Client\",\n+    retryable = false\n+)]\n+pub struct EntityNotFoundError {\n+    pub gts_id: String,\n+}\n+```\n+\n+#### Inheritance Hierarchy\n+\n+```\n+BaseError (gts.hx.core.errors.err.v1~)                              [base = true]\n+├── Transport Errors (hx.system.transport.*)                        [base = BaseError]\n+├── Runtime Errors (hx.system.runtime.*)                            [base = BaseError]\n+│   └── hx.types_registry.system.internal.v1~                       [base = runtime.internal]\n+├── HTTP Errors (hx.system.http.*)                                  [base = BaseError]\n+│   └── hx.auth.token_expired.v1~                                   [base = http.unauthorized]\n+├── gRPC Errors (hx.system.grpc.*)                                  [base = BaseError]\n+└── Logical Errors (hx.system.logical.*)                            [base = BaseError]\n+    ├── logical.not_found.v1~                                       [base = BaseError]\n+    │   ├── hx.types_registry.entity.not_found.v1~                  [base = logical.not_found]\n+    │   └── hx.db.entity.not_found.v1~                              [base = logical.not_found]\n+    ├── logical.already_exists.v1~                                  [base = BaseError]\n+    │   └── hx.types_registry.entity.already_exists.v1~             [base = logical.already_exists]\n+    └── logical.validation_failed.v1~                               [base = BaseError]\n+        └── hx.file_parser.validation.invalid_format.v1~            [base = logical.validation_failed]\n+```\n+\n+### R3: Trace ID Requirements\n+\n+- Every error response MUST include a non-empty `trace_id`\n+- Trace ID MUST be propagated from incoming request headers or generated\n+- Trace ID MUST be logged with the error for correlation\n+\n+### R4: Types Registry Integration\n+\n+- All error types MUST be registered in the types registry at startup\n+- Error schema MUST extend base error type: `gts.hx.core.errors.err.v1`\n+- Registration MUST include: code, title, status, category, retryable flag\n+\n+### R5: Standardized System Error Types\n+\n+See [GTS System Errors Catalog](#gts-system-errors-catalog) for the complete list of all system errors.\n+\n+### R6: Error Stack Propagation\n+\n+When a function calls another service/function that returns an error:\n+- The error SHOULD be wrapped with context\n+- `upstream_errors` array SHOULD contain the chain of errors\n+- Each upstream error includes: `code`, `title`, `detail`, `source`\n+- Propagation controlled by `error_stack` configuration flag\n+\n+---\n+\n+## GTS Error Code Format\n+\n+### Structure\n+\n+```\n+gts.<vendor>.<package>.<namespace>.<type>.<version>~<chain>\n+```\n+\n+### Components\n+\n+| Component | Description | Example |\n+|-----------|-------------|---------|\n+| `gts` | Global Type System prefix | `gts` |\n+| `vendor` | Organization identifier | `hx` (Hyperspot) |\n+| `package` | Module/service name | `types_registry`, `file_parser` |\n+| `namespace` | Error category | `entity`, `validation`, `runtime` |\n+| `type` | Specific error type | `not_found`, `invalid_format` |\n+| `version` | Schema version | `v1`, `v1.0` |\n+| `~chain` | Base type chain | `~hx.core.errors.err.v1` |\n+\n+### Validation Rules\n+\n+1. MUST start with `gts.`\n+2. All segments MUST be lowercase alphanumeric or underscore\n+3. No empty segments allowed\n+4. Final segment MUST be version format (`vN` or `vN.M`)\n+5. MUST chain from base error type\n+\n+### Short Name Derivation\n+\n+Short accessor names derived from final GTX segment:\n+```\n+gts.hx.core.errors.err.v1~hx.types_registry.entity.not_found.v1\n+                         └─────────────────────────────────────┘\n+                                          ↓\n+                         types_registry_entity_not_found_v1()\n+```\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Types Registry Integration\n+\n+### Error Type Schema\n+\n+```json\n+{\n+  \"gts_id\": \"gts.hx.types_registry.entity.not_found.v1~\",\n+  \"kind\": \"error\",\n+  \"schema\": {\n+    \"type\": \"object\",\n+    \"extends\": \"gts.hx.system.logical.not_found.v1~\",\n+    \"properties\": {\n+      \"status\": { \"const\": 404 },\n+      \"title\": { \"const\": \"Entity Not Found\" },\n+      \"category\": { \"const\": \"Client\" },\n+      \"retryable\": { \"const\": false }\n+    }\n+  },\n+  \"metadata\": {\n+    \"module\": \"types-registry\",\n+    \"documentation_url\": \"https://docs.hyperspot.com/errors/types_registry_entity_not_found_v1\"\n+  }\n+}\n+```\n+\n+### Registration Flow\n+\n+1. Module defines errors as explicit structs with `#[gts_error]` attribute in `src/errors.rs`\n+2. Each struct generates `ERROR_DEF` constant with GTS metadata\n+3. Module implements `all_error_definitions()` function returning all error definitions\n+4. At module startup (`on_ready`), errors are registered with types registry:\n+   ```rust\n+   impl Module for MyModule {\n+       async fn on_ready(&self, ctx: &ModuleContext) -> Result<()> {\n+           // Register all error types with types registry\n+           let errors = crate::errors::all_error_definitions();\n+           ctx.types_registry().register_errors(errors).await?;\n+           Ok(())\n+       }\n+   }\n+   ```\n+5. Types registry validates GTS format and schema compliance\n+6. Errors become discoverable via types registry API\n+\n+### API for Error Discovery\n+\n+```http\n+GET /api/types-registry/v1/types?kind=error&module=types-registry\n+\n+Response:\n+{\n+  \"items\": [\n+    {\n+      \"gts_id\": \"gts.hx.core.errors.err.v1~hx.types_registry.entity.not_found.v1\",\n+      \"status\": 404,\n+      \"title\": \"Entity Not Found\",\n+      \"category\": \"Client\",\n+      \"retryable\": false,\n+      \"documentation_url\": \"...\"\n+    }\n+  ]\n+}\n+```\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Implementation Rules\n+\n+### Rule 1: All Errors MUST Use Explicit Struct Definitions with `#[gts_error]`\n+\n+Errors are defined as explicit structs with the `#[gts_error]` attribute macro. This approach:\n+- Makes GTS IDs visible directly in code (better for LLM code generation)\n+- Provides compile-time validation\n+- Generates `Problem` conversion automatically\n+- Enables types registry integration\n+\n+```rust\n+// ✅ CORRECT - Explicit struct definition with visible GTS ID and base type reference\n+use modkit_errors::gts_error;\n+\n+// First, import the appropriate base error types from system errors\n+use modkit_errors::system::logical::{NotFoundError, AlreadyExistsError, ValidationFailedError};\n+\n+/// Entity was not found in the types registry.\n+#[gts_error(\n+    gts_id = \"gts.hx.types_registry.entity.not_found.v1~\",\n+    base = NotFoundError,  // Extends logical.not_found, not BaseError\n+    status = 404,\n+    title = \"Entity Not Found\",\n+    category = \"Client\",\n+    retryable = false\n+)]\n+pub struct EntityNotFoundError {\n+    /// The GTS ID that was not found\n+    pub gts_id: String,\n+}\n+\n+/// Entity already exists in the registry.\n+#[gts_error(\n+    gts_id = \"gts.hx.types_registry.entity.already_exists.v1~\",\n+    base = AlreadyExistsError,  // Extends logical.already_exists\n+    status = 409,\n+    title = \"Entity Already Exists\",\n+    category = \"Client\",\n+    retryable = false\n+)]\n+pub struct EntityAlreadyExistsError {\n+    /// The GTS ID that already exists\n+    pub gts_id: String,\n+}\n+\n+/// Invalid GTS ID format.\n+#[gts_error(\n+    gts_id = \"gts.hx.types_registry.validation.invalid_gts_id.v1~\",\n+    base = ValidationFailedError,  // Extends logical.validation_failed\n+    status = 400,\n+    title = \"Invalid GTS ID\",\n+    category = \"Client\",\n+    retryable = false\n+)]\n+pub struct InvalidGtsIdError {\n+    /// Description of the validation error\n+    pub message: String,\n+}\n+\n+// ❌ WRONG - Inline error definitions without GTS ID\n+impl From<DomainError> for Problem {\n+    fn from(e: DomainError) -> Self {\n+        Problem::new(StatusCode::NOT_FOUND, \"Not Found\", \"...\")\n+            .with_code(\"SOME_CODE\") // Not GTS format!\n+    }\n+}\n+\n+// ❌ WRONG - JSON-based declaration (GTS ID hidden in external file)\n+declare_errors! {\n+    path = \"gts/errors.json\",\n+    namespace = \"errors\",\n+    vis = \"pub\"\n+}\n+```\n+\n+### Rule 2: Error Struct Field Conventions\n+\n+Error structs contain context fields that become `metadata` in the Problem response:\n+\n+```rust\n+use modkit_errors::system::logical::ValidationFailedError as LogicalValidationFailed;\n+\n+/// Request validation failed (module-specific).\n+#[gts_error(\n+    gts_id = \"gts.hx.types_registry.validation.failed.v1~\",\n+    base = LogicalValidationFailed,  // Extends logical.validation_failed\n+    status = 422,\n+    title = \"Validation Failed\",\n+    category = \"Client\",\n+    retryable = false\n+)]\n+pub struct ValidationFailedError {\n+    /// Human-readable error message\n+    pub message: String,\n+    /// Field that failed validation (optional)\n+    #[gts_error(skip_metadata)]  // Don't include in metadata\n+    pub violations: Vec<ValidationViolation>,\n+}\n+```\n+\n+### Rule 3: Error Mapping Pattern\n+\n+```rust\n+use crate::errors::{EntityNotFoundError, EntityAlreadyExistsError, InvalidGtsIdError};\n+\n+pub fn domain_error_to_problem(e: &DomainError) -> Problem {\n+    match e {\n+        DomainError::NotFound { id } => {\n+            // into_problem() auto-populates trace_id from current tracing span\n+            EntityNotFoundError { gts_id: id.clone() }\n+                .into_problem()\n+                .with_detail(format!(\"Entity with GTS ID '{}' was not found\", id))\n+        }\n+        DomainError::AlreadyExists { id } => {\n+            EntityAlreadyExistsError { gts_id: id.clone() }\n+                .into_problem()\n+                .with_detail(format!(\"Entity with GTS ID '{}' already exists\", id))\n+        }\n+        DomainError::InvalidGtsId(msg) => {\n+            InvalidGtsIdError { message: msg.clone() }\n+                .into_problem()\n+        }\n+        // ...\n+    }\n+}\n+```\n+\n+### Rule 4: Trace ID Auto-Population\n+\n+Trace ID is **mandatory** in all error responses but **optional** in `into_problem()`. If not provided, it's auto-populated from the current tracing span.\n+\n+```rust\n+// Default: trace_id auto-populated from current tracing span\n+let problem = EntityNotFoundError { gts_id: id.clone() }\n+    .into_problem()  // trace_id extracted from tracing::Span::current()\n+    .with_detail(\"Entity not found\");\n+\n+// Override: explicitly pass trace_id if needed\n+let problem = EntityNotFoundError { gts_id: id.clone() }\n+    .into_problem()\n+    .with_trace_id(&custom_trace_id)  // Override auto-populated value\n+    .with_detail(\"Entity not found\");\n+```\n+\n+### Rule 5: Instance Auto-Population\n+\n+The `instance` field is **optional** and **auto-populated** from the request path in the Axum `IntoResponse` implementation. You don't need to pass it manually.\n+\n+```rust\n+// In Axum IntoResponse implementation\n+impl IntoResponse for Problem {\n+    fn into_response(self) -> Response {\n+        // Auto-populate instance from request URI if not set\n+        let problem = if self.instance.is_none() {\n+            // Instance is populated from request extensions or current URI\n+            if let Some(uri) = REQUEST_URI.try_with(|u| u.clone()).ok() {\n+                self.with_instance(uri.path())\n+            } else {\n+                self\n+            }\n+        } else {\n+            self\n+        };\n+        // ... rest of response building\n+    }\n+}\n+```\n+\n+If you need to override the instance manually, use `with_instance()`:\n+\n+```rust\n+let problem = EntityNotFoundError { gts_id: id.clone() }\n+    .into_problem()\n+    .with_instance(\"/custom/path\");  // Optional override\n+```\n+\n+### Rule 6: Error Registration at Startup\n+\n+Error definitions are **auto-collected** at compile time using the `#[gts_error]` macro with `linkme`. No manual registration list needed.\n+\n+#### How `linkme` Works\n+\n+The [`linkme`](https://docs.rs/linkme) crate provides **distributed slices** - a way to collect static items from across the crate into a single slice at link time.\n+\n+**Step 1: Define the collection point** (in `src/errors.rs`):\n+```rust\n+use linkme::distributed_slice;\n+\n+/// This is the \"collection point\" - an empty slice that will be filled at link time.\n+/// The linker will gather all items marked with #[distributed_slice(ERROR_DEFINITIONS)]\n+/// and place them contiguously in this slice.\n+#[distributed_slice]\n+pub static ERROR_DEFINITIONS: [&'static GtsErrorDefStatic];\n+```\n+\n+**Step 2: Each `#[gts_error]` macro generates a contributor**:\n+```rust\n+// When you write:\n+#[gts_error(\n+    gts_id = \"gts.hx.types_registry.entity.not_found.v1~\",\n+    base = NotFoundError,  // Extends logical.not_found\n+    status = 404,\n+    ...\n+)]\n+pub struct EntityNotFoundError { ... }\n+\n+// The macro generates (among other things):\n+impl EntityNotFoundError {\n+    pub const ERROR_DEF: GtsErrorDefStatic = GtsErrorDefStatic { ... };\n+}\n+\n+// AND this linkme contributor:\n+#[linkme::distributed_slice(crate::errors::ERROR_DEFINITIONS)]\n+#[linkme(crate = linkme)]\n+static __ENTITY_NOT_FOUND_ERROR_DEF: &'static GtsErrorDefStatic = &EntityNotFoundError::ERROR_DEF;\n+```\n+\n+**Step 3: At link time, the linker collects all contributors**:\n+```\n+┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n+│                    Link-Time Collection                          │\n+├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n+│                                                                  │\n+│  EntityNotFoundError::ERROR_DEF ──────┐                         │\n+│  EntityAlreadyExistsError::ERROR_DEF ─┼──► ERROR_DEFINITIONS[]  │\n+│  InvalidGtsIdError::ERROR_DEF ────────┤    (contiguous slice)   │\n+│  ValidationFailedError::ERROR_DEF ────┤                         │\n+│  ServiceNotReadyError::ERROR_DEF ─────┤                         │\n+│  InternalError::ERROR_DEF ────────────┘                         │\n+│                                                                  │\n+│  The linker places all #[distributed_slice(ERROR_DEFINITIONS)]  │\n+│  items into a contiguous memory section, making them accessible │\n+│  as a single &[&'static GtsErrorDefStatic] slice at runtime.    │\n+│                                                                  │\n+└─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘\n+```\n+\n+**Step 4: Access at runtime**:\n+```rust\n+pub fn all_error_definitions() -> &'static [&'static GtsErrorDefStatic] {\n+    &ERROR_DEFINITIONS  // Returns slice with ALL error defs, auto-collected\n+}\n+```\n+\n+#### Why This Works\n+\n+- **Linker magic**: `linkme` uses platform-specific linker sections (`.init_array` on Linux, `__DATA,__mod_init_func` on macOS) to collect items\n+- **Zero runtime cost**: Collection happens at link time, not runtime\n+- **Compile-time guarantee**: If you use `#[gts_error]`, it's automatically in the slice\n+- **No manual list**: Impossible to forget an error - the macro handles registration\n+\n+#### Module Startup\n+\n+```rust\n+impl Module for MyModule {\n+    async fn on_ready(&self, ctx: &ModuleContext) -> Result<()> {\n+        // All errors are auto-collected - no way to forget one!\n+        let errors = crate::errors::all_error_definitions();\n+        ctx.types_registry().register_errors(errors).await?;\n+        Ok(())\n+    }\n+}\n+```\n+\n+### Rule 7: Metadata for Dynamic Context\n+\n+```rust\n+// ✅ CORRECT - Use metadata for dynamic values\n+ValidationFailedError { message: \"Validation failed\".to_string(), violations: vec![] }\n+    .into_problem()  // trace_id auto-populated from tracing span\n+    .with_metadata([\n+        (\"field\", \"email\"),\n+        (\"constraint\", \"must be valid email format\"),\n+        (\"provided_value\", \"[REDACTED]\"), // Never expose sensitive data\n+    ])\n+\n+// ❌ WRONG - Parsing dynamic values from detail string\n+ValidationFailedError { \n+    message: \"Field 'email' failed constraint 'must be valid email'\".to_string(),\n+    violations: vec![] \n+}\n+    .into_problem()\n+```\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Migration Plan\n+\n+### Phase 1: Create `#[gts_error]` Macro\n+\n+1. Create new proc-macro crate `libs/modkit-errors-macro-v2/` with `#[gts_error]` attribute macro\n+2. Implement macro to generate:\n+   - `GTS_ID`, `STATUS`, `TITLE`, `CATEGORY`, `RETRYABLE` constants\n+   - `ERROR_DEF` static for registration\n+   - `into_problem()` method\n+   - `to_metadata()` for struct fields → HashMap conversion\n+   - `Display` and `Error` trait implementations\n+3. Add compile-time GTS format validation\n+4. Add field attribute `#[gts_error(skip_metadata)]` and `#[gts_error(as_errors)]`\n+\n+### Phase 2: Extend Problem Struct\n+\n+1. Extend `Problem` struct with new fields:\n+   - `category: ErrorCategory`\n+   - `retryable: bool`\n+   - `metadata: Option<HashMap<String, String>>`\n+   - `upstream_errors: Option<Vec<UpstreamError>>`\n+   - Make `trace_id` non-optional (String instead of Option<String>)\n+2. Add builder methods: `with_category()`, `with_retryable()`, `with_metadata()`\n+3. Update `IntoResponse` implementation\n+\n+### Phase 3: Types Registry Integration\n+\n+1. Define `GtsErrorDef` trait and `GtsErrorDefStatic` struct\n+2. Add error registration API to types registry\n+3. Implement `register_errors()` method in module context\n+4. Add error discovery endpoint: `GET /api/types-registry/v1/types?kind=error`\n+\n+### Phase 4: Module Migration\n+\n+Migrate modules to explicit struct-based errors:\n+1. `types-registry` - Create `src/errors.rs` with `#[gts_error]` structs\n+2. `file_parser` - Create `src/errors.rs` with `#[gts_error]` structs\n+3. `nodes_registry` - Create `src/errors.rs` with `#[gts_error]` structs\n+4. `api_gateway` - Create `src/errors.rs` with `#[gts_error]` structs\n+\n+### Phase 5: System Errors Library\n+\n+1. Create `libs/modkit-errors/src/system_errors.rs` with common errors:\n+   - `InternalServerError`, `ServiceUnavailableError`, `GatewayTimeoutError`\n+   - `UnauthorizedError`, `ForbiddenError`, `NotFoundError`\n+   - `BadRequestError`, `ValidationFailedError`, `ConflictError`\n+   - `RateLimitedError`\n+2. Export from `modkit::errors::system` for all modules to use\n+3. Register system errors at platform startup\n+\n+### Phase 6: Deprecate `declare_errors!`\n+\n+1. Mark `declare_errors!` macro as deprecated\n+2. Update `GTS_ERRORS.md` documentation\n+3. Add migration guide from JSON-based to struct-based errors\n+4. Remove JSON error catalogs from migrated modules\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Examples\n+\n+### Example 1: Complete Error Response\n+\n+```json\n+{\n+  \"type\": \"https://docs.hyperspot.com/errors/types_registry_entity_not_found_v1\",\n+  \"title\": \"Entity Not Found\",\n+  \"status\": 404,\n+  \"detail\": \"Entity with GTS ID 'gts.hx.example.test.v1' was not found in the registry\",\n+  \"instance\": \"/api/types-registry/v1/types/gts.hx.example.test.v1\",\n+  \"code\": \"gts.hx.core.errors.err.v1~hx.types_registry.entity.not_found.v1\",\n+  \"trace_id\": \"abc123-def456-ghi789\",\n+  \"category\": \"Client\",\n+  \"retryable\": false,\n+  \"metadata\": {\n+    \"gts_id\": \"gts.hx.example.test.v1\",\n+    \"searched_at\": \"2026-01-19T13:30:00Z\"\n+  }\n+}\n+```\n+\n+### Example 2: Validation Error with Multiple Violations\n+\n+```json\n+{\n+  \"type\": \"https://docs.hyperspot.com/errors/validation_failed_v1\",\n+  \"title\": \"Validation Failed\",\n+  \"status\": 422,\n+  \"detail\": \"Request validation failed with 2 errors\",\n+  \"instance\": \"/api/users/v1/users\",\n+  \"code\": \"gts.hx.core.errors.err.v1~hx.system.validation_failed.v1\",\n+  \"trace_id\": \"req-12345\",\n+  \"category\": \"Client\",\n+  \"retryable\": false,\n+  \"errors\": [\n+    {\n+      \"field\": \"email\",\n+      \"message\": \"Must be a valid email address\",\n+      \"code\": \"INVALID_EMAIL_FORMAT\"\n+    },\n+    {\n+      \"field\": \"age\",\n+      \"message\": \"Must be at least 18\",\n+      \"code\": \"MIN_VALUE_VIOLATION\"\n+    }\n+  ]\n+}\n+```\n+\n+### Example 3: Error with Upstream Chain\n+\n+```json\n+{\n+  \"type\": \"https://docs.hyperspot.com/errors/upstream_error_v1\",\n+  \"title\": \"Upstream Service Error\",\n+  \"status\": 502,\n+  \"detail\": \"Failed to fetch user data from identity service\",\n+  \"instance\": \"/api/users/v1/users/123/profile\",\n+  \"code\": \"gts.hx.core.errors.err.v1~hx.users.upstream.identity_failed.v1\",\n+  \"trace_id\": \"trace-abc-123\",\n+  \"category\": \"System\",\n+  \"retryable\": true,\n+  \"upstream_errors\": [\n+    {\n+      \"code\": \"gts.hx.core.errors.err.v1~hx.identity.user.not_found.v1\",\n+      \"title\": \"User Not Found\",\n+      \"detail\": \"User 123 not found in identity service\",\n+      \"source\": \"identity-service\"\n+    }\n+  ]\n+}\n+```\n+\n+### Example 4: Complete Error Module Definition\n+\n+```rust\n+//! Error definitions for the Types Registry module.\n+//!\n+//! All errors are defined as explicit structs with `#[gts_error]` attribute.\n+//! This makes GTS IDs visible in code for better LLM code generation.\n+\n+use modkit_errors::{gts_error, ValidationViolation};\n+use modkit_errors::system::logical::{NotFoundError, AlreadyExistsError, ValidationFailedError as LogicalValidationFailed, OperationFailedError};\n+use modkit_errors::system::runtime::{UnavailableError, InternalError as RuntimeInternalError};\n+\n+// =============================================================================\n+// Client Errors (4xx) - Extend logical errors\n+// =============================================================================\n+\n+/// Entity was not found in the types registry.\n+#[gts_error(\n+    gts_id = \"gts.hx.types_registry.entity.not_found.v1~\",\n+    base = NotFoundError,  // Extends gts.hx.system.logical.not_found.v1~\n+    status = 404,\n+    title = \"Entity Not Found\",\n+    category = \"Client\",\n+    retryable = false\n+)]\n+pub struct EntityNotFoundError {\n+    /// The GTS ID that was not found\n+    pub gts_id: String,\n+}\n+\n+/// Entity already exists in the registry.\n+#[gts_error(\n+    gts_id = \"gts.hx.types_registry.entity.already_exists.v1~\",\n+    base = AlreadyExistsError,  // Extends gts.hx.system.logical.already_exists.v1~\n+    status = 409,\n+    title = \"Entity Already Exists\",\n+    category = \"Client\",\n+    retryable = false\n+)]\n+pub struct EntityAlreadyExistsError {\n+    /// The GTS ID that already exists\n+    pub gts_id: String,\n+}\n+\n+/// Invalid GTS ID format provided.\n+#[gts_error(\n+    gts_id = \"gts.hx.types_registry.validation.invalid_gts_id.v1~\",\n+    base = LogicalValidationFailed,  // Extends gts.hx.system.logical.validation_failed.v1~\n+    status = 400,\n+    title = \"Invalid GTS ID\",\n+    category = \"Client\",\n+    retryable = false\n+)]\n+pub struct InvalidGtsIdError {\n+    /// Description of what's wrong with the GTS ID\n+    pub message: String,\n+}\n+\n+/// Request validation failed.\n+#[gts_error(\n+    gts_id = \"gts.hx.types_registry.validation.failed.v1~\",\n+    base = LogicalValidationFailed,  // Extends gts.hx.system.logical.validation_failed.v1~\n+    status = 422,\n+    title = \"Validation Failed\",\n+    category = \"Client\",\n+    retryable = false\n+)]\n+pub struct ValidationFailedError {\n+    /// Human-readable summary\n+    pub message: String,\n+    /// Individual validation violations\n+    #[gts_error(as_errors)]  // Maps to Problem.errors field\n+    pub violations: Vec<ValidationViolation>,\n+}\n+\n+// =============================================================================\n+// Operational Errors (5xx - Retryable) - Extend runtime/logical errors\n+// =============================================================================\n+\n+/// Service is not ready to accept requests.\n+#[gts_error(\n+    gts_id = \"gts.hx.types_registry.operational.not_ready.v1~\",\n+    base = UnavailableError,  // Extends gts.hx.system.runtime.unavailable.v1~\n+    status = 503,\n+    title = \"Service Not Ready\",\n+    category = \"Operational\",\n+    retryable = true\n+)]\n+pub struct ServiceNotReadyError;\n+\n+/// Registry activation failed due to validation errors.\n+#[gts_error(\n+    gts_id = \"gts.hx.types_registry.operational.activation_failed.v1~\",\n+    base = OperationFailedError,  // Extends gts.hx.system.logical.operation_failed.v1~\n+    status = 500,\n+    title = \"Registry Activation Failed\",\n+    category = \"Operational\",\n+    retryable = false\n+)]\n+pub struct ActivationFailedError {\n+    /// Number of validation errors\n+    pub error_count: usize,\n+    /// Summary of errors\n+    pub summary: String,\n+}\n+\n+// =============================================================================\n+// System Errors (5xx - Internal) - Extend runtime errors\n+// =============================================================================\n+\n+/// Internal server error.\n+#[gts_error(\n+    gts_id = \"gts.hx.types_registry.system.internal.v1~\",\n+    base = RuntimeInternalError,  // Extends gts.hx.system.runtime.internal.v1~\n+    status = 500,\n+    title = \"Internal Server Error\",\n+    category = \"System\",\n+    retryable = true\n+)]\n+pub struct InternalError;\n+\n+// =============================================================================\n+// Error Auto-Collection (via linkme)\n+// =============================================================================\n+\n+use linkme::distributed_slice;\n+\n+/// Auto-collected error definitions - no manual list needed!\n+/// Each #[gts_error] struct automatically registers itself here.\n+#[distributed_slice]\n+pub static ERROR_DEFINITIONS: [&'static GtsErrorDefStatic];\n+\n+/// Get all error definitions (auto-collected at compile time).\n+pub fn all_error_definitions() -> &'static [&'static GtsErrorDefStatic] {\n+    &ERROR_DEFINITIONS\n+}\n+\n+// Note: The manual list below is NO LONGER NEEDED - shown for reference only.\n+// Each #[gts_error] macro generates a #[distributed_slice] entry automatically.\n+//\n+// OLD APPROACH (error-prone, easy to forget):\n+// pub fn all_error_definitions() -> Vec<&'static dyn GtsErrorDef> {\n+//     vec![\n+//         &EntityNotFoundError::ERROR_DEF,\n+//         &EntityAlreadyExistsError::ERROR_DEF,\n+//         ...\n+//     ]\n+// }\n+```\n+\n+### Example 5: Complete Usage in Handler\n+\n+```rust\n+// In src/errors.rs - see Example 4 for full error definitions\n+\n+// In src/api/rest/error.rs\n+use crate::errors::*;\n+use crate::domain::error::DomainError;\n+\n+impl DomainError {\n+    /// Convert domain error to Problem response.\n+    ///\n+    /// Each error struct contains its GTS ID in the `#[gts_error]` attribute,\n+    /// making it visible to LLMs and developers reading the code.\n+    ///\n+    /// Note: `trace_id` and `instance` are auto-populated.\n+    pub fn to_problem(&self) -> Problem {\n+        match self {\n+            DomainError::NotFound(id) => {\n+                // GTS ID visible: gts.hx.types_registry.entity.not_found.v1~\n+                EntityNotFoundError { gts_id: id.clone() }\n+                    .into_problem()\n+                    .with_detail(format!(\"Entity with GTS ID '{}' was not found\", id))\n+            }\n+            DomainError::AlreadyExists(id) => {\n+                // GTS ID visible: gts.hx.types_registry.entity.already_exists.v1~\n+                EntityAlreadyExistsError { gts_id: id.clone() }\n+                    .into_problem()\n+                    .with_detail(format!(\"Entity with GTS ID '{}' already exists\", id))\n+            }\n+            DomainError::InvalidGtsId(msg) => {\n+                // GTS ID visible: gts.hx.types_registry.validation.invalid_gts_id.v1~\n+                InvalidGtsIdError { message: msg.clone() }\n+                    .into_problem()\n+            }\n+            DomainError::ValidationFailed { message, violations } => {\n+                // GTS ID visible: gts.hx.types_registry.validation.failed.v1~\n+                ValidationFailedError {\n+                    message: message.clone(),\n+                    violations: violations.clone(),\n+                }\n+                    .into_problem()\n+            }\n+            DomainError::NotInReadyMode => {\n+                // GTS ID visible: gts.hx.types_registry.operational.not_ready.v1~\n+                ServiceNotReadyError\n+                    .into_problem()\n+                    .with_detail(\"The types registry is not yet ready to accept requests\")\n+            }\n+            DomainError::ReadyCommitFailed(errors) => {\n+                // GTS ID visible: gts.hx.types_registry.operational.activation_failed.v1~\n+                ActivationFailedError {\n+                    error_count: errors.len(),\n+                    summary: errors.iter().map(|e| e.to_string()).collect::<Vec<_>>().join(\"; \"),\n+                }\n+                    .into_problem()\n+            }\n+            DomainError::Internal(e) => {\n+                tracing::error!(error = ?e, \"Internal error in types_registry\");\n+                // GTS ID visible: gts.hx.types_registry.system.internal.v1~\n+                InternalError\n+                    .into_problem()\n+                    .with_detail(\"An internal error occurred\")\n+            }\n+        }\n+    }\n+}\n+\n+// In handler - trace_id and instance are auto-populated\n+async fn get_type(\n+    State(state): State<AppState>,\n+    Path(gts_id): Path<String>,\n+) -> Result<Json<TypeDefinition>, Problem> {\n+    state.service\n+        .get_type(&gts_id)\n+        .await\n+        .map(Json)\n+        .map_err(|e| e.to_problem())\n+}\n+```\n+\n+### Example 6: Generated Code from `#[gts_error]` Macro\n+\n+The `#[gts_error]` attribute macro generates the following for each error struct:\n+\n+```rust\n+// Original:\n+#[gts_error(\n+    gts_id = \"gts.hx.types_registry.entity.not_found.v1~\",\n+    base = NotFoundError,  // Reference to logical.not_found parent struct\n+    status = 404,\n+    title = \"Entity Not Found\",\n+    category = \"Client\",\n+    retryable = false\n+)]\n+pub struct EntityNotFoundError {\n+    pub gts_id: String,\n+}\n+\n+// Generated:\n+pub struct EntityNotFoundError {\n+    pub gts_id: String,\n+}\n+\n+impl EntityNotFoundError {\n+    /// GTS error code identifier\n+    pub const GTS_ID: &'static str = \"gts.hx.types_registry.entity.not_found.v1~\";\n+    \n+    /// Base error type (resolved from NotFoundError::GTS_ID at compile time)\n+    pub const BASE: &'static str = NotFoundError::GTS_ID;  // \"gts.hx.system.logical.not_found.v1~\"\n+    \n+    /// HTTP status code\n+    pub const STATUS: u16 = 404;\n+    \n+    /// Human-readable title\n+    pub const TITLE: &'static str = \"Entity Not Found\";\n+    \n+    /// Error category\n+    pub const CATEGORY: ErrorCategory = ErrorCategory::Client;\n+    \n+    /// Whether this error is retryable\n+    pub const RETRYABLE: bool = false;\n+    \n+    /// Static error definition for registration\n+    pub const ERROR_DEF: GtsErrorDefStatic = GtsErrorDefStatic {\n+        gts_id: Self::GTS_ID,\n+        base: Self::BASE,\n+        status: Self::STATUS,\n+        title: Self::TITLE,\n+        category: Self::CATEGORY,\n+        retryable: Self::RETRYABLE,\n+        type_url: \"https://docs.hyperspot.com/errors/hx_types_registry_entity_not_found_v1\",","path":"intended_design/UNIFIED_ERROR_SYSTEM.md","commit_id":"5bdb0f43b25858af78999718f7247813802b9634","original_commit_id":"5bdb0f43b25858af78999718f7247813802b9634","user":{"login":"MikeFalcon77","id":3686170,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM2ODYxNzA=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3686170?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/MikeFalcon77","html_url":"https://github.com/MikeFalcon77","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MikeFalcon77/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MikeFalcon77/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MikeFalcon77/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MikeFalcon77/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MikeFalcon77/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MikeFalcon77/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MikeFalcon77/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MikeFalcon77/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MikeFalcon77/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Make sure type_url is stable and deterministic (no environment-dependent base URL). Ideally it should be a canonical documentation URL or a consistent internal URI scheme. I am not sure that `hyperspot.com` is ok (in this example)","created_at":"2026-01-28T11:56:09Z","updated_at":"2026-01-28T12:02:23Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/290#discussion_r2736298131","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/290","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2736298131"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/290#discussion_r2736298131"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/290"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2736298131/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":null,"original_line":1197,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"MEMBER","original_position":1197,"position":1,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2736301365","pull_request_review_id":3715718572,"id":2736301365,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs6jGKU1","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,1574 @@\n+# Unified Error System - Intention Document\n+\n+This document defines the architecture, rules, and implementation plan for a unified error handling system across the Hyperspot project. All REST API errors MUST have a GTS identifier, trace ID, and be registered in the types registry.\n+\n+## Table of Contents\n+\n+1. [Executive Summary](#executive-summary)\n+2. [Industry Research](#industry-research)\n+3. [Current State Analysis](#current-state-analysis)\n+4. [Requirements](#requirements)\n+5. [Implementation Rules](#implementation-rules)\n+6. [Migration Plan](#migration-plan)\n+7. [Examples](#examples)\n+8. [HTTP Headers](#http-headers)\n+9. [Security Considerations](#security-considerations)\n+10. [Appendix A: Error Category Definitions](#appendix-a-error-category-definitions)\n+11. [Appendix B: Retryable Error Guidelines](#appendix-b-retryable-error-guidelines)\n+12. [GTS System Errors Catalog](#gts-system-errors-catalog)\n+13. [References](#references)\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Executive Summary\n+\n+### Problem Statement\n+\n+The current error handling across Hyperspot modules is inconsistent:\n+- Some modules use `declare_errors!` macro with JSON catalogs\n+- Others define errors inline without GTS codes\n+- Errors are not registered in the types registry\n+- No standardized metadata/context fields\n+- Inconsistent trace ID propagation\n+\n+### Goals\n+\n+1. **Every REST API error** MUST have a valid GTS identifier\n+2. **Every error response** MUST include a trace ID for debugging\n+3. **All error types** MUST be registered in the types registry\n+4. **Consistent error schema** across all modules following RFC 9457\n+5. **Machine-readable error codes** for programmatic handling\n+6. **Error stack propagation** for nested service calls\n+\n+### Non-Goals\n+\n+- Changing internal domain error types (only API-facing errors)\n+- Modifying logging infrastructure\n+- Changing HTTP status code semantics\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Industry Research\n+\n+### How Major Tech Companies Handle Errors\n+\n+| Company | Standard | Key Features |\n+|---------|----------|--------------|\n+| **Google** | AIP-193 + gRPC Status | `reason` (UPPER_SNAKE_CASE), `domain` (service name), `metadata` (key-value context), `ErrorInfo`, `LocalizedMessage`, `Help` links |\n+| **Amazon AWS** | Custom JSON | `errorType`, `httpStatus`, `requestId`, `message`, custom error object serialization |\n+| **Twitter/X** | JSON with `errors` array | `code` (CAPS_CASE), `message`, `parameter`, `details`, `value` |\n+| **RFC 9457** | Problem Details | `type` (URI), `title`, `status`, `detail`, `instance`, extension members |\n+\n+### Key Patterns Identified\n+\n+1. **Machine-readable identifiers** - Unique codes for programmatic handling (Google's `reason`, Twitter's `code`)\n+2. **Domain/namespace separation** - Identify error source (Google's `domain`, our GTS vendor.package)\n+3. **Structured metadata** - Key-value context without parsing messages (Google's `ErrorInfo.metadata`)\n+4. **Trace/Request IDs** - Correlation for debugging (AWS `requestId`, our `trace_id`)\n+5. **Documentation links** - URIs to error documentation (RFC 9457 `type`, Google's `Help`)\n+6. **Error categorization** - System vs User-defined, Retryable vs Non-retryable\n+\n+### Google AIP-193 ErrorInfo Structure (Reference)\n+\n+```json\n+{\n+  \"error\": {\n+    \"code\": 429,\n+    \"message\": \"The zone 'us-east1-a' does not have enough resources...\",\n+    \"status\": \"RESOURCE_EXHAUSTED\",\n+    \"details\": [\n+      {\n+        \"@type\": \"type.googleapis.com/google.rpc.ErrorInfo\",\n+        \"reason\": \"RESOURCE_AVAILABILITY\",\n+        \"domain\": \"compute.googleapis.com\",\n+        \"metadata\": {\n+          \"zone\": \"us-east1-a\",\n+          \"vmType\": \"e2-medium\"\n+        }\n+      }\n+    ]\n+  }\n+}\n+```\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Current State Analysis\n+\n+### Existing Infrastructure\n+\n+1. **`Problem` struct** (`libs/modkit-errors/src/problem.rs`) - RFC 9457 compliant\n+   - Fields: `type_url`, `title`, `status`, `detail`, `instance`, `code`, `trace_id`, `errors`\n+   - Implements `IntoResponse` for Axum with automatic trace ID enrichment\n+\n+2. **`struct_to_gts_schema` macro** (`modules/types-registry/gts-rust/gts-macros/src/lib.rs`)\n+   - Attribute macro for explicit struct definitions with GTS IDs visible in code\n+   - Generates constants: `GTS_SCHEMA_ID`, `GTS_SCHEMA_JSON`, etc.\n+   - **This pattern will be adapted for error definitions**\n+\n+3. **`declare_errors!` macro** (`libs/modkit-errors-macro/src/lib.rs`) - **TO BE DEPRECATED**\n+   - Generates type-safe error enums from JSON catalogs\n+   - Problem: GTS IDs hidden in external JSON files, not visible to LLMs\n+   - Used by: `users_info` example, `modkit-odata`\n+\n+### Gaps Identified\n+\n+| Gap | Current State | Required State |\n+|-----|---------------|----------------|\n+| **Hidden GTS IDs** | JSON-based `declare_errors!` | Explicit `#[gts_error]` structs with visible GTS IDs |\n+| **Inconsistent definitions** | Some modules use inline errors | All modules use `#[gts_error]` structs |\n+| **No types registry** | Errors not registered | All errors registered as GTS types |\n+| **Missing metadata** | No structured context | Struct fields → `metadata` map |\n+| **Partial trace IDs** | Only in `IntoResponse` | Mandatory in all error responses |\n+| **No error categories** | Flat error codes | System/Operational/Client categories |\n+| **No error stack** | Single error | Upstream error chain propagation |\n+\n+### Current Module Migration Status\n+\n+| Module | Location | Status | Issues |\n+|--------|----------|--------|--------|\n+| **file_parser** | `modules/file_parser/` | 🔴 Not migrated | No GTS IDs, inline `Problem::new()` |\n+| **types-registry** | `modules/system/types-registry/` | 🟡 Partial | Has codes but not GTS format (e.g., `TYPES_REGISTRY_NOT_FOUND`) |\n+| **nodes_registry** | `modules/system/nodes_registry/` | 🔴 Not migrated | Non-GTS codes (e.g., `NODES_NOT_FOUND`) |\n+| **api_gateway** | `modules/system/api_gateway/` | 🔴 Not migrated | No Problem struct, simple error codes |\n+| **tenant_resolver** | `modules/system/tenant_resolver/` | 🔴 Not migrated | No GTS IDs |\n+| **simple-user-settings** | `modules/simple-user-settings/` | 🟡 Partial | Uses `declare_errors!` with old chain format |\n+| **modkit-auth** | `libs/modkit-auth/` | 🔴 Not migrated | No GTS IDs, custom `IntoResponse` |\n+| **modkit-odata** | `libs/modkit-odata/` | 🟡 Partial | Uses `declare_errors!` with old chain format |\n+| **users_info** (example) | `examples/modkit/users_info/` | 🟡 Partial | Uses `declare_errors!` with old chain format |\n+\n+#### Legend\n+- 🟢 **Migrated** - Uses `#[gts_error]` structs with proper base types\n+- 🟡 **Partial** - Has GTS IDs but uses deprecated `declare_errors!` or old format\n+- 🔴 **Not migrated** - No GTS IDs or non-GTS format codes\n+\n+#### GTS ID Format Note\n+\n+**Old chain format** (used by `declare_errors!`):\n+```\n+gts.hx.core.errors.err.v1~hx.module.error_name.v1\n+```\n+\n+**New format** (with `base` field):\n+```\n+gts.hx.module.namespace.error_name.v1~\n+```\n+The `base` field in `#[gts_error]` replaces the chain suffix, making inheritance explicit in code.\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Requirements\n+\n+### R1: Error Schema Requirements\n+\n+Every error returned from REST API MUST conform to the unified schema:\n+\n+```rust\n+pub struct Problem {\n+    // =========================================================================\n+    // REQUIRED FIELDS - Core error identification\n+    // =========================================================================\n+    \n+    /// URI reference identifying the problem type (GTS-based)\n+    /// Example: \"https://docs.hyperspot.com/errors/types_registry_entity_not_found_v1\"\n+    #[serde(rename = \"type\")]\n+    pub type_url: String,\n+    \n+    /// Human-readable summary of the problem type (static per error type)\n+    pub title: String,\n+    \n+    /// GTS error code (machine-readable identifier)\n+    pub code: String,\n+    \n+    /// Trace ID for request correlation\n+    pub trace_id: String,\n+    \n+    // =========================================================================\n+    // CONTEXTUAL FIELDS - Optional based on error context\n+    // =========================================================================\n+    \n+    /// HTTP status code. Optional because:\n+    /// - gRPC errors use different status codes\n+    /// - Internal/domain errors may not have HTTP context\n+    /// - Event-driven systems have no request/response\n+    /// When serializing for HTTP response, this is populated from error definition.\n+    #[serde(skip_serializing_if = \"Option::is_none\")]\n+    pub status: Option<u16>,\n+    \n+    /// Human-readable explanation specific to this occurrence.\n+    /// Optional - title may be sufficient for simple errors.\n+    #[serde(skip_serializing_if = \"Option::is_none\")]\n+    pub detail: Option<String>,\n+    \n+    /// Error category for client handling.\n+    /// Optional - can be inferred from base type hierarchy.\n+    #[serde(skip_serializing_if = \"Option::is_none\")]\n+    pub category: Option<ErrorCategory>,\n+    \n+    /// Whether client can retry this request.\n+    /// Optional - can be inferred from base type; not relevant for all contexts.\n+    #[serde(skip_serializing_if = \"Option::is_none\")]\n+    pub retryable: Option<bool>,\n+    \n+    /// URI identifying this specific occurrence (auto-populated from request path)\n+    #[serde(skip_serializing_if = \"Option::is_none\")]\n+    pub instance: Option<String>,\n+    \n+    /// Structured metadata (key-value context)\n+    #[serde(skip_serializing_if = \"Option::is_none\")]\n+    pub metadata: Option<HashMap<String, String>>,\n+    \n+    /// Validation errors for 4xx responses\n+    #[serde(skip_serializing_if = \"Option::is_none\")]\n+    pub errors: Option<Vec<ValidationViolation>>,\n+    \n+    /// Upstream error chain (when error_stack enabled)\n+    #[serde(skip_serializing_if = \"Option::is_none\")]\n+    pub upstream_errors: Option<Vec<UpstreamError>>,\n+}\n+\n+pub enum ErrorCategory {\n+    /// Platform-level execution errors (panics, OOM, internal bugs)\n+    System,\n+    /// Infrastructure/operational issues (DB unavailable, service down, rate limits)\n+    Operational,\n+    /// Client input/request errors (validation, not found, unauthorized)\n+    Client,\n+}\n+```\n+\n+#### Field Requirements Summary\n+\n+| Field | Required | Reason |\n+|-------|----------|--------|\n+| `type_url` | ✅ Yes | RFC 9457 requires problem type URI |\n+| `title` | ✅ Yes | Human-readable error name (static per type) |\n+| `code` | ✅ Yes | GTS identifier for machine processing |\n+| `trace_id` | ✅ Yes | Request correlation for debugging |\n+| `status` | ❌ No | Only relevant for HTTP; gRPC/events/domain errors don't need it |\n+| `detail` | ❌ No | Instance-specific message; title may suffice |\n+| `category` | ❌ No | Inherited from base type hierarchy |\n+| `retryable` | ❌ No | Inherited from base type; not relevant for all contexts |\n+| `instance` | ❌ No | Auto-populated from request path when applicable |\n+| `metadata` | ❌ No | Additional context key-value pairs |\n+| `errors` | ❌ No | Validation violations for 4xx errors |\n+| `upstream_errors` | ❌ No | Error chain from upstream services |\n+\n+**Note:** When converting to HTTP response, `status` is populated from the error definition. When the error is used in non-HTTP contexts (gRPC, domain logic, events), `status` remains `None`.\n+\n+### R2: GTS Identifier and Base Type Requirements\n+\n+Every error MUST have a valid GTS identifier and specify its base type using the `base` field.\n+\n+#### GTS ID Format\n+\n+```\n+gts.<vendor>.<package>.<namespace>.<type>.v<version>~\n+```\n+\n+**Examples:**\n+- `gts.hx.types_registry.entity.not_found.v1~` - Types registry not found error\n+- `gts.hx.file_parser.validation.invalid_format.v1~` - File parser validation error\n+- `gts.hx.system.runtime.timeout.v1~` - System timeout error\n+\n+#### Base Type Chaining\n+\n+Errors form an inheritance chain using the `base` field. The `base` field references another error struct type (not a string literal), similar to how `struct_to_gts_schema` works.\n+\n+The root base error type is:\n+\n+```rust\n+/// Root error type for all GTS errors.\n+#[gts_error(\n+    gts_id = \"gts.hx.core.errors.err.v1~\",\n+    base = true,  // Marks this as a root base type (no parent)\n+    title = \"Error\",\n+    // Optional attributes with defaults for inheritance:\n+    status = 500,        // Default HTTP status (optional, inherited by children)\n+    category = \"System\", // Default category (optional, inherited by children)\n+    retryable = false    // Default retryable (optional, inherited by children)\n+)]\n+pub struct BaseError;\n+```\n+\n+All module-specific errors MUST reference their base type as a struct (extending the appropriate logical/system error):\n+\n+```rust\n+use modkit_errors::system::logical::NotFoundError;\n+\n+/// Entity was not found in the types registry.\n+/// Note: status, category, retryable are inherited from NotFoundError if not specified.\n+#[gts_error(\n+    gts_id = \"gts.hx.types_registry.entity.not_found.v1~\",\n+    base = NotFoundError,  // Extends logical.not_found, not BaseError\n+    title = \"Entity Not Found\",\n+    // These are optional - inherited from base if omitted:\n+    // status = 404,      // Inherited from NotFoundError\n+    // category = \"Client\", // Inherited from NotFoundError  \n+    // retryable = false,   // Inherited from NotFoundError\n+)]\n+pub struct EntityNotFoundError {\n+    pub gts_id: String,\n+}\n+```\n+\n+#### Multi-Level Inheritance\n+\n+Errors can form deeper inheritance chains:\n+\n+```rust\n+/// Logical not found error (platform-level).\n+#[gts_error(\n+    gts_id = \"gts.hx.system.logical.not_found.v1~\",\n+    base = BaseError,  // Platform errors extend BaseError\n+    status = 404,\n+    title = \"Not Found\",\n+    category = \"Client\",\n+    retryable = false\n+)]\n+pub struct NotFoundError;\n+\n+/// Types registry entity not found (module-level).\n+#[gts_error(\n+    gts_id = \"gts.hx.types_registry.entity.not_found.v1~\",\n+    base = NotFoundError,  // Module errors extend logical errors\n+    status = 404,\n+    title = \"Entity Not Found\",\n+    category = \"Client\",\n+    retryable = false\n+)]\n+pub struct EntityNotFoundError {\n+    pub gts_id: String,\n+}\n+```\n+\n+#### Inheritance Hierarchy\n+\n+```\n+BaseError (gts.hx.core.errors.err.v1~)                              [base = true]\n+├── Transport Errors (hx.system.transport.*)                        [base = BaseError]\n+├── Runtime Errors (hx.system.runtime.*)                            [base = BaseError]\n+│   └── hx.types_registry.system.internal.v1~                       [base = runtime.internal]\n+├── HTTP Errors (hx.system.http.*)                                  [base = BaseError]\n+│   └── hx.auth.token_expired.v1~                                   [base = http.unauthorized]\n+├── gRPC Errors (hx.system.grpc.*)                                  [base = BaseError]\n+└── Logical Errors (hx.system.logical.*)                            [base = BaseError]\n+    ├── logical.not_found.v1~                                       [base = BaseError]\n+    │   ├── hx.types_registry.entity.not_found.v1~                  [base = logical.not_found]\n+    │   └── hx.db.entity.not_found.v1~                              [base = logical.not_found]\n+    ├── logical.already_exists.v1~                                  [base = BaseError]\n+    │   └── hx.types_registry.entity.already_exists.v1~             [base = logical.already_exists]\n+    └── logical.validation_failed.v1~                               [base = BaseError]\n+        └── hx.file_parser.validation.invalid_format.v1~            [base = logical.validation_failed]\n+```\n+\n+### R3: Trace ID Requirements\n+\n+- Every error response MUST include a non-empty `trace_id`\n+- Trace ID MUST be propagated from incoming request headers or generated\n+- Trace ID MUST be logged with the error for correlation\n+\n+### R4: Types Registry Integration\n+\n+- All error types MUST be registered in the types registry at startup\n+- Error schema MUST extend base error type: `gts.hx.core.errors.err.v1`\n+- Registration MUST include: code, title, status, category, retryable flag\n+\n+### R5: Standardized System Error Types\n+\n+See [GTS System Errors Catalog](#gts-system-errors-catalog) for the complete list of all system errors.\n+\n+### R6: Error Stack Propagation\n+\n+When a function calls another service/function that returns an error:\n+- The error SHOULD be wrapped with context\n+- `upstream_errors` array SHOULD contain the chain of errors\n+- Each upstream error includes: `code`, `title`, `detail`, `source`\n+- Propagation controlled by `error_stack` configuration flag\n+\n+---\n+\n+## GTS Error Code Format\n+\n+### Structure\n+\n+```\n+gts.<vendor>.<package>.<namespace>.<type>.<version>~<chain>\n+```\n+\n+### Components\n+\n+| Component | Description | Example |\n+|-----------|-------------|---------|\n+| `gts` | Global Type System prefix | `gts` |\n+| `vendor` | Organization identifier | `hx` (Hyperspot) |\n+| `package` | Module/service name | `types_registry`, `file_parser` |\n+| `namespace` | Error category | `entity`, `validation`, `runtime` |\n+| `type` | Specific error type | `not_found`, `invalid_format` |\n+| `version` | Schema version | `v1`, `v1.0` |\n+| `~chain` | Base type chain | `~hx.core.errors.err.v1` |\n+\n+### Validation Rules\n+\n+1. MUST start with `gts.`\n+2. All segments MUST be lowercase alphanumeric or underscore\n+3. No empty segments allowed\n+4. Final segment MUST be version format (`vN` or `vN.M`)\n+5. MUST chain from base error type\n+\n+### Short Name Derivation\n+\n+Short accessor names derived from final GTX segment:\n+```\n+gts.hx.core.errors.err.v1~hx.types_registry.entity.not_found.v1\n+                         └─────────────────────────────────────┘\n+                                          ↓\n+                         types_registry_entity_not_found_v1()\n+```\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Types Registry Integration\n+\n+### Error Type Schema\n+\n+```json\n+{\n+  \"gts_id\": \"gts.hx.types_registry.entity.not_found.v1~\",\n+  \"kind\": \"error\",\n+  \"schema\": {\n+    \"type\": \"object\",\n+    \"extends\": \"gts.hx.system.logical.not_found.v1~\",\n+    \"properties\": {\n+      \"status\": { \"const\": 404 },\n+      \"title\": { \"const\": \"Entity Not Found\" },\n+      \"category\": { \"const\": \"Client\" },\n+      \"retryable\": { \"const\": false }\n+    }\n+  },\n+  \"metadata\": {\n+    \"module\": \"types-registry\",\n+    \"documentation_url\": \"https://docs.hyperspot.com/errors/types_registry_entity_not_found_v1\"\n+  }\n+}\n+```\n+\n+### Registration Flow\n+\n+1. Module defines errors as explicit structs with `#[gts_error]` attribute in `src/errors.rs`\n+2. Each struct generates `ERROR_DEF` constant with GTS metadata\n+3. Module implements `all_error_definitions()` function returning all error definitions\n+4. At module startup (`on_ready`), errors are registered with types registry:\n+   ```rust\n+   impl Module for MyModule {\n+       async fn on_ready(&self, ctx: &ModuleContext) -> Result<()> {\n+           // Register all error types with types registry\n+           let errors = crate::errors::all_error_definitions();\n+           ctx.types_registry().register_errors(errors).await?;\n+           Ok(())\n+       }\n+   }\n+   ```\n+5. Types registry validates GTS format and schema compliance\n+6. Errors become discoverable via types registry API\n+\n+### API for Error Discovery\n+\n+```http\n+GET /api/types-registry/v1/types?kind=error&module=types-registry\n+\n+Response:\n+{\n+  \"items\": [\n+    {\n+      \"gts_id\": \"gts.hx.core.errors.err.v1~hx.types_registry.entity.not_found.v1\",\n+      \"status\": 404,\n+      \"title\": \"Entity Not Found\",\n+      \"category\": \"Client\",\n+      \"retryable\": false,\n+      \"documentation_url\": \"...\"\n+    }\n+  ]\n+}\n+```\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Implementation Rules\n+\n+### Rule 1: All Errors MUST Use Explicit Struct Definitions with `#[gts_error]`\n+\n+Errors are defined as explicit structs with the `#[gts_error]` attribute macro. This approach:\n+- Makes GTS IDs visible directly in code (better for LLM code generation)\n+- Provides compile-time validation\n+- Generates `Problem` conversion automatically\n+- Enables types registry integration\n+\n+```rust\n+// ✅ CORRECT - Explicit struct definition with visible GTS ID and base type reference\n+use modkit_errors::gts_error;\n+\n+// First, import the appropriate base error types from system errors\n+use modkit_errors::system::logical::{NotFoundError, AlreadyExistsError, ValidationFailedError};\n+\n+/// Entity was not found in the types registry.\n+#[gts_error(\n+    gts_id = \"gts.hx.types_registry.entity.not_found.v1~\",\n+    base = NotFoundError,  // Extends logical.not_found, not BaseError\n+    status = 404,\n+    title = \"Entity Not Found\",\n+    category = \"Client\",\n+    retryable = false\n+)]\n+pub struct EntityNotFoundError {\n+    /// The GTS ID that was not found\n+    pub gts_id: String,\n+}\n+\n+/// Entity already exists in the registry.\n+#[gts_error(\n+    gts_id = \"gts.hx.types_registry.entity.already_exists.v1~\",\n+    base = AlreadyExistsError,  // Extends logical.already_exists\n+    status = 409,\n+    title = \"Entity Already Exists\",\n+    category = \"Client\",\n+    retryable = false\n+)]\n+pub struct EntityAlreadyExistsError {\n+    /// The GTS ID that already exists\n+    pub gts_id: String,\n+}\n+\n+/// Invalid GTS ID format.\n+#[gts_error(\n+    gts_id = \"gts.hx.types_registry.validation.invalid_gts_id.v1~\",\n+    base = ValidationFailedError,  // Extends logical.validation_failed\n+    status = 400,\n+    title = \"Invalid GTS ID\",\n+    category = \"Client\",\n+    retryable = false\n+)]\n+pub struct InvalidGtsIdError {\n+    /// Description of the validation error\n+    pub message: String,\n+}\n+\n+// ❌ WRONG - Inline error definitions without GTS ID\n+impl From<DomainError> for Problem {\n+    fn from(e: DomainError) -> Self {\n+        Problem::new(StatusCode::NOT_FOUND, \"Not Found\", \"...\")\n+            .with_code(\"SOME_CODE\") // Not GTS format!\n+    }\n+}\n+\n+// ❌ WRONG - JSON-based declaration (GTS ID hidden in external file)\n+declare_errors! {\n+    path = \"gts/errors.json\",\n+    namespace = \"errors\",\n+    vis = \"pub\"\n+}\n+```\n+\n+### Rule 2: Error Struct Field Conventions\n+\n+Error structs contain context fields that become `metadata` in the Problem response:\n+\n+```rust\n+use modkit_errors::system::logical::ValidationFailedError as LogicalValidationFailed;\n+\n+/// Request validation failed (module-specific).\n+#[gts_error(\n+    gts_id = \"gts.hx.types_registry.validation.failed.v1~\",\n+    base = LogicalValidationFailed,  // Extends logical.validation_failed\n+    status = 422,\n+    title = \"Validation Failed\",\n+    category = \"Client\",\n+    retryable = false\n+)]\n+pub struct ValidationFailedError {\n+    /// Human-readable error message\n+    pub message: String,\n+    /// Field that failed validation (optional)\n+    #[gts_error(skip_metadata)]  // Don't include in metadata\n+    pub violations: Vec<ValidationViolation>,\n+}\n+```\n+\n+### Rule 3: Error Mapping Pattern\n+\n+```rust\n+use crate::errors::{EntityNotFoundError, EntityAlreadyExistsError, InvalidGtsIdError};\n+\n+pub fn domain_error_to_problem(e: &DomainError) -> Problem {\n+    match e {\n+        DomainError::NotFound { id } => {\n+            // into_problem() auto-populates trace_id from current tracing span\n+            EntityNotFoundError { gts_id: id.clone() }\n+                .into_problem()\n+                .with_detail(format!(\"Entity with GTS ID '{}' was not found\", id))","path":"intended_design/UNIFIED_ERROR_SYSTEM.md","commit_id":"5bdb0f43b25858af78999718f7247813802b9634","original_commit_id":"5bdb0f43b25858af78999718f7247813802b9634","user":{"login":"MikeFalcon77","id":3686170,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM2ODYxNzA=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3686170?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/MikeFalcon77","html_url":"https://github.com/MikeFalcon77","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MikeFalcon77/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MikeFalcon77/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MikeFalcon77/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MikeFalcon77/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MikeFalcon77/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MikeFalcon77/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MikeFalcon77/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MikeFalcon77/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MikeFalcon77/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Please ensure detail does not leak internal data (DB errors, upstream raw errors, secrets). Consider mapping internal causes to sanitized messages, while logging full context server-side.","created_at":"2026-01-28T11:57:00Z","updated_at":"2026-01-28T12:02:23Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/290#discussion_r2736301365","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/290","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2736301365"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/290#discussion_r2736301365"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/290"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2736301365/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":null,"original_line":608,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"MEMBER","original_position":608,"position":1,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2736320525","pull_request_review_id":3715718572,"id":2736320525,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs6jGPAN","diff_hunk":"","path":"docs/GTS_ERRORS.md","commit_id":"5bdb0f43b25858af78999718f7247813802b9634","original_commit_id":"5bdb0f43b25858af78999718f7247813802b9634","user":{"login":"MikeFalcon77","id":3686170,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM2ODYxNzA=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3686170?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/MikeFalcon77","html_url":"https://github.com/MikeFalcon77","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MikeFalcon77/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MikeFalcon77/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MikeFalcon77/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MikeFalcon77/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MikeFalcon77/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MikeFalcon77/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MikeFalcon77/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MikeFalcon77/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MikeFalcon77/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"General thoughts about error versioning and GTS:\n\n**Concern: error definitions change frequently, so treating them like versioned “registry contracts” will create churn and operational coupling.**  \nIf errors are registered in types-registry as `kind=error`, we need a clear policy for what happens when an error is modified (title/status/semantics) and how re-registration works. Requiring manual re-registration or strict compatibility/versioning for every change is not realistic and will slow down iteration.\n\n**Options:**\n1) **Best-effort informational registry (recommended MVP):**  \n  Register only a stable set of *public* error codes. Registration is an **idempotent upsert by `id/code`** on service startup (or periodic background retry). Changes to metadata (`title`, docs, extra fields) simply overwrite the registry entry. No strict compatibility rules enforced by the registry.\n\n2) **Version only on breaking semantic changes:**  \n    Keep `code` stable for the same meaning; introduce a new `code` only when semantics/status handling changes in a way that affects clients. Do **not** bump versions for minor wording/metadata changes.\n\n3) **Do not register errors at all (or keep it optional):**  \n    If we can’t define a stable public error surface, make error registration opt-in/disabled by default and avoid implying that registry is the source of truth for runtime behavior.\n\n **Hard requirement regardless of option:** runtime error generation must not depend on types-registry availability; registry registration must be non-blocking and should never prevent service startup","created_at":"2026-01-28T12:02:10Z","updated_at":"2026-01-28T12:02:23Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/290#discussion_r2736320525","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/290","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2736320525"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/290#discussion_r2736320525"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/290"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2736320525/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":1,"original_line":1,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"MEMBER","original_position":1,"position":1,"subject_type":"file"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2747820053","pull_request_review_id":3710446544,"id":2747820053,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs6jyGgV","diff_hunk":"","path":"docs/GTS_ERRORS.md","commit_id":"5bdb0f43b25858af78999718f7247813802b9634","original_commit_id":"5bdb0f43b25858af78999718f7247813802b9634","user":{"login":"Artifizer","id":192502778,"node_id":"U_kgDOC3lb-g","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/192502778?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer","html_url":"https://github.com/Artifizer","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"@MikeFalcon77 \n\nI think that:\n1. Error definitions will unlikely change much as they reflect objective problems and there are no that many attributes\n2. we can safely ignore minor version bump for now, until the code becomes production ready and we see errors are part of contracts. There could be external test/CI system to control only those errors that became \"contracts\"","created_at":"2026-01-30T20:05:39Z","updated_at":"2026-01-30T21:23:02Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/290#discussion_r2747820053","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/290","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2747820053"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/290#discussion_r2747820053"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/290"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2747820053/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":1,"original_line":1,"side":"RIGHT","in_reply_to_id":2736320525,"author_association":"MEMBER","original_position":1,"position":1,"subject_type":"file"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2747829205","pull_request_review_id":3710446544,"id":2747829205,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs6jyIvV","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,417 @@\n+# GTS Error System Documentation\n+\n+This document describes how errors are defined, structured, transformed, and used in the Hyperspot/gts-rust project.\n+\n+## Overview\n+\n+The error system follows **RFC 9457 Problem Details for HTTP APIs** and uses a **GTS (Global Type System)** format for error codes. The system provides:\n+\n+- **Compile-time validated** error catalogs via JSON files\n+- **Type-safe** error code enums generated by proc-macros\n+- **Layered error transformation** from domain → API → HTTP response\n+- **Consistent error format** across all modules\n+\n+## Architecture\n+\n+```\n+┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n+│                           Error Flow                                     │\n+├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n+│                                                                          │\n+│  gts/errors.json  ──────►  declare_errors! macro  ──────►  ErrorCode    │\n+│  (Source of Truth)         (Compile-time)                  (Enum)       │\n+│                                                                          │\n+│  DomainError  ──────►  ErrorCode::xxx().with_context()  ──────►  Problem│\n+│  (Business Logic)      (Mapping Layer)                        (RFC 9457)│\n+│                                                                          │\n+│  Problem  ──────►  IntoResponse (Axum)  ──────►  HTTP Response          │\n+│  (Data)            (Framework Integration)       (JSON + Headers)       │\n+│                                                                          │\n+└─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘\n+```\n+\n+## Components\n+\n+### 1. Error Catalog JSON (`gts/errors.json`)\n+\n+The source of truth for error definitions. Located in each module's `gts/` directory.\n+\n+**File Location Pattern:** `<module>/gts/errors.json`\n+\n+**Schema:**\n+```json\n+[\n+  {\n+    \"status\": 404,\n+    \"title\": \"User Not Found\",\n+    \"code\": \"gts.hx.core.errors.err.v1~hx.example1.user.not_found.v1\",\n+    \"type\": \"https://errors.example.com/...\",  // optional\n+    \"alias\": \"user_not_found\"                   // optional\n+  }\n+]\n+```\n+\n+**Fields:**\n+| Field | Required | Description |\n+|-------|----------|-------------|\n+| `status` | Yes | HTTP status code (100-599) |\n+| `title` | Yes | Human-readable error title |\n+| `code` | Yes | GTS-formatted error code |\n+| `type` | No | URI for error documentation |\n+| `alias` | No | Short name override for generated accessor |\n+\n+### 2. GTS Code Format\n+\n+GTS codes follow a strict format for global type identification:\n+\n+```\n+gts.vendor.package.namespace.type.version~chain1~chain2~...~instanceGTX\n+```\n+\n+**Structure:**\n+- **Prefix:** Always starts with `gts.`","path":"docs/GTS_ERRORS.md","commit_id":"5bdb0f43b25858af78999718f7247813802b9634","original_commit_id":"5bdb0f43b25858af78999718f7247813802b9634","user":{"login":"Artifizer","id":192502778,"node_id":"U_kgDOC3lb-g","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/192502778?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer","html_url":"https://github.com/Artifizer","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"I think we can omit it and just refer to GTS spec","created_at":"2026-01-30T20:08:52Z","updated_at":"2026-01-30T21:23:01Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/290#discussion_r2747829205","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/290","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2747829205"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/290#discussion_r2747829205"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/290"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2747829205/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":null,"original_line":72,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"MEMBER","original_position":72,"position":1,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2747831463","pull_request_review_id":3710446544,"id":2747831463,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs6jyJSn","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,417 @@\n+# GTS Error System Documentation\n+\n+This document describes how errors are defined, structured, transformed, and used in the Hyperspot/gts-rust project.\n+\n+## Overview\n+\n+The error system follows **RFC 9457 Problem Details for HTTP APIs** and uses a **GTS (Global Type System)** format for error codes. The system provides:\n+\n+- **Compile-time validated** error catalogs via JSON files\n+- **Type-safe** error code enums generated by proc-macros\n+- **Layered error transformation** from domain → API → HTTP response\n+- **Consistent error format** across all modules\n+\n+## Architecture\n+\n+```\n+┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n+│                           Error Flow                                     │\n+├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n+│                                                                          │\n+│  gts/errors.json  ──────►  declare_errors! macro  ──────►  ErrorCode    │\n+│  (Source of Truth)         (Compile-time)                  (Enum)       │\n+│                                                                          │\n+│  DomainError  ──────►  ErrorCode::xxx().with_context()  ──────►  Problem│\n+│  (Business Logic)      (Mapping Layer)                        (RFC 9457)│\n+│                                                                          │\n+│  Problem  ──────►  IntoResponse (Axum)  ──────►  HTTP Response          │\n+│  (Data)            (Framework Integration)       (JSON + Headers)       │\n+│                                                                          │\n+└─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘\n+```\n+\n+## Components\n+\n+### 1. Error Catalog JSON (`gts/errors.json`)\n+\n+The source of truth for error definitions. Located in each module's `gts/` directory.\n+\n+**File Location Pattern:** `<module>/gts/errors.json`\n+\n+**Schema:**\n+```json\n+[\n+  {\n+    \"status\": 404,\n+    \"title\": \"User Not Found\",\n+    \"code\": \"gts.hx.core.errors.err.v1~hx.example1.user.not_found.v1\",\n+    \"type\": \"https://errors.example.com/...\",  // optional\n+    \"alias\": \"user_not_found\"                   // optional\n+  }\n+]\n+```\n+\n+**Fields:**\n+| Field | Required | Description |\n+|-------|----------|-------------|\n+| `status` | Yes | HTTP status code (100-599) |\n+| `title` | Yes | Human-readable error title |\n+| `code` | Yes | GTS-formatted error code |\n+| `type` | No | URI for error documentation |\n+| `alias` | No | Short name override for generated accessor |\n+\n+### 2. GTS Code Format\n+\n+GTS codes follow a strict format for global type identification:\n+\n+```\n+gts.vendor.package.namespace.type.version~chain1~chain2~...~instanceGTX\n+```\n+\n+**Structure:**\n+- **Prefix:** Always starts with `gts.`\n+- **Chain separator:** `~` separates GTX segments\n+- **Segment separator:** `.` separates parts within a GTX\n+- **Final GTX:** Must have at least 5 segments: `vendor.package.namespace.type.version`","path":"docs/GTS_ERRORS.md","commit_id":"5bdb0f43b25858af78999718f7247813802b9634","original_commit_id":"5bdb0f43b25858af78999718f7247813802b9634","user":{"login":"Artifizer","id":192502778,"node_id":"U_kgDOC3lb-g","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/192502778?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer","html_url":"https://github.com/Artifizer","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"@devjow , agree, it's called `segment` now, not `GTX`","created_at":"2026-01-30T20:09:45Z","updated_at":"2026-01-30T21:23:01Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/290#discussion_r2747831463","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/290","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2747831463"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/290#discussion_r2747831463"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/290"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2747831463/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":null,"original_line":75,"side":"RIGHT","in_reply_to_id":2731520996,"author_association":"MEMBER","original_position":75,"position":1,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2747838392","pull_request_review_id":3710446544,"id":2747838392,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs6jyK-4","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,417 @@\n+# GTS Error System Documentation\n+\n+This document describes how errors are defined, structured, transformed, and used in the Hyperspot/gts-rust project.\n+\n+## Overview\n+\n+The error system follows **RFC 9457 Problem Details for HTTP APIs** and uses a **GTS (Global Type System)** format for error codes. The system provides:\n+\n+- **Compile-time validated** error catalogs via JSON files\n+- **Type-safe** error code enums generated by proc-macros\n+- **Layered error transformation** from domain → API → HTTP response\n+- **Consistent error format** across all modules\n+\n+## Architecture\n+\n+```\n+┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n+│                           Error Flow                                     │\n+├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n+│                                                                          │\n+│  gts/errors.json  ──────►  declare_errors! macro  ──────►  ErrorCode    │\n+│  (Source of Truth)         (Compile-time)                  (Enum)       │\n+│                                                                          │\n+│  DomainError  ──────►  ErrorCode::xxx().with_context()  ──────►  Problem│\n+│  (Business Logic)      (Mapping Layer)                        (RFC 9457)│\n+│                                                                          │\n+│  Problem  ──────►  IntoResponse (Axum)  ──────►  HTTP Response          │\n+│  (Data)            (Framework Integration)       (JSON + Headers)       │\n+│                                                                          │\n+└─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘\n+```\n+\n+## Components\n+\n+### 1. Error Catalog JSON (`gts/errors.json`)\n+\n+The source of truth for error definitions. Located in each module's `gts/` directory.\n+\n+**File Location Pattern:** `<module>/gts/errors.json`\n+\n+**Schema:**\n+```json\n+[\n+  {\n+    \"status\": 404,\n+    \"title\": \"User Not Found\",\n+    \"code\": \"gts.hx.core.errors.err.v1~hx.example1.user.not_found.v1\",\n+    \"type\": \"https://errors.example.com/...\",  // optional\n+    \"alias\": \"user_not_found\"                   // optional\n+  }\n+]\n+```\n+\n+**Fields:**\n+| Field | Required | Description |\n+|-------|----------|-------------|\n+| `status` | Yes | HTTP status code (100-599) |\n+| `title` | Yes | Human-readable error title |\n+| `code` | Yes | GTS-formatted error code |\n+| `type` | No | URI for error documentation |\n+| `alias` | No | Short name override for generated accessor |\n+\n+### 2. GTS Code Format\n+\n+GTS codes follow a strict format for global type identification:\n+\n+```\n+gts.vendor.package.namespace.type.version~chain1~chain2~...~instanceGTX\n+```\n+\n+**Structure:**\n+- **Prefix:** Always starts with `gts.`\n+- **Chain separator:** `~` separates GTX segments\n+- **Segment separator:** `.` separates parts within a GTX\n+- **Final GTX:** Must have at least 5 segments: `vendor.package.namespace.type.version`\n+- **Version:** Must end with `vN` or `vN.M` format\n+\n+**Example Breakdown:**\n+```\n+gts.hx.core.errors.err.v1~hx.example1.user.not_found.v1\n+│   │  │    │      │   │  │  │        │    │         │\n+│   │  │    │      │   │  │  │        │    │         └─ version\n+│   │  │    │      │   │  │  │        │    └─ type (not_found)\n+│   │  │    │      │   │  │  │        └─ namespace (user)\n+│   │  │    │      │   │  │  └─ package (example1)\n+│   │  │    │      │   │  └─ vendor (hx)\n+│   │  │    │      │   └─ version\n+│   │  │    │      └─ type (err)\n+│   │  │    └─ namespace (errors)\n+│   │  └─ package (core)\n+│   └─ vendor (hx)\n+└─ prefix\n+```\n+\n+**Validation Rules:**\n+1. Must start with `gts.`\n+2. All segments must be lowercase alphanumeric or underscore\n+3. No empty segments allowed\n+4. Final GTX must have ≥5 segments after vendor\n+5. Must end with valid version format (`v1`, `v1.2`, etc.)\n+\n+### 3. Proc-Macro: `declare_errors!`\n+\n+Generates type-safe error code enums from JSON at compile time.\n+\n+**Location:** `libs/modkit-errors-macro/src/lib.rs`\n+\n+**Usage:**\n+```rust\n+use modkit_errors_macro::declare_errors;\n+\n+declare_errors! {\n+    path = \"gts/errors.json\",\n+    namespace = \"errors\",\n+    vis = \"pub\"\n+}\n+```\n+\n+**Parameters:**\n+| Parameter | Required | Description |\n+|-----------|----------|-------------|\n+| `path` | Yes | Path to JSON file relative to `CARGO_MANIFEST_DIR` |\n+| `namespace` | Yes | Module name for generated code |\n+| `vis` | No | Visibility (`\"pub\"` or private) |\n+\n+**Generated Code:**\n+```rust\n+// Enum with all error codes\n+#[derive(Debug, Clone, Copy, PartialEq, Eq, Hash)]\n+pub enum ErrorCode {\n+    gts_hx_core_errors_err_v1_hx_example1_user_not_found_v1,\n+    // ...\n+}\n+\n+impl ErrorCode {\n+    // Get HTTP status\n+    pub const fn status(&self) -> u16 { ... }\n+    \n+    // Get full error definition\n+    pub const fn def(&self) -> ErrDef { ... }\n+    \n+    // Convert to Problem with detail\n+    pub fn as_problem(&self, detail: impl Into<String>) -> Problem { ... }\n+    \n+    // Create Problem with context (instance + trace_id)\n+    pub fn with_context(\n+        &self,\n+        detail: impl Into<String>,\n+        instance: &str,\n+        trace_id: Option<String>,\n+    ) -> Problem { ... }\n+    \n+    // Short accessor (derived from GTS or alias)\n+    pub const fn example1_user_not_found_v1() -> Self { ... }\n+}\n+\n+// Compile-time validated macro\n+macro_rules! problem_from_catalog { ... }\n+macro_rules! response_from_catalog { ... }\n+```\n+\n+### 4. Core Types\n+\n+#### `ErrDef` (Error Definition)\n+**Location:** `libs/modkit-errors/src/catalog.rs`\n+\n+```rust\n+pub struct ErrDef {\n+    pub status: u16,\n+    pub title: &'static str,\n+    pub code: &'static str,\n+    pub type_url: &'static str,\n+}\n+\n+impl ErrDef {\n+    pub fn as_problem(&self, detail: impl Into<String>) -> Problem { ... }\n+}\n+```\n+\n+#### `Problem` (RFC 9457)\n+**Location:** `libs/modkit-errors/src/problem.rs`\n+\n+```rust\n+pub struct Problem {\n+    pub type_url: String,      // URI reference for problem type\n+    pub title: String,         // Human-readable summary\n+    pub status: StatusCode,    // HTTP status code","path":"docs/GTS_ERRORS.md","commit_id":"5bdb0f43b25858af78999718f7247813802b9634","original_commit_id":"5bdb0f43b25858af78999718f7247813802b9634","user":{"login":"Artifizer","id":192502778,"node_id":"U_kgDOC3lb-g","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/192502778?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer","html_url":"https://github.com/Artifizer","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"could it be `HttpStatusCode` btw? ","created_at":"2026-01-30T20:12:15Z","updated_at":"2026-01-30T21:23:01Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/290#discussion_r2747838392","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/290","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2747838392"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/290#discussion_r2747838392"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/290"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2747838392/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":null,"original_line":187,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"MEMBER","original_position":187,"position":1,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2747848178","pull_request_review_id":3710446544,"id":2747848178,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs6jyNXy","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,417 @@\n+# GTS Error System Documentation\n+\n+This document describes how errors are defined, structured, transformed, and used in the Hyperspot/gts-rust project.\n+\n+## Overview\n+\n+The error system follows **RFC 9457 Problem Details for HTTP APIs** and uses a **GTS (Global Type System)** format for error codes. The system provides:\n+\n+- **Compile-time validated** error catalogs via JSON files\n+- **Type-safe** error code enums generated by proc-macros\n+- **Layered error transformation** from domain → API → HTTP response\n+- **Consistent error format** across all modules\n+\n+## Architecture\n+\n+```\n+┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n+│                           Error Flow                                     │\n+├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n+│                                                                          │\n+│  gts/errors.json  ──────►  declare_errors! macro  ──────►  ErrorCode    │\n+│  (Source of Truth)         (Compile-time)                  (Enum)       │\n+│                                                                          │\n+│  DomainError  ──────►  ErrorCode::xxx().with_context()  ──────►  Problem│\n+│  (Business Logic)      (Mapping Layer)                        (RFC 9457)│\n+│                                                                          │\n+│  Problem  ──────►  IntoResponse (Axum)  ──────►  HTTP Response          │\n+│  (Data)            (Framework Integration)       (JSON + Headers)       │\n+│                                                                          │\n+└─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘\n+```\n+\n+## Components\n+\n+### 1. Error Catalog JSON (`gts/errors.json`)\n+\n+The source of truth for error definitions. Located in each module's `gts/` directory.\n+\n+**File Location Pattern:** `<module>/gts/errors.json`\n+\n+**Schema:**\n+```json\n+[\n+  {\n+    \"status\": 404,\n+    \"title\": \"User Not Found\",\n+    \"code\": \"gts.hx.core.errors.err.v1~hx.example1.user.not_found.v1\",\n+    \"type\": \"https://errors.example.com/...\",  // optional\n+    \"alias\": \"user_not_found\"                   // optional\n+  }\n+]\n+```\n+\n+**Fields:**\n+| Field | Required | Description |\n+|-------|----------|-------------|\n+| `status` | Yes | HTTP status code (100-599) |\n+| `title` | Yes | Human-readable error title |\n+| `code` | Yes | GTS-formatted error code |\n+| `type` | No | URI for error documentation |\n+| `alias` | No | Short name override for generated accessor |\n+\n+### 2. GTS Code Format\n+\n+GTS codes follow a strict format for global type identification:\n+\n+```\n+gts.vendor.package.namespace.type.version~chain1~chain2~...~instanceGTX\n+```\n+\n+**Structure:**\n+- **Prefix:** Always starts with `gts.`\n+- **Chain separator:** `~` separates GTX segments\n+- **Segment separator:** `.` separates parts within a GTX\n+- **Final GTX:** Must have at least 5 segments: `vendor.package.namespace.type.version`\n+- **Version:** Must end with `vN` or `vN.M` format\n+\n+**Example Breakdown:**\n+```\n+gts.hx.core.errors.err.v1~hx.example1.user.not_found.v1\n+│   │  │    │      │   │  │  │        │    │         │\n+│   │  │    │      │   │  │  │        │    │         └─ version\n+│   │  │    │      │   │  │  │        │    └─ type (not_found)\n+│   │  │    │      │   │  │  │        └─ namespace (user)\n+│   │  │    │      │   │  │  └─ package (example1)\n+│   │  │    │      │   │  └─ vendor (hx)\n+│   │  │    │      │   └─ version\n+│   │  │    │      └─ type (err)\n+│   │  │    └─ namespace (errors)\n+│   │  └─ package (core)\n+│   └─ vendor (hx)\n+└─ prefix\n+```\n+\n+**Validation Rules:**\n+1. Must start with `gts.`\n+2. All segments must be lowercase alphanumeric or underscore\n+3. No empty segments allowed\n+4. Final GTX must have ≥5 segments after vendor\n+5. Must end with valid version format (`v1`, `v1.2`, etc.)\n+\n+### 3. Proc-Macro: `declare_errors!`\n+\n+Generates type-safe error code enums from JSON at compile time.\n+\n+**Location:** `libs/modkit-errors-macro/src/lib.rs`\n+\n+**Usage:**\n+```rust\n+use modkit_errors_macro::declare_errors;\n+\n+declare_errors! {\n+    path = \"gts/errors.json\",\n+    namespace = \"errors\",\n+    vis = \"pub\"\n+}\n+```\n+\n+**Parameters:**\n+| Parameter | Required | Description |\n+|-----------|----------|-------------|\n+| `path` | Yes | Path to JSON file relative to `CARGO_MANIFEST_DIR` |\n+| `namespace` | Yes | Module name for generated code |\n+| `vis` | No | Visibility (`\"pub\"` or private) |\n+\n+**Generated Code:**\n+```rust\n+// Enum with all error codes\n+#[derive(Debug, Clone, Copy, PartialEq, Eq, Hash)]\n+pub enum ErrorCode {\n+    gts_hx_core_errors_err_v1_hx_example1_user_not_found_v1,\n+    // ...\n+}\n+\n+impl ErrorCode {\n+    // Get HTTP status\n+    pub const fn status(&self) -> u16 { ... }\n+    \n+    // Get full error definition\n+    pub const fn def(&self) -> ErrDef { ... }\n+    \n+    // Convert to Problem with detail\n+    pub fn as_problem(&self, detail: impl Into<String>) -> Problem { ... }\n+    \n+    // Create Problem with context (instance + trace_id)\n+    pub fn with_context(\n+        &self,\n+        detail: impl Into<String>,\n+        instance: &str,\n+        trace_id: Option<String>,\n+    ) -> Problem { ... }\n+    \n+    // Short accessor (derived from GTS or alias)\n+    pub const fn example1_user_not_found_v1() -> Self { ... }\n+}\n+\n+// Compile-time validated macro\n+macro_rules! problem_from_catalog { ... }\n+macro_rules! response_from_catalog { ... }\n+```\n+\n+### 4. Core Types\n+\n+#### `ErrDef` (Error Definition)\n+**Location:** `libs/modkit-errors/src/catalog.rs`\n+\n+```rust\n+pub struct ErrDef {\n+    pub status: u16,\n+    pub title: &'static str,\n+    pub code: &'static str,\n+    pub type_url: &'static str,\n+}\n+\n+impl ErrDef {\n+    pub fn as_problem(&self, detail: impl Into<String>) -> Problem { ... }\n+}\n+```\n+\n+#### `Problem` (RFC 9457)\n+**Location:** `libs/modkit-errors/src/problem.rs`\n+\n+```rust\n+pub struct Problem {\n+    pub type_url: String,      // URI reference for problem type\n+    pub title: String,         // Human-readable summary\n+    pub status: StatusCode,    // HTTP status code\n+    pub detail: String,        // Specific occurrence explanation\n+    pub instance: String,      // URI for this occurrence\n+    pub code: String,          // Machine-readable error code\n+    pub trace_id: Option<String>,\n+    pub errors: Option<Vec<ValidationViolation>>,\n+}\n+```\n+\n+**Builder Pattern:**\n+```rust\n+Problem::new(StatusCode::NOT_FOUND, \"Not Found\", \"User not found\")\n+    .with_code(\"gts.hx....\")\n+    .with_type(\"https://...\")\n+    .with_instance(\"/api/users/123\")\n+    .with_trace_id(\"req-456\")\n+    .with_errors(vec![...])\n+```\n+\n+## Error Flow by Layer\n+\n+### Layer 1: Domain Errors\n+\n+Domain errors represent business logic failures. They are internal and don't contain HTTP-specific information.\n+\n+**Location:** `<module>/src/domain/error.rs`\n+\n+```rust\n+#[derive(Error, Debug)]\n+pub enum DomainError {\n+    #[error(\"User not found: {id}\")]\n+    UserNotFound { id: Uuid },\n+    \n+    #[error(\"Email '{email}' already exists\")]\n+    EmailAlreadyExists { email: String },\n+    \n+    #[error(\"Database error: {message}\")]\n+    Database { message: String },\n+    // ...\n+}\n+```\n+\n+### Layer 2: SDK Errors (Public API)\n+\n+SDK errors are exposed to other modules via the client trait. They are simplified and safe to expose.\n+\n+**Location:** `<module>-sdk/src/errors.rs`\n+\n+```rust\n+#[derive(Error, Debug, Clone)]\n+pub enum UsersInfoError {\n+    #[error(\"Resource not found: {id}\")]\n+    NotFound { id: Uuid },\n+    \n+    #[error(\"Validation error: {message}\")]\n+    Validation { message: String },\n+    \n+    #[error(\"Internal error\")]\n+    Internal,\n+}\n+```\n+\n+### Layer 3: API Error Mapping\n+\n+The API layer maps domain errors to RFC 9457 Problems using the error catalog.\n+\n+**Location:** `<module>/src/api/rest/error.rs`\n+\n+```rust\n+use crate::errors::ErrorCode;\n+\n+pub fn domain_error_to_problem(e: &DomainError, instance: &str) -> Problem {\n+    let trace_id = tracing::Span::current()\n+        .id()\n+        .map(|id| id.into_u64().to_string());\n+\n+    match &e {\n+        DomainError::UserNotFound { id } => {\n+            ErrorCode::example1_user_not_found_v1().with_context(\n+                format!(\"User with id {id} was not found\"),\n+                instance,\n+                trace_id,\n+            )\n+        }\n+        DomainError::Database { .. } => {\n+            tracing::error!(error = ?e, \"Database error occurred\");\n+            ErrorCode::example1_user_internal_database_v1().with_context(\n+                \"An internal database error occurred\",\n+                instance,\n+                trace_id,\n+            )\n+        }\n+        // ...\n+    }\n+}\n+```\n+\n+### Layer 4: HTTP Response\n+\n+`Problem` implements `IntoResponse` for Axum, automatically:\n+- Setting the correct HTTP status code\n+- Setting `Content-Type: application/problem+json`\n+- Enriching with trace ID from current span if not set\n+\n+```rust\n+// In handler\n+async fn get_user(...) -> Result<Json<User>, Problem> {\n+    let user = service.get_user(id).await\n+        .map_err(|e| domain_error_to_problem(&e, &path))?;\n+    Ok(Json(user))\n+}\n+```\n+\n+## Creating a New Error Catalog\n+\n+### Step 1: Create `gts/errors.json`\n+\n+```json\n+[\n+  {\n+    \"status\": 404,\n+    \"title\": \"Resource Not Found\",\n+    \"code\": \"gts.hx.core.errors.err.v1~hx.mymodule.resource.not_found.v1\"\n+  },\n+  {\n+    \"status\": 422,\n+    \"title\": \"Validation Error\",\n+    \"code\": \"gts.hx.core.errors.err.v1~hx.mymodule.validation.invalid_input.v1\"\n+  }\n+]\n+```\n+\n+### Step 2: Create `src/errors.rs`\n+\n+```rust\n+use modkit_errors_macro::declare_errors;\n+\n+declare_errors! {\n+    path = \"gts/errors.json\",\n+    namespace = \"errors\",\n+    vis = \"pub\"\n+}\n+```\n+\n+### Step 3: Add to `Cargo.toml`\n+\n+```toml\n+[dependencies]\n+modkit-errors-macro = { path = \"../../libs/modkit-errors-macro\" }\n+modkit-errors = { path = \"../../libs/modkit-errors\" }\n+```\n+\n+### Step 4: Use in API Layer\n+\n+```rust\n+use crate::errors::ErrorCode;\n+\n+fn map_error(e: &MyDomainError, instance: &str) -> Problem {\n+    match e {\n+        MyDomainError::NotFound => {\n+            ErrorCode::mymodule_resource_not_found_v1()\n+                .with_context(\"Resource not found\", instance, None)\n+        }\n+        // ...\n+    }\n+}\n+```\n+\n+## Short Name Derivation\n+\n+Short accessor names are derived from the final GTX segment:\n+\n+```\n+gts.hx.core.errors.err.v1~hx.example1.user.not_found.v1\n+                         └─────────────────────────────┘","path":"docs/GTS_ERRORS.md","commit_id":"5bdb0f43b25858af78999718f7247813802b9634","original_commit_id":"5bdb0f43b25858af78999718f7247813802b9634","user":{"login":"Artifizer","id":192502778,"node_id":"U_kgDOC3lb-g","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/192502778?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer","html_url":"https://github.com/Artifizer","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"hx -> x","created_at":"2026-01-30T20:15:00Z","updated_at":"2026-01-30T21:23:01Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/290#discussion_r2747848178","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/290","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2747848178"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/290#discussion_r2747848178"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/290"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2747848178/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":null,"original_line":361,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"MEMBER","original_position":361,"position":1,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2747848678","pull_request_review_id":3710446544,"id":2747848678,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs6jyNfm","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,417 @@\n+# GTS Error System Documentation\n+\n+This document describes how errors are defined, structured, transformed, and used in the Hyperspot/gts-rust project.\n+\n+## Overview\n+\n+The error system follows **RFC 9457 Problem Details for HTTP APIs** and uses a **GTS (Global Type System)** format for error codes. The system provides:\n+\n+- **Compile-time validated** error catalogs via JSON files\n+- **Type-safe** error code enums generated by proc-macros\n+- **Layered error transformation** from domain → API → HTTP response\n+- **Consistent error format** across all modules\n+\n+## Architecture\n+\n+```\n+┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n+│                           Error Flow                                     │\n+├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n+│                                                                          │\n+│  gts/errors.json  ──────►  declare_errors! macro  ──────►  ErrorCode    │\n+│  (Source of Truth)         (Compile-time)                  (Enum)       │\n+│                                                                          │\n+│  DomainError  ──────►  ErrorCode::xxx().with_context()  ──────►  Problem│\n+│  (Business Logic)      (Mapping Layer)                        (RFC 9457)│\n+│                                                                          │\n+│  Problem  ──────►  IntoResponse (Axum)  ──────►  HTTP Response          │\n+│  (Data)            (Framework Integration)       (JSON + Headers)       │\n+│                                                                          │\n+└─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘\n+```\n+\n+## Components\n+\n+### 1. Error Catalog JSON (`gts/errors.json`)\n+\n+The source of truth for error definitions. Located in each module's `gts/` directory.\n+\n+**File Location Pattern:** `<module>/gts/errors.json`\n+\n+**Schema:**\n+```json\n+[\n+  {\n+    \"status\": 404,\n+    \"title\": \"User Not Found\",\n+    \"code\": \"gts.hx.core.errors.err.v1~hx.example1.user.not_found.v1\",\n+    \"type\": \"https://errors.example.com/...\",  // optional\n+    \"alias\": \"user_not_found\"                   // optional\n+  }\n+]\n+```\n+\n+**Fields:**\n+| Field | Required | Description |\n+|-------|----------|-------------|\n+| `status` | Yes | HTTP status code (100-599) |\n+| `title` | Yes | Human-readable error title |\n+| `code` | Yes | GTS-formatted error code |\n+| `type` | No | URI for error documentation |\n+| `alias` | No | Short name override for generated accessor |\n+\n+### 2. GTS Code Format\n+\n+GTS codes follow a strict format for global type identification:\n+\n+```\n+gts.vendor.package.namespace.type.version~chain1~chain2~...~instanceGTX\n+```\n+\n+**Structure:**\n+- **Prefix:** Always starts with `gts.`\n+- **Chain separator:** `~` separates GTX segments\n+- **Segment separator:** `.` separates parts within a GTX\n+- **Final GTX:** Must have at least 5 segments: `vendor.package.namespace.type.version`\n+- **Version:** Must end with `vN` or `vN.M` format\n+\n+**Example Breakdown:**\n+```\n+gts.hx.core.errors.err.v1~hx.example1.user.not_found.v1\n+│   │  │    │      │   │  │  │        │    │         │\n+│   │  │    │      │   │  │  │        │    │         └─ version\n+│   │  │    │      │   │  │  │        │    └─ type (not_found)\n+│   │  │    │      │   │  │  │        └─ namespace (user)\n+│   │  │    │      │   │  │  └─ package (example1)\n+│   │  │    │      │   │  └─ vendor (hx)\n+│   │  │    │      │   └─ version\n+│   │  │    │      └─ type (err)\n+│   │  │    └─ namespace (errors)\n+│   │  └─ package (core)\n+│   └─ vendor (hx)\n+└─ prefix\n+```\n+\n+**Validation Rules:**\n+1. Must start with `gts.`\n+2. All segments must be lowercase alphanumeric or underscore\n+3. No empty segments allowed\n+4. Final GTX must have ≥5 segments after vendor\n+5. Must end with valid version format (`v1`, `v1.2`, etc.)\n+\n+### 3. Proc-Macro: `declare_errors!`\n+\n+Generates type-safe error code enums from JSON at compile time.\n+\n+**Location:** `libs/modkit-errors-macro/src/lib.rs`\n+\n+**Usage:**\n+```rust\n+use modkit_errors_macro::declare_errors;\n+\n+declare_errors! {\n+    path = \"gts/errors.json\",\n+    namespace = \"errors\",\n+    vis = \"pub\"\n+}\n+```\n+\n+**Parameters:**\n+| Parameter | Required | Description |\n+|-----------|----------|-------------|\n+| `path` | Yes | Path to JSON file relative to `CARGO_MANIFEST_DIR` |\n+| `namespace` | Yes | Module name for generated code |\n+| `vis` | No | Visibility (`\"pub\"` or private) |\n+\n+**Generated Code:**\n+```rust\n+// Enum with all error codes\n+#[derive(Debug, Clone, Copy, PartialEq, Eq, Hash)]\n+pub enum ErrorCode {\n+    gts_hx_core_errors_err_v1_hx_example1_user_not_found_v1,\n+    // ...\n+}\n+\n+impl ErrorCode {\n+    // Get HTTP status\n+    pub const fn status(&self) -> u16 { ... }\n+    \n+    // Get full error definition\n+    pub const fn def(&self) -> ErrDef { ... }\n+    \n+    // Convert to Problem with detail\n+    pub fn as_problem(&self, detail: impl Into<String>) -> Problem { ... }\n+    \n+    // Create Problem with context (instance + trace_id)\n+    pub fn with_context(\n+        &self,\n+        detail: impl Into<String>,\n+        instance: &str,\n+        trace_id: Option<String>,\n+    ) -> Problem { ... }\n+    \n+    // Short accessor (derived from GTS or alias)\n+    pub const fn example1_user_not_found_v1() -> Self { ... }\n+}\n+\n+// Compile-time validated macro\n+macro_rules! problem_from_catalog { ... }\n+macro_rules! response_from_catalog { ... }\n+```\n+\n+### 4. Core Types\n+\n+#### `ErrDef` (Error Definition)\n+**Location:** `libs/modkit-errors/src/catalog.rs`\n+\n+```rust\n+pub struct ErrDef {\n+    pub status: u16,\n+    pub title: &'static str,\n+    pub code: &'static str,\n+    pub type_url: &'static str,\n+}\n+\n+impl ErrDef {\n+    pub fn as_problem(&self, detail: impl Into<String>) -> Problem { ... }\n+}\n+```\n+\n+#### `Problem` (RFC 9457)\n+**Location:** `libs/modkit-errors/src/problem.rs`\n+\n+```rust\n+pub struct Problem {\n+    pub type_url: String,      // URI reference for problem type\n+    pub title: String,         // Human-readable summary\n+    pub status: StatusCode,    // HTTP status code\n+    pub detail: String,        // Specific occurrence explanation\n+    pub instance: String,      // URI for this occurrence\n+    pub code: String,          // Machine-readable error code\n+    pub trace_id: Option<String>,\n+    pub errors: Option<Vec<ValidationViolation>>,\n+}\n+```\n+\n+**Builder Pattern:**\n+```rust\n+Problem::new(StatusCode::NOT_FOUND, \"Not Found\", \"User not found\")\n+    .with_code(\"gts.hx....\")\n+    .with_type(\"https://...\")\n+    .with_instance(\"/api/users/123\")\n+    .with_trace_id(\"req-456\")\n+    .with_errors(vec![...])\n+```\n+\n+## Error Flow by Layer\n+\n+### Layer 1: Domain Errors\n+\n+Domain errors represent business logic failures. They are internal and don't contain HTTP-specific information.\n+\n+**Location:** `<module>/src/domain/error.rs`\n+\n+```rust\n+#[derive(Error, Debug)]\n+pub enum DomainError {\n+    #[error(\"User not found: {id}\")]\n+    UserNotFound { id: Uuid },\n+    \n+    #[error(\"Email '{email}' already exists\")]\n+    EmailAlreadyExists { email: String },\n+    \n+    #[error(\"Database error: {message}\")]\n+    Database { message: String },\n+    // ...\n+}\n+```\n+\n+### Layer 2: SDK Errors (Public API)\n+\n+SDK errors are exposed to other modules via the client trait. They are simplified and safe to expose.\n+\n+**Location:** `<module>-sdk/src/errors.rs`\n+\n+```rust\n+#[derive(Error, Debug, Clone)]\n+pub enum UsersInfoError {\n+    #[error(\"Resource not found: {id}\")]\n+    NotFound { id: Uuid },\n+    \n+    #[error(\"Validation error: {message}\")]\n+    Validation { message: String },\n+    \n+    #[error(\"Internal error\")]\n+    Internal,\n+}\n+```\n+\n+### Layer 3: API Error Mapping\n+\n+The API layer maps domain errors to RFC 9457 Problems using the error catalog.\n+\n+**Location:** `<module>/src/api/rest/error.rs`\n+\n+```rust\n+use crate::errors::ErrorCode;\n+\n+pub fn domain_error_to_problem(e: &DomainError, instance: &str) -> Problem {\n+    let trace_id = tracing::Span::current()\n+        .id()\n+        .map(|id| id.into_u64().to_string());\n+\n+    match &e {\n+        DomainError::UserNotFound { id } => {\n+            ErrorCode::example1_user_not_found_v1().with_context(\n+                format!(\"User with id {id} was not found\"),\n+                instance,\n+                trace_id,\n+            )\n+        }\n+        DomainError::Database { .. } => {\n+            tracing::error!(error = ?e, \"Database error occurred\");\n+            ErrorCode::example1_user_internal_database_v1().with_context(\n+                \"An internal database error occurred\",\n+                instance,\n+                trace_id,\n+            )\n+        }\n+        // ...\n+    }\n+}\n+```\n+\n+### Layer 4: HTTP Response\n+\n+`Problem` implements `IntoResponse` for Axum, automatically:\n+- Setting the correct HTTP status code\n+- Setting `Content-Type: application/problem+json`\n+- Enriching with trace ID from current span if not set\n+\n+```rust\n+// In handler\n+async fn get_user(...) -> Result<Json<User>, Problem> {\n+    let user = service.get_user(id).await\n+        .map_err(|e| domain_error_to_problem(&e, &path))?;\n+    Ok(Json(user))\n+}\n+```\n+\n+## Creating a New Error Catalog\n+\n+### Step 1: Create `gts/errors.json`\n+\n+```json\n+[\n+  {\n+    \"status\": 404,\n+    \"title\": \"Resource Not Found\",\n+    \"code\": \"gts.hx.core.errors.err.v1~hx.mymodule.resource.not_found.v1\"\n+  },\n+  {\n+    \"status\": 422,\n+    \"title\": \"Validation Error\",\n+    \"code\": \"gts.hx.core.errors.err.v1~hx.mymodule.validation.invalid_input.v1\"\n+  }\n+]\n+```\n+\n+### Step 2: Create `src/errors.rs`\n+\n+```rust\n+use modkit_errors_macro::declare_errors;\n+\n+declare_errors! {\n+    path = \"gts/errors.json\",\n+    namespace = \"errors\",\n+    vis = \"pub\"\n+}\n+```\n+\n+### Step 3: Add to `Cargo.toml`\n+\n+```toml\n+[dependencies]\n+modkit-errors-macro = { path = \"../../libs/modkit-errors-macro\" }\n+modkit-errors = { path = \"../../libs/modkit-errors\" }\n+```\n+\n+### Step 4: Use in API Layer\n+\n+```rust\n+use crate::errors::ErrorCode;\n+\n+fn map_error(e: &MyDomainError, instance: &str) -> Problem {\n+    match e {\n+        MyDomainError::NotFound => {\n+            ErrorCode::mymodule_resource_not_found_v1()\n+                .with_context(\"Resource not found\", instance, None)\n+        }\n+        // ...\n+    }\n+}\n+```\n+\n+## Short Name Derivation\n+\n+Short accessor names are derived from the final GTX segment:\n+\n+```\n+gts.hx.core.errors.err.v1~hx.example1.user.not_found.v1\n+                         └─────────────────────────────┘\n+                                    ↓\n+                         example1_user_not_found_v1()\n+```\n+\n+**Rules:**\n+1. Extract final GTX (after last `~`)\n+2. Drop vendor (first segment)\n+3. Join remaining segments with `_`\n+4. Prefix with `_` if starts with digit\n+\n+**Override with `alias`:**\n+```json\n+{\n+  \"code\": \"gts.hx.core.errors.err.v1~hx.example1.user.not_found.v1\",","path":"docs/GTS_ERRORS.md","commit_id":"5bdb0f43b25858af78999718f7247813802b9634","original_commit_id":"5bdb0f43b25858af78999718f7247813802b9634","user":{"login":"Artifizer","id":192502778,"node_id":"U_kgDOC3lb-g","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/192502778?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer","html_url":"https://github.com/Artifizer","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"hx -> cf","created_at":"2026-01-30T20:15:11Z","updated_at":"2026-01-30T21:23:01Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/290#discussion_r2747848678","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/290","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2747848678"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/290#discussion_r2747848678"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/290"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2747848678/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":null,"original_line":375,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"MEMBER","original_position":375,"position":1,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2747853692","pull_request_review_id":3710446544,"id":2747853692,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs6jyOt8","diff_hunk":"","path":"intended_design/UNIFIED_ERROR_SYSTEM.md","commit_id":"a14d31841e0d559695e4ab49973b4f815551ccf3","original_commit_id":"5bdb0f43b25858af78999718f7247813802b9634","user":{"login":"Artifizer","id":192502778,"node_id":"U_kgDOC3lb-g","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/192502778?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer","html_url":"https://github.com/Artifizer","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Agree, we'd need to restructure the document and split it to:\nPRD - problem statement and requirements - we need unique error codes encoding true error origin\nADR - what options we had - what options we reviewed, how others are solving similar problem\nDESIGN - what is the final design ...","created_at":"2026-01-30T20:16:37Z","updated_at":"2026-01-30T21:23:01Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/290#discussion_r2747853692","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/290","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2747853692"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/290#discussion_r2747853692"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/290"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2747853692/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":1,"original_line":1,"side":"RIGHT","in_reply_to_id":2720926697,"author_association":"MEMBER","original_position":1,"position":1,"subject_type":"file"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2747860815","pull_request_review_id":3710446544,"id":2747860815,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs6jyQdP","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,1574 @@\n+# Unified Error System - Intention Document\n+\n+This document defines the architecture, rules, and implementation plan for a unified error handling system across the Hyperspot project. All REST API errors MUST have a GTS identifier, trace ID, and be registered in the types registry.\n+\n+## Table of Contents\n+\n+1. [Executive Summary](#executive-summary)\n+2. [Industry Research](#industry-research)\n+3. [Current State Analysis](#current-state-analysis)\n+4. [Requirements](#requirements)\n+5. [Implementation Rules](#implementation-rules)\n+6. [Migration Plan](#migration-plan)\n+7. [Examples](#examples)\n+8. [HTTP Headers](#http-headers)\n+9. [Security Considerations](#security-considerations)\n+10. [Appendix A: Error Category Definitions](#appendix-a-error-category-definitions)\n+11. [Appendix B: Retryable Error Guidelines](#appendix-b-retryable-error-guidelines)\n+12. [GTS System Errors Catalog](#gts-system-errors-catalog)\n+13. [References](#references)\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Executive Summary\n+\n+### Problem Statement\n+\n+The current error handling across Hyperspot modules is inconsistent:\n+- Some modules use `declare_errors!` macro with JSON catalogs\n+- Others define errors inline without GTS codes\n+- Errors are not registered in the types registry\n+- No standardized metadata/context fields\n+- Inconsistent trace ID propagation\n+\n+### Goals\n+\n+1. **Every REST API error** MUST have a valid GTS identifier\n+2. **Every error response** MUST include a trace ID for debugging\n+3. **All error types** MUST be registered in the types registry","path":"intended_design/UNIFIED_ERROR_SYSTEM.md","commit_id":"a14d31841e0d559695e4ab49973b4f815551ccf3","original_commit_id":"5bdb0f43b25858af78999718f7247813802b9634","user":{"login":"Artifizer","id":192502778,"node_id":"U_kgDOC3lb-g","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/192502778?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer","html_url":"https://github.com/Artifizer","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"all HTTP error types, not just all error types, correct?","created_at":"2026-01-30T20:18:40Z","updated_at":"2026-01-30T21:23:01Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/290#discussion_r2747860815","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/290","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2747860815"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/290#discussion_r2747860815"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/290"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2747860815/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":null,"original_line":38,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"MEMBER","original_position":38,"position":1,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2747873793","pull_request_review_id":3710446544,"id":2747873793,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs6jyToB","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,1574 @@\n+# Unified Error System - Intention Document\n+\n+This document defines the architecture, rules, and implementation plan for a unified error handling system across the Hyperspot project. All REST API errors MUST have a GTS identifier, trace ID, and be registered in the types registry.\n+\n+## Table of Contents\n+\n+1. [Executive Summary](#executive-summary)\n+2. [Industry Research](#industry-research)\n+3. [Current State Analysis](#current-state-analysis)\n+4. [Requirements](#requirements)\n+5. [Implementation Rules](#implementation-rules)\n+6. [Migration Plan](#migration-plan)\n+7. [Examples](#examples)\n+8. [HTTP Headers](#http-headers)\n+9. [Security Considerations](#security-considerations)\n+10. [Appendix A: Error Category Definitions](#appendix-a-error-category-definitions)\n+11. [Appendix B: Retryable Error Guidelines](#appendix-b-retryable-error-guidelines)\n+12. [GTS System Errors Catalog](#gts-system-errors-catalog)\n+13. [References](#references)\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Executive Summary\n+\n+### Problem Statement\n+\n+The current error handling across Hyperspot modules is inconsistent:\n+- Some modules use `declare_errors!` macro with JSON catalogs\n+- Others define errors inline without GTS codes\n+- Errors are not registered in the types registry\n+- No standardized metadata/context fields\n+- Inconsistent trace ID propagation\n+\n+### Goals\n+\n+1. **Every REST API error** MUST have a valid GTS identifier\n+2. **Every error response** MUST include a trace ID for debugging\n+3. **All error types** MUST be registered in the types registry\n+4. **Consistent error schema** across all modules following RFC 9457\n+5. **Machine-readable error codes** for programmatic handling\n+6. **Error stack propagation** for nested service calls\n+\n+### Non-Goals\n+\n+- Changing internal domain error types (only API-facing errors)\n+- Modifying logging infrastructure\n+- Changing HTTP status code semantics\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Industry Research\n+\n+### How Major Tech Companies Handle Errors\n+\n+| Company | Standard | Key Features |\n+|---------|----------|--------------|\n+| **Google** | AIP-193 + gRPC Status | `reason` (UPPER_SNAKE_CASE), `domain` (service name), `metadata` (key-value context), `ErrorInfo`, `LocalizedMessage`, `Help` links |\n+| **Amazon AWS** | Custom JSON | `errorType`, `httpStatus`, `requestId`, `message`, custom error object serialization |\n+| **Twitter/X** | JSON with `errors` array | `code` (CAPS_CASE), `message`, `parameter`, `details`, `value` |\n+| **RFC 9457** | Problem Details | `type` (URI), `title`, `status`, `detail`, `instance`, extension members |\n+\n+### Key Patterns Identified\n+\n+1. **Machine-readable identifiers** - Unique codes for programmatic handling (Google's `reason`, Twitter's `code`)\n+2. **Domain/namespace separation** - Identify error source (Google's `domain`, our GTS vendor.package)\n+3. **Structured metadata** - Key-value context without parsing messages (Google's `ErrorInfo.metadata`)\n+4. **Trace/Request IDs** - Correlation for debugging (AWS `requestId`, our `trace_id`)\n+5. **Documentation links** - URIs to error documentation (RFC 9457 `type`, Google's `Help`)\n+6. **Error categorization** - System vs User-defined, Retryable vs Non-retryable\n+\n+### Google AIP-193 ErrorInfo Structure (Reference)\n+\n+```json\n+{\n+  \"error\": {\n+    \"code\": 429,\n+    \"message\": \"The zone 'us-east1-a' does not have enough resources...\",\n+    \"status\": \"RESOURCE_EXHAUSTED\",\n+    \"details\": [\n+      {\n+        \"@type\": \"type.googleapis.com/google.rpc.ErrorInfo\",\n+        \"reason\": \"RESOURCE_AVAILABILITY\",\n+        \"domain\": \"compute.googleapis.com\",\n+        \"metadata\": {\n+          \"zone\": \"us-east1-a\",\n+          \"vmType\": \"e2-medium\"\n+        }\n+      }\n+    ]\n+  }\n+}\n+```\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Current State Analysis\n+\n+### Existing Infrastructure\n+\n+1. **`Problem` struct** (`libs/modkit-errors/src/problem.rs`) - RFC 9457 compliant\n+   - Fields: `type_url`, `title`, `status`, `detail`, `instance`, `code`, `trace_id`, `errors`\n+   - Implements `IntoResponse` for Axum with automatic trace ID enrichment\n+\n+2. **`struct_to_gts_schema` macro** (`modules/types-registry/gts-rust/gts-macros/src/lib.rs`)\n+   - Attribute macro for explicit struct definitions with GTS IDs visible in code\n+   - Generates constants: `GTS_SCHEMA_ID`, `GTS_SCHEMA_JSON`, etc.\n+   - **This pattern will be adapted for error definitions**\n+\n+3. **`declare_errors!` macro** (`libs/modkit-errors-macro/src/lib.rs`) - **TO BE DEPRECATED**\n+   - Generates type-safe error enums from JSON catalogs\n+   - Problem: GTS IDs hidden in external JSON files, not visible to LLMs\n+   - Used by: `users_info` example, `modkit-odata`\n+\n+### Gaps Identified\n+\n+| Gap | Current State | Required State |\n+|-----|---------------|----------------|\n+| **Hidden GTS IDs** | JSON-based `declare_errors!` | Explicit `#[gts_error]` structs with visible GTS IDs |\n+| **Inconsistent definitions** | Some modules use inline errors | All modules use `#[gts_error]` structs |\n+| **No types registry** | Errors not registered | All errors registered as GTS types |","path":"intended_design/UNIFIED_ERROR_SYSTEM.md","commit_id":"5bdb0f43b25858af78999718f7247813802b9634","original_commit_id":"5bdb0f43b25858af78999718f7247813802b9634","user":{"login":"Artifizer","id":192502778,"node_id":"U_kgDOC3lb-g","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/192502778?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer","html_url":"https://github.com/Artifizer","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"All _API-facing_ errors registered as GTS types","created_at":"2026-01-30T20:23:30Z","updated_at":"2026-01-30T21:23:01Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/290#discussion_r2747873793","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/290","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2747873793"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/290#discussion_r2747873793"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/290"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2747873793/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":null,"original_line":120,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"MEMBER","original_position":120,"position":1,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2747888228","pull_request_review_id":3710446544,"id":2747888228,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs6jyXJk","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,1574 @@\n+# Unified Error System - Intention Document\n+\n+This document defines the architecture, rules, and implementation plan for a unified error handling system across the Hyperspot project. All REST API errors MUST have a GTS identifier, trace ID, and be registered in the types registry.\n+\n+## Table of Contents\n+\n+1. [Executive Summary](#executive-summary)\n+2. [Industry Research](#industry-research)\n+3. [Current State Analysis](#current-state-analysis)\n+4. [Requirements](#requirements)\n+5. [Implementation Rules](#implementation-rules)\n+6. [Migration Plan](#migration-plan)\n+7. [Examples](#examples)\n+8. [HTTP Headers](#http-headers)\n+9. [Security Considerations](#security-considerations)\n+10. [Appendix A: Error Category Definitions](#appendix-a-error-category-definitions)\n+11. [Appendix B: Retryable Error Guidelines](#appendix-b-retryable-error-guidelines)\n+12. [GTS System Errors Catalog](#gts-system-errors-catalog)\n+13. [References](#references)\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Executive Summary\n+\n+### Problem Statement\n+\n+The current error handling across Hyperspot modules is inconsistent:\n+- Some modules use `declare_errors!` macro with JSON catalogs\n+- Others define errors inline without GTS codes\n+- Errors are not registered in the types registry\n+- No standardized metadata/context fields\n+- Inconsistent trace ID propagation\n+\n+### Goals\n+\n+1. **Every REST API error** MUST have a valid GTS identifier\n+2. **Every error response** MUST include a trace ID for debugging\n+3. **All error types** MUST be registered in the types registry\n+4. **Consistent error schema** across all modules following RFC 9457\n+5. **Machine-readable error codes** for programmatic handling\n+6. **Error stack propagation** for nested service calls\n+\n+### Non-Goals\n+\n+- Changing internal domain error types (only API-facing errors)\n+- Modifying logging infrastructure\n+- Changing HTTP status code semantics\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Industry Research\n+\n+### How Major Tech Companies Handle Errors\n+\n+| Company | Standard | Key Features |\n+|---------|----------|--------------|\n+| **Google** | AIP-193 + gRPC Status | `reason` (UPPER_SNAKE_CASE), `domain` (service name), `metadata` (key-value context), `ErrorInfo`, `LocalizedMessage`, `Help` links |\n+| **Amazon AWS** | Custom JSON | `errorType`, `httpStatus`, `requestId`, `message`, custom error object serialization |\n+| **Twitter/X** | JSON with `errors` array | `code` (CAPS_CASE), `message`, `parameter`, `details`, `value` |\n+| **RFC 9457** | Problem Details | `type` (URI), `title`, `status`, `detail`, `instance`, extension members |\n+\n+### Key Patterns Identified\n+\n+1. **Machine-readable identifiers** - Unique codes for programmatic handling (Google's `reason`, Twitter's `code`)\n+2. **Domain/namespace separation** - Identify error source (Google's `domain`, our GTS vendor.package)\n+3. **Structured metadata** - Key-value context without parsing messages (Google's `ErrorInfo.metadata`)\n+4. **Trace/Request IDs** - Correlation for debugging (AWS `requestId`, our `trace_id`)\n+5. **Documentation links** - URIs to error documentation (RFC 9457 `type`, Google's `Help`)\n+6. **Error categorization** - System vs User-defined, Retryable vs Non-retryable\n+\n+### Google AIP-193 ErrorInfo Structure (Reference)\n+\n+```json\n+{\n+  \"error\": {\n+    \"code\": 429,\n+    \"message\": \"The zone 'us-east1-a' does not have enough resources...\",\n+    \"status\": \"RESOURCE_EXHAUSTED\",\n+    \"details\": [\n+      {\n+        \"@type\": \"type.googleapis.com/google.rpc.ErrorInfo\",\n+        \"reason\": \"RESOURCE_AVAILABILITY\",\n+        \"domain\": \"compute.googleapis.com\",\n+        \"metadata\": {\n+          \"zone\": \"us-east1-a\",\n+          \"vmType\": \"e2-medium\"\n+        }\n+      }\n+    ]\n+  }\n+}\n+```\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Current State Analysis\n+\n+### Existing Infrastructure\n+\n+1. **`Problem` struct** (`libs/modkit-errors/src/problem.rs`) - RFC 9457 compliant\n+   - Fields: `type_url`, `title`, `status`, `detail`, `instance`, `code`, `trace_id`, `errors`\n+   - Implements `IntoResponse` for Axum with automatic trace ID enrichment\n+\n+2. **`struct_to_gts_schema` macro** (`modules/types-registry/gts-rust/gts-macros/src/lib.rs`)\n+   - Attribute macro for explicit struct definitions with GTS IDs visible in code\n+   - Generates constants: `GTS_SCHEMA_ID`, `GTS_SCHEMA_JSON`, etc.\n+   - **This pattern will be adapted for error definitions**\n+\n+3. **`declare_errors!` macro** (`libs/modkit-errors-macro/src/lib.rs`) - **TO BE DEPRECATED**\n+   - Generates type-safe error enums from JSON catalogs\n+   - Problem: GTS IDs hidden in external JSON files, not visible to LLMs\n+   - Used by: `users_info` example, `modkit-odata`\n+\n+### Gaps Identified\n+\n+| Gap | Current State | Required State |\n+|-----|---------------|----------------|\n+| **Hidden GTS IDs** | JSON-based `declare_errors!` | Explicit `#[gts_error]` structs with visible GTS IDs |\n+| **Inconsistent definitions** | Some modules use inline errors | All modules use `#[gts_error]` structs |\n+| **No types registry** | Errors not registered | All errors registered as GTS types |\n+| **Missing metadata** | No structured context | Struct fields → `metadata` map |\n+| **Partial trace IDs** | Only in `IntoResponse` | Mandatory in all error responses |\n+| **No error categories** | Flat error codes | System/Operational/Client categories |\n+| **No error stack** | Single error | Upstream error chain propagation |\n+\n+### Current Module Migration Status\n+\n+| Module | Location | Status | Issues |\n+|--------|----------|--------|--------|\n+| **file_parser** | `modules/file_parser/` | 🔴 Not migrated | No GTS IDs, inline `Problem::new()` |\n+| **types-registry** | `modules/system/types-registry/` | 🟡 Partial | Has codes but not GTS format (e.g., `TYPES_REGISTRY_NOT_FOUND`) |\n+| **nodes_registry** | `modules/system/nodes_registry/` | 🔴 Not migrated | Non-GTS codes (e.g., `NODES_NOT_FOUND`) |\n+| **api_gateway** | `modules/system/api_gateway/` | 🔴 Not migrated | No Problem struct, simple error codes |\n+| **tenant_resolver** | `modules/system/tenant_resolver/` | 🔴 Not migrated | No GTS IDs |\n+| **simple-user-settings** | `modules/simple-user-settings/` | 🟡 Partial | Uses `declare_errors!` with old chain format |\n+| **modkit-auth** | `libs/modkit-auth/` | 🔴 Not migrated | No GTS IDs, custom `IntoResponse` |\n+| **modkit-odata** | `libs/modkit-odata/` | 🟡 Partial | Uses `declare_errors!` with old chain format |\n+| **users_info** (example) | `examples/modkit/users_info/` | 🟡 Partial | Uses `declare_errors!` with old chain format |\n+\n+#### Legend\n+- 🟢 **Migrated** - Uses `#[gts_error]` structs with proper base types\n+- 🟡 **Partial** - Has GTS IDs but uses deprecated `declare_errors!` or old format\n+- 🔴 **Not migrated** - No GTS IDs or non-GTS format codes\n+\n+#### GTS ID Format Note\n+\n+**Old chain format** (used by `declare_errors!`):\n+```\n+gts.hx.core.errors.err.v1~hx.module.error_name.v1\n+```\n+\n+**New format** (with `base` field):\n+```\n+gts.hx.module.namespace.error_name.v1~","path":"intended_design/UNIFIED_ERROR_SYSTEM.md","commit_id":"5bdb0f43b25858af78999718f7247813802b9634","original_commit_id":"5bdb0f43b25858af78999718f7247813802b9634","user":{"login":"Artifizer","id":192502778,"node_id":"U_kgDOC3lb-g","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/192502778?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer","html_url":"https://github.com/Artifizer","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"This is a bit wrong I believe, because:\n1. If you make it like this, every error can technically have it's own schema\n2. you can't use just schema, you need an instance, right? So you'd have `gts.hx.module.namespace.error_name.v1~a.b.c.d.v1` anyway, as you need to initialize fields values\n3. we'll end up with hundreds of base classes... and every class would have just single instance\n\nI think original definition was correct:\n```gts.cf.core.errors.err.v1~<vendor>.<module>.<namespace>.<error_name>.v1```\n\nSo `gts.cf.core.errors.err.v1~` defines schema for all errors, while the instance defines exact values\n","created_at":"2026-01-30T20:28:59Z","updated_at":"2026-01-30T21:23:02Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/290#discussion_r2747888228","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/290","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2747888228"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/290#discussion_r2747888228"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/290"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2747888228/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":null,"original_line":154,"side":"RIGHT","in_reply_to_id":2735807271,"author_association":"MEMBER","original_position":154,"position":1,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2747889953","pull_request_review_id":3710446544,"id":2747889953,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs6jyXkh","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,1574 @@\n+# Unified Error System - Intention Document\n+\n+This document defines the architecture, rules, and implementation plan for a unified error handling system across the Hyperspot project. All REST API errors MUST have a GTS identifier, trace ID, and be registered in the types registry.\n+\n+## Table of Contents\n+\n+1. [Executive Summary](#executive-summary)\n+2. [Industry Research](#industry-research)\n+3. [Current State Analysis](#current-state-analysis)\n+4. [Requirements](#requirements)\n+5. [Implementation Rules](#implementation-rules)\n+6. [Migration Plan](#migration-plan)\n+7. [Examples](#examples)\n+8. [HTTP Headers](#http-headers)\n+9. [Security Considerations](#security-considerations)\n+10. [Appendix A: Error Category Definitions](#appendix-a-error-category-definitions)\n+11. [Appendix B: Retryable Error Guidelines](#appendix-b-retryable-error-guidelines)\n+12. [GTS System Errors Catalog](#gts-system-errors-catalog)\n+13. [References](#references)\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Executive Summary\n+\n+### Problem Statement\n+\n+The current error handling across Hyperspot modules is inconsistent:\n+- Some modules use `declare_errors!` macro with JSON catalogs\n+- Others define errors inline without GTS codes\n+- Errors are not registered in the types registry\n+- No standardized metadata/context fields\n+- Inconsistent trace ID propagation\n+\n+### Goals\n+\n+1. **Every REST API error** MUST have a valid GTS identifier\n+2. **Every error response** MUST include a trace ID for debugging\n+3. **All error types** MUST be registered in the types registry\n+4. **Consistent error schema** across all modules following RFC 9457\n+5. **Machine-readable error codes** for programmatic handling\n+6. **Error stack propagation** for nested service calls\n+\n+### Non-Goals\n+\n+- Changing internal domain error types (only API-facing errors)\n+- Modifying logging infrastructure\n+- Changing HTTP status code semantics\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Industry Research\n+\n+### How Major Tech Companies Handle Errors\n+\n+| Company | Standard | Key Features |\n+|---------|----------|--------------|\n+| **Google** | AIP-193 + gRPC Status | `reason` (UPPER_SNAKE_CASE), `domain` (service name), `metadata` (key-value context), `ErrorInfo`, `LocalizedMessage`, `Help` links |\n+| **Amazon AWS** | Custom JSON | `errorType`, `httpStatus`, `requestId`, `message`, custom error object serialization |\n+| **Twitter/X** | JSON with `errors` array | `code` (CAPS_CASE), `message`, `parameter`, `details`, `value` |\n+| **RFC 9457** | Problem Details | `type` (URI), `title`, `status`, `detail`, `instance`, extension members |\n+\n+### Key Patterns Identified\n+\n+1. **Machine-readable identifiers** - Unique codes for programmatic handling (Google's `reason`, Twitter's `code`)\n+2. **Domain/namespace separation** - Identify error source (Google's `domain`, our GTS vendor.package)\n+3. **Structured metadata** - Key-value context without parsing messages (Google's `ErrorInfo.metadata`)\n+4. **Trace/Request IDs** - Correlation for debugging (AWS `requestId`, our `trace_id`)\n+5. **Documentation links** - URIs to error documentation (RFC 9457 `type`, Google's `Help`)\n+6. **Error categorization** - System vs User-defined, Retryable vs Non-retryable\n+\n+### Google AIP-193 ErrorInfo Structure (Reference)\n+\n+```json\n+{\n+  \"error\": {\n+    \"code\": 429,\n+    \"message\": \"The zone 'us-east1-a' does not have enough resources...\",\n+    \"status\": \"RESOURCE_EXHAUSTED\",\n+    \"details\": [\n+      {\n+        \"@type\": \"type.googleapis.com/google.rpc.ErrorInfo\",\n+        \"reason\": \"RESOURCE_AVAILABILITY\",\n+        \"domain\": \"compute.googleapis.com\",\n+        \"metadata\": {\n+          \"zone\": \"us-east1-a\",\n+          \"vmType\": \"e2-medium\"\n+        }\n+      }\n+    ]\n+  }\n+}\n+```\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Current State Analysis\n+\n+### Existing Infrastructure\n+\n+1. **`Problem` struct** (`libs/modkit-errors/src/problem.rs`) - RFC 9457 compliant\n+   - Fields: `type_url`, `title`, `status`, `detail`, `instance`, `code`, `trace_id`, `errors`\n+   - Implements `IntoResponse` for Axum with automatic trace ID enrichment\n+\n+2. **`struct_to_gts_schema` macro** (`modules/types-registry/gts-rust/gts-macros/src/lib.rs`)\n+   - Attribute macro for explicit struct definitions with GTS IDs visible in code\n+   - Generates constants: `GTS_SCHEMA_ID`, `GTS_SCHEMA_JSON`, etc.\n+   - **This pattern will be adapted for error definitions**\n+\n+3. **`declare_errors!` macro** (`libs/modkit-errors-macro/src/lib.rs`) - **TO BE DEPRECATED**\n+   - Generates type-safe error enums from JSON catalogs\n+   - Problem: GTS IDs hidden in external JSON files, not visible to LLMs\n+   - Used by: `users_info` example, `modkit-odata`\n+\n+### Gaps Identified\n+\n+| Gap | Current State | Required State |\n+|-----|---------------|----------------|\n+| **Hidden GTS IDs** | JSON-based `declare_errors!` | Explicit `#[gts_error]` structs with visible GTS IDs |\n+| **Inconsistent definitions** | Some modules use inline errors | All modules use `#[gts_error]` structs |\n+| **No types registry** | Errors not registered | All errors registered as GTS types |\n+| **Missing metadata** | No structured context | Struct fields → `metadata` map |\n+| **Partial trace IDs** | Only in `IntoResponse` | Mandatory in all error responses |\n+| **No error categories** | Flat error codes | System/Operational/Client categories |\n+| **No error stack** | Single error | Upstream error chain propagation |\n+\n+### Current Module Migration Status\n+\n+| Module | Location | Status | Issues |\n+|--------|----------|--------|--------|\n+| **file_parser** | `modules/file_parser/` | 🔴 Not migrated | No GTS IDs, inline `Problem::new()` |\n+| **types-registry** | `modules/system/types-registry/` | 🟡 Partial | Has codes but not GTS format (e.g., `TYPES_REGISTRY_NOT_FOUND`) |\n+| **nodes_registry** | `modules/system/nodes_registry/` | 🔴 Not migrated | Non-GTS codes (e.g., `NODES_NOT_FOUND`) |\n+| **api_gateway** | `modules/system/api_gateway/` | 🔴 Not migrated | No Problem struct, simple error codes |\n+| **tenant_resolver** | `modules/system/tenant_resolver/` | 🔴 Not migrated | No GTS IDs |\n+| **simple-user-settings** | `modules/simple-user-settings/` | 🟡 Partial | Uses `declare_errors!` with old chain format |\n+| **modkit-auth** | `libs/modkit-auth/` | 🔴 Not migrated | No GTS IDs, custom `IntoResponse` |\n+| **modkit-odata** | `libs/modkit-odata/` | 🟡 Partial | Uses `declare_errors!` with old chain format |\n+| **users_info** (example) | `examples/modkit/users_info/` | 🟡 Partial | Uses `declare_errors!` with old chain format |\n+\n+#### Legend\n+- 🟢 **Migrated** - Uses `#[gts_error]` structs with proper base types\n+- 🟡 **Partial** - Has GTS IDs but uses deprecated `declare_errors!` or old format\n+- 🔴 **Not migrated** - No GTS IDs or non-GTS format codes\n+\n+#### GTS ID Format Note\n+\n+**Old chain format** (used by `declare_errors!`):\n+```\n+gts.hx.core.errors.err.v1~hx.module.error_name.v1\n+```\n+\n+**New format** (with `base` field):\n+```\n+gts.hx.module.namespace.error_name.v1~\n+```\n+The `base` field in `#[gts_error]` replaces the chain suffix, making inheritance explicit in code.\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Requirements\n+\n+### R1: Error Schema Requirements\n+\n+Every error returned from REST API MUST conform to the unified schema:\n+\n+```rust\n+pub struct Problem {\n+    // =========================================================================\n+    // REQUIRED FIELDS - Core error identification\n+    // =========================================================================\n+    \n+    /// URI reference identifying the problem type (GTS-based)\n+    /// Example: \"https://docs.hyperspot.com/errors/types_registry_entity_not_found_v1\"\n+    #[serde(rename = \"type\")]\n+    pub type_url: String,\n+    \n+    /// Human-readable summary of the problem type (static per error type)\n+    pub title: String,\n+    \n+    /// GTS error code (machine-readable identifier)\n+    pub code: String,\n+    \n+    /// Trace ID for request correlation\n+    pub trace_id: String,\n+    \n+    // =========================================================================\n+    // CONTEXTUAL FIELDS - Optional based on error context\n+    // =========================================================================\n+    \n+    /// HTTP status code. Optional because:\n+    /// - gRPC errors use different status codes\n+    /// - Internal/domain errors may not have HTTP context\n+    /// - Event-driven systems have no request/response\n+    /// When serializing for HTTP response, this is populated from error definition.\n+    #[serde(skip_serializing_if = \"Option::is_none\")]\n+    pub status: Option<u16>,\n+    \n+    /// Human-readable explanation specific to this occurrence.\n+    /// Optional - title may be sufficient for simple errors.\n+    #[serde(skip_serializing_if = \"Option::is_none\")]\n+    pub detail: Option<String>,\n+    \n+    /// Error category for client handling.\n+    /// Optional - can be inferred from base type hierarchy.\n+    #[serde(skip_serializing_if = \"Option::is_none\")]\n+    pub category: Option<ErrorCategory>,","path":"intended_design/UNIFIED_ERROR_SYSTEM.md","commit_id":"5bdb0f43b25858af78999718f7247813802b9634","original_commit_id":"5bdb0f43b25858af78999718f7247813802b9634","user":{"login":"Artifizer","id":192502778,"node_id":"U_kgDOC3lb-g","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/192502778?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer","html_url":"https://github.com/Artifizer","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"can it be GTS reference as well?","created_at":"2026-01-30T20:29:37Z","updated_at":"2026-01-30T21:23:01Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/290#discussion_r2747889953","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/290","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2747889953"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/290#discussion_r2747889953"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/290"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2747889953/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":null,"original_line":206,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"MEMBER","original_position":206,"position":1,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2747910208","pull_request_review_id":3710446544,"id":2747910208,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs6jychA","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,1574 @@\n+# Unified Error System - Intention Document\n+\n+This document defines the architecture, rules, and implementation plan for a unified error handling system across the Hyperspot project. All REST API errors MUST have a GTS identifier, trace ID, and be registered in the types registry.\n+\n+## Table of Contents\n+\n+1. [Executive Summary](#executive-summary)\n+2. [Industry Research](#industry-research)\n+3. [Current State Analysis](#current-state-analysis)\n+4. [Requirements](#requirements)\n+5. [Implementation Rules](#implementation-rules)\n+6. [Migration Plan](#migration-plan)\n+7. [Examples](#examples)\n+8. [HTTP Headers](#http-headers)\n+9. [Security Considerations](#security-considerations)\n+10. [Appendix A: Error Category Definitions](#appendix-a-error-category-definitions)\n+11. [Appendix B: Retryable Error Guidelines](#appendix-b-retryable-error-guidelines)\n+12. [GTS System Errors Catalog](#gts-system-errors-catalog)\n+13. [References](#references)\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Executive Summary\n+\n+### Problem Statement\n+\n+The current error handling across Hyperspot modules is inconsistent:\n+- Some modules use `declare_errors!` macro with JSON catalogs\n+- Others define errors inline without GTS codes\n+- Errors are not registered in the types registry\n+- No standardized metadata/context fields\n+- Inconsistent trace ID propagation\n+\n+### Goals\n+\n+1. **Every REST API error** MUST have a valid GTS identifier\n+2. **Every error response** MUST include a trace ID for debugging\n+3. **All error types** MUST be registered in the types registry\n+4. **Consistent error schema** across all modules following RFC 9457\n+5. **Machine-readable error codes** for programmatic handling\n+6. **Error stack propagation** for nested service calls\n+\n+### Non-Goals\n+\n+- Changing internal domain error types (only API-facing errors)\n+- Modifying logging infrastructure\n+- Changing HTTP status code semantics\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Industry Research\n+\n+### How Major Tech Companies Handle Errors\n+\n+| Company | Standard | Key Features |\n+|---------|----------|--------------|\n+| **Google** | AIP-193 + gRPC Status | `reason` (UPPER_SNAKE_CASE), `domain` (service name), `metadata` (key-value context), `ErrorInfo`, `LocalizedMessage`, `Help` links |\n+| **Amazon AWS** | Custom JSON | `errorType`, `httpStatus`, `requestId`, `message`, custom error object serialization |\n+| **Twitter/X** | JSON with `errors` array | `code` (CAPS_CASE), `message`, `parameter`, `details`, `value` |\n+| **RFC 9457** | Problem Details | `type` (URI), `title`, `status`, `detail`, `instance`, extension members |\n+\n+### Key Patterns Identified\n+\n+1. **Machine-readable identifiers** - Unique codes for programmatic handling (Google's `reason`, Twitter's `code`)\n+2. **Domain/namespace separation** - Identify error source (Google's `domain`, our GTS vendor.package)\n+3. **Structured metadata** - Key-value context without parsing messages (Google's `ErrorInfo.metadata`)\n+4. **Trace/Request IDs** - Correlation for debugging (AWS `requestId`, our `trace_id`)\n+5. **Documentation links** - URIs to error documentation (RFC 9457 `type`, Google's `Help`)\n+6. **Error categorization** - System vs User-defined, Retryable vs Non-retryable\n+\n+### Google AIP-193 ErrorInfo Structure (Reference)\n+\n+```json\n+{\n+  \"error\": {\n+    \"code\": 429,\n+    \"message\": \"The zone 'us-east1-a' does not have enough resources...\",\n+    \"status\": \"RESOURCE_EXHAUSTED\",\n+    \"details\": [\n+      {\n+        \"@type\": \"type.googleapis.com/google.rpc.ErrorInfo\",\n+        \"reason\": \"RESOURCE_AVAILABILITY\",\n+        \"domain\": \"compute.googleapis.com\",\n+        \"metadata\": {\n+          \"zone\": \"us-east1-a\",\n+          \"vmType\": \"e2-medium\"\n+        }\n+      }\n+    ]\n+  }\n+}\n+```\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Current State Analysis\n+\n+### Existing Infrastructure\n+\n+1. **`Problem` struct** (`libs/modkit-errors/src/problem.rs`) - RFC 9457 compliant\n+   - Fields: `type_url`, `title`, `status`, `detail`, `instance`, `code`, `trace_id`, `errors`\n+   - Implements `IntoResponse` for Axum with automatic trace ID enrichment\n+\n+2. **`struct_to_gts_schema` macro** (`modules/types-registry/gts-rust/gts-macros/src/lib.rs`)\n+   - Attribute macro for explicit struct definitions with GTS IDs visible in code\n+   - Generates constants: `GTS_SCHEMA_ID`, `GTS_SCHEMA_JSON`, etc.\n+   - **This pattern will be adapted for error definitions**\n+\n+3. **`declare_errors!` macro** (`libs/modkit-errors-macro/src/lib.rs`) - **TO BE DEPRECATED**\n+   - Generates type-safe error enums from JSON catalogs\n+   - Problem: GTS IDs hidden in external JSON files, not visible to LLMs\n+   - Used by: `users_info` example, `modkit-odata`\n+\n+### Gaps Identified\n+\n+| Gap | Current State | Required State |\n+|-----|---------------|----------------|\n+| **Hidden GTS IDs** | JSON-based `declare_errors!` | Explicit `#[gts_error]` structs with visible GTS IDs |\n+| **Inconsistent definitions** | Some modules use inline errors | All modules use `#[gts_error]` structs |\n+| **No types registry** | Errors not registered | All errors registered as GTS types |\n+| **Missing metadata** | No structured context | Struct fields → `metadata` map |\n+| **Partial trace IDs** | Only in `IntoResponse` | Mandatory in all error responses |\n+| **No error categories** | Flat error codes | System/Operational/Client categories |\n+| **No error stack** | Single error | Upstream error chain propagation |\n+\n+### Current Module Migration Status\n+\n+| Module | Location | Status | Issues |\n+|--------|----------|--------|--------|\n+| **file_parser** | `modules/file_parser/` | 🔴 Not migrated | No GTS IDs, inline `Problem::new()` |\n+| **types-registry** | `modules/system/types-registry/` | 🟡 Partial | Has codes but not GTS format (e.g., `TYPES_REGISTRY_NOT_FOUND`) |\n+| **nodes_registry** | `modules/system/nodes_registry/` | 🔴 Not migrated | Non-GTS codes (e.g., `NODES_NOT_FOUND`) |\n+| **api_gateway** | `modules/system/api_gateway/` | 🔴 Not migrated | No Problem struct, simple error codes |\n+| **tenant_resolver** | `modules/system/tenant_resolver/` | 🔴 Not migrated | No GTS IDs |\n+| **simple-user-settings** | `modules/simple-user-settings/` | 🟡 Partial | Uses `declare_errors!` with old chain format |\n+| **modkit-auth** | `libs/modkit-auth/` | 🔴 Not migrated | No GTS IDs, custom `IntoResponse` |\n+| **modkit-odata** | `libs/modkit-odata/` | 🟡 Partial | Uses `declare_errors!` with old chain format |\n+| **users_info** (example) | `examples/modkit/users_info/` | 🟡 Partial | Uses `declare_errors!` with old chain format |\n+\n+#### Legend\n+- 🟢 **Migrated** - Uses `#[gts_error]` structs with proper base types\n+- 🟡 **Partial** - Has GTS IDs but uses deprecated `declare_errors!` or old format\n+- 🔴 **Not migrated** - No GTS IDs or non-GTS format codes\n+\n+#### GTS ID Format Note\n+\n+**Old chain format** (used by `declare_errors!`):\n+```\n+gts.hx.core.errors.err.v1~hx.module.error_name.v1\n+```\n+\n+**New format** (with `base` field):\n+```\n+gts.hx.module.namespace.error_name.v1~\n+```\n+The `base` field in `#[gts_error]` replaces the chain suffix, making inheritance explicit in code.\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Requirements\n+\n+### R1: Error Schema Requirements\n+\n+Every error returned from REST API MUST conform to the unified schema:\n+\n+```rust\n+pub struct Problem {\n+    // =========================================================================\n+    // REQUIRED FIELDS - Core error identification\n+    // =========================================================================\n+    \n+    /// URI reference identifying the problem type (GTS-based)\n+    /// Example: \"https://docs.hyperspot.com/errors/types_registry_entity_not_found_v1\"\n+    #[serde(rename = \"type\")]\n+    pub type_url: String,\n+    \n+    /// Human-readable summary of the problem type (static per error type)\n+    pub title: String,\n+    \n+    /// GTS error code (machine-readable identifier)\n+    pub code: String,\n+    \n+    /// Trace ID for request correlation\n+    pub trace_id: String,\n+    \n+    // =========================================================================\n+    // CONTEXTUAL FIELDS - Optional based on error context\n+    // =========================================================================\n+    \n+    /// HTTP status code. Optional because:\n+    /// - gRPC errors use different status codes\n+    /// - Internal/domain errors may not have HTTP context\n+    /// - Event-driven systems have no request/response\n+    /// When serializing for HTTP response, this is populated from error definition.\n+    #[serde(skip_serializing_if = \"Option::is_none\")]\n+    pub status: Option<u16>,\n+    \n+    /// Human-readable explanation specific to this occurrence.\n+    /// Optional - title may be sufficient for simple errors.\n+    #[serde(skip_serializing_if = \"Option::is_none\")]\n+    pub detail: Option<String>,\n+    \n+    /// Error category for client handling.\n+    /// Optional - can be inferred from base type hierarchy.\n+    #[serde(skip_serializing_if = \"Option::is_none\")]\n+    pub category: Option<ErrorCategory>,\n+    \n+    /// Whether client can retry this request.\n+    /// Optional - can be inferred from base type; not relevant for all contexts.\n+    #[serde(skip_serializing_if = \"Option::is_none\")]\n+    pub retryable: Option<bool>,\n+    \n+    /// URI identifying this specific occurrence (auto-populated from request path)\n+    #[serde(skip_serializing_if = \"Option::is_none\")]\n+    pub instance: Option<String>,","path":"intended_design/UNIFIED_ERROR_SYSTEM.md","commit_id":"5bdb0f43b25858af78999718f7247813802b9634","original_commit_id":"5bdb0f43b25858af78999718f7247813802b9634","user":{"login":"Artifizer","id":192502778,"node_id":"U_kgDOC3lb-g","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/192502778?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer","html_url":"https://github.com/Artifizer","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"if you want to put current URL into 'instance' that it's an ALERT: it could become a security breach if your return original URI to the client or store it into log, imagine this is an upstream call within a system and it has unsafe secrets in URI","created_at":"2026-01-30T20:37:26Z","updated_at":"2026-01-30T21:23:01Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/290#discussion_r2747910208","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/290","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2747910208"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/290#discussion_r2747910208"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/290"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2747910208/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":null,"original_line":215,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"MEMBER","original_position":215,"position":1,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2747915573","pull_request_review_id":3710446544,"id":2747915573,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs6jyd01","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,1574 @@\n+# Unified Error System - Intention Document\n+\n+This document defines the architecture, rules, and implementation plan for a unified error handling system across the Hyperspot project. All REST API errors MUST have a GTS identifier, trace ID, and be registered in the types registry.\n+\n+## Table of Contents\n+\n+1. [Executive Summary](#executive-summary)\n+2. [Industry Research](#industry-research)\n+3. [Current State Analysis](#current-state-analysis)\n+4. [Requirements](#requirements)\n+5. [Implementation Rules](#implementation-rules)\n+6. [Migration Plan](#migration-plan)\n+7. [Examples](#examples)\n+8. [HTTP Headers](#http-headers)\n+9. [Security Considerations](#security-considerations)\n+10. [Appendix A: Error Category Definitions](#appendix-a-error-category-definitions)\n+11. [Appendix B: Retryable Error Guidelines](#appendix-b-retryable-error-guidelines)\n+12. [GTS System Errors Catalog](#gts-system-errors-catalog)\n+13. [References](#references)\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Executive Summary\n+\n+### Problem Statement\n+\n+The current error handling across Hyperspot modules is inconsistent:\n+- Some modules use `declare_errors!` macro with JSON catalogs\n+- Others define errors inline without GTS codes\n+- Errors are not registered in the types registry\n+- No standardized metadata/context fields\n+- Inconsistent trace ID propagation\n+\n+### Goals\n+\n+1. **Every REST API error** MUST have a valid GTS identifier\n+2. **Every error response** MUST include a trace ID for debugging\n+3. **All error types** MUST be registered in the types registry\n+4. **Consistent error schema** across all modules following RFC 9457\n+5. **Machine-readable error codes** for programmatic handling\n+6. **Error stack propagation** for nested service calls\n+\n+### Non-Goals\n+\n+- Changing internal domain error types (only API-facing errors)\n+- Modifying logging infrastructure\n+- Changing HTTP status code semantics\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Industry Research\n+\n+### How Major Tech Companies Handle Errors\n+\n+| Company | Standard | Key Features |\n+|---------|----------|--------------|\n+| **Google** | AIP-193 + gRPC Status | `reason` (UPPER_SNAKE_CASE), `domain` (service name), `metadata` (key-value context), `ErrorInfo`, `LocalizedMessage`, `Help` links |\n+| **Amazon AWS** | Custom JSON | `errorType`, `httpStatus`, `requestId`, `message`, custom error object serialization |\n+| **Twitter/X** | JSON with `errors` array | `code` (CAPS_CASE), `message`, `parameter`, `details`, `value` |\n+| **RFC 9457** | Problem Details | `type` (URI), `title`, `status`, `detail`, `instance`, extension members |\n+\n+### Key Patterns Identified\n+\n+1. **Machine-readable identifiers** - Unique codes for programmatic handling (Google's `reason`, Twitter's `code`)\n+2. **Domain/namespace separation** - Identify error source (Google's `domain`, our GTS vendor.package)\n+3. **Structured metadata** - Key-value context without parsing messages (Google's `ErrorInfo.metadata`)\n+4. **Trace/Request IDs** - Correlation for debugging (AWS `requestId`, our `trace_id`)\n+5. **Documentation links** - URIs to error documentation (RFC 9457 `type`, Google's `Help`)\n+6. **Error categorization** - System vs User-defined, Retryable vs Non-retryable\n+\n+### Google AIP-193 ErrorInfo Structure (Reference)\n+\n+```json\n+{\n+  \"error\": {\n+    \"code\": 429,\n+    \"message\": \"The zone 'us-east1-a' does not have enough resources...\",\n+    \"status\": \"RESOURCE_EXHAUSTED\",\n+    \"details\": [\n+      {\n+        \"@type\": \"type.googleapis.com/google.rpc.ErrorInfo\",\n+        \"reason\": \"RESOURCE_AVAILABILITY\",\n+        \"domain\": \"compute.googleapis.com\",\n+        \"metadata\": {\n+          \"zone\": \"us-east1-a\",\n+          \"vmType\": \"e2-medium\"\n+        }\n+      }\n+    ]\n+  }\n+}\n+```\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Current State Analysis\n+\n+### Existing Infrastructure\n+\n+1. **`Problem` struct** (`libs/modkit-errors/src/problem.rs`) - RFC 9457 compliant\n+   - Fields: `type_url`, `title`, `status`, `detail`, `instance`, `code`, `trace_id`, `errors`\n+   - Implements `IntoResponse` for Axum with automatic trace ID enrichment\n+\n+2. **`struct_to_gts_schema` macro** (`modules/types-registry/gts-rust/gts-macros/src/lib.rs`)\n+   - Attribute macro for explicit struct definitions with GTS IDs visible in code\n+   - Generates constants: `GTS_SCHEMA_ID`, `GTS_SCHEMA_JSON`, etc.\n+   - **This pattern will be adapted for error definitions**\n+\n+3. **`declare_errors!` macro** (`libs/modkit-errors-macro/src/lib.rs`) - **TO BE DEPRECATED**\n+   - Generates type-safe error enums from JSON catalogs\n+   - Problem: GTS IDs hidden in external JSON files, not visible to LLMs\n+   - Used by: `users_info` example, `modkit-odata`\n+\n+### Gaps Identified\n+\n+| Gap | Current State | Required State |\n+|-----|---------------|----------------|\n+| **Hidden GTS IDs** | JSON-based `declare_errors!` | Explicit `#[gts_error]` structs with visible GTS IDs |\n+| **Inconsistent definitions** | Some modules use inline errors | All modules use `#[gts_error]` structs |\n+| **No types registry** | Errors not registered | All errors registered as GTS types |\n+| **Missing metadata** | No structured context | Struct fields → `metadata` map |\n+| **Partial trace IDs** | Only in `IntoResponse` | Mandatory in all error responses |\n+| **No error categories** | Flat error codes | System/Operational/Client categories |\n+| **No error stack** | Single error | Upstream error chain propagation |\n+\n+### Current Module Migration Status\n+\n+| Module | Location | Status | Issues |\n+|--------|----------|--------|--------|\n+| **file_parser** | `modules/file_parser/` | 🔴 Not migrated | No GTS IDs, inline `Problem::new()` |\n+| **types-registry** | `modules/system/types-registry/` | 🟡 Partial | Has codes but not GTS format (e.g., `TYPES_REGISTRY_NOT_FOUND`) |\n+| **nodes_registry** | `modules/system/nodes_registry/` | 🔴 Not migrated | Non-GTS codes (e.g., `NODES_NOT_FOUND`) |\n+| **api_gateway** | `modules/system/api_gateway/` | 🔴 Not migrated | No Problem struct, simple error codes |\n+| **tenant_resolver** | `modules/system/tenant_resolver/` | 🔴 Not migrated | No GTS IDs |\n+| **simple-user-settings** | `modules/simple-user-settings/` | 🟡 Partial | Uses `declare_errors!` with old chain format |\n+| **modkit-auth** | `libs/modkit-auth/` | 🔴 Not migrated | No GTS IDs, custom `IntoResponse` |\n+| **modkit-odata** | `libs/modkit-odata/` | 🟡 Partial | Uses `declare_errors!` with old chain format |\n+| **users_info** (example) | `examples/modkit/users_info/` | 🟡 Partial | Uses `declare_errors!` with old chain format |\n+\n+#### Legend\n+- 🟢 **Migrated** - Uses `#[gts_error]` structs with proper base types\n+- 🟡 **Partial** - Has GTS IDs but uses deprecated `declare_errors!` or old format\n+- 🔴 **Not migrated** - No GTS IDs or non-GTS format codes\n+\n+#### GTS ID Format Note\n+\n+**Old chain format** (used by `declare_errors!`):\n+```\n+gts.hx.core.errors.err.v1~hx.module.error_name.v1\n+```\n+\n+**New format** (with `base` field):\n+```\n+gts.hx.module.namespace.error_name.v1~\n+```\n+The `base` field in `#[gts_error]` replaces the chain suffix, making inheritance explicit in code.\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Requirements\n+\n+### R1: Error Schema Requirements\n+\n+Every error returned from REST API MUST conform to the unified schema:\n+\n+```rust\n+pub struct Problem {\n+    // =========================================================================\n+    // REQUIRED FIELDS - Core error identification\n+    // =========================================================================\n+    \n+    /// URI reference identifying the problem type (GTS-based)\n+    /// Example: \"https://docs.hyperspot.com/errors/types_registry_entity_not_found_v1\"","path":"intended_design/UNIFIED_ERROR_SYSTEM.md","commit_id":"5bdb0f43b25858af78999718f7247813802b9634","original_commit_id":"5bdb0f43b25858af78999718f7247813802b9634","user":{"login":"Artifizer","id":192502778,"node_id":"U_kgDOC3lb-g","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/192502778?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer","html_url":"https://github.com/Artifizer","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"I believe we do not need both 'type' and 'code', because 'type' can refer to exact GTS code:\n\n```\nExample: \"gts://gts.cf.core.errors.err.v1~a.b.c.my_error.v1\n```","created_at":"2026-01-30T20:39:42Z","updated_at":"2026-01-30T21:23:01Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/290#discussion_r2747915573","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/290","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2747915573"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/290#discussion_r2747915573"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/290"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2747915573/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":null,"original_line":173,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"MEMBER","original_position":173,"position":1,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2747929483","pull_request_review_id":3710446544,"id":2747929483,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs6jyhOL","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,1574 @@\n+# Unified Error System - Intention Document\n+\n+This document defines the architecture, rules, and implementation plan for a unified error handling system across the Hyperspot project. All REST API errors MUST have a GTS identifier, trace ID, and be registered in the types registry.\n+\n+## Table of Contents\n+\n+1. [Executive Summary](#executive-summary)\n+2. [Industry Research](#industry-research)\n+3. [Current State Analysis](#current-state-analysis)\n+4. [Requirements](#requirements)\n+5. [Implementation Rules](#implementation-rules)\n+6. [Migration Plan](#migration-plan)\n+7. [Examples](#examples)\n+8. [HTTP Headers](#http-headers)\n+9. [Security Considerations](#security-considerations)\n+10. [Appendix A: Error Category Definitions](#appendix-a-error-category-definitions)\n+11. [Appendix B: Retryable Error Guidelines](#appendix-b-retryable-error-guidelines)\n+12. [GTS System Errors Catalog](#gts-system-errors-catalog)\n+13. [References](#references)\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Executive Summary\n+\n+### Problem Statement\n+\n+The current error handling across Hyperspot modules is inconsistent:\n+- Some modules use `declare_errors!` macro with JSON catalogs\n+- Others define errors inline without GTS codes\n+- Errors are not registered in the types registry\n+- No standardized metadata/context fields\n+- Inconsistent trace ID propagation\n+\n+### Goals\n+\n+1. **Every REST API error** MUST have a valid GTS identifier\n+2. **Every error response** MUST include a trace ID for debugging\n+3. **All error types** MUST be registered in the types registry\n+4. **Consistent error schema** across all modules following RFC 9457\n+5. **Machine-readable error codes** for programmatic handling\n+6. **Error stack propagation** for nested service calls\n+\n+### Non-Goals\n+\n+- Changing internal domain error types (only API-facing errors)\n+- Modifying logging infrastructure\n+- Changing HTTP status code semantics\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Industry Research\n+\n+### How Major Tech Companies Handle Errors\n+\n+| Company | Standard | Key Features |\n+|---------|----------|--------------|\n+| **Google** | AIP-193 + gRPC Status | `reason` (UPPER_SNAKE_CASE), `domain` (service name), `metadata` (key-value context), `ErrorInfo`, `LocalizedMessage`, `Help` links |\n+| **Amazon AWS** | Custom JSON | `errorType`, `httpStatus`, `requestId`, `message`, custom error object serialization |\n+| **Twitter/X** | JSON with `errors` array | `code` (CAPS_CASE), `message`, `parameter`, `details`, `value` |\n+| **RFC 9457** | Problem Details | `type` (URI), `title`, `status`, `detail`, `instance`, extension members |\n+\n+### Key Patterns Identified\n+\n+1. **Machine-readable identifiers** - Unique codes for programmatic handling (Google's `reason`, Twitter's `code`)\n+2. **Domain/namespace separation** - Identify error source (Google's `domain`, our GTS vendor.package)\n+3. **Structured metadata** - Key-value context without parsing messages (Google's `ErrorInfo.metadata`)\n+4. **Trace/Request IDs** - Correlation for debugging (AWS `requestId`, our `trace_id`)\n+5. **Documentation links** - URIs to error documentation (RFC 9457 `type`, Google's `Help`)\n+6. **Error categorization** - System vs User-defined, Retryable vs Non-retryable\n+\n+### Google AIP-193 ErrorInfo Structure (Reference)\n+\n+```json\n+{\n+  \"error\": {\n+    \"code\": 429,\n+    \"message\": \"The zone 'us-east1-a' does not have enough resources...\",\n+    \"status\": \"RESOURCE_EXHAUSTED\",\n+    \"details\": [\n+      {\n+        \"@type\": \"type.googleapis.com/google.rpc.ErrorInfo\",\n+        \"reason\": \"RESOURCE_AVAILABILITY\",\n+        \"domain\": \"compute.googleapis.com\",\n+        \"metadata\": {\n+          \"zone\": \"us-east1-a\",\n+          \"vmType\": \"e2-medium\"\n+        }\n+      }\n+    ]\n+  }\n+}\n+```\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Current State Analysis\n+\n+### Existing Infrastructure\n+\n+1. **`Problem` struct** (`libs/modkit-errors/src/problem.rs`) - RFC 9457 compliant\n+   - Fields: `type_url`, `title`, `status`, `detail`, `instance`, `code`, `trace_id`, `errors`\n+   - Implements `IntoResponse` for Axum with automatic trace ID enrichment\n+\n+2. **`struct_to_gts_schema` macro** (`modules/types-registry/gts-rust/gts-macros/src/lib.rs`)\n+   - Attribute macro for explicit struct definitions with GTS IDs visible in code\n+   - Generates constants: `GTS_SCHEMA_ID`, `GTS_SCHEMA_JSON`, etc.\n+   - **This pattern will be adapted for error definitions**\n+\n+3. **`declare_errors!` macro** (`libs/modkit-errors-macro/src/lib.rs`) - **TO BE DEPRECATED**\n+   - Generates type-safe error enums from JSON catalogs\n+   - Problem: GTS IDs hidden in external JSON files, not visible to LLMs\n+   - Used by: `users_info` example, `modkit-odata`\n+\n+### Gaps Identified\n+\n+| Gap | Current State | Required State |\n+|-----|---------------|----------------|\n+| **Hidden GTS IDs** | JSON-based `declare_errors!` | Explicit `#[gts_error]` structs with visible GTS IDs |\n+| **Inconsistent definitions** | Some modules use inline errors | All modules use `#[gts_error]` structs |\n+| **No types registry** | Errors not registered | All errors registered as GTS types |\n+| **Missing metadata** | No structured context | Struct fields → `metadata` map |\n+| **Partial trace IDs** | Only in `IntoResponse` | Mandatory in all error responses |\n+| **No error categories** | Flat error codes | System/Operational/Client categories |\n+| **No error stack** | Single error | Upstream error chain propagation |\n+\n+### Current Module Migration Status\n+\n+| Module | Location | Status | Issues |\n+|--------|----------|--------|--------|\n+| **file_parser** | `modules/file_parser/` | 🔴 Not migrated | No GTS IDs, inline `Problem::new()` |\n+| **types-registry** | `modules/system/types-registry/` | 🟡 Partial | Has codes but not GTS format (e.g., `TYPES_REGISTRY_NOT_FOUND`) |\n+| **nodes_registry** | `modules/system/nodes_registry/` | 🔴 Not migrated | Non-GTS codes (e.g., `NODES_NOT_FOUND`) |\n+| **api_gateway** | `modules/system/api_gateway/` | 🔴 Not migrated | No Problem struct, simple error codes |\n+| **tenant_resolver** | `modules/system/tenant_resolver/` | 🔴 Not migrated | No GTS IDs |\n+| **simple-user-settings** | `modules/simple-user-settings/` | 🟡 Partial | Uses `declare_errors!` with old chain format |\n+| **modkit-auth** | `libs/modkit-auth/` | 🔴 Not migrated | No GTS IDs, custom `IntoResponse` |\n+| **modkit-odata** | `libs/modkit-odata/` | 🟡 Partial | Uses `declare_errors!` with old chain format |\n+| **users_info** (example) | `examples/modkit/users_info/` | 🟡 Partial | Uses `declare_errors!` with old chain format |\n+\n+#### Legend\n+- 🟢 **Migrated** - Uses `#[gts_error]` structs with proper base types\n+- 🟡 **Partial** - Has GTS IDs but uses deprecated `declare_errors!` or old format\n+- 🔴 **Not migrated** - No GTS IDs or non-GTS format codes\n+\n+#### GTS ID Format Note\n+\n+**Old chain format** (used by `declare_errors!`):\n+```\n+gts.hx.core.errors.err.v1~hx.module.error_name.v1\n+```\n+\n+**New format** (with `base` field):\n+```\n+gts.hx.module.namespace.error_name.v1~\n+```\n+The `base` field in `#[gts_error]` replaces the chain suffix, making inheritance explicit in code.\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Requirements\n+\n+### R1: Error Schema Requirements\n+\n+Every error returned from REST API MUST conform to the unified schema:\n+\n+```rust\n+pub struct Problem {\n+    // =========================================================================\n+    // REQUIRED FIELDS - Core error identification\n+    // =========================================================================\n+    \n+    /// URI reference identifying the problem type (GTS-based)\n+    /// Example: \"https://docs.hyperspot.com/errors/types_registry_entity_not_found_v1\"\n+    #[serde(rename = \"type\")]\n+    pub type_url: String,\n+    \n+    /// Human-readable summary of the problem type (static per error type)\n+    pub title: String,\n+    \n+    /// GTS error code (machine-readable identifier)\n+    pub code: String,","path":"intended_design/UNIFIED_ERROR_SYSTEM.md","commit_id":"5bdb0f43b25858af78999718f7247813802b9634","original_commit_id":"5bdb0f43b25858af78999718f7247813802b9634","user":{"login":"Artifizer","id":192502778,"node_id":"U_kgDOC3lb-g","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/192502778?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer","html_url":"https://github.com/Artifizer","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"... if we use type, the code is not need anymore","created_at":"2026-01-30T20:44:49Z","updated_at":"2026-01-30T21:23:01Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/290#discussion_r2747929483","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/290","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2747929483"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/290#discussion_r2747929483"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/290"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2747929483/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":null,"original_line":181,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"MEMBER","original_position":181,"position":1,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2747933453","pull_request_review_id":3710446544,"id":2747933453,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs6jyiMN","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,1574 @@\n+# Unified Error System - Intention Document\n+\n+This document defines the architecture, rules, and implementation plan for a unified error handling system across the Hyperspot project. All REST API errors MUST have a GTS identifier, trace ID, and be registered in the types registry.\n+\n+## Table of Contents\n+\n+1. [Executive Summary](#executive-summary)\n+2. [Industry Research](#industry-research)\n+3. [Current State Analysis](#current-state-analysis)\n+4. [Requirements](#requirements)\n+5. [Implementation Rules](#implementation-rules)\n+6. [Migration Plan](#migration-plan)\n+7. [Examples](#examples)\n+8. [HTTP Headers](#http-headers)\n+9. [Security Considerations](#security-considerations)\n+10. [Appendix A: Error Category Definitions](#appendix-a-error-category-definitions)\n+11. [Appendix B: Retryable Error Guidelines](#appendix-b-retryable-error-guidelines)\n+12. [GTS System Errors Catalog](#gts-system-errors-catalog)\n+13. [References](#references)\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Executive Summary\n+\n+### Problem Statement\n+\n+The current error handling across Hyperspot modules is inconsistent:\n+- Some modules use `declare_errors!` macro with JSON catalogs\n+- Others define errors inline without GTS codes\n+- Errors are not registered in the types registry\n+- No standardized metadata/context fields\n+- Inconsistent trace ID propagation\n+\n+### Goals\n+\n+1. **Every REST API error** MUST have a valid GTS identifier\n+2. **Every error response** MUST include a trace ID for debugging\n+3. **All error types** MUST be registered in the types registry\n+4. **Consistent error schema** across all modules following RFC 9457\n+5. **Machine-readable error codes** for programmatic handling\n+6. **Error stack propagation** for nested service calls\n+\n+### Non-Goals\n+\n+- Changing internal domain error types (only API-facing errors)\n+- Modifying logging infrastructure\n+- Changing HTTP status code semantics\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Industry Research\n+\n+### How Major Tech Companies Handle Errors\n+\n+| Company | Standard | Key Features |\n+|---------|----------|--------------|\n+| **Google** | AIP-193 + gRPC Status | `reason` (UPPER_SNAKE_CASE), `domain` (service name), `metadata` (key-value context), `ErrorInfo`, `LocalizedMessage`, `Help` links |\n+| **Amazon AWS** | Custom JSON | `errorType`, `httpStatus`, `requestId`, `message`, custom error object serialization |\n+| **Twitter/X** | JSON with `errors` array | `code` (CAPS_CASE), `message`, `parameter`, `details`, `value` |\n+| **RFC 9457** | Problem Details | `type` (URI), `title`, `status`, `detail`, `instance`, extension members |\n+\n+### Key Patterns Identified\n+\n+1. **Machine-readable identifiers** - Unique codes for programmatic handling (Google's `reason`, Twitter's `code`)\n+2. **Domain/namespace separation** - Identify error source (Google's `domain`, our GTS vendor.package)\n+3. **Structured metadata** - Key-value context without parsing messages (Google's `ErrorInfo.metadata`)\n+4. **Trace/Request IDs** - Correlation for debugging (AWS `requestId`, our `trace_id`)\n+5. **Documentation links** - URIs to error documentation (RFC 9457 `type`, Google's `Help`)\n+6. **Error categorization** - System vs User-defined, Retryable vs Non-retryable\n+\n+### Google AIP-193 ErrorInfo Structure (Reference)\n+\n+```json\n+{\n+  \"error\": {\n+    \"code\": 429,\n+    \"message\": \"The zone 'us-east1-a' does not have enough resources...\",\n+    \"status\": \"RESOURCE_EXHAUSTED\",\n+    \"details\": [\n+      {\n+        \"@type\": \"type.googleapis.com/google.rpc.ErrorInfo\",\n+        \"reason\": \"RESOURCE_AVAILABILITY\",\n+        \"domain\": \"compute.googleapis.com\",\n+        \"metadata\": {\n+          \"zone\": \"us-east1-a\",\n+          \"vmType\": \"e2-medium\"\n+        }\n+      }\n+    ]\n+  }\n+}\n+```\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Current State Analysis\n+\n+### Existing Infrastructure\n+\n+1. **`Problem` struct** (`libs/modkit-errors/src/problem.rs`) - RFC 9457 compliant\n+   - Fields: `type_url`, `title`, `status`, `detail`, `instance`, `code`, `trace_id`, `errors`\n+   - Implements `IntoResponse` for Axum with automatic trace ID enrichment\n+\n+2. **`struct_to_gts_schema` macro** (`modules/types-registry/gts-rust/gts-macros/src/lib.rs`)\n+   - Attribute macro for explicit struct definitions with GTS IDs visible in code\n+   - Generates constants: `GTS_SCHEMA_ID`, `GTS_SCHEMA_JSON`, etc.\n+   - **This pattern will be adapted for error definitions**\n+\n+3. **`declare_errors!` macro** (`libs/modkit-errors-macro/src/lib.rs`) - **TO BE DEPRECATED**\n+   - Generates type-safe error enums from JSON catalogs\n+   - Problem: GTS IDs hidden in external JSON files, not visible to LLMs\n+   - Used by: `users_info` example, `modkit-odata`\n+\n+### Gaps Identified\n+\n+| Gap | Current State | Required State |\n+|-----|---------------|----------------|\n+| **Hidden GTS IDs** | JSON-based `declare_errors!` | Explicit `#[gts_error]` structs with visible GTS IDs |\n+| **Inconsistent definitions** | Some modules use inline errors | All modules use `#[gts_error]` structs |\n+| **No types registry** | Errors not registered | All errors registered as GTS types |\n+| **Missing metadata** | No structured context | Struct fields → `metadata` map |\n+| **Partial trace IDs** | Only in `IntoResponse` | Mandatory in all error responses |\n+| **No error categories** | Flat error codes | System/Operational/Client categories |\n+| **No error stack** | Single error | Upstream error chain propagation |\n+\n+### Current Module Migration Status\n+\n+| Module | Location | Status | Issues |\n+|--------|----------|--------|--------|\n+| **file_parser** | `modules/file_parser/` | 🔴 Not migrated | No GTS IDs, inline `Problem::new()` |\n+| **types-registry** | `modules/system/types-registry/` | 🟡 Partial | Has codes but not GTS format (e.g., `TYPES_REGISTRY_NOT_FOUND`) |\n+| **nodes_registry** | `modules/system/nodes_registry/` | 🔴 Not migrated | Non-GTS codes (e.g., `NODES_NOT_FOUND`) |\n+| **api_gateway** | `modules/system/api_gateway/` | 🔴 Not migrated | No Problem struct, simple error codes |\n+| **tenant_resolver** | `modules/system/tenant_resolver/` | 🔴 Not migrated | No GTS IDs |\n+| **simple-user-settings** | `modules/simple-user-settings/` | 🟡 Partial | Uses `declare_errors!` with old chain format |\n+| **modkit-auth** | `libs/modkit-auth/` | 🔴 Not migrated | No GTS IDs, custom `IntoResponse` |\n+| **modkit-odata** | `libs/modkit-odata/` | 🟡 Partial | Uses `declare_errors!` with old chain format |\n+| **users_info** (example) | `examples/modkit/users_info/` | 🟡 Partial | Uses `declare_errors!` with old chain format |\n+\n+#### Legend\n+- 🟢 **Migrated** - Uses `#[gts_error]` structs with proper base types\n+- 🟡 **Partial** - Has GTS IDs but uses deprecated `declare_errors!` or old format\n+- 🔴 **Not migrated** - No GTS IDs or non-GTS format codes\n+\n+#### GTS ID Format Note\n+\n+**Old chain format** (used by `declare_errors!`):\n+```\n+gts.hx.core.errors.err.v1~hx.module.error_name.v1\n+```\n+\n+**New format** (with `base` field):\n+```\n+gts.hx.module.namespace.error_name.v1~\n+```\n+The `base` field in `#[gts_error]` replaces the chain suffix, making inheritance explicit in code.\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Requirements\n+\n+### R1: Error Schema Requirements\n+\n+Every error returned from REST API MUST conform to the unified schema:\n+\n+```rust\n+pub struct Problem {\n+    // =========================================================================\n+    // REQUIRED FIELDS - Core error identification\n+    // =========================================================================\n+    \n+    /// URI reference identifying the problem type (GTS-based)\n+    /// Example: \"https://docs.hyperspot.com/errors/types_registry_entity_not_found_v1\"\n+    #[serde(rename = \"type\")]\n+    pub type_url: String,\n+    \n+    /// Human-readable summary of the problem type (static per error type)\n+    pub title: String,\n+    \n+    /// GTS error code (machine-readable identifier)\n+    pub code: String,\n+    \n+    /// Trace ID for request correlation\n+    pub trace_id: String,\n+    \n+    // =========================================================================\n+    // CONTEXTUAL FIELDS - Optional based on error context\n+    // =========================================================================\n+    \n+    /// HTTP status code. Optional because:\n+    /// - gRPC errors use different status codes\n+    /// - Internal/domain errors may not have HTTP context\n+    /// - Event-driven systems have no request/response\n+    /// When serializing for HTTP response, this is populated from error definition.\n+    #[serde(skip_serializing_if = \"Option::is_none\")]\n+    pub status: Option<u16>,\n+    \n+    /// Human-readable explanation specific to this occurrence.\n+    /// Optional - title may be sufficient for simple errors.\n+    #[serde(skip_serializing_if = \"Option::is_none\")]\n+    pub detail: Option<String>,\n+    \n+    /// Error category for client handling.\n+    /// Optional - can be inferred from base type hierarchy.\n+    #[serde(skip_serializing_if = \"Option::is_none\")]\n+    pub category: Option<ErrorCategory>,\n+    \n+    /// Whether client can retry this request.\n+    /// Optional - can be inferred from base type; not relevant for all contexts.\n+    #[serde(skip_serializing_if = \"Option::is_none\")]\n+    pub retryable: Option<bool>,","path":"intended_design/UNIFIED_ERROR_SYSTEM.md","commit_id":"5bdb0f43b25858af78999718f7247813802b9634","original_commit_id":"5bdb0f43b25858af78999718f7247813802b9634","user":{"login":"Artifizer","id":192502778,"node_id":"U_kgDOC3lb-g","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/192502778?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer","html_url":"https://github.com/Artifizer","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Well, technically it's advisory only, and clients can technically retry whatever error (not just 5xx, but even 404 if object has not been created yet....). So I'd just remove it","created_at":"2026-01-30T20:46:37Z","updated_at":"2026-01-30T21:23:01Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/290#discussion_r2747933453","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/290","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2747933453"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/290#discussion_r2747933453"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/290"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2747933453/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":null,"original_line":211,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"MEMBER","original_position":211,"position":1,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2747943818","pull_request_review_id":3710446544,"id":2747943818,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs6jykuK","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,1574 @@\n+# Unified Error System - Intention Document\n+\n+This document defines the architecture, rules, and implementation plan for a unified error handling system across the Hyperspot project. All REST API errors MUST have a GTS identifier, trace ID, and be registered in the types registry.\n+\n+## Table of Contents\n+\n+1. [Executive Summary](#executive-summary)\n+2. [Industry Research](#industry-research)\n+3. [Current State Analysis](#current-state-analysis)\n+4. [Requirements](#requirements)\n+5. [Implementation Rules](#implementation-rules)\n+6. [Migration Plan](#migration-plan)\n+7. [Examples](#examples)\n+8. [HTTP Headers](#http-headers)\n+9. [Security Considerations](#security-considerations)\n+10. [Appendix A: Error Category Definitions](#appendix-a-error-category-definitions)\n+11. [Appendix B: Retryable Error Guidelines](#appendix-b-retryable-error-guidelines)\n+12. [GTS System Errors Catalog](#gts-system-errors-catalog)\n+13. [References](#references)\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Executive Summary\n+\n+### Problem Statement\n+\n+The current error handling across Hyperspot modules is inconsistent:\n+- Some modules use `declare_errors!` macro with JSON catalogs\n+- Others define errors inline without GTS codes\n+- Errors are not registered in the types registry\n+- No standardized metadata/context fields\n+- Inconsistent trace ID propagation\n+\n+### Goals\n+\n+1. **Every REST API error** MUST have a valid GTS identifier\n+2. **Every error response** MUST include a trace ID for debugging\n+3. **All error types** MUST be registered in the types registry\n+4. **Consistent error schema** across all modules following RFC 9457\n+5. **Machine-readable error codes** for programmatic handling\n+6. **Error stack propagation** for nested service calls\n+\n+### Non-Goals\n+\n+- Changing internal domain error types (only API-facing errors)\n+- Modifying logging infrastructure\n+- Changing HTTP status code semantics\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Industry Research\n+\n+### How Major Tech Companies Handle Errors\n+\n+| Company | Standard | Key Features |\n+|---------|----------|--------------|\n+| **Google** | AIP-193 + gRPC Status | `reason` (UPPER_SNAKE_CASE), `domain` (service name), `metadata` (key-value context), `ErrorInfo`, `LocalizedMessage`, `Help` links |\n+| **Amazon AWS** | Custom JSON | `errorType`, `httpStatus`, `requestId`, `message`, custom error object serialization |\n+| **Twitter/X** | JSON with `errors` array | `code` (CAPS_CASE), `message`, `parameter`, `details`, `value` |\n+| **RFC 9457** | Problem Details | `type` (URI), `title`, `status`, `detail`, `instance`, extension members |\n+\n+### Key Patterns Identified\n+\n+1. **Machine-readable identifiers** - Unique codes for programmatic handling (Google's `reason`, Twitter's `code`)\n+2. **Domain/namespace separation** - Identify error source (Google's `domain`, our GTS vendor.package)\n+3. **Structured metadata** - Key-value context without parsing messages (Google's `ErrorInfo.metadata`)\n+4. **Trace/Request IDs** - Correlation for debugging (AWS `requestId`, our `trace_id`)\n+5. **Documentation links** - URIs to error documentation (RFC 9457 `type`, Google's `Help`)\n+6. **Error categorization** - System vs User-defined, Retryable vs Non-retryable\n+\n+### Google AIP-193 ErrorInfo Structure (Reference)\n+\n+```json\n+{\n+  \"error\": {\n+    \"code\": 429,\n+    \"message\": \"The zone 'us-east1-a' does not have enough resources...\",\n+    \"status\": \"RESOURCE_EXHAUSTED\",\n+    \"details\": [\n+      {\n+        \"@type\": \"type.googleapis.com/google.rpc.ErrorInfo\",\n+        \"reason\": \"RESOURCE_AVAILABILITY\",\n+        \"domain\": \"compute.googleapis.com\",\n+        \"metadata\": {\n+          \"zone\": \"us-east1-a\",\n+          \"vmType\": \"e2-medium\"\n+        }\n+      }\n+    ]\n+  }\n+}\n+```\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Current State Analysis\n+\n+### Existing Infrastructure\n+\n+1. **`Problem` struct** (`libs/modkit-errors/src/problem.rs`) - RFC 9457 compliant\n+   - Fields: `type_url`, `title`, `status`, `detail`, `instance`, `code`, `trace_id`, `errors`\n+   - Implements `IntoResponse` for Axum with automatic trace ID enrichment\n+\n+2. **`struct_to_gts_schema` macro** (`modules/types-registry/gts-rust/gts-macros/src/lib.rs`)\n+   - Attribute macro for explicit struct definitions with GTS IDs visible in code\n+   - Generates constants: `GTS_SCHEMA_ID`, `GTS_SCHEMA_JSON`, etc.\n+   - **This pattern will be adapted for error definitions**\n+\n+3. **`declare_errors!` macro** (`libs/modkit-errors-macro/src/lib.rs`) - **TO BE DEPRECATED**\n+   - Generates type-safe error enums from JSON catalogs\n+   - Problem: GTS IDs hidden in external JSON files, not visible to LLMs\n+   - Used by: `users_info` example, `modkit-odata`\n+\n+### Gaps Identified\n+\n+| Gap | Current State | Required State |\n+|-----|---------------|----------------|\n+| **Hidden GTS IDs** | JSON-based `declare_errors!` | Explicit `#[gts_error]` structs with visible GTS IDs |\n+| **Inconsistent definitions** | Some modules use inline errors | All modules use `#[gts_error]` structs |\n+| **No types registry** | Errors not registered | All errors registered as GTS types |\n+| **Missing metadata** | No structured context | Struct fields → `metadata` map |\n+| **Partial trace IDs** | Only in `IntoResponse` | Mandatory in all error responses |\n+| **No error categories** | Flat error codes | System/Operational/Client categories |\n+| **No error stack** | Single error | Upstream error chain propagation |\n+\n+### Current Module Migration Status\n+\n+| Module | Location | Status | Issues |\n+|--------|----------|--------|--------|\n+| **file_parser** | `modules/file_parser/` | 🔴 Not migrated | No GTS IDs, inline `Problem::new()` |\n+| **types-registry** | `modules/system/types-registry/` | 🟡 Partial | Has codes but not GTS format (e.g., `TYPES_REGISTRY_NOT_FOUND`) |\n+| **nodes_registry** | `modules/system/nodes_registry/` | 🔴 Not migrated | Non-GTS codes (e.g., `NODES_NOT_FOUND`) |\n+| **api_gateway** | `modules/system/api_gateway/` | 🔴 Not migrated | No Problem struct, simple error codes |\n+| **tenant_resolver** | `modules/system/tenant_resolver/` | 🔴 Not migrated | No GTS IDs |\n+| **simple-user-settings** | `modules/simple-user-settings/` | 🟡 Partial | Uses `declare_errors!` with old chain format |\n+| **modkit-auth** | `libs/modkit-auth/` | 🔴 Not migrated | No GTS IDs, custom `IntoResponse` |\n+| **modkit-odata** | `libs/modkit-odata/` | 🟡 Partial | Uses `declare_errors!` with old chain format |\n+| **users_info** (example) | `examples/modkit/users_info/` | 🟡 Partial | Uses `declare_errors!` with old chain format |\n+\n+#### Legend\n+- 🟢 **Migrated** - Uses `#[gts_error]` structs with proper base types\n+- 🟡 **Partial** - Has GTS IDs but uses deprecated `declare_errors!` or old format\n+- 🔴 **Not migrated** - No GTS IDs or non-GTS format codes\n+\n+#### GTS ID Format Note\n+\n+**Old chain format** (used by `declare_errors!`):\n+```\n+gts.hx.core.errors.err.v1~hx.module.error_name.v1\n+```\n+\n+**New format** (with `base` field):\n+```\n+gts.hx.module.namespace.error_name.v1~\n+```\n+The `base` field in `#[gts_error]` replaces the chain suffix, making inheritance explicit in code.\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Requirements\n+\n+### R1: Error Schema Requirements\n+\n+Every error returned from REST API MUST conform to the unified schema:\n+\n+```rust\n+pub struct Problem {\n+    // =========================================================================\n+    // REQUIRED FIELDS - Core error identification\n+    // =========================================================================\n+    \n+    /// URI reference identifying the problem type (GTS-based)\n+    /// Example: \"https://docs.hyperspot.com/errors/types_registry_entity_not_found_v1\"\n+    #[serde(rename = \"type\")]\n+    pub type_url: String,\n+    \n+    /// Human-readable summary of the problem type (static per error type)\n+    pub title: String,\n+    \n+    /// GTS error code (machine-readable identifier)\n+    pub code: String,\n+    \n+    /// Trace ID for request correlation\n+    pub trace_id: String,\n+    \n+    // =========================================================================\n+    // CONTEXTUAL FIELDS - Optional based on error context\n+    // =========================================================================\n+    \n+    /// HTTP status code. Optional because:\n+    /// - gRPC errors use different status codes\n+    /// - Internal/domain errors may not have HTTP context\n+    /// - Event-driven systems have no request/response\n+    /// When serializing for HTTP response, this is populated from error definition.\n+    #[serde(skip_serializing_if = \"Option::is_none\")]\n+    pub status: Option<u16>,","path":"intended_design/UNIFIED_ERROR_SYSTEM.md","commit_id":"5bdb0f43b25858af78999718f7247813802b9634","original_commit_id":"5bdb0f43b25858af78999718f7247813802b9634","user":{"login":"Artifizer","id":192502778,"node_id":"U_kgDOC3lb-g","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/192502778?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer","html_url":"https://github.com/Artifizer","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"I believe it must be:\n\n```\npub status: Option<HttpStatusCode>\n```\n\ninstead of raw u16. Even if serialized as number.\nThis prevents invalid values (999, 42, etc).","created_at":"2026-01-30T20:50:50Z","updated_at":"2026-01-30T21:23:01Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/290#discussion_r2747943818","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/290","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2747943818"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/290#discussion_r2747943818"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/290"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2747943818/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":null,"original_line":196,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"MEMBER","original_position":196,"position":1,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2747949318","pull_request_review_id":3710446544,"id":2747949318,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs6jymEG","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,1574 @@\n+# Unified Error System - Intention Document\n+\n+This document defines the architecture, rules, and implementation plan for a unified error handling system across the Hyperspot project. All REST API errors MUST have a GTS identifier, trace ID, and be registered in the types registry.\n+\n+## Table of Contents\n+\n+1. [Executive Summary](#executive-summary)\n+2. [Industry Research](#industry-research)\n+3. [Current State Analysis](#current-state-analysis)\n+4. [Requirements](#requirements)\n+5. [Implementation Rules](#implementation-rules)\n+6. [Migration Plan](#migration-plan)\n+7. [Examples](#examples)\n+8. [HTTP Headers](#http-headers)\n+9. [Security Considerations](#security-considerations)\n+10. [Appendix A: Error Category Definitions](#appendix-a-error-category-definitions)\n+11. [Appendix B: Retryable Error Guidelines](#appendix-b-retryable-error-guidelines)\n+12. [GTS System Errors Catalog](#gts-system-errors-catalog)\n+13. [References](#references)\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Executive Summary\n+\n+### Problem Statement\n+\n+The current error handling across Hyperspot modules is inconsistent:\n+- Some modules use `declare_errors!` macro with JSON catalogs\n+- Others define errors inline without GTS codes\n+- Errors are not registered in the types registry\n+- No standardized metadata/context fields\n+- Inconsistent trace ID propagation\n+\n+### Goals\n+\n+1. **Every REST API error** MUST have a valid GTS identifier\n+2. **Every error response** MUST include a trace ID for debugging\n+3. **All error types** MUST be registered in the types registry\n+4. **Consistent error schema** across all modules following RFC 9457\n+5. **Machine-readable error codes** for programmatic handling\n+6. **Error stack propagation** for nested service calls\n+\n+### Non-Goals\n+\n+- Changing internal domain error types (only API-facing errors)\n+- Modifying logging infrastructure\n+- Changing HTTP status code semantics\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Industry Research\n+\n+### How Major Tech Companies Handle Errors\n+\n+| Company | Standard | Key Features |\n+|---------|----------|--------------|\n+| **Google** | AIP-193 + gRPC Status | `reason` (UPPER_SNAKE_CASE), `domain` (service name), `metadata` (key-value context), `ErrorInfo`, `LocalizedMessage`, `Help` links |\n+| **Amazon AWS** | Custom JSON | `errorType`, `httpStatus`, `requestId`, `message`, custom error object serialization |\n+| **Twitter/X** | JSON with `errors` array | `code` (CAPS_CASE), `message`, `parameter`, `details`, `value` |\n+| **RFC 9457** | Problem Details | `type` (URI), `title`, `status`, `detail`, `instance`, extension members |\n+\n+### Key Patterns Identified\n+\n+1. **Machine-readable identifiers** - Unique codes for programmatic handling (Google's `reason`, Twitter's `code`)\n+2. **Domain/namespace separation** - Identify error source (Google's `domain`, our GTS vendor.package)\n+3. **Structured metadata** - Key-value context without parsing messages (Google's `ErrorInfo.metadata`)\n+4. **Trace/Request IDs** - Correlation for debugging (AWS `requestId`, our `trace_id`)\n+5. **Documentation links** - URIs to error documentation (RFC 9457 `type`, Google's `Help`)\n+6. **Error categorization** - System vs User-defined, Retryable vs Non-retryable\n+\n+### Google AIP-193 ErrorInfo Structure (Reference)\n+\n+```json\n+{\n+  \"error\": {\n+    \"code\": 429,\n+    \"message\": \"The zone 'us-east1-a' does not have enough resources...\",\n+    \"status\": \"RESOURCE_EXHAUSTED\",\n+    \"details\": [\n+      {\n+        \"@type\": \"type.googleapis.com/google.rpc.ErrorInfo\",\n+        \"reason\": \"RESOURCE_AVAILABILITY\",\n+        \"domain\": \"compute.googleapis.com\",\n+        \"metadata\": {\n+          \"zone\": \"us-east1-a\",\n+          \"vmType\": \"e2-medium\"\n+        }\n+      }\n+    ]\n+  }\n+}\n+```\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Current State Analysis\n+\n+### Existing Infrastructure\n+\n+1. **`Problem` struct** (`libs/modkit-errors/src/problem.rs`) - RFC 9457 compliant\n+   - Fields: `type_url`, `title`, `status`, `detail`, `instance`, `code`, `trace_id`, `errors`\n+   - Implements `IntoResponse` for Axum with automatic trace ID enrichment\n+\n+2. **`struct_to_gts_schema` macro** (`modules/types-registry/gts-rust/gts-macros/src/lib.rs`)\n+   - Attribute macro for explicit struct definitions with GTS IDs visible in code\n+   - Generates constants: `GTS_SCHEMA_ID`, `GTS_SCHEMA_JSON`, etc.\n+   - **This pattern will be adapted for error definitions**\n+\n+3. **`declare_errors!` macro** (`libs/modkit-errors-macro/src/lib.rs`) - **TO BE DEPRECATED**\n+   - Generates type-safe error enums from JSON catalogs\n+   - Problem: GTS IDs hidden in external JSON files, not visible to LLMs\n+   - Used by: `users_info` example, `modkit-odata`\n+\n+### Gaps Identified\n+\n+| Gap | Current State | Required State |\n+|-----|---------------|----------------|\n+| **Hidden GTS IDs** | JSON-based `declare_errors!` | Explicit `#[gts_error]` structs with visible GTS IDs |\n+| **Inconsistent definitions** | Some modules use inline errors | All modules use `#[gts_error]` structs |\n+| **No types registry** | Errors not registered | All errors registered as GTS types |\n+| **Missing metadata** | No structured context | Struct fields → `metadata` map |\n+| **Partial trace IDs** | Only in `IntoResponse` | Mandatory in all error responses |\n+| **No error categories** | Flat error codes | System/Operational/Client categories |\n+| **No error stack** | Single error | Upstream error chain propagation |\n+\n+### Current Module Migration Status\n+\n+| Module | Location | Status | Issues |\n+|--------|----------|--------|--------|\n+| **file_parser** | `modules/file_parser/` | 🔴 Not migrated | No GTS IDs, inline `Problem::new()` |\n+| **types-registry** | `modules/system/types-registry/` | 🟡 Partial | Has codes but not GTS format (e.g., `TYPES_REGISTRY_NOT_FOUND`) |\n+| **nodes_registry** | `modules/system/nodes_registry/` | 🔴 Not migrated | Non-GTS codes (e.g., `NODES_NOT_FOUND`) |\n+| **api_gateway** | `modules/system/api_gateway/` | 🔴 Not migrated | No Problem struct, simple error codes |\n+| **tenant_resolver** | `modules/system/tenant_resolver/` | 🔴 Not migrated | No GTS IDs |\n+| **simple-user-settings** | `modules/simple-user-settings/` | 🟡 Partial | Uses `declare_errors!` with old chain format |\n+| **modkit-auth** | `libs/modkit-auth/` | 🔴 Not migrated | No GTS IDs, custom `IntoResponse` |\n+| **modkit-odata** | `libs/modkit-odata/` | 🟡 Partial | Uses `declare_errors!` with old chain format |\n+| **users_info** (example) | `examples/modkit/users_info/` | 🟡 Partial | Uses `declare_errors!` with old chain format |\n+\n+#### Legend\n+- 🟢 **Migrated** - Uses `#[gts_error]` structs with proper base types\n+- 🟡 **Partial** - Has GTS IDs but uses deprecated `declare_errors!` or old format\n+- 🔴 **Not migrated** - No GTS IDs or non-GTS format codes\n+\n+#### GTS ID Format Note\n+\n+**Old chain format** (used by `declare_errors!`):\n+```\n+gts.hx.core.errors.err.v1~hx.module.error_name.v1\n+```\n+\n+**New format** (with `base` field):\n+```\n+gts.hx.module.namespace.error_name.v1~\n+```\n+The `base` field in `#[gts_error]` replaces the chain suffix, making inheritance explicit in code.\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Requirements\n+\n+### R1: Error Schema Requirements\n+\n+Every error returned from REST API MUST conform to the unified schema:\n+\n+```rust\n+pub struct Problem {\n+    // =========================================================================\n+    // REQUIRED FIELDS - Core error identification\n+    // =========================================================================\n+    \n+    /// URI reference identifying the problem type (GTS-based)\n+    /// Example: \"https://docs.hyperspot.com/errors/types_registry_entity_not_found_v1\"\n+    #[serde(rename = \"type\")]\n+    pub type_url: String,\n+    \n+    /// Human-readable summary of the problem type (static per error type)\n+    pub title: String,\n+    \n+    /// GTS error code (machine-readable identifier)\n+    pub code: String,\n+    \n+    /// Trace ID for request correlation\n+    pub trace_id: String,\n+    \n+    // =========================================================================\n+    // CONTEXTUAL FIELDS - Optional based on error context\n+    // =========================================================================\n+    \n+    /// HTTP status code. Optional because:\n+    /// - gRPC errors use different status codes\n+    /// - Internal/domain errors may not have HTTP context\n+    /// - Event-driven systems have no request/response\n+    /// When serializing for HTTP response, this is populated from error definition.\n+    #[serde(skip_serializing_if = \"Option::is_none\")]\n+    pub status: Option<u16>,\n+    \n+    /// Human-readable explanation specific to this occurrence.\n+    /// Optional - title may be sufficient for simple errors.\n+    #[serde(skip_serializing_if = \"Option::is_none\")]\n+    pub detail: Option<String>,","path":"intended_design/UNIFIED_ERROR_SYSTEM.md","commit_id":"5bdb0f43b25858af78999718f7247813802b9634","original_commit_id":"5bdb0f43b25858af78999718f7247813802b9634","user":{"login":"Artifizer","id":192502778,"node_id":"U_kgDOC3lb-g","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/192502778?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer","html_url":"https://github.com/Artifizer","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"This field is dangerous.\n\nNot wrong — but easy to misuse. Typical failures -developers put:\n- exception messages\n- SQL errors\n- stack traces\n- filesystem paths\n- internal hostnames\n\nIt's better to document restrictions clearly and then have some secrets sanitization in the middleware","created_at":"2026-01-30T20:52:58Z","updated_at":"2026-01-30T21:23:01Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/290#discussion_r2747949318","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/290","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2747949318"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/290#discussion_r2747949318"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/290"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2747949318/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":null,"original_line":201,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"MEMBER","original_position":201,"position":1,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2747962213","pull_request_review_id":3710446544,"id":2747962213,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs6jypNl","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,1574 @@\n+# Unified Error System - Intention Document\n+\n+This document defines the architecture, rules, and implementation plan for a unified error handling system across the Hyperspot project. All REST API errors MUST have a GTS identifier, trace ID, and be registered in the types registry.\n+\n+## Table of Contents\n+\n+1. [Executive Summary](#executive-summary)\n+2. [Industry Research](#industry-research)\n+3. [Current State Analysis](#current-state-analysis)\n+4. [Requirements](#requirements)\n+5. [Implementation Rules](#implementation-rules)\n+6. [Migration Plan](#migration-plan)\n+7. [Examples](#examples)\n+8. [HTTP Headers](#http-headers)\n+9. [Security Considerations](#security-considerations)\n+10. [Appendix A: Error Category Definitions](#appendix-a-error-category-definitions)\n+11. [Appendix B: Retryable Error Guidelines](#appendix-b-retryable-error-guidelines)\n+12. [GTS System Errors Catalog](#gts-system-errors-catalog)\n+13. [References](#references)\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Executive Summary\n+\n+### Problem Statement\n+\n+The current error handling across Hyperspot modules is inconsistent:\n+- Some modules use `declare_errors!` macro with JSON catalogs\n+- Others define errors inline without GTS codes\n+- Errors are not registered in the types registry\n+- No standardized metadata/context fields\n+- Inconsistent trace ID propagation\n+\n+### Goals\n+\n+1. **Every REST API error** MUST have a valid GTS identifier\n+2. **Every error response** MUST include a trace ID for debugging\n+3. **All error types** MUST be registered in the types registry\n+4. **Consistent error schema** across all modules following RFC 9457\n+5. **Machine-readable error codes** for programmatic handling\n+6. **Error stack propagation** for nested service calls\n+\n+### Non-Goals\n+\n+- Changing internal domain error types (only API-facing errors)\n+- Modifying logging infrastructure\n+- Changing HTTP status code semantics\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Industry Research\n+\n+### How Major Tech Companies Handle Errors\n+\n+| Company | Standard | Key Features |\n+|---------|----------|--------------|\n+| **Google** | AIP-193 + gRPC Status | `reason` (UPPER_SNAKE_CASE), `domain` (service name), `metadata` (key-value context), `ErrorInfo`, `LocalizedMessage`, `Help` links |\n+| **Amazon AWS** | Custom JSON | `errorType`, `httpStatus`, `requestId`, `message`, custom error object serialization |\n+| **Twitter/X** | JSON with `errors` array | `code` (CAPS_CASE), `message`, `parameter`, `details`, `value` |\n+| **RFC 9457** | Problem Details | `type` (URI), `title`, `status`, `detail`, `instance`, extension members |\n+\n+### Key Patterns Identified\n+\n+1. **Machine-readable identifiers** - Unique codes for programmatic handling (Google's `reason`, Twitter's `code`)\n+2. **Domain/namespace separation** - Identify error source (Google's `domain`, our GTS vendor.package)\n+3. **Structured metadata** - Key-value context without parsing messages (Google's `ErrorInfo.metadata`)\n+4. **Trace/Request IDs** - Correlation for debugging (AWS `requestId`, our `trace_id`)\n+5. **Documentation links** - URIs to error documentation (RFC 9457 `type`, Google's `Help`)\n+6. **Error categorization** - System vs User-defined, Retryable vs Non-retryable\n+\n+### Google AIP-193 ErrorInfo Structure (Reference)\n+\n+```json\n+{\n+  \"error\": {\n+    \"code\": 429,\n+    \"message\": \"The zone 'us-east1-a' does not have enough resources...\",\n+    \"status\": \"RESOURCE_EXHAUSTED\",\n+    \"details\": [\n+      {\n+        \"@type\": \"type.googleapis.com/google.rpc.ErrorInfo\",\n+        \"reason\": \"RESOURCE_AVAILABILITY\",\n+        \"domain\": \"compute.googleapis.com\",\n+        \"metadata\": {\n+          \"zone\": \"us-east1-a\",\n+          \"vmType\": \"e2-medium\"\n+        }\n+      }\n+    ]\n+  }\n+}\n+```\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Current State Analysis\n+\n+### Existing Infrastructure\n+\n+1. **`Problem` struct** (`libs/modkit-errors/src/problem.rs`) - RFC 9457 compliant\n+   - Fields: `type_url`, `title`, `status`, `detail`, `instance`, `code`, `trace_id`, `errors`\n+   - Implements `IntoResponse` for Axum with automatic trace ID enrichment\n+\n+2. **`struct_to_gts_schema` macro** (`modules/types-registry/gts-rust/gts-macros/src/lib.rs`)\n+   - Attribute macro for explicit struct definitions with GTS IDs visible in code\n+   - Generates constants: `GTS_SCHEMA_ID`, `GTS_SCHEMA_JSON`, etc.\n+   - **This pattern will be adapted for error definitions**\n+\n+3. **`declare_errors!` macro** (`libs/modkit-errors-macro/src/lib.rs`) - **TO BE DEPRECATED**\n+   - Generates type-safe error enums from JSON catalogs\n+   - Problem: GTS IDs hidden in external JSON files, not visible to LLMs\n+   - Used by: `users_info` example, `modkit-odata`\n+\n+### Gaps Identified\n+\n+| Gap | Current State | Required State |\n+|-----|---------------|----------------|\n+| **Hidden GTS IDs** | JSON-based `declare_errors!` | Explicit `#[gts_error]` structs with visible GTS IDs |\n+| **Inconsistent definitions** | Some modules use inline errors | All modules use `#[gts_error]` structs |\n+| **No types registry** | Errors not registered | All errors registered as GTS types |\n+| **Missing metadata** | No structured context | Struct fields → `metadata` map |\n+| **Partial trace IDs** | Only in `IntoResponse` | Mandatory in all error responses |\n+| **No error categories** | Flat error codes | System/Operational/Client categories |\n+| **No error stack** | Single error | Upstream error chain propagation |\n+\n+### Current Module Migration Status\n+\n+| Module | Location | Status | Issues |\n+|--------|----------|--------|--------|\n+| **file_parser** | `modules/file_parser/` | 🔴 Not migrated | No GTS IDs, inline `Problem::new()` |\n+| **types-registry** | `modules/system/types-registry/` | 🟡 Partial | Has codes but not GTS format (e.g., `TYPES_REGISTRY_NOT_FOUND`) |\n+| **nodes_registry** | `modules/system/nodes_registry/` | 🔴 Not migrated | Non-GTS codes (e.g., `NODES_NOT_FOUND`) |\n+| **api_gateway** | `modules/system/api_gateway/` | 🔴 Not migrated | No Problem struct, simple error codes |\n+| **tenant_resolver** | `modules/system/tenant_resolver/` | 🔴 Not migrated | No GTS IDs |\n+| **simple-user-settings** | `modules/simple-user-settings/` | 🟡 Partial | Uses `declare_errors!` with old chain format |\n+| **modkit-auth** | `libs/modkit-auth/` | 🔴 Not migrated | No GTS IDs, custom `IntoResponse` |\n+| **modkit-odata** | `libs/modkit-odata/` | 🟡 Partial | Uses `declare_errors!` with old chain format |\n+| **users_info** (example) | `examples/modkit/users_info/` | 🟡 Partial | Uses `declare_errors!` with old chain format |\n+\n+#### Legend\n+- 🟢 **Migrated** - Uses `#[gts_error]` structs with proper base types\n+- 🟡 **Partial** - Has GTS IDs but uses deprecated `declare_errors!` or old format\n+- 🔴 **Not migrated** - No GTS IDs or non-GTS format codes\n+\n+#### GTS ID Format Note\n+\n+**Old chain format** (used by `declare_errors!`):\n+```\n+gts.hx.core.errors.err.v1~hx.module.error_name.v1\n+```\n+\n+**New format** (with `base` field):\n+```\n+gts.hx.module.namespace.error_name.v1~\n+```\n+The `base` field in `#[gts_error]` replaces the chain suffix, making inheritance explicit in code.\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Requirements\n+\n+### R1: Error Schema Requirements\n+\n+Every error returned from REST API MUST conform to the unified schema:\n+\n+```rust\n+pub struct Problem {\n+    // =========================================================================\n+    // REQUIRED FIELDS - Core error identification\n+    // =========================================================================\n+    \n+    /// URI reference identifying the problem type (GTS-based)\n+    /// Example: \"https://docs.hyperspot.com/errors/types_registry_entity_not_found_v1\"\n+    #[serde(rename = \"type\")]\n+    pub type_url: String,\n+    \n+    /// Human-readable summary of the problem type (static per error type)\n+    pub title: String,\n+    \n+    /// GTS error code (machine-readable identifier)\n+    pub code: String,\n+    \n+    /// Trace ID for request correlation\n+    pub trace_id: String,\n+    \n+    // =========================================================================\n+    // CONTEXTUAL FIELDS - Optional based on error context\n+    // =========================================================================\n+    \n+    /// HTTP status code. Optional because:\n+    /// - gRPC errors use different status codes\n+    /// - Internal/domain errors may not have HTTP context\n+    /// - Event-driven systems have no request/response\n+    /// When serializing for HTTP response, this is populated from error definition.\n+    #[serde(skip_serializing_if = \"Option::is_none\")]\n+    pub status: Option<u16>,\n+    \n+    /// Human-readable explanation specific to this occurrence.\n+    /// Optional - title may be sufficient for simple errors.\n+    #[serde(skip_serializing_if = \"Option::is_none\")]\n+    pub detail: Option<String>,\n+    \n+    /// Error category for client handling.\n+    /// Optional - can be inferred from base type hierarchy.\n+    #[serde(skip_serializing_if = \"Option::is_none\")]\n+    pub category: Option<ErrorCategory>,\n+    \n+    /// Whether client can retry this request.\n+    /// Optional - can be inferred from base type; not relevant for all contexts.\n+    #[serde(skip_serializing_if = \"Option::is_none\")]\n+    pub retryable: Option<bool>,\n+    \n+    /// URI identifying this specific occurrence (auto-populated from request path)\n+    #[serde(skip_serializing_if = \"Option::is_none\")]\n+    pub instance: Option<String>,\n+    \n+    /// Structured metadata (key-value context)\n+    #[serde(skip_serializing_if = \"Option::is_none\")]\n+    pub metadata: Option<HashMap<String, String>>,\n+    \n+    /// Validation errors for 4xx responses\n+    #[serde(skip_serializing_if = \"Option::is_none\")]\n+    pub errors: Option<Vec<ValidationViolation>>,\n+    \n+    /// Upstream error chain (when error_stack enabled)\n+    #[serde(skip_serializing_if = \"Option::is_none\")]\n+    pub upstream_errors: Option<Vec<UpstreamError>>,","path":"intended_design/UNIFIED_ERROR_SYSTEM.md","commit_id":"5bdb0f43b25858af78999718f7247813802b9634","original_commit_id":"5bdb0f43b25858af78999718f7247813802b9634","user":{"login":"Artifizer","id":192502778,"node_id":"U_kgDOC3lb-g","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/192502778?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer","html_url":"https://github.com/Artifizer","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Better to remove - why, because it may reveal internal taxonomy to attackers!\n\nBetter approach is to use trace_id (as you do) and allow developers/QA/support to see the stack elsewhere, but not in API response ","created_at":"2026-01-30T20:57:13Z","updated_at":"2026-01-30T21:23:01Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/290#discussion_r2747962213","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/290","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2747962213"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/290#discussion_r2747962213"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/290"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2747962213/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":null,"original_line":227,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"MEMBER","original_position":227,"position":1,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2747970722","pull_request_review_id":3710446544,"id":2747970722,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs6jyrSi","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,1574 @@\n+# Unified Error System - Intention Document\n+\n+This document defines the architecture, rules, and implementation plan for a unified error handling system across the Hyperspot project. All REST API errors MUST have a GTS identifier, trace ID, and be registered in the types registry.\n+\n+## Table of Contents\n+\n+1. [Executive Summary](#executive-summary)\n+2. [Industry Research](#industry-research)\n+3. [Current State Analysis](#current-state-analysis)\n+4. [Requirements](#requirements)\n+5. [Implementation Rules](#implementation-rules)\n+6. [Migration Plan](#migration-plan)\n+7. [Examples](#examples)\n+8. [HTTP Headers](#http-headers)\n+9. [Security Considerations](#security-considerations)\n+10. [Appendix A: Error Category Definitions](#appendix-a-error-category-definitions)\n+11. [Appendix B: Retryable Error Guidelines](#appendix-b-retryable-error-guidelines)\n+12. [GTS System Errors Catalog](#gts-system-errors-catalog)\n+13. [References](#references)\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Executive Summary\n+\n+### Problem Statement\n+\n+The current error handling across Hyperspot modules is inconsistent:\n+- Some modules use `declare_errors!` macro with JSON catalogs\n+- Others define errors inline without GTS codes\n+- Errors are not registered in the types registry\n+- No standardized metadata/context fields\n+- Inconsistent trace ID propagation\n+\n+### Goals\n+\n+1. **Every REST API error** MUST have a valid GTS identifier\n+2. **Every error response** MUST include a trace ID for debugging\n+3. **All error types** MUST be registered in the types registry\n+4. **Consistent error schema** across all modules following RFC 9457\n+5. **Machine-readable error codes** for programmatic handling\n+6. **Error stack propagation** for nested service calls\n+\n+### Non-Goals\n+\n+- Changing internal domain error types (only API-facing errors)\n+- Modifying logging infrastructure\n+- Changing HTTP status code semantics\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Industry Research\n+\n+### How Major Tech Companies Handle Errors\n+\n+| Company | Standard | Key Features |\n+|---------|----------|--------------|\n+| **Google** | AIP-193 + gRPC Status | `reason` (UPPER_SNAKE_CASE), `domain` (service name), `metadata` (key-value context), `ErrorInfo`, `LocalizedMessage`, `Help` links |\n+| **Amazon AWS** | Custom JSON | `errorType`, `httpStatus`, `requestId`, `message`, custom error object serialization |\n+| **Twitter/X** | JSON with `errors` array | `code` (CAPS_CASE), `message`, `parameter`, `details`, `value` |\n+| **RFC 9457** | Problem Details | `type` (URI), `title`, `status`, `detail`, `instance`, extension members |\n+\n+### Key Patterns Identified\n+\n+1. **Machine-readable identifiers** - Unique codes for programmatic handling (Google's `reason`, Twitter's `code`)\n+2. **Domain/namespace separation** - Identify error source (Google's `domain`, our GTS vendor.package)\n+3. **Structured metadata** - Key-value context without parsing messages (Google's `ErrorInfo.metadata`)\n+4. **Trace/Request IDs** - Correlation for debugging (AWS `requestId`, our `trace_id`)\n+5. **Documentation links** - URIs to error documentation (RFC 9457 `type`, Google's `Help`)\n+6. **Error categorization** - System vs User-defined, Retryable vs Non-retryable\n+\n+### Google AIP-193 ErrorInfo Structure (Reference)\n+\n+```json\n+{\n+  \"error\": {\n+    \"code\": 429,\n+    \"message\": \"The zone 'us-east1-a' does not have enough resources...\",\n+    \"status\": \"RESOURCE_EXHAUSTED\",\n+    \"details\": [\n+      {\n+        \"@type\": \"type.googleapis.com/google.rpc.ErrorInfo\",\n+        \"reason\": \"RESOURCE_AVAILABILITY\",\n+        \"domain\": \"compute.googleapis.com\",\n+        \"metadata\": {\n+          \"zone\": \"us-east1-a\",\n+          \"vmType\": \"e2-medium\"\n+        }\n+      }\n+    ]\n+  }\n+}\n+```\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Current State Analysis\n+\n+### Existing Infrastructure\n+\n+1. **`Problem` struct** (`libs/modkit-errors/src/problem.rs`) - RFC 9457 compliant\n+   - Fields: `type_url`, `title`, `status`, `detail`, `instance`, `code`, `trace_id`, `errors`\n+   - Implements `IntoResponse` for Axum with automatic trace ID enrichment\n+\n+2. **`struct_to_gts_schema` macro** (`modules/types-registry/gts-rust/gts-macros/src/lib.rs`)\n+   - Attribute macro for explicit struct definitions with GTS IDs visible in code\n+   - Generates constants: `GTS_SCHEMA_ID`, `GTS_SCHEMA_JSON`, etc.\n+   - **This pattern will be adapted for error definitions**\n+\n+3. **`declare_errors!` macro** (`libs/modkit-errors-macro/src/lib.rs`) - **TO BE DEPRECATED**\n+   - Generates type-safe error enums from JSON catalogs\n+   - Problem: GTS IDs hidden in external JSON files, not visible to LLMs\n+   - Used by: `users_info` example, `modkit-odata`\n+\n+### Gaps Identified\n+\n+| Gap | Current State | Required State |\n+|-----|---------------|----------------|\n+| **Hidden GTS IDs** | JSON-based `declare_errors!` | Explicit `#[gts_error]` structs with visible GTS IDs |\n+| **Inconsistent definitions** | Some modules use inline errors | All modules use `#[gts_error]` structs |\n+| **No types registry** | Errors not registered | All errors registered as GTS types |\n+| **Missing metadata** | No structured context | Struct fields → `metadata` map |\n+| **Partial trace IDs** | Only in `IntoResponse` | Mandatory in all error responses |\n+| **No error categories** | Flat error codes | System/Operational/Client categories |\n+| **No error stack** | Single error | Upstream error chain propagation |\n+\n+### Current Module Migration Status\n+\n+| Module | Location | Status | Issues |\n+|--------|----------|--------|--------|\n+| **file_parser** | `modules/file_parser/` | 🔴 Not migrated | No GTS IDs, inline `Problem::new()` |\n+| **types-registry** | `modules/system/types-registry/` | 🟡 Partial | Has codes but not GTS format (e.g., `TYPES_REGISTRY_NOT_FOUND`) |\n+| **nodes_registry** | `modules/system/nodes_registry/` | 🔴 Not migrated | Non-GTS codes (e.g., `NODES_NOT_FOUND`) |\n+| **api_gateway** | `modules/system/api_gateway/` | 🔴 Not migrated | No Problem struct, simple error codes |\n+| **tenant_resolver** | `modules/system/tenant_resolver/` | 🔴 Not migrated | No GTS IDs |\n+| **simple-user-settings** | `modules/simple-user-settings/` | 🟡 Partial | Uses `declare_errors!` with old chain format |\n+| **modkit-auth** | `libs/modkit-auth/` | 🔴 Not migrated | No GTS IDs, custom `IntoResponse` |\n+| **modkit-odata** | `libs/modkit-odata/` | 🟡 Partial | Uses `declare_errors!` with old chain format |\n+| **users_info** (example) | `examples/modkit/users_info/` | 🟡 Partial | Uses `declare_errors!` with old chain format |\n+\n+#### Legend\n+- 🟢 **Migrated** - Uses `#[gts_error]` structs with proper base types\n+- 🟡 **Partial** - Has GTS IDs but uses deprecated `declare_errors!` or old format\n+- 🔴 **Not migrated** - No GTS IDs or non-GTS format codes\n+\n+#### GTS ID Format Note\n+\n+**Old chain format** (used by `declare_errors!`):\n+```\n+gts.hx.core.errors.err.v1~hx.module.error_name.v1\n+```\n+\n+**New format** (with `base` field):\n+```\n+gts.hx.module.namespace.error_name.v1~\n+```\n+The `base` field in `#[gts_error]` replaces the chain suffix, making inheritance explicit in code.\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Requirements\n+\n+### R1: Error Schema Requirements\n+\n+Every error returned from REST API MUST conform to the unified schema:\n+\n+```rust\n+pub struct Problem {\n+    // =========================================================================\n+    // REQUIRED FIELDS - Core error identification\n+    // =========================================================================\n+    \n+    /// URI reference identifying the problem type (GTS-based)\n+    /// Example: \"https://docs.hyperspot.com/errors/types_registry_entity_not_found_v1\"\n+    #[serde(rename = \"type\")]\n+    pub type_url: String,\n+    \n+    /// Human-readable summary of the problem type (static per error type)\n+    pub title: String,\n+    \n+    /// GTS error code (machine-readable identifier)\n+    pub code: String,\n+    \n+    /// Trace ID for request correlation\n+    pub trace_id: String,","path":"intended_design/UNIFIED_ERROR_SYSTEM.md","commit_id":"5bdb0f43b25858af78999718f7247813802b9634","original_commit_id":"5bdb0f43b25858af78999718f7247813802b9634","user":{"login":"Artifizer","id":192502778,"node_id":"U_kgDOC3lb-g","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/192502778?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer","html_url":"https://github.com/Artifizer","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Put here an example. Do not reveal full W3C trace ID here to the clients:\n\nInternally you can use full trace:\n```\ntraceparent: 00-4bf92f3577b34da6a3ce929d0e0e4736-00f067aa0ba902b7-01\n```\n\nthe API clients must see only:\n```\ntrace_id = 4bf92f3577b34da6a3ce929d0e0e4736\n```","created_at":"2026-01-30T21:00:47Z","updated_at":"2026-01-30T21:23:01Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/290#discussion_r2747970722","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/290","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2747970722"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/290#discussion_r2747970722"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/290"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2747970722/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":null,"original_line":184,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"MEMBER","original_position":184,"position":1,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2747972865","pull_request_review_id":3710446544,"id":2747972865,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs6jyr0B","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,1574 @@\n+# Unified Error System - Intention Document\n+\n+This document defines the architecture, rules, and implementation plan for a unified error handling system across the Hyperspot project. All REST API errors MUST have a GTS identifier, trace ID, and be registered in the types registry.\n+\n+## Table of Contents\n+\n+1. [Executive Summary](#executive-summary)\n+2. [Industry Research](#industry-research)\n+3. [Current State Analysis](#current-state-analysis)\n+4. [Requirements](#requirements)\n+5. [Implementation Rules](#implementation-rules)\n+6. [Migration Plan](#migration-plan)\n+7. [Examples](#examples)\n+8. [HTTP Headers](#http-headers)\n+9. [Security Considerations](#security-considerations)\n+10. [Appendix A: Error Category Definitions](#appendix-a-error-category-definitions)\n+11. [Appendix B: Retryable Error Guidelines](#appendix-b-retryable-error-guidelines)\n+12. [GTS System Errors Catalog](#gts-system-errors-catalog)\n+13. [References](#references)\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Executive Summary\n+\n+### Problem Statement\n+\n+The current error handling across Hyperspot modules is inconsistent:\n+- Some modules use `declare_errors!` macro with JSON catalogs\n+- Others define errors inline without GTS codes\n+- Errors are not registered in the types registry\n+- No standardized metadata/context fields\n+- Inconsistent trace ID propagation\n+\n+### Goals\n+\n+1. **Every REST API error** MUST have a valid GTS identifier\n+2. **Every error response** MUST include a trace ID for debugging\n+3. **All error types** MUST be registered in the types registry\n+4. **Consistent error schema** across all modules following RFC 9457\n+5. **Machine-readable error codes** for programmatic handling\n+6. **Error stack propagation** for nested service calls\n+\n+### Non-Goals\n+\n+- Changing internal domain error types (only API-facing errors)\n+- Modifying logging infrastructure\n+- Changing HTTP status code semantics\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Industry Research\n+\n+### How Major Tech Companies Handle Errors\n+\n+| Company | Standard | Key Features |\n+|---------|----------|--------------|\n+| **Google** | AIP-193 + gRPC Status | `reason` (UPPER_SNAKE_CASE), `domain` (service name), `metadata` (key-value context), `ErrorInfo`, `LocalizedMessage`, `Help` links |\n+| **Amazon AWS** | Custom JSON | `errorType`, `httpStatus`, `requestId`, `message`, custom error object serialization |\n+| **Twitter/X** | JSON with `errors` array | `code` (CAPS_CASE), `message`, `parameter`, `details`, `value` |\n+| **RFC 9457** | Problem Details | `type` (URI), `title`, `status`, `detail`, `instance`, extension members |\n+\n+### Key Patterns Identified\n+\n+1. **Machine-readable identifiers** - Unique codes for programmatic handling (Google's `reason`, Twitter's `code`)\n+2. **Domain/namespace separation** - Identify error source (Google's `domain`, our GTS vendor.package)\n+3. **Structured metadata** - Key-value context without parsing messages (Google's `ErrorInfo.metadata`)\n+4. **Trace/Request IDs** - Correlation for debugging (AWS `requestId`, our `trace_id`)\n+5. **Documentation links** - URIs to error documentation (RFC 9457 `type`, Google's `Help`)\n+6. **Error categorization** - System vs User-defined, Retryable vs Non-retryable\n+\n+### Google AIP-193 ErrorInfo Structure (Reference)\n+\n+```json\n+{\n+  \"error\": {\n+    \"code\": 429,\n+    \"message\": \"The zone 'us-east1-a' does not have enough resources...\",\n+    \"status\": \"RESOURCE_EXHAUSTED\",\n+    \"details\": [\n+      {\n+        \"@type\": \"type.googleapis.com/google.rpc.ErrorInfo\",\n+        \"reason\": \"RESOURCE_AVAILABILITY\",\n+        \"domain\": \"compute.googleapis.com\",\n+        \"metadata\": {\n+          \"zone\": \"us-east1-a\",\n+          \"vmType\": \"e2-medium\"\n+        }\n+      }\n+    ]\n+  }\n+}\n+```\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Current State Analysis\n+\n+### Existing Infrastructure\n+\n+1. **`Problem` struct** (`libs/modkit-errors/src/problem.rs`) - RFC 9457 compliant\n+   - Fields: `type_url`, `title`, `status`, `detail`, `instance`, `code`, `trace_id`, `errors`\n+   - Implements `IntoResponse` for Axum with automatic trace ID enrichment\n+\n+2. **`struct_to_gts_schema` macro** (`modules/types-registry/gts-rust/gts-macros/src/lib.rs`)\n+   - Attribute macro for explicit struct definitions with GTS IDs visible in code\n+   - Generates constants: `GTS_SCHEMA_ID`, `GTS_SCHEMA_JSON`, etc.\n+   - **This pattern will be adapted for error definitions**\n+\n+3. **`declare_errors!` macro** (`libs/modkit-errors-macro/src/lib.rs`) - **TO BE DEPRECATED**\n+   - Generates type-safe error enums from JSON catalogs\n+   - Problem: GTS IDs hidden in external JSON files, not visible to LLMs\n+   - Used by: `users_info` example, `modkit-odata`\n+\n+### Gaps Identified\n+\n+| Gap | Current State | Required State |\n+|-----|---------------|----------------|\n+| **Hidden GTS IDs** | JSON-based `declare_errors!` | Explicit `#[gts_error]` structs with visible GTS IDs |\n+| **Inconsistent definitions** | Some modules use inline errors | All modules use `#[gts_error]` structs |\n+| **No types registry** | Errors not registered | All errors registered as GTS types |\n+| **Missing metadata** | No structured context | Struct fields → `metadata` map |\n+| **Partial trace IDs** | Only in `IntoResponse` | Mandatory in all error responses |\n+| **No error categories** | Flat error codes | System/Operational/Client categories |\n+| **No error stack** | Single error | Upstream error chain propagation |\n+\n+### Current Module Migration Status\n+\n+| Module | Location | Status | Issues |\n+|--------|----------|--------|--------|\n+| **file_parser** | `modules/file_parser/` | 🔴 Not migrated | No GTS IDs, inline `Problem::new()` |\n+| **types-registry** | `modules/system/types-registry/` | 🟡 Partial | Has codes but not GTS format (e.g., `TYPES_REGISTRY_NOT_FOUND`) |\n+| **nodes_registry** | `modules/system/nodes_registry/` | 🔴 Not migrated | Non-GTS codes (e.g., `NODES_NOT_FOUND`) |\n+| **api_gateway** | `modules/system/api_gateway/` | 🔴 Not migrated | No Problem struct, simple error codes |\n+| **tenant_resolver** | `modules/system/tenant_resolver/` | 🔴 Not migrated | No GTS IDs |\n+| **simple-user-settings** | `modules/simple-user-settings/` | 🟡 Partial | Uses `declare_errors!` with old chain format |\n+| **modkit-auth** | `libs/modkit-auth/` | 🔴 Not migrated | No GTS IDs, custom `IntoResponse` |\n+| **modkit-odata** | `libs/modkit-odata/` | 🟡 Partial | Uses `declare_errors!` with old chain format |\n+| **users_info** (example) | `examples/modkit/users_info/` | 🟡 Partial | Uses `declare_errors!` with old chain format |\n+\n+#### Legend\n+- 🟢 **Migrated** - Uses `#[gts_error]` structs with proper base types\n+- 🟡 **Partial** - Has GTS IDs but uses deprecated `declare_errors!` or old format\n+- 🔴 **Not migrated** - No GTS IDs or non-GTS format codes\n+\n+#### GTS ID Format Note\n+\n+**Old chain format** (used by `declare_errors!`):\n+```\n+gts.hx.core.errors.err.v1~hx.module.error_name.v1\n+```\n+\n+**New format** (with `base` field):\n+```\n+gts.hx.module.namespace.error_name.v1~\n+```\n+The `base` field in `#[gts_error]` replaces the chain suffix, making inheritance explicit in code.\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Requirements\n+\n+### R1: Error Schema Requirements\n+\n+Every error returned from REST API MUST conform to the unified schema:\n+\n+```rust\n+pub struct Problem {\n+    // =========================================================================\n+    // REQUIRED FIELDS - Core error identification\n+    // =========================================================================\n+    \n+    /// URI reference identifying the problem type (GTS-based)\n+    /// Example: \"https://docs.hyperspot.com/errors/types_registry_entity_not_found_v1\"\n+    #[serde(rename = \"type\")]\n+    pub type_url: String,\n+    \n+    /// Human-readable summary of the problem type (static per error type)\n+    pub title: String,\n+    \n+    /// GTS error code (machine-readable identifier)\n+    pub code: String,\n+    \n+    /// Trace ID for request correlation\n+    pub trace_id: String,\n+    \n+    // =========================================================================\n+    // CONTEXTUAL FIELDS - Optional based on error context\n+    // =========================================================================\n+    \n+    /// HTTP status code. Optional because:\n+    /// - gRPC errors use different status codes\n+    /// - Internal/domain errors may not have HTTP context\n+    /// - Event-driven systems have no request/response\n+    /// When serializing for HTTP response, this is populated from error definition.\n+    #[serde(skip_serializing_if = \"Option::is_none\")]\n+    pub status: Option<u16>,\n+    \n+    /// Human-readable explanation specific to this occurrence.\n+    /// Optional - title may be sufficient for simple errors.\n+    #[serde(skip_serializing_if = \"Option::is_none\")]\n+    pub detail: Option<String>,\n+    \n+    /// Error category for client handling.\n+    /// Optional - can be inferred from base type hierarchy.\n+    #[serde(skip_serializing_if = \"Option::is_none\")]\n+    pub category: Option<ErrorCategory>,\n+    \n+    /// Whether client can retry this request.\n+    /// Optional - can be inferred from base type; not relevant for all contexts.\n+    #[serde(skip_serializing_if = \"Option::is_none\")]\n+    pub retryable: Option<bool>,\n+    \n+    /// URI identifying this specific occurrence (auto-populated from request path)\n+    #[serde(skip_serializing_if = \"Option::is_none\")]\n+    pub instance: Option<String>,\n+    \n+    /// Structured metadata (key-value context)\n+    #[serde(skip_serializing_if = \"Option::is_none\")]\n+    pub metadata: Option<HashMap<String, String>>,\n+    \n+    /// Validation errors for 4xx responses\n+    #[serde(skip_serializing_if = \"Option::is_none\")]\n+    pub errors: Option<Vec<ValidationViolation>>,\n+    \n+    /// Upstream error chain (when error_stack enabled)\n+    #[serde(skip_serializing_if = \"Option::is_none\")]\n+    pub upstream_errors: Option<Vec<UpstreamError>>,\n+}\n+\n+pub enum ErrorCategory {\n+    /// Platform-level execution errors (panics, OOM, internal bugs)\n+    System,\n+    /// Infrastructure/operational issues (DB unavailable, service down, rate limits)\n+    Operational,\n+    /// Client input/request errors (validation, not found, unauthorized)\n+    Client,\n+}\n+```\n+\n+#### Field Requirements Summary\n+\n+| Field | Required | Reason |\n+|-------|----------|--------|\n+| `type_url` | ✅ Yes | RFC 9457 requires problem type URI |\n+| `title` | ✅ Yes | Human-readable error name (static per type) |\n+| `code` | ✅ Yes | GTS identifier for machine processing |\n+| `trace_id` | ✅ Yes | Request correlation for debugging |\n+| `status` | ❌ No | Only relevant for HTTP; gRPC/events/domain errors don't need it |\n+| `detail` | ❌ No | Instance-specific message; title may suffice |\n+| `category` | ❌ No | Inherited from base type hierarchy |\n+| `retryable` | ❌ No | Inherited from base type; not relevant for all contexts |\n+| `instance` | ❌ No | Auto-populated from request path when applicable |\n+| `metadata` | ❌ No | Additional context key-value pairs |\n+| `errors` | ❌ No | Validation violations for 4xx errors |\n+| `upstream_errors` | ❌ No | Error chain from upstream services |\n+\n+**Note:** When converting to HTTP response, `status` is populated from the error definition. When the error is used in non-HTTP contexts (gRPC, domain logic, events), `status` remains `None`.\n+\n+### R2: GTS Identifier and Base Type Requirements\n+\n+Every error MUST have a valid GTS identifier and specify its base type using the `base` field.\n+\n+#### GTS ID Format\n+\n+```\n+gts.<vendor>.<package>.<namespace>.<type>.v<version>~\n+```\n+\n+**Examples:**\n+- `gts.hx.types_registry.entity.not_found.v1~` - Types registry not found error","path":"intended_design/UNIFIED_ERROR_SYSTEM.md","commit_id":"5bdb0f43b25858af78999718f7247813802b9634","original_commit_id":"5bdb0f43b25858af78999718f7247813802b9634","user":{"login":"Artifizer","id":192502778,"node_id":"U_kgDOC3lb-g","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/192502778?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer","html_url":"https://github.com/Artifizer","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"as I mentioned above, these are bad options ...","created_at":"2026-01-30T21:01:43Z","updated_at":"2026-01-30T21:23:01Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/290#discussion_r2747972865","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/290","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2747972865"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/290#discussion_r2747972865"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/290"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2747972865/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":null,"original_line":270,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"MEMBER","original_position":270,"position":1,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2747976625","pull_request_review_id":3710446544,"id":2747976625,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs6jysux","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,1574 @@\n+# Unified Error System - Intention Document\n+\n+This document defines the architecture, rules, and implementation plan for a unified error handling system across the Hyperspot project. All REST API errors MUST have a GTS identifier, trace ID, and be registered in the types registry.\n+\n+## Table of Contents\n+\n+1. [Executive Summary](#executive-summary)\n+2. [Industry Research](#industry-research)\n+3. [Current State Analysis](#current-state-analysis)\n+4. [Requirements](#requirements)\n+5. [Implementation Rules](#implementation-rules)\n+6. [Migration Plan](#migration-plan)\n+7. [Examples](#examples)\n+8. [HTTP Headers](#http-headers)\n+9. [Security Considerations](#security-considerations)\n+10. [Appendix A: Error Category Definitions](#appendix-a-error-category-definitions)\n+11. [Appendix B: Retryable Error Guidelines](#appendix-b-retryable-error-guidelines)\n+12. [GTS System Errors Catalog](#gts-system-errors-catalog)\n+13. [References](#references)\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Executive Summary\n+\n+### Problem Statement\n+\n+The current error handling across Hyperspot modules is inconsistent:\n+- Some modules use `declare_errors!` macro with JSON catalogs\n+- Others define errors inline without GTS codes\n+- Errors are not registered in the types registry\n+- No standardized metadata/context fields\n+- Inconsistent trace ID propagation\n+\n+### Goals\n+\n+1. **Every REST API error** MUST have a valid GTS identifier\n+2. **Every error response** MUST include a trace ID for debugging\n+3. **All error types** MUST be registered in the types registry\n+4. **Consistent error schema** across all modules following RFC 9457\n+5. **Machine-readable error codes** for programmatic handling\n+6. **Error stack propagation** for nested service calls\n+\n+### Non-Goals\n+\n+- Changing internal domain error types (only API-facing errors)\n+- Modifying logging infrastructure\n+- Changing HTTP status code semantics\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Industry Research\n+\n+### How Major Tech Companies Handle Errors\n+\n+| Company | Standard | Key Features |\n+|---------|----------|--------------|\n+| **Google** | AIP-193 + gRPC Status | `reason` (UPPER_SNAKE_CASE), `domain` (service name), `metadata` (key-value context), `ErrorInfo`, `LocalizedMessage`, `Help` links |\n+| **Amazon AWS** | Custom JSON | `errorType`, `httpStatus`, `requestId`, `message`, custom error object serialization |\n+| **Twitter/X** | JSON with `errors` array | `code` (CAPS_CASE), `message`, `parameter`, `details`, `value` |\n+| **RFC 9457** | Problem Details | `type` (URI), `title`, `status`, `detail`, `instance`, extension members |\n+\n+### Key Patterns Identified\n+\n+1. **Machine-readable identifiers** - Unique codes for programmatic handling (Google's `reason`, Twitter's `code`)\n+2. **Domain/namespace separation** - Identify error source (Google's `domain`, our GTS vendor.package)\n+3. **Structured metadata** - Key-value context without parsing messages (Google's `ErrorInfo.metadata`)\n+4. **Trace/Request IDs** - Correlation for debugging (AWS `requestId`, our `trace_id`)\n+5. **Documentation links** - URIs to error documentation (RFC 9457 `type`, Google's `Help`)\n+6. **Error categorization** - System vs User-defined, Retryable vs Non-retryable\n+\n+### Google AIP-193 ErrorInfo Structure (Reference)\n+\n+```json\n+{\n+  \"error\": {\n+    \"code\": 429,\n+    \"message\": \"The zone 'us-east1-a' does not have enough resources...\",\n+    \"status\": \"RESOURCE_EXHAUSTED\",\n+    \"details\": [\n+      {\n+        \"@type\": \"type.googleapis.com/google.rpc.ErrorInfo\",\n+        \"reason\": \"RESOURCE_AVAILABILITY\",\n+        \"domain\": \"compute.googleapis.com\",\n+        \"metadata\": {\n+          \"zone\": \"us-east1-a\",\n+          \"vmType\": \"e2-medium\"\n+        }\n+      }\n+    ]\n+  }\n+}\n+```\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Current State Analysis\n+\n+### Existing Infrastructure\n+\n+1. **`Problem` struct** (`libs/modkit-errors/src/problem.rs`) - RFC 9457 compliant\n+   - Fields: `type_url`, `title`, `status`, `detail`, `instance`, `code`, `trace_id`, `errors`\n+   - Implements `IntoResponse` for Axum with automatic trace ID enrichment\n+\n+2. **`struct_to_gts_schema` macro** (`modules/types-registry/gts-rust/gts-macros/src/lib.rs`)\n+   - Attribute macro for explicit struct definitions with GTS IDs visible in code\n+   - Generates constants: `GTS_SCHEMA_ID`, `GTS_SCHEMA_JSON`, etc.\n+   - **This pattern will be adapted for error definitions**\n+\n+3. **`declare_errors!` macro** (`libs/modkit-errors-macro/src/lib.rs`) - **TO BE DEPRECATED**\n+   - Generates type-safe error enums from JSON catalogs\n+   - Problem: GTS IDs hidden in external JSON files, not visible to LLMs\n+   - Used by: `users_info` example, `modkit-odata`\n+\n+### Gaps Identified\n+\n+| Gap | Current State | Required State |\n+|-----|---------------|----------------|\n+| **Hidden GTS IDs** | JSON-based `declare_errors!` | Explicit `#[gts_error]` structs with visible GTS IDs |\n+| **Inconsistent definitions** | Some modules use inline errors | All modules use `#[gts_error]` structs |\n+| **No types registry** | Errors not registered | All errors registered as GTS types |\n+| **Missing metadata** | No structured context | Struct fields → `metadata` map |\n+| **Partial trace IDs** | Only in `IntoResponse` | Mandatory in all error responses |\n+| **No error categories** | Flat error codes | System/Operational/Client categories |\n+| **No error stack** | Single error | Upstream error chain propagation |\n+\n+### Current Module Migration Status\n+\n+| Module | Location | Status | Issues |\n+|--------|----------|--------|--------|\n+| **file_parser** | `modules/file_parser/` | 🔴 Not migrated | No GTS IDs, inline `Problem::new()` |\n+| **types-registry** | `modules/system/types-registry/` | 🟡 Partial | Has codes but not GTS format (e.g., `TYPES_REGISTRY_NOT_FOUND`) |\n+| **nodes_registry** | `modules/system/nodes_registry/` | 🔴 Not migrated | Non-GTS codes (e.g., `NODES_NOT_FOUND`) |\n+| **api_gateway** | `modules/system/api_gateway/` | 🔴 Not migrated | No Problem struct, simple error codes |\n+| **tenant_resolver** | `modules/system/tenant_resolver/` | 🔴 Not migrated | No GTS IDs |\n+| **simple-user-settings** | `modules/simple-user-settings/` | 🟡 Partial | Uses `declare_errors!` with old chain format |\n+| **modkit-auth** | `libs/modkit-auth/` | 🔴 Not migrated | No GTS IDs, custom `IntoResponse` |\n+| **modkit-odata** | `libs/modkit-odata/` | 🟡 Partial | Uses `declare_errors!` with old chain format |\n+| **users_info** (example) | `examples/modkit/users_info/` | 🟡 Partial | Uses `declare_errors!` with old chain format |\n+\n+#### Legend\n+- 🟢 **Migrated** - Uses `#[gts_error]` structs with proper base types\n+- 🟡 **Partial** - Has GTS IDs but uses deprecated `declare_errors!` or old format\n+- 🔴 **Not migrated** - No GTS IDs or non-GTS format codes\n+\n+#### GTS ID Format Note\n+\n+**Old chain format** (used by `declare_errors!`):\n+```\n+gts.hx.core.errors.err.v1~hx.module.error_name.v1\n+```\n+\n+**New format** (with `base` field):\n+```\n+gts.hx.module.namespace.error_name.v1~\n+```\n+The `base` field in `#[gts_error]` replaces the chain suffix, making inheritance explicit in code.\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Requirements\n+\n+### R1: Error Schema Requirements\n+\n+Every error returned from REST API MUST conform to the unified schema:\n+\n+```rust\n+pub struct Problem {\n+    // =========================================================================\n+    // REQUIRED FIELDS - Core error identification\n+    // =========================================================================\n+    \n+    /// URI reference identifying the problem type (GTS-based)\n+    /// Example: \"https://docs.hyperspot.com/errors/types_registry_entity_not_found_v1\"\n+    #[serde(rename = \"type\")]\n+    pub type_url: String,\n+    \n+    /// Human-readable summary of the problem type (static per error type)\n+    pub title: String,\n+    \n+    /// GTS error code (machine-readable identifier)\n+    pub code: String,\n+    \n+    /// Trace ID for request correlation\n+    pub trace_id: String,\n+    \n+    // =========================================================================\n+    // CONTEXTUAL FIELDS - Optional based on error context\n+    // =========================================================================\n+    \n+    /// HTTP status code. Optional because:\n+    /// - gRPC errors use different status codes\n+    /// - Internal/domain errors may not have HTTP context\n+    /// - Event-driven systems have no request/response\n+    /// When serializing for HTTP response, this is populated from error definition.\n+    #[serde(skip_serializing_if = \"Option::is_none\")]\n+    pub status: Option<u16>,\n+    \n+    /// Human-readable explanation specific to this occurrence.\n+    /// Optional - title may be sufficient for simple errors.\n+    #[serde(skip_serializing_if = \"Option::is_none\")]\n+    pub detail: Option<String>,\n+    \n+    /// Error category for client handling.\n+    /// Optional - can be inferred from base type hierarchy.\n+    #[serde(skip_serializing_if = \"Option::is_none\")]\n+    pub category: Option<ErrorCategory>,\n+    \n+    /// Whether client can retry this request.\n+    /// Optional - can be inferred from base type; not relevant for all contexts.\n+    #[serde(skip_serializing_if = \"Option::is_none\")]\n+    pub retryable: Option<bool>,\n+    \n+    /// URI identifying this specific occurrence (auto-populated from request path)\n+    #[serde(skip_serializing_if = \"Option::is_none\")]\n+    pub instance: Option<String>,\n+    \n+    /// Structured metadata (key-value context)\n+    #[serde(skip_serializing_if = \"Option::is_none\")]\n+    pub metadata: Option<HashMap<String, String>>,\n+    \n+    /// Validation errors for 4xx responses\n+    #[serde(skip_serializing_if = \"Option::is_none\")]\n+    pub errors: Option<Vec<ValidationViolation>>,\n+    \n+    /// Upstream error chain (when error_stack enabled)\n+    #[serde(skip_serializing_if = \"Option::is_none\")]\n+    pub upstream_errors: Option<Vec<UpstreamError>>,\n+}\n+\n+pub enum ErrorCategory {\n+    /// Platform-level execution errors (panics, OOM, internal bugs)\n+    System,\n+    /// Infrastructure/operational issues (DB unavailable, service down, rate limits)\n+    Operational,\n+    /// Client input/request errors (validation, not found, unauthorized)\n+    Client,\n+}\n+```\n+\n+#### Field Requirements Summary\n+\n+| Field | Required | Reason |\n+|-------|----------|--------|\n+| `type_url` | ✅ Yes | RFC 9457 requires problem type URI |\n+| `title` | ✅ Yes | Human-readable error name (static per type) |\n+| `code` | ✅ Yes | GTS identifier for machine processing |\n+| `trace_id` | ✅ Yes | Request correlation for debugging |\n+| `status` | ❌ No | Only relevant for HTTP; gRPC/events/domain errors don't need it |\n+| `detail` | ❌ No | Instance-specific message; title may suffice |\n+| `category` | ❌ No | Inherited from base type hierarchy |\n+| `retryable` | ❌ No | Inherited from base type; not relevant for all contexts |\n+| `instance` | ❌ No | Auto-populated from request path when applicable |\n+| `metadata` | ❌ No | Additional context key-value pairs |\n+| `errors` | ❌ No | Validation violations for 4xx errors |\n+| `upstream_errors` | ❌ No | Error chain from upstream services |\n+\n+**Note:** When converting to HTTP response, `status` is populated from the error definition. When the error is used in non-HTTP contexts (gRPC, domain logic, events), `status` remains `None`.\n+\n+### R2: GTS Identifier and Base Type Requirements\n+\n+Every error MUST have a valid GTS identifier and specify its base type using the `base` field.\n+\n+#### GTS ID Format\n+\n+```\n+gts.<vendor>.<package>.<namespace>.<type>.v<version>~\n+```\n+\n+**Examples:**\n+- `gts.hx.types_registry.entity.not_found.v1~` - Types registry not found error\n+- `gts.hx.file_parser.validation.invalid_format.v1~` - File parser validation error\n+- `gts.hx.system.runtime.timeout.v1~` - System timeout error\n+\n+#### Base Type Chaining\n+\n+Errors form an inheritance chain using the `base` field. The `base` field references another error struct type (not a string literal), similar to how `struct_to_gts_schema` works.\n+\n+The root base error type is:\n+\n+```rust\n+/// Root error type for all GTS errors.\n+#[gts_error(\n+    gts_id = \"gts.hx.core.errors.err.v1~\",\n+    base = true,  // Marks this as a root base type (no parent)\n+    title = \"Error\",\n+    // Optional attributes with defaults for inheritance:\n+    status = 500,        // Default HTTP status (optional, inherited by children)\n+    category = \"System\", // Default category (optional, inherited by children)\n+    retryable = false    // Default retryable (optional, inherited by children)\n+)]\n+pub struct BaseError;","path":"intended_design/UNIFIED_ERROR_SYSTEM.md","commit_id":"5bdb0f43b25858af78999718f7247813802b9634","original_commit_id":"5bdb0f43b25858af78999718f7247813802b9634","user":{"login":"Artifizer","id":192502778,"node_id":"U_kgDOC3lb-g","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/192502778?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer","html_url":"https://github.com/Artifizer","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"I like this macro :)","created_at":"2026-01-30T21:03:18Z","updated_at":"2026-01-30T21:23:01Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/290#discussion_r2747976625","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/290","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2747976625"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/290#discussion_r2747976625"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/290"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2747976625/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":1,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":null,"original_line":291,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"MEMBER","original_position":291,"position":1,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2747980786","pull_request_review_id":3710446544,"id":2747980786,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs6jytvy","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,1574 @@\n+# Unified Error System - Intention Document\n+\n+This document defines the architecture, rules, and implementation plan for a unified error handling system across the Hyperspot project. All REST API errors MUST have a GTS identifier, trace ID, and be registered in the types registry.\n+\n+## Table of Contents\n+\n+1. [Executive Summary](#executive-summary)\n+2. [Industry Research](#industry-research)\n+3. [Current State Analysis](#current-state-analysis)\n+4. [Requirements](#requirements)\n+5. [Implementation Rules](#implementation-rules)\n+6. [Migration Plan](#migration-plan)\n+7. [Examples](#examples)\n+8. [HTTP Headers](#http-headers)\n+9. [Security Considerations](#security-considerations)\n+10. [Appendix A: Error Category Definitions](#appendix-a-error-category-definitions)\n+11. [Appendix B: Retryable Error Guidelines](#appendix-b-retryable-error-guidelines)\n+12. [GTS System Errors Catalog](#gts-system-errors-catalog)\n+13. [References](#references)\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Executive Summary\n+\n+### Problem Statement\n+\n+The current error handling across Hyperspot modules is inconsistent:\n+- Some modules use `declare_errors!` macro with JSON catalogs\n+- Others define errors inline without GTS codes\n+- Errors are not registered in the types registry\n+- No standardized metadata/context fields\n+- Inconsistent trace ID propagation\n+\n+### Goals\n+\n+1. **Every REST API error** MUST have a valid GTS identifier\n+2. **Every error response** MUST include a trace ID for debugging\n+3. **All error types** MUST be registered in the types registry\n+4. **Consistent error schema** across all modules following RFC 9457\n+5. **Machine-readable error codes** for programmatic handling\n+6. **Error stack propagation** for nested service calls\n+\n+### Non-Goals\n+\n+- Changing internal domain error types (only API-facing errors)\n+- Modifying logging infrastructure\n+- Changing HTTP status code semantics\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Industry Research\n+\n+### How Major Tech Companies Handle Errors\n+\n+| Company | Standard | Key Features |\n+|---------|----------|--------------|\n+| **Google** | AIP-193 + gRPC Status | `reason` (UPPER_SNAKE_CASE), `domain` (service name), `metadata` (key-value context), `ErrorInfo`, `LocalizedMessage`, `Help` links |\n+| **Amazon AWS** | Custom JSON | `errorType`, `httpStatus`, `requestId`, `message`, custom error object serialization |\n+| **Twitter/X** | JSON with `errors` array | `code` (CAPS_CASE), `message`, `parameter`, `details`, `value` |\n+| **RFC 9457** | Problem Details | `type` (URI), `title`, `status`, `detail`, `instance`, extension members |\n+\n+### Key Patterns Identified\n+\n+1. **Machine-readable identifiers** - Unique codes for programmatic handling (Google's `reason`, Twitter's `code`)\n+2. **Domain/namespace separation** - Identify error source (Google's `domain`, our GTS vendor.package)\n+3. **Structured metadata** - Key-value context without parsing messages (Google's `ErrorInfo.metadata`)\n+4. **Trace/Request IDs** - Correlation for debugging (AWS `requestId`, our `trace_id`)\n+5. **Documentation links** - URIs to error documentation (RFC 9457 `type`, Google's `Help`)\n+6. **Error categorization** - System vs User-defined, Retryable vs Non-retryable\n+\n+### Google AIP-193 ErrorInfo Structure (Reference)\n+\n+```json\n+{\n+  \"error\": {\n+    \"code\": 429,\n+    \"message\": \"The zone 'us-east1-a' does not have enough resources...\",\n+    \"status\": \"RESOURCE_EXHAUSTED\",\n+    \"details\": [\n+      {\n+        \"@type\": \"type.googleapis.com/google.rpc.ErrorInfo\",\n+        \"reason\": \"RESOURCE_AVAILABILITY\",\n+        \"domain\": \"compute.googleapis.com\",\n+        \"metadata\": {\n+          \"zone\": \"us-east1-a\",\n+          \"vmType\": \"e2-medium\"\n+        }\n+      }\n+    ]\n+  }\n+}\n+```\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Current State Analysis\n+\n+### Existing Infrastructure\n+\n+1. **`Problem` struct** (`libs/modkit-errors/src/problem.rs`) - RFC 9457 compliant\n+   - Fields: `type_url`, `title`, `status`, `detail`, `instance`, `code`, `trace_id`, `errors`\n+   - Implements `IntoResponse` for Axum with automatic trace ID enrichment\n+\n+2. **`struct_to_gts_schema` macro** (`modules/types-registry/gts-rust/gts-macros/src/lib.rs`)\n+   - Attribute macro for explicit struct definitions with GTS IDs visible in code\n+   - Generates constants: `GTS_SCHEMA_ID`, `GTS_SCHEMA_JSON`, etc.\n+   - **This pattern will be adapted for error definitions**\n+\n+3. **`declare_errors!` macro** (`libs/modkit-errors-macro/src/lib.rs`) - **TO BE DEPRECATED**\n+   - Generates type-safe error enums from JSON catalogs\n+   - Problem: GTS IDs hidden in external JSON files, not visible to LLMs\n+   - Used by: `users_info` example, `modkit-odata`\n+\n+### Gaps Identified\n+\n+| Gap | Current State | Required State |\n+|-----|---------------|----------------|\n+| **Hidden GTS IDs** | JSON-based `declare_errors!` | Explicit `#[gts_error]` structs with visible GTS IDs |\n+| **Inconsistent definitions** | Some modules use inline errors | All modules use `#[gts_error]` structs |\n+| **No types registry** | Errors not registered | All errors registered as GTS types |\n+| **Missing metadata** | No structured context | Struct fields → `metadata` map |\n+| **Partial trace IDs** | Only in `IntoResponse` | Mandatory in all error responses |\n+| **No error categories** | Flat error codes | System/Operational/Client categories |\n+| **No error stack** | Single error | Upstream error chain propagation |\n+\n+### Current Module Migration Status\n+\n+| Module | Location | Status | Issues |\n+|--------|----------|--------|--------|\n+| **file_parser** | `modules/file_parser/` | 🔴 Not migrated | No GTS IDs, inline `Problem::new()` |\n+| **types-registry** | `modules/system/types-registry/` | 🟡 Partial | Has codes but not GTS format (e.g., `TYPES_REGISTRY_NOT_FOUND`) |\n+| **nodes_registry** | `modules/system/nodes_registry/` | 🔴 Not migrated | Non-GTS codes (e.g., `NODES_NOT_FOUND`) |\n+| **api_gateway** | `modules/system/api_gateway/` | 🔴 Not migrated | No Problem struct, simple error codes |\n+| **tenant_resolver** | `modules/system/tenant_resolver/` | 🔴 Not migrated | No GTS IDs |\n+| **simple-user-settings** | `modules/simple-user-settings/` | 🟡 Partial | Uses `declare_errors!` with old chain format |\n+| **modkit-auth** | `libs/modkit-auth/` | 🔴 Not migrated | No GTS IDs, custom `IntoResponse` |\n+| **modkit-odata** | `libs/modkit-odata/` | 🟡 Partial | Uses `declare_errors!` with old chain format |\n+| **users_info** (example) | `examples/modkit/users_info/` | 🟡 Partial | Uses `declare_errors!` with old chain format |\n+\n+#### Legend\n+- 🟢 **Migrated** - Uses `#[gts_error]` structs with proper base types\n+- 🟡 **Partial** - Has GTS IDs but uses deprecated `declare_errors!` or old format\n+- 🔴 **Not migrated** - No GTS IDs or non-GTS format codes\n+\n+#### GTS ID Format Note\n+\n+**Old chain format** (used by `declare_errors!`):\n+```\n+gts.hx.core.errors.err.v1~hx.module.error_name.v1\n+```\n+\n+**New format** (with `base` field):\n+```\n+gts.hx.module.namespace.error_name.v1~\n+```\n+The `base` field in `#[gts_error]` replaces the chain suffix, making inheritance explicit in code.\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Requirements\n+\n+### R1: Error Schema Requirements\n+\n+Every error returned from REST API MUST conform to the unified schema:\n+\n+```rust\n+pub struct Problem {\n+    // =========================================================================\n+    // REQUIRED FIELDS - Core error identification\n+    // =========================================================================\n+    \n+    /// URI reference identifying the problem type (GTS-based)\n+    /// Example: \"https://docs.hyperspot.com/errors/types_registry_entity_not_found_v1\"\n+    #[serde(rename = \"type\")]\n+    pub type_url: String,\n+    \n+    /// Human-readable summary of the problem type (static per error type)\n+    pub title: String,\n+    \n+    /// GTS error code (machine-readable identifier)\n+    pub code: String,\n+    \n+    /// Trace ID for request correlation\n+    pub trace_id: String,\n+    \n+    // =========================================================================\n+    // CONTEXTUAL FIELDS - Optional based on error context\n+    // =========================================================================\n+    \n+    /// HTTP status code. Optional because:\n+    /// - gRPC errors use different status codes\n+    /// - Internal/domain errors may not have HTTP context\n+    /// - Event-driven systems have no request/response\n+    /// When serializing for HTTP response, this is populated from error definition.\n+    #[serde(skip_serializing_if = \"Option::is_none\")]\n+    pub status: Option<u16>,\n+    \n+    /// Human-readable explanation specific to this occurrence.\n+    /// Optional - title may be sufficient for simple errors.\n+    #[serde(skip_serializing_if = \"Option::is_none\")]\n+    pub detail: Option<String>,\n+    \n+    /// Error category for client handling.\n+    /// Optional - can be inferred from base type hierarchy.\n+    #[serde(skip_serializing_if = \"Option::is_none\")]\n+    pub category: Option<ErrorCategory>,\n+    \n+    /// Whether client can retry this request.\n+    /// Optional - can be inferred from base type; not relevant for all contexts.\n+    #[serde(skip_serializing_if = \"Option::is_none\")]\n+    pub retryable: Option<bool>,\n+    \n+    /// URI identifying this specific occurrence (auto-populated from request path)\n+    #[serde(skip_serializing_if = \"Option::is_none\")]\n+    pub instance: Option<String>,\n+    \n+    /// Structured metadata (key-value context)\n+    #[serde(skip_serializing_if = \"Option::is_none\")]\n+    pub metadata: Option<HashMap<String, String>>,\n+    \n+    /// Validation errors for 4xx responses\n+    #[serde(skip_serializing_if = \"Option::is_none\")]\n+    pub errors: Option<Vec<ValidationViolation>>,\n+    \n+    /// Upstream error chain (when error_stack enabled)\n+    #[serde(skip_serializing_if = \"Option::is_none\")]\n+    pub upstream_errors: Option<Vec<UpstreamError>>,\n+}\n+\n+pub enum ErrorCategory {\n+    /// Platform-level execution errors (panics, OOM, internal bugs)\n+    System,\n+    /// Infrastructure/operational issues (DB unavailable, service down, rate limits)\n+    Operational,\n+    /// Client input/request errors (validation, not found, unauthorized)\n+    Client,\n+}\n+```\n+\n+#### Field Requirements Summary\n+\n+| Field | Required | Reason |\n+|-------|----------|--------|\n+| `type_url` | ✅ Yes | RFC 9457 requires problem type URI |\n+| `title` | ✅ Yes | Human-readable error name (static per type) |\n+| `code` | ✅ Yes | GTS identifier for machine processing |\n+| `trace_id` | ✅ Yes | Request correlation for debugging |\n+| `status` | ❌ No | Only relevant for HTTP; gRPC/events/domain errors don't need it |\n+| `detail` | ❌ No | Instance-specific message; title may suffice |\n+| `category` | ❌ No | Inherited from base type hierarchy |\n+| `retryable` | ❌ No | Inherited from base type; not relevant for all contexts |\n+| `instance` | ❌ No | Auto-populated from request path when applicable |\n+| `metadata` | ❌ No | Additional context key-value pairs |\n+| `errors` | ❌ No | Validation violations for 4xx errors |\n+| `upstream_errors` | ❌ No | Error chain from upstream services |\n+\n+**Note:** When converting to HTTP response, `status` is populated from the error definition. When the error is used in non-HTTP contexts (gRPC, domain logic, events), `status` remains `None`.\n+\n+### R2: GTS Identifier and Base Type Requirements\n+\n+Every error MUST have a valid GTS identifier and specify its base type using the `base` field.\n+\n+#### GTS ID Format\n+\n+```\n+gts.<vendor>.<package>.<namespace>.<type>.v<version>~\n+```\n+\n+**Examples:**\n+- `gts.hx.types_registry.entity.not_found.v1~` - Types registry not found error\n+- `gts.hx.file_parser.validation.invalid_format.v1~` - File parser validation error\n+- `gts.hx.system.runtime.timeout.v1~` - System timeout error\n+\n+#### Base Type Chaining\n+\n+Errors form an inheritance chain using the `base` field. The `base` field references another error struct type (not a string literal), similar to how `struct_to_gts_schema` works.\n+\n+The root base error type is:\n+\n+```rust\n+/// Root error type for all GTS errors.\n+#[gts_error(\n+    gts_id = \"gts.hx.core.errors.err.v1~\",","path":"intended_design/UNIFIED_ERROR_SYSTEM.md","commit_id":"5bdb0f43b25858af78999718f7247813802b9634","original_commit_id":"5bdb0f43b25858af78999718f7247813802b9634","user":{"login":"Artifizer","id":192502778,"node_id":"U_kgDOC3lb-g","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/192502778?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer","html_url":"https://github.com/Artifizer","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"can we just use original field names, e.g. `type` in this case? So developers would see it like - what you put here is what you get in API","created_at":"2026-01-30T21:04:58Z","updated_at":"2026-01-30T21:23:01Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/290#discussion_r2747980786","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/290","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2747980786"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/290#discussion_r2747980786"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/290"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2747980786/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":null,"original_line":283,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"MEMBER","original_position":283,"position":1,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2747987436","pull_request_review_id":3710446544,"id":2747987436,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs6jyvXs","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,1574 @@\n+# Unified Error System - Intention Document\n+\n+This document defines the architecture, rules, and implementation plan for a unified error handling system across the Hyperspot project. All REST API errors MUST have a GTS identifier, trace ID, and be registered in the types registry.\n+\n+## Table of Contents\n+\n+1. [Executive Summary](#executive-summary)\n+2. [Industry Research](#industry-research)\n+3. [Current State Analysis](#current-state-analysis)\n+4. [Requirements](#requirements)\n+5. [Implementation Rules](#implementation-rules)\n+6. [Migration Plan](#migration-plan)\n+7. [Examples](#examples)\n+8. [HTTP Headers](#http-headers)\n+9. [Security Considerations](#security-considerations)\n+10. [Appendix A: Error Category Definitions](#appendix-a-error-category-definitions)\n+11. [Appendix B: Retryable Error Guidelines](#appendix-b-retryable-error-guidelines)\n+12. [GTS System Errors Catalog](#gts-system-errors-catalog)\n+13. [References](#references)\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Executive Summary\n+\n+### Problem Statement\n+\n+The current error handling across Hyperspot modules is inconsistent:\n+- Some modules use `declare_errors!` macro with JSON catalogs\n+- Others define errors inline without GTS codes\n+- Errors are not registered in the types registry\n+- No standardized metadata/context fields\n+- Inconsistent trace ID propagation\n+\n+### Goals\n+\n+1. **Every REST API error** MUST have a valid GTS identifier\n+2. **Every error response** MUST include a trace ID for debugging\n+3. **All error types** MUST be registered in the types registry\n+4. **Consistent error schema** across all modules following RFC 9457\n+5. **Machine-readable error codes** for programmatic handling\n+6. **Error stack propagation** for nested service calls\n+\n+### Non-Goals\n+\n+- Changing internal domain error types (only API-facing errors)\n+- Modifying logging infrastructure\n+- Changing HTTP status code semantics\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Industry Research\n+\n+### How Major Tech Companies Handle Errors\n+\n+| Company | Standard | Key Features |\n+|---------|----------|--------------|\n+| **Google** | AIP-193 + gRPC Status | `reason` (UPPER_SNAKE_CASE), `domain` (service name), `metadata` (key-value context), `ErrorInfo`, `LocalizedMessage`, `Help` links |\n+| **Amazon AWS** | Custom JSON | `errorType`, `httpStatus`, `requestId`, `message`, custom error object serialization |\n+| **Twitter/X** | JSON with `errors` array | `code` (CAPS_CASE), `message`, `parameter`, `details`, `value` |\n+| **RFC 9457** | Problem Details | `type` (URI), `title`, `status`, `detail`, `instance`, extension members |\n+\n+### Key Patterns Identified\n+\n+1. **Machine-readable identifiers** - Unique codes for programmatic handling (Google's `reason`, Twitter's `code`)\n+2. **Domain/namespace separation** - Identify error source (Google's `domain`, our GTS vendor.package)\n+3. **Structured metadata** - Key-value context without parsing messages (Google's `ErrorInfo.metadata`)\n+4. **Trace/Request IDs** - Correlation for debugging (AWS `requestId`, our `trace_id`)\n+5. **Documentation links** - URIs to error documentation (RFC 9457 `type`, Google's `Help`)\n+6. **Error categorization** - System vs User-defined, Retryable vs Non-retryable\n+\n+### Google AIP-193 ErrorInfo Structure (Reference)\n+\n+```json\n+{\n+  \"error\": {\n+    \"code\": 429,\n+    \"message\": \"The zone 'us-east1-a' does not have enough resources...\",\n+    \"status\": \"RESOURCE_EXHAUSTED\",\n+    \"details\": [\n+      {\n+        \"@type\": \"type.googleapis.com/google.rpc.ErrorInfo\",\n+        \"reason\": \"RESOURCE_AVAILABILITY\",\n+        \"domain\": \"compute.googleapis.com\",\n+        \"metadata\": {\n+          \"zone\": \"us-east1-a\",\n+          \"vmType\": \"e2-medium\"\n+        }\n+      }\n+    ]\n+  }\n+}\n+```\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Current State Analysis\n+\n+### Existing Infrastructure\n+\n+1. **`Problem` struct** (`libs/modkit-errors/src/problem.rs`) - RFC 9457 compliant\n+   - Fields: `type_url`, `title`, `status`, `detail`, `instance`, `code`, `trace_id`, `errors`\n+   - Implements `IntoResponse` for Axum with automatic trace ID enrichment\n+\n+2. **`struct_to_gts_schema` macro** (`modules/types-registry/gts-rust/gts-macros/src/lib.rs`)\n+   - Attribute macro for explicit struct definitions with GTS IDs visible in code\n+   - Generates constants: `GTS_SCHEMA_ID`, `GTS_SCHEMA_JSON`, etc.\n+   - **This pattern will be adapted for error definitions**\n+\n+3. **`declare_errors!` macro** (`libs/modkit-errors-macro/src/lib.rs`) - **TO BE DEPRECATED**\n+   - Generates type-safe error enums from JSON catalogs\n+   - Problem: GTS IDs hidden in external JSON files, not visible to LLMs\n+   - Used by: `users_info` example, `modkit-odata`\n+\n+### Gaps Identified\n+\n+| Gap | Current State | Required State |\n+|-----|---------------|----------------|\n+| **Hidden GTS IDs** | JSON-based `declare_errors!` | Explicit `#[gts_error]` structs with visible GTS IDs |\n+| **Inconsistent definitions** | Some modules use inline errors | All modules use `#[gts_error]` structs |\n+| **No types registry** | Errors not registered | All errors registered as GTS types |\n+| **Missing metadata** | No structured context | Struct fields → `metadata` map |\n+| **Partial trace IDs** | Only in `IntoResponse` | Mandatory in all error responses |\n+| **No error categories** | Flat error codes | System/Operational/Client categories |\n+| **No error stack** | Single error | Upstream error chain propagation |\n+\n+### Current Module Migration Status\n+\n+| Module | Location | Status | Issues |\n+|--------|----------|--------|--------|\n+| **file_parser** | `modules/file_parser/` | 🔴 Not migrated | No GTS IDs, inline `Problem::new()` |\n+| **types-registry** | `modules/system/types-registry/` | 🟡 Partial | Has codes but not GTS format (e.g., `TYPES_REGISTRY_NOT_FOUND`) |\n+| **nodes_registry** | `modules/system/nodes_registry/` | 🔴 Not migrated | Non-GTS codes (e.g., `NODES_NOT_FOUND`) |\n+| **api_gateway** | `modules/system/api_gateway/` | 🔴 Not migrated | No Problem struct, simple error codes |\n+| **tenant_resolver** | `modules/system/tenant_resolver/` | 🔴 Not migrated | No GTS IDs |\n+| **simple-user-settings** | `modules/simple-user-settings/` | 🟡 Partial | Uses `declare_errors!` with old chain format |\n+| **modkit-auth** | `libs/modkit-auth/` | 🔴 Not migrated | No GTS IDs, custom `IntoResponse` |\n+| **modkit-odata** | `libs/modkit-odata/` | 🟡 Partial | Uses `declare_errors!` with old chain format |\n+| **users_info** (example) | `examples/modkit/users_info/` | 🟡 Partial | Uses `declare_errors!` with old chain format |\n+\n+#### Legend\n+- 🟢 **Migrated** - Uses `#[gts_error]` structs with proper base types\n+- 🟡 **Partial** - Has GTS IDs but uses deprecated `declare_errors!` or old format\n+- 🔴 **Not migrated** - No GTS IDs or non-GTS format codes\n+\n+#### GTS ID Format Note\n+\n+**Old chain format** (used by `declare_errors!`):\n+```\n+gts.hx.core.errors.err.v1~hx.module.error_name.v1\n+```\n+\n+**New format** (with `base` field):\n+```\n+gts.hx.module.namespace.error_name.v1~\n+```\n+The `base` field in `#[gts_error]` replaces the chain suffix, making inheritance explicit in code.\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Requirements\n+\n+### R1: Error Schema Requirements\n+\n+Every error returned from REST API MUST conform to the unified schema:\n+\n+```rust\n+pub struct Problem {\n+    // =========================================================================\n+    // REQUIRED FIELDS - Core error identification\n+    // =========================================================================\n+    \n+    /// URI reference identifying the problem type (GTS-based)\n+    /// Example: \"https://docs.hyperspot.com/errors/types_registry_entity_not_found_v1\"\n+    #[serde(rename = \"type\")]\n+    pub type_url: String,\n+    \n+    /// Human-readable summary of the problem type (static per error type)\n+    pub title: String,\n+    \n+    /// GTS error code (machine-readable identifier)\n+    pub code: String,\n+    \n+    /// Trace ID for request correlation\n+    pub trace_id: String,\n+    \n+    // =========================================================================\n+    // CONTEXTUAL FIELDS - Optional based on error context\n+    // =========================================================================\n+    \n+    /// HTTP status code. Optional because:\n+    /// - gRPC errors use different status codes\n+    /// - Internal/domain errors may not have HTTP context\n+    /// - Event-driven systems have no request/response\n+    /// When serializing for HTTP response, this is populated from error definition.\n+    #[serde(skip_serializing_if = \"Option::is_none\")]\n+    pub status: Option<u16>,\n+    \n+    /// Human-readable explanation specific to this occurrence.\n+    /// Optional - title may be sufficient for simple errors.\n+    #[serde(skip_serializing_if = \"Option::is_none\")]\n+    pub detail: Option<String>,\n+    \n+    /// Error category for client handling.\n+    /// Optional - can be inferred from base type hierarchy.\n+    #[serde(skip_serializing_if = \"Option::is_none\")]\n+    pub category: Option<ErrorCategory>,\n+    \n+    /// Whether client can retry this request.\n+    /// Optional - can be inferred from base type; not relevant for all contexts.\n+    #[serde(skip_serializing_if = \"Option::is_none\")]\n+    pub retryable: Option<bool>,\n+    \n+    /// URI identifying this specific occurrence (auto-populated from request path)\n+    #[serde(skip_serializing_if = \"Option::is_none\")]\n+    pub instance: Option<String>,\n+    \n+    /// Structured metadata (key-value context)\n+    #[serde(skip_serializing_if = \"Option::is_none\")]\n+    pub metadata: Option<HashMap<String, String>>,\n+    \n+    /// Validation errors for 4xx responses\n+    #[serde(skip_serializing_if = \"Option::is_none\")]\n+    pub errors: Option<Vec<ValidationViolation>>,\n+    \n+    /// Upstream error chain (when error_stack enabled)\n+    #[serde(skip_serializing_if = \"Option::is_none\")]\n+    pub upstream_errors: Option<Vec<UpstreamError>>,\n+}\n+\n+pub enum ErrorCategory {\n+    /// Platform-level execution errors (panics, OOM, internal bugs)\n+    System,\n+    /// Infrastructure/operational issues (DB unavailable, service down, rate limits)\n+    Operational,\n+    /// Client input/request errors (validation, not found, unauthorized)\n+    Client,\n+}\n+```\n+\n+#### Field Requirements Summary\n+\n+| Field | Required | Reason |\n+|-------|----------|--------|\n+| `type_url` | ✅ Yes | RFC 9457 requires problem type URI |\n+| `title` | ✅ Yes | Human-readable error name (static per type) |\n+| `code` | ✅ Yes | GTS identifier for machine processing |\n+| `trace_id` | ✅ Yes | Request correlation for debugging |\n+| `status` | ❌ No | Only relevant for HTTP; gRPC/events/domain errors don't need it |\n+| `detail` | ❌ No | Instance-specific message; title may suffice |\n+| `category` | ❌ No | Inherited from base type hierarchy |\n+| `retryable` | ❌ No | Inherited from base type; not relevant for all contexts |\n+| `instance` | ❌ No | Auto-populated from request path when applicable |\n+| `metadata` | ❌ No | Additional context key-value pairs |\n+| `errors` | ❌ No | Validation violations for 4xx errors |\n+| `upstream_errors` | ❌ No | Error chain from upstream services |\n+\n+**Note:** When converting to HTTP response, `status` is populated from the error definition. When the error is used in non-HTTP contexts (gRPC, domain logic, events), `status` remains `None`.\n+\n+### R2: GTS Identifier and Base Type Requirements\n+\n+Every error MUST have a valid GTS identifier and specify its base type using the `base` field.\n+\n+#### GTS ID Format\n+\n+```\n+gts.<vendor>.<package>.<namespace>.<type>.v<version>~\n+```\n+\n+**Examples:**\n+- `gts.hx.types_registry.entity.not_found.v1~` - Types registry not found error\n+- `gts.hx.file_parser.validation.invalid_format.v1~` - File parser validation error\n+- `gts.hx.system.runtime.timeout.v1~` - System timeout error\n+\n+#### Base Type Chaining\n+\n+Errors form an inheritance chain using the `base` field. The `base` field references another error struct type (not a string literal), similar to how `struct_to_gts_schema` works.\n+\n+The root base error type is:\n+\n+```rust\n+/// Root error type for all GTS errors.\n+#[gts_error(\n+    gts_id = \"gts.hx.core.errors.err.v1~\",\n+    base = true,  // Marks this as a root base type (no parent)\n+    title = \"Error\",\n+    // Optional attributes with defaults for inheritance:\n+    status = 500,        // Default HTTP status (optional, inherited by children)\n+    category = \"System\", // Default category (optional, inherited by children)\n+    retryable = false    // Default retryable (optional, inherited by children)\n+)]\n+pub struct BaseError;\n+```\n+\n+All module-specific errors MUST reference their base type as a struct (extending the appropriate logical/system error):\n+\n+```rust\n+use modkit_errors::system::logical::NotFoundError;\n+\n+/// Entity was not found in the types registry.\n+/// Note: status, category, retryable are inherited from NotFoundError if not specified.\n+#[gts_error(\n+    gts_id = \"gts.hx.types_registry.entity.not_found.v1~\",\n+    base = NotFoundError,  // Extends logical.not_found, not BaseError\n+    title = \"Entity Not Found\",\n+    // These are optional - inherited from base if omitted:\n+    // status = 404,      // Inherited from NotFoundError\n+    // category = \"Client\", // Inherited from NotFoundError  \n+    // retryable = false,   // Inherited from NotFoundError\n+)]\n+pub struct EntityNotFoundError {\n+    pub gts_id: String,\n+}","path":"intended_design/UNIFIED_ERROR_SYSTEM.md","commit_id":"5bdb0f43b25858af78999718f7247813802b9634","original_commit_id":"5bdb0f43b25858af78999718f7247813802b9634","user":{"login":"Artifizer","id":192502778,"node_id":"U_kgDOC3lb-g","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/192502778?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer","html_url":"https://github.com/Artifizer","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Please show an example of how such error needs to be instantiated in the code","created_at":"2026-01-30T21:07:31Z","updated_at":"2026-01-30T21:23:01Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/290#discussion_r2747987436","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/290","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2747987436"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/290#discussion_r2747987436"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/290"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2747987436/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":null,"original_line":312,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"MEMBER","original_position":312,"position":1,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2747994773","pull_request_review_id":3710446544,"id":2747994773,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs6jyxKV","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,1574 @@\n+# Unified Error System - Intention Document\n+\n+This document defines the architecture, rules, and implementation plan for a unified error handling system across the Hyperspot project. All REST API errors MUST have a GTS identifier, trace ID, and be registered in the types registry.\n+\n+## Table of Contents\n+\n+1. [Executive Summary](#executive-summary)\n+2. [Industry Research](#industry-research)\n+3. [Current State Analysis](#current-state-analysis)\n+4. [Requirements](#requirements)\n+5. [Implementation Rules](#implementation-rules)\n+6. [Migration Plan](#migration-plan)\n+7. [Examples](#examples)\n+8. [HTTP Headers](#http-headers)\n+9. [Security Considerations](#security-considerations)\n+10. [Appendix A: Error Category Definitions](#appendix-a-error-category-definitions)\n+11. [Appendix B: Retryable Error Guidelines](#appendix-b-retryable-error-guidelines)\n+12. [GTS System Errors Catalog](#gts-system-errors-catalog)\n+13. [References](#references)\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Executive Summary\n+\n+### Problem Statement\n+\n+The current error handling across Hyperspot modules is inconsistent:\n+- Some modules use `declare_errors!` macro with JSON catalogs\n+- Others define errors inline without GTS codes\n+- Errors are not registered in the types registry\n+- No standardized metadata/context fields\n+- Inconsistent trace ID propagation\n+\n+### Goals\n+\n+1. **Every REST API error** MUST have a valid GTS identifier\n+2. **Every error response** MUST include a trace ID for debugging\n+3. **All error types** MUST be registered in the types registry\n+4. **Consistent error schema** across all modules following RFC 9457\n+5. **Machine-readable error codes** for programmatic handling\n+6. **Error stack propagation** for nested service calls\n+\n+### Non-Goals\n+\n+- Changing internal domain error types (only API-facing errors)\n+- Modifying logging infrastructure\n+- Changing HTTP status code semantics\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Industry Research\n+\n+### How Major Tech Companies Handle Errors\n+\n+| Company | Standard | Key Features |\n+|---------|----------|--------------|\n+| **Google** | AIP-193 + gRPC Status | `reason` (UPPER_SNAKE_CASE), `domain` (service name), `metadata` (key-value context), `ErrorInfo`, `LocalizedMessage`, `Help` links |\n+| **Amazon AWS** | Custom JSON | `errorType`, `httpStatus`, `requestId`, `message`, custom error object serialization |\n+| **Twitter/X** | JSON with `errors` array | `code` (CAPS_CASE), `message`, `parameter`, `details`, `value` |\n+| **RFC 9457** | Problem Details | `type` (URI), `title`, `status`, `detail`, `instance`, extension members |\n+\n+### Key Patterns Identified\n+\n+1. **Machine-readable identifiers** - Unique codes for programmatic handling (Google's `reason`, Twitter's `code`)\n+2. **Domain/namespace separation** - Identify error source (Google's `domain`, our GTS vendor.package)\n+3. **Structured metadata** - Key-value context without parsing messages (Google's `ErrorInfo.metadata`)\n+4. **Trace/Request IDs** - Correlation for debugging (AWS `requestId`, our `trace_id`)\n+5. **Documentation links** - URIs to error documentation (RFC 9457 `type`, Google's `Help`)\n+6. **Error categorization** - System vs User-defined, Retryable vs Non-retryable\n+\n+### Google AIP-193 ErrorInfo Structure (Reference)\n+\n+```json\n+{\n+  \"error\": {\n+    \"code\": 429,\n+    \"message\": \"The zone 'us-east1-a' does not have enough resources...\",\n+    \"status\": \"RESOURCE_EXHAUSTED\",\n+    \"details\": [\n+      {\n+        \"@type\": \"type.googleapis.com/google.rpc.ErrorInfo\",\n+        \"reason\": \"RESOURCE_AVAILABILITY\",\n+        \"domain\": \"compute.googleapis.com\",\n+        \"metadata\": {\n+          \"zone\": \"us-east1-a\",\n+          \"vmType\": \"e2-medium\"\n+        }\n+      }\n+    ]\n+  }\n+}\n+```\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Current State Analysis\n+\n+### Existing Infrastructure\n+\n+1. **`Problem` struct** (`libs/modkit-errors/src/problem.rs`) - RFC 9457 compliant\n+   - Fields: `type_url`, `title`, `status`, `detail`, `instance`, `code`, `trace_id`, `errors`\n+   - Implements `IntoResponse` for Axum with automatic trace ID enrichment\n+\n+2. **`struct_to_gts_schema` macro** (`modules/types-registry/gts-rust/gts-macros/src/lib.rs`)\n+   - Attribute macro for explicit struct definitions with GTS IDs visible in code\n+   - Generates constants: `GTS_SCHEMA_ID`, `GTS_SCHEMA_JSON`, etc.\n+   - **This pattern will be adapted for error definitions**\n+\n+3. **`declare_errors!` macro** (`libs/modkit-errors-macro/src/lib.rs`) - **TO BE DEPRECATED**\n+   - Generates type-safe error enums from JSON catalogs\n+   - Problem: GTS IDs hidden in external JSON files, not visible to LLMs\n+   - Used by: `users_info` example, `modkit-odata`\n+\n+### Gaps Identified\n+\n+| Gap | Current State | Required State |\n+|-----|---------------|----------------|\n+| **Hidden GTS IDs** | JSON-based `declare_errors!` | Explicit `#[gts_error]` structs with visible GTS IDs |\n+| **Inconsistent definitions** | Some modules use inline errors | All modules use `#[gts_error]` structs |\n+| **No types registry** | Errors not registered | All errors registered as GTS types |\n+| **Missing metadata** | No structured context | Struct fields → `metadata` map |\n+| **Partial trace IDs** | Only in `IntoResponse` | Mandatory in all error responses |\n+| **No error categories** | Flat error codes | System/Operational/Client categories |\n+| **No error stack** | Single error | Upstream error chain propagation |\n+\n+### Current Module Migration Status\n+\n+| Module | Location | Status | Issues |\n+|--------|----------|--------|--------|\n+| **file_parser** | `modules/file_parser/` | 🔴 Not migrated | No GTS IDs, inline `Problem::new()` |\n+| **types-registry** | `modules/system/types-registry/` | 🟡 Partial | Has codes but not GTS format (e.g., `TYPES_REGISTRY_NOT_FOUND`) |\n+| **nodes_registry** | `modules/system/nodes_registry/` | 🔴 Not migrated | Non-GTS codes (e.g., `NODES_NOT_FOUND`) |\n+| **api_gateway** | `modules/system/api_gateway/` | 🔴 Not migrated | No Problem struct, simple error codes |\n+| **tenant_resolver** | `modules/system/tenant_resolver/` | 🔴 Not migrated | No GTS IDs |\n+| **simple-user-settings** | `modules/simple-user-settings/` | 🟡 Partial | Uses `declare_errors!` with old chain format |\n+| **modkit-auth** | `libs/modkit-auth/` | 🔴 Not migrated | No GTS IDs, custom `IntoResponse` |\n+| **modkit-odata** | `libs/modkit-odata/` | 🟡 Partial | Uses `declare_errors!` with old chain format |\n+| **users_info** (example) | `examples/modkit/users_info/` | 🟡 Partial | Uses `declare_errors!` with old chain format |\n+\n+#### Legend\n+- 🟢 **Migrated** - Uses `#[gts_error]` structs with proper base types\n+- 🟡 **Partial** - Has GTS IDs but uses deprecated `declare_errors!` or old format\n+- 🔴 **Not migrated** - No GTS IDs or non-GTS format codes\n+\n+#### GTS ID Format Note\n+\n+**Old chain format** (used by `declare_errors!`):\n+```\n+gts.hx.core.errors.err.v1~hx.module.error_name.v1\n+```\n+\n+**New format** (with `base` field):\n+```\n+gts.hx.module.namespace.error_name.v1~\n+```\n+The `base` field in `#[gts_error]` replaces the chain suffix, making inheritance explicit in code.\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Requirements\n+\n+### R1: Error Schema Requirements\n+\n+Every error returned from REST API MUST conform to the unified schema:\n+\n+```rust\n+pub struct Problem {\n+    // =========================================================================\n+    // REQUIRED FIELDS - Core error identification\n+    // =========================================================================\n+    \n+    /// URI reference identifying the problem type (GTS-based)\n+    /// Example: \"https://docs.hyperspot.com/errors/types_registry_entity_not_found_v1\"\n+    #[serde(rename = \"type\")]\n+    pub type_url: String,\n+    \n+    /// Human-readable summary of the problem type (static per error type)\n+    pub title: String,\n+    \n+    /// GTS error code (machine-readable identifier)\n+    pub code: String,\n+    \n+    /// Trace ID for request correlation\n+    pub trace_id: String,\n+    \n+    // =========================================================================\n+    // CONTEXTUAL FIELDS - Optional based on error context\n+    // =========================================================================\n+    \n+    /// HTTP status code. Optional because:\n+    /// - gRPC errors use different status codes\n+    /// - Internal/domain errors may not have HTTP context\n+    /// - Event-driven systems have no request/response\n+    /// When serializing for HTTP response, this is populated from error definition.\n+    #[serde(skip_serializing_if = \"Option::is_none\")]\n+    pub status: Option<u16>,\n+    \n+    /// Human-readable explanation specific to this occurrence.\n+    /// Optional - title may be sufficient for simple errors.\n+    #[serde(skip_serializing_if = \"Option::is_none\")]\n+    pub detail: Option<String>,\n+    \n+    /// Error category for client handling.\n+    /// Optional - can be inferred from base type hierarchy.\n+    #[serde(skip_serializing_if = \"Option::is_none\")]\n+    pub category: Option<ErrorCategory>,\n+    \n+    /// Whether client can retry this request.\n+    /// Optional - can be inferred from base type; not relevant for all contexts.\n+    #[serde(skip_serializing_if = \"Option::is_none\")]\n+    pub retryable: Option<bool>,\n+    \n+    /// URI identifying this specific occurrence (auto-populated from request path)\n+    #[serde(skip_serializing_if = \"Option::is_none\")]\n+    pub instance: Option<String>,\n+    \n+    /// Structured metadata (key-value context)\n+    #[serde(skip_serializing_if = \"Option::is_none\")]\n+    pub metadata: Option<HashMap<String, String>>,\n+    \n+    /// Validation errors for 4xx responses\n+    #[serde(skip_serializing_if = \"Option::is_none\")]\n+    pub errors: Option<Vec<ValidationViolation>>,\n+    \n+    /// Upstream error chain (when error_stack enabled)\n+    #[serde(skip_serializing_if = \"Option::is_none\")]\n+    pub upstream_errors: Option<Vec<UpstreamError>>,\n+}\n+\n+pub enum ErrorCategory {\n+    /// Platform-level execution errors (panics, OOM, internal bugs)\n+    System,\n+    /// Infrastructure/operational issues (DB unavailable, service down, rate limits)\n+    Operational,\n+    /// Client input/request errors (validation, not found, unauthorized)\n+    Client,\n+}\n+```\n+\n+#### Field Requirements Summary\n+\n+| Field | Required | Reason |\n+|-------|----------|--------|\n+| `type_url` | ✅ Yes | RFC 9457 requires problem type URI |\n+| `title` | ✅ Yes | Human-readable error name (static per type) |\n+| `code` | ✅ Yes | GTS identifier for machine processing |\n+| `trace_id` | ✅ Yes | Request correlation for debugging |\n+| `status` | ❌ No | Only relevant for HTTP; gRPC/events/domain errors don't need it |\n+| `detail` | ❌ No | Instance-specific message; title may suffice |\n+| `category` | ❌ No | Inherited from base type hierarchy |\n+| `retryable` | ❌ No | Inherited from base type; not relevant for all contexts |\n+| `instance` | ❌ No | Auto-populated from request path when applicable |\n+| `metadata` | ❌ No | Additional context key-value pairs |\n+| `errors` | ❌ No | Validation violations for 4xx errors |\n+| `upstream_errors` | ❌ No | Error chain from upstream services |\n+\n+**Note:** When converting to HTTP response, `status` is populated from the error definition. When the error is used in non-HTTP contexts (gRPC, domain logic, events), `status` remains `None`.\n+\n+### R2: GTS Identifier and Base Type Requirements\n+\n+Every error MUST have a valid GTS identifier and specify its base type using the `base` field.\n+\n+#### GTS ID Format\n+\n+```\n+gts.<vendor>.<package>.<namespace>.<type>.v<version>~\n+```\n+\n+**Examples:**\n+- `gts.hx.types_registry.entity.not_found.v1~` - Types registry not found error\n+- `gts.hx.file_parser.validation.invalid_format.v1~` - File parser validation error\n+- `gts.hx.system.runtime.timeout.v1~` - System timeout error\n+\n+#### Base Type Chaining\n+\n+Errors form an inheritance chain using the `base` field. The `base` field references another error struct type (not a string literal), similar to how `struct_to_gts_schema` works.\n+\n+The root base error type is:\n+\n+```rust\n+/// Root error type for all GTS errors.\n+#[gts_error(\n+    gts_id = \"gts.hx.core.errors.err.v1~\",\n+    base = true,  // Marks this as a root base type (no parent)\n+    title = \"Error\",\n+    // Optional attributes with defaults for inheritance:\n+    status = 500,        // Default HTTP status (optional, inherited by children)\n+    category = \"System\", // Default category (optional, inherited by children)\n+    retryable = false    // Default retryable (optional, inherited by children)\n+)]\n+pub struct BaseError;\n+```\n+\n+All module-specific errors MUST reference their base type as a struct (extending the appropriate logical/system error):\n+\n+```rust\n+use modkit_errors::system::logical::NotFoundError;\n+\n+/// Entity was not found in the types registry.\n+/// Note: status, category, retryable are inherited from NotFoundError if not specified.\n+#[gts_error(\n+    gts_id = \"gts.hx.types_registry.entity.not_found.v1~\",\n+    base = NotFoundError,  // Extends logical.not_found, not BaseError\n+    title = \"Entity Not Found\",\n+    // These are optional - inherited from base if omitted:\n+    // status = 404,      // Inherited from NotFoundError\n+    // category = \"Client\", // Inherited from NotFoundError  \n+    // retryable = false,   // Inherited from NotFoundError\n+)]\n+pub struct EntityNotFoundError {\n+    pub gts_id: String,\n+}\n+```\n+\n+#### Multi-Level Inheritance\n+\n+Errors can form deeper inheritance chains:\n+\n+```rust\n+/// Logical not found error (platform-level).\n+#[gts_error(\n+    gts_id = \"gts.hx.system.logical.not_found.v1~\",\n+    base = BaseError,  // Platform errors extend BaseError\n+    status = 404,\n+    title = \"Not Found\",\n+    category = \"Client\",\n+    retryable = false\n+)]\n+pub struct NotFoundError;\n+\n+/// Types registry entity not found (module-level).\n+#[gts_error(\n+    gts_id = \"gts.hx.types_registry.entity.not_found.v1~\",\n+    base = NotFoundError,  // Module errors extend logical errors\n+    status = 404,\n+    title = \"Entity Not Found\",\n+    category = \"Client\",\n+    retryable = false\n+)]\n+pub struct EntityNotFoundError {\n+    pub gts_id: String,\n+}\n+```\n+\n+#### Inheritance Hierarchy\n+\n+```\n+BaseError (gts.hx.core.errors.err.v1~)                              [base = true]\n+├── Transport Errors (hx.system.transport.*)                        [base = BaseError]","path":"intended_design/UNIFIED_ERROR_SYSTEM.md","commit_id":"5bdb0f43b25858af78999718f7247813802b9634","original_commit_id":"5bdb0f43b25858af78999718f7247813802b9634","user":{"login":"Artifizer","id":192502778,"node_id":"U_kgDOC3lb-g","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/192502778?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer","html_url":"https://github.com/Artifizer","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"This inheritance is not expressed in GTS way... I'd suggest to have it like:\n```\ngts.cf.core.errors.err.v1~cf.core._.runtime.v1~...\ngts.cf.core.errors.err.v1~cf.core._.http.v1~cf.core._.not_found.v.1\n```\n","created_at":"2026-01-30T21:10:36Z","updated_at":"2026-01-30T21:23:01Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/290#discussion_r2747994773","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/290","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2747994773"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/290#discussion_r2747994773"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/290"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2747994773/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":null,"original_line":349,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"MEMBER","original_position":349,"position":1,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2747997213","pull_request_review_id":3710446544,"id":2747997213,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs6jyxwd","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,1574 @@\n+# Unified Error System - Intention Document\n+\n+This document defines the architecture, rules, and implementation plan for a unified error handling system across the Hyperspot project. All REST API errors MUST have a GTS identifier, trace ID, and be registered in the types registry.\n+\n+## Table of Contents\n+\n+1. [Executive Summary](#executive-summary)\n+2. [Industry Research](#industry-research)\n+3. [Current State Analysis](#current-state-analysis)\n+4. [Requirements](#requirements)\n+5. [Implementation Rules](#implementation-rules)\n+6. [Migration Plan](#migration-plan)\n+7. [Examples](#examples)\n+8. [HTTP Headers](#http-headers)\n+9. [Security Considerations](#security-considerations)\n+10. [Appendix A: Error Category Definitions](#appendix-a-error-category-definitions)\n+11. [Appendix B: Retryable Error Guidelines](#appendix-b-retryable-error-guidelines)\n+12. [GTS System Errors Catalog](#gts-system-errors-catalog)\n+13. [References](#references)\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Executive Summary\n+\n+### Problem Statement\n+\n+The current error handling across Hyperspot modules is inconsistent:\n+- Some modules use `declare_errors!` macro with JSON catalogs\n+- Others define errors inline without GTS codes\n+- Errors are not registered in the types registry\n+- No standardized metadata/context fields\n+- Inconsistent trace ID propagation\n+\n+### Goals\n+\n+1. **Every REST API error** MUST have a valid GTS identifier\n+2. **Every error response** MUST include a trace ID for debugging\n+3. **All error types** MUST be registered in the types registry\n+4. **Consistent error schema** across all modules following RFC 9457\n+5. **Machine-readable error codes** for programmatic handling\n+6. **Error stack propagation** for nested service calls\n+\n+### Non-Goals\n+\n+- Changing internal domain error types (only API-facing errors)\n+- Modifying logging infrastructure\n+- Changing HTTP status code semantics\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Industry Research\n+\n+### How Major Tech Companies Handle Errors\n+\n+| Company | Standard | Key Features |\n+|---------|----------|--------------|\n+| **Google** | AIP-193 + gRPC Status | `reason` (UPPER_SNAKE_CASE), `domain` (service name), `metadata` (key-value context), `ErrorInfo`, `LocalizedMessage`, `Help` links |\n+| **Amazon AWS** | Custom JSON | `errorType`, `httpStatus`, `requestId`, `message`, custom error object serialization |\n+| **Twitter/X** | JSON with `errors` array | `code` (CAPS_CASE), `message`, `parameter`, `details`, `value` |\n+| **RFC 9457** | Problem Details | `type` (URI), `title`, `status`, `detail`, `instance`, extension members |\n+\n+### Key Patterns Identified\n+\n+1. **Machine-readable identifiers** - Unique codes for programmatic handling (Google's `reason`, Twitter's `code`)\n+2. **Domain/namespace separation** - Identify error source (Google's `domain`, our GTS vendor.package)\n+3. **Structured metadata** - Key-value context without parsing messages (Google's `ErrorInfo.metadata`)\n+4. **Trace/Request IDs** - Correlation for debugging (AWS `requestId`, our `trace_id`)\n+5. **Documentation links** - URIs to error documentation (RFC 9457 `type`, Google's `Help`)\n+6. **Error categorization** - System vs User-defined, Retryable vs Non-retryable\n+\n+### Google AIP-193 ErrorInfo Structure (Reference)\n+\n+```json\n+{\n+  \"error\": {\n+    \"code\": 429,\n+    \"message\": \"The zone 'us-east1-a' does not have enough resources...\",\n+    \"status\": \"RESOURCE_EXHAUSTED\",\n+    \"details\": [\n+      {\n+        \"@type\": \"type.googleapis.com/google.rpc.ErrorInfo\",\n+        \"reason\": \"RESOURCE_AVAILABILITY\",\n+        \"domain\": \"compute.googleapis.com\",\n+        \"metadata\": {\n+          \"zone\": \"us-east1-a\",\n+          \"vmType\": \"e2-medium\"\n+        }\n+      }\n+    ]\n+  }\n+}\n+```\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Current State Analysis\n+\n+### Existing Infrastructure\n+\n+1. **`Problem` struct** (`libs/modkit-errors/src/problem.rs`) - RFC 9457 compliant\n+   - Fields: `type_url`, `title`, `status`, `detail`, `instance`, `code`, `trace_id`, `errors`\n+   - Implements `IntoResponse` for Axum with automatic trace ID enrichment\n+\n+2. **`struct_to_gts_schema` macro** (`modules/types-registry/gts-rust/gts-macros/src/lib.rs`)\n+   - Attribute macro for explicit struct definitions with GTS IDs visible in code\n+   - Generates constants: `GTS_SCHEMA_ID`, `GTS_SCHEMA_JSON`, etc.\n+   - **This pattern will be adapted for error definitions**\n+\n+3. **`declare_errors!` macro** (`libs/modkit-errors-macro/src/lib.rs`) - **TO BE DEPRECATED**\n+   - Generates type-safe error enums from JSON catalogs\n+   - Problem: GTS IDs hidden in external JSON files, not visible to LLMs\n+   - Used by: `users_info` example, `modkit-odata`\n+\n+### Gaps Identified\n+\n+| Gap | Current State | Required State |\n+|-----|---------------|----------------|\n+| **Hidden GTS IDs** | JSON-based `declare_errors!` | Explicit `#[gts_error]` structs with visible GTS IDs |\n+| **Inconsistent definitions** | Some modules use inline errors | All modules use `#[gts_error]` structs |\n+| **No types registry** | Errors not registered | All errors registered as GTS types |\n+| **Missing metadata** | No structured context | Struct fields → `metadata` map |\n+| **Partial trace IDs** | Only in `IntoResponse` | Mandatory in all error responses |\n+| **No error categories** | Flat error codes | System/Operational/Client categories |\n+| **No error stack** | Single error | Upstream error chain propagation |\n+\n+### Current Module Migration Status\n+\n+| Module | Location | Status | Issues |\n+|--------|----------|--------|--------|\n+| **file_parser** | `modules/file_parser/` | 🔴 Not migrated | No GTS IDs, inline `Problem::new()` |\n+| **types-registry** | `modules/system/types-registry/` | 🟡 Partial | Has codes but not GTS format (e.g., `TYPES_REGISTRY_NOT_FOUND`) |\n+| **nodes_registry** | `modules/system/nodes_registry/` | 🔴 Not migrated | Non-GTS codes (e.g., `NODES_NOT_FOUND`) |\n+| **api_gateway** | `modules/system/api_gateway/` | 🔴 Not migrated | No Problem struct, simple error codes |\n+| **tenant_resolver** | `modules/system/tenant_resolver/` | 🔴 Not migrated | No GTS IDs |\n+| **simple-user-settings** | `modules/simple-user-settings/` | 🟡 Partial | Uses `declare_errors!` with old chain format |\n+| **modkit-auth** | `libs/modkit-auth/` | 🔴 Not migrated | No GTS IDs, custom `IntoResponse` |\n+| **modkit-odata** | `libs/modkit-odata/` | 🟡 Partial | Uses `declare_errors!` with old chain format |\n+| **users_info** (example) | `examples/modkit/users_info/` | 🟡 Partial | Uses `declare_errors!` with old chain format |\n+\n+#### Legend\n+- 🟢 **Migrated** - Uses `#[gts_error]` structs with proper base types\n+- 🟡 **Partial** - Has GTS IDs but uses deprecated `declare_errors!` or old format\n+- 🔴 **Not migrated** - No GTS IDs or non-GTS format codes\n+\n+#### GTS ID Format Note\n+\n+**Old chain format** (used by `declare_errors!`):\n+```\n+gts.hx.core.errors.err.v1~hx.module.error_name.v1\n+```\n+\n+**New format** (with `base` field):\n+```\n+gts.hx.module.namespace.error_name.v1~\n+```\n+The `base` field in `#[gts_error]` replaces the chain suffix, making inheritance explicit in code.\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Requirements\n+\n+### R1: Error Schema Requirements\n+\n+Every error returned from REST API MUST conform to the unified schema:\n+\n+```rust\n+pub struct Problem {\n+    // =========================================================================\n+    // REQUIRED FIELDS - Core error identification\n+    // =========================================================================\n+    \n+    /// URI reference identifying the problem type (GTS-based)\n+    /// Example: \"https://docs.hyperspot.com/errors/types_registry_entity_not_found_v1\"\n+    #[serde(rename = \"type\")]\n+    pub type_url: String,\n+    \n+    /// Human-readable summary of the problem type (static per error type)\n+    pub title: String,\n+    \n+    /// GTS error code (machine-readable identifier)\n+    pub code: String,\n+    \n+    /// Trace ID for request correlation\n+    pub trace_id: String,\n+    \n+    // =========================================================================\n+    // CONTEXTUAL FIELDS - Optional based on error context\n+    // =========================================================================\n+    \n+    /// HTTP status code. Optional because:\n+    /// - gRPC errors use different status codes\n+    /// - Internal/domain errors may not have HTTP context\n+    /// - Event-driven systems have no request/response\n+    /// When serializing for HTTP response, this is populated from error definition.\n+    #[serde(skip_serializing_if = \"Option::is_none\")]\n+    pub status: Option<u16>,\n+    \n+    /// Human-readable explanation specific to this occurrence.\n+    /// Optional - title may be sufficient for simple errors.\n+    #[serde(skip_serializing_if = \"Option::is_none\")]\n+    pub detail: Option<String>,\n+    \n+    /// Error category for client handling.\n+    /// Optional - can be inferred from base type hierarchy.\n+    #[serde(skip_serializing_if = \"Option::is_none\")]\n+    pub category: Option<ErrorCategory>,\n+    \n+    /// Whether client can retry this request.\n+    /// Optional - can be inferred from base type; not relevant for all contexts.\n+    #[serde(skip_serializing_if = \"Option::is_none\")]\n+    pub retryable: Option<bool>,\n+    \n+    /// URI identifying this specific occurrence (auto-populated from request path)\n+    #[serde(skip_serializing_if = \"Option::is_none\")]\n+    pub instance: Option<String>,\n+    \n+    /// Structured metadata (key-value context)\n+    #[serde(skip_serializing_if = \"Option::is_none\")]\n+    pub metadata: Option<HashMap<String, String>>,\n+    \n+    /// Validation errors for 4xx responses\n+    #[serde(skip_serializing_if = \"Option::is_none\")]\n+    pub errors: Option<Vec<ValidationViolation>>,\n+    \n+    /// Upstream error chain (when error_stack enabled)\n+    #[serde(skip_serializing_if = \"Option::is_none\")]\n+    pub upstream_errors: Option<Vec<UpstreamError>>,\n+}\n+\n+pub enum ErrorCategory {\n+    /// Platform-level execution errors (panics, OOM, internal bugs)\n+    System,\n+    /// Infrastructure/operational issues (DB unavailable, service down, rate limits)\n+    Operational,\n+    /// Client input/request errors (validation, not found, unauthorized)\n+    Client,\n+}\n+```\n+\n+#### Field Requirements Summary\n+\n+| Field | Required | Reason |\n+|-------|----------|--------|\n+| `type_url` | ✅ Yes | RFC 9457 requires problem type URI |\n+| `title` | ✅ Yes | Human-readable error name (static per type) |\n+| `code` | ✅ Yes | GTS identifier for machine processing |\n+| `trace_id` | ✅ Yes | Request correlation for debugging |\n+| `status` | ❌ No | Only relevant for HTTP; gRPC/events/domain errors don't need it |\n+| `detail` | ❌ No | Instance-specific message; title may suffice |\n+| `category` | ❌ No | Inherited from base type hierarchy |\n+| `retryable` | ❌ No | Inherited from base type; not relevant for all contexts |\n+| `instance` | ❌ No | Auto-populated from request path when applicable |\n+| `metadata` | ❌ No | Additional context key-value pairs |\n+| `errors` | ❌ No | Validation violations for 4xx errors |\n+| `upstream_errors` | ❌ No | Error chain from upstream services |\n+\n+**Note:** When converting to HTTP response, `status` is populated from the error definition. When the error is used in non-HTTP contexts (gRPC, domain logic, events), `status` remains `None`.\n+\n+### R2: GTS Identifier and Base Type Requirements\n+\n+Every error MUST have a valid GTS identifier and specify its base type using the `base` field.\n+\n+#### GTS ID Format\n+\n+```\n+gts.<vendor>.<package>.<namespace>.<type>.v<version>~\n+```\n+\n+**Examples:**\n+- `gts.hx.types_registry.entity.not_found.v1~` - Types registry not found error\n+- `gts.hx.file_parser.validation.invalid_format.v1~` - File parser validation error\n+- `gts.hx.system.runtime.timeout.v1~` - System timeout error\n+\n+#### Base Type Chaining\n+\n+Errors form an inheritance chain using the `base` field. The `base` field references another error struct type (not a string literal), similar to how `struct_to_gts_schema` works.\n+\n+The root base error type is:\n+\n+```rust\n+/// Root error type for all GTS errors.\n+#[gts_error(\n+    gts_id = \"gts.hx.core.errors.err.v1~\",\n+    base = true,  // Marks this as a root base type (no parent)\n+    title = \"Error\",\n+    // Optional attributes with defaults for inheritance:\n+    status = 500,        // Default HTTP status (optional, inherited by children)\n+    category = \"System\", // Default category (optional, inherited by children)\n+    retryable = false    // Default retryable (optional, inherited by children)\n+)]\n+pub struct BaseError;\n+```\n+\n+All module-specific errors MUST reference their base type as a struct (extending the appropriate logical/system error):\n+\n+```rust\n+use modkit_errors::system::logical::NotFoundError;\n+\n+/// Entity was not found in the types registry.\n+/// Note: status, category, retryable are inherited from NotFoundError if not specified.\n+#[gts_error(\n+    gts_id = \"gts.hx.types_registry.entity.not_found.v1~\",\n+    base = NotFoundError,  // Extends logical.not_found, not BaseError\n+    title = \"Entity Not Found\",\n+    // These are optional - inherited from base if omitted:\n+    // status = 404,      // Inherited from NotFoundError\n+    // category = \"Client\", // Inherited from NotFoundError  \n+    // retryable = false,   // Inherited from NotFoundError\n+)]\n+pub struct EntityNotFoundError {\n+    pub gts_id: String,\n+}\n+```\n+\n+#### Multi-Level Inheritance\n+\n+Errors can form deeper inheritance chains:\n+\n+```rust\n+/// Logical not found error (platform-level).\n+#[gts_error(\n+    gts_id = \"gts.hx.system.logical.not_found.v1~\",\n+    base = BaseError,  // Platform errors extend BaseError\n+    status = 404,\n+    title = \"Not Found\",\n+    category = \"Client\",\n+    retryable = false\n+)]\n+pub struct NotFoundError;\n+\n+/// Types registry entity not found (module-level).\n+#[gts_error(\n+    gts_id = \"gts.hx.types_registry.entity.not_found.v1~\",\n+    base = NotFoundError,  // Module errors extend logical errors\n+    status = 404,\n+    title = \"Entity Not Found\",\n+    category = \"Client\",\n+    retryable = false\n+)]\n+pub struct EntityNotFoundError {\n+    pub gts_id: String,\n+}\n+```\n+\n+#### Inheritance Hierarchy\n+\n+```\n+BaseError (gts.hx.core.errors.err.v1~)                              [base = true]\n+├── Transport Errors (hx.system.transport.*)                        [base = BaseError]\n+├── Runtime Errors (hx.system.runtime.*)                            [base = BaseError]\n+│   └── hx.types_registry.system.internal.v1~                       [base = runtime.internal]\n+├── HTTP Errors (hx.system.http.*)                                  [base = BaseError]\n+│   └── hx.auth.token_expired.v1~                                   [base = http.unauthorized]\n+├── gRPC Errors (hx.system.grpc.*)                                  [base = BaseError]\n+└── Logical Errors (hx.system.logical.*)                            [base = BaseError]\n+    ├── logical.not_found.v1~                                       [base = BaseError]\n+    │   ├── hx.types_registry.entity.not_found.v1~                  [base = logical.not_found]\n+    │   └── hx.db.entity.not_found.v1~                              [base = logical.not_found]\n+    ├── logical.already_exists.v1~                                  [base = BaseError]\n+    │   └── hx.types_registry.entity.already_exists.v1~             [base = logical.already_exists]\n+    └── logical.validation_failed.v1~                               [base = BaseError]\n+        └── hx.file_parser.validation.invalid_format.v1~            [base = logical.validation_failed]\n+```\n+\n+### R3: Trace ID Requirements\n+\n+- Every error response MUST include a non-empty `trace_id`\n+- Trace ID MUST be propagated from incoming request headers or generated\n+- Trace ID MUST be logged with the error for correlation","path":"intended_design/UNIFIED_ERROR_SYSTEM.md","commit_id":"5bdb0f43b25858af78999718f7247813802b9634","original_commit_id":"5bdb0f43b25858af78999718f7247813802b9634","user":{"login":"Artifizer","id":192502778,"node_id":"U_kgDOC3lb-g","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/192502778?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer","html_url":"https://github.com/Artifizer","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"IMPORTANT:\nWe log the full trace `00-<trace-id>-<span-id>-<flags>`\nBut we return only one segment in API: `<trace-id>`\n\n","created_at":"2026-01-30T21:11:38Z","updated_at":"2026-01-30T21:23:01Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/290#discussion_r2747997213","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/290","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2747997213"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/290#discussion_r2747997213"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/290"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2747997213/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":null,"original_line":369,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"MEMBER","original_position":369,"position":1,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2747999366","pull_request_review_id":3710446544,"id":2747999366,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs6jyySG","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,1574 @@\n+# Unified Error System - Intention Document\n+\n+This document defines the architecture, rules, and implementation plan for a unified error handling system across the Hyperspot project. All REST API errors MUST have a GTS identifier, trace ID, and be registered in the types registry.\n+\n+## Table of Contents\n+\n+1. [Executive Summary](#executive-summary)\n+2. [Industry Research](#industry-research)\n+3. [Current State Analysis](#current-state-analysis)\n+4. [Requirements](#requirements)\n+5. [Implementation Rules](#implementation-rules)\n+6. [Migration Plan](#migration-plan)\n+7. [Examples](#examples)\n+8. [HTTP Headers](#http-headers)\n+9. [Security Considerations](#security-considerations)\n+10. [Appendix A: Error Category Definitions](#appendix-a-error-category-definitions)\n+11. [Appendix B: Retryable Error Guidelines](#appendix-b-retryable-error-guidelines)\n+12. [GTS System Errors Catalog](#gts-system-errors-catalog)\n+13. [References](#references)\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Executive Summary\n+\n+### Problem Statement\n+\n+The current error handling across Hyperspot modules is inconsistent:\n+- Some modules use `declare_errors!` macro with JSON catalogs\n+- Others define errors inline without GTS codes\n+- Errors are not registered in the types registry\n+- No standardized metadata/context fields\n+- Inconsistent trace ID propagation\n+\n+### Goals\n+\n+1. **Every REST API error** MUST have a valid GTS identifier\n+2. **Every error response** MUST include a trace ID for debugging\n+3. **All error types** MUST be registered in the types registry\n+4. **Consistent error schema** across all modules following RFC 9457\n+5. **Machine-readable error codes** for programmatic handling\n+6. **Error stack propagation** for nested service calls\n+\n+### Non-Goals\n+\n+- Changing internal domain error types (only API-facing errors)\n+- Modifying logging infrastructure\n+- Changing HTTP status code semantics\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Industry Research\n+\n+### How Major Tech Companies Handle Errors\n+\n+| Company | Standard | Key Features |\n+|---------|----------|--------------|\n+| **Google** | AIP-193 + gRPC Status | `reason` (UPPER_SNAKE_CASE), `domain` (service name), `metadata` (key-value context), `ErrorInfo`, `LocalizedMessage`, `Help` links |\n+| **Amazon AWS** | Custom JSON | `errorType`, `httpStatus`, `requestId`, `message`, custom error object serialization |\n+| **Twitter/X** | JSON with `errors` array | `code` (CAPS_CASE), `message`, `parameter`, `details`, `value` |\n+| **RFC 9457** | Problem Details | `type` (URI), `title`, `status`, `detail`, `instance`, extension members |\n+\n+### Key Patterns Identified\n+\n+1. **Machine-readable identifiers** - Unique codes for programmatic handling (Google's `reason`, Twitter's `code`)\n+2. **Domain/namespace separation** - Identify error source (Google's `domain`, our GTS vendor.package)\n+3. **Structured metadata** - Key-value context without parsing messages (Google's `ErrorInfo.metadata`)\n+4. **Trace/Request IDs** - Correlation for debugging (AWS `requestId`, our `trace_id`)\n+5. **Documentation links** - URIs to error documentation (RFC 9457 `type`, Google's `Help`)\n+6. **Error categorization** - System vs User-defined, Retryable vs Non-retryable\n+\n+### Google AIP-193 ErrorInfo Structure (Reference)\n+\n+```json\n+{\n+  \"error\": {\n+    \"code\": 429,\n+    \"message\": \"The zone 'us-east1-a' does not have enough resources...\",\n+    \"status\": \"RESOURCE_EXHAUSTED\",\n+    \"details\": [\n+      {\n+        \"@type\": \"type.googleapis.com/google.rpc.ErrorInfo\",\n+        \"reason\": \"RESOURCE_AVAILABILITY\",\n+        \"domain\": \"compute.googleapis.com\",\n+        \"metadata\": {\n+          \"zone\": \"us-east1-a\",\n+          \"vmType\": \"e2-medium\"\n+        }\n+      }\n+    ]\n+  }\n+}\n+```\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Current State Analysis\n+\n+### Existing Infrastructure\n+\n+1. **`Problem` struct** (`libs/modkit-errors/src/problem.rs`) - RFC 9457 compliant\n+   - Fields: `type_url`, `title`, `status`, `detail`, `instance`, `code`, `trace_id`, `errors`\n+   - Implements `IntoResponse` for Axum with automatic trace ID enrichment\n+\n+2. **`struct_to_gts_schema` macro** (`modules/types-registry/gts-rust/gts-macros/src/lib.rs`)\n+   - Attribute macro for explicit struct definitions with GTS IDs visible in code\n+   - Generates constants: `GTS_SCHEMA_ID`, `GTS_SCHEMA_JSON`, etc.\n+   - **This pattern will be adapted for error definitions**\n+\n+3. **`declare_errors!` macro** (`libs/modkit-errors-macro/src/lib.rs`) - **TO BE DEPRECATED**\n+   - Generates type-safe error enums from JSON catalogs\n+   - Problem: GTS IDs hidden in external JSON files, not visible to LLMs\n+   - Used by: `users_info` example, `modkit-odata`\n+\n+### Gaps Identified\n+\n+| Gap | Current State | Required State |\n+|-----|---------------|----------------|\n+| **Hidden GTS IDs** | JSON-based `declare_errors!` | Explicit `#[gts_error]` structs with visible GTS IDs |\n+| **Inconsistent definitions** | Some modules use inline errors | All modules use `#[gts_error]` structs |\n+| **No types registry** | Errors not registered | All errors registered as GTS types |\n+| **Missing metadata** | No structured context | Struct fields → `metadata` map |\n+| **Partial trace IDs** | Only in `IntoResponse` | Mandatory in all error responses |\n+| **No error categories** | Flat error codes | System/Operational/Client categories |\n+| **No error stack** | Single error | Upstream error chain propagation |\n+\n+### Current Module Migration Status\n+\n+| Module | Location | Status | Issues |\n+|--------|----------|--------|--------|\n+| **file_parser** | `modules/file_parser/` | 🔴 Not migrated | No GTS IDs, inline `Problem::new()` |\n+| **types-registry** | `modules/system/types-registry/` | 🟡 Partial | Has codes but not GTS format (e.g., `TYPES_REGISTRY_NOT_FOUND`) |\n+| **nodes_registry** | `modules/system/nodes_registry/` | 🔴 Not migrated | Non-GTS codes (e.g., `NODES_NOT_FOUND`) |\n+| **api_gateway** | `modules/system/api_gateway/` | 🔴 Not migrated | No Problem struct, simple error codes |\n+| **tenant_resolver** | `modules/system/tenant_resolver/` | 🔴 Not migrated | No GTS IDs |\n+| **simple-user-settings** | `modules/simple-user-settings/` | 🟡 Partial | Uses `declare_errors!` with old chain format |\n+| **modkit-auth** | `libs/modkit-auth/` | 🔴 Not migrated | No GTS IDs, custom `IntoResponse` |\n+| **modkit-odata** | `libs/modkit-odata/` | 🟡 Partial | Uses `declare_errors!` with old chain format |\n+| **users_info** (example) | `examples/modkit/users_info/` | 🟡 Partial | Uses `declare_errors!` with old chain format |\n+\n+#### Legend\n+- 🟢 **Migrated** - Uses `#[gts_error]` structs with proper base types\n+- 🟡 **Partial** - Has GTS IDs but uses deprecated `declare_errors!` or old format\n+- 🔴 **Not migrated** - No GTS IDs or non-GTS format codes\n+\n+#### GTS ID Format Note\n+\n+**Old chain format** (used by `declare_errors!`):\n+```\n+gts.hx.core.errors.err.v1~hx.module.error_name.v1\n+```\n+\n+**New format** (with `base` field):\n+```\n+gts.hx.module.namespace.error_name.v1~\n+```\n+The `base` field in `#[gts_error]` replaces the chain suffix, making inheritance explicit in code.\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Requirements\n+\n+### R1: Error Schema Requirements\n+\n+Every error returned from REST API MUST conform to the unified schema:\n+\n+```rust\n+pub struct Problem {\n+    // =========================================================================\n+    // REQUIRED FIELDS - Core error identification\n+    // =========================================================================\n+    \n+    /// URI reference identifying the problem type (GTS-based)\n+    /// Example: \"https://docs.hyperspot.com/errors/types_registry_entity_not_found_v1\"\n+    #[serde(rename = \"type\")]\n+    pub type_url: String,\n+    \n+    /// Human-readable summary of the problem type (static per error type)\n+    pub title: String,\n+    \n+    /// GTS error code (machine-readable identifier)\n+    pub code: String,\n+    \n+    /// Trace ID for request correlation\n+    pub trace_id: String,\n+    \n+    // =========================================================================\n+    // CONTEXTUAL FIELDS - Optional based on error context\n+    // =========================================================================\n+    \n+    /// HTTP status code. Optional because:\n+    /// - gRPC errors use different status codes\n+    /// - Internal/domain errors may not have HTTP context\n+    /// - Event-driven systems have no request/response\n+    /// When serializing for HTTP response, this is populated from error definition.\n+    #[serde(skip_serializing_if = \"Option::is_none\")]\n+    pub status: Option<u16>,\n+    \n+    /// Human-readable explanation specific to this occurrence.\n+    /// Optional - title may be sufficient for simple errors.\n+    #[serde(skip_serializing_if = \"Option::is_none\")]\n+    pub detail: Option<String>,\n+    \n+    /// Error category for client handling.\n+    /// Optional - can be inferred from base type hierarchy.\n+    #[serde(skip_serializing_if = \"Option::is_none\")]\n+    pub category: Option<ErrorCategory>,\n+    \n+    /// Whether client can retry this request.\n+    /// Optional - can be inferred from base type; not relevant for all contexts.\n+    #[serde(skip_serializing_if = \"Option::is_none\")]\n+    pub retryable: Option<bool>,\n+    \n+    /// URI identifying this specific occurrence (auto-populated from request path)\n+    #[serde(skip_serializing_if = \"Option::is_none\")]\n+    pub instance: Option<String>,\n+    \n+    /// Structured metadata (key-value context)\n+    #[serde(skip_serializing_if = \"Option::is_none\")]\n+    pub metadata: Option<HashMap<String, String>>,\n+    \n+    /// Validation errors for 4xx responses\n+    #[serde(skip_serializing_if = \"Option::is_none\")]\n+    pub errors: Option<Vec<ValidationViolation>>,\n+    \n+    /// Upstream error chain (when error_stack enabled)\n+    #[serde(skip_serializing_if = \"Option::is_none\")]\n+    pub upstream_errors: Option<Vec<UpstreamError>>,\n+}\n+\n+pub enum ErrorCategory {\n+    /// Platform-level execution errors (panics, OOM, internal bugs)\n+    System,\n+    /// Infrastructure/operational issues (DB unavailable, service down, rate limits)\n+    Operational,\n+    /// Client input/request errors (validation, not found, unauthorized)\n+    Client,\n+}\n+```\n+\n+#### Field Requirements Summary\n+\n+| Field | Required | Reason |\n+|-------|----------|--------|\n+| `type_url` | ✅ Yes | RFC 9457 requires problem type URI |\n+| `title` | ✅ Yes | Human-readable error name (static per type) |\n+| `code` | ✅ Yes | GTS identifier for machine processing |\n+| `trace_id` | ✅ Yes | Request correlation for debugging |\n+| `status` | ❌ No | Only relevant for HTTP; gRPC/events/domain errors don't need it |\n+| `detail` | ❌ No | Instance-specific message; title may suffice |\n+| `category` | ❌ No | Inherited from base type hierarchy |\n+| `retryable` | ❌ No | Inherited from base type; not relevant for all contexts |\n+| `instance` | ❌ No | Auto-populated from request path when applicable |\n+| `metadata` | ❌ No | Additional context key-value pairs |\n+| `errors` | ❌ No | Validation violations for 4xx errors |\n+| `upstream_errors` | ❌ No | Error chain from upstream services |\n+\n+**Note:** When converting to HTTP response, `status` is populated from the error definition. When the error is used in non-HTTP contexts (gRPC, domain logic, events), `status` remains `None`.\n+\n+### R2: GTS Identifier and Base Type Requirements\n+\n+Every error MUST have a valid GTS identifier and specify its base type using the `base` field.\n+\n+#### GTS ID Format\n+\n+```\n+gts.<vendor>.<package>.<namespace>.<type>.v<version>~\n+```\n+\n+**Examples:**\n+- `gts.hx.types_registry.entity.not_found.v1~` - Types registry not found error\n+- `gts.hx.file_parser.validation.invalid_format.v1~` - File parser validation error\n+- `gts.hx.system.runtime.timeout.v1~` - System timeout error\n+\n+#### Base Type Chaining\n+\n+Errors form an inheritance chain using the `base` field. The `base` field references another error struct type (not a string literal), similar to how `struct_to_gts_schema` works.\n+\n+The root base error type is:\n+\n+```rust\n+/// Root error type for all GTS errors.\n+#[gts_error(\n+    gts_id = \"gts.hx.core.errors.err.v1~\",\n+    base = true,  // Marks this as a root base type (no parent)\n+    title = \"Error\",\n+    // Optional attributes with defaults for inheritance:\n+    status = 500,        // Default HTTP status (optional, inherited by children)\n+    category = \"System\", // Default category (optional, inherited by children)\n+    retryable = false    // Default retryable (optional, inherited by children)\n+)]\n+pub struct BaseError;\n+```\n+\n+All module-specific errors MUST reference their base type as a struct (extending the appropriate logical/system error):\n+\n+```rust\n+use modkit_errors::system::logical::NotFoundError;\n+\n+/// Entity was not found in the types registry.\n+/// Note: status, category, retryable are inherited from NotFoundError if not specified.\n+#[gts_error(\n+    gts_id = \"gts.hx.types_registry.entity.not_found.v1~\",\n+    base = NotFoundError,  // Extends logical.not_found, not BaseError\n+    title = \"Entity Not Found\",\n+    // These are optional - inherited from base if omitted:\n+    // status = 404,      // Inherited from NotFoundError\n+    // category = \"Client\", // Inherited from NotFoundError  \n+    // retryable = false,   // Inherited from NotFoundError\n+)]\n+pub struct EntityNotFoundError {\n+    pub gts_id: String,\n+}\n+```\n+\n+#### Multi-Level Inheritance\n+\n+Errors can form deeper inheritance chains:\n+\n+```rust\n+/// Logical not found error (platform-level).\n+#[gts_error(\n+    gts_id = \"gts.hx.system.logical.not_found.v1~\",\n+    base = BaseError,  // Platform errors extend BaseError\n+    status = 404,\n+    title = \"Not Found\",\n+    category = \"Client\",\n+    retryable = false\n+)]\n+pub struct NotFoundError;\n+\n+/// Types registry entity not found (module-level).\n+#[gts_error(\n+    gts_id = \"gts.hx.types_registry.entity.not_found.v1~\",\n+    base = NotFoundError,  // Module errors extend logical errors\n+    status = 404,\n+    title = \"Entity Not Found\",\n+    category = \"Client\",\n+    retryable = false\n+)]\n+pub struct EntityNotFoundError {\n+    pub gts_id: String,\n+}\n+```\n+\n+#### Inheritance Hierarchy\n+\n+```\n+BaseError (gts.hx.core.errors.err.v1~)                              [base = true]\n+├── Transport Errors (hx.system.transport.*)                        [base = BaseError]\n+├── Runtime Errors (hx.system.runtime.*)                            [base = BaseError]\n+│   └── hx.types_registry.system.internal.v1~                       [base = runtime.internal]\n+├── HTTP Errors (hx.system.http.*)                                  [base = BaseError]\n+│   └── hx.auth.token_expired.v1~                                   [base = http.unauthorized]\n+├── gRPC Errors (hx.system.grpc.*)                                  [base = BaseError]\n+└── Logical Errors (hx.system.logical.*)                            [base = BaseError]\n+    ├── logical.not_found.v1~                                       [base = BaseError]\n+    │   ├── hx.types_registry.entity.not_found.v1~                  [base = logical.not_found]\n+    │   └── hx.db.entity.not_found.v1~                              [base = logical.not_found]\n+    ├── logical.already_exists.v1~                                  [base = BaseError]\n+    │   └── hx.types_registry.entity.already_exists.v1~             [base = logical.already_exists]\n+    └── logical.validation_failed.v1~                               [base = BaseError]\n+        └── hx.file_parser.validation.invalid_format.v1~            [base = logical.validation_failed]\n+```\n+\n+### R3: Trace ID Requirements\n+\n+- Every error response MUST include a non-empty `trace_id`\n+- Trace ID MUST be propagated from incoming request headers or generated\n+- Trace ID MUST be logged with the error for correlation\n+\n+### R4: Types Registry Integration\n+\n+- All error types MUST be registered in the types registry at startup\n+- Error schema MUST extend base error type: `gts.hx.core.errors.err.v1`","path":"intended_design/UNIFIED_ERROR_SYSTEM.md","commit_id":"5bdb0f43b25858af78999718f7247813802b9634","original_commit_id":"5bdb0f43b25858af78999718f7247813802b9634","user":{"login":"Artifizer","id":192502778,"node_id":"U_kgDOC3lb-g","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/192502778?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer","html_url":"https://github.com/Artifizer","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"gts.hx.core.errors.err.v1\n->\ngts.cf.core.errors.err.v1~\n\nthis is correct approach, but before you did not want it to be inherited, I'm puzzled now ...","created_at":"2026-01-30T21:12:32Z","updated_at":"2026-01-30T21:23:01Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/290#discussion_r2747999366","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/290","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2747999366"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/290#discussion_r2747999366"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/290"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2747999366/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":null,"original_line":374,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"MEMBER","original_position":374,"position":1,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2748000810","pull_request_review_id":3710446544,"id":2748000810,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs6jyyoq","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,1574 @@\n+# Unified Error System - Intention Document\n+\n+This document defines the architecture, rules, and implementation plan for a unified error handling system across the Hyperspot project. All REST API errors MUST have a GTS identifier, trace ID, and be registered in the types registry.\n+\n+## Table of Contents\n+\n+1. [Executive Summary](#executive-summary)\n+2. [Industry Research](#industry-research)\n+3. [Current State Analysis](#current-state-analysis)\n+4. [Requirements](#requirements)\n+5. [Implementation Rules](#implementation-rules)\n+6. [Migration Plan](#migration-plan)\n+7. [Examples](#examples)\n+8. [HTTP Headers](#http-headers)\n+9. [Security Considerations](#security-considerations)\n+10. [Appendix A: Error Category Definitions](#appendix-a-error-category-definitions)\n+11. [Appendix B: Retryable Error Guidelines](#appendix-b-retryable-error-guidelines)\n+12. [GTS System Errors Catalog](#gts-system-errors-catalog)\n+13. [References](#references)\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Executive Summary\n+\n+### Problem Statement\n+\n+The current error handling across Hyperspot modules is inconsistent:\n+- Some modules use `declare_errors!` macro with JSON catalogs\n+- Others define errors inline without GTS codes\n+- Errors are not registered in the types registry\n+- No standardized metadata/context fields\n+- Inconsistent trace ID propagation\n+\n+### Goals\n+\n+1. **Every REST API error** MUST have a valid GTS identifier\n+2. **Every error response** MUST include a trace ID for debugging\n+3. **All error types** MUST be registered in the types registry\n+4. **Consistent error schema** across all modules following RFC 9457\n+5. **Machine-readable error codes** for programmatic handling\n+6. **Error stack propagation** for nested service calls\n+\n+### Non-Goals\n+\n+- Changing internal domain error types (only API-facing errors)\n+- Modifying logging infrastructure\n+- Changing HTTP status code semantics\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Industry Research\n+\n+### How Major Tech Companies Handle Errors\n+\n+| Company | Standard | Key Features |\n+|---------|----------|--------------|\n+| **Google** | AIP-193 + gRPC Status | `reason` (UPPER_SNAKE_CASE), `domain` (service name), `metadata` (key-value context), `ErrorInfo`, `LocalizedMessage`, `Help` links |\n+| **Amazon AWS** | Custom JSON | `errorType`, `httpStatus`, `requestId`, `message`, custom error object serialization |\n+| **Twitter/X** | JSON with `errors` array | `code` (CAPS_CASE), `message`, `parameter`, `details`, `value` |\n+| **RFC 9457** | Problem Details | `type` (URI), `title`, `status`, `detail`, `instance`, extension members |\n+\n+### Key Patterns Identified\n+\n+1. **Machine-readable identifiers** - Unique codes for programmatic handling (Google's `reason`, Twitter's `code`)\n+2. **Domain/namespace separation** - Identify error source (Google's `domain`, our GTS vendor.package)\n+3. **Structured metadata** - Key-value context without parsing messages (Google's `ErrorInfo.metadata`)\n+4. **Trace/Request IDs** - Correlation for debugging (AWS `requestId`, our `trace_id`)\n+5. **Documentation links** - URIs to error documentation (RFC 9457 `type`, Google's `Help`)\n+6. **Error categorization** - System vs User-defined, Retryable vs Non-retryable\n+\n+### Google AIP-193 ErrorInfo Structure (Reference)\n+\n+```json\n+{\n+  \"error\": {\n+    \"code\": 429,\n+    \"message\": \"The zone 'us-east1-a' does not have enough resources...\",\n+    \"status\": \"RESOURCE_EXHAUSTED\",\n+    \"details\": [\n+      {\n+        \"@type\": \"type.googleapis.com/google.rpc.ErrorInfo\",\n+        \"reason\": \"RESOURCE_AVAILABILITY\",\n+        \"domain\": \"compute.googleapis.com\",\n+        \"metadata\": {\n+          \"zone\": \"us-east1-a\",\n+          \"vmType\": \"e2-medium\"\n+        }\n+      }\n+    ]\n+  }\n+}\n+```\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Current State Analysis\n+\n+### Existing Infrastructure\n+\n+1. **`Problem` struct** (`libs/modkit-errors/src/problem.rs`) - RFC 9457 compliant\n+   - Fields: `type_url`, `title`, `status`, `detail`, `instance`, `code`, `trace_id`, `errors`\n+   - Implements `IntoResponse` for Axum with automatic trace ID enrichment\n+\n+2. **`struct_to_gts_schema` macro** (`modules/types-registry/gts-rust/gts-macros/src/lib.rs`)\n+   - Attribute macro for explicit struct definitions with GTS IDs visible in code\n+   - Generates constants: `GTS_SCHEMA_ID`, `GTS_SCHEMA_JSON`, etc.\n+   - **This pattern will be adapted for error definitions**\n+\n+3. **`declare_errors!` macro** (`libs/modkit-errors-macro/src/lib.rs`) - **TO BE DEPRECATED**\n+   - Generates type-safe error enums from JSON catalogs\n+   - Problem: GTS IDs hidden in external JSON files, not visible to LLMs\n+   - Used by: `users_info` example, `modkit-odata`\n+\n+### Gaps Identified\n+\n+| Gap | Current State | Required State |\n+|-----|---------------|----------------|\n+| **Hidden GTS IDs** | JSON-based `declare_errors!` | Explicit `#[gts_error]` structs with visible GTS IDs |\n+| **Inconsistent definitions** | Some modules use inline errors | All modules use `#[gts_error]` structs |\n+| **No types registry** | Errors not registered | All errors registered as GTS types |\n+| **Missing metadata** | No structured context | Struct fields → `metadata` map |\n+| **Partial trace IDs** | Only in `IntoResponse` | Mandatory in all error responses |\n+| **No error categories** | Flat error codes | System/Operational/Client categories |\n+| **No error stack** | Single error | Upstream error chain propagation |\n+\n+### Current Module Migration Status\n+\n+| Module | Location | Status | Issues |\n+|--------|----------|--------|--------|\n+| **file_parser** | `modules/file_parser/` | 🔴 Not migrated | No GTS IDs, inline `Problem::new()` |\n+| **types-registry** | `modules/system/types-registry/` | 🟡 Partial | Has codes but not GTS format (e.g., `TYPES_REGISTRY_NOT_FOUND`) |\n+| **nodes_registry** | `modules/system/nodes_registry/` | 🔴 Not migrated | Non-GTS codes (e.g., `NODES_NOT_FOUND`) |\n+| **api_gateway** | `modules/system/api_gateway/` | 🔴 Not migrated | No Problem struct, simple error codes |\n+| **tenant_resolver** | `modules/system/tenant_resolver/` | 🔴 Not migrated | No GTS IDs |\n+| **simple-user-settings** | `modules/simple-user-settings/` | 🟡 Partial | Uses `declare_errors!` with old chain format |\n+| **modkit-auth** | `libs/modkit-auth/` | 🔴 Not migrated | No GTS IDs, custom `IntoResponse` |\n+| **modkit-odata** | `libs/modkit-odata/` | 🟡 Partial | Uses `declare_errors!` with old chain format |\n+| **users_info** (example) | `examples/modkit/users_info/` | 🟡 Partial | Uses `declare_errors!` with old chain format |\n+\n+#### Legend\n+- 🟢 **Migrated** - Uses `#[gts_error]` structs with proper base types\n+- 🟡 **Partial** - Has GTS IDs but uses deprecated `declare_errors!` or old format\n+- 🔴 **Not migrated** - No GTS IDs or non-GTS format codes\n+\n+#### GTS ID Format Note\n+\n+**Old chain format** (used by `declare_errors!`):\n+```\n+gts.hx.core.errors.err.v1~hx.module.error_name.v1\n+```\n+\n+**New format** (with `base` field):\n+```\n+gts.hx.module.namespace.error_name.v1~\n+```\n+The `base` field in `#[gts_error]` replaces the chain suffix, making inheritance explicit in code.\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Requirements\n+\n+### R1: Error Schema Requirements\n+\n+Every error returned from REST API MUST conform to the unified schema:\n+\n+```rust\n+pub struct Problem {\n+    // =========================================================================\n+    // REQUIRED FIELDS - Core error identification\n+    // =========================================================================\n+    \n+    /// URI reference identifying the problem type (GTS-based)\n+    /// Example: \"https://docs.hyperspot.com/errors/types_registry_entity_not_found_v1\"\n+    #[serde(rename = \"type\")]\n+    pub type_url: String,\n+    \n+    /// Human-readable summary of the problem type (static per error type)\n+    pub title: String,\n+    \n+    /// GTS error code (machine-readable identifier)\n+    pub code: String,\n+    \n+    /// Trace ID for request correlation\n+    pub trace_id: String,\n+    \n+    // =========================================================================\n+    // CONTEXTUAL FIELDS - Optional based on error context\n+    // =========================================================================\n+    \n+    /// HTTP status code. Optional because:\n+    /// - gRPC errors use different status codes\n+    /// - Internal/domain errors may not have HTTP context\n+    /// - Event-driven systems have no request/response\n+    /// When serializing for HTTP response, this is populated from error definition.\n+    #[serde(skip_serializing_if = \"Option::is_none\")]\n+    pub status: Option<u16>,\n+    \n+    /// Human-readable explanation specific to this occurrence.\n+    /// Optional - title may be sufficient for simple errors.\n+    #[serde(skip_serializing_if = \"Option::is_none\")]\n+    pub detail: Option<String>,\n+    \n+    /// Error category for client handling.\n+    /// Optional - can be inferred from base type hierarchy.\n+    #[serde(skip_serializing_if = \"Option::is_none\")]\n+    pub category: Option<ErrorCategory>,\n+    \n+    /// Whether client can retry this request.\n+    /// Optional - can be inferred from base type; not relevant for all contexts.\n+    #[serde(skip_serializing_if = \"Option::is_none\")]\n+    pub retryable: Option<bool>,\n+    \n+    /// URI identifying this specific occurrence (auto-populated from request path)\n+    #[serde(skip_serializing_if = \"Option::is_none\")]\n+    pub instance: Option<String>,\n+    \n+    /// Structured metadata (key-value context)\n+    #[serde(skip_serializing_if = \"Option::is_none\")]\n+    pub metadata: Option<HashMap<String, String>>,\n+    \n+    /// Validation errors for 4xx responses\n+    #[serde(skip_serializing_if = \"Option::is_none\")]\n+    pub errors: Option<Vec<ValidationViolation>>,\n+    \n+    /// Upstream error chain (when error_stack enabled)\n+    #[serde(skip_serializing_if = \"Option::is_none\")]\n+    pub upstream_errors: Option<Vec<UpstreamError>>,\n+}\n+\n+pub enum ErrorCategory {\n+    /// Platform-level execution errors (panics, OOM, internal bugs)\n+    System,\n+    /// Infrastructure/operational issues (DB unavailable, service down, rate limits)\n+    Operational,\n+    /// Client input/request errors (validation, not found, unauthorized)\n+    Client,\n+}\n+```\n+\n+#### Field Requirements Summary\n+\n+| Field | Required | Reason |\n+|-------|----------|--------|\n+| `type_url` | ✅ Yes | RFC 9457 requires problem type URI |\n+| `title` | ✅ Yes | Human-readable error name (static per type) |\n+| `code` | ✅ Yes | GTS identifier for machine processing |\n+| `trace_id` | ✅ Yes | Request correlation for debugging |\n+| `status` | ❌ No | Only relevant for HTTP; gRPC/events/domain errors don't need it |\n+| `detail` | ❌ No | Instance-specific message; title may suffice |\n+| `category` | ❌ No | Inherited from base type hierarchy |\n+| `retryable` | ❌ No | Inherited from base type; not relevant for all contexts |\n+| `instance` | ❌ No | Auto-populated from request path when applicable |\n+| `metadata` | ❌ No | Additional context key-value pairs |\n+| `errors` | ❌ No | Validation violations for 4xx errors |\n+| `upstream_errors` | ❌ No | Error chain from upstream services |\n+\n+**Note:** When converting to HTTP response, `status` is populated from the error definition. When the error is used in non-HTTP contexts (gRPC, domain logic, events), `status` remains `None`.\n+\n+### R2: GTS Identifier and Base Type Requirements\n+\n+Every error MUST have a valid GTS identifier and specify its base type using the `base` field.\n+\n+#### GTS ID Format\n+\n+```\n+gts.<vendor>.<package>.<namespace>.<type>.v<version>~\n+```\n+\n+**Examples:**\n+- `gts.hx.types_registry.entity.not_found.v1~` - Types registry not found error\n+- `gts.hx.file_parser.validation.invalid_format.v1~` - File parser validation error\n+- `gts.hx.system.runtime.timeout.v1~` - System timeout error\n+\n+#### Base Type Chaining\n+\n+Errors form an inheritance chain using the `base` field. The `base` field references another error struct type (not a string literal), similar to how `struct_to_gts_schema` works.\n+\n+The root base error type is:\n+\n+```rust\n+/// Root error type for all GTS errors.\n+#[gts_error(\n+    gts_id = \"gts.hx.core.errors.err.v1~\",\n+    base = true,  // Marks this as a root base type (no parent)\n+    title = \"Error\",\n+    // Optional attributes with defaults for inheritance:\n+    status = 500,        // Default HTTP status (optional, inherited by children)\n+    category = \"System\", // Default category (optional, inherited by children)\n+    retryable = false    // Default retryable (optional, inherited by children)\n+)]\n+pub struct BaseError;\n+```\n+\n+All module-specific errors MUST reference their base type as a struct (extending the appropriate logical/system error):\n+\n+```rust\n+use modkit_errors::system::logical::NotFoundError;\n+\n+/// Entity was not found in the types registry.\n+/// Note: status, category, retryable are inherited from NotFoundError if not specified.\n+#[gts_error(\n+    gts_id = \"gts.hx.types_registry.entity.not_found.v1~\",\n+    base = NotFoundError,  // Extends logical.not_found, not BaseError\n+    title = \"Entity Not Found\",\n+    // These are optional - inherited from base if omitted:\n+    // status = 404,      // Inherited from NotFoundError\n+    // category = \"Client\", // Inherited from NotFoundError  \n+    // retryable = false,   // Inherited from NotFoundError\n+)]\n+pub struct EntityNotFoundError {\n+    pub gts_id: String,\n+}\n+```\n+\n+#### Multi-Level Inheritance\n+\n+Errors can form deeper inheritance chains:\n+\n+```rust\n+/// Logical not found error (platform-level).\n+#[gts_error(\n+    gts_id = \"gts.hx.system.logical.not_found.v1~\",\n+    base = BaseError,  // Platform errors extend BaseError\n+    status = 404,\n+    title = \"Not Found\",\n+    category = \"Client\",\n+    retryable = false\n+)]\n+pub struct NotFoundError;\n+\n+/// Types registry entity not found (module-level).\n+#[gts_error(\n+    gts_id = \"gts.hx.types_registry.entity.not_found.v1~\",\n+    base = NotFoundError,  // Module errors extend logical errors\n+    status = 404,\n+    title = \"Entity Not Found\",\n+    category = \"Client\",\n+    retryable = false\n+)]\n+pub struct EntityNotFoundError {\n+    pub gts_id: String,\n+}\n+```\n+\n+#### Inheritance Hierarchy\n+\n+```\n+BaseError (gts.hx.core.errors.err.v1~)                              [base = true]\n+├── Transport Errors (hx.system.transport.*)                        [base = BaseError]\n+├── Runtime Errors (hx.system.runtime.*)                            [base = BaseError]\n+│   └── hx.types_registry.system.internal.v1~                       [base = runtime.internal]\n+├── HTTP Errors (hx.system.http.*)                                  [base = BaseError]\n+│   └── hx.auth.token_expired.v1~                                   [base = http.unauthorized]\n+├── gRPC Errors (hx.system.grpc.*)                                  [base = BaseError]\n+└── Logical Errors (hx.system.logical.*)                            [base = BaseError]\n+    ├── logical.not_found.v1~                                       [base = BaseError]\n+    │   ├── hx.types_registry.entity.not_found.v1~                  [base = logical.not_found]\n+    │   └── hx.db.entity.not_found.v1~                              [base = logical.not_found]\n+    ├── logical.already_exists.v1~                                  [base = BaseError]\n+    │   └── hx.types_registry.entity.already_exists.v1~             [base = logical.already_exists]\n+    └── logical.validation_failed.v1~                               [base = BaseError]\n+        └── hx.file_parser.validation.invalid_format.v1~            [base = logical.validation_failed]\n+```\n+\n+### R3: Trace ID Requirements\n+\n+- Every error response MUST include a non-empty `trace_id`\n+- Trace ID MUST be propagated from incoming request headers or generated\n+- Trace ID MUST be logged with the error for correlation\n+\n+### R4: Types Registry Integration\n+\n+- All error types MUST be registered in the types registry at startup\n+- Error schema MUST extend base error type: `gts.hx.core.errors.err.v1`\n+- Registration MUST include: code, title, status, category, retryable flag\n+\n+### R5: Standardized System Error Types\n+\n+See [GTS System Errors Catalog](#gts-system-errors-catalog) for the complete list of all system errors.\n+\n+### R6: Error Stack Propagation\n+\n+When a function calls another service/function that returns an error:\n+- The error SHOULD be wrapped with context\n+- `upstream_errors` array SHOULD contain the chain of errors\n+- Each upstream error includes: `code`, `title`, `detail`, `source`\n+- Propagation controlled by `error_stack` configuration flag\n+\n+---\n+\n+## GTS Error Code Format\n+\n+### Structure\n+\n+```\n+gts.<vendor>.<package>.<namespace>.<type>.<version>~<chain>\n+```\n+\n+### Components\n+\n+| Component | Description | Example |\n+|-----------|-------------|---------|\n+| `gts` | Global Type System prefix | `gts` |\n+| `vendor` | Organization identifier | `hx` (Hyperspot) |","path":"intended_design/UNIFIED_ERROR_SYSTEM.md","commit_id":"5bdb0f43b25858af78999718f7247813802b9634","original_commit_id":"5bdb0f43b25858af78999718f7247813802b9634","user":{"login":"Artifizer","id":192502778,"node_id":"U_kgDOC3lb-g","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/192502778?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer","html_url":"https://github.com/Artifizer","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"`cf` - CyberFabric","created_at":"2026-01-30T21:13:12Z","updated_at":"2026-01-30T21:23:01Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/290#discussion_r2748000810","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/290","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2748000810"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/290#discussion_r2748000810"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/290"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2748000810/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":null,"original_line":404,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"MEMBER","original_position":404,"position":1,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2748002365","pull_request_review_id":3710446544,"id":2748002365,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs6jyzA9","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,1574 @@\n+# Unified Error System - Intention Document\n+\n+This document defines the architecture, rules, and implementation plan for a unified error handling system across the Hyperspot project. All REST API errors MUST have a GTS identifier, trace ID, and be registered in the types registry.\n+\n+## Table of Contents\n+\n+1. [Executive Summary](#executive-summary)\n+2. [Industry Research](#industry-research)\n+3. [Current State Analysis](#current-state-analysis)\n+4. [Requirements](#requirements)\n+5. [Implementation Rules](#implementation-rules)\n+6. [Migration Plan](#migration-plan)\n+7. [Examples](#examples)\n+8. [HTTP Headers](#http-headers)\n+9. [Security Considerations](#security-considerations)\n+10. [Appendix A: Error Category Definitions](#appendix-a-error-category-definitions)\n+11. [Appendix B: Retryable Error Guidelines](#appendix-b-retryable-error-guidelines)\n+12. [GTS System Errors Catalog](#gts-system-errors-catalog)\n+13. [References](#references)\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Executive Summary\n+\n+### Problem Statement\n+\n+The current error handling across Hyperspot modules is inconsistent:\n+- Some modules use `declare_errors!` macro with JSON catalogs\n+- Others define errors inline without GTS codes\n+- Errors are not registered in the types registry\n+- No standardized metadata/context fields\n+- Inconsistent trace ID propagation\n+\n+### Goals\n+\n+1. **Every REST API error** MUST have a valid GTS identifier\n+2. **Every error response** MUST include a trace ID for debugging\n+3. **All error types** MUST be registered in the types registry\n+4. **Consistent error schema** across all modules following RFC 9457\n+5. **Machine-readable error codes** for programmatic handling\n+6. **Error stack propagation** for nested service calls\n+\n+### Non-Goals\n+\n+- Changing internal domain error types (only API-facing errors)\n+- Modifying logging infrastructure\n+- Changing HTTP status code semantics\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Industry Research\n+\n+### How Major Tech Companies Handle Errors\n+\n+| Company | Standard | Key Features |\n+|---------|----------|--------------|\n+| **Google** | AIP-193 + gRPC Status | `reason` (UPPER_SNAKE_CASE), `domain` (service name), `metadata` (key-value context), `ErrorInfo`, `LocalizedMessage`, `Help` links |\n+| **Amazon AWS** | Custom JSON | `errorType`, `httpStatus`, `requestId`, `message`, custom error object serialization |\n+| **Twitter/X** | JSON with `errors` array | `code` (CAPS_CASE), `message`, `parameter`, `details`, `value` |\n+| **RFC 9457** | Problem Details | `type` (URI), `title`, `status`, `detail`, `instance`, extension members |\n+\n+### Key Patterns Identified\n+\n+1. **Machine-readable identifiers** - Unique codes for programmatic handling (Google's `reason`, Twitter's `code`)\n+2. **Domain/namespace separation** - Identify error source (Google's `domain`, our GTS vendor.package)\n+3. **Structured metadata** - Key-value context without parsing messages (Google's `ErrorInfo.metadata`)\n+4. **Trace/Request IDs** - Correlation for debugging (AWS `requestId`, our `trace_id`)\n+5. **Documentation links** - URIs to error documentation (RFC 9457 `type`, Google's `Help`)\n+6. **Error categorization** - System vs User-defined, Retryable vs Non-retryable\n+\n+### Google AIP-193 ErrorInfo Structure (Reference)\n+\n+```json\n+{\n+  \"error\": {\n+    \"code\": 429,\n+    \"message\": \"The zone 'us-east1-a' does not have enough resources...\",\n+    \"status\": \"RESOURCE_EXHAUSTED\",\n+    \"details\": [\n+      {\n+        \"@type\": \"type.googleapis.com/google.rpc.ErrorInfo\",\n+        \"reason\": \"RESOURCE_AVAILABILITY\",\n+        \"domain\": \"compute.googleapis.com\",\n+        \"metadata\": {\n+          \"zone\": \"us-east1-a\",\n+          \"vmType\": \"e2-medium\"\n+        }\n+      }\n+    ]\n+  }\n+}\n+```\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Current State Analysis\n+\n+### Existing Infrastructure\n+\n+1. **`Problem` struct** (`libs/modkit-errors/src/problem.rs`) - RFC 9457 compliant\n+   - Fields: `type_url`, `title`, `status`, `detail`, `instance`, `code`, `trace_id`, `errors`\n+   - Implements `IntoResponse` for Axum with automatic trace ID enrichment\n+\n+2. **`struct_to_gts_schema` macro** (`modules/types-registry/gts-rust/gts-macros/src/lib.rs`)\n+   - Attribute macro for explicit struct definitions with GTS IDs visible in code\n+   - Generates constants: `GTS_SCHEMA_ID`, `GTS_SCHEMA_JSON`, etc.\n+   - **This pattern will be adapted for error definitions**\n+\n+3. **`declare_errors!` macro** (`libs/modkit-errors-macro/src/lib.rs`) - **TO BE DEPRECATED**\n+   - Generates type-safe error enums from JSON catalogs\n+   - Problem: GTS IDs hidden in external JSON files, not visible to LLMs\n+   - Used by: `users_info` example, `modkit-odata`\n+\n+### Gaps Identified\n+\n+| Gap | Current State | Required State |\n+|-----|---------------|----------------|\n+| **Hidden GTS IDs** | JSON-based `declare_errors!` | Explicit `#[gts_error]` structs with visible GTS IDs |\n+| **Inconsistent definitions** | Some modules use inline errors | All modules use `#[gts_error]` structs |\n+| **No types registry** | Errors not registered | All errors registered as GTS types |\n+| **Missing metadata** | No structured context | Struct fields → `metadata` map |\n+| **Partial trace IDs** | Only in `IntoResponse` | Mandatory in all error responses |\n+| **No error categories** | Flat error codes | System/Operational/Client categories |\n+| **No error stack** | Single error | Upstream error chain propagation |\n+\n+### Current Module Migration Status\n+\n+| Module | Location | Status | Issues |\n+|--------|----------|--------|--------|\n+| **file_parser** | `modules/file_parser/` | 🔴 Not migrated | No GTS IDs, inline `Problem::new()` |\n+| **types-registry** | `modules/system/types-registry/` | 🟡 Partial | Has codes but not GTS format (e.g., `TYPES_REGISTRY_NOT_FOUND`) |\n+| **nodes_registry** | `modules/system/nodes_registry/` | 🔴 Not migrated | Non-GTS codes (e.g., `NODES_NOT_FOUND`) |\n+| **api_gateway** | `modules/system/api_gateway/` | 🔴 Not migrated | No Problem struct, simple error codes |\n+| **tenant_resolver** | `modules/system/tenant_resolver/` | 🔴 Not migrated | No GTS IDs |\n+| **simple-user-settings** | `modules/simple-user-settings/` | 🟡 Partial | Uses `declare_errors!` with old chain format |\n+| **modkit-auth** | `libs/modkit-auth/` | 🔴 Not migrated | No GTS IDs, custom `IntoResponse` |\n+| **modkit-odata** | `libs/modkit-odata/` | 🟡 Partial | Uses `declare_errors!` with old chain format |\n+| **users_info** (example) | `examples/modkit/users_info/` | 🟡 Partial | Uses `declare_errors!` with old chain format |\n+\n+#### Legend\n+- 🟢 **Migrated** - Uses `#[gts_error]` structs with proper base types\n+- 🟡 **Partial** - Has GTS IDs but uses deprecated `declare_errors!` or old format\n+- 🔴 **Not migrated** - No GTS IDs or non-GTS format codes\n+\n+#### GTS ID Format Note\n+\n+**Old chain format** (used by `declare_errors!`):\n+```\n+gts.hx.core.errors.err.v1~hx.module.error_name.v1\n+```\n+\n+**New format** (with `base` field):\n+```\n+gts.hx.module.namespace.error_name.v1~\n+```\n+The `base` field in `#[gts_error]` replaces the chain suffix, making inheritance explicit in code.\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Requirements\n+\n+### R1: Error Schema Requirements\n+\n+Every error returned from REST API MUST conform to the unified schema:\n+\n+```rust\n+pub struct Problem {\n+    // =========================================================================\n+    // REQUIRED FIELDS - Core error identification\n+    // =========================================================================\n+    \n+    /// URI reference identifying the problem type (GTS-based)\n+    /// Example: \"https://docs.hyperspot.com/errors/types_registry_entity_not_found_v1\"\n+    #[serde(rename = \"type\")]\n+    pub type_url: String,\n+    \n+    /// Human-readable summary of the problem type (static per error type)\n+    pub title: String,\n+    \n+    /// GTS error code (machine-readable identifier)\n+    pub code: String,\n+    \n+    /// Trace ID for request correlation\n+    pub trace_id: String,\n+    \n+    // =========================================================================\n+    // CONTEXTUAL FIELDS - Optional based on error context\n+    // =========================================================================\n+    \n+    /// HTTP status code. Optional because:\n+    /// - gRPC errors use different status codes\n+    /// - Internal/domain errors may not have HTTP context\n+    /// - Event-driven systems have no request/response\n+    /// When serializing for HTTP response, this is populated from error definition.\n+    #[serde(skip_serializing_if = \"Option::is_none\")]\n+    pub status: Option<u16>,\n+    \n+    /// Human-readable explanation specific to this occurrence.\n+    /// Optional - title may be sufficient for simple errors.\n+    #[serde(skip_serializing_if = \"Option::is_none\")]\n+    pub detail: Option<String>,\n+    \n+    /// Error category for client handling.\n+    /// Optional - can be inferred from base type hierarchy.\n+    #[serde(skip_serializing_if = \"Option::is_none\")]\n+    pub category: Option<ErrorCategory>,\n+    \n+    /// Whether client can retry this request.\n+    /// Optional - can be inferred from base type; not relevant for all contexts.\n+    #[serde(skip_serializing_if = \"Option::is_none\")]\n+    pub retryable: Option<bool>,\n+    \n+    /// URI identifying this specific occurrence (auto-populated from request path)\n+    #[serde(skip_serializing_if = \"Option::is_none\")]\n+    pub instance: Option<String>,\n+    \n+    /// Structured metadata (key-value context)\n+    #[serde(skip_serializing_if = \"Option::is_none\")]\n+    pub metadata: Option<HashMap<String, String>>,\n+    \n+    /// Validation errors for 4xx responses\n+    #[serde(skip_serializing_if = \"Option::is_none\")]\n+    pub errors: Option<Vec<ValidationViolation>>,\n+    \n+    /// Upstream error chain (when error_stack enabled)\n+    #[serde(skip_serializing_if = \"Option::is_none\")]\n+    pub upstream_errors: Option<Vec<UpstreamError>>,\n+}\n+\n+pub enum ErrorCategory {\n+    /// Platform-level execution errors (panics, OOM, internal bugs)\n+    System,\n+    /// Infrastructure/operational issues (DB unavailable, service down, rate limits)\n+    Operational,\n+    /// Client input/request errors (validation, not found, unauthorized)\n+    Client,\n+}\n+```\n+\n+#### Field Requirements Summary\n+\n+| Field | Required | Reason |\n+|-------|----------|--------|\n+| `type_url` | ✅ Yes | RFC 9457 requires problem type URI |\n+| `title` | ✅ Yes | Human-readable error name (static per type) |\n+| `code` | ✅ Yes | GTS identifier for machine processing |\n+| `trace_id` | ✅ Yes | Request correlation for debugging |\n+| `status` | ❌ No | Only relevant for HTTP; gRPC/events/domain errors don't need it |\n+| `detail` | ❌ No | Instance-specific message; title may suffice |\n+| `category` | ❌ No | Inherited from base type hierarchy |\n+| `retryable` | ❌ No | Inherited from base type; not relevant for all contexts |\n+| `instance` | ❌ No | Auto-populated from request path when applicable |\n+| `metadata` | ❌ No | Additional context key-value pairs |\n+| `errors` | ❌ No | Validation violations for 4xx errors |\n+| `upstream_errors` | ❌ No | Error chain from upstream services |\n+\n+**Note:** When converting to HTTP response, `status` is populated from the error definition. When the error is used in non-HTTP contexts (gRPC, domain logic, events), `status` remains `None`.\n+\n+### R2: GTS Identifier and Base Type Requirements\n+\n+Every error MUST have a valid GTS identifier and specify its base type using the `base` field.\n+\n+#### GTS ID Format\n+\n+```\n+gts.<vendor>.<package>.<namespace>.<type>.v<version>~\n+```\n+\n+**Examples:**\n+- `gts.hx.types_registry.entity.not_found.v1~` - Types registry not found error\n+- `gts.hx.file_parser.validation.invalid_format.v1~` - File parser validation error\n+- `gts.hx.system.runtime.timeout.v1~` - System timeout error\n+\n+#### Base Type Chaining\n+\n+Errors form an inheritance chain using the `base` field. The `base` field references another error struct type (not a string literal), similar to how `struct_to_gts_schema` works.\n+\n+The root base error type is:\n+\n+```rust\n+/// Root error type for all GTS errors.\n+#[gts_error(\n+    gts_id = \"gts.hx.core.errors.err.v1~\",\n+    base = true,  // Marks this as a root base type (no parent)\n+    title = \"Error\",\n+    // Optional attributes with defaults for inheritance:\n+    status = 500,        // Default HTTP status (optional, inherited by children)\n+    category = \"System\", // Default category (optional, inherited by children)\n+    retryable = false    // Default retryable (optional, inherited by children)\n+)]\n+pub struct BaseError;\n+```\n+\n+All module-specific errors MUST reference their base type as a struct (extending the appropriate logical/system error):\n+\n+```rust\n+use modkit_errors::system::logical::NotFoundError;\n+\n+/// Entity was not found in the types registry.\n+/// Note: status, category, retryable are inherited from NotFoundError if not specified.\n+#[gts_error(\n+    gts_id = \"gts.hx.types_registry.entity.not_found.v1~\",\n+    base = NotFoundError,  // Extends logical.not_found, not BaseError\n+    title = \"Entity Not Found\",\n+    // These are optional - inherited from base if omitted:\n+    // status = 404,      // Inherited from NotFoundError\n+    // category = \"Client\", // Inherited from NotFoundError  \n+    // retryable = false,   // Inherited from NotFoundError\n+)]\n+pub struct EntityNotFoundError {\n+    pub gts_id: String,\n+}\n+```\n+\n+#### Multi-Level Inheritance\n+\n+Errors can form deeper inheritance chains:\n+\n+```rust\n+/// Logical not found error (platform-level).\n+#[gts_error(\n+    gts_id = \"gts.hx.system.logical.not_found.v1~\",\n+    base = BaseError,  // Platform errors extend BaseError\n+    status = 404,\n+    title = \"Not Found\",\n+    category = \"Client\",\n+    retryable = false\n+)]\n+pub struct NotFoundError;\n+\n+/// Types registry entity not found (module-level).\n+#[gts_error(\n+    gts_id = \"gts.hx.types_registry.entity.not_found.v1~\",\n+    base = NotFoundError,  // Module errors extend logical errors\n+    status = 404,\n+    title = \"Entity Not Found\",\n+    category = \"Client\",\n+    retryable = false\n+)]\n+pub struct EntityNotFoundError {\n+    pub gts_id: String,\n+}\n+```\n+\n+#### Inheritance Hierarchy\n+\n+```\n+BaseError (gts.hx.core.errors.err.v1~)                              [base = true]\n+├── Transport Errors (hx.system.transport.*)                        [base = BaseError]\n+├── Runtime Errors (hx.system.runtime.*)                            [base = BaseError]\n+│   └── hx.types_registry.system.internal.v1~                       [base = runtime.internal]\n+├── HTTP Errors (hx.system.http.*)                                  [base = BaseError]\n+│   └── hx.auth.token_expired.v1~                                   [base = http.unauthorized]\n+├── gRPC Errors (hx.system.grpc.*)                                  [base = BaseError]\n+└── Logical Errors (hx.system.logical.*)                            [base = BaseError]\n+    ├── logical.not_found.v1~                                       [base = BaseError]\n+    │   ├── hx.types_registry.entity.not_found.v1~                  [base = logical.not_found]\n+    │   └── hx.db.entity.not_found.v1~                              [base = logical.not_found]\n+    ├── logical.already_exists.v1~                                  [base = BaseError]\n+    │   └── hx.types_registry.entity.already_exists.v1~             [base = logical.already_exists]\n+    └── logical.validation_failed.v1~                               [base = BaseError]\n+        └── hx.file_parser.validation.invalid_format.v1~            [base = logical.validation_failed]\n+```\n+\n+### R3: Trace ID Requirements\n+\n+- Every error response MUST include a non-empty `trace_id`\n+- Trace ID MUST be propagated from incoming request headers or generated\n+- Trace ID MUST be logged with the error for correlation\n+\n+### R4: Types Registry Integration\n+\n+- All error types MUST be registered in the types registry at startup\n+- Error schema MUST extend base error type: `gts.hx.core.errors.err.v1`\n+- Registration MUST include: code, title, status, category, retryable flag\n+\n+### R5: Standardized System Error Types\n+\n+See [GTS System Errors Catalog](#gts-system-errors-catalog) for the complete list of all system errors.\n+\n+### R6: Error Stack Propagation\n+\n+When a function calls another service/function that returns an error:\n+- The error SHOULD be wrapped with context\n+- `upstream_errors` array SHOULD contain the chain of errors\n+- Each upstream error includes: `code`, `title`, `detail`, `source`\n+- Propagation controlled by `error_stack` configuration flag\n+\n+---\n+\n+## GTS Error Code Format\n+\n+### Structure\n+\n+```\n+gts.<vendor>.<package>.<namespace>.<type>.<version>~<chain>\n+```\n+\n+### Components\n+\n+| Component | Description | Example |\n+|-----------|-------------|---------|\n+| `gts` | Global Type System prefix | `gts` |\n+| `vendor` | Organization identifier | `hx` (Hyperspot) |\n+| `package` | Module/service name | `types_registry`, `file_parser` |\n+| `namespace` | Error category | `entity`, `validation`, `runtime` |\n+| `type` | Specific error type | `not_found`, `invalid_format` |\n+| `version` | Schema version | `v1`, `v1.0` |\n+| `~chain` | Base type chain | `~hx.core.errors.err.v1` |\n+\n+### Validation Rules\n+\n+1. MUST start with `gts.`\n+2. All segments MUST be lowercase alphanumeric or underscore\n+3. No empty segments allowed\n+4. Final segment MUST be version format (`vN` or `vN.M`)\n+5. MUST chain from base error type\n+\n+### Short Name Derivation\n+\n+Short accessor names derived from final GTX segment:\n+```\n+gts.hx.core.errors.err.v1~hx.types_registry.entity.not_found.v1\n+                         └─────────────────────────────────────┘\n+                                          ↓\n+                         types_registry_entity_not_found_v1()\n+```\n+\n+---\n+","path":"intended_design/UNIFIED_ERROR_SYSTEM.md","commit_id":"5bdb0f43b25858af78999718f7247813802b9634","original_commit_id":"5bdb0f43b25858af78999718f7247813802b9634","user":{"login":"Artifizer","id":192502778,"node_id":"U_kgDOC3lb-g","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/192502778?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer","html_url":"https://github.com/Artifizer","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Why you repeat it!?","created_at":"2026-01-30T21:13:53Z","updated_at":"2026-01-30T21:23:01Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/290#discussion_r2748002365","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/290","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2748002365"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/290#discussion_r2748002365"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/290"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2748002365/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":null,"original_line":430,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"MEMBER","original_position":430,"position":1,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2748011016","pull_request_review_id":3710446544,"id":2748011016,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs6jy1II","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,1574 @@\n+# Unified Error System - Intention Document\n+\n+This document defines the architecture, rules, and implementation plan for a unified error handling system across the Hyperspot project. All REST API errors MUST have a GTS identifier, trace ID, and be registered in the types registry.\n+\n+## Table of Contents\n+\n+1. [Executive Summary](#executive-summary)\n+2. [Industry Research](#industry-research)\n+3. [Current State Analysis](#current-state-analysis)\n+4. [Requirements](#requirements)\n+5. [Implementation Rules](#implementation-rules)\n+6. [Migration Plan](#migration-plan)\n+7. [Examples](#examples)\n+8. [HTTP Headers](#http-headers)\n+9. [Security Considerations](#security-considerations)\n+10. [Appendix A: Error Category Definitions](#appendix-a-error-category-definitions)\n+11. [Appendix B: Retryable Error Guidelines](#appendix-b-retryable-error-guidelines)\n+12. [GTS System Errors Catalog](#gts-system-errors-catalog)\n+13. [References](#references)\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Executive Summary\n+\n+### Problem Statement\n+\n+The current error handling across Hyperspot modules is inconsistent:\n+- Some modules use `declare_errors!` macro with JSON catalogs\n+- Others define errors inline without GTS codes\n+- Errors are not registered in the types registry\n+- No standardized metadata/context fields\n+- Inconsistent trace ID propagation\n+\n+### Goals\n+\n+1. **Every REST API error** MUST have a valid GTS identifier\n+2. **Every error response** MUST include a trace ID for debugging\n+3. **All error types** MUST be registered in the types registry\n+4. **Consistent error schema** across all modules following RFC 9457\n+5. **Machine-readable error codes** for programmatic handling\n+6. **Error stack propagation** for nested service calls\n+\n+### Non-Goals\n+\n+- Changing internal domain error types (only API-facing errors)\n+- Modifying logging infrastructure\n+- Changing HTTP status code semantics\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Industry Research\n+\n+### How Major Tech Companies Handle Errors\n+\n+| Company | Standard | Key Features |\n+|---------|----------|--------------|\n+| **Google** | AIP-193 + gRPC Status | `reason` (UPPER_SNAKE_CASE), `domain` (service name), `metadata` (key-value context), `ErrorInfo`, `LocalizedMessage`, `Help` links |\n+| **Amazon AWS** | Custom JSON | `errorType`, `httpStatus`, `requestId`, `message`, custom error object serialization |\n+| **Twitter/X** | JSON with `errors` array | `code` (CAPS_CASE), `message`, `parameter`, `details`, `value` |\n+| **RFC 9457** | Problem Details | `type` (URI), `title`, `status`, `detail`, `instance`, extension members |\n+\n+### Key Patterns Identified\n+\n+1. **Machine-readable identifiers** - Unique codes for programmatic handling (Google's `reason`, Twitter's `code`)\n+2. **Domain/namespace separation** - Identify error source (Google's `domain`, our GTS vendor.package)\n+3. **Structured metadata** - Key-value context without parsing messages (Google's `ErrorInfo.metadata`)\n+4. **Trace/Request IDs** - Correlation for debugging (AWS `requestId`, our `trace_id`)\n+5. **Documentation links** - URIs to error documentation (RFC 9457 `type`, Google's `Help`)\n+6. **Error categorization** - System vs User-defined, Retryable vs Non-retryable\n+\n+### Google AIP-193 ErrorInfo Structure (Reference)\n+\n+```json\n+{\n+  \"error\": {\n+    \"code\": 429,\n+    \"message\": \"The zone 'us-east1-a' does not have enough resources...\",\n+    \"status\": \"RESOURCE_EXHAUSTED\",\n+    \"details\": [\n+      {\n+        \"@type\": \"type.googleapis.com/google.rpc.ErrorInfo\",\n+        \"reason\": \"RESOURCE_AVAILABILITY\",\n+        \"domain\": \"compute.googleapis.com\",\n+        \"metadata\": {\n+          \"zone\": \"us-east1-a\",\n+          \"vmType\": \"e2-medium\"\n+        }\n+      }\n+    ]\n+  }\n+}\n+```\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Current State Analysis\n+\n+### Existing Infrastructure\n+\n+1. **`Problem` struct** (`libs/modkit-errors/src/problem.rs`) - RFC 9457 compliant\n+   - Fields: `type_url`, `title`, `status`, `detail`, `instance`, `code`, `trace_id`, `errors`\n+   - Implements `IntoResponse` for Axum with automatic trace ID enrichment\n+\n+2. **`struct_to_gts_schema` macro** (`modules/types-registry/gts-rust/gts-macros/src/lib.rs`)\n+   - Attribute macro for explicit struct definitions with GTS IDs visible in code\n+   - Generates constants: `GTS_SCHEMA_ID`, `GTS_SCHEMA_JSON`, etc.\n+   - **This pattern will be adapted for error definitions**\n+\n+3. **`declare_errors!` macro** (`libs/modkit-errors-macro/src/lib.rs`) - **TO BE DEPRECATED**\n+   - Generates type-safe error enums from JSON catalogs\n+   - Problem: GTS IDs hidden in external JSON files, not visible to LLMs\n+   - Used by: `users_info` example, `modkit-odata`\n+\n+### Gaps Identified\n+\n+| Gap | Current State | Required State |\n+|-----|---------------|----------------|\n+| **Hidden GTS IDs** | JSON-based `declare_errors!` | Explicit `#[gts_error]` structs with visible GTS IDs |\n+| **Inconsistent definitions** | Some modules use inline errors | All modules use `#[gts_error]` structs |\n+| **No types registry** | Errors not registered | All errors registered as GTS types |\n+| **Missing metadata** | No structured context | Struct fields → `metadata` map |\n+| **Partial trace IDs** | Only in `IntoResponse` | Mandatory in all error responses |\n+| **No error categories** | Flat error codes | System/Operational/Client categories |\n+| **No error stack** | Single error | Upstream error chain propagation |\n+\n+### Current Module Migration Status\n+\n+| Module | Location | Status | Issues |\n+|--------|----------|--------|--------|\n+| **file_parser** | `modules/file_parser/` | 🔴 Not migrated | No GTS IDs, inline `Problem::new()` |\n+| **types-registry** | `modules/system/types-registry/` | 🟡 Partial | Has codes but not GTS format (e.g., `TYPES_REGISTRY_NOT_FOUND`) |\n+| **nodes_registry** | `modules/system/nodes_registry/` | 🔴 Not migrated | Non-GTS codes (e.g., `NODES_NOT_FOUND`) |\n+| **api_gateway** | `modules/system/api_gateway/` | 🔴 Not migrated | No Problem struct, simple error codes |\n+| **tenant_resolver** | `modules/system/tenant_resolver/` | 🔴 Not migrated | No GTS IDs |\n+| **simple-user-settings** | `modules/simple-user-settings/` | 🟡 Partial | Uses `declare_errors!` with old chain format |\n+| **modkit-auth** | `libs/modkit-auth/` | 🔴 Not migrated | No GTS IDs, custom `IntoResponse` |\n+| **modkit-odata** | `libs/modkit-odata/` | 🟡 Partial | Uses `declare_errors!` with old chain format |\n+| **users_info** (example) | `examples/modkit/users_info/` | 🟡 Partial | Uses `declare_errors!` with old chain format |\n+\n+#### Legend\n+- 🟢 **Migrated** - Uses `#[gts_error]` structs with proper base types\n+- 🟡 **Partial** - Has GTS IDs but uses deprecated `declare_errors!` or old format\n+- 🔴 **Not migrated** - No GTS IDs or non-GTS format codes\n+\n+#### GTS ID Format Note\n+\n+**Old chain format** (used by `declare_errors!`):\n+```\n+gts.hx.core.errors.err.v1~hx.module.error_name.v1\n+```\n+\n+**New format** (with `base` field):\n+```\n+gts.hx.module.namespace.error_name.v1~\n+```\n+The `base` field in `#[gts_error]` replaces the chain suffix, making inheritance explicit in code.\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Requirements\n+\n+### R1: Error Schema Requirements\n+\n+Every error returned from REST API MUST conform to the unified schema:\n+\n+```rust\n+pub struct Problem {\n+    // =========================================================================\n+    // REQUIRED FIELDS - Core error identification\n+    // =========================================================================\n+    \n+    /// URI reference identifying the problem type (GTS-based)\n+    /// Example: \"https://docs.hyperspot.com/errors/types_registry_entity_not_found_v1\"\n+    #[serde(rename = \"type\")]\n+    pub type_url: String,\n+    \n+    /// Human-readable summary of the problem type (static per error type)\n+    pub title: String,\n+    \n+    /// GTS error code (machine-readable identifier)\n+    pub code: String,\n+    \n+    /// Trace ID for request correlation\n+    pub trace_id: String,\n+    \n+    // =========================================================================\n+    // CONTEXTUAL FIELDS - Optional based on error context\n+    // =========================================================================\n+    \n+    /// HTTP status code. Optional because:\n+    /// - gRPC errors use different status codes\n+    /// - Internal/domain errors may not have HTTP context\n+    /// - Event-driven systems have no request/response\n+    /// When serializing for HTTP response, this is populated from error definition.\n+    #[serde(skip_serializing_if = \"Option::is_none\")]\n+    pub status: Option<u16>,\n+    \n+    /// Human-readable explanation specific to this occurrence.\n+    /// Optional - title may be sufficient for simple errors.\n+    #[serde(skip_serializing_if = \"Option::is_none\")]\n+    pub detail: Option<String>,\n+    \n+    /// Error category for client handling.\n+    /// Optional - can be inferred from base type hierarchy.\n+    #[serde(skip_serializing_if = \"Option::is_none\")]\n+    pub category: Option<ErrorCategory>,\n+    \n+    /// Whether client can retry this request.\n+    /// Optional - can be inferred from base type; not relevant for all contexts.\n+    #[serde(skip_serializing_if = \"Option::is_none\")]\n+    pub retryable: Option<bool>,\n+    \n+    /// URI identifying this specific occurrence (auto-populated from request path)\n+    #[serde(skip_serializing_if = \"Option::is_none\")]\n+    pub instance: Option<String>,\n+    \n+    /// Structured metadata (key-value context)\n+    #[serde(skip_serializing_if = \"Option::is_none\")]\n+    pub metadata: Option<HashMap<String, String>>,\n+    \n+    /// Validation errors for 4xx responses\n+    #[serde(skip_serializing_if = \"Option::is_none\")]\n+    pub errors: Option<Vec<ValidationViolation>>,\n+    \n+    /// Upstream error chain (when error_stack enabled)\n+    #[serde(skip_serializing_if = \"Option::is_none\")]\n+    pub upstream_errors: Option<Vec<UpstreamError>>,\n+}\n+\n+pub enum ErrorCategory {\n+    /// Platform-level execution errors (panics, OOM, internal bugs)\n+    System,\n+    /// Infrastructure/operational issues (DB unavailable, service down, rate limits)\n+    Operational,\n+    /// Client input/request errors (validation, not found, unauthorized)\n+    Client,\n+}\n+```\n+\n+#### Field Requirements Summary\n+\n+| Field | Required | Reason |\n+|-------|----------|--------|\n+| `type_url` | ✅ Yes | RFC 9457 requires problem type URI |\n+| `title` | ✅ Yes | Human-readable error name (static per type) |\n+| `code` | ✅ Yes | GTS identifier for machine processing |\n+| `trace_id` | ✅ Yes | Request correlation for debugging |\n+| `status` | ❌ No | Only relevant for HTTP; gRPC/events/domain errors don't need it |\n+| `detail` | ❌ No | Instance-specific message; title may suffice |\n+| `category` | ❌ No | Inherited from base type hierarchy |\n+| `retryable` | ❌ No | Inherited from base type; not relevant for all contexts |\n+| `instance` | ❌ No | Auto-populated from request path when applicable |\n+| `metadata` | ❌ No | Additional context key-value pairs |\n+| `errors` | ❌ No | Validation violations for 4xx errors |\n+| `upstream_errors` | ❌ No | Error chain from upstream services |\n+\n+**Note:** When converting to HTTP response, `status` is populated from the error definition. When the error is used in non-HTTP contexts (gRPC, domain logic, events), `status` remains `None`.\n+\n+### R2: GTS Identifier and Base Type Requirements\n+\n+Every error MUST have a valid GTS identifier and specify its base type using the `base` field.\n+\n+#### GTS ID Format\n+\n+```\n+gts.<vendor>.<package>.<namespace>.<type>.v<version>~\n+```\n+\n+**Examples:**\n+- `gts.hx.types_registry.entity.not_found.v1~` - Types registry not found error\n+- `gts.hx.file_parser.validation.invalid_format.v1~` - File parser validation error\n+- `gts.hx.system.runtime.timeout.v1~` - System timeout error\n+\n+#### Base Type Chaining\n+\n+Errors form an inheritance chain using the `base` field. The `base` field references another error struct type (not a string literal), similar to how `struct_to_gts_schema` works.\n+\n+The root base error type is:\n+\n+```rust\n+/// Root error type for all GTS errors.\n+#[gts_error(\n+    gts_id = \"gts.hx.core.errors.err.v1~\",\n+    base = true,  // Marks this as a root base type (no parent)\n+    title = \"Error\",\n+    // Optional attributes with defaults for inheritance:\n+    status = 500,        // Default HTTP status (optional, inherited by children)\n+    category = \"System\", // Default category (optional, inherited by children)\n+    retryable = false    // Default retryable (optional, inherited by children)\n+)]\n+pub struct BaseError;\n+```\n+\n+All module-specific errors MUST reference their base type as a struct (extending the appropriate logical/system error):\n+\n+```rust\n+use modkit_errors::system::logical::NotFoundError;\n+\n+/// Entity was not found in the types registry.\n+/// Note: status, category, retryable are inherited from NotFoundError if not specified.\n+#[gts_error(\n+    gts_id = \"gts.hx.types_registry.entity.not_found.v1~\",\n+    base = NotFoundError,  // Extends logical.not_found, not BaseError\n+    title = \"Entity Not Found\",\n+    // These are optional - inherited from base if omitted:\n+    // status = 404,      // Inherited from NotFoundError\n+    // category = \"Client\", // Inherited from NotFoundError  \n+    // retryable = false,   // Inherited from NotFoundError\n+)]\n+pub struct EntityNotFoundError {\n+    pub gts_id: String,\n+}\n+```\n+\n+#### Multi-Level Inheritance\n+\n+Errors can form deeper inheritance chains:\n+\n+```rust\n+/// Logical not found error (platform-level).\n+#[gts_error(\n+    gts_id = \"gts.hx.system.logical.not_found.v1~\",\n+    base = BaseError,  // Platform errors extend BaseError\n+    status = 404,\n+    title = \"Not Found\",\n+    category = \"Client\",\n+    retryable = false\n+)]\n+pub struct NotFoundError;\n+\n+/// Types registry entity not found (module-level).\n+#[gts_error(\n+    gts_id = \"gts.hx.types_registry.entity.not_found.v1~\",\n+    base = NotFoundError,  // Module errors extend logical errors\n+    status = 404,\n+    title = \"Entity Not Found\",\n+    category = \"Client\",\n+    retryable = false\n+)]\n+pub struct EntityNotFoundError {\n+    pub gts_id: String,\n+}\n+```\n+\n+#### Inheritance Hierarchy\n+\n+```\n+BaseError (gts.hx.core.errors.err.v1~)                              [base = true]\n+├── Transport Errors (hx.system.transport.*)                        [base = BaseError]\n+├── Runtime Errors (hx.system.runtime.*)                            [base = BaseError]\n+│   └── hx.types_registry.system.internal.v1~                       [base = runtime.internal]\n+├── HTTP Errors (hx.system.http.*)                                  [base = BaseError]\n+│   └── hx.auth.token_expired.v1~                                   [base = http.unauthorized]\n+├── gRPC Errors (hx.system.grpc.*)                                  [base = BaseError]\n+└── Logical Errors (hx.system.logical.*)                            [base = BaseError]\n+    ├── logical.not_found.v1~                                       [base = BaseError]\n+    │   ├── hx.types_registry.entity.not_found.v1~                  [base = logical.not_found]\n+    │   └── hx.db.entity.not_found.v1~                              [base = logical.not_found]\n+    ├── logical.already_exists.v1~                                  [base = BaseError]\n+    │   └── hx.types_registry.entity.already_exists.v1~             [base = logical.already_exists]\n+    └── logical.validation_failed.v1~                               [base = BaseError]\n+        └── hx.file_parser.validation.invalid_format.v1~            [base = logical.validation_failed]\n+```\n+\n+### R3: Trace ID Requirements\n+\n+- Every error response MUST include a non-empty `trace_id`\n+- Trace ID MUST be propagated from incoming request headers or generated\n+- Trace ID MUST be logged with the error for correlation\n+\n+### R4: Types Registry Integration\n+\n+- All error types MUST be registered in the types registry at startup\n+- Error schema MUST extend base error type: `gts.hx.core.errors.err.v1`\n+- Registration MUST include: code, title, status, category, retryable flag\n+\n+### R5: Standardized System Error Types\n+\n+See [GTS System Errors Catalog](#gts-system-errors-catalog) for the complete list of all system errors.\n+\n+### R6: Error Stack Propagation\n+\n+When a function calls another service/function that returns an error:\n+- The error SHOULD be wrapped with context\n+- `upstream_errors` array SHOULD contain the chain of errors\n+- Each upstream error includes: `code`, `title`, `detail`, `source`\n+- Propagation controlled by `error_stack` configuration flag\n+\n+---\n+\n+## GTS Error Code Format\n+\n+### Structure\n+\n+```\n+gts.<vendor>.<package>.<namespace>.<type>.<version>~<chain>\n+```\n+\n+### Components\n+\n+| Component | Description | Example |\n+|-----------|-------------|---------|\n+| `gts` | Global Type System prefix | `gts` |\n+| `vendor` | Organization identifier | `hx` (Hyperspot) |\n+| `package` | Module/service name | `types_registry`, `file_parser` |\n+| `namespace` | Error category | `entity`, `validation`, `runtime` |\n+| `type` | Specific error type | `not_found`, `invalid_format` |\n+| `version` | Schema version | `v1`, `v1.0` |\n+| `~chain` | Base type chain | `~hx.core.errors.err.v1` |\n+\n+### Validation Rules\n+\n+1. MUST start with `gts.`\n+2. All segments MUST be lowercase alphanumeric or underscore\n+3. No empty segments allowed\n+4. Final segment MUST be version format (`vN` or `vN.M`)\n+5. MUST chain from base error type\n+\n+### Short Name Derivation\n+\n+Short accessor names derived from final GTX segment:\n+```\n+gts.hx.core.errors.err.v1~hx.types_registry.entity.not_found.v1\n+                         └─────────────────────────────────────┘\n+                                          ↓\n+                         types_registry_entity_not_found_v1()\n+```\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Types Registry Integration\n+\n+### Error Type Schema\n+\n+```json\n+{\n+  \"gts_id\": \"gts.hx.types_registry.entity.not_found.v1~\",\n+  \"kind\": \"error\",\n+  \"schema\": {\n+    \"type\": \"object\",\n+    \"extends\": \"gts.hx.system.logical.not_found.v1~\",\n+    \"properties\": {\n+      \"status\": { \"const\": 404 },\n+      \"title\": { \"const\": \"Entity Not Found\" },\n+      \"category\": { \"const\": \"Client\" },\n+      \"retryable\": { \"const\": false }\n+    }\n+  },\n+  \"metadata\": {\n+    \"module\": \"types-registry\",\n+    \"documentation_url\": \"https://docs.hyperspot.com/errors/types_registry_entity_not_found_v1\"\n+  }\n+}\n+```\n+\n+### Registration Flow\n+\n+1. Module defines errors as explicit structs with `#[gts_error]` attribute in `src/errors.rs`\n+2. Each struct generates `ERROR_DEF` constant with GTS metadata\n+3. Module implements `all_error_definitions()` function returning all error definitions\n+4. At module startup (`on_ready`), errors are registered with types registry:","path":"intended_design/UNIFIED_ERROR_SYSTEM.md","commit_id":"5bdb0f43b25858af78999718f7247813802b9634","original_commit_id":"5bdb0f43b25858af78999718f7247813802b9634","user":{"login":"Artifizer","id":192502778,"node_id":"U_kgDOC3lb-g","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/192502778?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer","html_url":"https://github.com/Artifizer","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"We still need to have eventual consistency, it's a must. No any timetouts - infinite retry","created_at":"2026-01-30T21:17:32Z","updated_at":"2026-01-30T21:23:02Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/290#discussion_r2748011016","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/290","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2748011016"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/290#discussion_r2748011016"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/290"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2748011016/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":null,"original_line":461,"side":"RIGHT","in_reply_to_id":2736265169,"author_association":"MEMBER","original_position":461,"position":1,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2748012376","pull_request_review_id":3710446544,"id":2748012376,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs6jy1dY","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,1574 @@\n+# Unified Error System - Intention Document\n+\n+This document defines the architecture, rules, and implementation plan for a unified error handling system across the Hyperspot project. All REST API errors MUST have a GTS identifier, trace ID, and be registered in the types registry.\n+\n+## Table of Contents\n+\n+1. [Executive Summary](#executive-summary)\n+2. [Industry Research](#industry-research)\n+3. [Current State Analysis](#current-state-analysis)\n+4. [Requirements](#requirements)\n+5. [Implementation Rules](#implementation-rules)\n+6. [Migration Plan](#migration-plan)\n+7. [Examples](#examples)\n+8. [HTTP Headers](#http-headers)\n+9. [Security Considerations](#security-considerations)\n+10. [Appendix A: Error Category Definitions](#appendix-a-error-category-definitions)\n+11. [Appendix B: Retryable Error Guidelines](#appendix-b-retryable-error-guidelines)\n+12. [GTS System Errors Catalog](#gts-system-errors-catalog)\n+13. [References](#references)\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Executive Summary\n+\n+### Problem Statement\n+\n+The current error handling across Hyperspot modules is inconsistent:\n+- Some modules use `declare_errors!` macro with JSON catalogs\n+- Others define errors inline without GTS codes\n+- Errors are not registered in the types registry\n+- No standardized metadata/context fields\n+- Inconsistent trace ID propagation\n+\n+### Goals\n+\n+1. **Every REST API error** MUST have a valid GTS identifier\n+2. **Every error response** MUST include a trace ID for debugging\n+3. **All error types** MUST be registered in the types registry\n+4. **Consistent error schema** across all modules following RFC 9457\n+5. **Machine-readable error codes** for programmatic handling\n+6. **Error stack propagation** for nested service calls\n+\n+### Non-Goals\n+\n+- Changing internal domain error types (only API-facing errors)\n+- Modifying logging infrastructure\n+- Changing HTTP status code semantics\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Industry Research\n+\n+### How Major Tech Companies Handle Errors\n+\n+| Company | Standard | Key Features |\n+|---------|----------|--------------|\n+| **Google** | AIP-193 + gRPC Status | `reason` (UPPER_SNAKE_CASE), `domain` (service name), `metadata` (key-value context), `ErrorInfo`, `LocalizedMessage`, `Help` links |\n+| **Amazon AWS** | Custom JSON | `errorType`, `httpStatus`, `requestId`, `message`, custom error object serialization |\n+| **Twitter/X** | JSON with `errors` array | `code` (CAPS_CASE), `message`, `parameter`, `details`, `value` |\n+| **RFC 9457** | Problem Details | `type` (URI), `title`, `status`, `detail`, `instance`, extension members |\n+\n+### Key Patterns Identified\n+\n+1. **Machine-readable identifiers** - Unique codes for programmatic handling (Google's `reason`, Twitter's `code`)\n+2. **Domain/namespace separation** - Identify error source (Google's `domain`, our GTS vendor.package)\n+3. **Structured metadata** - Key-value context without parsing messages (Google's `ErrorInfo.metadata`)\n+4. **Trace/Request IDs** - Correlation for debugging (AWS `requestId`, our `trace_id`)\n+5. **Documentation links** - URIs to error documentation (RFC 9457 `type`, Google's `Help`)\n+6. **Error categorization** - System vs User-defined, Retryable vs Non-retryable\n+\n+### Google AIP-193 ErrorInfo Structure (Reference)\n+\n+```json\n+{\n+  \"error\": {\n+    \"code\": 429,\n+    \"message\": \"The zone 'us-east1-a' does not have enough resources...\",\n+    \"status\": \"RESOURCE_EXHAUSTED\",\n+    \"details\": [\n+      {\n+        \"@type\": \"type.googleapis.com/google.rpc.ErrorInfo\",\n+        \"reason\": \"RESOURCE_AVAILABILITY\",\n+        \"domain\": \"compute.googleapis.com\",\n+        \"metadata\": {\n+          \"zone\": \"us-east1-a\",\n+          \"vmType\": \"e2-medium\"\n+        }\n+      }\n+    ]\n+  }\n+}\n+```\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Current State Analysis\n+\n+### Existing Infrastructure\n+\n+1. **`Problem` struct** (`libs/modkit-errors/src/problem.rs`) - RFC 9457 compliant\n+   - Fields: `type_url`, `title`, `status`, `detail`, `instance`, `code`, `trace_id`, `errors`\n+   - Implements `IntoResponse` for Axum with automatic trace ID enrichment\n+\n+2. **`struct_to_gts_schema` macro** (`modules/types-registry/gts-rust/gts-macros/src/lib.rs`)\n+   - Attribute macro for explicit struct definitions with GTS IDs visible in code\n+   - Generates constants: `GTS_SCHEMA_ID`, `GTS_SCHEMA_JSON`, etc.\n+   - **This pattern will be adapted for error definitions**\n+\n+3. **`declare_errors!` macro** (`libs/modkit-errors-macro/src/lib.rs`) - **TO BE DEPRECATED**\n+   - Generates type-safe error enums from JSON catalogs\n+   - Problem: GTS IDs hidden in external JSON files, not visible to LLMs\n+   - Used by: `users_info` example, `modkit-odata`\n+\n+### Gaps Identified\n+\n+| Gap | Current State | Required State |\n+|-----|---------------|----------------|\n+| **Hidden GTS IDs** | JSON-based `declare_errors!` | Explicit `#[gts_error]` structs with visible GTS IDs |\n+| **Inconsistent definitions** | Some modules use inline errors | All modules use `#[gts_error]` structs |\n+| **No types registry** | Errors not registered | All errors registered as GTS types |\n+| **Missing metadata** | No structured context | Struct fields → `metadata` map |\n+| **Partial trace IDs** | Only in `IntoResponse` | Mandatory in all error responses |\n+| **No error categories** | Flat error codes | System/Operational/Client categories |\n+| **No error stack** | Single error | Upstream error chain propagation |\n+\n+### Current Module Migration Status\n+\n+| Module | Location | Status | Issues |\n+|--------|----------|--------|--------|\n+| **file_parser** | `modules/file_parser/` | 🔴 Not migrated | No GTS IDs, inline `Problem::new()` |\n+| **types-registry** | `modules/system/types-registry/` | 🟡 Partial | Has codes but not GTS format (e.g., `TYPES_REGISTRY_NOT_FOUND`) |\n+| **nodes_registry** | `modules/system/nodes_registry/` | 🔴 Not migrated | Non-GTS codes (e.g., `NODES_NOT_FOUND`) |\n+| **api_gateway** | `modules/system/api_gateway/` | 🔴 Not migrated | No Problem struct, simple error codes |\n+| **tenant_resolver** | `modules/system/tenant_resolver/` | 🔴 Not migrated | No GTS IDs |\n+| **simple-user-settings** | `modules/simple-user-settings/` | 🟡 Partial | Uses `declare_errors!` with old chain format |\n+| **modkit-auth** | `libs/modkit-auth/` | 🔴 Not migrated | No GTS IDs, custom `IntoResponse` |\n+| **modkit-odata** | `libs/modkit-odata/` | 🟡 Partial | Uses `declare_errors!` with old chain format |\n+| **users_info** (example) | `examples/modkit/users_info/` | 🟡 Partial | Uses `declare_errors!` with old chain format |\n+\n+#### Legend\n+- 🟢 **Migrated** - Uses `#[gts_error]` structs with proper base types\n+- 🟡 **Partial** - Has GTS IDs but uses deprecated `declare_errors!` or old format\n+- 🔴 **Not migrated** - No GTS IDs or non-GTS format codes\n+\n+#### GTS ID Format Note\n+\n+**Old chain format** (used by `declare_errors!`):\n+```\n+gts.hx.core.errors.err.v1~hx.module.error_name.v1\n+```\n+\n+**New format** (with `base` field):\n+```\n+gts.hx.module.namespace.error_name.v1~\n+```\n+The `base` field in `#[gts_error]` replaces the chain suffix, making inheritance explicit in code.\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Requirements\n+\n+### R1: Error Schema Requirements\n+\n+Every error returned from REST API MUST conform to the unified schema:\n+\n+```rust\n+pub struct Problem {\n+    // =========================================================================\n+    // REQUIRED FIELDS - Core error identification\n+    // =========================================================================\n+    \n+    /// URI reference identifying the problem type (GTS-based)\n+    /// Example: \"https://docs.hyperspot.com/errors/types_registry_entity_not_found_v1\"\n+    #[serde(rename = \"type\")]\n+    pub type_url: String,\n+    \n+    /// Human-readable summary of the problem type (static per error type)\n+    pub title: String,\n+    \n+    /// GTS error code (machine-readable identifier)\n+    pub code: String,\n+    \n+    /// Trace ID for request correlation\n+    pub trace_id: String,\n+    \n+    // =========================================================================\n+    // CONTEXTUAL FIELDS - Optional based on error context\n+    // =========================================================================\n+    \n+    /// HTTP status code. Optional because:\n+    /// - gRPC errors use different status codes\n+    /// - Internal/domain errors may not have HTTP context\n+    /// - Event-driven systems have no request/response\n+    /// When serializing for HTTP response, this is populated from error definition.\n+    #[serde(skip_serializing_if = \"Option::is_none\")]\n+    pub status: Option<u16>,\n+    \n+    /// Human-readable explanation specific to this occurrence.\n+    /// Optional - title may be sufficient for simple errors.\n+    #[serde(skip_serializing_if = \"Option::is_none\")]\n+    pub detail: Option<String>,\n+    \n+    /// Error category for client handling.\n+    /// Optional - can be inferred from base type hierarchy.\n+    #[serde(skip_serializing_if = \"Option::is_none\")]\n+    pub category: Option<ErrorCategory>,\n+    \n+    /// Whether client can retry this request.\n+    /// Optional - can be inferred from base type; not relevant for all contexts.\n+    #[serde(skip_serializing_if = \"Option::is_none\")]\n+    pub retryable: Option<bool>,\n+    \n+    /// URI identifying this specific occurrence (auto-populated from request path)\n+    #[serde(skip_serializing_if = \"Option::is_none\")]\n+    pub instance: Option<String>,\n+    \n+    /// Structured metadata (key-value context)\n+    #[serde(skip_serializing_if = \"Option::is_none\")]\n+    pub metadata: Option<HashMap<String, String>>,\n+    \n+    /// Validation errors for 4xx responses\n+    #[serde(skip_serializing_if = \"Option::is_none\")]\n+    pub errors: Option<Vec<ValidationViolation>>,\n+    \n+    /// Upstream error chain (when error_stack enabled)\n+    #[serde(skip_serializing_if = \"Option::is_none\")]\n+    pub upstream_errors: Option<Vec<UpstreamError>>,\n+}\n+\n+pub enum ErrorCategory {\n+    /// Platform-level execution errors (panics, OOM, internal bugs)\n+    System,\n+    /// Infrastructure/operational issues (DB unavailable, service down, rate limits)\n+    Operational,\n+    /// Client input/request errors (validation, not found, unauthorized)\n+    Client,\n+}\n+```\n+\n+#### Field Requirements Summary\n+\n+| Field | Required | Reason |\n+|-------|----------|--------|\n+| `type_url` | ✅ Yes | RFC 9457 requires problem type URI |\n+| `title` | ✅ Yes | Human-readable error name (static per type) |\n+| `code` | ✅ Yes | GTS identifier for machine processing |\n+| `trace_id` | ✅ Yes | Request correlation for debugging |\n+| `status` | ❌ No | Only relevant for HTTP; gRPC/events/domain errors don't need it |\n+| `detail` | ❌ No | Instance-specific message; title may suffice |\n+| `category` | ❌ No | Inherited from base type hierarchy |\n+| `retryable` | ❌ No | Inherited from base type; not relevant for all contexts |\n+| `instance` | ❌ No | Auto-populated from request path when applicable |\n+| `metadata` | ❌ No | Additional context key-value pairs |\n+| `errors` | ❌ No | Validation violations for 4xx errors |\n+| `upstream_errors` | ❌ No | Error chain from upstream services |\n+\n+**Note:** When converting to HTTP response, `status` is populated from the error definition. When the error is used in non-HTTP contexts (gRPC, domain logic, events), `status` remains `None`.\n+\n+### R2: GTS Identifier and Base Type Requirements\n+\n+Every error MUST have a valid GTS identifier and specify its base type using the `base` field.\n+\n+#### GTS ID Format\n+\n+```\n+gts.<vendor>.<package>.<namespace>.<type>.v<version>~\n+```\n+\n+**Examples:**\n+- `gts.hx.types_registry.entity.not_found.v1~` - Types registry not found error\n+- `gts.hx.file_parser.validation.invalid_format.v1~` - File parser validation error\n+- `gts.hx.system.runtime.timeout.v1~` - System timeout error\n+\n+#### Base Type Chaining\n+\n+Errors form an inheritance chain using the `base` field. The `base` field references another error struct type (not a string literal), similar to how `struct_to_gts_schema` works.\n+\n+The root base error type is:\n+\n+```rust\n+/// Root error type for all GTS errors.\n+#[gts_error(\n+    gts_id = \"gts.hx.core.errors.err.v1~\",\n+    base = true,  // Marks this as a root base type (no parent)\n+    title = \"Error\",\n+    // Optional attributes with defaults for inheritance:\n+    status = 500,        // Default HTTP status (optional, inherited by children)\n+    category = \"System\", // Default category (optional, inherited by children)\n+    retryable = false    // Default retryable (optional, inherited by children)\n+)]\n+pub struct BaseError;\n+```\n+\n+All module-specific errors MUST reference their base type as a struct (extending the appropriate logical/system error):\n+\n+```rust\n+use modkit_errors::system::logical::NotFoundError;\n+\n+/// Entity was not found in the types registry.\n+/// Note: status, category, retryable are inherited from NotFoundError if not specified.\n+#[gts_error(\n+    gts_id = \"gts.hx.types_registry.entity.not_found.v1~\",\n+    base = NotFoundError,  // Extends logical.not_found, not BaseError\n+    title = \"Entity Not Found\",\n+    // These are optional - inherited from base if omitted:\n+    // status = 404,      // Inherited from NotFoundError\n+    // category = \"Client\", // Inherited from NotFoundError  \n+    // retryable = false,   // Inherited from NotFoundError\n+)]\n+pub struct EntityNotFoundError {\n+    pub gts_id: String,\n+}\n+```\n+\n+#### Multi-Level Inheritance\n+\n+Errors can form deeper inheritance chains:\n+\n+```rust\n+/// Logical not found error (platform-level).\n+#[gts_error(\n+    gts_id = \"gts.hx.system.logical.not_found.v1~\",\n+    base = BaseError,  // Platform errors extend BaseError\n+    status = 404,\n+    title = \"Not Found\",\n+    category = \"Client\",\n+    retryable = false\n+)]\n+pub struct NotFoundError;\n+\n+/// Types registry entity not found (module-level).\n+#[gts_error(\n+    gts_id = \"gts.hx.types_registry.entity.not_found.v1~\",\n+    base = NotFoundError,  // Module errors extend logical errors\n+    status = 404,\n+    title = \"Entity Not Found\",\n+    category = \"Client\",\n+    retryable = false\n+)]\n+pub struct EntityNotFoundError {\n+    pub gts_id: String,\n+}\n+```\n+\n+#### Inheritance Hierarchy\n+\n+```\n+BaseError (gts.hx.core.errors.err.v1~)                              [base = true]\n+├── Transport Errors (hx.system.transport.*)                        [base = BaseError]\n+├── Runtime Errors (hx.system.runtime.*)                            [base = BaseError]\n+│   └── hx.types_registry.system.internal.v1~                       [base = runtime.internal]\n+├── HTTP Errors (hx.system.http.*)                                  [base = BaseError]\n+│   └── hx.auth.token_expired.v1~                                   [base = http.unauthorized]\n+├── gRPC Errors (hx.system.grpc.*)                                  [base = BaseError]\n+└── Logical Errors (hx.system.logical.*)                            [base = BaseError]\n+    ├── logical.not_found.v1~                                       [base = BaseError]\n+    │   ├── hx.types_registry.entity.not_found.v1~                  [base = logical.not_found]\n+    │   └── hx.db.entity.not_found.v1~                              [base = logical.not_found]\n+    ├── logical.already_exists.v1~                                  [base = BaseError]\n+    │   └── hx.types_registry.entity.already_exists.v1~             [base = logical.already_exists]\n+    └── logical.validation_failed.v1~                               [base = BaseError]\n+        └── hx.file_parser.validation.invalid_format.v1~            [base = logical.validation_failed]\n+```\n+\n+### R3: Trace ID Requirements\n+\n+- Every error response MUST include a non-empty `trace_id`\n+- Trace ID MUST be propagated from incoming request headers or generated\n+- Trace ID MUST be logged with the error for correlation\n+\n+### R4: Types Registry Integration\n+\n+- All error types MUST be registered in the types registry at startup\n+- Error schema MUST extend base error type: `gts.hx.core.errors.err.v1`\n+- Registration MUST include: code, title, status, category, retryable flag\n+\n+### R5: Standardized System Error Types\n+\n+See [GTS System Errors Catalog](#gts-system-errors-catalog) for the complete list of all system errors.\n+\n+### R6: Error Stack Propagation\n+\n+When a function calls another service/function that returns an error:\n+- The error SHOULD be wrapped with context\n+- `upstream_errors` array SHOULD contain the chain of errors\n+- Each upstream error includes: `code`, `title`, `detail`, `source`\n+- Propagation controlled by `error_stack` configuration flag\n+\n+---\n+\n+## GTS Error Code Format\n+\n+### Structure\n+\n+```\n+gts.<vendor>.<package>.<namespace>.<type>.<version>~<chain>\n+```\n+\n+### Components\n+\n+| Component | Description | Example |\n+|-----------|-------------|---------|\n+| `gts` | Global Type System prefix | `gts` |\n+| `vendor` | Organization identifier | `hx` (Hyperspot) |\n+| `package` | Module/service name | `types_registry`, `file_parser` |\n+| `namespace` | Error category | `entity`, `validation`, `runtime` |\n+| `type` | Specific error type | `not_found`, `invalid_format` |\n+| `version` | Schema version | `v1`, `v1.0` |\n+| `~chain` | Base type chain | `~hx.core.errors.err.v1` |\n+\n+### Validation Rules\n+\n+1. MUST start with `gts.`\n+2. All segments MUST be lowercase alphanumeric or underscore\n+3. No empty segments allowed\n+4. Final segment MUST be version format (`vN` or `vN.M`)\n+5. MUST chain from base error type\n+\n+### Short Name Derivation\n+\n+Short accessor names derived from final GTX segment:\n+```\n+gts.hx.core.errors.err.v1~hx.types_registry.entity.not_found.v1\n+                         └─────────────────────────────────────┘\n+                                          ↓\n+                         types_registry_entity_not_found_v1()\n+```\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Types Registry Integration\n+\n+### Error Type Schema\n+\n+```json\n+{\n+  \"gts_id\": \"gts.hx.types_registry.entity.not_found.v1~\",\n+  \"kind\": \"error\",\n+  \"schema\": {\n+    \"type\": \"object\",\n+    \"extends\": \"gts.hx.system.logical.not_found.v1~\",\n+    \"properties\": {\n+      \"status\": { \"const\": 404 },\n+      \"title\": { \"const\": \"Entity Not Found\" },\n+      \"category\": { \"const\": \"Client\" },\n+      \"retryable\": { \"const\": false }\n+    }\n+  },\n+  \"metadata\": {\n+    \"module\": \"types-registry\",\n+    \"documentation_url\": \"https://docs.hyperspot.com/errors/types_registry_entity_not_found_v1\"\n+  }\n+}\n+```\n+\n+### Registration Flow\n+\n+1. Module defines errors as explicit structs with `#[gts_error]` attribute in `src/errors.rs`\n+2. Each struct generates `ERROR_DEF` constant with GTS metadata\n+3. Module implements `all_error_definitions()` function returning all error definitions\n+4. At module startup (`on_ready`), errors are registered with types registry:\n+   ```rust\n+   impl Module for MyModule {\n+       async fn on_ready(&self, ctx: &ModuleContext) -> Result<()> {\n+           // Register all error types with types registry\n+           let errors = crate::errors::all_error_definitions();\n+           ctx.types_registry().register_errors(errors).await?;\n+           Ok(())\n+       }\n+   }\n+   ```\n+5. Types registry validates GTS format and schema compliance\n+6. Errors become discoverable via types registry API\n+\n+### API for Error Discovery\n+\n+```http\n+GET /api/types-registry/v1/types?kind=error&module=types-registry\n+\n+Response:\n+{\n+  \"items\": [\n+    {\n+      \"gts_id\": \"gts.hx.core.errors.err.v1~hx.types_registry.entity.not_found.v1\",","path":"intended_design/UNIFIED_ERROR_SYSTEM.md","commit_id":"5bdb0f43b25858af78999718f7247813802b9634","original_commit_id":"5bdb0f43b25858af78999718f7247813802b9634","user":{"login":"Artifizer","id":192502778,"node_id":"U_kgDOC3lb-g","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/192502778?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer","html_url":"https://github.com/Artifizer","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Again, I see now proper GTS structure... I'm puzzled","created_at":"2026-01-30T21:18:09Z","updated_at":"2026-01-30T21:23:01Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/290#discussion_r2748012376","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/290","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2748012376"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/290#discussion_r2748012376"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/290"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2748012376/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":null,"original_line":484,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"MEMBER","original_position":484,"position":1,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2763706707","pull_request_review_id":3750715303,"id":2763706707,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs6kutFT","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,1574 @@\n+# Unified Error System - Intention Document\n+\n+This document defines the architecture, rules, and implementation plan for a unified error handling system across the Hyperspot project. All REST API errors MUST have a GTS identifier, trace ID, and be registered in the types registry.\n+\n+## Table of Contents\n+\n+1. [Executive Summary](#executive-summary)\n+2. [Industry Research](#industry-research)\n+3. [Current State Analysis](#current-state-analysis)\n+4. [Requirements](#requirements)\n+5. [Implementation Rules](#implementation-rules)\n+6. [Migration Plan](#migration-plan)\n+7. [Examples](#examples)\n+8. [HTTP Headers](#http-headers)\n+9. [Security Considerations](#security-considerations)\n+10. [Appendix A: Error Category Definitions](#appendix-a-error-category-definitions)\n+11. [Appendix B: Retryable Error Guidelines](#appendix-b-retryable-error-guidelines)\n+12. [GTS System Errors Catalog](#gts-system-errors-catalog)\n+13. [References](#references)\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Executive Summary\n+\n+### Problem Statement\n+\n+The current error handling across Hyperspot modules is inconsistent:\n+- Some modules use `declare_errors!` macro with JSON catalogs\n+- Others define errors inline without GTS codes\n+- Errors are not registered in the types registry\n+- No standardized metadata/context fields\n+- Inconsistent trace ID propagation\n+\n+### Goals\n+\n+1. **Every REST API error** MUST have a valid GTS identifier\n+2. **Every error response** MUST include a trace ID for debugging\n+3. **All error types** MUST be registered in the types registry","path":"intended_design/UNIFIED_ERROR_SYSTEM.md","commit_id":"a14d31841e0d559695e4ab49973b4f815551ccf3","original_commit_id":"5bdb0f43b25858af78999718f7247813802b9634","user":{"login":"alizid10","id":247960800,"node_id":"U_kgDODseU4A","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/247960800?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/alizid10","html_url":"https://github.com/alizid10","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alizid10/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alizid10/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alizid10/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alizid10/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alizid10/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alizid10/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alizid10/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alizid10/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alizid10/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"> all HTTP error types, not just all error types, correct?\n\nYes, all GTS error types, including non-HTTP ones","created_at":"2026-02-04T12:12:56Z","updated_at":"2026-02-06T15:55:48Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/290#discussion_r2763706707","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/290","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2763706707"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/290#discussion_r2763706707"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/290"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2763706707/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":null,"original_line":38,"side":"RIGHT","in_reply_to_id":2747860815,"author_association":"MEMBER","original_position":38,"position":1,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2763719241","pull_request_review_id":3750715303,"id":2763719241,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs6kuwJJ","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,1574 @@\n+# Unified Error System - Intention Document\n+\n+This document defines the architecture, rules, and implementation plan for a unified error handling system across the Hyperspot project. All REST API errors MUST have a GTS identifier, trace ID, and be registered in the types registry.\n+\n+## Table of Contents\n+\n+1. [Executive Summary](#executive-summary)\n+2. [Industry Research](#industry-research)\n+3. [Current State Analysis](#current-state-analysis)\n+4. [Requirements](#requirements)\n+5. [Implementation Rules](#implementation-rules)\n+6. [Migration Plan](#migration-plan)\n+7. [Examples](#examples)\n+8. [HTTP Headers](#http-headers)\n+9. [Security Considerations](#security-considerations)\n+10. [Appendix A: Error Category Definitions](#appendix-a-error-category-definitions)\n+11. [Appendix B: Retryable Error Guidelines](#appendix-b-retryable-error-guidelines)\n+12. [GTS System Errors Catalog](#gts-system-errors-catalog)\n+13. [References](#references)\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Executive Summary\n+\n+### Problem Statement\n+\n+The current error handling across Hyperspot modules is inconsistent:\n+- Some modules use `declare_errors!` macro with JSON catalogs\n+- Others define errors inline without GTS codes\n+- Errors are not registered in the types registry\n+- No standardized metadata/context fields\n+- Inconsistent trace ID propagation\n+\n+### Goals\n+\n+1. **Every REST API error** MUST have a valid GTS identifier\n+2. **Every error response** MUST include a trace ID for debugging\n+3. **All error types** MUST be registered in the types registry\n+4. **Consistent error schema** across all modules following RFC 9457\n+5. **Machine-readable error codes** for programmatic handling\n+6. **Error stack propagation** for nested service calls\n+\n+### Non-Goals\n+\n+- Changing internal domain error types (only API-facing errors)\n+- Modifying logging infrastructure\n+- Changing HTTP status code semantics\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Industry Research\n+\n+### How Major Tech Companies Handle Errors\n+\n+| Company | Standard | Key Features |\n+|---------|----------|--------------|\n+| **Google** | AIP-193 + gRPC Status | `reason` (UPPER_SNAKE_CASE), `domain` (service name), `metadata` (key-value context), `ErrorInfo`, `LocalizedMessage`, `Help` links |\n+| **Amazon AWS** | Custom JSON | `errorType`, `httpStatus`, `requestId`, `message`, custom error object serialization |\n+| **Twitter/X** | JSON with `errors` array | `code` (CAPS_CASE), `message`, `parameter`, `details`, `value` |\n+| **RFC 9457** | Problem Details | `type` (URI), `title`, `status`, `detail`, `instance`, extension members |\n+\n+### Key Patterns Identified\n+\n+1. **Machine-readable identifiers** - Unique codes for programmatic handling (Google's `reason`, Twitter's `code`)\n+2. **Domain/namespace separation** - Identify error source (Google's `domain`, our GTS vendor.package)\n+3. **Structured metadata** - Key-value context without parsing messages (Google's `ErrorInfo.metadata`)\n+4. **Trace/Request IDs** - Correlation for debugging (AWS `requestId`, our `trace_id`)\n+5. **Documentation links** - URIs to error documentation (RFC 9457 `type`, Google's `Help`)\n+6. **Error categorization** - System vs User-defined, Retryable vs Non-retryable\n+\n+### Google AIP-193 ErrorInfo Structure (Reference)\n+\n+```json\n+{\n+  \"error\": {\n+    \"code\": 429,\n+    \"message\": \"The zone 'us-east1-a' does not have enough resources...\",\n+    \"status\": \"RESOURCE_EXHAUSTED\",\n+    \"details\": [\n+      {\n+        \"@type\": \"type.googleapis.com/google.rpc.ErrorInfo\",\n+        \"reason\": \"RESOURCE_AVAILABILITY\",\n+        \"domain\": \"compute.googleapis.com\",\n+        \"metadata\": {\n+          \"zone\": \"us-east1-a\",\n+          \"vmType\": \"e2-medium\"\n+        }\n+      }\n+    ]\n+  }\n+}\n+```\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Current State Analysis\n+\n+### Existing Infrastructure\n+\n+1. **`Problem` struct** (`libs/modkit-errors/src/problem.rs`) - RFC 9457 compliant\n+   - Fields: `type_url`, `title`, `status`, `detail`, `instance`, `code`, `trace_id`, `errors`\n+   - Implements `IntoResponse` for Axum with automatic trace ID enrichment\n+\n+2. **`struct_to_gts_schema` macro** (`modules/types-registry/gts-rust/gts-macros/src/lib.rs`)\n+   - Attribute macro for explicit struct definitions with GTS IDs visible in code\n+   - Generates constants: `GTS_SCHEMA_ID`, `GTS_SCHEMA_JSON`, etc.\n+   - **This pattern will be adapted for error definitions**\n+\n+3. **`declare_errors!` macro** (`libs/modkit-errors-macro/src/lib.rs`) - **TO BE DEPRECATED**\n+   - Generates type-safe error enums from JSON catalogs\n+   - Problem: GTS IDs hidden in external JSON files, not visible to LLMs\n+   - Used by: `users_info` example, `modkit-odata`\n+\n+### Gaps Identified\n+\n+| Gap | Current State | Required State |\n+|-----|---------------|----------------|\n+| **Hidden GTS IDs** | JSON-based `declare_errors!` | Explicit `#[gts_error]` structs with visible GTS IDs |\n+| **Inconsistent definitions** | Some modules use inline errors | All modules use `#[gts_error]` structs |\n+| **No types registry** | Errors not registered | All errors registered as GTS types |","path":"intended_design/UNIFIED_ERROR_SYSTEM.md","commit_id":"5bdb0f43b25858af78999718f7247813802b9634","original_commit_id":"5bdb0f43b25858af78999718f7247813802b9634","user":{"login":"alizid10","id":247960800,"node_id":"U_kgDODseU4A","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/247960800?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/alizid10","html_url":"https://github.com/alizid10","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alizid10/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alizid10/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alizid10/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alizid10/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alizid10/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alizid10/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alizid10/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alizid10/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alizid10/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"This table shows the differences between the current and desired states. All errors declared with  #[gts_error]  must be registered in the types registry, even if they are not API-facing.","created_at":"2026-02-04T12:16:27Z","updated_at":"2026-02-06T15:55:48Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/290#discussion_r2763719241","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/290","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2763719241"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/290#discussion_r2763719241"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/290"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2763719241/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":null,"original_line":120,"side":"RIGHT","in_reply_to_id":2747873793,"author_association":"MEMBER","original_position":120,"position":1,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2774826522","pull_request_review_id":3750715303,"id":2774826522,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs6lZH4a","diff_hunk":"","path":"intended_design/UNIFIED_ERROR_SYSTEM.md","commit_id":"a14d31841e0d559695e4ab49973b4f815551ccf3","original_commit_id":"5bdb0f43b25858af78999718f7247813802b9634","user":{"login":"alizid10","id":247960800,"node_id":"U_kgDODseU4A","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/247960800?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/alizid10","html_url":"https://github.com/alizid10","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alizid10/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alizid10/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alizid10/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alizid10/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alizid10/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alizid10/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alizid10/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alizid10/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alizid10/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"will be reworked after https://github.com/hypernetix/hyperspot/pull/465","created_at":"2026-02-06T15:55:20Z","updated_at":"2026-02-06T15:55:48Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/290#discussion_r2774826522","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/290","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2774826522"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/290#discussion_r2774826522"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/290"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2774826522/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":1,"original_line":1,"side":"RIGHT","in_reply_to_id":2720926697,"author_association":"MEMBER","original_position":1,"position":1,"subject_type":"file"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2774836983","pull_request_review_id":3763858295,"id":2774836983,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs6lZKb3","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,417 @@\n+# GTS Error System Documentation\n+\n+This document describes how errors are defined, structured, transformed, and used in the Hyperspot/gts-rust project.\n+\n+## Overview\n+\n+The error system follows **RFC 9457 Problem Details for HTTP APIs** and uses a **GTS (Global Type System)** format for error codes. The system provides:\n+\n+- **Compile-time validated** error catalogs via JSON files\n+- **Type-safe** error code enums generated by proc-macros\n+- **Layered error transformation** from domain → API → HTTP response\n+- **Consistent error format** across all modules\n+\n+## Architecture\n+\n+```\n+┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n+│                           Error Flow                                     │\n+├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n+│                                                                          │\n+│  gts/errors.json  ──────►  declare_errors! macro  ──────►  ErrorCode    │\n+│  (Source of Truth)         (Compile-time)                  (Enum)       │\n+│                                                                          │\n+│  DomainError  ──────►  ErrorCode::xxx().with_context()  ──────►  Problem│\n+│  (Business Logic)      (Mapping Layer)                        (RFC 9457)│\n+│                                                                          │\n+│  Problem  ──────►  IntoResponse (Axum)  ──────►  HTTP Response          │","path":"docs/GTS_ERRORS.md","commit_id":"5bdb0f43b25858af78999718f7247813802b9634","original_commit_id":"5bdb0f43b25858af78999718f7247813802b9634","user":{"login":"alizid10","id":247960800,"node_id":"U_kgDODseU4A","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/247960800?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/alizid10","html_url":"https://github.com/alizid10","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alizid10/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alizid10/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alizid10/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alizid10/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alizid10/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alizid10/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alizid10/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alizid10/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alizid10/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"this doc described how it works now, removed.","created_at":"2026-02-06T15:57:28Z","updated_at":"2026-02-06T15:57:29Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/290#discussion_r2774836983","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/290","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2774836983"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/290#discussion_r2774836983"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/290"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2774836983/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":null,"original_line":27,"side":"RIGHT","in_reply_to_id":2720785173,"author_association":"MEMBER","original_position":27,"position":1,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2774838726","pull_request_review_id":3763860291,"id":2774838726,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs6lZK3G","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,417 @@\n+# GTS Error System Documentation\n+\n+This document describes how errors are defined, structured, transformed, and used in the Hyperspot/gts-rust project.\n+\n+## Overview\n+\n+The error system follows **RFC 9457 Problem Details for HTTP APIs** and uses a **GTS (Global Type System)** format for error codes. The system provides:\n+\n+- **Compile-time validated** error catalogs via JSON files\n+- **Type-safe** error code enums generated by proc-macros\n+- **Layered error transformation** from domain → API → HTTP response\n+- **Consistent error format** across all modules\n+\n+## Architecture\n+\n+```\n+┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n+│                           Error Flow                                     │\n+├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n+│                                                                          │\n+│  gts/errors.json  ──────►  declare_errors! macro  ──────►  ErrorCode    │\n+│  (Source of Truth)         (Compile-time)                  (Enum)       │\n+│                                                                          │\n+│  DomainError  ──────►  ErrorCode::xxx().with_context()  ──────►  Problem│\n+│  (Business Logic)      (Mapping Layer)                        (RFC 9457)│\n+│                                                                          │\n+│  Problem  ──────►  IntoResponse (Axum)  ──────►  HTTP Response          │\n+│  (Data)            (Framework Integration)       (JSON + Headers)       │\n+│                                                                          │\n+└─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘\n+```\n+\n+## Components\n+\n+### 1. Error Catalog JSON (`gts/errors.json`)\n+\n+The source of truth for error definitions. Located in each module's `gts/` directory.\n+\n+**File Location Pattern:** `<module>/gts/errors.json`\n+\n+**Schema:**\n+```json\n+[\n+  {\n+    \"status\": 404,\n+    \"title\": \"User Not Found\",\n+    \"code\": \"gts.hx.core.errors.err.v1~hx.example1.user.not_found.v1\",\n+    \"type\": \"https://errors.example.com/...\",  // optional\n+    \"alias\": \"user_not_found\"                   // optional\n+  }\n+]\n+```\n+\n+**Fields:**\n+| Field | Required | Description |\n+|-------|----------|-------------|\n+| `status` | Yes | HTTP status code (100-599) |\n+| `title` | Yes | Human-readable error title |\n+| `code` | Yes | GTS-formatted error code |\n+| `type` | No | URI for error documentation |\n+| `alias` | No | Short name override for generated accessor |\n+\n+### 2. GTS Code Format\n+\n+GTS codes follow a strict format for global type identification:\n+\n+```\n+gts.vendor.package.namespace.type.version~chain1~chain2~...~instanceGTX\n+```\n+\n+**Structure:**\n+- **Prefix:** Always starts with `gts.`\n+- **Chain separator:** `~` separates GTX segments\n+- **Segment separator:** `.` separates parts within a GTX\n+- **Final GTX:** Must have at least 5 segments: `vendor.package.namespace.type.version`\n+- **Version:** Must end with `vN` or `vN.M` format\n+\n+**Example Breakdown:**\n+```\n+gts.hx.core.errors.err.v1~hx.example1.user.not_found.v1\n+│   │  │    │      │   │  │  │        │    │         │\n+│   │  │    │      │   │  │  │        │    │         └─ version\n+│   │  │    │      │   │  │  │        │    └─ type (not_found)\n+│   │  │    │      │   │  │  │        └─ namespace (user)\n+│   │  │    │      │   │  │  └─ package (example1)\n+│   │  │    │      │   │  └─ vendor (hx)\n+│   │  │    │      │   └─ version\n+│   │  │    │      └─ type (err)\n+│   │  │    └─ namespace (errors)\n+│   │  └─ package (core)\n+│   └─ vendor (hx)\n+└─ prefix\n+```\n+\n+**Validation Rules:**\n+1. Must start with `gts.`\n+2. All segments must be lowercase alphanumeric or underscore\n+3. No empty segments allowed\n+4. Final GTX must have ≥5 segments after vendor\n+5. Must end with valid version format (`v1`, `v1.2`, etc.)\n+\n+### 3. Proc-Macro: `declare_errors!`\n+\n+Generates type-safe error code enums from JSON at compile time.\n+\n+**Location:** `libs/modkit-errors-macro/src/lib.rs`\n+\n+**Usage:**\n+```rust\n+use modkit_errors_macro::declare_errors;\n+\n+declare_errors! {\n+    path = \"gts/errors.json\",\n+    namespace = \"errors\",\n+    vis = \"pub\"\n+}\n+```\n+\n+**Parameters:**\n+| Parameter | Required | Description |\n+|-----------|----------|-------------|\n+| `path` | Yes | Path to JSON file relative to `CARGO_MANIFEST_DIR` |\n+| `namespace` | Yes | Module name for generated code |\n+| `vis` | No | Visibility (`\"pub\"` or private) |\n+\n+**Generated Code:**\n+```rust\n+// Enum with all error codes\n+#[derive(Debug, Clone, Copy, PartialEq, Eq, Hash)]\n+pub enum ErrorCode {\n+    gts_hx_core_errors_err_v1_hx_example1_user_not_found_v1,\n+    // ...\n+}\n+\n+impl ErrorCode {\n+    // Get HTTP status\n+    pub const fn status(&self) -> u16 { ... }\n+    \n+    // Get full error definition\n+    pub const fn def(&self) -> ErrDef { ... }\n+    \n+    // Convert to Problem with detail\n+    pub fn as_problem(&self, detail: impl Into<String>) -> Problem { ... }\n+    \n+    // Create Problem with context (instance + trace_id)\n+    pub fn with_context(\n+        &self,\n+        detail: impl Into<String>,\n+        instance: &str,\n+        trace_id: Option<String>,\n+    ) -> Problem { ... }\n+    \n+    // Short accessor (derived from GTS or alias)\n+    pub const fn example1_user_not_found_v1() -> Self { ... }\n+}\n+\n+// Compile-time validated macro\n+macro_rules! problem_from_catalog { ... }\n+macro_rules! response_from_catalog { ... }\n+```\n+\n+### 4. Core Types\n+\n+#### `ErrDef` (Error Definition)\n+**Location:** `libs/modkit-errors/src/catalog.rs`\n+\n+```rust\n+pub struct ErrDef {\n+    pub status: u16,\n+    pub title: &'static str,\n+    pub code: &'static str,\n+    pub type_url: &'static str,\n+}\n+\n+impl ErrDef {\n+    pub fn as_problem(&self, detail: impl Into<String>) -> Problem { ... }\n+}\n+```\n+\n+#### `Problem` (RFC 9457)\n+**Location:** `libs/modkit-errors/src/problem.rs`\n+\n+```rust\n+pub struct Problem {\n+    pub type_url: String,      // URI reference for problem type\n+    pub title: String,         // Human-readable summary\n+    pub status: StatusCode,    // HTTP status code\n+    pub detail: String,        // Specific occurrence explanation\n+    pub instance: String,      // URI for this occurrence\n+    pub code: String,          // Machine-readable error code\n+    pub trace_id: Option<String>,\n+    pub errors: Option<Vec<ValidationViolation>>,\n+}\n+```\n+\n+**Builder Pattern:**\n+```rust\n+Problem::new(StatusCode::NOT_FOUND, \"Not Found\", \"User not found\")","path":"docs/GTS_ERRORS.md","commit_id":"5bdb0f43b25858af78999718f7247813802b9634","original_commit_id":"5bdb0f43b25858af78999718f7247813802b9634","user":{"login":"alizid10","id":247960800,"node_id":"U_kgDODseU4A","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/247960800?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/alizid10","html_url":"https://github.com/alizid10","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alizid10/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alizid10/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alizid10/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alizid10/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alizid10/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alizid10/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alizid10/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alizid10/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alizid10/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"this doc described how it works now, removed.","created_at":"2026-02-06T15:57:54Z","updated_at":"2026-02-06T15:57:54Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/290#discussion_r2774838726","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/290","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2774838726"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/290#discussion_r2774838726"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/290"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2774838726/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":null,"original_line":198,"side":"RIGHT","in_reply_to_id":2720838362,"author_association":"MEMBER","original_position":198,"position":1,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2774839123","pull_request_review_id":3763860710,"id":2774839123,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs6lZK9T","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,417 @@\n+# GTS Error System Documentation\n+\n+This document describes how errors are defined, structured, transformed, and used in the Hyperspot/gts-rust project.\n+\n+## Overview\n+\n+The error system follows **RFC 9457 Problem Details for HTTP APIs** and uses a **GTS (Global Type System)** format for error codes. The system provides:\n+\n+- **Compile-time validated** error catalogs via JSON files\n+- **Type-safe** error code enums generated by proc-macros\n+- **Layered error transformation** from domain → API → HTTP response\n+- **Consistent error format** across all modules\n+\n+## Architecture\n+\n+```\n+┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n+│                           Error Flow                                     │\n+├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n+│                                                                          │\n+│  gts/errors.json  ──────►  declare_errors! macro  ──────►  ErrorCode    │\n+│  (Source of Truth)         (Compile-time)                  (Enum)       │\n+│                                                                          │\n+│  DomainError  ──────►  ErrorCode::xxx().with_context()  ──────►  Problem│\n+│  (Business Logic)      (Mapping Layer)                        (RFC 9457)│\n+│                                                                          │\n+│  Problem  ──────►  IntoResponse (Axum)  ──────►  HTTP Response          │\n+│  (Data)            (Framework Integration)       (JSON + Headers)       │\n+│                                                                          │\n+└─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘\n+```\n+\n+## Components\n+\n+### 1. Error Catalog JSON (`gts/errors.json`)\n+\n+The source of truth for error definitions. Located in each module's `gts/` directory.\n+\n+**File Location Pattern:** `<module>/gts/errors.json`\n+\n+**Schema:**\n+```json\n+[\n+  {\n+    \"status\": 404,\n+    \"title\": \"User Not Found\",\n+    \"code\": \"gts.hx.core.errors.err.v1~hx.example1.user.not_found.v1\",\n+    \"type\": \"https://errors.example.com/...\",  // optional\n+    \"alias\": \"user_not_found\"                   // optional\n+  }\n+]\n+```\n+\n+**Fields:**\n+| Field | Required | Description |\n+|-------|----------|-------------|\n+| `status` | Yes | HTTP status code (100-599) |\n+| `title` | Yes | Human-readable error title |\n+| `code` | Yes | GTS-formatted error code |\n+| `type` | No | URI for error documentation |\n+| `alias` | No | Short name override for generated accessor |\n+\n+### 2. GTS Code Format\n+\n+GTS codes follow a strict format for global type identification:\n+\n+```\n+gts.vendor.package.namespace.type.version~chain1~chain2~...~instanceGTX\n+```\n+\n+**Structure:**\n+- **Prefix:** Always starts with `gts.`\n+- **Chain separator:** `~` separates GTX segments\n+- **Segment separator:** `.` separates parts within a GTX\n+- **Final GTX:** Must have at least 5 segments: `vendor.package.namespace.type.version`\n+- **Version:** Must end with `vN` or `vN.M` format\n+\n+**Example Breakdown:**\n+```\n+gts.hx.core.errors.err.v1~hx.example1.user.not_found.v1\n+│   │  │    │      │   │  │  │        │    │         │\n+│   │  │    │      │   │  │  │        │    │         └─ version\n+│   │  │    │      │   │  │  │        │    └─ type (not_found)\n+│   │  │    │      │   │  │  │        └─ namespace (user)\n+│   │  │    │      │   │  │  └─ package (example1)\n+│   │  │    │      │   │  └─ vendor (hx)\n+│   │  │    │      │   └─ version\n+│   │  │    │      └─ type (err)\n+│   │  │    └─ namespace (errors)\n+│   │  └─ package (core)\n+│   └─ vendor (hx)\n+└─ prefix\n+```\n+\n+**Validation Rules:**\n+1. Must start with `gts.`\n+2. All segments must be lowercase alphanumeric or underscore\n+3. No empty segments allowed\n+4. Final GTX must have ≥5 segments after vendor\n+5. Must end with valid version format (`v1`, `v1.2`, etc.)\n+\n+### 3. Proc-Macro: `declare_errors!`\n+\n+Generates type-safe error code enums from JSON at compile time.\n+\n+**Location:** `libs/modkit-errors-macro/src/lib.rs`\n+\n+**Usage:**\n+```rust\n+use modkit_errors_macro::declare_errors;\n+\n+declare_errors! {\n+    path = \"gts/errors.json\",\n+    namespace = \"errors\",\n+    vis = \"pub\"\n+}\n+```\n+\n+**Parameters:**\n+| Parameter | Required | Description |\n+|-----------|----------|-------------|\n+| `path` | Yes | Path to JSON file relative to `CARGO_MANIFEST_DIR` |\n+| `namespace` | Yes | Module name for generated code |\n+| `vis` | No | Visibility (`\"pub\"` or private) |\n+\n+**Generated Code:**\n+```rust\n+// Enum with all error codes\n+#[derive(Debug, Clone, Copy, PartialEq, Eq, Hash)]\n+pub enum ErrorCode {\n+    gts_hx_core_errors_err_v1_hx_example1_user_not_found_v1,\n+    // ...\n+}\n+\n+impl ErrorCode {\n+    // Get HTTP status\n+    pub const fn status(&self) -> u16 { ... }\n+    \n+    // Get full error definition\n+    pub const fn def(&self) -> ErrDef { ... }\n+    \n+    // Convert to Problem with detail\n+    pub fn as_problem(&self, detail: impl Into<String>) -> Problem { ... }\n+    \n+    // Create Problem with context (instance + trace_id)\n+    pub fn with_context(\n+        &self,\n+        detail: impl Into<String>,\n+        instance: &str,\n+        trace_id: Option<String>,\n+    ) -> Problem { ... }\n+    \n+    // Short accessor (derived from GTS or alias)\n+    pub const fn example1_user_not_found_v1() -> Self { ... }\n+}\n+\n+// Compile-time validated macro\n+macro_rules! problem_from_catalog { ... }\n+macro_rules! response_from_catalog { ... }\n+```\n+\n+### 4. Core Types\n+\n+#### `ErrDef` (Error Definition)\n+**Location:** `libs/modkit-errors/src/catalog.rs`\n+\n+```rust\n+pub struct ErrDef {\n+    pub status: u16,\n+    pub title: &'static str,\n+    pub code: &'static str,\n+    pub type_url: &'static str,\n+}\n+\n+impl ErrDef {\n+    pub fn as_problem(&self, detail: impl Into<String>) -> Problem { ... }\n+}\n+```\n+\n+#### `Problem` (RFC 9457)\n+**Location:** `libs/modkit-errors/src/problem.rs`\n+\n+```rust\n+pub struct Problem {\n+    pub type_url: String,      // URI reference for problem type\n+    pub title: String,         // Human-readable summary\n+    pub status: StatusCode,    // HTTP status code\n+    pub detail: String,        // Specific occurrence explanation\n+    pub instance: String,      // URI for this occurrence\n+    pub code: String,          // Machine-readable error code\n+    pub trace_id: Option<String>,\n+    pub errors: Option<Vec<ValidationViolation>>,\n+}\n+```\n+\n+**Builder Pattern:**\n+```rust\n+Problem::new(StatusCode::NOT_FOUND, \"Not Found\", \"User not found\")\n+    .with_code(\"gts.hx....\")\n+    .with_type(\"https://...\")\n+    .with_instance(\"/api/users/123\")\n+    .with_trace_id(\"req-456\")\n+    .with_errors(vec![...])\n+```\n+\n+## Error Flow by Layer\n+\n+### Layer 1: Domain Errors\n+\n+Domain errors represent business logic failures. They are internal and don't contain HTTP-specific information.\n+\n+**Location:** `<module>/src/domain/error.rs`\n+\n+```rust\n+#[derive(Error, Debug)]","path":"docs/GTS_ERRORS.md","commit_id":"5bdb0f43b25858af78999718f7247813802b9634","original_commit_id":"5bdb0f43b25858af78999718f7247813802b9634","user":{"login":"alizid10","id":247960800,"node_id":"U_kgDODseU4A","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/247960800?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/alizid10","html_url":"https://github.com/alizid10","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alizid10/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alizid10/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alizid10/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alizid10/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alizid10/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alizid10/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alizid10/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alizid10/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alizid10/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"this doc described how it works now, removed.","created_at":"2026-02-06T15:57:59Z","updated_at":"2026-02-06T15:58:00Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/290#discussion_r2774839123","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/290","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2774839123"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/290#discussion_r2774839123"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/290"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2774839123/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":null,"original_line":215,"side":"RIGHT","in_reply_to_id":2720840144,"author_association":"MEMBER","original_position":215,"position":1,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2774839477","pull_request_review_id":3763861067,"id":2774839477,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs6lZLC1","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,417 @@\n+# GTS Error System Documentation\n+\n+This document describes how errors are defined, structured, transformed, and used in the Hyperspot/gts-rust project.\n+\n+## Overview\n+\n+The error system follows **RFC 9457 Problem Details for HTTP APIs** and uses a **GTS (Global Type System)** format for error codes. The system provides:\n+\n+- **Compile-time validated** error catalogs via JSON files\n+- **Type-safe** error code enums generated by proc-macros\n+- **Layered error transformation** from domain → API → HTTP response\n+- **Consistent error format** across all modules\n+\n+## Architecture\n+\n+```\n+┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n+│                           Error Flow                                     │\n+├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n+│                                                                          │\n+│  gts/errors.json  ──────►  declare_errors! macro  ──────►  ErrorCode    │\n+│  (Source of Truth)         (Compile-time)                  (Enum)       │\n+│                                                                          │\n+│  DomainError  ──────►  ErrorCode::xxx().with_context()  ──────►  Problem│\n+│  (Business Logic)      (Mapping Layer)                        (RFC 9457)│\n+│                                                                          │\n+│  Problem  ──────►  IntoResponse (Axum)  ──────►  HTTP Response          │\n+│  (Data)            (Framework Integration)       (JSON + Headers)       │\n+│                                                                          │\n+└─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘\n+```\n+\n+## Components\n+\n+### 1. Error Catalog JSON (`gts/errors.json`)\n+\n+The source of truth for error definitions. Located in each module's `gts/` directory.\n+\n+**File Location Pattern:** `<module>/gts/errors.json`\n+\n+**Schema:**\n+```json\n+[\n+  {\n+    \"status\": 404,\n+    \"title\": \"User Not Found\",\n+    \"code\": \"gts.hx.core.errors.err.v1~hx.example1.user.not_found.v1\",\n+    \"type\": \"https://errors.example.com/...\",  // optional\n+    \"alias\": \"user_not_found\"                   // optional\n+  }\n+]\n+```\n+\n+**Fields:**\n+| Field | Required | Description |\n+|-------|----------|-------------|\n+| `status` | Yes | HTTP status code (100-599) |\n+| `title` | Yes | Human-readable error title |\n+| `code` | Yes | GTS-formatted error code |\n+| `type` | No | URI for error documentation |\n+| `alias` | No | Short name override for generated accessor |\n+\n+### 2. GTS Code Format\n+\n+GTS codes follow a strict format for global type identification:\n+\n+```\n+gts.vendor.package.namespace.type.version~chain1~chain2~...~instanceGTX\n+```\n+\n+**Structure:**\n+- **Prefix:** Always starts with `gts.`\n+- **Chain separator:** `~` separates GTX segments\n+- **Segment separator:** `.` separates parts within a GTX\n+- **Final GTX:** Must have at least 5 segments: `vendor.package.namespace.type.version`\n+- **Version:** Must end with `vN` or `vN.M` format\n+\n+**Example Breakdown:**\n+```\n+gts.hx.core.errors.err.v1~hx.example1.user.not_found.v1\n+│   │  │    │      │   │  │  │        │    │         │\n+│   │  │    │      │   │  │  │        │    │         └─ version\n+│   │  │    │      │   │  │  │        │    └─ type (not_found)\n+│   │  │    │      │   │  │  │        └─ namespace (user)\n+│   │  │    │      │   │  │  └─ package (example1)\n+│   │  │    │      │   │  └─ vendor (hx)\n+│   │  │    │      │   └─ version\n+│   │  │    │      └─ type (err)\n+│   │  │    └─ namespace (errors)\n+│   │  └─ package (core)\n+│   └─ vendor (hx)\n+└─ prefix\n+```\n+\n+**Validation Rules:**\n+1. Must start with `gts.`\n+2. All segments must be lowercase alphanumeric or underscore\n+3. No empty segments allowed\n+4. Final GTX must have ≥5 segments after vendor\n+5. Must end with valid version format (`v1`, `v1.2`, etc.)\n+\n+### 3. Proc-Macro: `declare_errors!`\n+\n+Generates type-safe error code enums from JSON at compile time.\n+\n+**Location:** `libs/modkit-errors-macro/src/lib.rs`\n+\n+**Usage:**\n+```rust\n+use modkit_errors_macro::declare_errors;\n+\n+declare_errors! {\n+    path = \"gts/errors.json\",\n+    namespace = \"errors\",\n+    vis = \"pub\"\n+}\n+```\n+\n+**Parameters:**\n+| Parameter | Required | Description |\n+|-----------|----------|-------------|\n+| `path` | Yes | Path to JSON file relative to `CARGO_MANIFEST_DIR` |\n+| `namespace` | Yes | Module name for generated code |\n+| `vis` | No | Visibility (`\"pub\"` or private) |\n+\n+**Generated Code:**\n+```rust\n+// Enum with all error codes\n+#[derive(Debug, Clone, Copy, PartialEq, Eq, Hash)]\n+pub enum ErrorCode {\n+    gts_hx_core_errors_err_v1_hx_example1_user_not_found_v1,\n+    // ...\n+}\n+\n+impl ErrorCode {\n+    // Get HTTP status\n+    pub const fn status(&self) -> u16 { ... }\n+    \n+    // Get full error definition\n+    pub const fn def(&self) -> ErrDef { ... }\n+    \n+    // Convert to Problem with detail\n+    pub fn as_problem(&self, detail: impl Into<String>) -> Problem { ... }\n+    \n+    // Create Problem with context (instance + trace_id)\n+    pub fn with_context(\n+        &self,\n+        detail: impl Into<String>,\n+        instance: &str,\n+        trace_id: Option<String>,\n+    ) -> Problem { ... }\n+    \n+    // Short accessor (derived from GTS or alias)\n+    pub const fn example1_user_not_found_v1() -> Self { ... }\n+}\n+\n+// Compile-time validated macro\n+macro_rules! problem_from_catalog { ... }\n+macro_rules! response_from_catalog { ... }\n+```\n+\n+### 4. Core Types\n+\n+#### `ErrDef` (Error Definition)\n+**Location:** `libs/modkit-errors/src/catalog.rs`\n+\n+```rust\n+pub struct ErrDef {\n+    pub status: u16,\n+    pub title: &'static str,\n+    pub code: &'static str,\n+    pub type_url: &'static str,\n+}\n+\n+impl ErrDef {\n+    pub fn as_problem(&self, detail: impl Into<String>) -> Problem { ... }\n+}\n+```\n+\n+#### `Problem` (RFC 9457)\n+**Location:** `libs/modkit-errors/src/problem.rs`\n+\n+```rust\n+pub struct Problem {\n+    pub type_url: String,      // URI reference for problem type\n+    pub title: String,         // Human-readable summary\n+    pub status: StatusCode,    // HTTP status code\n+    pub detail: String,        // Specific occurrence explanation\n+    pub instance: String,      // URI for this occurrence\n+    pub code: String,          // Machine-readable error code\n+    pub trace_id: Option<String>,\n+    pub errors: Option<Vec<ValidationViolation>>,\n+}\n+```\n+\n+**Builder Pattern:**\n+```rust\n+Problem::new(StatusCode::NOT_FOUND, \"Not Found\", \"User not found\")\n+    .with_code(\"gts.hx....\")\n+    .with_type(\"https://...\")\n+    .with_instance(\"/api/users/123\")\n+    .with_trace_id(\"req-456\")\n+    .with_errors(vec![...])\n+```\n+\n+## Error Flow by Layer\n+\n+### Layer 1: Domain Errors\n+\n+Domain errors represent business logic failures. They are internal and don't contain HTTP-specific information.\n+\n+**Location:** `<module>/src/domain/error.rs`\n+\n+```rust\n+#[derive(Error, Debug)]\n+pub enum DomainError {\n+    #[error(\"User not found: {id}\")]\n+    UserNotFound { id: Uuid },\n+    \n+    #[error(\"Email '{email}' already exists\")]\n+    EmailAlreadyExists { email: String },\n+    \n+    #[error(\"Database error: {message}\")]\n+    Database { message: String },\n+    // ...\n+}\n+```\n+\n+### Layer 2: SDK Errors (Public API)\n+\n+SDK errors are exposed to other modules via the client trait. They are simplified and safe to expose.\n+\n+**Location:** `<module>-sdk/src/errors.rs`\n+\n+```rust\n+#[derive(Error, Debug, Clone)]\n+pub enum UsersInfoError {\n+    #[error(\"Resource not found: {id}\")]\n+    NotFound { id: Uuid },\n+    \n+    #[error(\"Validation error: {message}\")]\n+    Validation { message: String },\n+    \n+    #[error(\"Internal error\")]\n+    Internal,\n+}\n+```\n+\n+### Layer 3: API Error Mapping\n+\n+The API layer maps domain errors to RFC 9457 Problems using the error catalog.\n+\n+**Location:** `<module>/src/api/rest/error.rs`\n+\n+```rust\n+use crate::errors::ErrorCode;\n+\n+pub fn domain_error_to_problem(e: &DomainError, instance: &str) -> Problem {\n+    let trace_id = tracing::Span::current()\n+        .id()\n+        .map(|id| id.into_u64().to_string());\n+\n+    match &e {\n+        DomainError::UserNotFound { id } => {\n+            ErrorCode::example1_user_not_found_v1().with_context(\n+                format!(\"User with id {id} was not found\"),\n+                instance,\n+                trace_id,\n+            )\n+        }\n+        DomainError::Database { .. } => {\n+            tracing::error!(error = ?e, \"Database error occurred\");\n+            ErrorCode::example1_user_internal_database_v1().with_context(\n+                \"An internal database error occurred\",\n+                instance,\n+                trace_id,\n+            )\n+        }\n+        // ...\n+    }\n+}\n+```\n+\n+### Layer 4: HTTP Response\n+\n+`Problem` implements `IntoResponse` for Axum, automatically:\n+- Setting the correct HTTP status code\n+- Setting `Content-Type: application/problem+json`\n+- Enriching with trace ID from current span if not set\n+\n+```rust\n+// In handler\n+async fn get_user(...) -> Result<Json<User>, Problem> {\n+    let user = service.get_user(id).await","path":"docs/GTS_ERRORS.md","commit_id":"5bdb0f43b25858af78999718f7247813802b9634","original_commit_id":"5bdb0f43b25858af78999718f7247813802b9634","user":{"login":"alizid10","id":247960800,"node_id":"U_kgDODseU4A","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/247960800?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/alizid10","html_url":"https://github.com/alizid10","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alizid10/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alizid10/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alizid10/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alizid10/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alizid10/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alizid10/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alizid10/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alizid10/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alizid10/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"this doc described how it works now, removed.","created_at":"2026-02-06T15:58:05Z","updated_at":"2026-02-06T15:58:05Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/290#discussion_r2774839477","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/290","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2774839477"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/290#discussion_r2774839477"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/290"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2774839477/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":null,"original_line":294,"side":"RIGHT","in_reply_to_id":2720920191,"author_association":"MEMBER","original_position":294,"position":1,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2774839919","pull_request_review_id":3763861526,"id":2774839919,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs6lZLJv","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,417 @@\n+# GTS Error System Documentation\n+\n+This document describes how errors are defined, structured, transformed, and used in the Hyperspot/gts-rust project.\n+\n+## Overview\n+\n+The error system follows **RFC 9457 Problem Details for HTTP APIs** and uses a **GTS (Global Type System)** format for error codes. The system provides:\n+\n+- **Compile-time validated** error catalogs via JSON files\n+- **Type-safe** error code enums generated by proc-macros\n+- **Layered error transformation** from domain → API → HTTP response\n+- **Consistent error format** across all modules\n+\n+## Architecture\n+\n+```\n+┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n+│                           Error Flow                                     │\n+├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n+│                                                                          │\n+│  gts/errors.json  ──────►  declare_errors! macro  ──────►  ErrorCode    │\n+│  (Source of Truth)         (Compile-time)                  (Enum)       │\n+│                                                                          │\n+│  DomainError  ──────►  ErrorCode::xxx().with_context()  ──────►  Problem│\n+│  (Business Logic)      (Mapping Layer)                        (RFC 9457)│\n+│                                                                          │\n+│  Problem  ──────►  IntoResponse (Axum)  ──────►  HTTP Response          │\n+│  (Data)            (Framework Integration)       (JSON + Headers)       │\n+│                                                                          │\n+└─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘\n+```\n+\n+## Components\n+\n+### 1. Error Catalog JSON (`gts/errors.json`)\n+\n+The source of truth for error definitions. Located in each module's `gts/` directory.\n+\n+**File Location Pattern:** `<module>/gts/errors.json`\n+\n+**Schema:**\n+```json\n+[\n+  {\n+    \"status\": 404,\n+    \"title\": \"User Not Found\",\n+    \"code\": \"gts.hx.core.errors.err.v1~hx.example1.user.not_found.v1\",\n+    \"type\": \"https://errors.example.com/...\",  // optional\n+    \"alias\": \"user_not_found\"                   // optional\n+  }\n+]\n+```\n+\n+**Fields:**\n+| Field | Required | Description |\n+|-------|----------|-------------|\n+| `status` | Yes | HTTP status code (100-599) |\n+| `title` | Yes | Human-readable error title |\n+| `code` | Yes | GTS-formatted error code |\n+| `type` | No | URI for error documentation |\n+| `alias` | No | Short name override for generated accessor |\n+\n+### 2. GTS Code Format\n+\n+GTS codes follow a strict format for global type identification:\n+\n+```\n+gts.vendor.package.namespace.type.version~chain1~chain2~...~instanceGTX\n+```\n+\n+**Structure:**\n+- **Prefix:** Always starts with `gts.`\n+- **Chain separator:** `~` separates GTX segments\n+- **Segment separator:** `.` separates parts within a GTX\n+- **Final GTX:** Must have at least 5 segments: `vendor.package.namespace.type.version`\n+- **Version:** Must end with `vN` or `vN.M` format\n+\n+**Example Breakdown:**\n+```\n+gts.hx.core.errors.err.v1~hx.example1.user.not_found.v1\n+│   │  │    │      │   │  │  │        │    │         │\n+│   │  │    │      │   │  │  │        │    │         └─ version\n+│   │  │    │      │   │  │  │        │    └─ type (not_found)\n+│   │  │    │      │   │  │  │        └─ namespace (user)\n+│   │  │    │      │   │  │  └─ package (example1)\n+│   │  │    │      │   │  └─ vendor (hx)\n+│   │  │    │      │   └─ version\n+│   │  │    │      └─ type (err)\n+│   │  │    └─ namespace (errors)\n+│   │  └─ package (core)\n+│   └─ vendor (hx)\n+└─ prefix\n+```\n+\n+**Validation Rules:**\n+1. Must start with `gts.`\n+2. All segments must be lowercase alphanumeric or underscore\n+3. No empty segments allowed\n+4. Final GTX must have ≥5 segments after vendor\n+5. Must end with valid version format (`v1`, `v1.2`, etc.)\n+\n+### 3. Proc-Macro: `declare_errors!`\n+\n+Generates type-safe error code enums from JSON at compile time.\n+\n+**Location:** `libs/modkit-errors-macro/src/lib.rs`\n+\n+**Usage:**\n+```rust\n+use modkit_errors_macro::declare_errors;\n+\n+declare_errors! {\n+    path = \"gts/errors.json\",\n+    namespace = \"errors\",\n+    vis = \"pub\"\n+}\n+```\n+\n+**Parameters:**\n+| Parameter | Required | Description |\n+|-----------|----------|-------------|\n+| `path` | Yes | Path to JSON file relative to `CARGO_MANIFEST_DIR` |\n+| `namespace` | Yes | Module name for generated code |\n+| `vis` | No | Visibility (`\"pub\"` or private) |\n+\n+**Generated Code:**\n+```rust\n+// Enum with all error codes\n+#[derive(Debug, Clone, Copy, PartialEq, Eq, Hash)]\n+pub enum ErrorCode {\n+    gts_hx_core_errors_err_v1_hx_example1_user_not_found_v1,\n+    // ...\n+}\n+\n+impl ErrorCode {\n+    // Get HTTP status\n+    pub const fn status(&self) -> u16 { ... }\n+    \n+    // Get full error definition\n+    pub const fn def(&self) -> ErrDef { ... }\n+    \n+    // Convert to Problem with detail\n+    pub fn as_problem(&self, detail: impl Into<String>) -> Problem { ... }\n+    \n+    // Create Problem with context (instance + trace_id)\n+    pub fn with_context(\n+        &self,\n+        detail: impl Into<String>,\n+        instance: &str,\n+        trace_id: Option<String>,\n+    ) -> Problem { ... }\n+    \n+    // Short accessor (derived from GTS or alias)\n+    pub const fn example1_user_not_found_v1() -> Self { ... }\n+}\n+\n+// Compile-time validated macro\n+macro_rules! problem_from_catalog { ... }\n+macro_rules! response_from_catalog { ... }\n+```\n+\n+### 4. Core Types\n+\n+#### `ErrDef` (Error Definition)\n+**Location:** `libs/modkit-errors/src/catalog.rs`\n+\n+```rust\n+pub struct ErrDef {\n+    pub status: u16,\n+    pub title: &'static str,\n+    pub code: &'static str,\n+    pub type_url: &'static str,\n+}\n+\n+impl ErrDef {\n+    pub fn as_problem(&self, detail: impl Into<String>) -> Problem { ... }\n+}\n+```\n+\n+#### `Problem` (RFC 9457)\n+**Location:** `libs/modkit-errors/src/problem.rs`\n+\n+```rust\n+pub struct Problem {\n+    pub type_url: String,      // URI reference for problem type\n+    pub title: String,         // Human-readable summary\n+    pub status: StatusCode,    // HTTP status code\n+    pub detail: String,        // Specific occurrence explanation\n+    pub instance: String,      // URI for this occurrence\n+    pub code: String,          // Machine-readable error code\n+    pub trace_id: Option<String>,\n+    pub errors: Option<Vec<ValidationViolation>>,\n+}\n+```\n+\n+**Builder Pattern:**\n+```rust\n+Problem::new(StatusCode::NOT_FOUND, \"Not Found\", \"User not found\")\n+    .with_code(\"gts.hx....\")\n+    .with_type(\"https://...\")\n+    .with_instance(\"/api/users/123\")\n+    .with_trace_id(\"req-456\")\n+    .with_errors(vec![...])\n+```\n+\n+## Error Flow by Layer\n+\n+### Layer 1: Domain Errors\n+\n+Domain errors represent business logic failures. They are internal and don't contain HTTP-specific information.\n+\n+**Location:** `<module>/src/domain/error.rs`\n+\n+```rust\n+#[derive(Error, Debug)]\n+pub enum DomainError {\n+    #[error(\"User not found: {id}\")]\n+    UserNotFound { id: Uuid },\n+    \n+    #[error(\"Email '{email}' already exists\")]\n+    EmailAlreadyExists { email: String },\n+    \n+    #[error(\"Database error: {message}\")]\n+    Database { message: String },\n+    // ...\n+}\n+```\n+\n+### Layer 2: SDK Errors (Public API)\n+\n+SDK errors are exposed to other modules via the client trait. They are simplified and safe to expose.\n+\n+**Location:** `<module>-sdk/src/errors.rs`\n+\n+```rust\n+#[derive(Error, Debug, Clone)]\n+pub enum UsersInfoError {\n+    #[error(\"Resource not found: {id}\")]\n+    NotFound { id: Uuid },\n+    \n+    #[error(\"Validation error: {message}\")]\n+    Validation { message: String },\n+    \n+    #[error(\"Internal error\")]\n+    Internal,\n+}\n+```\n+\n+### Layer 3: API Error Mapping\n+\n+The API layer maps domain errors to RFC 9457 Problems using the error catalog.\n+\n+**Location:** `<module>/src/api/rest/error.rs`\n+\n+```rust\n+use crate::errors::ErrorCode;\n+\n+pub fn domain_error_to_problem(e: &DomainError, instance: &str) -> Problem {\n+    let trace_id = tracing::Span::current()\n+        .id()\n+        .map(|id| id.into_u64().to_string());\n+\n+    match &e {\n+        DomainError::UserNotFound { id } => {\n+            ErrorCode::example1_user_not_found_v1().with_context(\n+                format!(\"User with id {id} was not found\"),\n+                instance,\n+                trace_id,\n+            )\n+        }\n+        DomainError::Database { .. } => {\n+            tracing::error!(error = ?e, \"Database error occurred\");\n+            ErrorCode::example1_user_internal_database_v1().with_context(\n+                \"An internal database error occurred\",\n+                instance,\n+                trace_id,\n+            )\n+        }\n+        // ...\n+    }\n+}\n+```\n+\n+### Layer 4: HTTP Response\n+\n+`Problem` implements `IntoResponse` for Axum, automatically:\n+- Setting the correct HTTP status code\n+- Setting `Content-Type: application/problem+json`\n+- Enriching with trace ID from current span if not set\n+\n+```rust\n+// In handler\n+async fn get_user(...) -> Result<Json<User>, Problem> {\n+    let user = service.get_user(id).await\n+        .map_err(|e| domain_error_to_problem(&e, &path))?;\n+    Ok(Json(user))\n+}\n+```\n+\n+## Creating a New Error Catalog\n+\n+### Step 1: Create `gts/errors.json`\n+\n+```json\n+[\n+  {\n+    \"status\": 404,\n+    \"title\": \"Resource Not Found\",\n+    \"code\": \"gts.hx.core.errors.err.v1~hx.mymodule.resource.not_found.v1\"\n+  },\n+  {\n+    \"status\": 422,\n+    \"title\": \"Validation Error\",\n+    \"code\": \"gts.hx.core.errors.err.v1~hx.mymodule.validation.invalid_input.v1\"\n+  }\n+]\n+```\n+\n+### Step 2: Create `src/errors.rs`\n+\n+```rust\n+use modkit_errors_macro::declare_errors;\n+\n+declare_errors! {\n+    path = \"gts/errors.json\",\n+    namespace = \"errors\",\n+    vis = \"pub\"\n+}\n+```\n+\n+### Step 3: Add to `Cargo.toml`\n+\n+```toml\n+[dependencies]\n+modkit-errors-macro = { path = \"../../libs/modkit-errors-macro\" }","path":"docs/GTS_ERRORS.md","commit_id":"5bdb0f43b25858af78999718f7247813802b9634","original_commit_id":"5bdb0f43b25858af78999718f7247813802b9634","user":{"login":"alizid10","id":247960800,"node_id":"U_kgDODseU4A","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/247960800?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/alizid10","html_url":"https://github.com/alizid10","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alizid10/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alizid10/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alizid10/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alizid10/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alizid10/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alizid10/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alizid10/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alizid10/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alizid10/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"this doc described how it works now, removed.","created_at":"2026-02-06T15:58:11Z","updated_at":"2026-02-06T15:58:12Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/290#discussion_r2774839919","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/290","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2774839919"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/290#discussion_r2774839919"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/290"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2774839919/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":null,"original_line":335,"side":"RIGHT","in_reply_to_id":2720921701,"author_association":"MEMBER","original_position":335,"position":1,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2774840695","pull_request_review_id":3763862457,"id":2774840695,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs6lZLV3","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,417 @@\n+# GTS Error System Documentation\n+\n+This document describes how errors are defined, structured, transformed, and used in the Hyperspot/gts-rust project.\n+\n+## Overview\n+\n+The error system follows **RFC 9457 Problem Details for HTTP APIs** and uses a **GTS (Global Type System)** format for error codes. The system provides:\n+\n+- **Compile-time validated** error catalogs via JSON files\n+- **Type-safe** error code enums generated by proc-macros\n+- **Layered error transformation** from domain → API → HTTP response\n+- **Consistent error format** across all modules\n+\n+## Architecture\n+\n+```\n+┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n+│                           Error Flow                                     │\n+├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n+│                                                                          │\n+│  gts/errors.json  ──────►  declare_errors! macro  ──────►  ErrorCode    │\n+│  (Source of Truth)         (Compile-time)                  (Enum)       │\n+│                                                                          │\n+│  DomainError  ──────►  ErrorCode::xxx().with_context()  ──────►  Problem│\n+│  (Business Logic)      (Mapping Layer)                        (RFC 9457)│\n+│                                                                          │\n+│  Problem  ──────►  IntoResponse (Axum)  ──────►  HTTP Response          │\n+│  (Data)            (Framework Integration)       (JSON + Headers)       │\n+│                                                                          │\n+└─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘\n+```\n+\n+## Components\n+\n+### 1. Error Catalog JSON (`gts/errors.json`)\n+\n+The source of truth for error definitions. Located in each module's `gts/` directory.\n+\n+**File Location Pattern:** `<module>/gts/errors.json`\n+\n+**Schema:**\n+```json\n+[\n+  {\n+    \"status\": 404,\n+    \"title\": \"User Not Found\",\n+    \"code\": \"gts.hx.core.errors.err.v1~hx.example1.user.not_found.v1\",\n+    \"type\": \"https://errors.example.com/...\",  // optional\n+    \"alias\": \"user_not_found\"                   // optional\n+  }\n+]\n+```\n+\n+**Fields:**\n+| Field | Required | Description |\n+|-------|----------|-------------|\n+| `status` | Yes | HTTP status code (100-599) |\n+| `title` | Yes | Human-readable error title |\n+| `code` | Yes | GTS-formatted error code |\n+| `type` | No | URI for error documentation |\n+| `alias` | No | Short name override for generated accessor |\n+\n+### 2. GTS Code Format\n+\n+GTS codes follow a strict format for global type identification:\n+\n+```\n+gts.vendor.package.namespace.type.version~chain1~chain2~...~instanceGTX\n+```\n+\n+**Structure:**\n+- **Prefix:** Always starts with `gts.`\n+- **Chain separator:** `~` separates GTX segments\n+- **Segment separator:** `.` separates parts within a GTX\n+- **Final GTX:** Must have at least 5 segments: `vendor.package.namespace.type.version`\n+- **Version:** Must end with `vN` or `vN.M` format\n+\n+**Example Breakdown:**\n+```\n+gts.hx.core.errors.err.v1~hx.example1.user.not_found.v1\n+│   │  │    │      │   │  │  │        │    │         │\n+│   │  │    │      │   │  │  │        │    │         └─ version\n+│   │  │    │      │   │  │  │        │    └─ type (not_found)\n+│   │  │    │      │   │  │  │        └─ namespace (user)\n+│   │  │    │      │   │  │  └─ package (example1)\n+│   │  │    │      │   │  └─ vendor (hx)\n+│   │  │    │      │   └─ version\n+│   │  │    │      └─ type (err)\n+│   │  │    └─ namespace (errors)\n+│   │  └─ package (core)\n+│   └─ vendor (hx)\n+└─ prefix\n+```\n+\n+**Validation Rules:**\n+1. Must start with `gts.`\n+2. All segments must be lowercase alphanumeric or underscore\n+3. No empty segments allowed\n+4. Final GTX must have ≥5 segments after vendor\n+5. Must end with valid version format (`v1`, `v1.2`, etc.)\n+\n+### 3. Proc-Macro: `declare_errors!`\n+\n+Generates type-safe error code enums from JSON at compile time.\n+\n+**Location:** `libs/modkit-errors-macro/src/lib.rs`\n+\n+**Usage:**\n+```rust\n+use modkit_errors_macro::declare_errors;\n+\n+declare_errors! {\n+    path = \"gts/errors.json\",\n+    namespace = \"errors\",\n+    vis = \"pub\"\n+}\n+```\n+\n+**Parameters:**\n+| Parameter | Required | Description |\n+|-----------|----------|-------------|\n+| `path` | Yes | Path to JSON file relative to `CARGO_MANIFEST_DIR` |\n+| `namespace` | Yes | Module name for generated code |\n+| `vis` | No | Visibility (`\"pub\"` or private) |\n+\n+**Generated Code:**\n+```rust\n+// Enum with all error codes\n+#[derive(Debug, Clone, Copy, PartialEq, Eq, Hash)]\n+pub enum ErrorCode {\n+    gts_hx_core_errors_err_v1_hx_example1_user_not_found_v1,\n+    // ...\n+}\n+\n+impl ErrorCode {\n+    // Get HTTP status\n+    pub const fn status(&self) -> u16 { ... }\n+    \n+    // Get full error definition\n+    pub const fn def(&self) -> ErrDef { ... }\n+    \n+    // Convert to Problem with detail\n+    pub fn as_problem(&self, detail: impl Into<String>) -> Problem { ... }\n+    \n+    // Create Problem with context (instance + trace_id)\n+    pub fn with_context(\n+        &self,\n+        detail: impl Into<String>,\n+        instance: &str,\n+        trace_id: Option<String>,\n+    ) -> Problem { ... }\n+    \n+    // Short accessor (derived from GTS or alias)\n+    pub const fn example1_user_not_found_v1() -> Self { ... }\n+}\n+\n+// Compile-time validated macro\n+macro_rules! problem_from_catalog { ... }\n+macro_rules! response_from_catalog { ... }\n+```\n+\n+### 4. Core Types\n+\n+#### `ErrDef` (Error Definition)\n+**Location:** `libs/modkit-errors/src/catalog.rs`\n+\n+```rust\n+pub struct ErrDef {\n+    pub status: u16,\n+    pub title: &'static str,\n+    pub code: &'static str,\n+    pub type_url: &'static str,\n+}\n+\n+impl ErrDef {\n+    pub fn as_problem(&self, detail: impl Into<String>) -> Problem { ... }\n+}\n+```\n+\n+#### `Problem` (RFC 9457)\n+**Location:** `libs/modkit-errors/src/problem.rs`\n+\n+```rust\n+pub struct Problem {\n+    pub type_url: String,      // URI reference for problem type\n+    pub title: String,         // Human-readable summary\n+    pub status: StatusCode,    // HTTP status code\n+    pub detail: String,        // Specific occurrence explanation\n+    pub instance: String,      // URI for this occurrence\n+    pub code: String,          // Machine-readable error code\n+    pub trace_id: Option<String>,\n+    pub errors: Option<Vec<ValidationViolation>>,\n+}\n+```\n+\n+**Builder Pattern:**\n+```rust\n+Problem::new(StatusCode::NOT_FOUND, \"Not Found\", \"User not found\")\n+    .with_code(\"gts.hx....\")\n+    .with_type(\"https://...\")\n+    .with_instance(\"/api/users/123\")\n+    .with_trace_id(\"req-456\")\n+    .with_errors(vec![...])\n+```\n+\n+## Error Flow by Layer\n+\n+### Layer 1: Domain Errors\n+\n+Domain errors represent business logic failures. They are internal and don't contain HTTP-specific information.\n+\n+**Location:** `<module>/src/domain/error.rs`\n+\n+```rust\n+#[derive(Error, Debug)]\n+pub enum DomainError {\n+    #[error(\"User not found: {id}\")]\n+    UserNotFound { id: Uuid },\n+    \n+    #[error(\"Email '{email}' already exists\")]\n+    EmailAlreadyExists { email: String },\n+    \n+    #[error(\"Database error: {message}\")]\n+    Database { message: String },\n+    // ...\n+}\n+```\n+\n+### Layer 2: SDK Errors (Public API)\n+\n+SDK errors are exposed to other modules via the client trait. They are simplified and safe to expose.\n+\n+**Location:** `<module>-sdk/src/errors.rs`\n+\n+```rust\n+#[derive(Error, Debug, Clone)]","path":"docs/GTS_ERRORS.md","commit_id":"5bdb0f43b25858af78999718f7247813802b9634","original_commit_id":"5bdb0f43b25858af78999718f7247813802b9634","user":{"login":"alizid10","id":247960800,"node_id":"U_kgDODseU4A","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/247960800?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/alizid10","html_url":"https://github.com/alizid10","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alizid10/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alizid10/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alizid10/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alizid10/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alizid10/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alizid10/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alizid10/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alizid10/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alizid10/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"this doc described how it works now, removed.","created_at":"2026-02-06T15:58:22Z","updated_at":"2026-02-06T15:58:23Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/290#discussion_r2774840695","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/290","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2774840695"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/290#discussion_r2774840695"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/290"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2774840695/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":null,"original_line":236,"side":"RIGHT","in_reply_to_id":2720841138,"author_association":"MEMBER","original_position":236,"position":1,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2774843580","pull_request_review_id":3763865582,"id":2774843580,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs6lZMC8","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,417 @@\n+# GTS Error System Documentation\n+\n+This document describes how errors are defined, structured, transformed, and used in the Hyperspot/gts-rust project.\n+\n+## Overview\n+\n+The error system follows **RFC 9457 Problem Details for HTTP APIs** and uses a **GTS (Global Type System)** format for error codes. The system provides:\n+\n+- **Compile-time validated** error catalogs via JSON files\n+- **Type-safe** error code enums generated by proc-macros\n+- **Layered error transformation** from domain → API → HTTP response\n+- **Consistent error format** across all modules\n+\n+## Architecture\n+\n+```\n+┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n+│                           Error Flow                                     │\n+├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n+│                                                                          │\n+│  gts/errors.json  ──────►  declare_errors! macro  ──────►  ErrorCode    │\n+│  (Source of Truth)         (Compile-time)                  (Enum)       │\n+│                                                                          │\n+│  DomainError  ──────►  ErrorCode::xxx().with_context()  ──────►  Problem│\n+│  (Business Logic)      (Mapping Layer)                        (RFC 9457)│\n+│                                                                          │\n+│  Problem  ──────►  IntoResponse (Axum)  ──────►  HTTP Response          │\n+│  (Data)            (Framework Integration)       (JSON + Headers)       │\n+│                                                                          │\n+└─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘\n+```\n+\n+## Components\n+\n+### 1. Error Catalog JSON (`gts/errors.json`)\n+\n+The source of truth for error definitions. Located in each module's `gts/` directory.\n+\n+**File Location Pattern:** `<module>/gts/errors.json`\n+\n+**Schema:**\n+```json\n+[\n+  {\n+    \"status\": 404,\n+    \"title\": \"User Not Found\",\n+    \"code\": \"gts.hx.core.errors.err.v1~hx.example1.user.not_found.v1\",\n+    \"type\": \"https://errors.example.com/...\",  // optional\n+    \"alias\": \"user_not_found\"                   // optional\n+  }\n+]\n+```\n+\n+**Fields:**\n+| Field | Required | Description |\n+|-------|----------|-------------|\n+| `status` | Yes | HTTP status code (100-599) |\n+| `title` | Yes | Human-readable error title |\n+| `code` | Yes | GTS-formatted error code |\n+| `type` | No | URI for error documentation |\n+| `alias` | No | Short name override for generated accessor |\n+\n+### 2. GTS Code Format\n+\n+GTS codes follow a strict format for global type identification:\n+\n+```\n+gts.vendor.package.namespace.type.version~chain1~chain2~...~instanceGTX\n+```\n+\n+**Structure:**\n+- **Prefix:** Always starts with `gts.`\n+- **Chain separator:** `~` separates GTX segments\n+- **Segment separator:** `.` separates parts within a GTX\n+- **Final GTX:** Must have at least 5 segments: `vendor.package.namespace.type.version`","path":"docs/GTS_ERRORS.md","commit_id":"5bdb0f43b25858af78999718f7247813802b9634","original_commit_id":"5bdb0f43b25858af78999718f7247813802b9634","user":{"login":"alizid10","id":247960800,"node_id":"U_kgDODseU4A","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/247960800?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/alizid10","html_url":"https://github.com/alizid10","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alizid10/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alizid10/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alizid10/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alizid10/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alizid10/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alizid10/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alizid10/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alizid10/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alizid10/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"removed","created_at":"2026-02-06T15:59:04Z","updated_at":"2026-02-06T15:59:04Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/290#discussion_r2774843580","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/290","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2774843580"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/290#discussion_r2774843580"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/290"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2774843580/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":null,"original_line":75,"side":"RIGHT","in_reply_to_id":2731520996,"author_association":"MEMBER","original_position":75,"position":1,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2774845489","pull_request_review_id":3763867631,"id":2774845489,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs6lZMgx","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,1574 @@\n+# Unified Error System - Intention Document\n+\n+This document defines the architecture, rules, and implementation plan for a unified error handling system across the Hyperspot project. All REST API errors MUST have a GTS identifier, trace ID, and be registered in the types registry.\n+\n+## Table of Contents\n+\n+1. [Executive Summary](#executive-summary)\n+2. [Industry Research](#industry-research)\n+3. [Current State Analysis](#current-state-analysis)\n+4. [Requirements](#requirements)\n+5. [Implementation Rules](#implementation-rules)\n+6. [Migration Plan](#migration-plan)\n+7. [Examples](#examples)\n+8. [HTTP Headers](#http-headers)\n+9. [Security Considerations](#security-considerations)\n+10. [Appendix A: Error Category Definitions](#appendix-a-error-category-definitions)\n+11. [Appendix B: Retryable Error Guidelines](#appendix-b-retryable-error-guidelines)\n+12. [GTS System Errors Catalog](#gts-system-errors-catalog)\n+13. [References](#references)\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Executive Summary\n+\n+### Problem Statement\n+\n+The current error handling across Hyperspot modules is inconsistent:\n+- Some modules use `declare_errors!` macro with JSON catalogs\n+- Others define errors inline without GTS codes\n+- Errors are not registered in the types registry\n+- No standardized metadata/context fields\n+- Inconsistent trace ID propagation\n+\n+### Goals\n+\n+1. **Every REST API error** MUST have a valid GTS identifier\n+2. **Every error response** MUST include a trace ID for debugging\n+3. **All error types** MUST be registered in the types registry\n+4. **Consistent error schema** across all modules following RFC 9457\n+5. **Machine-readable error codes** for programmatic handling\n+6. **Error stack propagation** for nested service calls\n+\n+### Non-Goals\n+\n+- Changing internal domain error types (only API-facing errors)\n+- Modifying logging infrastructure\n+- Changing HTTP status code semantics\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Industry Research\n+\n+### How Major Tech Companies Handle Errors\n+\n+| Company | Standard | Key Features |\n+|---------|----------|--------------|\n+| **Google** | AIP-193 + gRPC Status | `reason` (UPPER_SNAKE_CASE), `domain` (service name), `metadata` (key-value context), `ErrorInfo`, `LocalizedMessage`, `Help` links |\n+| **Amazon AWS** | Custom JSON | `errorType`, `httpStatus`, `requestId`, `message`, custom error object serialization |\n+| **Twitter/X** | JSON with `errors` array | `code` (CAPS_CASE), `message`, `parameter`, `details`, `value` |\n+| **RFC 9457** | Problem Details | `type` (URI), `title`, `status`, `detail`, `instance`, extension members |\n+\n+### Key Patterns Identified\n+\n+1. **Machine-readable identifiers** - Unique codes for programmatic handling (Google's `reason`, Twitter's `code`)\n+2. **Domain/namespace separation** - Identify error source (Google's `domain`, our GTS vendor.package)\n+3. **Structured metadata** - Key-value context without parsing messages (Google's `ErrorInfo.metadata`)\n+4. **Trace/Request IDs** - Correlation for debugging (AWS `requestId`, our `trace_id`)\n+5. **Documentation links** - URIs to error documentation (RFC 9457 `type`, Google's `Help`)\n+6. **Error categorization** - System vs User-defined, Retryable vs Non-retryable\n+\n+### Google AIP-193 ErrorInfo Structure (Reference)\n+\n+```json\n+{\n+  \"error\": {\n+    \"code\": 429,\n+    \"message\": \"The zone 'us-east1-a' does not have enough resources...\",\n+    \"status\": \"RESOURCE_EXHAUSTED\",\n+    \"details\": [\n+      {\n+        \"@type\": \"type.googleapis.com/google.rpc.ErrorInfo\",\n+        \"reason\": \"RESOURCE_AVAILABILITY\",\n+        \"domain\": \"compute.googleapis.com\",\n+        \"metadata\": {\n+          \"zone\": \"us-east1-a\",\n+          \"vmType\": \"e2-medium\"\n+        }\n+      }\n+    ]\n+  }\n+}\n+```\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Current State Analysis\n+\n+### Existing Infrastructure\n+\n+1. **`Problem` struct** (`libs/modkit-errors/src/problem.rs`) - RFC 9457 compliant\n+   - Fields: `type_url`, `title`, `status`, `detail`, `instance`, `code`, `trace_id`, `errors`\n+   - Implements `IntoResponse` for Axum with automatic trace ID enrichment\n+\n+2. **`struct_to_gts_schema` macro** (`modules/types-registry/gts-rust/gts-macros/src/lib.rs`)\n+   - Attribute macro for explicit struct definitions with GTS IDs visible in code\n+   - Generates constants: `GTS_SCHEMA_ID`, `GTS_SCHEMA_JSON`, etc.\n+   - **This pattern will be adapted for error definitions**\n+\n+3. **`declare_errors!` macro** (`libs/modkit-errors-macro/src/lib.rs`) - **TO BE DEPRECATED**\n+   - Generates type-safe error enums from JSON catalogs\n+   - Problem: GTS IDs hidden in external JSON files, not visible to LLMs\n+   - Used by: `users_info` example, `modkit-odata`\n+\n+### Gaps Identified\n+\n+| Gap | Current State | Required State |\n+|-----|---------------|----------------|\n+| **Hidden GTS IDs** | JSON-based `declare_errors!` | Explicit `#[gts_error]` structs with visible GTS IDs |\n+| **Inconsistent definitions** | Some modules use inline errors | All modules use `#[gts_error]` structs |\n+| **No types registry** | Errors not registered | All errors registered as GTS types |\n+| **Missing metadata** | No structured context | Struct fields → `metadata` map |\n+| **Partial trace IDs** | Only in `IntoResponse` | Mandatory in all error responses |\n+| **No error categories** | Flat error codes | System/Operational/Client categories |\n+| **No error stack** | Single error | Upstream error chain propagation |\n+\n+### Current Module Migration Status\n+\n+| Module | Location | Status | Issues |\n+|--------|----------|--------|--------|\n+| **file_parser** | `modules/file_parser/` | 🔴 Not migrated | No GTS IDs, inline `Problem::new()` |\n+| **types-registry** | `modules/system/types-registry/` | 🟡 Partial | Has codes but not GTS format (e.g., `TYPES_REGISTRY_NOT_FOUND`) |\n+| **nodes_registry** | `modules/system/nodes_registry/` | 🔴 Not migrated | Non-GTS codes (e.g., `NODES_NOT_FOUND`) |\n+| **api_gateway** | `modules/system/api_gateway/` | 🔴 Not migrated | No Problem struct, simple error codes |\n+| **tenant_resolver** | `modules/system/tenant_resolver/` | 🔴 Not migrated | No GTS IDs |\n+| **simple-user-settings** | `modules/simple-user-settings/` | 🟡 Partial | Uses `declare_errors!` with old chain format |\n+| **modkit-auth** | `libs/modkit-auth/` | 🔴 Not migrated | No GTS IDs, custom `IntoResponse` |\n+| **modkit-odata** | `libs/modkit-odata/` | 🟡 Partial | Uses `declare_errors!` with old chain format |\n+| **users_info** (example) | `examples/modkit/users_info/` | 🟡 Partial | Uses `declare_errors!` with old chain format |\n+\n+#### Legend\n+- 🟢 **Migrated** - Uses `#[gts_error]` structs with proper base types\n+- 🟡 **Partial** - Has GTS IDs but uses deprecated `declare_errors!` or old format\n+- 🔴 **Not migrated** - No GTS IDs or non-GTS format codes\n+\n+#### GTS ID Format Note\n+\n+**Old chain format** (used by `declare_errors!`):\n+```\n+gts.hx.core.errors.err.v1~hx.module.error_name.v1\n+```\n+\n+**New format** (with `base` field):\n+```\n+gts.hx.module.namespace.error_name.v1~\n+```\n+The `base` field in `#[gts_error]` replaces the chain suffix, making inheritance explicit in code.\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Requirements\n+\n+### R1: Error Schema Requirements\n+\n+Every error returned from REST API MUST conform to the unified schema:\n+\n+```rust\n+pub struct Problem {\n+    // =========================================================================\n+    // REQUIRED FIELDS - Core error identification\n+    // =========================================================================\n+    \n+    /// URI reference identifying the problem type (GTS-based)\n+    /// Example: \"https://docs.hyperspot.com/errors/types_registry_entity_not_found_v1\"\n+    #[serde(rename = \"type\")]\n+    pub type_url: String,\n+    \n+    /// Human-readable summary of the problem type (static per error type)\n+    pub title: String,\n+    \n+    /// GTS error code (machine-readable identifier)\n+    pub code: String,\n+    \n+    /// Trace ID for request correlation\n+    pub trace_id: String,\n+    \n+    // =========================================================================\n+    // CONTEXTUAL FIELDS - Optional based on error context\n+    // =========================================================================\n+    \n+    /// HTTP status code. Optional because:\n+    /// - gRPC errors use different status codes\n+    /// - Internal/domain errors may not have HTTP context\n+    /// - Event-driven systems have no request/response\n+    /// When serializing for HTTP response, this is populated from error definition.\n+    #[serde(skip_serializing_if = \"Option::is_none\")]\n+    pub status: Option<u16>,\n+    \n+    /// Human-readable explanation specific to this occurrence.\n+    /// Optional - title may be sufficient for simple errors.\n+    #[serde(skip_serializing_if = \"Option::is_none\")]\n+    pub detail: Option<String>,\n+    \n+    /// Error category for client handling.\n+    /// Optional - can be inferred from base type hierarchy.\n+    #[serde(skip_serializing_if = \"Option::is_none\")]\n+    pub category: Option<ErrorCategory>,\n+    \n+    /// Whether client can retry this request.\n+    /// Optional - can be inferred from base type; not relevant for all contexts.\n+    #[serde(skip_serializing_if = \"Option::is_none\")]\n+    pub retryable: Option<bool>,\n+    \n+    /// URI identifying this specific occurrence (auto-populated from request path)\n+    #[serde(skip_serializing_if = \"Option::is_none\")]\n+    pub instance: Option<String>,\n+    \n+    /// Structured metadata (key-value context)\n+    #[serde(skip_serializing_if = \"Option::is_none\")]\n+    pub metadata: Option<HashMap<String, String>>,\n+    \n+    /// Validation errors for 4xx responses\n+    #[serde(skip_serializing_if = \"Option::is_none\")]\n+    pub errors: Option<Vec<ValidationViolation>>,\n+    \n+    /// Upstream error chain (when error_stack enabled)\n+    #[serde(skip_serializing_if = \"Option::is_none\")]\n+    pub upstream_errors: Option<Vec<UpstreamError>>,\n+}\n+\n+pub enum ErrorCategory {\n+    /// Platform-level execution errors (panics, OOM, internal bugs)\n+    System,\n+    /// Infrastructure/operational issues (DB unavailable, service down, rate limits)\n+    Operational,\n+    /// Client input/request errors (validation, not found, unauthorized)\n+    Client,\n+}\n+```\n+\n+#### Field Requirements Summary\n+\n+| Field | Required | Reason |\n+|-------|----------|--------|\n+| `type_url` | ✅ Yes | RFC 9457 requires problem type URI |\n+| `title` | ✅ Yes | Human-readable error name (static per type) |\n+| `code` | ✅ Yes | GTS identifier for machine processing |\n+| `trace_id` | ✅ Yes | Request correlation for debugging |\n+| `status` | ❌ No | Only relevant for HTTP; gRPC/events/domain errors don't need it |\n+| `detail` | ❌ No | Instance-specific message; title may suffice |\n+| `category` | ❌ No | Inherited from base type hierarchy |\n+| `retryable` | ❌ No | Inherited from base type; not relevant for all contexts |\n+| `instance` | ❌ No | Auto-populated from request path when applicable |\n+| `metadata` | ❌ No | Additional context key-value pairs |\n+| `errors` | ❌ No | Validation violations for 4xx errors |\n+| `upstream_errors` | ❌ No | Error chain from upstream services |\n+\n+**Note:** When converting to HTTP response, `status` is populated from the error definition. When the error is used in non-HTTP contexts (gRPC, domain logic, events), `status` remains `None`.\n+\n+### R2: GTS Identifier and Base Type Requirements\n+\n+Every error MUST have a valid GTS identifier and specify its base type using the `base` field.\n+\n+#### GTS ID Format\n+\n+```\n+gts.<vendor>.<package>.<namespace>.<type>.v<version>~\n+```\n+\n+**Examples:**\n+- `gts.hx.types_registry.entity.not_found.v1~` - Types registry not found error\n+- `gts.hx.file_parser.validation.invalid_format.v1~` - File parser validation error\n+- `gts.hx.system.runtime.timeout.v1~` - System timeout error\n+\n+#### Base Type Chaining\n+\n+Errors form an inheritance chain using the `base` field. The `base` field references another error struct type (not a string literal), similar to how `struct_to_gts_schema` works.\n+\n+The root base error type is:\n+\n+```rust\n+/// Root error type for all GTS errors.\n+#[gts_error(\n+    gts_id = \"gts.hx.core.errors.err.v1~\",\n+    base = true,  // Marks this as a root base type (no parent)\n+    title = \"Error\",\n+    // Optional attributes with defaults for inheritance:\n+    status = 500,        // Default HTTP status (optional, inherited by children)\n+    category = \"System\", // Default category (optional, inherited by children)\n+    retryable = false    // Default retryable (optional, inherited by children)\n+)]\n+pub struct BaseError;\n+```\n+\n+All module-specific errors MUST reference their base type as a struct (extending the appropriate logical/system error):\n+\n+```rust\n+use modkit_errors::system::logical::NotFoundError;\n+\n+/// Entity was not found in the types registry.\n+/// Note: status, category, retryable are inherited from NotFoundError if not specified.\n+#[gts_error(\n+    gts_id = \"gts.hx.types_registry.entity.not_found.v1~\",\n+    base = NotFoundError,  // Extends logical.not_found, not BaseError\n+    title = \"Entity Not Found\",\n+    // These are optional - inherited from base if omitted:\n+    // status = 404,      // Inherited from NotFoundError\n+    // category = \"Client\", // Inherited from NotFoundError  \n+    // retryable = false,   // Inherited from NotFoundError\n+)]\n+pub struct EntityNotFoundError {\n+    pub gts_id: String,\n+}\n+```\n+\n+#### Multi-Level Inheritance\n+\n+Errors can form deeper inheritance chains:\n+\n+```rust\n+/// Logical not found error (platform-level).\n+#[gts_error(\n+    gts_id = \"gts.hx.system.logical.not_found.v1~\",\n+    base = BaseError,  // Platform errors extend BaseError\n+    status = 404,\n+    title = \"Not Found\",\n+    category = \"Client\",\n+    retryable = false\n+)]\n+pub struct NotFoundError;\n+\n+/// Types registry entity not found (module-level).\n+#[gts_error(\n+    gts_id = \"gts.hx.types_registry.entity.not_found.v1~\",\n+    base = NotFoundError,  // Module errors extend logical errors\n+    status = 404,\n+    title = \"Entity Not Found\",\n+    category = \"Client\",\n+    retryable = false\n+)]\n+pub struct EntityNotFoundError {\n+    pub gts_id: String,\n+}\n+```\n+\n+#### Inheritance Hierarchy\n+\n+```\n+BaseError (gts.hx.core.errors.err.v1~)                              [base = true]\n+├── Transport Errors (hx.system.transport.*)                        [base = BaseError]\n+├── Runtime Errors (hx.system.runtime.*)                            [base = BaseError]\n+│   └── hx.types_registry.system.internal.v1~                       [base = runtime.internal]\n+├── HTTP Errors (hx.system.http.*)                                  [base = BaseError]\n+│   └── hx.auth.token_expired.v1~                                   [base = http.unauthorized]\n+├── gRPC Errors (hx.system.grpc.*)                                  [base = BaseError]\n+└── Logical Errors (hx.system.logical.*)                            [base = BaseError]\n+    ├── logical.not_found.v1~                                       [base = BaseError]\n+    │   ├── hx.types_registry.entity.not_found.v1~                  [base = logical.not_found]\n+    │   └── hx.db.entity.not_found.v1~                              [base = logical.not_found]\n+    ├── logical.already_exists.v1~                                  [base = BaseError]\n+    │   └── hx.types_registry.entity.already_exists.v1~             [base = logical.already_exists]\n+    └── logical.validation_failed.v1~                               [base = BaseError]\n+        └── hx.file_parser.validation.invalid_format.v1~            [base = logical.validation_failed]\n+```\n+\n+### R3: Trace ID Requirements\n+\n+- Every error response MUST include a non-empty `trace_id`\n+- Trace ID MUST be propagated from incoming request headers or generated\n+- Trace ID MUST be logged with the error for correlation\n+\n+### R4: Types Registry Integration\n+\n+- All error types MUST be registered in the types registry at startup\n+- Error schema MUST extend base error type: `gts.hx.core.errors.err.v1`\n+- Registration MUST include: code, title, status, category, retryable flag\n+\n+### R5: Standardized System Error Types\n+\n+See [GTS System Errors Catalog](#gts-system-errors-catalog) for the complete list of all system errors.\n+\n+### R6: Error Stack Propagation\n+\n+When a function calls another service/function that returns an error:\n+- The error SHOULD be wrapped with context\n+- `upstream_errors` array SHOULD contain the chain of errors\n+- Each upstream error includes: `code`, `title`, `detail`, `source`\n+- Propagation controlled by `error_stack` configuration flag\n+\n+---\n+\n+## GTS Error Code Format\n+\n+### Structure\n+\n+```\n+gts.<vendor>.<package>.<namespace>.<type>.<version>~<chain>\n+```\n+\n+### Components\n+\n+| Component | Description | Example |\n+|-----------|-------------|---------|\n+| `gts` | Global Type System prefix | `gts` |\n+| `vendor` | Organization identifier | `hx` (Hyperspot) |\n+| `package` | Module/service name | `types_registry`, `file_parser` |\n+| `namespace` | Error category | `entity`, `validation`, `runtime` |\n+| `type` | Specific error type | `not_found`, `invalid_format` |\n+| `version` | Schema version | `v1`, `v1.0` |\n+| `~chain` | Base type chain | `~hx.core.errors.err.v1` |\n+\n+### Validation Rules\n+\n+1. MUST start with `gts.`\n+2. All segments MUST be lowercase alphanumeric or underscore\n+3. No empty segments allowed\n+4. Final segment MUST be version format (`vN` or `vN.M`)\n+5. MUST chain from base error type\n+\n+### Short Name Derivation\n+\n+Short accessor names derived from final GTX segment:\n+```\n+gts.hx.core.errors.err.v1~hx.types_registry.entity.not_found.v1\n+                         └─────────────────────────────────────┘\n+                                          ↓\n+                         types_registry_entity_not_found_v1()\n+```\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Types Registry Integration\n+\n+### Error Type Schema\n+\n+```json\n+{\n+  \"gts_id\": \"gts.hx.types_registry.entity.not_found.v1~\",\n+  \"kind\": \"error\",\n+  \"schema\": {\n+    \"type\": \"object\",\n+    \"extends\": \"gts.hx.system.logical.not_found.v1~\",\n+    \"properties\": {\n+      \"status\": { \"const\": 404 },\n+      \"title\": { \"const\": \"Entity Not Found\" },\n+      \"category\": { \"const\": \"Client\" },\n+      \"retryable\": { \"const\": false }\n+    }\n+  },\n+  \"metadata\": {\n+    \"module\": \"types-registry\",\n+    \"documentation_url\": \"https://docs.hyperspot.com/errors/types_registry_entity_not_found_v1\"\n+  }\n+}\n+```\n+\n+### Registration Flow\n+\n+1. Module defines errors as explicit structs with `#[gts_error]` attribute in `src/errors.rs`\n+2. Each struct generates `ERROR_DEF` constant with GTS metadata\n+3. Module implements `all_error_definitions()` function returning all error definitions\n+4. At module startup (`on_ready`), errors are registered with types registry:\n+   ```rust\n+   impl Module for MyModule {\n+       async fn on_ready(&self, ctx: &ModuleContext) -> Result<()> {\n+           // Register all error types with types registry\n+           let errors = crate::errors::all_error_definitions();\n+           ctx.types_registry().register_errors(errors).await?;\n+           Ok(())\n+       }\n+   }\n+   ```\n+5. Types registry validates GTS format and schema compliance\n+6. Errors become discoverable via types registry API\n+\n+### API for Error Discovery\n+\n+```http\n+GET /api/types-registry/v1/types?kind=error&module=types-registry\n+\n+Response:\n+{\n+  \"items\": [\n+    {\n+      \"gts_id\": \"gts.hx.core.errors.err.v1~hx.types_registry.entity.not_found.v1\",\n+      \"status\": 404,\n+      \"title\": \"Entity Not Found\",\n+      \"category\": \"Client\",\n+      \"retryable\": false,\n+      \"documentation_url\": \"...\"\n+    }\n+  ]\n+}\n+```\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Implementation Rules\n+\n+### Rule 1: All Errors MUST Use Explicit Struct Definitions with `#[gts_error]`\n+\n+Errors are defined as explicit structs with the `#[gts_error]` attribute macro. This approach:\n+- Makes GTS IDs visible directly in code (better for LLM code generation)\n+- Provides compile-time validation\n+- Generates `Problem` conversion automatically\n+- Enables types registry integration\n+\n+```rust\n+// ✅ CORRECT - Explicit struct definition with visible GTS ID and base type reference\n+use modkit_errors::gts_error;\n+\n+// First, import the appropriate base error types from system errors\n+use modkit_errors::system::logical::{NotFoundError, AlreadyExistsError, ValidationFailedError};\n+\n+/// Entity was not found in the types registry.\n+#[gts_error(\n+    gts_id = \"gts.hx.types_registry.entity.not_found.v1~\",\n+    base = NotFoundError,  // Extends logical.not_found, not BaseError\n+    status = 404,\n+    title = \"Entity Not Found\",\n+    category = \"Client\",\n+    retryable = false\n+)]\n+pub struct EntityNotFoundError {\n+    /// The GTS ID that was not found\n+    pub gts_id: String,\n+}\n+\n+/// Entity already exists in the registry.\n+#[gts_error(\n+    gts_id = \"gts.hx.types_registry.entity.already_exists.v1~\",\n+    base = AlreadyExistsError,  // Extends logical.already_exists\n+    status = 409,\n+    title = \"Entity Already Exists\",\n+    category = \"Client\",\n+    retryable = false\n+)]\n+pub struct EntityAlreadyExistsError {\n+    /// The GTS ID that already exists\n+    pub gts_id: String,\n+}\n+\n+/// Invalid GTS ID format.\n+#[gts_error(\n+    gts_id = \"gts.hx.types_registry.validation.invalid_gts_id.v1~\",\n+    base = ValidationFailedError,  // Extends logical.validation_failed\n+    status = 400,\n+    title = \"Invalid GTS ID\",\n+    category = \"Client\",\n+    retryable = false\n+)]\n+pub struct InvalidGtsIdError {\n+    /// Description of the validation error\n+    pub message: String,\n+}\n+\n+// ❌ WRONG - Inline error definitions without GTS ID\n+impl From<DomainError> for Problem {\n+    fn from(e: DomainError) -> Self {\n+        Problem::new(StatusCode::NOT_FOUND, \"Not Found\", \"...\")\n+            .with_code(\"SOME_CODE\") // Not GTS format!\n+    }\n+}\n+\n+// ❌ WRONG - JSON-based declaration (GTS ID hidden in external file)\n+declare_errors! {\n+    path = \"gts/errors.json\",\n+    namespace = \"errors\",\n+    vis = \"pub\"\n+}\n+```\n+\n+### Rule 2: Error Struct Field Conventions\n+\n+Error structs contain context fields that become `metadata` in the Problem response:\n+\n+```rust\n+use modkit_errors::system::logical::ValidationFailedError as LogicalValidationFailed;\n+\n+/// Request validation failed (module-specific).\n+#[gts_error(\n+    gts_id = \"gts.hx.types_registry.validation.failed.v1~\",\n+    base = LogicalValidationFailed,  // Extends logical.validation_failed\n+    status = 422,\n+    title = \"Validation Failed\",\n+    category = \"Client\",\n+    retryable = false\n+)]\n+pub struct ValidationFailedError {\n+    /// Human-readable error message\n+    pub message: String,\n+    /// Field that failed validation (optional)\n+    #[gts_error(skip_metadata)]  // Don't include in metadata\n+    pub violations: Vec<ValidationViolation>,\n+}\n+```\n+\n+### Rule 3: Error Mapping Pattern\n+\n+```rust\n+use crate::errors::{EntityNotFoundError, EntityAlreadyExistsError, InvalidGtsIdError};\n+\n+pub fn domain_error_to_problem(e: &DomainError) -> Problem {\n+    match e {\n+        DomainError::NotFound { id } => {\n+            // into_problem() auto-populates trace_id from current tracing span\n+            EntityNotFoundError { gts_id: id.clone() }\n+                .into_problem()\n+                .with_detail(format!(\"Entity with GTS ID '{}' was not found\", id))\n+        }\n+        DomainError::AlreadyExists { id } => {\n+            EntityAlreadyExistsError { gts_id: id.clone() }\n+                .into_problem()\n+                .with_detail(format!(\"Entity with GTS ID '{}' already exists\", id))\n+        }\n+        DomainError::InvalidGtsId(msg) => {\n+            InvalidGtsIdError { message: msg.clone() }\n+                .into_problem()\n+        }\n+        // ...\n+    }\n+}\n+```\n+\n+### Rule 4: Trace ID Auto-Population\n+\n+Trace ID is **mandatory** in all error responses but **optional** in `into_problem()`. If not provided, it's auto-populated from the current tracing span.\n+\n+```rust\n+// Default: trace_id auto-populated from current tracing span\n+let problem = EntityNotFoundError { gts_id: id.clone() }\n+    .into_problem()  // trace_id extracted from tracing::Span::current()\n+    .with_detail(\"Entity not found\");\n+\n+// Override: explicitly pass trace_id if needed\n+let problem = EntityNotFoundError { gts_id: id.clone() }\n+    .into_problem()\n+    .with_trace_id(&custom_trace_id)  // Override auto-populated value\n+    .with_detail(\"Entity not found\");\n+```\n+\n+### Rule 5: Instance Auto-Population\n+\n+The `instance` field is **optional** and **auto-populated** from the request path in the Axum `IntoResponse` implementation. You don't need to pass it manually.\n+\n+```rust\n+// In Axum IntoResponse implementation\n+impl IntoResponse for Problem {\n+    fn into_response(self) -> Response {\n+        // Auto-populate instance from request URI if not set\n+        let problem = if self.instance.is_none() {\n+            // Instance is populated from request extensions or current URI\n+            if let Some(uri) = REQUEST_URI.try_with(|u| u.clone()).ok() {\n+                self.with_instance(uri.path())\n+            } else {\n+                self\n+            }\n+        } else {\n+            self\n+        };\n+        // ... rest of response building\n+    }\n+}\n+```\n+\n+If you need to override the instance manually, use `with_instance()`:\n+\n+```rust\n+let problem = EntityNotFoundError { gts_id: id.clone() }\n+    .into_problem()\n+    .with_instance(\"/custom/path\");  // Optional override\n+```\n+\n+### Rule 6: Error Registration at Startup\n+\n+Error definitions are **auto-collected** at compile time using the `#[gts_error]` macro with `linkme`. No manual registration list needed.\n+\n+#### How `linkme` Works\n+\n+The [`linkme`](https://docs.rs/linkme) crate provides **distributed slices** - a way to collect static items from across the crate into a single slice at link time.\n+\n+**Step 1: Define the collection point** (in `src/errors.rs`):\n+```rust\n+use linkme::distributed_slice;\n+\n+/// This is the \"collection point\" - an empty slice that will be filled at link time.\n+/// The linker will gather all items marked with #[distributed_slice(ERROR_DEFINITIONS)]\n+/// and place them contiguously in this slice.\n+#[distributed_slice]\n+pub static ERROR_DEFINITIONS: [&'static GtsErrorDefStatic];\n+```\n+\n+**Step 2: Each `#[gts_error]` macro generates a contributor**:\n+```rust\n+// When you write:\n+#[gts_error(\n+    gts_id = \"gts.hx.types_registry.entity.not_found.v1~\",\n+    base = NotFoundError,  // Extends logical.not_found\n+    status = 404,\n+    ...\n+)]\n+pub struct EntityNotFoundError { ... }\n+\n+// The macro generates (among other things):\n+impl EntityNotFoundError {\n+    pub const ERROR_DEF: GtsErrorDefStatic = GtsErrorDefStatic { ... };\n+}\n+\n+// AND this linkme contributor:\n+#[linkme::distributed_slice(crate::errors::ERROR_DEFINITIONS)]\n+#[linkme(crate = linkme)]\n+static __ENTITY_NOT_FOUND_ERROR_DEF: &'static GtsErrorDefStatic = &EntityNotFoundError::ERROR_DEF;\n+```\n+\n+**Step 3: At link time, the linker collects all contributors**:\n+```\n+┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n+│                    Link-Time Collection                          │\n+├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n+│                                                                  │\n+│  EntityNotFoundError::ERROR_DEF ──────┐                         │\n+│  EntityAlreadyExistsError::ERROR_DEF ─┼──► ERROR_DEFINITIONS[]  │\n+│  InvalidGtsIdError::ERROR_DEF ────────┤    (contiguous slice)   │\n+│  ValidationFailedError::ERROR_DEF ────┤                         │\n+│  ServiceNotReadyError::ERROR_DEF ─────┤                         │\n+│  InternalError::ERROR_DEF ────────────┘                         │\n+│                                                                  │\n+│  The linker places all #[distributed_slice(ERROR_DEFINITIONS)]  │\n+│  items into a contiguous memory section, making them accessible │\n+│  as a single &[&'static GtsErrorDefStatic] slice at runtime.    │\n+│                                                                  │\n+└─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘\n+```\n+\n+**Step 4: Access at runtime**:\n+```rust\n+pub fn all_error_definitions() -> &'static [&'static GtsErrorDefStatic] {\n+    &ERROR_DEFINITIONS  // Returns slice with ALL error defs, auto-collected\n+}\n+```\n+\n+#### Why This Works\n+\n+- **Linker magic**: `linkme` uses platform-specific linker sections (`.init_array` on Linux, `__DATA,__mod_init_func` on macOS) to collect items\n+- **Zero runtime cost**: Collection happens at link time, not runtime\n+- **Compile-time guarantee**: If you use `#[gts_error]`, it's automatically in the slice\n+- **No manual list**: Impossible to forget an error - the macro handles registration\n+\n+#### Module Startup\n+\n+```rust\n+impl Module for MyModule {\n+    async fn on_ready(&self, ctx: &ModuleContext) -> Result<()> {\n+        // All errors are auto-collected - no way to forget one!\n+        let errors = crate::errors::all_error_definitions();\n+        ctx.types_registry().register_errors(errors).await?;\n+        Ok(())\n+    }\n+}\n+```\n+\n+### Rule 7: Metadata for Dynamic Context\n+\n+```rust\n+// ✅ CORRECT - Use metadata for dynamic values\n+ValidationFailedError { message: \"Validation failed\".to_string(), violations: vec![] }\n+    .into_problem()  // trace_id auto-populated from tracing span\n+    .with_metadata([\n+        (\"field\", \"email\"),\n+        (\"constraint\", \"must be valid email format\"),\n+        (\"provided_value\", \"[REDACTED]\"), // Never expose sensitive data\n+    ])\n+\n+// ❌ WRONG - Parsing dynamic values from detail string\n+ValidationFailedError { \n+    message: \"Field 'email' failed constraint 'must be valid email'\".to_string(),\n+    violations: vec![] \n+}\n+    .into_problem()\n+```\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Migration Plan\n+\n+### Phase 1: Create `#[gts_error]` Macro\n+\n+1. Create new proc-macro crate `libs/modkit-errors-macro-v2/` with `#[gts_error]` attribute macro\n+2. Implement macro to generate:\n+   - `GTS_ID`, `STATUS`, `TITLE`, `CATEGORY`, `RETRYABLE` constants\n+   - `ERROR_DEF` static for registration\n+   - `into_problem()` method\n+   - `to_metadata()` for struct fields → HashMap conversion\n+   - `Display` and `Error` trait implementations\n+3. Add compile-time GTS format validation\n+4. Add field attribute `#[gts_error(skip_metadata)]` and `#[gts_error(as_errors)]`\n+\n+### Phase 2: Extend Problem Struct\n+\n+1. Extend `Problem` struct with new fields:\n+   - `category: ErrorCategory`\n+   - `retryable: bool`\n+   - `metadata: Option<HashMap<String, String>>`\n+   - `upstream_errors: Option<Vec<UpstreamError>>`\n+   - Make `trace_id` non-optional (String instead of Option<String>)\n+2. Add builder methods: `with_category()`, `with_retryable()`, `with_metadata()`\n+3. Update `IntoResponse` implementation\n+\n+### Phase 3: Types Registry Integration\n+\n+1. Define `GtsErrorDef` trait and `GtsErrorDefStatic` struct\n+2. Add error registration API to types registry\n+3. Implement `register_errors()` method in module context\n+4. Add error discovery endpoint: `GET /api/types-registry/v1/types?kind=error`\n+\n+### Phase 4: Module Migration\n+\n+Migrate modules to explicit struct-based errors:\n+1. `types-registry` - Create `src/errors.rs` with `#[gts_error]` structs\n+2. `file_parser` - Create `src/errors.rs` with `#[gts_error]` structs\n+3. `nodes_registry` - Create `src/errors.rs` with `#[gts_error]` structs\n+4. `api_gateway` - Create `src/errors.rs` with `#[gts_error]` structs\n+\n+### Phase 5: System Errors Library\n+\n+1. Create `libs/modkit-errors/src/system_errors.rs` with common errors:\n+   - `InternalServerError`, `ServiceUnavailableError`, `GatewayTimeoutError`\n+   - `UnauthorizedError`, `ForbiddenError`, `NotFoundError`\n+   - `BadRequestError`, `ValidationFailedError`, `ConflictError`\n+   - `RateLimitedError`\n+2. Export from `modkit::errors::system` for all modules to use\n+3. Register system errors at platform startup\n+\n+### Phase 6: Deprecate `declare_errors!`\n+\n+1. Mark `declare_errors!` macro as deprecated\n+2. Update `GTS_ERRORS.md` documentation\n+3. Add migration guide from JSON-based to struct-based errors\n+4. Remove JSON error catalogs from migrated modules\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Examples\n+\n+### Example 1: Complete Error Response\n+\n+```json\n+{\n+  \"type\": \"https://docs.hyperspot.com/errors/types_registry_entity_not_found_v1\",\n+  \"title\": \"Entity Not Found\",\n+  \"status\": 404,\n+  \"detail\": \"Entity with GTS ID 'gts.hx.example.test.v1' was not found in the registry\",\n+  \"instance\": \"/api/types-registry/v1/types/gts.hx.example.test.v1\",\n+  \"code\": \"gts.hx.core.errors.err.v1~hx.types_registry.entity.not_found.v1\",\n+  \"trace_id\": \"abc123-def456-ghi789\",\n+  \"category\": \"Client\",\n+  \"retryable\": false,\n+  \"metadata\": {\n+    \"gts_id\": \"gts.hx.example.test.v1\",\n+    \"searched_at\": \"2026-01-19T13:30:00Z\"\n+  }\n+}\n+```\n+\n+### Example 2: Validation Error with Multiple Violations\n+\n+```json\n+{\n+  \"type\": \"https://docs.hyperspot.com/errors/validation_failed_v1\",\n+  \"title\": \"Validation Failed\",\n+  \"status\": 422,\n+  \"detail\": \"Request validation failed with 2 errors\",\n+  \"instance\": \"/api/users/v1/users\",\n+  \"code\": \"gts.hx.core.errors.err.v1~hx.system.validation_failed.v1\",\n+  \"trace_id\": \"req-12345\",\n+  \"category\": \"Client\",\n+  \"retryable\": false,\n+  \"errors\": [\n+    {\n+      \"field\": \"email\",\n+      \"message\": \"Must be a valid email address\",\n+      \"code\": \"INVALID_EMAIL_FORMAT\"\n+    },\n+    {\n+      \"field\": \"age\",\n+      \"message\": \"Must be at least 18\",\n+      \"code\": \"MIN_VALUE_VIOLATION\"\n+    }\n+  ]\n+}\n+```\n+\n+### Example 3: Error with Upstream Chain\n+\n+```json\n+{\n+  \"type\": \"https://docs.hyperspot.com/errors/upstream_error_v1\",\n+  \"title\": \"Upstream Service Error\",\n+  \"status\": 502,\n+  \"detail\": \"Failed to fetch user data from identity service\",\n+  \"instance\": \"/api/users/v1/users/123/profile\",\n+  \"code\": \"gts.hx.core.errors.err.v1~hx.users.upstream.identity_failed.v1\",\n+  \"trace_id\": \"trace-abc-123\",\n+  \"category\": \"System\",\n+  \"retryable\": true,\n+  \"upstream_errors\": [\n+    {\n+      \"code\": \"gts.hx.core.errors.err.v1~hx.identity.user.not_found.v1\",\n+      \"title\": \"User Not Found\",\n+      \"detail\": \"User 123 not found in identity service\",\n+      \"source\": \"identity-service\"\n+    }\n+  ]\n+}\n+```\n+\n+### Example 4: Complete Error Module Definition","path":"intended_design/UNIFIED_ERROR_SYSTEM.md","commit_id":"5bdb0f43b25858af78999718f7247813802b9634","original_commit_id":"5bdb0f43b25858af78999718f7247813802b9634","user":{"login":"alizid10","id":247960800,"node_id":"U_kgDODseU4A","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/247960800?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/alizid10","html_url":"https://github.com/alizid10","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alizid10/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alizid10/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alizid10/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alizid10/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alizid10/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alizid10/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alizid10/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alizid10/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alizid10/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"replaced","created_at":"2026-02-06T15:59:30Z","updated_at":"2026-02-06T15:59:31Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/290#discussion_r2774845489","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/290","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2774845489"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/290#discussion_r2774845489"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/290"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2774845489/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":null,"original_line":916,"side":"RIGHT","in_reply_to_id":2731757110,"author_association":"MEMBER","original_position":916,"position":1,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2774846409","pull_request_review_id":3763868539,"id":2774846409,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs6lZMvJ","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,1574 @@\n+# Unified Error System - Intention Document\n+\n+This document defines the architecture, rules, and implementation plan for a unified error handling system across the Hyperspot project. All REST API errors MUST have a GTS identifier, trace ID, and be registered in the types registry.\n+\n+## Table of Contents\n+\n+1. [Executive Summary](#executive-summary)\n+2. [Industry Research](#industry-research)\n+3. [Current State Analysis](#current-state-analysis)\n+4. [Requirements](#requirements)\n+5. [Implementation Rules](#implementation-rules)\n+6. [Migration Plan](#migration-plan)\n+7. [Examples](#examples)\n+8. [HTTP Headers](#http-headers)\n+9. [Security Considerations](#security-considerations)\n+10. [Appendix A: Error Category Definitions](#appendix-a-error-category-definitions)\n+11. [Appendix B: Retryable Error Guidelines](#appendix-b-retryable-error-guidelines)\n+12. [GTS System Errors Catalog](#gts-system-errors-catalog)\n+13. [References](#references)\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Executive Summary\n+\n+### Problem Statement\n+\n+The current error handling across Hyperspot modules is inconsistent:\n+- Some modules use `declare_errors!` macro with JSON catalogs\n+- Others define errors inline without GTS codes\n+- Errors are not registered in the types registry\n+- No standardized metadata/context fields\n+- Inconsistent trace ID propagation\n+\n+### Goals\n+\n+1. **Every REST API error** MUST have a valid GTS identifier\n+2. **Every error response** MUST include a trace ID for debugging\n+3. **All error types** MUST be registered in the types registry\n+4. **Consistent error schema** across all modules following RFC 9457\n+5. **Machine-readable error codes** for programmatic handling\n+6. **Error stack propagation** for nested service calls\n+\n+### Non-Goals\n+\n+- Changing internal domain error types (only API-facing errors)\n+- Modifying logging infrastructure\n+- Changing HTTP status code semantics\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Industry Research\n+\n+### How Major Tech Companies Handle Errors\n+\n+| Company | Standard | Key Features |\n+|---------|----------|--------------|\n+| **Google** | AIP-193 + gRPC Status | `reason` (UPPER_SNAKE_CASE), `domain` (service name), `metadata` (key-value context), `ErrorInfo`, `LocalizedMessage`, `Help` links |\n+| **Amazon AWS** | Custom JSON | `errorType`, `httpStatus`, `requestId`, `message`, custom error object serialization |\n+| **Twitter/X** | JSON with `errors` array | `code` (CAPS_CASE), `message`, `parameter`, `details`, `value` |\n+| **RFC 9457** | Problem Details | `type` (URI), `title`, `status`, `detail`, `instance`, extension members |\n+\n+### Key Patterns Identified\n+\n+1. **Machine-readable identifiers** - Unique codes for programmatic handling (Google's `reason`, Twitter's `code`)\n+2. **Domain/namespace separation** - Identify error source (Google's `domain`, our GTS vendor.package)\n+3. **Structured metadata** - Key-value context without parsing messages (Google's `ErrorInfo.metadata`)\n+4. **Trace/Request IDs** - Correlation for debugging (AWS `requestId`, our `trace_id`)\n+5. **Documentation links** - URIs to error documentation (RFC 9457 `type`, Google's `Help`)\n+6. **Error categorization** - System vs User-defined, Retryable vs Non-retryable\n+\n+### Google AIP-193 ErrorInfo Structure (Reference)\n+\n+```json\n+{\n+  \"error\": {\n+    \"code\": 429,\n+    \"message\": \"The zone 'us-east1-a' does not have enough resources...\",\n+    \"status\": \"RESOURCE_EXHAUSTED\",\n+    \"details\": [\n+      {\n+        \"@type\": \"type.googleapis.com/google.rpc.ErrorInfo\",\n+        \"reason\": \"RESOURCE_AVAILABILITY\",\n+        \"domain\": \"compute.googleapis.com\",\n+        \"metadata\": {\n+          \"zone\": \"us-east1-a\",\n+          \"vmType\": \"e2-medium\"\n+        }\n+      }\n+    ]\n+  }\n+}\n+```\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Current State Analysis\n+\n+### Existing Infrastructure\n+\n+1. **`Problem` struct** (`libs/modkit-errors/src/problem.rs`) - RFC 9457 compliant\n+   - Fields: `type_url`, `title`, `status`, `detail`, `instance`, `code`, `trace_id`, `errors`\n+   - Implements `IntoResponse` for Axum with automatic trace ID enrichment\n+\n+2. **`struct_to_gts_schema` macro** (`modules/types-registry/gts-rust/gts-macros/src/lib.rs`)\n+   - Attribute macro for explicit struct definitions with GTS IDs visible in code\n+   - Generates constants: `GTS_SCHEMA_ID`, `GTS_SCHEMA_JSON`, etc.\n+   - **This pattern will be adapted for error definitions**\n+\n+3. **`declare_errors!` macro** (`libs/modkit-errors-macro/src/lib.rs`) - **TO BE DEPRECATED**\n+   - Generates type-safe error enums from JSON catalogs\n+   - Problem: GTS IDs hidden in external JSON files, not visible to LLMs\n+   - Used by: `users_info` example, `modkit-odata`\n+\n+### Gaps Identified\n+\n+| Gap | Current State | Required State |\n+|-----|---------------|----------------|\n+| **Hidden GTS IDs** | JSON-based `declare_errors!` | Explicit `#[gts_error]` structs with visible GTS IDs |\n+| **Inconsistent definitions** | Some modules use inline errors | All modules use `#[gts_error]` structs |\n+| **No types registry** | Errors not registered | All errors registered as GTS types |\n+| **Missing metadata** | No structured context | Struct fields → `metadata` map |\n+| **Partial trace IDs** | Only in `IntoResponse` | Mandatory in all error responses |\n+| **No error categories** | Flat error codes | System/Operational/Client categories |\n+| **No error stack** | Single error | Upstream error chain propagation |\n+\n+### Current Module Migration Status\n+\n+| Module | Location | Status | Issues |\n+|--------|----------|--------|--------|\n+| **file_parser** | `modules/file_parser/` | 🔴 Not migrated | No GTS IDs, inline `Problem::new()` |\n+| **types-registry** | `modules/system/types-registry/` | 🟡 Partial | Has codes but not GTS format (e.g., `TYPES_REGISTRY_NOT_FOUND`) |\n+| **nodes_registry** | `modules/system/nodes_registry/` | 🔴 Not migrated | Non-GTS codes (e.g., `NODES_NOT_FOUND`) |\n+| **api_gateway** | `modules/system/api_gateway/` | 🔴 Not migrated | No Problem struct, simple error codes |\n+| **tenant_resolver** | `modules/system/tenant_resolver/` | 🔴 Not migrated | No GTS IDs |\n+| **simple-user-settings** | `modules/simple-user-settings/` | 🟡 Partial | Uses `declare_errors!` with old chain format |\n+| **modkit-auth** | `libs/modkit-auth/` | 🔴 Not migrated | No GTS IDs, custom `IntoResponse` |\n+| **modkit-odata** | `libs/modkit-odata/` | 🟡 Partial | Uses `declare_errors!` with old chain format |\n+| **users_info** (example) | `examples/modkit/users_info/` | 🟡 Partial | Uses `declare_errors!` with old chain format |\n+\n+#### Legend\n+- 🟢 **Migrated** - Uses `#[gts_error]` structs with proper base types\n+- 🟡 **Partial** - Has GTS IDs but uses deprecated `declare_errors!` or old format\n+- 🔴 **Not migrated** - No GTS IDs or non-GTS format codes\n+\n+#### GTS ID Format Note\n+\n+**Old chain format** (used by `declare_errors!`):\n+```\n+gts.hx.core.errors.err.v1~hx.module.error_name.v1\n+```\n+\n+**New format** (with `base` field):\n+```\n+gts.hx.module.namespace.error_name.v1~\n+```\n+The `base` field in `#[gts_error]` replaces the chain suffix, making inheritance explicit in code.\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Requirements\n+\n+### R1: Error Schema Requirements\n+\n+Every error returned from REST API MUST conform to the unified schema:\n+\n+```rust\n+pub struct Problem {\n+    // =========================================================================\n+    // REQUIRED FIELDS - Core error identification\n+    // =========================================================================\n+    \n+    /// URI reference identifying the problem type (GTS-based)\n+    /// Example: \"https://docs.hyperspot.com/errors/types_registry_entity_not_found_v1\"\n+    #[serde(rename = \"type\")]\n+    pub type_url: String,\n+    \n+    /// Human-readable summary of the problem type (static per error type)\n+    pub title: String,\n+    \n+    /// GTS error code (machine-readable identifier)\n+    pub code: String,\n+    \n+    /// Trace ID for request correlation\n+    pub trace_id: String,\n+    \n+    // =========================================================================\n+    // CONTEXTUAL FIELDS - Optional based on error context\n+    // =========================================================================\n+    \n+    /// HTTP status code. Optional because:\n+    /// - gRPC errors use different status codes\n+    /// - Internal/domain errors may not have HTTP context\n+    /// - Event-driven systems have no request/response\n+    /// When serializing for HTTP response, this is populated from error definition.\n+    #[serde(skip_serializing_if = \"Option::is_none\")]\n+    pub status: Option<u16>,\n+    \n+    /// Human-readable explanation specific to this occurrence.\n+    /// Optional - title may be sufficient for simple errors.\n+    #[serde(skip_serializing_if = \"Option::is_none\")]\n+    pub detail: Option<String>,\n+    \n+    /// Error category for client handling.\n+    /// Optional - can be inferred from base type hierarchy.\n+    #[serde(skip_serializing_if = \"Option::is_none\")]\n+    pub category: Option<ErrorCategory>,\n+    \n+    /// Whether client can retry this request.\n+    /// Optional - can be inferred from base type; not relevant for all contexts.\n+    #[serde(skip_serializing_if = \"Option::is_none\")]\n+    pub retryable: Option<bool>,\n+    \n+    /// URI identifying this specific occurrence (auto-populated from request path)\n+    #[serde(skip_serializing_if = \"Option::is_none\")]\n+    pub instance: Option<String>,\n+    \n+    /// Structured metadata (key-value context)\n+    #[serde(skip_serializing_if = \"Option::is_none\")]\n+    pub metadata: Option<HashMap<String, String>>,\n+    \n+    /// Validation errors for 4xx responses\n+    #[serde(skip_serializing_if = \"Option::is_none\")]\n+    pub errors: Option<Vec<ValidationViolation>>,\n+    \n+    /// Upstream error chain (when error_stack enabled)\n+    #[serde(skip_serializing_if = \"Option::is_none\")]\n+    pub upstream_errors: Option<Vec<UpstreamError>>,\n+}\n+\n+pub enum ErrorCategory {\n+    /// Platform-level execution errors (panics, OOM, internal bugs)\n+    System,\n+    /// Infrastructure/operational issues (DB unavailable, service down, rate limits)\n+    Operational,\n+    /// Client input/request errors (validation, not found, unauthorized)\n+    Client,\n+}\n+```\n+\n+#### Field Requirements Summary\n+\n+| Field | Required | Reason |\n+|-------|----------|--------|\n+| `type_url` | ✅ Yes | RFC 9457 requires problem type URI |\n+| `title` | ✅ Yes | Human-readable error name (static per type) |\n+| `code` | ✅ Yes | GTS identifier for machine processing |\n+| `trace_id` | ✅ Yes | Request correlation for debugging |\n+| `status` | ❌ No | Only relevant for HTTP; gRPC/events/domain errors don't need it |\n+| `detail` | ❌ No | Instance-specific message; title may suffice |\n+| `category` | ❌ No | Inherited from base type hierarchy |\n+| `retryable` | ❌ No | Inherited from base type; not relevant for all contexts |\n+| `instance` | ❌ No | Auto-populated from request path when applicable |\n+| `metadata` | ❌ No | Additional context key-value pairs |\n+| `errors` | ❌ No | Validation violations for 4xx errors |\n+| `upstream_errors` | ❌ No | Error chain from upstream services |\n+\n+**Note:** When converting to HTTP response, `status` is populated from the error definition. When the error is used in non-HTTP contexts (gRPC, domain logic, events), `status` remains `None`.\n+\n+### R2: GTS Identifier and Base Type Requirements\n+\n+Every error MUST have a valid GTS identifier and specify its base type using the `base` field.\n+\n+#### GTS ID Format\n+\n+```\n+gts.<vendor>.<package>.<namespace>.<type>.v<version>~\n+```\n+\n+**Examples:**\n+- `gts.hx.types_registry.entity.not_found.v1~` - Types registry not found error\n+- `gts.hx.file_parser.validation.invalid_format.v1~` - File parser validation error\n+- `gts.hx.system.runtime.timeout.v1~` - System timeout error\n+\n+#### Base Type Chaining\n+\n+Errors form an inheritance chain using the `base` field. The `base` field references another error struct type (not a string literal), similar to how `struct_to_gts_schema` works.\n+\n+The root base error type is:\n+\n+```rust\n+/// Root error type for all GTS errors.\n+#[gts_error(\n+    gts_id = \"gts.hx.core.errors.err.v1~\",\n+    base = true,  // Marks this as a root base type (no parent)\n+    title = \"Error\",\n+    // Optional attributes with defaults for inheritance:\n+    status = 500,        // Default HTTP status (optional, inherited by children)\n+    category = \"System\", // Default category (optional, inherited by children)\n+    retryable = false    // Default retryable (optional, inherited by children)\n+)]\n+pub struct BaseError;\n+```\n+\n+All module-specific errors MUST reference their base type as a struct (extending the appropriate logical/system error):\n+\n+```rust\n+use modkit_errors::system::logical::NotFoundError;\n+\n+/// Entity was not found in the types registry.\n+/// Note: status, category, retryable are inherited from NotFoundError if not specified.\n+#[gts_error(\n+    gts_id = \"gts.hx.types_registry.entity.not_found.v1~\",\n+    base = NotFoundError,  // Extends logical.not_found, not BaseError\n+    title = \"Entity Not Found\",\n+    // These are optional - inherited from base if omitted:\n+    // status = 404,      // Inherited from NotFoundError\n+    // category = \"Client\", // Inherited from NotFoundError  \n+    // retryable = false,   // Inherited from NotFoundError\n+)]\n+pub struct EntityNotFoundError {\n+    pub gts_id: String,\n+}\n+```\n+\n+#### Multi-Level Inheritance\n+\n+Errors can form deeper inheritance chains:\n+\n+```rust\n+/// Logical not found error (platform-level).\n+#[gts_error(\n+    gts_id = \"gts.hx.system.logical.not_found.v1~\",\n+    base = BaseError,  // Platform errors extend BaseError\n+    status = 404,\n+    title = \"Not Found\",\n+    category = \"Client\",\n+    retryable = false\n+)]\n+pub struct NotFoundError;\n+\n+/// Types registry entity not found (module-level).\n+#[gts_error(\n+    gts_id = \"gts.hx.types_registry.entity.not_found.v1~\",\n+    base = NotFoundError,  // Module errors extend logical errors\n+    status = 404,\n+    title = \"Entity Not Found\",\n+    category = \"Client\",\n+    retryable = false\n+)]\n+pub struct EntityNotFoundError {\n+    pub gts_id: String,\n+}\n+```\n+\n+#### Inheritance Hierarchy\n+\n+```\n+BaseError (gts.hx.core.errors.err.v1~)                              [base = true]\n+├── Transport Errors (hx.system.transport.*)                        [base = BaseError]\n+├── Runtime Errors (hx.system.runtime.*)                            [base = BaseError]\n+│   └── hx.types_registry.system.internal.v1~                       [base = runtime.internal]\n+├── HTTP Errors (hx.system.http.*)                                  [base = BaseError]\n+│   └── hx.auth.token_expired.v1~                                   [base = http.unauthorized]\n+├── gRPC Errors (hx.system.grpc.*)                                  [base = BaseError]\n+└── Logical Errors (hx.system.logical.*)                            [base = BaseError]\n+    ├── logical.not_found.v1~                                       [base = BaseError]\n+    │   ├── hx.types_registry.entity.not_found.v1~                  [base = logical.not_found]\n+    │   └── hx.db.entity.not_found.v1~                              [base = logical.not_found]\n+    ├── logical.already_exists.v1~                                  [base = BaseError]\n+    │   └── hx.types_registry.entity.already_exists.v1~             [base = logical.already_exists]\n+    └── logical.validation_failed.v1~                               [base = BaseError]\n+        └── hx.file_parser.validation.invalid_format.v1~            [base = logical.validation_failed]\n+```\n+\n+### R3: Trace ID Requirements\n+\n+- Every error response MUST include a non-empty `trace_id`\n+- Trace ID MUST be propagated from incoming request headers or generated\n+- Trace ID MUST be logged with the error for correlation\n+\n+### R4: Types Registry Integration\n+\n+- All error types MUST be registered in the types registry at startup\n+- Error schema MUST extend base error type: `gts.hx.core.errors.err.v1`\n+- Registration MUST include: code, title, status, category, retryable flag\n+\n+### R5: Standardized System Error Types\n+\n+See [GTS System Errors Catalog](#gts-system-errors-catalog) for the complete list of all system errors.\n+\n+### R6: Error Stack Propagation\n+\n+When a function calls another service/function that returns an error:\n+- The error SHOULD be wrapped with context\n+- `upstream_errors` array SHOULD contain the chain of errors\n+- Each upstream error includes: `code`, `title`, `detail`, `source`\n+- Propagation controlled by `error_stack` configuration flag\n+\n+---\n+\n+## GTS Error Code Format\n+\n+### Structure\n+\n+```\n+gts.<vendor>.<package>.<namespace>.<type>.<version>~<chain>\n+```\n+\n+### Components\n+\n+| Component | Description | Example |\n+|-----------|-------------|---------|\n+| `gts` | Global Type System prefix | `gts` |\n+| `vendor` | Organization identifier | `hx` (Hyperspot) |\n+| `package` | Module/service name | `types_registry`, `file_parser` |\n+| `namespace` | Error category | `entity`, `validation`, `runtime` |\n+| `type` | Specific error type | `not_found`, `invalid_format` |\n+| `version` | Schema version | `v1`, `v1.0` |\n+| `~chain` | Base type chain | `~hx.core.errors.err.v1` |\n+\n+### Validation Rules\n+\n+1. MUST start with `gts.`\n+2. All segments MUST be lowercase alphanumeric or underscore\n+3. No empty segments allowed\n+4. Final segment MUST be version format (`vN` or `vN.M`)\n+5. MUST chain from base error type\n+\n+### Short Name Derivation\n+\n+Short accessor names derived from final GTX segment:\n+```\n+gts.hx.core.errors.err.v1~hx.types_registry.entity.not_found.v1\n+                         └─────────────────────────────────────┘\n+                                          ↓\n+                         types_registry_entity_not_found_v1()\n+```\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Types Registry Integration\n+\n+### Error Type Schema\n+\n+```json\n+{\n+  \"gts_id\": \"gts.hx.types_registry.entity.not_found.v1~\",\n+  \"kind\": \"error\",\n+  \"schema\": {\n+    \"type\": \"object\",\n+    \"extends\": \"gts.hx.system.logical.not_found.v1~\",\n+    \"properties\": {\n+      \"status\": { \"const\": 404 },\n+      \"title\": { \"const\": \"Entity Not Found\" },\n+      \"category\": { \"const\": \"Client\" },\n+      \"retryable\": { \"const\": false }\n+    }\n+  },\n+  \"metadata\": {\n+    \"module\": \"types-registry\",\n+    \"documentation_url\": \"https://docs.hyperspot.com/errors/types_registry_entity_not_found_v1\"\n+  }\n+}\n+```\n+\n+### Registration Flow\n+\n+1. Module defines errors as explicit structs with `#[gts_error]` attribute in `src/errors.rs`\n+2. Each struct generates `ERROR_DEF` constant with GTS metadata\n+3. Module implements `all_error_definitions()` function returning all error definitions\n+4. At module startup (`on_ready`), errors are registered with types registry:\n+   ```rust\n+   impl Module for MyModule {\n+       async fn on_ready(&self, ctx: &ModuleContext) -> Result<()> {\n+           // Register all error types with types registry\n+           let errors = crate::errors::all_error_definitions();\n+           ctx.types_registry().register_errors(errors).await?;\n+           Ok(())\n+       }\n+   }\n+   ```\n+5. Types registry validates GTS format and schema compliance\n+6. Errors become discoverable via types registry API\n+\n+### API for Error Discovery\n+\n+```http\n+GET /api/types-registry/v1/types?kind=error&module=types-registry\n+\n+Response:\n+{\n+  \"items\": [\n+    {\n+      \"gts_id\": \"gts.hx.core.errors.err.v1~hx.types_registry.entity.not_found.v1\",","path":"intended_design/UNIFIED_ERROR_SYSTEM.md","commit_id":"5bdb0f43b25858af78999718f7247813802b9634","original_commit_id":"5bdb0f43b25858af78999718f7247813802b9634","user":{"login":"alizid10","id":247960800,"node_id":"U_kgDODseU4A","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/247960800?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/alizid10","html_url":"https://github.com/alizid10","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alizid10/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alizid10/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alizid10/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alizid10/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alizid10/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alizid10/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alizid10/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alizid10/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alizid10/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"fixed","created_at":"2026-02-06T15:59:42Z","updated_at":"2026-02-06T15:59:43Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/290#discussion_r2774846409","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/290","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2774846409"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/290#discussion_r2774846409"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/290"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2774846409/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":null,"original_line":484,"side":"RIGHT","in_reply_to_id":2748012376,"author_association":"MEMBER","original_position":484,"position":1,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2774847197","pull_request_review_id":3763869295,"id":2774847197,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs6lZM7d","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,1574 @@\n+# Unified Error System - Intention Document\n+\n+This document defines the architecture, rules, and implementation plan for a unified error handling system across the Hyperspot project. All REST API errors MUST have a GTS identifier, trace ID, and be registered in the types registry.\n+\n+## Table of Contents\n+\n+1. [Executive Summary](#executive-summary)\n+2. [Industry Research](#industry-research)\n+3. [Current State Analysis](#current-state-analysis)\n+4. [Requirements](#requirements)\n+5. [Implementation Rules](#implementation-rules)\n+6. [Migration Plan](#migration-plan)\n+7. [Examples](#examples)\n+8. [HTTP Headers](#http-headers)\n+9. [Security Considerations](#security-considerations)\n+10. [Appendix A: Error Category Definitions](#appendix-a-error-category-definitions)\n+11. [Appendix B: Retryable Error Guidelines](#appendix-b-retryable-error-guidelines)\n+12. [GTS System Errors Catalog](#gts-system-errors-catalog)\n+13. [References](#references)\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Executive Summary\n+\n+### Problem Statement\n+\n+The current error handling across Hyperspot modules is inconsistent:\n+- Some modules use `declare_errors!` macro with JSON catalogs\n+- Others define errors inline without GTS codes\n+- Errors are not registered in the types registry\n+- No standardized metadata/context fields\n+- Inconsistent trace ID propagation\n+\n+### Goals\n+\n+1. **Every REST API error** MUST have a valid GTS identifier\n+2. **Every error response** MUST include a trace ID for debugging\n+3. **All error types** MUST be registered in the types registry\n+4. **Consistent error schema** across all modules following RFC 9457\n+5. **Machine-readable error codes** for programmatic handling\n+6. **Error stack propagation** for nested service calls\n+\n+### Non-Goals\n+\n+- Changing internal domain error types (only API-facing errors)\n+- Modifying logging infrastructure\n+- Changing HTTP status code semantics\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Industry Research\n+\n+### How Major Tech Companies Handle Errors\n+\n+| Company | Standard | Key Features |\n+|---------|----------|--------------|\n+| **Google** | AIP-193 + gRPC Status | `reason` (UPPER_SNAKE_CASE), `domain` (service name), `metadata` (key-value context), `ErrorInfo`, `LocalizedMessage`, `Help` links |\n+| **Amazon AWS** | Custom JSON | `errorType`, `httpStatus`, `requestId`, `message`, custom error object serialization |\n+| **Twitter/X** | JSON with `errors` array | `code` (CAPS_CASE), `message`, `parameter`, `details`, `value` |\n+| **RFC 9457** | Problem Details | `type` (URI), `title`, `status`, `detail`, `instance`, extension members |\n+\n+### Key Patterns Identified\n+\n+1. **Machine-readable identifiers** - Unique codes for programmatic handling (Google's `reason`, Twitter's `code`)\n+2. **Domain/namespace separation** - Identify error source (Google's `domain`, our GTS vendor.package)\n+3. **Structured metadata** - Key-value context without parsing messages (Google's `ErrorInfo.metadata`)\n+4. **Trace/Request IDs** - Correlation for debugging (AWS `requestId`, our `trace_id`)\n+5. **Documentation links** - URIs to error documentation (RFC 9457 `type`, Google's `Help`)\n+6. **Error categorization** - System vs User-defined, Retryable vs Non-retryable\n+\n+### Google AIP-193 ErrorInfo Structure (Reference)\n+\n+```json\n+{\n+  \"error\": {\n+    \"code\": 429,\n+    \"message\": \"The zone 'us-east1-a' does not have enough resources...\",\n+    \"status\": \"RESOURCE_EXHAUSTED\",\n+    \"details\": [\n+      {\n+        \"@type\": \"type.googleapis.com/google.rpc.ErrorInfo\",\n+        \"reason\": \"RESOURCE_AVAILABILITY\",\n+        \"domain\": \"compute.googleapis.com\",\n+        \"metadata\": {\n+          \"zone\": \"us-east1-a\",\n+          \"vmType\": \"e2-medium\"\n+        }\n+      }\n+    ]\n+  }\n+}\n+```\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Current State Analysis\n+\n+### Existing Infrastructure\n+\n+1. **`Problem` struct** (`libs/modkit-errors/src/problem.rs`) - RFC 9457 compliant\n+   - Fields: `type_url`, `title`, `status`, `detail`, `instance`, `code`, `trace_id`, `errors`\n+   - Implements `IntoResponse` for Axum with automatic trace ID enrichment\n+\n+2. **`struct_to_gts_schema` macro** (`modules/types-registry/gts-rust/gts-macros/src/lib.rs`)\n+   - Attribute macro for explicit struct definitions with GTS IDs visible in code\n+   - Generates constants: `GTS_SCHEMA_ID`, `GTS_SCHEMA_JSON`, etc.\n+   - **This pattern will be adapted for error definitions**\n+\n+3. **`declare_errors!` macro** (`libs/modkit-errors-macro/src/lib.rs`) - **TO BE DEPRECATED**\n+   - Generates type-safe error enums from JSON catalogs\n+   - Problem: GTS IDs hidden in external JSON files, not visible to LLMs\n+   - Used by: `users_info` example, `modkit-odata`\n+\n+### Gaps Identified\n+\n+| Gap | Current State | Required State |\n+|-----|---------------|----------------|\n+| **Hidden GTS IDs** | JSON-based `declare_errors!` | Explicit `#[gts_error]` structs with visible GTS IDs |\n+| **Inconsistent definitions** | Some modules use inline errors | All modules use `#[gts_error]` structs |\n+| **No types registry** | Errors not registered | All errors registered as GTS types |\n+| **Missing metadata** | No structured context | Struct fields → `metadata` map |\n+| **Partial trace IDs** | Only in `IntoResponse` | Mandatory in all error responses |\n+| **No error categories** | Flat error codes | System/Operational/Client categories |\n+| **No error stack** | Single error | Upstream error chain propagation |\n+\n+### Current Module Migration Status\n+\n+| Module | Location | Status | Issues |\n+|--------|----------|--------|--------|\n+| **file_parser** | `modules/file_parser/` | 🔴 Not migrated | No GTS IDs, inline `Problem::new()` |\n+| **types-registry** | `modules/system/types-registry/` | 🟡 Partial | Has codes but not GTS format (e.g., `TYPES_REGISTRY_NOT_FOUND`) |\n+| **nodes_registry** | `modules/system/nodes_registry/` | 🔴 Not migrated | Non-GTS codes (e.g., `NODES_NOT_FOUND`) |\n+| **api_gateway** | `modules/system/api_gateway/` | 🔴 Not migrated | No Problem struct, simple error codes |\n+| **tenant_resolver** | `modules/system/tenant_resolver/` | 🔴 Not migrated | No GTS IDs |\n+| **simple-user-settings** | `modules/simple-user-settings/` | 🟡 Partial | Uses `declare_errors!` with old chain format |\n+| **modkit-auth** | `libs/modkit-auth/` | 🔴 Not migrated | No GTS IDs, custom `IntoResponse` |\n+| **modkit-odata** | `libs/modkit-odata/` | 🟡 Partial | Uses `declare_errors!` with old chain format |\n+| **users_info** (example) | `examples/modkit/users_info/` | 🟡 Partial | Uses `declare_errors!` with old chain format |\n+\n+#### Legend\n+- 🟢 **Migrated** - Uses `#[gts_error]` structs with proper base types\n+- 🟡 **Partial** - Has GTS IDs but uses deprecated `declare_errors!` or old format\n+- 🔴 **Not migrated** - No GTS IDs or non-GTS format codes\n+\n+#### GTS ID Format Note\n+\n+**Old chain format** (used by `declare_errors!`):\n+```\n+gts.hx.core.errors.err.v1~hx.module.error_name.v1\n+```\n+\n+**New format** (with `base` field):\n+```\n+gts.hx.module.namespace.error_name.v1~\n+```\n+The `base` field in `#[gts_error]` replaces the chain suffix, making inheritance explicit in code.\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Requirements\n+\n+### R1: Error Schema Requirements\n+\n+Every error returned from REST API MUST conform to the unified schema:\n+\n+```rust\n+pub struct Problem {\n+    // =========================================================================\n+    // REQUIRED FIELDS - Core error identification\n+    // =========================================================================\n+    \n+    /// URI reference identifying the problem type (GTS-based)\n+    /// Example: \"https://docs.hyperspot.com/errors/types_registry_entity_not_found_v1\"\n+    #[serde(rename = \"type\")]\n+    pub type_url: String,\n+    \n+    /// Human-readable summary of the problem type (static per error type)\n+    pub title: String,\n+    \n+    /// GTS error code (machine-readable identifier)\n+    pub code: String,\n+    \n+    /// Trace ID for request correlation\n+    pub trace_id: String,\n+    \n+    // =========================================================================\n+    // CONTEXTUAL FIELDS - Optional based on error context\n+    // =========================================================================\n+    \n+    /// HTTP status code. Optional because:\n+    /// - gRPC errors use different status codes\n+    /// - Internal/domain errors may not have HTTP context\n+    /// - Event-driven systems have no request/response\n+    /// When serializing for HTTP response, this is populated from error definition.\n+    #[serde(skip_serializing_if = \"Option::is_none\")]\n+    pub status: Option<u16>,\n+    \n+    /// Human-readable explanation specific to this occurrence.\n+    /// Optional - title may be sufficient for simple errors.\n+    #[serde(skip_serializing_if = \"Option::is_none\")]\n+    pub detail: Option<String>,\n+    \n+    /// Error category for client handling.\n+    /// Optional - can be inferred from base type hierarchy.\n+    #[serde(skip_serializing_if = \"Option::is_none\")]\n+    pub category: Option<ErrorCategory>,\n+    \n+    /// Whether client can retry this request.\n+    /// Optional - can be inferred from base type; not relevant for all contexts.\n+    #[serde(skip_serializing_if = \"Option::is_none\")]\n+    pub retryable: Option<bool>,\n+    \n+    /// URI identifying this specific occurrence (auto-populated from request path)\n+    #[serde(skip_serializing_if = \"Option::is_none\")]\n+    pub instance: Option<String>,\n+    \n+    /// Structured metadata (key-value context)\n+    #[serde(skip_serializing_if = \"Option::is_none\")]\n+    pub metadata: Option<HashMap<String, String>>,\n+    \n+    /// Validation errors for 4xx responses\n+    #[serde(skip_serializing_if = \"Option::is_none\")]\n+    pub errors: Option<Vec<ValidationViolation>>,\n+    \n+    /// Upstream error chain (when error_stack enabled)\n+    #[serde(skip_serializing_if = \"Option::is_none\")]\n+    pub upstream_errors: Option<Vec<UpstreamError>>,\n+}\n+\n+pub enum ErrorCategory {\n+    /// Platform-level execution errors (panics, OOM, internal bugs)\n+    System,\n+    /// Infrastructure/operational issues (DB unavailable, service down, rate limits)\n+    Operational,\n+    /// Client input/request errors (validation, not found, unauthorized)\n+    Client,\n+}\n+```\n+\n+#### Field Requirements Summary\n+\n+| Field | Required | Reason |\n+|-------|----------|--------|\n+| `type_url` | ✅ Yes | RFC 9457 requires problem type URI |\n+| `title` | ✅ Yes | Human-readable error name (static per type) |\n+| `code` | ✅ Yes | GTS identifier for machine processing |\n+| `trace_id` | ✅ Yes | Request correlation for debugging |\n+| `status` | ❌ No | Only relevant for HTTP; gRPC/events/domain errors don't need it |\n+| `detail` | ❌ No | Instance-specific message; title may suffice |\n+| `category` | ❌ No | Inherited from base type hierarchy |\n+| `retryable` | ❌ No | Inherited from base type; not relevant for all contexts |\n+| `instance` | ❌ No | Auto-populated from request path when applicable |\n+| `metadata` | ❌ No | Additional context key-value pairs |\n+| `errors` | ❌ No | Validation violations for 4xx errors |\n+| `upstream_errors` | ❌ No | Error chain from upstream services |\n+\n+**Note:** When converting to HTTP response, `status` is populated from the error definition. When the error is used in non-HTTP contexts (gRPC, domain logic, events), `status` remains `None`.\n+\n+### R2: GTS Identifier and Base Type Requirements\n+\n+Every error MUST have a valid GTS identifier and specify its base type using the `base` field.\n+\n+#### GTS ID Format\n+\n+```\n+gts.<vendor>.<package>.<namespace>.<type>.v<version>~\n+```\n+\n+**Examples:**\n+- `gts.hx.types_registry.entity.not_found.v1~` - Types registry not found error\n+- `gts.hx.file_parser.validation.invalid_format.v1~` - File parser validation error\n+- `gts.hx.system.runtime.timeout.v1~` - System timeout error\n+\n+#### Base Type Chaining\n+\n+Errors form an inheritance chain using the `base` field. The `base` field references another error struct type (not a string literal), similar to how `struct_to_gts_schema` works.\n+\n+The root base error type is:\n+\n+```rust\n+/// Root error type for all GTS errors.\n+#[gts_error(\n+    gts_id = \"gts.hx.core.errors.err.v1~\",\n+    base = true,  // Marks this as a root base type (no parent)\n+    title = \"Error\",\n+    // Optional attributes with defaults for inheritance:\n+    status = 500,        // Default HTTP status (optional, inherited by children)\n+    category = \"System\", // Default category (optional, inherited by children)\n+    retryable = false    // Default retryable (optional, inherited by children)\n+)]\n+pub struct BaseError;\n+```\n+\n+All module-specific errors MUST reference their base type as a struct (extending the appropriate logical/system error):\n+\n+```rust\n+use modkit_errors::system::logical::NotFoundError;\n+\n+/// Entity was not found in the types registry.\n+/// Note: status, category, retryable are inherited from NotFoundError if not specified.\n+#[gts_error(\n+    gts_id = \"gts.hx.types_registry.entity.not_found.v1~\",\n+    base = NotFoundError,  // Extends logical.not_found, not BaseError\n+    title = \"Entity Not Found\",\n+    // These are optional - inherited from base if omitted:\n+    // status = 404,      // Inherited from NotFoundError\n+    // category = \"Client\", // Inherited from NotFoundError  \n+    // retryable = false,   // Inherited from NotFoundError\n+)]\n+pub struct EntityNotFoundError {\n+    pub gts_id: String,\n+}\n+```\n+\n+#### Multi-Level Inheritance\n+\n+Errors can form deeper inheritance chains:\n+\n+```rust\n+/// Logical not found error (platform-level).\n+#[gts_error(\n+    gts_id = \"gts.hx.system.logical.not_found.v1~\",\n+    base = BaseError,  // Platform errors extend BaseError\n+    status = 404,\n+    title = \"Not Found\",\n+    category = \"Client\",\n+    retryable = false\n+)]\n+pub struct NotFoundError;\n+\n+/// Types registry entity not found (module-level).\n+#[gts_error(\n+    gts_id = \"gts.hx.types_registry.entity.not_found.v1~\",\n+    base = NotFoundError,  // Module errors extend logical errors\n+    status = 404,\n+    title = \"Entity Not Found\",\n+    category = \"Client\",\n+    retryable = false\n+)]\n+pub struct EntityNotFoundError {\n+    pub gts_id: String,\n+}\n+```\n+\n+#### Inheritance Hierarchy\n+\n+```\n+BaseError (gts.hx.core.errors.err.v1~)                              [base = true]\n+├── Transport Errors (hx.system.transport.*)                        [base = BaseError]\n+├── Runtime Errors (hx.system.runtime.*)                            [base = BaseError]\n+│   └── hx.types_registry.system.internal.v1~                       [base = runtime.internal]\n+├── HTTP Errors (hx.system.http.*)                                  [base = BaseError]\n+│   └── hx.auth.token_expired.v1~                                   [base = http.unauthorized]\n+├── gRPC Errors (hx.system.grpc.*)                                  [base = BaseError]\n+└── Logical Errors (hx.system.logical.*)                            [base = BaseError]\n+    ├── logical.not_found.v1~                                       [base = BaseError]\n+    │   ├── hx.types_registry.entity.not_found.v1~                  [base = logical.not_found]\n+    │   └── hx.db.entity.not_found.v1~                              [base = logical.not_found]\n+    ├── logical.already_exists.v1~                                  [base = BaseError]\n+    │   └── hx.types_registry.entity.already_exists.v1~             [base = logical.already_exists]\n+    └── logical.validation_failed.v1~                               [base = BaseError]\n+        └── hx.file_parser.validation.invalid_format.v1~            [base = logical.validation_failed]\n+```\n+\n+### R3: Trace ID Requirements\n+\n+- Every error response MUST include a non-empty `trace_id`\n+- Trace ID MUST be propagated from incoming request headers or generated\n+- Trace ID MUST be logged with the error for correlation\n+\n+### R4: Types Registry Integration\n+\n+- All error types MUST be registered in the types registry at startup\n+- Error schema MUST extend base error type: `gts.hx.core.errors.err.v1`\n+- Registration MUST include: code, title, status, category, retryable flag\n+\n+### R5: Standardized System Error Types\n+\n+See [GTS System Errors Catalog](#gts-system-errors-catalog) for the complete list of all system errors.\n+\n+### R6: Error Stack Propagation\n+\n+When a function calls another service/function that returns an error:\n+- The error SHOULD be wrapped with context\n+- `upstream_errors` array SHOULD contain the chain of errors\n+- Each upstream error includes: `code`, `title`, `detail`, `source`\n+- Propagation controlled by `error_stack` configuration flag\n+\n+---\n+\n+## GTS Error Code Format\n+\n+### Structure\n+\n+```\n+gts.<vendor>.<package>.<namespace>.<type>.<version>~<chain>\n+```\n+\n+### Components\n+\n+| Component | Description | Example |\n+|-----------|-------------|---------|\n+| `gts` | Global Type System prefix | `gts` |\n+| `vendor` | Organization identifier | `hx` (Hyperspot) |\n+| `package` | Module/service name | `types_registry`, `file_parser` |\n+| `namespace` | Error category | `entity`, `validation`, `runtime` |\n+| `type` | Specific error type | `not_found`, `invalid_format` |\n+| `version` | Schema version | `v1`, `v1.0` |\n+| `~chain` | Base type chain | `~hx.core.errors.err.v1` |\n+\n+### Validation Rules\n+\n+1. MUST start with `gts.`\n+2. All segments MUST be lowercase alphanumeric or underscore\n+3. No empty segments allowed\n+4. Final segment MUST be version format (`vN` or `vN.M`)\n+5. MUST chain from base error type\n+\n+### Short Name Derivation\n+\n+Short accessor names derived from final GTX segment:\n+```\n+gts.hx.core.errors.err.v1~hx.types_registry.entity.not_found.v1\n+                         └─────────────────────────────────────┘\n+                                          ↓\n+                         types_registry_entity_not_found_v1()\n+```\n+\n+---\n+","path":"intended_design/UNIFIED_ERROR_SYSTEM.md","commit_id":"5bdb0f43b25858af78999718f7247813802b9634","original_commit_id":"5bdb0f43b25858af78999718f7247813802b9634","user":{"login":"alizid10","id":247960800,"node_id":"U_kgDODseU4A","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/247960800?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/alizid10","html_url":"https://github.com/alizid10","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alizid10/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alizid10/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alizid10/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alizid10/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alizid10/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alizid10/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alizid10/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alizid10/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alizid10/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"fixed","created_at":"2026-02-06T15:59:53Z","updated_at":"2026-02-06T15:59:53Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/290#discussion_r2774847197","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/290","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2774847197"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/290#discussion_r2774847197"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/290"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2774847197/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":null,"original_line":430,"side":"RIGHT","in_reply_to_id":2748002365,"author_association":"MEMBER","original_position":430,"position":1,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2774848166","pull_request_review_id":3763870248,"id":2774848166,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs6lZNKm","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,1574 @@\n+# Unified Error System - Intention Document\n+\n+This document defines the architecture, rules, and implementation plan for a unified error handling system across the Hyperspot project. All REST API errors MUST have a GTS identifier, trace ID, and be registered in the types registry.\n+\n+## Table of Contents\n+\n+1. [Executive Summary](#executive-summary)\n+2. [Industry Research](#industry-research)\n+3. [Current State Analysis](#current-state-analysis)\n+4. [Requirements](#requirements)\n+5. [Implementation Rules](#implementation-rules)\n+6. [Migration Plan](#migration-plan)\n+7. [Examples](#examples)\n+8. [HTTP Headers](#http-headers)\n+9. [Security Considerations](#security-considerations)\n+10. [Appendix A: Error Category Definitions](#appendix-a-error-category-definitions)\n+11. [Appendix B: Retryable Error Guidelines](#appendix-b-retryable-error-guidelines)\n+12. [GTS System Errors Catalog](#gts-system-errors-catalog)\n+13. [References](#references)\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Executive Summary\n+\n+### Problem Statement\n+\n+The current error handling across Hyperspot modules is inconsistent:\n+- Some modules use `declare_errors!` macro with JSON catalogs\n+- Others define errors inline without GTS codes\n+- Errors are not registered in the types registry\n+- No standardized metadata/context fields\n+- Inconsistent trace ID propagation\n+\n+### Goals\n+\n+1. **Every REST API error** MUST have a valid GTS identifier\n+2. **Every error response** MUST include a trace ID for debugging\n+3. **All error types** MUST be registered in the types registry\n+4. **Consistent error schema** across all modules following RFC 9457\n+5. **Machine-readable error codes** for programmatic handling\n+6. **Error stack propagation** for nested service calls\n+\n+### Non-Goals\n+\n+- Changing internal domain error types (only API-facing errors)\n+- Modifying logging infrastructure\n+- Changing HTTP status code semantics\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Industry Research\n+\n+### How Major Tech Companies Handle Errors\n+\n+| Company | Standard | Key Features |\n+|---------|----------|--------------|\n+| **Google** | AIP-193 + gRPC Status | `reason` (UPPER_SNAKE_CASE), `domain` (service name), `metadata` (key-value context), `ErrorInfo`, `LocalizedMessage`, `Help` links |\n+| **Amazon AWS** | Custom JSON | `errorType`, `httpStatus`, `requestId`, `message`, custom error object serialization |\n+| **Twitter/X** | JSON with `errors` array | `code` (CAPS_CASE), `message`, `parameter`, `details`, `value` |\n+| **RFC 9457** | Problem Details | `type` (URI), `title`, `status`, `detail`, `instance`, extension members |\n+\n+### Key Patterns Identified\n+\n+1. **Machine-readable identifiers** - Unique codes for programmatic handling (Google's `reason`, Twitter's `code`)\n+2. **Domain/namespace separation** - Identify error source (Google's `domain`, our GTS vendor.package)\n+3. **Structured metadata** - Key-value context without parsing messages (Google's `ErrorInfo.metadata`)\n+4. **Trace/Request IDs** - Correlation for debugging (AWS `requestId`, our `trace_id`)\n+5. **Documentation links** - URIs to error documentation (RFC 9457 `type`, Google's `Help`)\n+6. **Error categorization** - System vs User-defined, Retryable vs Non-retryable\n+\n+### Google AIP-193 ErrorInfo Structure (Reference)\n+\n+```json\n+{\n+  \"error\": {\n+    \"code\": 429,\n+    \"message\": \"The zone 'us-east1-a' does not have enough resources...\",\n+    \"status\": \"RESOURCE_EXHAUSTED\",\n+    \"details\": [\n+      {\n+        \"@type\": \"type.googleapis.com/google.rpc.ErrorInfo\",\n+        \"reason\": \"RESOURCE_AVAILABILITY\",\n+        \"domain\": \"compute.googleapis.com\",\n+        \"metadata\": {\n+          \"zone\": \"us-east1-a\",\n+          \"vmType\": \"e2-medium\"\n+        }\n+      }\n+    ]\n+  }\n+}\n+```\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Current State Analysis\n+\n+### Existing Infrastructure\n+\n+1. **`Problem` struct** (`libs/modkit-errors/src/problem.rs`) - RFC 9457 compliant\n+   - Fields: `type_url`, `title`, `status`, `detail`, `instance`, `code`, `trace_id`, `errors`\n+   - Implements `IntoResponse` for Axum with automatic trace ID enrichment\n+\n+2. **`struct_to_gts_schema` macro** (`modules/types-registry/gts-rust/gts-macros/src/lib.rs`)\n+   - Attribute macro for explicit struct definitions with GTS IDs visible in code\n+   - Generates constants: `GTS_SCHEMA_ID`, `GTS_SCHEMA_JSON`, etc.\n+   - **This pattern will be adapted for error definitions**\n+\n+3. **`declare_errors!` macro** (`libs/modkit-errors-macro/src/lib.rs`) - **TO BE DEPRECATED**\n+   - Generates type-safe error enums from JSON catalogs\n+   - Problem: GTS IDs hidden in external JSON files, not visible to LLMs\n+   - Used by: `users_info` example, `modkit-odata`\n+\n+### Gaps Identified\n+\n+| Gap | Current State | Required State |\n+|-----|---------------|----------------|\n+| **Hidden GTS IDs** | JSON-based `declare_errors!` | Explicit `#[gts_error]` structs with visible GTS IDs |\n+| **Inconsistent definitions** | Some modules use inline errors | All modules use `#[gts_error]` structs |\n+| **No types registry** | Errors not registered | All errors registered as GTS types |\n+| **Missing metadata** | No structured context | Struct fields → `metadata` map |\n+| **Partial trace IDs** | Only in `IntoResponse` | Mandatory in all error responses |\n+| **No error categories** | Flat error codes | System/Operational/Client categories |\n+| **No error stack** | Single error | Upstream error chain propagation |\n+\n+### Current Module Migration Status\n+\n+| Module | Location | Status | Issues |\n+|--------|----------|--------|--------|\n+| **file_parser** | `modules/file_parser/` | 🔴 Not migrated | No GTS IDs, inline `Problem::new()` |\n+| **types-registry** | `modules/system/types-registry/` | 🟡 Partial | Has codes but not GTS format (e.g., `TYPES_REGISTRY_NOT_FOUND`) |\n+| **nodes_registry** | `modules/system/nodes_registry/` | 🔴 Not migrated | Non-GTS codes (e.g., `NODES_NOT_FOUND`) |\n+| **api_gateway** | `modules/system/api_gateway/` | 🔴 Not migrated | No Problem struct, simple error codes |\n+| **tenant_resolver** | `modules/system/tenant_resolver/` | 🔴 Not migrated | No GTS IDs |\n+| **simple-user-settings** | `modules/simple-user-settings/` | 🟡 Partial | Uses `declare_errors!` with old chain format |\n+| **modkit-auth** | `libs/modkit-auth/` | 🔴 Not migrated | No GTS IDs, custom `IntoResponse` |\n+| **modkit-odata** | `libs/modkit-odata/` | 🟡 Partial | Uses `declare_errors!` with old chain format |\n+| **users_info** (example) | `examples/modkit/users_info/` | 🟡 Partial | Uses `declare_errors!` with old chain format |\n+\n+#### Legend\n+- 🟢 **Migrated** - Uses `#[gts_error]` structs with proper base types\n+- 🟡 **Partial** - Has GTS IDs but uses deprecated `declare_errors!` or old format\n+- 🔴 **Not migrated** - No GTS IDs or non-GTS format codes\n+\n+#### GTS ID Format Note\n+\n+**Old chain format** (used by `declare_errors!`):\n+```\n+gts.hx.core.errors.err.v1~hx.module.error_name.v1\n+```\n+\n+**New format** (with `base` field):\n+```\n+gts.hx.module.namespace.error_name.v1~\n+```\n+The `base` field in `#[gts_error]` replaces the chain suffix, making inheritance explicit in code.\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Requirements\n+\n+### R1: Error Schema Requirements\n+\n+Every error returned from REST API MUST conform to the unified schema:\n+\n+```rust\n+pub struct Problem {\n+    // =========================================================================\n+    // REQUIRED FIELDS - Core error identification\n+    // =========================================================================\n+    \n+    /// URI reference identifying the problem type (GTS-based)\n+    /// Example: \"https://docs.hyperspot.com/errors/types_registry_entity_not_found_v1\"\n+    #[serde(rename = \"type\")]\n+    pub type_url: String,\n+    \n+    /// Human-readable summary of the problem type (static per error type)\n+    pub title: String,\n+    \n+    /// GTS error code (machine-readable identifier)\n+    pub code: String,\n+    \n+    /// Trace ID for request correlation\n+    pub trace_id: String,\n+    \n+    // =========================================================================\n+    // CONTEXTUAL FIELDS - Optional based on error context\n+    // =========================================================================\n+    \n+    /// HTTP status code. Optional because:\n+    /// - gRPC errors use different status codes\n+    /// - Internal/domain errors may not have HTTP context\n+    /// - Event-driven systems have no request/response\n+    /// When serializing for HTTP response, this is populated from error definition.\n+    #[serde(skip_serializing_if = \"Option::is_none\")]\n+    pub status: Option<u16>,\n+    \n+    /// Human-readable explanation specific to this occurrence.\n+    /// Optional - title may be sufficient for simple errors.\n+    #[serde(skip_serializing_if = \"Option::is_none\")]\n+    pub detail: Option<String>,\n+    \n+    /// Error category for client handling.\n+    /// Optional - can be inferred from base type hierarchy.\n+    #[serde(skip_serializing_if = \"Option::is_none\")]\n+    pub category: Option<ErrorCategory>,\n+    \n+    /// Whether client can retry this request.\n+    /// Optional - can be inferred from base type; not relevant for all contexts.\n+    #[serde(skip_serializing_if = \"Option::is_none\")]\n+    pub retryable: Option<bool>,\n+    \n+    /// URI identifying this specific occurrence (auto-populated from request path)\n+    #[serde(skip_serializing_if = \"Option::is_none\")]\n+    pub instance: Option<String>,\n+    \n+    /// Structured metadata (key-value context)\n+    #[serde(skip_serializing_if = \"Option::is_none\")]\n+    pub metadata: Option<HashMap<String, String>>,\n+    \n+    /// Validation errors for 4xx responses\n+    #[serde(skip_serializing_if = \"Option::is_none\")]\n+    pub errors: Option<Vec<ValidationViolation>>,\n+    \n+    /// Upstream error chain (when error_stack enabled)\n+    #[serde(skip_serializing_if = \"Option::is_none\")]\n+    pub upstream_errors: Option<Vec<UpstreamError>>,\n+}\n+\n+pub enum ErrorCategory {\n+    /// Platform-level execution errors (panics, OOM, internal bugs)\n+    System,\n+    /// Infrastructure/operational issues (DB unavailable, service down, rate limits)\n+    Operational,\n+    /// Client input/request errors (validation, not found, unauthorized)\n+    Client,\n+}\n+```\n+\n+#### Field Requirements Summary\n+\n+| Field | Required | Reason |\n+|-------|----------|--------|\n+| `type_url` | ✅ Yes | RFC 9457 requires problem type URI |\n+| `title` | ✅ Yes | Human-readable error name (static per type) |\n+| `code` | ✅ Yes | GTS identifier for machine processing |\n+| `trace_id` | ✅ Yes | Request correlation for debugging |\n+| `status` | ❌ No | Only relevant for HTTP; gRPC/events/domain errors don't need it |\n+| `detail` | ❌ No | Instance-specific message; title may suffice |\n+| `category` | ❌ No | Inherited from base type hierarchy |\n+| `retryable` | ❌ No | Inherited from base type; not relevant for all contexts |\n+| `instance` | ❌ No | Auto-populated from request path when applicable |\n+| `metadata` | ❌ No | Additional context key-value pairs |\n+| `errors` | ❌ No | Validation violations for 4xx errors |\n+| `upstream_errors` | ❌ No | Error chain from upstream services |\n+\n+**Note:** When converting to HTTP response, `status` is populated from the error definition. When the error is used in non-HTTP contexts (gRPC, domain logic, events), `status` remains `None`.\n+\n+### R2: GTS Identifier and Base Type Requirements\n+\n+Every error MUST have a valid GTS identifier and specify its base type using the `base` field.\n+\n+#### GTS ID Format\n+\n+```\n+gts.<vendor>.<package>.<namespace>.<type>.v<version>~\n+```\n+\n+**Examples:**\n+- `gts.hx.types_registry.entity.not_found.v1~` - Types registry not found error\n+- `gts.hx.file_parser.validation.invalid_format.v1~` - File parser validation error\n+- `gts.hx.system.runtime.timeout.v1~` - System timeout error\n+\n+#### Base Type Chaining\n+\n+Errors form an inheritance chain using the `base` field. The `base` field references another error struct type (not a string literal), similar to how `struct_to_gts_schema` works.\n+\n+The root base error type is:\n+\n+```rust\n+/// Root error type for all GTS errors.\n+#[gts_error(\n+    gts_id = \"gts.hx.core.errors.err.v1~\",\n+    base = true,  // Marks this as a root base type (no parent)\n+    title = \"Error\",\n+    // Optional attributes with defaults for inheritance:\n+    status = 500,        // Default HTTP status (optional, inherited by children)\n+    category = \"System\", // Default category (optional, inherited by children)\n+    retryable = false    // Default retryable (optional, inherited by children)\n+)]\n+pub struct BaseError;\n+```\n+\n+All module-specific errors MUST reference their base type as a struct (extending the appropriate logical/system error):\n+\n+```rust\n+use modkit_errors::system::logical::NotFoundError;\n+\n+/// Entity was not found in the types registry.\n+/// Note: status, category, retryable are inherited from NotFoundError if not specified.\n+#[gts_error(\n+    gts_id = \"gts.hx.types_registry.entity.not_found.v1~\",\n+    base = NotFoundError,  // Extends logical.not_found, not BaseError\n+    title = \"Entity Not Found\",\n+    // These are optional - inherited from base if omitted:\n+    // status = 404,      // Inherited from NotFoundError\n+    // category = \"Client\", // Inherited from NotFoundError  \n+    // retryable = false,   // Inherited from NotFoundError\n+)]\n+pub struct EntityNotFoundError {\n+    pub gts_id: String,\n+}\n+```\n+\n+#### Multi-Level Inheritance\n+\n+Errors can form deeper inheritance chains:\n+\n+```rust\n+/// Logical not found error (platform-level).\n+#[gts_error(\n+    gts_id = \"gts.hx.system.logical.not_found.v1~\",\n+    base = BaseError,  // Platform errors extend BaseError\n+    status = 404,\n+    title = \"Not Found\",\n+    category = \"Client\",\n+    retryable = false\n+)]\n+pub struct NotFoundError;\n+\n+/// Types registry entity not found (module-level).\n+#[gts_error(\n+    gts_id = \"gts.hx.types_registry.entity.not_found.v1~\",\n+    base = NotFoundError,  // Module errors extend logical errors\n+    status = 404,\n+    title = \"Entity Not Found\",\n+    category = \"Client\",\n+    retryable = false\n+)]\n+pub struct EntityNotFoundError {\n+    pub gts_id: String,\n+}\n+```\n+\n+#### Inheritance Hierarchy\n+\n+```\n+BaseError (gts.hx.core.errors.err.v1~)                              [base = true]\n+├── Transport Errors (hx.system.transport.*)                        [base = BaseError]\n+├── Runtime Errors (hx.system.runtime.*)                            [base = BaseError]\n+│   └── hx.types_registry.system.internal.v1~                       [base = runtime.internal]\n+├── HTTP Errors (hx.system.http.*)                                  [base = BaseError]\n+│   └── hx.auth.token_expired.v1~                                   [base = http.unauthorized]\n+├── gRPC Errors (hx.system.grpc.*)                                  [base = BaseError]\n+└── Logical Errors (hx.system.logical.*)                            [base = BaseError]\n+    ├── logical.not_found.v1~                                       [base = BaseError]\n+    │   ├── hx.types_registry.entity.not_found.v1~                  [base = logical.not_found]\n+    │   └── hx.db.entity.not_found.v1~                              [base = logical.not_found]\n+    ├── logical.already_exists.v1~                                  [base = BaseError]\n+    │   └── hx.types_registry.entity.already_exists.v1~             [base = logical.already_exists]\n+    └── logical.validation_failed.v1~                               [base = BaseError]\n+        └── hx.file_parser.validation.invalid_format.v1~            [base = logical.validation_failed]\n+```\n+\n+### R3: Trace ID Requirements\n+\n+- Every error response MUST include a non-empty `trace_id`\n+- Trace ID MUST be propagated from incoming request headers or generated\n+- Trace ID MUST be logged with the error for correlation\n+\n+### R4: Types Registry Integration\n+\n+- All error types MUST be registered in the types registry at startup\n+- Error schema MUST extend base error type: `gts.hx.core.errors.err.v1`\n+- Registration MUST include: code, title, status, category, retryable flag\n+\n+### R5: Standardized System Error Types\n+\n+See [GTS System Errors Catalog](#gts-system-errors-catalog) for the complete list of all system errors.\n+\n+### R6: Error Stack Propagation\n+\n+When a function calls another service/function that returns an error:\n+- The error SHOULD be wrapped with context\n+- `upstream_errors` array SHOULD contain the chain of errors\n+- Each upstream error includes: `code`, `title`, `detail`, `source`\n+- Propagation controlled by `error_stack` configuration flag\n+\n+---\n+\n+## GTS Error Code Format\n+\n+### Structure\n+\n+```\n+gts.<vendor>.<package>.<namespace>.<type>.<version>~<chain>\n+```\n+\n+### Components\n+\n+| Component | Description | Example |\n+|-----------|-------------|---------|\n+| `gts` | Global Type System prefix | `gts` |\n+| `vendor` | Organization identifier | `hx` (Hyperspot) |","path":"intended_design/UNIFIED_ERROR_SYSTEM.md","commit_id":"5bdb0f43b25858af78999718f7247813802b9634","original_commit_id":"5bdb0f43b25858af78999718f7247813802b9634","user":{"login":"alizid10","id":247960800,"node_id":"U_kgDODseU4A","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/247960800?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/alizid10","html_url":"https://github.com/alizid10","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alizid10/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alizid10/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alizid10/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alizid10/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alizid10/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alizid10/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alizid10/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alizid10/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alizid10/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"fixed","created_at":"2026-02-06T16:00:07Z","updated_at":"2026-02-06T16:00:07Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/290#discussion_r2774848166","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/290","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2774848166"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/290#discussion_r2774848166"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/290"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2774848166/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":null,"original_line":404,"side":"RIGHT","in_reply_to_id":2748000810,"author_association":"MEMBER","original_position":404,"position":1,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2774849258","pull_request_review_id":3763871375,"id":2774849258,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs6lZNbq","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,1574 @@\n+# Unified Error System - Intention Document\n+\n+This document defines the architecture, rules, and implementation plan for a unified error handling system across the Hyperspot project. All REST API errors MUST have a GTS identifier, trace ID, and be registered in the types registry.\n+\n+## Table of Contents\n+\n+1. [Executive Summary](#executive-summary)\n+2. [Industry Research](#industry-research)\n+3. [Current State Analysis](#current-state-analysis)\n+4. [Requirements](#requirements)\n+5. [Implementation Rules](#implementation-rules)\n+6. [Migration Plan](#migration-plan)\n+7. [Examples](#examples)\n+8. [HTTP Headers](#http-headers)\n+9. [Security Considerations](#security-considerations)\n+10. [Appendix A: Error Category Definitions](#appendix-a-error-category-definitions)\n+11. [Appendix B: Retryable Error Guidelines](#appendix-b-retryable-error-guidelines)\n+12. [GTS System Errors Catalog](#gts-system-errors-catalog)\n+13. [References](#references)\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Executive Summary\n+\n+### Problem Statement\n+\n+The current error handling across Hyperspot modules is inconsistent:\n+- Some modules use `declare_errors!` macro with JSON catalogs\n+- Others define errors inline without GTS codes\n+- Errors are not registered in the types registry\n+- No standardized metadata/context fields\n+- Inconsistent trace ID propagation\n+\n+### Goals\n+\n+1. **Every REST API error** MUST have a valid GTS identifier\n+2. **Every error response** MUST include a trace ID for debugging\n+3. **All error types** MUST be registered in the types registry\n+4. **Consistent error schema** across all modules following RFC 9457\n+5. **Machine-readable error codes** for programmatic handling\n+6. **Error stack propagation** for nested service calls\n+\n+### Non-Goals\n+\n+- Changing internal domain error types (only API-facing errors)\n+- Modifying logging infrastructure\n+- Changing HTTP status code semantics\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Industry Research\n+\n+### How Major Tech Companies Handle Errors\n+\n+| Company | Standard | Key Features |\n+|---------|----------|--------------|\n+| **Google** | AIP-193 + gRPC Status | `reason` (UPPER_SNAKE_CASE), `domain` (service name), `metadata` (key-value context), `ErrorInfo`, `LocalizedMessage`, `Help` links |\n+| **Amazon AWS** | Custom JSON | `errorType`, `httpStatus`, `requestId`, `message`, custom error object serialization |\n+| **Twitter/X** | JSON with `errors` array | `code` (CAPS_CASE), `message`, `parameter`, `details`, `value` |\n+| **RFC 9457** | Problem Details | `type` (URI), `title`, `status`, `detail`, `instance`, extension members |\n+\n+### Key Patterns Identified\n+\n+1. **Machine-readable identifiers** - Unique codes for programmatic handling (Google's `reason`, Twitter's `code`)\n+2. **Domain/namespace separation** - Identify error source (Google's `domain`, our GTS vendor.package)\n+3. **Structured metadata** - Key-value context without parsing messages (Google's `ErrorInfo.metadata`)\n+4. **Trace/Request IDs** - Correlation for debugging (AWS `requestId`, our `trace_id`)\n+5. **Documentation links** - URIs to error documentation (RFC 9457 `type`, Google's `Help`)\n+6. **Error categorization** - System vs User-defined, Retryable vs Non-retryable\n+\n+### Google AIP-193 ErrorInfo Structure (Reference)\n+\n+```json\n+{\n+  \"error\": {\n+    \"code\": 429,\n+    \"message\": \"The zone 'us-east1-a' does not have enough resources...\",\n+    \"status\": \"RESOURCE_EXHAUSTED\",\n+    \"details\": [\n+      {\n+        \"@type\": \"type.googleapis.com/google.rpc.ErrorInfo\",\n+        \"reason\": \"RESOURCE_AVAILABILITY\",\n+        \"domain\": \"compute.googleapis.com\",\n+        \"metadata\": {\n+          \"zone\": \"us-east1-a\",\n+          \"vmType\": \"e2-medium\"\n+        }\n+      }\n+    ]\n+  }\n+}\n+```\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Current State Analysis\n+\n+### Existing Infrastructure\n+\n+1. **`Problem` struct** (`libs/modkit-errors/src/problem.rs`) - RFC 9457 compliant\n+   - Fields: `type_url`, `title`, `status`, `detail`, `instance`, `code`, `trace_id`, `errors`\n+   - Implements `IntoResponse` for Axum with automatic trace ID enrichment\n+\n+2. **`struct_to_gts_schema` macro** (`modules/types-registry/gts-rust/gts-macros/src/lib.rs`)\n+   - Attribute macro for explicit struct definitions with GTS IDs visible in code\n+   - Generates constants: `GTS_SCHEMA_ID`, `GTS_SCHEMA_JSON`, etc.\n+   - **This pattern will be adapted for error definitions**\n+\n+3. **`declare_errors!` macro** (`libs/modkit-errors-macro/src/lib.rs`) - **TO BE DEPRECATED**\n+   - Generates type-safe error enums from JSON catalogs\n+   - Problem: GTS IDs hidden in external JSON files, not visible to LLMs\n+   - Used by: `users_info` example, `modkit-odata`\n+\n+### Gaps Identified\n+\n+| Gap | Current State | Required State |\n+|-----|---------------|----------------|\n+| **Hidden GTS IDs** | JSON-based `declare_errors!` | Explicit `#[gts_error]` structs with visible GTS IDs |\n+| **Inconsistent definitions** | Some modules use inline errors | All modules use `#[gts_error]` structs |\n+| **No types registry** | Errors not registered | All errors registered as GTS types |\n+| **Missing metadata** | No structured context | Struct fields → `metadata` map |\n+| **Partial trace IDs** | Only in `IntoResponse` | Mandatory in all error responses |\n+| **No error categories** | Flat error codes | System/Operational/Client categories |\n+| **No error stack** | Single error | Upstream error chain propagation |\n+\n+### Current Module Migration Status\n+\n+| Module | Location | Status | Issues |\n+|--------|----------|--------|--------|\n+| **file_parser** | `modules/file_parser/` | 🔴 Not migrated | No GTS IDs, inline `Problem::new()` |\n+| **types-registry** | `modules/system/types-registry/` | 🟡 Partial | Has codes but not GTS format (e.g., `TYPES_REGISTRY_NOT_FOUND`) |\n+| **nodes_registry** | `modules/system/nodes_registry/` | 🔴 Not migrated | Non-GTS codes (e.g., `NODES_NOT_FOUND`) |\n+| **api_gateway** | `modules/system/api_gateway/` | 🔴 Not migrated | No Problem struct, simple error codes |\n+| **tenant_resolver** | `modules/system/tenant_resolver/` | 🔴 Not migrated | No GTS IDs |\n+| **simple-user-settings** | `modules/simple-user-settings/` | 🟡 Partial | Uses `declare_errors!` with old chain format |\n+| **modkit-auth** | `libs/modkit-auth/` | 🔴 Not migrated | No GTS IDs, custom `IntoResponse` |\n+| **modkit-odata** | `libs/modkit-odata/` | 🟡 Partial | Uses `declare_errors!` with old chain format |\n+| **users_info** (example) | `examples/modkit/users_info/` | 🟡 Partial | Uses `declare_errors!` with old chain format |\n+\n+#### Legend\n+- 🟢 **Migrated** - Uses `#[gts_error]` structs with proper base types\n+- 🟡 **Partial** - Has GTS IDs but uses deprecated `declare_errors!` or old format\n+- 🔴 **Not migrated** - No GTS IDs or non-GTS format codes\n+\n+#### GTS ID Format Note\n+\n+**Old chain format** (used by `declare_errors!`):\n+```\n+gts.hx.core.errors.err.v1~hx.module.error_name.v1\n+```\n+\n+**New format** (with `base` field):\n+```\n+gts.hx.module.namespace.error_name.v1~\n+```\n+The `base` field in `#[gts_error]` replaces the chain suffix, making inheritance explicit in code.\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Requirements\n+\n+### R1: Error Schema Requirements\n+\n+Every error returned from REST API MUST conform to the unified schema:\n+\n+```rust\n+pub struct Problem {\n+    // =========================================================================\n+    // REQUIRED FIELDS - Core error identification\n+    // =========================================================================\n+    \n+    /// URI reference identifying the problem type (GTS-based)\n+    /// Example: \"https://docs.hyperspot.com/errors/types_registry_entity_not_found_v1\"\n+    #[serde(rename = \"type\")]\n+    pub type_url: String,\n+    \n+    /// Human-readable summary of the problem type (static per error type)\n+    pub title: String,\n+    \n+    /// GTS error code (machine-readable identifier)\n+    pub code: String,\n+    \n+    /// Trace ID for request correlation\n+    pub trace_id: String,\n+    \n+    // =========================================================================\n+    // CONTEXTUAL FIELDS - Optional based on error context\n+    // =========================================================================\n+    \n+    /// HTTP status code. Optional because:\n+    /// - gRPC errors use different status codes\n+    /// - Internal/domain errors may not have HTTP context\n+    /// - Event-driven systems have no request/response\n+    /// When serializing for HTTP response, this is populated from error definition.\n+    #[serde(skip_serializing_if = \"Option::is_none\")]\n+    pub status: Option<u16>,\n+    \n+    /// Human-readable explanation specific to this occurrence.\n+    /// Optional - title may be sufficient for simple errors.\n+    #[serde(skip_serializing_if = \"Option::is_none\")]\n+    pub detail: Option<String>,\n+    \n+    /// Error category for client handling.\n+    /// Optional - can be inferred from base type hierarchy.\n+    #[serde(skip_serializing_if = \"Option::is_none\")]\n+    pub category: Option<ErrorCategory>,\n+    \n+    /// Whether client can retry this request.\n+    /// Optional - can be inferred from base type; not relevant for all contexts.\n+    #[serde(skip_serializing_if = \"Option::is_none\")]\n+    pub retryable: Option<bool>,\n+    \n+    /// URI identifying this specific occurrence (auto-populated from request path)\n+    #[serde(skip_serializing_if = \"Option::is_none\")]\n+    pub instance: Option<String>,\n+    \n+    /// Structured metadata (key-value context)\n+    #[serde(skip_serializing_if = \"Option::is_none\")]\n+    pub metadata: Option<HashMap<String, String>>,\n+    \n+    /// Validation errors for 4xx responses\n+    #[serde(skip_serializing_if = \"Option::is_none\")]\n+    pub errors: Option<Vec<ValidationViolation>>,\n+    \n+    /// Upstream error chain (when error_stack enabled)\n+    #[serde(skip_serializing_if = \"Option::is_none\")]\n+    pub upstream_errors: Option<Vec<UpstreamError>>,\n+}\n+\n+pub enum ErrorCategory {\n+    /// Platform-level execution errors (panics, OOM, internal bugs)\n+    System,\n+    /// Infrastructure/operational issues (DB unavailable, service down, rate limits)\n+    Operational,\n+    /// Client input/request errors (validation, not found, unauthorized)\n+    Client,\n+}\n+```\n+\n+#### Field Requirements Summary\n+\n+| Field | Required | Reason |\n+|-------|----------|--------|\n+| `type_url` | ✅ Yes | RFC 9457 requires problem type URI |\n+| `title` | ✅ Yes | Human-readable error name (static per type) |\n+| `code` | ✅ Yes | GTS identifier for machine processing |\n+| `trace_id` | ✅ Yes | Request correlation for debugging |\n+| `status` | ❌ No | Only relevant for HTTP; gRPC/events/domain errors don't need it |\n+| `detail` | ❌ No | Instance-specific message; title may suffice |\n+| `category` | ❌ No | Inherited from base type hierarchy |\n+| `retryable` | ❌ No | Inherited from base type; not relevant for all contexts |\n+| `instance` | ❌ No | Auto-populated from request path when applicable |\n+| `metadata` | ❌ No | Additional context key-value pairs |\n+| `errors` | ❌ No | Validation violations for 4xx errors |\n+| `upstream_errors` | ❌ No | Error chain from upstream services |\n+\n+**Note:** When converting to HTTP response, `status` is populated from the error definition. When the error is used in non-HTTP contexts (gRPC, domain logic, events), `status` remains `None`.\n+\n+### R2: GTS Identifier and Base Type Requirements\n+\n+Every error MUST have a valid GTS identifier and specify its base type using the `base` field.\n+\n+#### GTS ID Format\n+\n+```\n+gts.<vendor>.<package>.<namespace>.<type>.v<version>~\n+```\n+\n+**Examples:**\n+- `gts.hx.types_registry.entity.not_found.v1~` - Types registry not found error\n+- `gts.hx.file_parser.validation.invalid_format.v1~` - File parser validation error\n+- `gts.hx.system.runtime.timeout.v1~` - System timeout error\n+\n+#### Base Type Chaining\n+\n+Errors form an inheritance chain using the `base` field. The `base` field references another error struct type (not a string literal), similar to how `struct_to_gts_schema` works.\n+\n+The root base error type is:\n+\n+```rust\n+/// Root error type for all GTS errors.\n+#[gts_error(\n+    gts_id = \"gts.hx.core.errors.err.v1~\",\n+    base = true,  // Marks this as a root base type (no parent)\n+    title = \"Error\",\n+    // Optional attributes with defaults for inheritance:\n+    status = 500,        // Default HTTP status (optional, inherited by children)\n+    category = \"System\", // Default category (optional, inherited by children)\n+    retryable = false    // Default retryable (optional, inherited by children)\n+)]\n+pub struct BaseError;\n+```\n+\n+All module-specific errors MUST reference their base type as a struct (extending the appropriate logical/system error):\n+\n+```rust\n+use modkit_errors::system::logical::NotFoundError;\n+\n+/// Entity was not found in the types registry.\n+/// Note: status, category, retryable are inherited from NotFoundError if not specified.\n+#[gts_error(\n+    gts_id = \"gts.hx.types_registry.entity.not_found.v1~\",\n+    base = NotFoundError,  // Extends logical.not_found, not BaseError\n+    title = \"Entity Not Found\",\n+    // These are optional - inherited from base if omitted:\n+    // status = 404,      // Inherited from NotFoundError\n+    // category = \"Client\", // Inherited from NotFoundError  \n+    // retryable = false,   // Inherited from NotFoundError\n+)]\n+pub struct EntityNotFoundError {\n+    pub gts_id: String,\n+}\n+```\n+\n+#### Multi-Level Inheritance\n+\n+Errors can form deeper inheritance chains:\n+\n+```rust\n+/// Logical not found error (platform-level).\n+#[gts_error(\n+    gts_id = \"gts.hx.system.logical.not_found.v1~\",\n+    base = BaseError,  // Platform errors extend BaseError\n+    status = 404,\n+    title = \"Not Found\",\n+    category = \"Client\",\n+    retryable = false\n+)]\n+pub struct NotFoundError;\n+\n+/// Types registry entity not found (module-level).\n+#[gts_error(\n+    gts_id = \"gts.hx.types_registry.entity.not_found.v1~\",\n+    base = NotFoundError,  // Module errors extend logical errors\n+    status = 404,\n+    title = \"Entity Not Found\",\n+    category = \"Client\",\n+    retryable = false\n+)]\n+pub struct EntityNotFoundError {\n+    pub gts_id: String,\n+}\n+```\n+\n+#### Inheritance Hierarchy\n+\n+```\n+BaseError (gts.hx.core.errors.err.v1~)                              [base = true]\n+├── Transport Errors (hx.system.transport.*)                        [base = BaseError]\n+├── Runtime Errors (hx.system.runtime.*)                            [base = BaseError]\n+│   └── hx.types_registry.system.internal.v1~                       [base = runtime.internal]\n+├── HTTP Errors (hx.system.http.*)                                  [base = BaseError]\n+│   └── hx.auth.token_expired.v1~                                   [base = http.unauthorized]\n+├── gRPC Errors (hx.system.grpc.*)                                  [base = BaseError]\n+└── Logical Errors (hx.system.logical.*)                            [base = BaseError]\n+    ├── logical.not_found.v1~                                       [base = BaseError]\n+    │   ├── hx.types_registry.entity.not_found.v1~                  [base = logical.not_found]\n+    │   └── hx.db.entity.not_found.v1~                              [base = logical.not_found]\n+    ├── logical.already_exists.v1~                                  [base = BaseError]\n+    │   └── hx.types_registry.entity.already_exists.v1~             [base = logical.already_exists]\n+    └── logical.validation_failed.v1~                               [base = BaseError]\n+        └── hx.file_parser.validation.invalid_format.v1~            [base = logical.validation_failed]\n+```\n+\n+### R3: Trace ID Requirements\n+\n+- Every error response MUST include a non-empty `trace_id`\n+- Trace ID MUST be propagated from incoming request headers or generated\n+- Trace ID MUST be logged with the error for correlation\n+\n+### R4: Types Registry Integration\n+\n+- All error types MUST be registered in the types registry at startup\n+- Error schema MUST extend base error type: `gts.hx.core.errors.err.v1`","path":"intended_design/UNIFIED_ERROR_SYSTEM.md","commit_id":"5bdb0f43b25858af78999718f7247813802b9634","original_commit_id":"5bdb0f43b25858af78999718f7247813802b9634","user":{"login":"alizid10","id":247960800,"node_id":"U_kgDODseU4A","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/247960800?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/alizid10","html_url":"https://github.com/alizid10","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alizid10/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alizid10/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alizid10/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alizid10/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alizid10/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alizid10/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alizid10/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alizid10/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alizid10/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"fixed","created_at":"2026-02-06T16:00:23Z","updated_at":"2026-02-06T16:00:23Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/290#discussion_r2774849258","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/290","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2774849258"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/290#discussion_r2774849258"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/290"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2774849258/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":null,"original_line":374,"side":"RIGHT","in_reply_to_id":2747999366,"author_association":"MEMBER","original_position":374,"position":1,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2774851279","pull_request_review_id":3763873544,"id":2774851279,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs6lZN7P","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,417 @@\n+# GTS Error System Documentation\n+\n+This document describes how errors are defined, structured, transformed, and used in the Hyperspot/gts-rust project.\n+\n+## Overview\n+\n+The error system follows **RFC 9457 Problem Details for HTTP APIs** and uses a **GTS (Global Type System)** format for error codes. The system provides:\n+\n+- **Compile-time validated** error catalogs via JSON files\n+- **Type-safe** error code enums generated by proc-macros\n+- **Layered error transformation** from domain → API → HTTP response\n+- **Consistent error format** across all modules\n+\n+## Architecture\n+\n+```\n+┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n+│                           Error Flow                                     │\n+├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n+│                                                                          │\n+│  gts/errors.json  ──────►  declare_errors! macro  ──────►  ErrorCode    │\n+│  (Source of Truth)         (Compile-time)                  (Enum)       │\n+│                                                                          │\n+│  DomainError  ──────►  ErrorCode::xxx().with_context()  ──────►  Problem│\n+│  (Business Logic)      (Mapping Layer)                        (RFC 9457)│\n+│                                                                          │\n+│  Problem  ──────►  IntoResponse (Axum)  ──────►  HTTP Response          │\n+│  (Data)            (Framework Integration)       (JSON + Headers)       │\n+│                                                                          │\n+└─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘\n+```\n+\n+## Components\n+\n+### 1. Error Catalog JSON (`gts/errors.json`)\n+\n+The source of truth for error definitions. Located in each module's `gts/` directory.\n+\n+**File Location Pattern:** `<module>/gts/errors.json`\n+\n+**Schema:**\n+```json\n+[\n+  {\n+    \"status\": 404,\n+    \"title\": \"User Not Found\",\n+    \"code\": \"gts.hx.core.errors.err.v1~hx.example1.user.not_found.v1\",\n+    \"type\": \"https://errors.example.com/...\",  // optional\n+    \"alias\": \"user_not_found\"                   // optional\n+  }\n+]\n+```\n+\n+**Fields:**\n+| Field | Required | Description |\n+|-------|----------|-------------|\n+| `status` | Yes | HTTP status code (100-599) |\n+| `title` | Yes | Human-readable error title |\n+| `code` | Yes | GTS-formatted error code |\n+| `type` | No | URI for error documentation |\n+| `alias` | No | Short name override for generated accessor |\n+\n+### 2. GTS Code Format\n+\n+GTS codes follow a strict format for global type identification:\n+\n+```\n+gts.vendor.package.namespace.type.version~chain1~chain2~...~instanceGTX\n+```\n+\n+**Structure:**\n+- **Prefix:** Always starts with `gts.`","path":"docs/GTS_ERRORS.md","commit_id":"5bdb0f43b25858af78999718f7247813802b9634","original_commit_id":"5bdb0f43b25858af78999718f7247813802b9634","user":{"login":"alizid10","id":247960800,"node_id":"U_kgDODseU4A","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/247960800?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/alizid10","html_url":"https://github.com/alizid10","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alizid10/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alizid10/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alizid10/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alizid10/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alizid10/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alizid10/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alizid10/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alizid10/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alizid10/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"fixed","created_at":"2026-02-06T16:00:52Z","updated_at":"2026-02-06T16:00:52Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/290#discussion_r2774851279","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/290","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2774851279"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/290#discussion_r2774851279"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/290"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2774851279/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":null,"original_line":72,"side":"RIGHT","in_reply_to_id":2747829205,"author_association":"MEMBER","original_position":72,"position":1,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2774852206","pull_request_review_id":3763874780,"id":2774852206,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs6lZOJu","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,417 @@\n+# GTS Error System Documentation\n+\n+This document describes how errors are defined, structured, transformed, and used in the Hyperspot/gts-rust project.\n+\n+## Overview\n+\n+The error system follows **RFC 9457 Problem Details for HTTP APIs** and uses a **GTS (Global Type System)** format for error codes. The system provides:\n+\n+- **Compile-time validated** error catalogs via JSON files\n+- **Type-safe** error code enums generated by proc-macros\n+- **Layered error transformation** from domain → API → HTTP response\n+- **Consistent error format** across all modules\n+\n+## Architecture\n+\n+```\n+┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n+│                           Error Flow                                     │\n+├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n+│                                                                          │\n+│  gts/errors.json  ──────►  declare_errors! macro  ──────►  ErrorCode    │\n+│  (Source of Truth)         (Compile-time)                  (Enum)       │\n+│                                                                          │\n+│  DomainError  ──────►  ErrorCode::xxx().with_context()  ──────►  Problem│\n+│  (Business Logic)      (Mapping Layer)                        (RFC 9457)│\n+│                                                                          │\n+│  Problem  ──────►  IntoResponse (Axum)  ──────►  HTTP Response          │\n+│  (Data)            (Framework Integration)       (JSON + Headers)       │\n+│                                                                          │\n+└─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘\n+```\n+\n+## Components\n+\n+### 1. Error Catalog JSON (`gts/errors.json`)\n+\n+The source of truth for error definitions. Located in each module's `gts/` directory.\n+\n+**File Location Pattern:** `<module>/gts/errors.json`\n+\n+**Schema:**\n+```json\n+[\n+  {\n+    \"status\": 404,\n+    \"title\": \"User Not Found\",\n+    \"code\": \"gts.hx.core.errors.err.v1~hx.example1.user.not_found.v1\",\n+    \"type\": \"https://errors.example.com/...\",  // optional\n+    \"alias\": \"user_not_found\"                   // optional\n+  }\n+]\n+```\n+\n+**Fields:**\n+| Field | Required | Description |\n+|-------|----------|-------------|\n+| `status` | Yes | HTTP status code (100-599) |\n+| `title` | Yes | Human-readable error title |\n+| `code` | Yes | GTS-formatted error code |\n+| `type` | No | URI for error documentation |\n+| `alias` | No | Short name override for generated accessor |\n+\n+### 2. GTS Code Format\n+\n+GTS codes follow a strict format for global type identification:\n+\n+```\n+gts.vendor.package.namespace.type.version~chain1~chain2~...~instanceGTX\n+```\n+\n+**Structure:**\n+- **Prefix:** Always starts with `gts.`\n+- **Chain separator:** `~` separates GTX segments\n+- **Segment separator:** `.` separates parts within a GTX\n+- **Final GTX:** Must have at least 5 segments: `vendor.package.namespace.type.version`\n+- **Version:** Must end with `vN` or `vN.M` format\n+\n+**Example Breakdown:**\n+```\n+gts.hx.core.errors.err.v1~hx.example1.user.not_found.v1\n+│   │  │    │      │   │  │  │        │    │         │\n+│   │  │    │      │   │  │  │        │    │         └─ version\n+│   │  │    │      │   │  │  │        │    └─ type (not_found)\n+│   │  │    │      │   │  │  │        └─ namespace (user)\n+│   │  │    │      │   │  │  └─ package (example1)\n+│   │  │    │      │   │  └─ vendor (hx)\n+│   │  │    │      │   └─ version\n+│   │  │    │      └─ type (err)\n+│   │  │    └─ namespace (errors)\n+│   │  └─ package (core)\n+│   └─ vendor (hx)\n+└─ prefix\n+```\n+\n+**Validation Rules:**\n+1. Must start with `gts.`\n+2. All segments must be lowercase alphanumeric or underscore\n+3. No empty segments allowed\n+4. Final GTX must have ≥5 segments after vendor\n+5. Must end with valid version format (`v1`, `v1.2`, etc.)\n+\n+### 3. Proc-Macro: `declare_errors!`\n+\n+Generates type-safe error code enums from JSON at compile time.\n+\n+**Location:** `libs/modkit-errors-macro/src/lib.rs`\n+\n+**Usage:**\n+```rust\n+use modkit_errors_macro::declare_errors;\n+\n+declare_errors! {\n+    path = \"gts/errors.json\",\n+    namespace = \"errors\",\n+    vis = \"pub\"\n+}\n+```\n+\n+**Parameters:**\n+| Parameter | Required | Description |\n+|-----------|----------|-------------|\n+| `path` | Yes | Path to JSON file relative to `CARGO_MANIFEST_DIR` |\n+| `namespace` | Yes | Module name for generated code |\n+| `vis` | No | Visibility (`\"pub\"` or private) |\n+\n+**Generated Code:**\n+```rust\n+// Enum with all error codes\n+#[derive(Debug, Clone, Copy, PartialEq, Eq, Hash)]\n+pub enum ErrorCode {\n+    gts_hx_core_errors_err_v1_hx_example1_user_not_found_v1,\n+    // ...\n+}\n+\n+impl ErrorCode {\n+    // Get HTTP status\n+    pub const fn status(&self) -> u16 { ... }\n+    \n+    // Get full error definition\n+    pub const fn def(&self) -> ErrDef { ... }\n+    \n+    // Convert to Problem with detail\n+    pub fn as_problem(&self, detail: impl Into<String>) -> Problem { ... }\n+    \n+    // Create Problem with context (instance + trace_id)\n+    pub fn with_context(\n+        &self,\n+        detail: impl Into<String>,\n+        instance: &str,\n+        trace_id: Option<String>,\n+    ) -> Problem { ... }\n+    \n+    // Short accessor (derived from GTS or alias)\n+    pub const fn example1_user_not_found_v1() -> Self { ... }\n+}\n+\n+// Compile-time validated macro\n+macro_rules! problem_from_catalog { ... }\n+macro_rules! response_from_catalog { ... }\n+```\n+\n+### 4. Core Types\n+\n+#### `ErrDef` (Error Definition)\n+**Location:** `libs/modkit-errors/src/catalog.rs`\n+\n+```rust\n+pub struct ErrDef {\n+    pub status: u16,\n+    pub title: &'static str,\n+    pub code: &'static str,\n+    pub type_url: &'static str,\n+}\n+\n+impl ErrDef {\n+    pub fn as_problem(&self, detail: impl Into<String>) -> Problem { ... }\n+}\n+```\n+\n+#### `Problem` (RFC 9457)\n+**Location:** `libs/modkit-errors/src/problem.rs`\n+\n+```rust\n+pub struct Problem {\n+    pub type_url: String,      // URI reference for problem type\n+    pub title: String,         // Human-readable summary\n+    pub status: StatusCode,    // HTTP status code","path":"docs/GTS_ERRORS.md","commit_id":"5bdb0f43b25858af78999718f7247813802b9634","original_commit_id":"5bdb0f43b25858af78999718f7247813802b9634","user":{"login":"alizid10","id":247960800,"node_id":"U_kgDODseU4A","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/247960800?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/alizid10","html_url":"https://github.com/alizid10","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alizid10/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alizid10/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alizid10/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alizid10/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alizid10/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alizid10/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alizid10/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alizid10/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alizid10/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"change","created_at":"2026-02-06T16:01:05Z","updated_at":"2026-02-06T16:01:05Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/290#discussion_r2774852206","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/290","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2774852206"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/290#discussion_r2774852206"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/290"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2774852206/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":null,"original_line":187,"side":"RIGHT","in_reply_to_id":2747838392,"author_association":"MEMBER","original_position":187,"position":1,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2774852696","pull_request_review_id":3763875276,"id":2774852696,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs6lZORY","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,417 @@\n+# GTS Error System Documentation\n+\n+This document describes how errors are defined, structured, transformed, and used in the Hyperspot/gts-rust project.\n+\n+## Overview\n+\n+The error system follows **RFC 9457 Problem Details for HTTP APIs** and uses a **GTS (Global Type System)** format for error codes. The system provides:\n+\n+- **Compile-time validated** error catalogs via JSON files\n+- **Type-safe** error code enums generated by proc-macros\n+- **Layered error transformation** from domain → API → HTTP response\n+- **Consistent error format** across all modules\n+\n+## Architecture\n+\n+```\n+┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n+│                           Error Flow                                     │\n+├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n+│                                                                          │\n+│  gts/errors.json  ──────►  declare_errors! macro  ──────►  ErrorCode    │\n+│  (Source of Truth)         (Compile-time)                  (Enum)       │\n+│                                                                          │\n+│  DomainError  ──────►  ErrorCode::xxx().with_context()  ──────►  Problem│\n+│  (Business Logic)      (Mapping Layer)                        (RFC 9457)│\n+│                                                                          │\n+│  Problem  ──────►  IntoResponse (Axum)  ──────►  HTTP Response          │\n+│  (Data)            (Framework Integration)       (JSON + Headers)       │\n+│                                                                          │\n+└─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘\n+```\n+\n+## Components\n+\n+### 1. Error Catalog JSON (`gts/errors.json`)\n+\n+The source of truth for error definitions. Located in each module's `gts/` directory.\n+\n+**File Location Pattern:** `<module>/gts/errors.json`\n+\n+**Schema:**\n+```json\n+[\n+  {\n+    \"status\": 404,\n+    \"title\": \"User Not Found\",\n+    \"code\": \"gts.hx.core.errors.err.v1~hx.example1.user.not_found.v1\",\n+    \"type\": \"https://errors.example.com/...\",  // optional\n+    \"alias\": \"user_not_found\"                   // optional\n+  }\n+]\n+```\n+\n+**Fields:**\n+| Field | Required | Description |\n+|-------|----------|-------------|\n+| `status` | Yes | HTTP status code (100-599) |\n+| `title` | Yes | Human-readable error title |\n+| `code` | Yes | GTS-formatted error code |\n+| `type` | No | URI for error documentation |\n+| `alias` | No | Short name override for generated accessor |\n+\n+### 2. GTS Code Format\n+\n+GTS codes follow a strict format for global type identification:\n+\n+```\n+gts.vendor.package.namespace.type.version~chain1~chain2~...~instanceGTX\n+```\n+\n+**Structure:**\n+- **Prefix:** Always starts with `gts.`\n+- **Chain separator:** `~` separates GTX segments\n+- **Segment separator:** `.` separates parts within a GTX\n+- **Final GTX:** Must have at least 5 segments: `vendor.package.namespace.type.version`\n+- **Version:** Must end with `vN` or `vN.M` format\n+\n+**Example Breakdown:**\n+```\n+gts.hx.core.errors.err.v1~hx.example1.user.not_found.v1\n+│   │  │    │      │   │  │  │        │    │         │\n+│   │  │    │      │   │  │  │        │    │         └─ version\n+│   │  │    │      │   │  │  │        │    └─ type (not_found)\n+│   │  │    │      │   │  │  │        └─ namespace (user)\n+│   │  │    │      │   │  │  └─ package (example1)\n+│   │  │    │      │   │  └─ vendor (hx)\n+│   │  │    │      │   └─ version\n+│   │  │    │      └─ type (err)\n+│   │  │    └─ namespace (errors)\n+│   │  └─ package (core)\n+│   └─ vendor (hx)\n+└─ prefix\n+```\n+\n+**Validation Rules:**\n+1. Must start with `gts.`\n+2. All segments must be lowercase alphanumeric or underscore\n+3. No empty segments allowed\n+4. Final GTX must have ≥5 segments after vendor\n+5. Must end with valid version format (`v1`, `v1.2`, etc.)\n+\n+### 3. Proc-Macro: `declare_errors!`\n+\n+Generates type-safe error code enums from JSON at compile time.\n+\n+**Location:** `libs/modkit-errors-macro/src/lib.rs`\n+\n+**Usage:**\n+```rust\n+use modkit_errors_macro::declare_errors;\n+\n+declare_errors! {\n+    path = \"gts/errors.json\",\n+    namespace = \"errors\",\n+    vis = \"pub\"\n+}\n+```\n+\n+**Parameters:**\n+| Parameter | Required | Description |\n+|-----------|----------|-------------|\n+| `path` | Yes | Path to JSON file relative to `CARGO_MANIFEST_DIR` |\n+| `namespace` | Yes | Module name for generated code |\n+| `vis` | No | Visibility (`\"pub\"` or private) |\n+\n+**Generated Code:**\n+```rust\n+// Enum with all error codes\n+#[derive(Debug, Clone, Copy, PartialEq, Eq, Hash)]\n+pub enum ErrorCode {\n+    gts_hx_core_errors_err_v1_hx_example1_user_not_found_v1,\n+    // ...\n+}\n+\n+impl ErrorCode {\n+    // Get HTTP status\n+    pub const fn status(&self) -> u16 { ... }\n+    \n+    // Get full error definition\n+    pub const fn def(&self) -> ErrDef { ... }\n+    \n+    // Convert to Problem with detail\n+    pub fn as_problem(&self, detail: impl Into<String>) -> Problem { ... }\n+    \n+    // Create Problem with context (instance + trace_id)\n+    pub fn with_context(\n+        &self,\n+        detail: impl Into<String>,\n+        instance: &str,\n+        trace_id: Option<String>,\n+    ) -> Problem { ... }\n+    \n+    // Short accessor (derived from GTS or alias)\n+    pub const fn example1_user_not_found_v1() -> Self { ... }\n+}\n+\n+// Compile-time validated macro\n+macro_rules! problem_from_catalog { ... }\n+macro_rules! response_from_catalog { ... }\n+```\n+\n+### 4. Core Types\n+\n+#### `ErrDef` (Error Definition)\n+**Location:** `libs/modkit-errors/src/catalog.rs`\n+\n+```rust\n+pub struct ErrDef {\n+    pub status: u16,\n+    pub title: &'static str,\n+    pub code: &'static str,\n+    pub type_url: &'static str,\n+}\n+\n+impl ErrDef {\n+    pub fn as_problem(&self, detail: impl Into<String>) -> Problem { ... }\n+}\n+```\n+\n+#### `Problem` (RFC 9457)\n+**Location:** `libs/modkit-errors/src/problem.rs`\n+\n+```rust\n+pub struct Problem {\n+    pub type_url: String,      // URI reference for problem type\n+    pub title: String,         // Human-readable summary\n+    pub status: StatusCode,    // HTTP status code\n+    pub detail: String,        // Specific occurrence explanation\n+    pub instance: String,      // URI for this occurrence\n+    pub code: String,          // Machine-readable error code\n+    pub trace_id: Option<String>,\n+    pub errors: Option<Vec<ValidationViolation>>,\n+}\n+```\n+\n+**Builder Pattern:**\n+```rust\n+Problem::new(StatusCode::NOT_FOUND, \"Not Found\", \"User not found\")\n+    .with_code(\"gts.hx....\")\n+    .with_type(\"https://...\")\n+    .with_instance(\"/api/users/123\")\n+    .with_trace_id(\"req-456\")\n+    .with_errors(vec![...])\n+```\n+\n+## Error Flow by Layer\n+\n+### Layer 1: Domain Errors\n+\n+Domain errors represent business logic failures. They are internal and don't contain HTTP-specific information.\n+\n+**Location:** `<module>/src/domain/error.rs`\n+\n+```rust\n+#[derive(Error, Debug)]\n+pub enum DomainError {\n+    #[error(\"User not found: {id}\")]\n+    UserNotFound { id: Uuid },\n+    \n+    #[error(\"Email '{email}' already exists\")]\n+    EmailAlreadyExists { email: String },\n+    \n+    #[error(\"Database error: {message}\")]\n+    Database { message: String },\n+    // ...\n+}\n+```\n+\n+### Layer 2: SDK Errors (Public API)\n+\n+SDK errors are exposed to other modules via the client trait. They are simplified and safe to expose.\n+\n+**Location:** `<module>-sdk/src/errors.rs`\n+\n+```rust\n+#[derive(Error, Debug, Clone)]\n+pub enum UsersInfoError {\n+    #[error(\"Resource not found: {id}\")]\n+    NotFound { id: Uuid },\n+    \n+    #[error(\"Validation error: {message}\")]\n+    Validation { message: String },\n+    \n+    #[error(\"Internal error\")]\n+    Internal,\n+}\n+```\n+\n+### Layer 3: API Error Mapping\n+\n+The API layer maps domain errors to RFC 9457 Problems using the error catalog.\n+\n+**Location:** `<module>/src/api/rest/error.rs`\n+\n+```rust\n+use crate::errors::ErrorCode;\n+\n+pub fn domain_error_to_problem(e: &DomainError, instance: &str) -> Problem {\n+    let trace_id = tracing::Span::current()\n+        .id()\n+        .map(|id| id.into_u64().to_string());\n+\n+    match &e {\n+        DomainError::UserNotFound { id } => {\n+            ErrorCode::example1_user_not_found_v1().with_context(\n+                format!(\"User with id {id} was not found\"),\n+                instance,\n+                trace_id,\n+            )\n+        }\n+        DomainError::Database { .. } => {\n+            tracing::error!(error = ?e, \"Database error occurred\");\n+            ErrorCode::example1_user_internal_database_v1().with_context(\n+                \"An internal database error occurred\",\n+                instance,\n+                trace_id,\n+            )\n+        }\n+        // ...\n+    }\n+}\n+```\n+\n+### Layer 4: HTTP Response\n+\n+`Problem` implements `IntoResponse` for Axum, automatically:\n+- Setting the correct HTTP status code\n+- Setting `Content-Type: application/problem+json`\n+- Enriching with trace ID from current span if not set\n+\n+```rust\n+// In handler\n+async fn get_user(...) -> Result<Json<User>, Problem> {\n+    let user = service.get_user(id).await\n+        .map_err(|e| domain_error_to_problem(&e, &path))?;\n+    Ok(Json(user))\n+}\n+```\n+\n+## Creating a New Error Catalog\n+\n+### Step 1: Create `gts/errors.json`\n+\n+```json\n+[\n+  {\n+    \"status\": 404,\n+    \"title\": \"Resource Not Found\",\n+    \"code\": \"gts.hx.core.errors.err.v1~hx.mymodule.resource.not_found.v1\"\n+  },\n+  {\n+    \"status\": 422,\n+    \"title\": \"Validation Error\",\n+    \"code\": \"gts.hx.core.errors.err.v1~hx.mymodule.validation.invalid_input.v1\"\n+  }\n+]\n+```\n+\n+### Step 2: Create `src/errors.rs`\n+\n+```rust\n+use modkit_errors_macro::declare_errors;\n+\n+declare_errors! {\n+    path = \"gts/errors.json\",\n+    namespace = \"errors\",\n+    vis = \"pub\"\n+}\n+```\n+\n+### Step 3: Add to `Cargo.toml`\n+\n+```toml\n+[dependencies]\n+modkit-errors-macro = { path = \"../../libs/modkit-errors-macro\" }\n+modkit-errors = { path = \"../../libs/modkit-errors\" }\n+```\n+\n+### Step 4: Use in API Layer\n+\n+```rust\n+use crate::errors::ErrorCode;\n+\n+fn map_error(e: &MyDomainError, instance: &str) -> Problem {\n+    match e {\n+        MyDomainError::NotFound => {\n+            ErrorCode::mymodule_resource_not_found_v1()\n+                .with_context(\"Resource not found\", instance, None)\n+        }\n+        // ...\n+    }\n+}\n+```\n+\n+## Short Name Derivation\n+\n+Short accessor names are derived from the final GTX segment:\n+\n+```\n+gts.hx.core.errors.err.v1~hx.example1.user.not_found.v1\n+                         └─────────────────────────────┘\n+                                    ↓\n+                         example1_user_not_found_v1()\n+```\n+\n+**Rules:**\n+1. Extract final GTX (after last `~`)\n+2. Drop vendor (first segment)\n+3. Join remaining segments with `_`\n+4. Prefix with `_` if starts with digit\n+\n+**Override with `alias`:**\n+```json\n+{\n+  \"code\": \"gts.hx.core.errors.err.v1~hx.example1.user.not_found.v1\",","path":"docs/GTS_ERRORS.md","commit_id":"5bdb0f43b25858af78999718f7247813802b9634","original_commit_id":"5bdb0f43b25858af78999718f7247813802b9634","user":{"login":"alizid10","id":247960800,"node_id":"U_kgDODseU4A","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/247960800?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/alizid10","html_url":"https://github.com/alizid10","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alizid10/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alizid10/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alizid10/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alizid10/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alizid10/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alizid10/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alizid10/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alizid10/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alizid10/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"done","created_at":"2026-02-06T16:01:12Z","updated_at":"2026-02-06T16:01:13Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/290#discussion_r2774852696","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/290","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2774852696"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/290#discussion_r2774852696"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/290"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2774852696/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":null,"original_line":375,"side":"RIGHT","in_reply_to_id":2747848678,"author_association":"MEMBER","original_position":375,"position":1,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2774854024","pull_request_review_id":3763876757,"id":2774854024,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs6lZOmI","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,1574 @@\n+# Unified Error System - Intention Document\n+\n+This document defines the architecture, rules, and implementation plan for a unified error handling system across the Hyperspot project. All REST API errors MUST have a GTS identifier, trace ID, and be registered in the types registry.\n+\n+## Table of Contents\n+\n+1. [Executive Summary](#executive-summary)\n+2. [Industry Research](#industry-research)\n+3. [Current State Analysis](#current-state-analysis)\n+4. [Requirements](#requirements)\n+5. [Implementation Rules](#implementation-rules)\n+6. [Migration Plan](#migration-plan)\n+7. [Examples](#examples)\n+8. [HTTP Headers](#http-headers)\n+9. [Security Considerations](#security-considerations)\n+10. [Appendix A: Error Category Definitions](#appendix-a-error-category-definitions)\n+11. [Appendix B: Retryable Error Guidelines](#appendix-b-retryable-error-guidelines)\n+12. [GTS System Errors Catalog](#gts-system-errors-catalog)\n+13. [References](#references)\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Executive Summary\n+\n+### Problem Statement\n+\n+The current error handling across Hyperspot modules is inconsistent:\n+- Some modules use `declare_errors!` macro with JSON catalogs\n+- Others define errors inline without GTS codes\n+- Errors are not registered in the types registry\n+- No standardized metadata/context fields\n+- Inconsistent trace ID propagation\n+\n+### Goals\n+\n+1. **Every REST API error** MUST have a valid GTS identifier\n+2. **Every error response** MUST include a trace ID for debugging\n+3. **All error types** MUST be registered in the types registry\n+4. **Consistent error schema** across all modules following RFC 9457\n+5. **Machine-readable error codes** for programmatic handling\n+6. **Error stack propagation** for nested service calls\n+\n+### Non-Goals\n+\n+- Changing internal domain error types (only API-facing errors)\n+- Modifying logging infrastructure\n+- Changing HTTP status code semantics\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Industry Research\n+\n+### How Major Tech Companies Handle Errors\n+\n+| Company | Standard | Key Features |\n+|---------|----------|--------------|\n+| **Google** | AIP-193 + gRPC Status | `reason` (UPPER_SNAKE_CASE), `domain` (service name), `metadata` (key-value context), `ErrorInfo`, `LocalizedMessage`, `Help` links |\n+| **Amazon AWS** | Custom JSON | `errorType`, `httpStatus`, `requestId`, `message`, custom error object serialization |\n+| **Twitter/X** | JSON with `errors` array | `code` (CAPS_CASE), `message`, `parameter`, `details`, `value` |\n+| **RFC 9457** | Problem Details | `type` (URI), `title`, `status`, `detail`, `instance`, extension members |\n+\n+### Key Patterns Identified\n+\n+1. **Machine-readable identifiers** - Unique codes for programmatic handling (Google's `reason`, Twitter's `code`)\n+2. **Domain/namespace separation** - Identify error source (Google's `domain`, our GTS vendor.package)\n+3. **Structured metadata** - Key-value context without parsing messages (Google's `ErrorInfo.metadata`)\n+4. **Trace/Request IDs** - Correlation for debugging (AWS `requestId`, our `trace_id`)\n+5. **Documentation links** - URIs to error documentation (RFC 9457 `type`, Google's `Help`)\n+6. **Error categorization** - System vs User-defined, Retryable vs Non-retryable\n+\n+### Google AIP-193 ErrorInfo Structure (Reference)\n+\n+```json\n+{\n+  \"error\": {\n+    \"code\": 429,\n+    \"message\": \"The zone 'us-east1-a' does not have enough resources...\",\n+    \"status\": \"RESOURCE_EXHAUSTED\",\n+    \"details\": [\n+      {\n+        \"@type\": \"type.googleapis.com/google.rpc.ErrorInfo\",\n+        \"reason\": \"RESOURCE_AVAILABILITY\",\n+        \"domain\": \"compute.googleapis.com\",\n+        \"metadata\": {\n+          \"zone\": \"us-east1-a\",\n+          \"vmType\": \"e2-medium\"\n+        }\n+      }\n+    ]\n+  }\n+}\n+```\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Current State Analysis\n+\n+### Existing Infrastructure\n+\n+1. **`Problem` struct** (`libs/modkit-errors/src/problem.rs`) - RFC 9457 compliant\n+   - Fields: `type_url`, `title`, `status`, `detail`, `instance`, `code`, `trace_id`, `errors`\n+   - Implements `IntoResponse` for Axum with automatic trace ID enrichment\n+\n+2. **`struct_to_gts_schema` macro** (`modules/types-registry/gts-rust/gts-macros/src/lib.rs`)\n+   - Attribute macro for explicit struct definitions with GTS IDs visible in code\n+   - Generates constants: `GTS_SCHEMA_ID`, `GTS_SCHEMA_JSON`, etc.\n+   - **This pattern will be adapted for error definitions**\n+\n+3. **`declare_errors!` macro** (`libs/modkit-errors-macro/src/lib.rs`) - **TO BE DEPRECATED**\n+   - Generates type-safe error enums from JSON catalogs\n+   - Problem: GTS IDs hidden in external JSON files, not visible to LLMs\n+   - Used by: `users_info` example, `modkit-odata`\n+\n+### Gaps Identified\n+\n+| Gap | Current State | Required State |\n+|-----|---------------|----------------|\n+| **Hidden GTS IDs** | JSON-based `declare_errors!` | Explicit `#[gts_error]` structs with visible GTS IDs |\n+| **Inconsistent definitions** | Some modules use inline errors | All modules use `#[gts_error]` structs |\n+| **No types registry** | Errors not registered | All errors registered as GTS types |\n+| **Missing metadata** | No structured context | Struct fields → `metadata` map |\n+| **Partial trace IDs** | Only in `IntoResponse` | Mandatory in all error responses |\n+| **No error categories** | Flat error codes | System/Operational/Client categories |\n+| **No error stack** | Single error | Upstream error chain propagation |\n+\n+### Current Module Migration Status\n+\n+| Module | Location | Status | Issues |\n+|--------|----------|--------|--------|\n+| **file_parser** | `modules/file_parser/` | 🔴 Not migrated | No GTS IDs, inline `Problem::new()` |\n+| **types-registry** | `modules/system/types-registry/` | 🟡 Partial | Has codes but not GTS format (e.g., `TYPES_REGISTRY_NOT_FOUND`) |\n+| **nodes_registry** | `modules/system/nodes_registry/` | 🔴 Not migrated | Non-GTS codes (e.g., `NODES_NOT_FOUND`) |\n+| **api_gateway** | `modules/system/api_gateway/` | 🔴 Not migrated | No Problem struct, simple error codes |\n+| **tenant_resolver** | `modules/system/tenant_resolver/` | 🔴 Not migrated | No GTS IDs |\n+| **simple-user-settings** | `modules/simple-user-settings/` | 🟡 Partial | Uses `declare_errors!` with old chain format |\n+| **modkit-auth** | `libs/modkit-auth/` | 🔴 Not migrated | No GTS IDs, custom `IntoResponse` |\n+| **modkit-odata** | `libs/modkit-odata/` | 🟡 Partial | Uses `declare_errors!` with old chain format |\n+| **users_info** (example) | `examples/modkit/users_info/` | 🟡 Partial | Uses `declare_errors!` with old chain format |\n+\n+#### Legend\n+- 🟢 **Migrated** - Uses `#[gts_error]` structs with proper base types\n+- 🟡 **Partial** - Has GTS IDs but uses deprecated `declare_errors!` or old format\n+- 🔴 **Not migrated** - No GTS IDs or non-GTS format codes\n+\n+#### GTS ID Format Note\n+\n+**Old chain format** (used by `declare_errors!`):\n+```\n+gts.hx.core.errors.err.v1~hx.module.error_name.v1\n+```\n+\n+**New format** (with `base` field):\n+```\n+gts.hx.module.namespace.error_name.v1~\n+```\n+The `base` field in `#[gts_error]` replaces the chain suffix, making inheritance explicit in code.\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Requirements\n+\n+### R1: Error Schema Requirements\n+\n+Every error returned from REST API MUST conform to the unified schema:\n+\n+```rust\n+pub struct Problem {\n+    // =========================================================================\n+    // REQUIRED FIELDS - Core error identification\n+    // =========================================================================\n+    \n+    /// URI reference identifying the problem type (GTS-based)\n+    /// Example: \"https://docs.hyperspot.com/errors/types_registry_entity_not_found_v1\"\n+    #[serde(rename = \"type\")]\n+    pub type_url: String,\n+    \n+    /// Human-readable summary of the problem type (static per error type)\n+    pub title: String,\n+    \n+    /// GTS error code (machine-readable identifier)\n+    pub code: String,\n+    \n+    /// Trace ID for request correlation\n+    pub trace_id: String,\n+    \n+    // =========================================================================\n+    // CONTEXTUAL FIELDS - Optional based on error context\n+    // =========================================================================\n+    \n+    /// HTTP status code. Optional because:\n+    /// - gRPC errors use different status codes\n+    /// - Internal/domain errors may not have HTTP context\n+    /// - Event-driven systems have no request/response\n+    /// When serializing for HTTP response, this is populated from error definition.\n+    #[serde(skip_serializing_if = \"Option::is_none\")]\n+    pub status: Option<u16>,\n+    \n+    /// Human-readable explanation specific to this occurrence.\n+    /// Optional - title may be sufficient for simple errors.\n+    #[serde(skip_serializing_if = \"Option::is_none\")]\n+    pub detail: Option<String>,\n+    \n+    /// Error category for client handling.\n+    /// Optional - can be inferred from base type hierarchy.\n+    #[serde(skip_serializing_if = \"Option::is_none\")]\n+    pub category: Option<ErrorCategory>,","path":"intended_design/UNIFIED_ERROR_SYSTEM.md","commit_id":"5bdb0f43b25858af78999718f7247813802b9634","original_commit_id":"5bdb0f43b25858af78999718f7247813802b9634","user":{"login":"alizid10","id":247960800,"node_id":"U_kgDODseU4A","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/247960800?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/alizid10","html_url":"https://github.com/alizid10","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alizid10/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alizid10/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alizid10/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alizid10/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alizid10/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alizid10/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alizid10/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alizid10/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alizid10/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"removed","created_at":"2026-02-06T16:01:31Z","updated_at":"2026-02-06T16:01:31Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/290#discussion_r2774854024","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/290","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2774854024"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/290#discussion_r2774854024"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/290"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2774854024/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":null,"original_line":206,"side":"RIGHT","in_reply_to_id":2747889953,"author_association":"MEMBER","original_position":206,"position":1,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2774854571","pull_request_review_id":3763877315,"id":2774854571,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs6lZOur","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,1574 @@\n+# Unified Error System - Intention Document\n+\n+This document defines the architecture, rules, and implementation plan for a unified error handling system across the Hyperspot project. All REST API errors MUST have a GTS identifier, trace ID, and be registered in the types registry.\n+\n+## Table of Contents\n+\n+1. [Executive Summary](#executive-summary)\n+2. [Industry Research](#industry-research)\n+3. [Current State Analysis](#current-state-analysis)\n+4. [Requirements](#requirements)\n+5. [Implementation Rules](#implementation-rules)\n+6. [Migration Plan](#migration-plan)\n+7. [Examples](#examples)\n+8. [HTTP Headers](#http-headers)\n+9. [Security Considerations](#security-considerations)\n+10. [Appendix A: Error Category Definitions](#appendix-a-error-category-definitions)\n+11. [Appendix B: Retryable Error Guidelines](#appendix-b-retryable-error-guidelines)\n+12. [GTS System Errors Catalog](#gts-system-errors-catalog)\n+13. [References](#references)\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Executive Summary\n+\n+### Problem Statement\n+\n+The current error handling across Hyperspot modules is inconsistent:\n+- Some modules use `declare_errors!` macro with JSON catalogs\n+- Others define errors inline without GTS codes\n+- Errors are not registered in the types registry\n+- No standardized metadata/context fields\n+- Inconsistent trace ID propagation\n+\n+### Goals\n+\n+1. **Every REST API error** MUST have a valid GTS identifier\n+2. **Every error response** MUST include a trace ID for debugging\n+3. **All error types** MUST be registered in the types registry\n+4. **Consistent error schema** across all modules following RFC 9457\n+5. **Machine-readable error codes** for programmatic handling\n+6. **Error stack propagation** for nested service calls\n+\n+### Non-Goals\n+\n+- Changing internal domain error types (only API-facing errors)\n+- Modifying logging infrastructure\n+- Changing HTTP status code semantics\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Industry Research\n+\n+### How Major Tech Companies Handle Errors\n+\n+| Company | Standard | Key Features |\n+|---------|----------|--------------|\n+| **Google** | AIP-193 + gRPC Status | `reason` (UPPER_SNAKE_CASE), `domain` (service name), `metadata` (key-value context), `ErrorInfo`, `LocalizedMessage`, `Help` links |\n+| **Amazon AWS** | Custom JSON | `errorType`, `httpStatus`, `requestId`, `message`, custom error object serialization |\n+| **Twitter/X** | JSON with `errors` array | `code` (CAPS_CASE), `message`, `parameter`, `details`, `value` |\n+| **RFC 9457** | Problem Details | `type` (URI), `title`, `status`, `detail`, `instance`, extension members |\n+\n+### Key Patterns Identified\n+\n+1. **Machine-readable identifiers** - Unique codes for programmatic handling (Google's `reason`, Twitter's `code`)\n+2. **Domain/namespace separation** - Identify error source (Google's `domain`, our GTS vendor.package)\n+3. **Structured metadata** - Key-value context without parsing messages (Google's `ErrorInfo.metadata`)\n+4. **Trace/Request IDs** - Correlation for debugging (AWS `requestId`, our `trace_id`)\n+5. **Documentation links** - URIs to error documentation (RFC 9457 `type`, Google's `Help`)\n+6. **Error categorization** - System vs User-defined, Retryable vs Non-retryable\n+\n+### Google AIP-193 ErrorInfo Structure (Reference)\n+\n+```json\n+{\n+  \"error\": {\n+    \"code\": 429,\n+    \"message\": \"The zone 'us-east1-a' does not have enough resources...\",\n+    \"status\": \"RESOURCE_EXHAUSTED\",\n+    \"details\": [\n+      {\n+        \"@type\": \"type.googleapis.com/google.rpc.ErrorInfo\",\n+        \"reason\": \"RESOURCE_AVAILABILITY\",\n+        \"domain\": \"compute.googleapis.com\",\n+        \"metadata\": {\n+          \"zone\": \"us-east1-a\",\n+          \"vmType\": \"e2-medium\"\n+        }\n+      }\n+    ]\n+  }\n+}\n+```\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Current State Analysis\n+\n+### Existing Infrastructure\n+\n+1. **`Problem` struct** (`libs/modkit-errors/src/problem.rs`) - RFC 9457 compliant\n+   - Fields: `type_url`, `title`, `status`, `detail`, `instance`, `code`, `trace_id`, `errors`\n+   - Implements `IntoResponse` for Axum with automatic trace ID enrichment\n+\n+2. **`struct_to_gts_schema` macro** (`modules/types-registry/gts-rust/gts-macros/src/lib.rs`)\n+   - Attribute macro for explicit struct definitions with GTS IDs visible in code\n+   - Generates constants: `GTS_SCHEMA_ID`, `GTS_SCHEMA_JSON`, etc.\n+   - **This pattern will be adapted for error definitions**\n+\n+3. **`declare_errors!` macro** (`libs/modkit-errors-macro/src/lib.rs`) - **TO BE DEPRECATED**\n+   - Generates type-safe error enums from JSON catalogs\n+   - Problem: GTS IDs hidden in external JSON files, not visible to LLMs\n+   - Used by: `users_info` example, `modkit-odata`\n+\n+### Gaps Identified\n+\n+| Gap | Current State | Required State |\n+|-----|---------------|----------------|\n+| **Hidden GTS IDs** | JSON-based `declare_errors!` | Explicit `#[gts_error]` structs with visible GTS IDs |\n+| **Inconsistent definitions** | Some modules use inline errors | All modules use `#[gts_error]` structs |\n+| **No types registry** | Errors not registered | All errors registered as GTS types |\n+| **Missing metadata** | No structured context | Struct fields → `metadata` map |\n+| **Partial trace IDs** | Only in `IntoResponse` | Mandatory in all error responses |\n+| **No error categories** | Flat error codes | System/Operational/Client categories |\n+| **No error stack** | Single error | Upstream error chain propagation |\n+\n+### Current Module Migration Status\n+\n+| Module | Location | Status | Issues |\n+|--------|----------|--------|--------|\n+| **file_parser** | `modules/file_parser/` | 🔴 Not migrated | No GTS IDs, inline `Problem::new()` |\n+| **types-registry** | `modules/system/types-registry/` | 🟡 Partial | Has codes but not GTS format (e.g., `TYPES_REGISTRY_NOT_FOUND`) |\n+| **nodes_registry** | `modules/system/nodes_registry/` | 🔴 Not migrated | Non-GTS codes (e.g., `NODES_NOT_FOUND`) |\n+| **api_gateway** | `modules/system/api_gateway/` | 🔴 Not migrated | No Problem struct, simple error codes |\n+| **tenant_resolver** | `modules/system/tenant_resolver/` | 🔴 Not migrated | No GTS IDs |\n+| **simple-user-settings** | `modules/simple-user-settings/` | 🟡 Partial | Uses `declare_errors!` with old chain format |\n+| **modkit-auth** | `libs/modkit-auth/` | 🔴 Not migrated | No GTS IDs, custom `IntoResponse` |\n+| **modkit-odata** | `libs/modkit-odata/` | 🟡 Partial | Uses `declare_errors!` with old chain format |\n+| **users_info** (example) | `examples/modkit/users_info/` | 🟡 Partial | Uses `declare_errors!` with old chain format |\n+\n+#### Legend\n+- 🟢 **Migrated** - Uses `#[gts_error]` structs with proper base types\n+- 🟡 **Partial** - Has GTS IDs but uses deprecated `declare_errors!` or old format\n+- 🔴 **Not migrated** - No GTS IDs or non-GTS format codes\n+\n+#### GTS ID Format Note\n+\n+**Old chain format** (used by `declare_errors!`):\n+```\n+gts.hx.core.errors.err.v1~hx.module.error_name.v1\n+```\n+\n+**New format** (with `base` field):\n+```\n+gts.hx.module.namespace.error_name.v1~\n+```\n+The `base` field in `#[gts_error]` replaces the chain suffix, making inheritance explicit in code.\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Requirements\n+\n+### R1: Error Schema Requirements\n+\n+Every error returned from REST API MUST conform to the unified schema:\n+\n+```rust\n+pub struct Problem {\n+    // =========================================================================\n+    // REQUIRED FIELDS - Core error identification\n+    // =========================================================================\n+    \n+    /// URI reference identifying the problem type (GTS-based)\n+    /// Example: \"https://docs.hyperspot.com/errors/types_registry_entity_not_found_v1\"\n+    #[serde(rename = \"type\")]\n+    pub type_url: String,\n+    \n+    /// Human-readable summary of the problem type (static per error type)\n+    pub title: String,\n+    \n+    /// GTS error code (machine-readable identifier)\n+    pub code: String,\n+    \n+    /// Trace ID for request correlation\n+    pub trace_id: String,\n+    \n+    // =========================================================================\n+    // CONTEXTUAL FIELDS - Optional based on error context\n+    // =========================================================================\n+    \n+    /// HTTP status code. Optional because:\n+    /// - gRPC errors use different status codes\n+    /// - Internal/domain errors may not have HTTP context\n+    /// - Event-driven systems have no request/response\n+    /// When serializing for HTTP response, this is populated from error definition.\n+    #[serde(skip_serializing_if = \"Option::is_none\")]\n+    pub status: Option<u16>,\n+    \n+    /// Human-readable explanation specific to this occurrence.\n+    /// Optional - title may be sufficient for simple errors.\n+    #[serde(skip_serializing_if = \"Option::is_none\")]\n+    pub detail: Option<String>,\n+    \n+    /// Error category for client handling.\n+    /// Optional - can be inferred from base type hierarchy.\n+    #[serde(skip_serializing_if = \"Option::is_none\")]\n+    pub category: Option<ErrorCategory>,\n+    \n+    /// Whether client can retry this request.\n+    /// Optional - can be inferred from base type; not relevant for all contexts.\n+    #[serde(skip_serializing_if = \"Option::is_none\")]\n+    pub retryable: Option<bool>,\n+    \n+    /// URI identifying this specific occurrence (auto-populated from request path)\n+    #[serde(skip_serializing_if = \"Option::is_none\")]\n+    pub instance: Option<String>,","path":"intended_design/UNIFIED_ERROR_SYSTEM.md","commit_id":"5bdb0f43b25858af78999718f7247813802b9634","original_commit_id":"5bdb0f43b25858af78999718f7247813802b9634","user":{"login":"alizid10","id":247960800,"node_id":"U_kgDODseU4A","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/247960800?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/alizid10","html_url":"https://github.com/alizid10","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alizid10/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alizid10/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alizid10/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alizid10/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alizid10/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alizid10/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alizid10/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alizid10/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alizid10/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"removed","created_at":"2026-02-06T16:01:39Z","updated_at":"2026-02-06T16:01:39Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/290#discussion_r2774854571","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/290","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2774854571"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/290#discussion_r2774854571"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/290"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2774854571/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":null,"original_line":215,"side":"RIGHT","in_reply_to_id":2747910208,"author_association":"MEMBER","original_position":215,"position":1,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2774855114","pull_request_review_id":3763877824,"id":2774855114,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs6lZO3K","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,1574 @@\n+# Unified Error System - Intention Document\n+\n+This document defines the architecture, rules, and implementation plan for a unified error handling system across the Hyperspot project. All REST API errors MUST have a GTS identifier, trace ID, and be registered in the types registry.\n+\n+## Table of Contents\n+\n+1. [Executive Summary](#executive-summary)\n+2. [Industry Research](#industry-research)\n+3. [Current State Analysis](#current-state-analysis)\n+4. [Requirements](#requirements)\n+5. [Implementation Rules](#implementation-rules)\n+6. [Migration Plan](#migration-plan)\n+7. [Examples](#examples)\n+8. [HTTP Headers](#http-headers)\n+9. [Security Considerations](#security-considerations)\n+10. [Appendix A: Error Category Definitions](#appendix-a-error-category-definitions)\n+11. [Appendix B: Retryable Error Guidelines](#appendix-b-retryable-error-guidelines)\n+12. [GTS System Errors Catalog](#gts-system-errors-catalog)\n+13. [References](#references)\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Executive Summary\n+\n+### Problem Statement\n+\n+The current error handling across Hyperspot modules is inconsistent:\n+- Some modules use `declare_errors!` macro with JSON catalogs\n+- Others define errors inline without GTS codes\n+- Errors are not registered in the types registry\n+- No standardized metadata/context fields\n+- Inconsistent trace ID propagation\n+\n+### Goals\n+\n+1. **Every REST API error** MUST have a valid GTS identifier\n+2. **Every error response** MUST include a trace ID for debugging\n+3. **All error types** MUST be registered in the types registry\n+4. **Consistent error schema** across all modules following RFC 9457\n+5. **Machine-readable error codes** for programmatic handling\n+6. **Error stack propagation** for nested service calls\n+\n+### Non-Goals\n+\n+- Changing internal domain error types (only API-facing errors)\n+- Modifying logging infrastructure\n+- Changing HTTP status code semantics\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Industry Research\n+\n+### How Major Tech Companies Handle Errors\n+\n+| Company | Standard | Key Features |\n+|---------|----------|--------------|\n+| **Google** | AIP-193 + gRPC Status | `reason` (UPPER_SNAKE_CASE), `domain` (service name), `metadata` (key-value context), `ErrorInfo`, `LocalizedMessage`, `Help` links |\n+| **Amazon AWS** | Custom JSON | `errorType`, `httpStatus`, `requestId`, `message`, custom error object serialization |\n+| **Twitter/X** | JSON with `errors` array | `code` (CAPS_CASE), `message`, `parameter`, `details`, `value` |\n+| **RFC 9457** | Problem Details | `type` (URI), `title`, `status`, `detail`, `instance`, extension members |\n+\n+### Key Patterns Identified\n+\n+1. **Machine-readable identifiers** - Unique codes for programmatic handling (Google's `reason`, Twitter's `code`)\n+2. **Domain/namespace separation** - Identify error source (Google's `domain`, our GTS vendor.package)\n+3. **Structured metadata** - Key-value context without parsing messages (Google's `ErrorInfo.metadata`)\n+4. **Trace/Request IDs** - Correlation for debugging (AWS `requestId`, our `trace_id`)\n+5. **Documentation links** - URIs to error documentation (RFC 9457 `type`, Google's `Help`)\n+6. **Error categorization** - System vs User-defined, Retryable vs Non-retryable\n+\n+### Google AIP-193 ErrorInfo Structure (Reference)\n+\n+```json\n+{\n+  \"error\": {\n+    \"code\": 429,\n+    \"message\": \"The zone 'us-east1-a' does not have enough resources...\",\n+    \"status\": \"RESOURCE_EXHAUSTED\",\n+    \"details\": [\n+      {\n+        \"@type\": \"type.googleapis.com/google.rpc.ErrorInfo\",\n+        \"reason\": \"RESOURCE_AVAILABILITY\",\n+        \"domain\": \"compute.googleapis.com\",\n+        \"metadata\": {\n+          \"zone\": \"us-east1-a\",\n+          \"vmType\": \"e2-medium\"\n+        }\n+      }\n+    ]\n+  }\n+}\n+```\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Current State Analysis\n+\n+### Existing Infrastructure\n+\n+1. **`Problem` struct** (`libs/modkit-errors/src/problem.rs`) - RFC 9457 compliant\n+   - Fields: `type_url`, `title`, `status`, `detail`, `instance`, `code`, `trace_id`, `errors`\n+   - Implements `IntoResponse` for Axum with automatic trace ID enrichment\n+\n+2. **`struct_to_gts_schema` macro** (`modules/types-registry/gts-rust/gts-macros/src/lib.rs`)\n+   - Attribute macro for explicit struct definitions with GTS IDs visible in code\n+   - Generates constants: `GTS_SCHEMA_ID`, `GTS_SCHEMA_JSON`, etc.\n+   - **This pattern will be adapted for error definitions**\n+\n+3. **`declare_errors!` macro** (`libs/modkit-errors-macro/src/lib.rs`) - **TO BE DEPRECATED**\n+   - Generates type-safe error enums from JSON catalogs\n+   - Problem: GTS IDs hidden in external JSON files, not visible to LLMs\n+   - Used by: `users_info` example, `modkit-odata`\n+\n+### Gaps Identified\n+\n+| Gap | Current State | Required State |\n+|-----|---------------|----------------|\n+| **Hidden GTS IDs** | JSON-based `declare_errors!` | Explicit `#[gts_error]` structs with visible GTS IDs |\n+| **Inconsistent definitions** | Some modules use inline errors | All modules use `#[gts_error]` structs |\n+| **No types registry** | Errors not registered | All errors registered as GTS types |\n+| **Missing metadata** | No structured context | Struct fields → `metadata` map |\n+| **Partial trace IDs** | Only in `IntoResponse` | Mandatory in all error responses |\n+| **No error categories** | Flat error codes | System/Operational/Client categories |\n+| **No error stack** | Single error | Upstream error chain propagation |\n+\n+### Current Module Migration Status\n+\n+| Module | Location | Status | Issues |\n+|--------|----------|--------|--------|\n+| **file_parser** | `modules/file_parser/` | 🔴 Not migrated | No GTS IDs, inline `Problem::new()` |\n+| **types-registry** | `modules/system/types-registry/` | 🟡 Partial | Has codes but not GTS format (e.g., `TYPES_REGISTRY_NOT_FOUND`) |\n+| **nodes_registry** | `modules/system/nodes_registry/` | 🔴 Not migrated | Non-GTS codes (e.g., `NODES_NOT_FOUND`) |\n+| **api_gateway** | `modules/system/api_gateway/` | 🔴 Not migrated | No Problem struct, simple error codes |\n+| **tenant_resolver** | `modules/system/tenant_resolver/` | 🔴 Not migrated | No GTS IDs |\n+| **simple-user-settings** | `modules/simple-user-settings/` | 🟡 Partial | Uses `declare_errors!` with old chain format |\n+| **modkit-auth** | `libs/modkit-auth/` | 🔴 Not migrated | No GTS IDs, custom `IntoResponse` |\n+| **modkit-odata** | `libs/modkit-odata/` | 🟡 Partial | Uses `declare_errors!` with old chain format |\n+| **users_info** (example) | `examples/modkit/users_info/` | 🟡 Partial | Uses `declare_errors!` with old chain format |\n+\n+#### Legend\n+- 🟢 **Migrated** - Uses `#[gts_error]` structs with proper base types\n+- 🟡 **Partial** - Has GTS IDs but uses deprecated `declare_errors!` or old format\n+- 🔴 **Not migrated** - No GTS IDs or non-GTS format codes\n+\n+#### GTS ID Format Note\n+\n+**Old chain format** (used by `declare_errors!`):\n+```\n+gts.hx.core.errors.err.v1~hx.module.error_name.v1\n+```\n+\n+**New format** (with `base` field):\n+```\n+gts.hx.module.namespace.error_name.v1~\n+```\n+The `base` field in `#[gts_error]` replaces the chain suffix, making inheritance explicit in code.\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Requirements\n+\n+### R1: Error Schema Requirements\n+\n+Every error returned from REST API MUST conform to the unified schema:\n+\n+```rust\n+pub struct Problem {\n+    // =========================================================================\n+    // REQUIRED FIELDS - Core error identification\n+    // =========================================================================\n+    \n+    /// URI reference identifying the problem type (GTS-based)\n+    /// Example: \"https://docs.hyperspot.com/errors/types_registry_entity_not_found_v1\"","path":"intended_design/UNIFIED_ERROR_SYSTEM.md","commit_id":"5bdb0f43b25858af78999718f7247813802b9634","original_commit_id":"5bdb0f43b25858af78999718f7247813802b9634","user":{"login":"alizid10","id":247960800,"node_id":"U_kgDODseU4A","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/247960800?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/alizid10","html_url":"https://github.com/alizid10","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alizid10/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alizid10/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alizid10/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alizid10/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alizid10/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alizid10/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alizid10/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alizid10/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alizid10/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"done","created_at":"2026-02-06T16:01:46Z","updated_at":"2026-02-06T16:01:46Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/290#discussion_r2774855114","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/290","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2774855114"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/290#discussion_r2774855114"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/290"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2774855114/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":null,"original_line":173,"side":"RIGHT","in_reply_to_id":2747915573,"author_association":"MEMBER","original_position":173,"position":1,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2774855802","pull_request_review_id":3763878591,"id":2774855802,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs6lZPB6","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,1574 @@\n+# Unified Error System - Intention Document\n+\n+This document defines the architecture, rules, and implementation plan for a unified error handling system across the Hyperspot project. All REST API errors MUST have a GTS identifier, trace ID, and be registered in the types registry.\n+\n+## Table of Contents\n+\n+1. [Executive Summary](#executive-summary)\n+2. [Industry Research](#industry-research)\n+3. [Current State Analysis](#current-state-analysis)\n+4. [Requirements](#requirements)\n+5. [Implementation Rules](#implementation-rules)\n+6. [Migration Plan](#migration-plan)\n+7. [Examples](#examples)\n+8. [HTTP Headers](#http-headers)\n+9. [Security Considerations](#security-considerations)\n+10. [Appendix A: Error Category Definitions](#appendix-a-error-category-definitions)\n+11. [Appendix B: Retryable Error Guidelines](#appendix-b-retryable-error-guidelines)\n+12. [GTS System Errors Catalog](#gts-system-errors-catalog)\n+13. [References](#references)\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Executive Summary\n+\n+### Problem Statement\n+\n+The current error handling across Hyperspot modules is inconsistent:\n+- Some modules use `declare_errors!` macro with JSON catalogs\n+- Others define errors inline without GTS codes\n+- Errors are not registered in the types registry\n+- No standardized metadata/context fields\n+- Inconsistent trace ID propagation\n+\n+### Goals\n+\n+1. **Every REST API error** MUST have a valid GTS identifier\n+2. **Every error response** MUST include a trace ID for debugging\n+3. **All error types** MUST be registered in the types registry\n+4. **Consistent error schema** across all modules following RFC 9457\n+5. **Machine-readable error codes** for programmatic handling\n+6. **Error stack propagation** for nested service calls\n+\n+### Non-Goals\n+\n+- Changing internal domain error types (only API-facing errors)\n+- Modifying logging infrastructure\n+- Changing HTTP status code semantics\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Industry Research\n+\n+### How Major Tech Companies Handle Errors\n+\n+| Company | Standard | Key Features |\n+|---------|----------|--------------|\n+| **Google** | AIP-193 + gRPC Status | `reason` (UPPER_SNAKE_CASE), `domain` (service name), `metadata` (key-value context), `ErrorInfo`, `LocalizedMessage`, `Help` links |\n+| **Amazon AWS** | Custom JSON | `errorType`, `httpStatus`, `requestId`, `message`, custom error object serialization |\n+| **Twitter/X** | JSON with `errors` array | `code` (CAPS_CASE), `message`, `parameter`, `details`, `value` |\n+| **RFC 9457** | Problem Details | `type` (URI), `title`, `status`, `detail`, `instance`, extension members |\n+\n+### Key Patterns Identified\n+\n+1. **Machine-readable identifiers** - Unique codes for programmatic handling (Google's `reason`, Twitter's `code`)\n+2. **Domain/namespace separation** - Identify error source (Google's `domain`, our GTS vendor.package)\n+3. **Structured metadata** - Key-value context without parsing messages (Google's `ErrorInfo.metadata`)\n+4. **Trace/Request IDs** - Correlation for debugging (AWS `requestId`, our `trace_id`)\n+5. **Documentation links** - URIs to error documentation (RFC 9457 `type`, Google's `Help`)\n+6. **Error categorization** - System vs User-defined, Retryable vs Non-retryable\n+\n+### Google AIP-193 ErrorInfo Structure (Reference)\n+\n+```json\n+{\n+  \"error\": {\n+    \"code\": 429,\n+    \"message\": \"The zone 'us-east1-a' does not have enough resources...\",\n+    \"status\": \"RESOURCE_EXHAUSTED\",\n+    \"details\": [\n+      {\n+        \"@type\": \"type.googleapis.com/google.rpc.ErrorInfo\",\n+        \"reason\": \"RESOURCE_AVAILABILITY\",\n+        \"domain\": \"compute.googleapis.com\",\n+        \"metadata\": {\n+          \"zone\": \"us-east1-a\",\n+          \"vmType\": \"e2-medium\"\n+        }\n+      }\n+    ]\n+  }\n+}\n+```\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Current State Analysis\n+\n+### Existing Infrastructure\n+\n+1. **`Problem` struct** (`libs/modkit-errors/src/problem.rs`) - RFC 9457 compliant\n+   - Fields: `type_url`, `title`, `status`, `detail`, `instance`, `code`, `trace_id`, `errors`\n+   - Implements `IntoResponse` for Axum with automatic trace ID enrichment\n+\n+2. **`struct_to_gts_schema` macro** (`modules/types-registry/gts-rust/gts-macros/src/lib.rs`)\n+   - Attribute macro for explicit struct definitions with GTS IDs visible in code\n+   - Generates constants: `GTS_SCHEMA_ID`, `GTS_SCHEMA_JSON`, etc.\n+   - **This pattern will be adapted for error definitions**\n+\n+3. **`declare_errors!` macro** (`libs/modkit-errors-macro/src/lib.rs`) - **TO BE DEPRECATED**\n+   - Generates type-safe error enums from JSON catalogs\n+   - Problem: GTS IDs hidden in external JSON files, not visible to LLMs\n+   - Used by: `users_info` example, `modkit-odata`\n+\n+### Gaps Identified\n+\n+| Gap | Current State | Required State |\n+|-----|---------------|----------------|\n+| **Hidden GTS IDs** | JSON-based `declare_errors!` | Explicit `#[gts_error]` structs with visible GTS IDs |\n+| **Inconsistent definitions** | Some modules use inline errors | All modules use `#[gts_error]` structs |\n+| **No types registry** | Errors not registered | All errors registered as GTS types |\n+| **Missing metadata** | No structured context | Struct fields → `metadata` map |\n+| **Partial trace IDs** | Only in `IntoResponse` | Mandatory in all error responses |\n+| **No error categories** | Flat error codes | System/Operational/Client categories |\n+| **No error stack** | Single error | Upstream error chain propagation |\n+\n+### Current Module Migration Status\n+\n+| Module | Location | Status | Issues |\n+|--------|----------|--------|--------|\n+| **file_parser** | `modules/file_parser/` | 🔴 Not migrated | No GTS IDs, inline `Problem::new()` |\n+| **types-registry** | `modules/system/types-registry/` | 🟡 Partial | Has codes but not GTS format (e.g., `TYPES_REGISTRY_NOT_FOUND`) |\n+| **nodes_registry** | `modules/system/nodes_registry/` | 🔴 Not migrated | Non-GTS codes (e.g., `NODES_NOT_FOUND`) |\n+| **api_gateway** | `modules/system/api_gateway/` | 🔴 Not migrated | No Problem struct, simple error codes |\n+| **tenant_resolver** | `modules/system/tenant_resolver/` | 🔴 Not migrated | No GTS IDs |\n+| **simple-user-settings** | `modules/simple-user-settings/` | 🟡 Partial | Uses `declare_errors!` with old chain format |\n+| **modkit-auth** | `libs/modkit-auth/` | 🔴 Not migrated | No GTS IDs, custom `IntoResponse` |\n+| **modkit-odata** | `libs/modkit-odata/` | 🟡 Partial | Uses `declare_errors!` with old chain format |\n+| **users_info** (example) | `examples/modkit/users_info/` | 🟡 Partial | Uses `declare_errors!` with old chain format |\n+\n+#### Legend\n+- 🟢 **Migrated** - Uses `#[gts_error]` structs with proper base types\n+- 🟡 **Partial** - Has GTS IDs but uses deprecated `declare_errors!` or old format\n+- 🔴 **Not migrated** - No GTS IDs or non-GTS format codes\n+\n+#### GTS ID Format Note\n+\n+**Old chain format** (used by `declare_errors!`):\n+```\n+gts.hx.core.errors.err.v1~hx.module.error_name.v1\n+```\n+\n+**New format** (with `base` field):\n+```\n+gts.hx.module.namespace.error_name.v1~\n+```\n+The `base` field in `#[gts_error]` replaces the chain suffix, making inheritance explicit in code.\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Requirements\n+\n+### R1: Error Schema Requirements\n+\n+Every error returned from REST API MUST conform to the unified schema:\n+\n+```rust\n+pub struct Problem {\n+    // =========================================================================\n+    // REQUIRED FIELDS - Core error identification\n+    // =========================================================================\n+    \n+    /// URI reference identifying the problem type (GTS-based)\n+    /// Example: \"https://docs.hyperspot.com/errors/types_registry_entity_not_found_v1\"\n+    #[serde(rename = \"type\")]\n+    pub type_url: String,\n+    \n+    /// Human-readable summary of the problem type (static per error type)\n+    pub title: String,\n+    \n+    /// GTS error code (machine-readable identifier)\n+    pub code: String,\n+    \n+    /// Trace ID for request correlation\n+    pub trace_id: String,\n+    \n+    // =========================================================================\n+    // CONTEXTUAL FIELDS - Optional based on error context\n+    // =========================================================================\n+    \n+    /// HTTP status code. Optional because:\n+    /// - gRPC errors use different status codes\n+    /// - Internal/domain errors may not have HTTP context\n+    /// - Event-driven systems have no request/response\n+    /// When serializing for HTTP response, this is populated from error definition.\n+    #[serde(skip_serializing_if = \"Option::is_none\")]\n+    pub status: Option<u16>,\n+    \n+    /// Human-readable explanation specific to this occurrence.\n+    /// Optional - title may be sufficient for simple errors.\n+    #[serde(skip_serializing_if = \"Option::is_none\")]\n+    pub detail: Option<String>,\n+    \n+    /// Error category for client handling.\n+    /// Optional - can be inferred from base type hierarchy.\n+    #[serde(skip_serializing_if = \"Option::is_none\")]\n+    pub category: Option<ErrorCategory>,\n+    \n+    /// Whether client can retry this request.\n+    /// Optional - can be inferred from base type; not relevant for all contexts.\n+    #[serde(skip_serializing_if = \"Option::is_none\")]\n+    pub retryable: Option<bool>,","path":"intended_design/UNIFIED_ERROR_SYSTEM.md","commit_id":"5bdb0f43b25858af78999718f7247813802b9634","original_commit_id":"5bdb0f43b25858af78999718f7247813802b9634","user":{"login":"alizid10","id":247960800,"node_id":"U_kgDODseU4A","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/247960800?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/alizid10","html_url":"https://github.com/alizid10","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alizid10/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alizid10/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alizid10/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alizid10/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alizid10/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alizid10/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alizid10/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alizid10/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alizid10/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"agree, removed","created_at":"2026-02-06T16:01:57Z","updated_at":"2026-02-06T16:01:57Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/290#discussion_r2774855802","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/290","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2774855802"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/290#discussion_r2774855802"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/290"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2774855802/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":null,"original_line":211,"side":"RIGHT","in_reply_to_id":2747933453,"author_association":"MEMBER","original_position":211,"position":1,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2774859550","pull_request_review_id":3763882443,"id":2774859550,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs6lZP8e","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,1574 @@\n+# Unified Error System - Intention Document\n+\n+This document defines the architecture, rules, and implementation plan for a unified error handling system across the Hyperspot project. All REST API errors MUST have a GTS identifier, trace ID, and be registered in the types registry.\n+\n+## Table of Contents\n+\n+1. [Executive Summary](#executive-summary)\n+2. [Industry Research](#industry-research)\n+3. [Current State Analysis](#current-state-analysis)\n+4. [Requirements](#requirements)\n+5. [Implementation Rules](#implementation-rules)\n+6. [Migration Plan](#migration-plan)\n+7. [Examples](#examples)\n+8. [HTTP Headers](#http-headers)\n+9. [Security Considerations](#security-considerations)\n+10. [Appendix A: Error Category Definitions](#appendix-a-error-category-definitions)\n+11. [Appendix B: Retryable Error Guidelines](#appendix-b-retryable-error-guidelines)\n+12. [GTS System Errors Catalog](#gts-system-errors-catalog)\n+13. [References](#references)\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Executive Summary\n+\n+### Problem Statement\n+\n+The current error handling across Hyperspot modules is inconsistent:\n+- Some modules use `declare_errors!` macro with JSON catalogs\n+- Others define errors inline without GTS codes\n+- Errors are not registered in the types registry\n+- No standardized metadata/context fields\n+- Inconsistent trace ID propagation\n+\n+### Goals\n+\n+1. **Every REST API error** MUST have a valid GTS identifier\n+2. **Every error response** MUST include a trace ID for debugging\n+3. **All error types** MUST be registered in the types registry\n+4. **Consistent error schema** across all modules following RFC 9457\n+5. **Machine-readable error codes** for programmatic handling\n+6. **Error stack propagation** for nested service calls\n+\n+### Non-Goals\n+\n+- Changing internal domain error types (only API-facing errors)\n+- Modifying logging infrastructure\n+- Changing HTTP status code semantics\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Industry Research\n+\n+### How Major Tech Companies Handle Errors\n+\n+| Company | Standard | Key Features |\n+|---------|----------|--------------|\n+| **Google** | AIP-193 + gRPC Status | `reason` (UPPER_SNAKE_CASE), `domain` (service name), `metadata` (key-value context), `ErrorInfo`, `LocalizedMessage`, `Help` links |\n+| **Amazon AWS** | Custom JSON | `errorType`, `httpStatus`, `requestId`, `message`, custom error object serialization |\n+| **Twitter/X** | JSON with `errors` array | `code` (CAPS_CASE), `message`, `parameter`, `details`, `value` |\n+| **RFC 9457** | Problem Details | `type` (URI), `title`, `status`, `detail`, `instance`, extension members |\n+\n+### Key Patterns Identified\n+\n+1. **Machine-readable identifiers** - Unique codes for programmatic handling (Google's `reason`, Twitter's `code`)\n+2. **Domain/namespace separation** - Identify error source (Google's `domain`, our GTS vendor.package)\n+3. **Structured metadata** - Key-value context without parsing messages (Google's `ErrorInfo.metadata`)\n+4. **Trace/Request IDs** - Correlation for debugging (AWS `requestId`, our `trace_id`)\n+5. **Documentation links** - URIs to error documentation (RFC 9457 `type`, Google's `Help`)\n+6. **Error categorization** - System vs User-defined, Retryable vs Non-retryable\n+\n+### Google AIP-193 ErrorInfo Structure (Reference)\n+\n+```json\n+{\n+  \"error\": {\n+    \"code\": 429,\n+    \"message\": \"The zone 'us-east1-a' does not have enough resources...\",\n+    \"status\": \"RESOURCE_EXHAUSTED\",\n+    \"details\": [\n+      {\n+        \"@type\": \"type.googleapis.com/google.rpc.ErrorInfo\",\n+        \"reason\": \"RESOURCE_AVAILABILITY\",\n+        \"domain\": \"compute.googleapis.com\",\n+        \"metadata\": {\n+          \"zone\": \"us-east1-a\",\n+          \"vmType\": \"e2-medium\"\n+        }\n+      }\n+    ]\n+  }\n+}\n+```\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Current State Analysis\n+\n+### Existing Infrastructure\n+\n+1. **`Problem` struct** (`libs/modkit-errors/src/problem.rs`) - RFC 9457 compliant\n+   - Fields: `type_url`, `title`, `status`, `detail`, `instance`, `code`, `trace_id`, `errors`\n+   - Implements `IntoResponse` for Axum with automatic trace ID enrichment\n+\n+2. **`struct_to_gts_schema` macro** (`modules/types-registry/gts-rust/gts-macros/src/lib.rs`)\n+   - Attribute macro for explicit struct definitions with GTS IDs visible in code\n+   - Generates constants: `GTS_SCHEMA_ID`, `GTS_SCHEMA_JSON`, etc.\n+   - **This pattern will be adapted for error definitions**\n+\n+3. **`declare_errors!` macro** (`libs/modkit-errors-macro/src/lib.rs`) - **TO BE DEPRECATED**\n+   - Generates type-safe error enums from JSON catalogs\n+   - Problem: GTS IDs hidden in external JSON files, not visible to LLMs\n+   - Used by: `users_info` example, `modkit-odata`\n+\n+### Gaps Identified\n+\n+| Gap | Current State | Required State |\n+|-----|---------------|----------------|\n+| **Hidden GTS IDs** | JSON-based `declare_errors!` | Explicit `#[gts_error]` structs with visible GTS IDs |\n+| **Inconsistent definitions** | Some modules use inline errors | All modules use `#[gts_error]` structs |\n+| **No types registry** | Errors not registered | All errors registered as GTS types |\n+| **Missing metadata** | No structured context | Struct fields → `metadata` map |\n+| **Partial trace IDs** | Only in `IntoResponse` | Mandatory in all error responses |\n+| **No error categories** | Flat error codes | System/Operational/Client categories |\n+| **No error stack** | Single error | Upstream error chain propagation |\n+\n+### Current Module Migration Status\n+\n+| Module | Location | Status | Issues |\n+|--------|----------|--------|--------|\n+| **file_parser** | `modules/file_parser/` | 🔴 Not migrated | No GTS IDs, inline `Problem::new()` |\n+| **types-registry** | `modules/system/types-registry/` | 🟡 Partial | Has codes but not GTS format (e.g., `TYPES_REGISTRY_NOT_FOUND`) |\n+| **nodes_registry** | `modules/system/nodes_registry/` | 🔴 Not migrated | Non-GTS codes (e.g., `NODES_NOT_FOUND`) |\n+| **api_gateway** | `modules/system/api_gateway/` | 🔴 Not migrated | No Problem struct, simple error codes |\n+| **tenant_resolver** | `modules/system/tenant_resolver/` | 🔴 Not migrated | No GTS IDs |\n+| **simple-user-settings** | `modules/simple-user-settings/` | 🟡 Partial | Uses `declare_errors!` with old chain format |\n+| **modkit-auth** | `libs/modkit-auth/` | 🔴 Not migrated | No GTS IDs, custom `IntoResponse` |\n+| **modkit-odata** | `libs/modkit-odata/` | 🟡 Partial | Uses `declare_errors!` with old chain format |\n+| **users_info** (example) | `examples/modkit/users_info/` | 🟡 Partial | Uses `declare_errors!` with old chain format |\n+\n+#### Legend\n+- 🟢 **Migrated** - Uses `#[gts_error]` structs with proper base types\n+- 🟡 **Partial** - Has GTS IDs but uses deprecated `declare_errors!` or old format\n+- 🔴 **Not migrated** - No GTS IDs or non-GTS format codes\n+\n+#### GTS ID Format Note\n+\n+**Old chain format** (used by `declare_errors!`):\n+```\n+gts.hx.core.errors.err.v1~hx.module.error_name.v1\n+```\n+\n+**New format** (with `base` field):\n+```\n+gts.hx.module.namespace.error_name.v1~\n+```\n+The `base` field in `#[gts_error]` replaces the chain suffix, making inheritance explicit in code.\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Requirements\n+\n+### R1: Error Schema Requirements\n+\n+Every error returned from REST API MUST conform to the unified schema:\n+\n+```rust\n+pub struct Problem {\n+    // =========================================================================\n+    // REQUIRED FIELDS - Core error identification\n+    // =========================================================================\n+    \n+    /// URI reference identifying the problem type (GTS-based)\n+    /// Example: \"https://docs.hyperspot.com/errors/types_registry_entity_not_found_v1\"\n+    #[serde(rename = \"type\")]\n+    pub type_url: String,\n+    \n+    /// Human-readable summary of the problem type (static per error type)\n+    pub title: String,\n+    \n+    /// GTS error code (machine-readable identifier)\n+    pub code: String,\n+    \n+    /// Trace ID for request correlation\n+    pub trace_id: String,\n+    \n+    // =========================================================================\n+    // CONTEXTUAL FIELDS - Optional based on error context\n+    // =========================================================================\n+    \n+    /// HTTP status code. Optional because:\n+    /// - gRPC errors use different status codes\n+    /// - Internal/domain errors may not have HTTP context\n+    /// - Event-driven systems have no request/response\n+    /// When serializing for HTTP response, this is populated from error definition.\n+    #[serde(skip_serializing_if = \"Option::is_none\")]\n+    pub status: Option<u16>,","path":"intended_design/UNIFIED_ERROR_SYSTEM.md","commit_id":"5bdb0f43b25858af78999718f7247813802b9634","original_commit_id":"5bdb0f43b25858af78999718f7247813802b9634","user":{"login":"alizid10","id":247960800,"node_id":"U_kgDODseU4A","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/247960800?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/alizid10","html_url":"https://github.com/alizid10","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alizid10/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alizid10/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alizid10/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alizid10/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alizid10/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alizid10/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alizid10/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alizid10/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alizid10/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"done","created_at":"2026-02-06T16:02:52Z","updated_at":"2026-02-06T16:02:52Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/290#discussion_r2774859550","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/290","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2774859550"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/290#discussion_r2774859550"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/290"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2774859550/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":null,"original_line":196,"side":"RIGHT","in_reply_to_id":2747943818,"author_association":"MEMBER","original_position":196,"position":1,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2774860191","pull_request_review_id":3763883067,"id":2774860191,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs6lZQGf","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,1574 @@\n+# Unified Error System - Intention Document\n+\n+This document defines the architecture, rules, and implementation plan for a unified error handling system across the Hyperspot project. All REST API errors MUST have a GTS identifier, trace ID, and be registered in the types registry.\n+\n+## Table of Contents\n+\n+1. [Executive Summary](#executive-summary)\n+2. [Industry Research](#industry-research)\n+3. [Current State Analysis](#current-state-analysis)\n+4. [Requirements](#requirements)\n+5. [Implementation Rules](#implementation-rules)\n+6. [Migration Plan](#migration-plan)\n+7. [Examples](#examples)\n+8. [HTTP Headers](#http-headers)\n+9. [Security Considerations](#security-considerations)\n+10. [Appendix A: Error Category Definitions](#appendix-a-error-category-definitions)\n+11. [Appendix B: Retryable Error Guidelines](#appendix-b-retryable-error-guidelines)\n+12. [GTS System Errors Catalog](#gts-system-errors-catalog)\n+13. [References](#references)\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Executive Summary\n+\n+### Problem Statement\n+\n+The current error handling across Hyperspot modules is inconsistent:\n+- Some modules use `declare_errors!` macro with JSON catalogs\n+- Others define errors inline without GTS codes\n+- Errors are not registered in the types registry\n+- No standardized metadata/context fields\n+- Inconsistent trace ID propagation\n+\n+### Goals\n+\n+1. **Every REST API error** MUST have a valid GTS identifier\n+2. **Every error response** MUST include a trace ID for debugging\n+3. **All error types** MUST be registered in the types registry\n+4. **Consistent error schema** across all modules following RFC 9457\n+5. **Machine-readable error codes** for programmatic handling\n+6. **Error stack propagation** for nested service calls\n+\n+### Non-Goals\n+\n+- Changing internal domain error types (only API-facing errors)\n+- Modifying logging infrastructure\n+- Changing HTTP status code semantics\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Industry Research\n+\n+### How Major Tech Companies Handle Errors\n+\n+| Company | Standard | Key Features |\n+|---------|----------|--------------|\n+| **Google** | AIP-193 + gRPC Status | `reason` (UPPER_SNAKE_CASE), `domain` (service name), `metadata` (key-value context), `ErrorInfo`, `LocalizedMessage`, `Help` links |\n+| **Amazon AWS** | Custom JSON | `errorType`, `httpStatus`, `requestId`, `message`, custom error object serialization |\n+| **Twitter/X** | JSON with `errors` array | `code` (CAPS_CASE), `message`, `parameter`, `details`, `value` |\n+| **RFC 9457** | Problem Details | `type` (URI), `title`, `status`, `detail`, `instance`, extension members |\n+\n+### Key Patterns Identified\n+\n+1. **Machine-readable identifiers** - Unique codes for programmatic handling (Google's `reason`, Twitter's `code`)\n+2. **Domain/namespace separation** - Identify error source (Google's `domain`, our GTS vendor.package)\n+3. **Structured metadata** - Key-value context without parsing messages (Google's `ErrorInfo.metadata`)\n+4. **Trace/Request IDs** - Correlation for debugging (AWS `requestId`, our `trace_id`)\n+5. **Documentation links** - URIs to error documentation (RFC 9457 `type`, Google's `Help`)\n+6. **Error categorization** - System vs User-defined, Retryable vs Non-retryable\n+\n+### Google AIP-193 ErrorInfo Structure (Reference)\n+\n+```json\n+{\n+  \"error\": {\n+    \"code\": 429,\n+    \"message\": \"The zone 'us-east1-a' does not have enough resources...\",\n+    \"status\": \"RESOURCE_EXHAUSTED\",\n+    \"details\": [\n+      {\n+        \"@type\": \"type.googleapis.com/google.rpc.ErrorInfo\",\n+        \"reason\": \"RESOURCE_AVAILABILITY\",\n+        \"domain\": \"compute.googleapis.com\",\n+        \"metadata\": {\n+          \"zone\": \"us-east1-a\",\n+          \"vmType\": \"e2-medium\"\n+        }\n+      }\n+    ]\n+  }\n+}\n+```\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Current State Analysis\n+\n+### Existing Infrastructure\n+\n+1. **`Problem` struct** (`libs/modkit-errors/src/problem.rs`) - RFC 9457 compliant\n+   - Fields: `type_url`, `title`, `status`, `detail`, `instance`, `code`, `trace_id`, `errors`\n+   - Implements `IntoResponse` for Axum with automatic trace ID enrichment\n+\n+2. **`struct_to_gts_schema` macro** (`modules/types-registry/gts-rust/gts-macros/src/lib.rs`)\n+   - Attribute macro for explicit struct definitions with GTS IDs visible in code\n+   - Generates constants: `GTS_SCHEMA_ID`, `GTS_SCHEMA_JSON`, etc.\n+   - **This pattern will be adapted for error definitions**\n+\n+3. **`declare_errors!` macro** (`libs/modkit-errors-macro/src/lib.rs`) - **TO BE DEPRECATED**\n+   - Generates type-safe error enums from JSON catalogs\n+   - Problem: GTS IDs hidden in external JSON files, not visible to LLMs\n+   - Used by: `users_info` example, `modkit-odata`\n+\n+### Gaps Identified\n+\n+| Gap | Current State | Required State |\n+|-----|---------------|----------------|\n+| **Hidden GTS IDs** | JSON-based `declare_errors!` | Explicit `#[gts_error]` structs with visible GTS IDs |\n+| **Inconsistent definitions** | Some modules use inline errors | All modules use `#[gts_error]` structs |\n+| **No types registry** | Errors not registered | All errors registered as GTS types |\n+| **Missing metadata** | No structured context | Struct fields → `metadata` map |\n+| **Partial trace IDs** | Only in `IntoResponse` | Mandatory in all error responses |\n+| **No error categories** | Flat error codes | System/Operational/Client categories |\n+| **No error stack** | Single error | Upstream error chain propagation |\n+\n+### Current Module Migration Status\n+\n+| Module | Location | Status | Issues |\n+|--------|----------|--------|--------|\n+| **file_parser** | `modules/file_parser/` | 🔴 Not migrated | No GTS IDs, inline `Problem::new()` |\n+| **types-registry** | `modules/system/types-registry/` | 🟡 Partial | Has codes but not GTS format (e.g., `TYPES_REGISTRY_NOT_FOUND`) |\n+| **nodes_registry** | `modules/system/nodes_registry/` | 🔴 Not migrated | Non-GTS codes (e.g., `NODES_NOT_FOUND`) |\n+| **api_gateway** | `modules/system/api_gateway/` | 🔴 Not migrated | No Problem struct, simple error codes |\n+| **tenant_resolver** | `modules/system/tenant_resolver/` | 🔴 Not migrated | No GTS IDs |\n+| **simple-user-settings** | `modules/simple-user-settings/` | 🟡 Partial | Uses `declare_errors!` with old chain format |\n+| **modkit-auth** | `libs/modkit-auth/` | 🔴 Not migrated | No GTS IDs, custom `IntoResponse` |\n+| **modkit-odata** | `libs/modkit-odata/` | 🟡 Partial | Uses `declare_errors!` with old chain format |\n+| **users_info** (example) | `examples/modkit/users_info/` | 🟡 Partial | Uses `declare_errors!` with old chain format |\n+\n+#### Legend\n+- 🟢 **Migrated** - Uses `#[gts_error]` structs with proper base types\n+- 🟡 **Partial** - Has GTS IDs but uses deprecated `declare_errors!` or old format\n+- 🔴 **Not migrated** - No GTS IDs or non-GTS format codes\n+\n+#### GTS ID Format Note\n+\n+**Old chain format** (used by `declare_errors!`):\n+```\n+gts.hx.core.errors.err.v1~hx.module.error_name.v1\n+```\n+\n+**New format** (with `base` field):\n+```\n+gts.hx.module.namespace.error_name.v1~\n+```\n+The `base` field in `#[gts_error]` replaces the chain suffix, making inheritance explicit in code.\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Requirements\n+\n+### R1: Error Schema Requirements\n+\n+Every error returned from REST API MUST conform to the unified schema:\n+\n+```rust\n+pub struct Problem {\n+    // =========================================================================\n+    // REQUIRED FIELDS - Core error identification\n+    // =========================================================================\n+    \n+    /// URI reference identifying the problem type (GTS-based)\n+    /// Example: \"https://docs.hyperspot.com/errors/types_registry_entity_not_found_v1\"\n+    #[serde(rename = \"type\")]\n+    pub type_url: String,\n+    \n+    /// Human-readable summary of the problem type (static per error type)\n+    pub title: String,\n+    \n+    /// GTS error code (machine-readable identifier)\n+    pub code: String,\n+    \n+    /// Trace ID for request correlation\n+    pub trace_id: String,\n+    \n+    // =========================================================================\n+    // CONTEXTUAL FIELDS - Optional based on error context\n+    // =========================================================================\n+    \n+    /// HTTP status code. Optional because:\n+    /// - gRPC errors use different status codes\n+    /// - Internal/domain errors may not have HTTP context\n+    /// - Event-driven systems have no request/response\n+    /// When serializing for HTTP response, this is populated from error definition.\n+    #[serde(skip_serializing_if = \"Option::is_none\")]\n+    pub status: Option<u16>,\n+    \n+    /// Human-readable explanation specific to this occurrence.\n+    /// Optional - title may be sufficient for simple errors.\n+    #[serde(skip_serializing_if = \"Option::is_none\")]\n+    pub detail: Option<String>,","path":"intended_design/UNIFIED_ERROR_SYSTEM.md","commit_id":"5bdb0f43b25858af78999718f7247813802b9634","original_commit_id":"5bdb0f43b25858af78999718f7247813802b9634","user":{"login":"alizid10","id":247960800,"node_id":"U_kgDODseU4A","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/247960800?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/alizid10","html_url":"https://github.com/alizid10","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alizid10/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alizid10/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alizid10/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alizid10/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alizid10/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alizid10/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alizid10/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alizid10/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alizid10/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"removed","created_at":"2026-02-06T16:03:00Z","updated_at":"2026-02-06T16:03:01Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/290#discussion_r2774860191","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/290","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2774860191"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/290#discussion_r2774860191"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/290"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2774860191/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":null,"original_line":201,"side":"RIGHT","in_reply_to_id":2747949318,"author_association":"MEMBER","original_position":201,"position":1,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2774860709","pull_request_review_id":3763883615,"id":2774860709,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs6lZQOl","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,1574 @@\n+# Unified Error System - Intention Document\n+\n+This document defines the architecture, rules, and implementation plan for a unified error handling system across the Hyperspot project. All REST API errors MUST have a GTS identifier, trace ID, and be registered in the types registry.\n+\n+## Table of Contents\n+\n+1. [Executive Summary](#executive-summary)\n+2. [Industry Research](#industry-research)\n+3. [Current State Analysis](#current-state-analysis)\n+4. [Requirements](#requirements)\n+5. [Implementation Rules](#implementation-rules)\n+6. [Migration Plan](#migration-plan)\n+7. [Examples](#examples)\n+8. [HTTP Headers](#http-headers)\n+9. [Security Considerations](#security-considerations)\n+10. [Appendix A: Error Category Definitions](#appendix-a-error-category-definitions)\n+11. [Appendix B: Retryable Error Guidelines](#appendix-b-retryable-error-guidelines)\n+12. [GTS System Errors Catalog](#gts-system-errors-catalog)\n+13. [References](#references)\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Executive Summary\n+\n+### Problem Statement\n+\n+The current error handling across Hyperspot modules is inconsistent:\n+- Some modules use `declare_errors!` macro with JSON catalogs\n+- Others define errors inline without GTS codes\n+- Errors are not registered in the types registry\n+- No standardized metadata/context fields\n+- Inconsistent trace ID propagation\n+\n+### Goals\n+\n+1. **Every REST API error** MUST have a valid GTS identifier\n+2. **Every error response** MUST include a trace ID for debugging\n+3. **All error types** MUST be registered in the types registry\n+4. **Consistent error schema** across all modules following RFC 9457\n+5. **Machine-readable error codes** for programmatic handling\n+6. **Error stack propagation** for nested service calls\n+\n+### Non-Goals\n+\n+- Changing internal domain error types (only API-facing errors)\n+- Modifying logging infrastructure\n+- Changing HTTP status code semantics\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Industry Research\n+\n+### How Major Tech Companies Handle Errors\n+\n+| Company | Standard | Key Features |\n+|---------|----------|--------------|\n+| **Google** | AIP-193 + gRPC Status | `reason` (UPPER_SNAKE_CASE), `domain` (service name), `metadata` (key-value context), `ErrorInfo`, `LocalizedMessage`, `Help` links |\n+| **Amazon AWS** | Custom JSON | `errorType`, `httpStatus`, `requestId`, `message`, custom error object serialization |\n+| **Twitter/X** | JSON with `errors` array | `code` (CAPS_CASE), `message`, `parameter`, `details`, `value` |\n+| **RFC 9457** | Problem Details | `type` (URI), `title`, `status`, `detail`, `instance`, extension members |\n+\n+### Key Patterns Identified\n+\n+1. **Machine-readable identifiers** - Unique codes for programmatic handling (Google's `reason`, Twitter's `code`)\n+2. **Domain/namespace separation** - Identify error source (Google's `domain`, our GTS vendor.package)\n+3. **Structured metadata** - Key-value context without parsing messages (Google's `ErrorInfo.metadata`)\n+4. **Trace/Request IDs** - Correlation for debugging (AWS `requestId`, our `trace_id`)\n+5. **Documentation links** - URIs to error documentation (RFC 9457 `type`, Google's `Help`)\n+6. **Error categorization** - System vs User-defined, Retryable vs Non-retryable\n+\n+### Google AIP-193 ErrorInfo Structure (Reference)\n+\n+```json\n+{\n+  \"error\": {\n+    \"code\": 429,\n+    \"message\": \"The zone 'us-east1-a' does not have enough resources...\",\n+    \"status\": \"RESOURCE_EXHAUSTED\",\n+    \"details\": [\n+      {\n+        \"@type\": \"type.googleapis.com/google.rpc.ErrorInfo\",\n+        \"reason\": \"RESOURCE_AVAILABILITY\",\n+        \"domain\": \"compute.googleapis.com\",\n+        \"metadata\": {\n+          \"zone\": \"us-east1-a\",\n+          \"vmType\": \"e2-medium\"\n+        }\n+      }\n+    ]\n+  }\n+}\n+```\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Current State Analysis\n+\n+### Existing Infrastructure\n+\n+1. **`Problem` struct** (`libs/modkit-errors/src/problem.rs`) - RFC 9457 compliant\n+   - Fields: `type_url`, `title`, `status`, `detail`, `instance`, `code`, `trace_id`, `errors`\n+   - Implements `IntoResponse` for Axum with automatic trace ID enrichment\n+\n+2. **`struct_to_gts_schema` macro** (`modules/types-registry/gts-rust/gts-macros/src/lib.rs`)\n+   - Attribute macro for explicit struct definitions with GTS IDs visible in code\n+   - Generates constants: `GTS_SCHEMA_ID`, `GTS_SCHEMA_JSON`, etc.\n+   - **This pattern will be adapted for error definitions**\n+\n+3. **`declare_errors!` macro** (`libs/modkit-errors-macro/src/lib.rs`) - **TO BE DEPRECATED**\n+   - Generates type-safe error enums from JSON catalogs\n+   - Problem: GTS IDs hidden in external JSON files, not visible to LLMs\n+   - Used by: `users_info` example, `modkit-odata`\n+\n+### Gaps Identified\n+\n+| Gap | Current State | Required State |\n+|-----|---------------|----------------|\n+| **Hidden GTS IDs** | JSON-based `declare_errors!` | Explicit `#[gts_error]` structs with visible GTS IDs |\n+| **Inconsistent definitions** | Some modules use inline errors | All modules use `#[gts_error]` structs |\n+| **No types registry** | Errors not registered | All errors registered as GTS types |\n+| **Missing metadata** | No structured context | Struct fields → `metadata` map |\n+| **Partial trace IDs** | Only in `IntoResponse` | Mandatory in all error responses |\n+| **No error categories** | Flat error codes | System/Operational/Client categories |\n+| **No error stack** | Single error | Upstream error chain propagation |\n+\n+### Current Module Migration Status\n+\n+| Module | Location | Status | Issues |\n+|--------|----------|--------|--------|\n+| **file_parser** | `modules/file_parser/` | 🔴 Not migrated | No GTS IDs, inline `Problem::new()` |\n+| **types-registry** | `modules/system/types-registry/` | 🟡 Partial | Has codes but not GTS format (e.g., `TYPES_REGISTRY_NOT_FOUND`) |\n+| **nodes_registry** | `modules/system/nodes_registry/` | 🔴 Not migrated | Non-GTS codes (e.g., `NODES_NOT_FOUND`) |\n+| **api_gateway** | `modules/system/api_gateway/` | 🔴 Not migrated | No Problem struct, simple error codes |\n+| **tenant_resolver** | `modules/system/tenant_resolver/` | 🔴 Not migrated | No GTS IDs |\n+| **simple-user-settings** | `modules/simple-user-settings/` | 🟡 Partial | Uses `declare_errors!` with old chain format |\n+| **modkit-auth** | `libs/modkit-auth/` | 🔴 Not migrated | No GTS IDs, custom `IntoResponse` |\n+| **modkit-odata** | `libs/modkit-odata/` | 🟡 Partial | Uses `declare_errors!` with old chain format |\n+| **users_info** (example) | `examples/modkit/users_info/` | 🟡 Partial | Uses `declare_errors!` with old chain format |\n+\n+#### Legend\n+- 🟢 **Migrated** - Uses `#[gts_error]` structs with proper base types\n+- 🟡 **Partial** - Has GTS IDs but uses deprecated `declare_errors!` or old format\n+- 🔴 **Not migrated** - No GTS IDs or non-GTS format codes\n+\n+#### GTS ID Format Note\n+\n+**Old chain format** (used by `declare_errors!`):\n+```\n+gts.hx.core.errors.err.v1~hx.module.error_name.v1\n+```\n+\n+**New format** (with `base` field):\n+```\n+gts.hx.module.namespace.error_name.v1~\n+```\n+The `base` field in `#[gts_error]` replaces the chain suffix, making inheritance explicit in code.\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Requirements\n+\n+### R1: Error Schema Requirements\n+\n+Every error returned from REST API MUST conform to the unified schema:\n+\n+```rust\n+pub struct Problem {\n+    // =========================================================================\n+    // REQUIRED FIELDS - Core error identification\n+    // =========================================================================\n+    \n+    /// URI reference identifying the problem type (GTS-based)\n+    /// Example: \"https://docs.hyperspot.com/errors/types_registry_entity_not_found_v1\"\n+    #[serde(rename = \"type\")]\n+    pub type_url: String,\n+    \n+    /// Human-readable summary of the problem type (static per error type)\n+    pub title: String,\n+    \n+    /// GTS error code (machine-readable identifier)\n+    pub code: String,\n+    \n+    /// Trace ID for request correlation\n+    pub trace_id: String,\n+    \n+    // =========================================================================\n+    // CONTEXTUAL FIELDS - Optional based on error context\n+    // =========================================================================\n+    \n+    /// HTTP status code. Optional because:\n+    /// - gRPC errors use different status codes\n+    /// - Internal/domain errors may not have HTTP context\n+    /// - Event-driven systems have no request/response\n+    /// When serializing for HTTP response, this is populated from error definition.\n+    #[serde(skip_serializing_if = \"Option::is_none\")]\n+    pub status: Option<u16>,\n+    \n+    /// Human-readable explanation specific to this occurrence.\n+    /// Optional - title may be sufficient for simple errors.\n+    #[serde(skip_serializing_if = \"Option::is_none\")]\n+    pub detail: Option<String>,\n+    \n+    /// Error category for client handling.\n+    /// Optional - can be inferred from base type hierarchy.\n+    #[serde(skip_serializing_if = \"Option::is_none\")]\n+    pub category: Option<ErrorCategory>,\n+    \n+    /// Whether client can retry this request.\n+    /// Optional - can be inferred from base type; not relevant for all contexts.\n+    #[serde(skip_serializing_if = \"Option::is_none\")]\n+    pub retryable: Option<bool>,\n+    \n+    /// URI identifying this specific occurrence (auto-populated from request path)\n+    #[serde(skip_serializing_if = \"Option::is_none\")]\n+    pub instance: Option<String>,\n+    \n+    /// Structured metadata (key-value context)\n+    #[serde(skip_serializing_if = \"Option::is_none\")]\n+    pub metadata: Option<HashMap<String, String>>,\n+    \n+    /// Validation errors for 4xx responses\n+    #[serde(skip_serializing_if = \"Option::is_none\")]\n+    pub errors: Option<Vec<ValidationViolation>>,\n+    \n+    /// Upstream error chain (when error_stack enabled)\n+    #[serde(skip_serializing_if = \"Option::is_none\")]\n+    pub upstream_errors: Option<Vec<UpstreamError>>,","path":"intended_design/UNIFIED_ERROR_SYSTEM.md","commit_id":"5bdb0f43b25858af78999718f7247813802b9634","original_commit_id":"5bdb0f43b25858af78999718f7247813802b9634","user":{"login":"alizid10","id":247960800,"node_id":"U_kgDODseU4A","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/247960800?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/alizid10","html_url":"https://github.com/alizid10","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alizid10/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alizid10/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alizid10/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alizid10/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alizid10/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alizid10/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alizid10/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alizid10/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alizid10/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"removed","created_at":"2026-02-06T16:03:08Z","updated_at":"2026-02-06T16:03:09Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/290#discussion_r2774860709","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/290","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2774860709"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/290#discussion_r2774860709"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/290"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2774860709/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":null,"original_line":227,"side":"RIGHT","in_reply_to_id":2747962213,"author_association":"MEMBER","original_position":227,"position":1,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2774861337","pull_request_review_id":3763884259,"id":2774861337,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs6lZQYZ","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,1574 @@\n+# Unified Error System - Intention Document\n+\n+This document defines the architecture, rules, and implementation plan for a unified error handling system across the Hyperspot project. All REST API errors MUST have a GTS identifier, trace ID, and be registered in the types registry.\n+\n+## Table of Contents\n+\n+1. [Executive Summary](#executive-summary)\n+2. [Industry Research](#industry-research)\n+3. [Current State Analysis](#current-state-analysis)\n+4. [Requirements](#requirements)\n+5. [Implementation Rules](#implementation-rules)\n+6. [Migration Plan](#migration-plan)\n+7. [Examples](#examples)\n+8. [HTTP Headers](#http-headers)\n+9. [Security Considerations](#security-considerations)\n+10. [Appendix A: Error Category Definitions](#appendix-a-error-category-definitions)\n+11. [Appendix B: Retryable Error Guidelines](#appendix-b-retryable-error-guidelines)\n+12. [GTS System Errors Catalog](#gts-system-errors-catalog)\n+13. [References](#references)\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Executive Summary\n+\n+### Problem Statement\n+\n+The current error handling across Hyperspot modules is inconsistent:\n+- Some modules use `declare_errors!` macro with JSON catalogs\n+- Others define errors inline without GTS codes\n+- Errors are not registered in the types registry\n+- No standardized metadata/context fields\n+- Inconsistent trace ID propagation\n+\n+### Goals\n+\n+1. **Every REST API error** MUST have a valid GTS identifier\n+2. **Every error response** MUST include a trace ID for debugging\n+3. **All error types** MUST be registered in the types registry\n+4. **Consistent error schema** across all modules following RFC 9457\n+5. **Machine-readable error codes** for programmatic handling\n+6. **Error stack propagation** for nested service calls\n+\n+### Non-Goals\n+\n+- Changing internal domain error types (only API-facing errors)\n+- Modifying logging infrastructure\n+- Changing HTTP status code semantics\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Industry Research\n+\n+### How Major Tech Companies Handle Errors\n+\n+| Company | Standard | Key Features |\n+|---------|----------|--------------|\n+| **Google** | AIP-193 + gRPC Status | `reason` (UPPER_SNAKE_CASE), `domain` (service name), `metadata` (key-value context), `ErrorInfo`, `LocalizedMessage`, `Help` links |\n+| **Amazon AWS** | Custom JSON | `errorType`, `httpStatus`, `requestId`, `message`, custom error object serialization |\n+| **Twitter/X** | JSON with `errors` array | `code` (CAPS_CASE), `message`, `parameter`, `details`, `value` |\n+| **RFC 9457** | Problem Details | `type` (URI), `title`, `status`, `detail`, `instance`, extension members |\n+\n+### Key Patterns Identified\n+\n+1. **Machine-readable identifiers** - Unique codes for programmatic handling (Google's `reason`, Twitter's `code`)\n+2. **Domain/namespace separation** - Identify error source (Google's `domain`, our GTS vendor.package)\n+3. **Structured metadata** - Key-value context without parsing messages (Google's `ErrorInfo.metadata`)\n+4. **Trace/Request IDs** - Correlation for debugging (AWS `requestId`, our `trace_id`)\n+5. **Documentation links** - URIs to error documentation (RFC 9457 `type`, Google's `Help`)\n+6. **Error categorization** - System vs User-defined, Retryable vs Non-retryable\n+\n+### Google AIP-193 ErrorInfo Structure (Reference)\n+\n+```json\n+{\n+  \"error\": {\n+    \"code\": 429,\n+    \"message\": \"The zone 'us-east1-a' does not have enough resources...\",\n+    \"status\": \"RESOURCE_EXHAUSTED\",\n+    \"details\": [\n+      {\n+        \"@type\": \"type.googleapis.com/google.rpc.ErrorInfo\",\n+        \"reason\": \"RESOURCE_AVAILABILITY\",\n+        \"domain\": \"compute.googleapis.com\",\n+        \"metadata\": {\n+          \"zone\": \"us-east1-a\",\n+          \"vmType\": \"e2-medium\"\n+        }\n+      }\n+    ]\n+  }\n+}\n+```\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Current State Analysis\n+\n+### Existing Infrastructure\n+\n+1. **`Problem` struct** (`libs/modkit-errors/src/problem.rs`) - RFC 9457 compliant\n+   - Fields: `type_url`, `title`, `status`, `detail`, `instance`, `code`, `trace_id`, `errors`\n+   - Implements `IntoResponse` for Axum with automatic trace ID enrichment\n+\n+2. **`struct_to_gts_schema` macro** (`modules/types-registry/gts-rust/gts-macros/src/lib.rs`)\n+   - Attribute macro for explicit struct definitions with GTS IDs visible in code\n+   - Generates constants: `GTS_SCHEMA_ID`, `GTS_SCHEMA_JSON`, etc.\n+   - **This pattern will be adapted for error definitions**\n+\n+3. **`declare_errors!` macro** (`libs/modkit-errors-macro/src/lib.rs`) - **TO BE DEPRECATED**\n+   - Generates type-safe error enums from JSON catalogs\n+   - Problem: GTS IDs hidden in external JSON files, not visible to LLMs\n+   - Used by: `users_info` example, `modkit-odata`\n+\n+### Gaps Identified\n+\n+| Gap | Current State | Required State |\n+|-----|---------------|----------------|\n+| **Hidden GTS IDs** | JSON-based `declare_errors!` | Explicit `#[gts_error]` structs with visible GTS IDs |\n+| **Inconsistent definitions** | Some modules use inline errors | All modules use `#[gts_error]` structs |\n+| **No types registry** | Errors not registered | All errors registered as GTS types |\n+| **Missing metadata** | No structured context | Struct fields → `metadata` map |\n+| **Partial trace IDs** | Only in `IntoResponse` | Mandatory in all error responses |\n+| **No error categories** | Flat error codes | System/Operational/Client categories |\n+| **No error stack** | Single error | Upstream error chain propagation |\n+\n+### Current Module Migration Status\n+\n+| Module | Location | Status | Issues |\n+|--------|----------|--------|--------|\n+| **file_parser** | `modules/file_parser/` | 🔴 Not migrated | No GTS IDs, inline `Problem::new()`