to_problem() conversion path and replace the\nabsolute “zero runtime resource allocation” wording with a softened statement\nthat allocations are minimal and limited to the created Problem and its fields\n(metadata), so readers understand possible String/HashMap allocations.\n\nIn `@docs/unified-error-system/PRD.md`:\n- Around line 285-314: The headings under \"## 8. Use Cases\" are using #### which\njumps two levels; change them to ### so they are direct subsections of the Use\nCases section (e.g., update \"#### Define Module Error\" and \"#### Handle API\nError Response\" to \"### Define Module Error\" and \"### Handle API Error\nResponse\"), ensuring any subsequent subitems (like checklists and flows) remain\nat the correct deeper levels.\n- Around line 17-22: Add a clear Goals bullet requiring a centralized \"unified\nerror documentation portal\" and mandated code-location metadata for every REST\nAPI error so consumers can navigate from an error \"type\" to its exact source;\nupdate the 1.3 Goals to include: (1) a portal that documents every registered\nerror and is searchable by \"type\", and (2) every error registered in the types\nregistry at module startup (via the existing modkit-errors macro) must emit\nsource_location metadata (module, file, git anchor/line) and a portal_url\nidentifier. Also add corresponding functional requirements: the portal must\nprovide deep links per error type and the error registration path (types\nregistry / modkit-errors) must populate the portal and source_location fields\nautomatically.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment by CodeRabbit for review status -->","state":"COMMENTED","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/290#pullrequestreview-3789636028","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/290","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","_links":{"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/290#pullrequestreview-3789636028"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/290"}},"submitted_at":"2026-02-12T09:02:12Z","commit_id":"8a052fb4bfbe084c473fafc9cf50dab48fd469ad"},{"id":3790098461,"node_id":"PRR_kwDOPaLyBs7h6FAd","user":{"login":"coderabbitai[bot]","id":136622811,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOCCSy2w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/347564?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/coderabbitai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"**Actionable comments posted: 1**\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Fix all issues with AI agents</summary>\n\n```\nIn @.cypilot-adapter/artifacts.json:\n- Around line 35-46: The artifacts.json contains ignore patterns for\nnon-existent modules \"modules/module_orchestrator/*\" and \"modules/api_ingress/*\"\nalongside the valid \"modules/llm-gateway/*\"; remove the two invalid pattern\nentries (the objects whose \"patterns\" are \"modules/module_orchestrator/*\" and\n\"modules/api_ingress/*\") from the JSON or replace them by creating the\ncorresponding module directories if you intend to keep them, leaving only valid\nignore patterns such as \"modules/llm-gateway/*\".\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>🧹 Nitpick comments (1)</summary><blockquote>\n\n<details>\n<summary>docs/unified-error-system/DESIGN.md (1)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`1-421`: **Consider adding Migration Plan and Open Questions sections.**\n\nBased on learnings, `design.md` files should include sections for Migration Plan and Open Questions. The current document is comprehensive but lacks these sections explicitly. The PRD mentions migration at a high level (§6.3 Compatibility Requirements), but the DESIGN document would benefit from:\n- **Migration Plan**: Steps for modules transitioning from `declare_errors!` to `#[gts_error]`\n- **Open Questions**: Any unresolved technical decisions (or explicit \"None\" if all resolved)\n\nThis is a recommended addition rather than a blocker.\n\n</blockquote></details>\n\n</blockquote></details>\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment by CodeRabbit for review status -->","state":"COMMENTED","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/290#pullrequestreview-3790098461","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/290","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","_links":{"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/290#pullrequestreview-3790098461"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/290"}},"submitted_at":"2026-02-12T10:34:12Z","commit_id":"29639fa9243ed7d2b2e6371ce6bb2d3a3ccea706"}]},{"source_pr_number":289,"source_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/289","source_state":"closed","source_author":"binarycode","target_issue_number":null,"title":"[PR #289] fix OoP modules example","status":"exported","mirrored_at":null,"comments_status":"none","comments_mirrored":0,"pr_head_ref":"fix/oop-modules-example","pr_head_sha":"5e6af8db4af53140a2217ab9e9aea34cb57f866e","pr_base_ref":"main","pr_head_owner":"binarycode","pr_from_fork":1,"source_data":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/289","id":3194487975,"node_id":"PR_kwDOPaLyBs6-aASn","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/289","diff_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/289.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/289.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/issues/289","number":289,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"fix OoP modules example","user":{"login":"binarycode","id":415262,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQxNTI2Mg==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/415262?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/binarycode","html_url":"https://github.com/binarycode","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/binarycode/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/binarycode/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/binarycode/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/binarycode/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/binarycode/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/binarycode/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/binarycode/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/binarycode/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/binarycode/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Currently `oop-modules` example does not work (see #279).\r\n\r\nThere is no obvious place to run `wire_client` as proposed in documentation, so this PR attempts to fix the problem by introducing `LocalCalculatorClient` module that is expected to be compiled to the main application that exposes `CalculatorClient` interface. This module will lazily try to find connected `calculator` OoP module in `DirectoryClient` and call it if found. Thus this module effectively replaces `wire_client` function.\r\n\r\n## Steps to reproduce the issue:\r\n- run `make oop-example` to execute main application\r\n- in a separate terminal run `MODKIT_DIRECTORY_ENDPOINT=\"unix:///tmp/hyperspot-grpc\" cargo run -p calculator --features=oop_module` to execute OoP module\r\n- in a separate terminal run `curl -X POST http://localhost:8087/calculator-gateway/v1/calculator/add -H \"Content-Type: application/json\" -d '{\"a\": 5, \"b\": 3}'`\r\n\r\n**Response before fix:**\r\n```json\r\n{\"type\":\"about:blank\",\"title\":\"Internal Server Error\",\"status\":500,\"detail\":\"Addition failed: internal error: CalculatorClient not available: client not found: type=dyn calculator_sdk::api::CalculatorClient\",\"instance\":\"\",\"code\":\"\",\"trace_id\":\"274877906946\",\"errors\":null}\r\n```\r\n\r\n**Response after fix:**\r\n```json\r\n{\"sum\":8}\r\n```\r\n\r\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai -->\r\n\r\n## Summary by CodeRabbit\r\n\r\n## Release Notes\r\n\r\n* **New Features**\r\n  * Added a local calculator module that automatically registers gRPC clients in the service hub with lazy initialization.\r\n  * Calculator SDK now provides automatic client registration and service discovery integration.\r\n\r\n* **Refactor**\r\n  * Updated calculator SDK public API to expose the gRPC client directly and proto types for improved accessibility.\r\n  * Module registration now uses automatic discovery instead of manual wiring configuration.\r\n\r\n<sub>✏️ Tip: You can customize this high-level summary in your review settings.</sub>\r\n\r\n<!-- end of auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai -->","created_at":"2026-01-21T09:38:25Z","updated_at":"2026-01-26T14:41:39Z","closed_at":"2026-01-26T14:41:39Z","merged_at":null,"merge_commit_sha":null,"assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[{"login":"MikeFalcon77","id":3686170,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM2ODYxNzA=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3686170?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/MikeFalcon77","html_url":"https://github.com/MikeFalcon77",