ils>\n> <details>\n> <summary>docs/MODKIT_UNIFIED_SYSTEM.md (1)</summary><blockquote>\n> \n> `575-596`: **Fix MD036: use headings instead of bold emphasis.**  \n> Convert the “Option 1/2” lines into proper headings to satisfy linting.  \n> \n> \n> <details>\n> <summary>✏️ Proposed doc fix</summary>\n> \n> ```diff\n> -**Option 1: Manual wiring (using `wire_client`)**\n> +### Option 1: Manual wiring (using `wire_client`)\n> ...\n> -**Option 2: Automatic registration via dedicated module (recommended)**\n> +### Option 2: Automatic registration via dedicated module (recommended)\n> ```\n> </details>\n> \n> </blockquote></details>\n> \n> </blockquote></details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Fix all issues with AI agents</summary>\n\n```\nIn `@examples/oop-modules/calculator/local-calculator/Cargo.toml`:\n- Around line 1-27: The workspace error occurs because the local-calculator\ncrate is using workspace-wide fields but is not listed in the root Cargo.toml\nmembers; open the root Cargo.toml and add the local-calculator crate’s directory\nto the workspace members array so the \"local-calculator\" package is included in\nthe workspace build (ensure the members entry matches the crate's relative\ndirectory name and commit the change).\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>🧹 Nitpick comments (1)</summary><blockquote>\n\n<details>\n<summary>examples/oop-modules/calculator/local-calculator/src/client.rs (1)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`11-96`: **Consider `tokio::sync::OnceCell` to simplify lazy init.**\n\nThis removes manual double-checked locking and avoids holding a write lock across async calls.\n\n\n\n\n<details>\n<summary>♻️ Suggested refactor (verify tokio version supports `OnceCell`)</summary>\n\n```diff\n-use tokio::sync::RwLock;\n+use tokio::sync::OnceCell;\n\n pub struct LocalCalculatorClient {\n     client_hub: Arc<ClientHub>,\n-    grpc_client: RwLock<Option<Arc<CalculatorGrpcClient>>>,\n+    grpc_client: OnceCell<Arc<CalculatorGrpcClient>>,\n }\n\n impl LocalCalculatorClient {\n     /// Create a new LocalCalculatorClient with a reference to ClientHub.\n     pub fn new(client_hub: Arc<ClientHub>) -> Self {\n         Self {\n             client_hub,\n-            grpc_client: RwLock::new(None),\n+            grpc_client: OnceCell::new(),\n         }\n     }\n\n     /// Get or initialize the gRPC client.\n     async fn get_client(&self) -> Result<Arc<CalculatorGrpcClient>, CalculatorError> {\n-        // Fast path: check if already initialized (read lock)\n-        {\n-            let guard = self.grpc_client.read().await;\n-            if let Some(client) = guard.as_ref() {\n-                return Ok(Arc::clone(client));\n-            }\n-        }\n-\n-        // Slow path: initialize the client (write lock)\n-        let mut guard = self.grpc_client.write().await;\n-\n-        // Double-check: another thread might have initialized it while we waited for the write lock\n-        if let Some(client) = guard.as_ref() {\n-            return Ok(Arc::clone(client));\n-        }\n-\n-        // Initialize the client\n-        let directory = self\n-            .client_hub\n-            .get::<dyn DirectoryClient>()\n-            .map_err(|e| {\n-                CalculatorError::Internal(format!(\n-                    \"DirectoryClient not available in ClientHub: {}\",\n-                    e\n-                ))\n-            })?;\n-\n-        // Resolve the service endpoint\n-        let endpoint = directory\n-            .resolve_grpc_service(SERVICE_NAME)\n-            .await\n-            .map_err(|e| {\n-                CalculatorError::Internal(format!(\n-                    \"Failed to resolve calculator service endpoint: {}\",\n-                    e\n-                ))\n-            })?;\n-\n-        // Connect to the gRPC service\n-        let grpc_client = CalculatorGrpcClient::connect(&endpoint.uri)\n-            .await\n-            .map_err(|e| {\n-                CalculatorError::Internal(format!(\n-                    \"Failed to connect to calculator service at {}: {}\",\n-                    endpoint.uri, e\n-                ))\n-            })?;\n-\n-        let grpc_client = Arc::new(grpc_client);\n-\n-        // Cache the client\n-        *guard = Some(Arc::clone(&grpc_client));\n-\n-        Ok(grpc_client)\n+        let client = self\n+            .grpc_client\n+            .get_or_try_init(|| async {\n+                let directory = self\n+                    .client_hub\n+                    .get::<dyn DirectoryClient>()\n+                    .map_err(|e| {\n+                        CalculatorError::Internal(format!(\n+                            \"DirectoryClient not available in ClientHub: {}\",\n+                            e\n+                        ))\n+                    })?;\n+\n+                let endpoint = directory\n+                    .resolve_grpc_service(SERVICE_NAME)\n+                    .await\n+                    .map_err(|e| {\n+                        CalculatorError::Internal(format!(\n+                            \"Failed to resolve calculator service endpoint: {}\",\n+                            e\n+                        ))\n+                    })?;\n+\n+                let grpc_client = CalculatorGrpcClient::connect(&endpoint.uri)\n+                    .await\n+                    .map_err(|e| {\n+                        CalculatorError::Internal(format!(\n+                            \"Failed to connect to calculator service at {}: {}\",\n+                            endpoint.uri, e\n+                        ))\n+                    })?;\n+\n+                Ok(Arc::new(grpc_client))\n+            })\n+            .await?;\n+\n+        Ok(Arc::clone(client))\n     }\n }\n```\n</details>\n\n</blockquote></details>\n\n</blockquote></details>\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment by CodeRabbit for review status -->","state":"COMMENTED","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/289#pullrequestreview-3686279707","pull