d (ADR) that defines a domain model and API contracts, and a NEXT_ADR_SCOPE file listing remaining PRD gaps and proposed future ADRs.\n\n## Changes\n\n| Cohort / File(s) | Summary |\n|---|---|\n| **Product Requirements** <br> `modules/serverless_runtime/docs/PRD.md` | New PRD specifying purpose, goals, scope, business requirements (BR-001…BR-135), acceptance criteria, non-functional requirements, target use cases, assumptions, and risks. |\n| **Domain Model & APIs (ADR)** <br> `modules/serverless_runtime/docs/ADR_DOMAIN_MODEL_AND_APIS.md` | New ADR defining core domain entities (Entrypoints, Invocations, Schedules, Triggers, TenantPolicy), GTS-based identifiers, IO schemas, limits, RetryPolicy, Implementation/adapters, WorkflowTraits, status/state machine, error types, timeline events, Rust domain types, and a ServerlessRuntime async trait API surface with examples. |\n| **Next ADR Scope** <br> `modules/serverless_runtime/docs/NEXT_ADR_SCOPE.md` | New scope doc enumerating unaddressed PRD items (P0/P1/P2) and proposed ADRs (ADR-2…ADR-7) with mapped PRD coverage. |\n\n## Sequence Diagram(s)\n\n```mermaid\nsequenceDiagram\n  participant Client as Client\n  participant API as ServerlessRuntime API\n  participant Scheduler as Scheduler/Worker\n  participant Adapter as Adapter\n  participant Store as Durable Store\n\n  Client->>API: Register Entrypoint (definition, IO schema, policy)\n  API->>Store: Persist EntrypointDefinition\n  Store-->>API: Ack\n  Client->>API: Invoke Entrypoint (payload)\n  API->>Scheduler: Create InvocationRecord, enqueue\n  Scheduler->>Store: Update Invocation timeline (started)\n  Scheduler->>Adapter: Execute implementation (payload)\n  Adapter-->>Scheduler: Result / Error\n  Scheduler->>Store: Persist InvocationStatus, timeline events\n  Scheduler-->>API: Return invocation outcome / schedule retries\n```\n\n## Estimated code review effort\n\n🎯 3 (Moderate) | ⏱️ ~20 minutes\n\n## Poem\n\n> 🐰 I nibble notes of runtimes bright,  \n> > Entrypoints planted, timelines take flight.  \n> > Policies penned, examples in sight,  \n> > I hop through docs with scholarly light. 🥕✨\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- walkthrough_end -->\n\n\n<!-- pre_merge_checks_walkthrough_start -->\n\n<details>\n<summary>🚥 Pre-merge checks | ✅ 3</summary>\n\n<details>\n<summary>✅ Passed checks (3 passed)</summary>\n\n|     Check name     | Status   | Explanation                                                                                                                                                               |\n| :----------------: | :------- | :------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ |\n|  Description Check | ✅ Passed | Check skipped - CodeRabbit’s high-level summary is enabled.                                                                                                               |\n|     Title check    | ✅ Passed | The title accurately summarizes the main changes: establishing business requirements (PRD.md) and domain model (ADR_DOMAIN_MODEL_AND_APIS.md) for the Serverless Runtime. |\n| Docstring Coverage | ✅ Passed | No functions found in the changed files to evaluate docstring coverage. Skipping docstring coverage check.                                                                |\n\n</details>\n\n<sub>✏️ Tip: You can configure your own custom pre-merge checks in the settings.</sub>\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- pre_merge_checks_walkthrough_end -->\n\n<!-- tips_start -->\n\n---\n\n\n\n<sub>Comment `@coderabbitai help` to get the list of available commands and usage tips.</sub>\n\n<!-- tips_end -->\n\n<!-- internal state start -->\n\n\n<!--  -->\n\n<!-- internal state end -->","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/issues/comments/3776845562/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,