"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/issues/comments/3776356903","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/287#issuecomment-3776356903","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/issues/287","id":3776356903,"node_id":"IC_kwDOPaLyBs7hFqIn","user":{"login":"coderabbitai[bot]","id":136622811,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOCCSy2w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/347564?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/coderabbitai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-01-21T06:05:35Z","updated_at":"2026-01-27T09:39:57Z","body":"<!-- This is an auto-generated comment: summarize by coderabbit.ai -->\n<!-- walkthrough_start -->\n\n<details>\n<summary>📝 Walkthrough</summary>\n\n## Walkthrough\n\nAdds markdown link validation: a new `make` target plus GitHub Actions jobs that run `broken-md-links` against `docs`, `examples`, `dylint_lints`, and `guidelines`; also small documentation edits (link removals/updates, relative-path corrections, submodule pointer update, and README tweaks).\n\n## Changes\n\n| Cohort / File(s) | Summary |\n|---|---|\n| **Markdown Link Validation Infrastructure** <br> `Makefile`, `.github/workflows/ci.yml` | Added `markdown-check` Makefile target. Added GitHub Actions job(s) (\"Check Markdown Links\") that install Rust/tooling and run `broken-md-links` against `docs`, `examples`, `dylint_lints`, and `guidelines` (two identical job entries present). |\n| **Docs: lints & README edits** <br> `dylint_lints/README.md` | DE0903 updated with vendor validation (`--vendor`) and allowed vendor list; removed `LINTS.md` from Resources; minor formatting changes. |\n| **Docs: removed/updated references** <br> `docs/SECURE-ORM.md`, `docs/MODKIT_PLUGINS.md` | Removed several external/quick-start/migration reference links and one \"types-registry\" further-reading link. |\n| **Guidelines updates** <br> `guidelines/NEW_MODULE.md`, `guidelines/README.md` | Repointed example module (`remote_accum` → `calculator_gateway`), adjusted indentation, and removed `PAGINATION.md` mention from REST API guidance. |\n| **Contributing doc** <br> `CONTRIBUTING.md` | Removed `PAGINATION.md` reference from REST API development guidance. |\n| **Relative Path Corrections** <br> `modules/system/types_registry/openspec/project.md` | Updated numerous relative links from `../../../` to `../../../../`. |\n| **Submodule pointer** <br> `guidelines/DNA` | Bumped submodule commit reference (record-only change). |\n\n## Sequence Diagram(s)\n\n```mermaid\nsequenceDiagram\n  participant GH as \"GitHub Actions\"\n  participant Runner as \"Runner\"\n  participant Repo as \"Repository\"\n  participant Toolchain as \"Rust toolchain\"\n  participant BML as \"broken-md-links\"\n\n  GH->>Runner: start \"Check Markdown Links\" job\n  Runner->>Repo: checkout code\n  Runner->>Toolchain: install stable Rust toolchain\n  Runner->>Runner: restore/cache Cargo/target\n  Runner->>Runner: install broken-md-links\n  Runner->>BML: run broken-md-links on docs, examples, dylint_lints, guidelines\n  BML-->>Runner: return results/exit code\n  Runner-->>GH: report job success/failure\n```\n\n## Estimated code review effort\n\n🎯 2 (Simple) | ⏱️ ~10 minutes\n\n## Suggested reviewers\n\n- Artifizer  \n- MikeFalcon77  \n- Bechma\n\n## Poem\n\n> 🐰 I hopped through docs to hunt a broken link,  \n> > nudged CI to check each markdown brink,  \n> > paths and readmes tidy, the workflow now sings,  \n> > carrots await me for small helpful things.\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- walkthrough_end -->\n\n\n<!-- pre_merge_checks_walkthrough_start -->\n\n<details>\n<summary>🚥 Pre-merge checks | ✅ 3</summary>\n\n<details>\n<summary>✅ Passed checks (3 passed)</summary>\n\n|     Check name     | Status   | Explanation                                                                                                                                   |\n| :----------------: | :------- | :-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n|  Description Check | ✅ Passed | Check skipped - CodeRabbit’s high-level summary is enabled.                                                                                   |\n|     Title check    | ✅ Passed | The title accurately reflects the main change: adding a tool (broken-md-links) to validate broken links in markdown files across the project. |\n| Docstring Coverage | ✅ Passed | Docstring coverage is 100.00% which is sufficient. The required threshold is 80.00%.                                                          |\n\n</details>\n\n<sub>✏️ Tip: You can configure your own custom pre-merge checks in the settings.</sub>\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- pre_merge_checks_walkthrough_end -->\n\n<!-- tips_start -->\n\n---\n\n\n\n<sub>Comment `@coderabbitai help` to get the list of available commands and usage tips.</sub>\n\n<!-- tips_end -->\n\n<!-- internal state start -->\n\n\n<!--  -->\n\n<!-- internal state end -->","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/issues/comments/3776356903/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":{"id":347564,"client_id":"Iv1.6aaafe4fe882736b","slug":"coderabbitai","node_id":"A_kwHOB96YWc4ABU2s","owner":{"login":"coderabbitai","id":132028505,"node_id":"O_kgDOB96YWQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/132028505?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai","html_url":"https://github.com/coderabbitai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/received_events","type":"Organization","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"name":"coderabbitai","description":"# Transforming Code Reviews with AI\r\n\r\n## Features\r\n\r\n**Automated Reviews**: Continuous reviews of the pull requests including incremental commits. \r\n\r\n**Summarization**: Generates high-level summary and a technical walkthrough of the PR changes. \r\n\r\n**Line-by-line review**: Provides line-by-line suggestions committable with one click.\r\n\r\n**Codebase verification**:  Verifies the impact on the overall codebase and identifies missing changes.\r\n\r\n**Insights into your code**:  Ask any questions on your codebase within the pull request \r\n\r\n**Chat about your code** : Chat with the bot around your code. The more you chat, the smarter it gets.\r\n\r\n**Issue Validation**:  Validates the PR against the linked issues and identifies other related issues \r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n","external_url":"https://coderabbit.ai?utm_source=cr_app&utm_medium=github","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/coderabbitai","created_at":"2023-06-14T15:47:27Z","updated_at":"2026-03-14T07:58:44Z","permissions":{"actions":"read","checks":"write","contents":"write","discussions":"read","issues":"write","members":"read","metadata":"read","pull_requests":"write","statuses":"write"},"events":["issues","issue_comment","label","organization","pull_request","pull_request_review","pull_request_review_comment","pull_request_review_thread","release","repository"]}},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/issues/comments/3776358926","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/287#issuecomment-3776358926","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/issues/287","id":3776358926,"node_id":"IC_kwDOPaLyBs7hFqoO","user":{"login":"mergify[bot]","id":37929162,"node_id":"MDM6Qm90Mzc5MjkxNjI=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/10562?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mergify%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/mergify","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mergify%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mergify%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mergify%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mergify%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mergify%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mergify%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mergify%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mergify%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mergify%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-01-21T06:06:26Z","updated_at":"2026-01-27T09:42:40Z","body":"<!--MERGIFY-CI-INSIGHTS-REPORT-->\n# 🧪 CI Insights\n\nHere's what we observed from your CI run for da4da12d.\n\n## 🟢 All jobs passed!\n\nBut CI Insights is watching 👀","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/issues/comments/3776358926/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":{"id":10562,"client_id":"Iv1.d035f68f69425dc1","slug":"mergify","node_id":"MDM6QXBwMTA1NjI=","owner":{"login":"Mergifyio","id":37838584,"node_id":"MDEyOk9yZ2FuaXphdGlvbjM3ODM4NTg0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/37838584?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mergifyio","html_url":"https://github.com/Mergifyio","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mergifyio/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mergifyio/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mergifyio/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mergifyio/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mergifyio/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mergifyio/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mergifyio/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mergifyio/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mergifyio/received_events","type":"Organization","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"name":"Mergify","description":"Pull requests automation service.","external_url":"https://mergify.com","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/mergify","created_at":"2018-03-30T10:19:51Z","updated_at":"2026-03-02T11:02:56Z","permissions":{"actions":"write","administration":"read","checks":"write","contents":"write","deployments":"write","emails":"read","issues":"write","members":"read","merge_queues":"read","metadata":"read","pages":"write","pull_requests":"write","statuses":"read","workflows":"write"},"events":["branch_protection_configuration","branch_protection_rule","check_run","check_suite","deployment_status","issue_comment","member","membership","merge_group","organization","pull_request","pull_request_review","pull_request_review_comment","pull_request_review_thread","push","repository","repository_ruleset","status","team","team_add","workflow_job","workflow_run"]}},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/issues/comments/3798476554","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/287#issuecomment-3798476554","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/issues/287","id":3798476554,"node_id":"IC_kwDOPaLyBs7iaCcK","user":{"login":"Artifizer","id":192502778,"node_id":"U_kgDOC3lb-g","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/192502778?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer","html_url":"https://github.com/Artifizer","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-01-26T08:47:24Z","updated_at":"2026-01-26T08:47:24Z","body":"It turns out that the task can be evolved to:\r\n\r\n1. Find appropriate cargo tools for proper markdown validation, incl links (the original task)\r\n2. Decide how we install it (use idiomatic Rust approach)\r\n3. add it to Makefile make check\r\n4. add it to CI","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/issues/comments/3798476554/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/issues/comments/3798709688","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/287#issuecomment-3798709688","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/issues/287","id":3798709688,"node_id":"IC_kwDOPaLyBs7ia7W4","user":{"login":"dominic1988-lgtm","id":206866400,"node_id":"U_kgDODFSH4A","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/206866400?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dominic1988-lgtm","html_url":"https://github.com/dominic1988-lgtm","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dominic1988-lgtm/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dominic1988-lgtm/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dominic1988-lgtm/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dominic1988-lgtm/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dominic1988-lgtm/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dominic1988-lgtm/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dominic1988-lgtm/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dominic1988-lgtm/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dominic1988-lgtm/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-01-26T09:49:24Z","updated_at":"2026-01-26T09:49:24Z","body":"> It turns out that the task can be evolved to:\r\n> \r\n> 1. Find appropriate cargo tools for proper markdown validation, incl links (the original task)\r\n> 2. Decide how we install it (use idiomatic Rust approach)\r\n> 3. add it to Makefile make check\r\n> 4. add it to CI\r\n\r\nPR is updated","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/issues/comments/3798709688/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null}],"source_review_comments":[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2711106006","pull_request_review_id":3685496172,"id":2711106006,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs6hmDHW","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,451 @@\n+//! Link checking functionality for Markdown files\n+//!\n+//! Validates that links in Markdown files are not broken:\n+//! - Checks local file references exist\n+//! - Checks HTTP/HTTPS URLs are reachable\n+//! - Detects anchor references to headings\n+\n+use std::collections::{HashMap, HashSet};\n+use std::fs;\n+use std::path::{Path, PathBuf};\n+\n+use regex::Regex;\n+use serde::Serialize;\n+\n+/// Represents a link found in a Markdown file\n+#[derive(Debug, Clone)]\n+pub struct MarkdownLink {\n+    pub text: String,\n+    pub url: String,\n+    pub line: usize,\n+    pub column: usize,\n+}\n+\n+/// Types of links\n+#[derive(Debug, Clone, PartialEq, Eq)]\n+pub enum LinkType {\n+    LocalFile,\n+    LocalAnchor,\n+    Http,\n+    Https,\n+    Mailto,\n+    Other,\n+}\n+\n+/// Represents a broken link error\n+#[derive(Debug, Clone, Serialize)]\n+pub struct LinkError {\n+    pub file: PathBuf,\n+    pub line: usize,\n+    pub column: usize,\n+    pub link_text: String,\n+    pub link_url: String,\n+    pub error: String,\n+}\n+\n+/// Result of link checking\n+#[derive(Debug, Default)]\n+pub struct LinkCheckResult {\n+    pub errors: Vec<LinkError>,\n+    pub files_scanned: usize,\n+    pub links_checked: usize,\n+}\n+\n+impl LinkCheckResult {\n+    #[must_use]\n+    pub fn new(files_scanned: usize) -> Self {\n+        Self {\n+            errors: Vec::new(),\n+            files_scanned,\n+            links_checked: 0,\n+        }\n+    }\n+\n+    pub fn add_error(&mut self, error: LinkError) {\n+        self.errors.push(error);\n+    }\n+\n+    pub fn increment_links_checked(&mut self) {\n+        self.links_checked += 1;\n+    }\n+\n+    #[must_use]\n+    pub fn is_ok(&self) -> bool {\n+        self.errors.is_empty()\n+    }\n+}\n+\n+/// Extract all Markdown links from content\n+/// Supports:\n+/// - [text](url)\n+/// - [text](url \"title\")\n+/// - <url>\n+#[must_use]\n+pub fn extract_markdown_links(content: &str) -> Vec<MarkdownLink> {\n+    let mut links = Vec::new();\n+\n+    // Pattern for [text](url) or [text](url \"title\")\n+    let link_pattern = Regex::new(r\"\\[([^\\]]+)\\]\\(([^\\)]+)\\)\").expect(\"Invalid regex\");\n+\n+    // Pattern for <url>\n+    let autolink_pattern = Regex::new(r\"<(https?://[^>]+)>\").expect(\"Invalid regex\");\n+\n+    let lines: Vec<&str> = content.lines().collect();\n+\n+    for (line_idx, line) in lines.iter().enumerate() {\n+        let line_num = line_idx + 1;\n+\n+        // Extract [text](url) style links\n+        for cap in link_pattern.captures_iter(line) {\n+            if let (Some(text_match), Some(url_match)) = (cap.get(1), cap.get(2)) {\n+                let text = text_match.as_str().to_owned();\n+                let url_full = url_match.as_str();\n+\n+                // Remove optional title from URL (e.g., \"url \"title\"\" -> \"url\")\n+                let url = url_full\n+                    .split_whitespace()\n+                    .next()\n+                    .unwrap_or(url_full)\n+                    .trim_matches('\"')\n+                    .to_owned();\n+\n+                links.push(MarkdownLink {\n+                    text,\n+                    url,\n+                    line: line_num,\n+                    column: url_match.start() + 1,\n+                });\n+            }\n+        }\n+\n+        // Extract <url> style autolinks\n+        for cap in autolink_pattern.captures_iter(line) {\n+            if let Some(url_match) = cap.get(1) {\n+                let url = url_match.as_str().to_owned();\n+                links.push(MarkdownLink {\n+                    text: url.clone(),\n+                    url,\n+                    line: line_num,\n+                    column: url_match.start() + 1,\n+                });\n+            }\n+        }\n+    }\n+\n+    links\n+}\n+\n+/// Determine the type of a link\n+#[must_use]\n+pub fn classify_link(url: &str) -> LinkType {\n+    if url.starts_with(\"http://\") {\n+        LinkType::Http\n+    } else if url.starts_with(\"https://\") {\n+        LinkType::Https\n+    } else if url.starts_with(\"mailto:\") {\n+        LinkType::Mailto\n+    } else if url.starts_with('#') {\n+        LinkType::LocalAnchor\n+    } else if url.starts_with(\"ftp://\") || url.starts_with(\"file://\") {\n+        LinkType::Other\n+    } else {\n+        LinkType::LocalFile\n+    }\n+}\n+\n+/// Extract headings from Markdown content for anchor validation\n+#[must_use]\n+pub fn extract_headings(content: &str) -> HashSet<String> {\n+    let mut headings = HashSet::new();\n+    let heading_pattern = Regex::new(r\"^#{1,6}\\s+(.+)$\").expect(\"Invalid regex\");\n+\n+    for line in content.lines() {\n+        if let Some(cap) = heading_pattern.captures(line) {\n+            if let Some(heading_match) = cap.get(1) {\n+                let heading = heading_match.as_str().trim();\n+                // Convert to anchor format: lowercase, replace spaces with hyphens\n+                let anchor = heading\n+                    .to_lowercase()\n+                    .replace(' ', \"-\")\n+                    .chars()\n+                    .filter(|c| c.is_alphanumeric() || *c == '-' || *c == '_')\n+                    .collect::<String>();\n+                headings.insert(format!(\"#{anchor}\"));\n+            }\n+        }\n+    }\n+\n+    headings\n+}\n+\n+/// Check if a local file link is valid\n+pub fn check_local_file_link(\n+    base_path: &Path,\n+    link_url: &str,\n+) -> Result<(), String> {\n+    // Split anchor from path\n+    let (file_path, anchor) = if let Some(pos) = link_url.find('#') {\n+        (&link_url[..pos], Some(&link_url[pos..]))\n+    } else {\n+        (link_url, None)\n+    };\n+\n+    // Resolve relative path\n+    let full_path = if file_path.is_empty() {\n+        // Just an anchor reference to current file\n+        base_path.to_path_buf()\n+    } else {\n+        let parent = base_path.parent().unwrap_or(base_path);\n+        parent.join(file_path)\n+    };\n+\n+    // Check if path exists (file or directory)\n+    if !full_path.exists() {\n+        return Err(format!(\"Path not found: {}\", full_path.display()));\n+    }\n+\n+    // If it's a directory, that's valid (directory links are allowed)\n+    if full_path.is_dir() {\n+        // Optionally check if directory contains a README.md\n+        let readme_path = full_path.join(\"README.md\");\n+        if !readme_path.exists() {\n+            // Just a warning in verbose mode, not an error\n+            // Directory links without README are still valid\n+        }\n+        return Ok(());\n+    }\n+\n+    // If it's a file, validate it exists (already checked above)\n+    // If there's an anchor, validate it exists in the target file\n+    if let Some(anchor_ref) = anchor {\n+        if full_path.extension().and_then(|e| e.to_str()) == Some(\"md\") {\n+            if let Ok(content) = fs::read_to_string(&full_path) {\n+                let headings = extract_headings(&content);\n+                if !headings.contains(anchor_ref) {\n+                    return Err(format!(\n+                        \"Anchor '{}' not found in {}\",\n+                        anchor_ref,\n+                        full_path.display()\n+                    ));\n+                }\n+            }\n+        }\n+    }\n+\n+    Ok(())\n+}\n+\n+/// Check if a local anchor exists in the given content\n+pub fn check_local_anchor(anchor: &str, headings: &HashSet<String>) -> Result<(), String> {\n+    if !headings.contains(anchor) {\n+        return Err(format!(\"Anchor '{anchor}' not found in current file\"));\n+    }\n+    Ok(())\n+}\n+\n+/// Check all links in a Markdown file\n+#[must_use]\n+pub fn check_links_in_file(\n+    file_path: &Path,\n+    check_http: bool,\n+    verbose: bool,\n+) -> Vec<LinkError> {\n+    let mut errors = Vec::new();\n+\n+    let content = match fs::read_to_string(file_path) {\n+        Ok(c) => c,\n+        Err(e) => {\n+            return vec![LinkError {\n+                file: file_path.to_path_buf(),\n+                line: 0,\n+                column: 0,\n+                link_text: String::new(),\n+                link_url: String::new(),\n+                error: format!(\"Failed to read file: {e}\"),\n+            }];\n+        }\n+    };\n+\n+    let links = extract_markdown_links(&content);\n+    let headings = extract_headings(&content);\n+\n+    for link in links {\n+        if verbose {\n+            eprintln!(\"    Checking link: {} -> {}\", link.text, link.url);\n+        }\n+\n+        let link_type = classify_link(&link.url);\n+\n+        let check_result = match link_type {\n+            LinkType::LocalFile => check_local_file_link(file_path, &link.url),\n+            LinkType::LocalAnchor => check_local_anchor(&link.url, &headings),\n+            LinkType::Http | LinkType::Https => {\n+                if check_http {\n+                    // HTTP checking would require async runtime\n+                    // For now, we'll skip HTTP checks in this implementation\n+                    // and focus on local file links\n+                    if verbose {\n+                        eprintln!(\"      Skipping HTTP check (not implemented yet)\");\n+                    }\n+                    Ok(())\n+                } else {\n+                    Ok(())\n+                }\n+            }\n+            LinkType::Mailto | LinkType::Other => {\n+                // Skip mailto and other special links\n+                Ok(())\n+            }\n+        };\n+\n+        if let Err(error_msg) = check_result {\n+            errors.push(LinkError {\n+                file: file_path.to_path_buf(),\n+                line: link.line,\n+                column: link.column,\n+                link_text: link.text,\n+                link_url: link.url,\n+                error: error_msg,\n+            });\n+        }\n+    }\n+\n+    errors\n+}\n+\n+/// Check links in multiple files\n+#[must_use]\n+pub fn check_links_in_files(\n+    files: &[PathBuf],\n+    check_http: bool,\n+    verbose: bool,\n+) -> LinkCheckResult {\n+    let mut result = LinkCheckResult::new(files.len());\n+\n+    for file_path in files {\n+        if verbose {\n+            eprintln!(\"  Checking links in: {}\", file_path.display());\n+        }\n+\n+        let errors = check_links_in_file(file_path, check_http, verbose);\n+        result.links_checked += extract_markdown_links(\n+            &fs::read_to_string(file_path).unwrap_or_default()\n+        ).len();","path":"apps/gts-docs-validator/src/link_checker.rs","commit_id":"4e6fda46a32379f0662631fda0b4e6c73dc1ddfc","original_commit_id":"4e6fda46a32379f0662631fda0b4e6c73dc1ddfc","user":{"login":"graphite-app[bot]","id":96075541,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOBbn_FQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/158384?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/graphite-app%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/graphite-app","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/graphite-app%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/graphite-app%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/graphite-app%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/graphite-app%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/graphite-app%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/graphite-app%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/graphite-app%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/graphite-app%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/graphite-app%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"The file is being read twice for each file processed, which causes a performance issue and potential race condition. The file was already read in `check_links_in_file()` at line 255, but here it's read again just to count links.\n\n**Impact:** If the file is modified or deleted between the two reads, the link count could be inconsistent with the actual errors reported. Also causes unnecessary I/O overhead.\n\n**Fix:** Return the link count from `check_links_in_file()` or refactor to extract links once:\n\n```rust\nlet (errors, link_count) = check_links_in_file(file_path, check_http, verbose);\nresult.links_checked += link_count;\n```\n\nAnd modify `check_links_in_file` to return `(Vec<LinkError>, usize)` tuple with the link count.\n```suggestion\n        result.links_checked += link_count;\n```\n  \n\n*Spotted by [Graphite Agent](https://app.graphite.com/diamond/?org=hypernetix&ref=ai-review-comment)*<i class='graphite__hidden'><br /><br /><a href=\"https://app.graphite.com/github/pr/hypernetix/hyperspot/287?chatWithGeneratedComment=672cac31-5233-4787-9142-24335775d688\"><picture><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\" srcset=\"https://static.graphite.dev/github-diamond-fix-in-graphite-dark.svg\"><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\" srcset=\"https://static.graphite.dev/github-diamond-fix-in-graphite-light.svg\"><img alt=\"Fix in Graphite\" src=\"https://static.graphite.dev/github-diamond-fix-in-graphite-dark.svg\"></picture></a></i><i class='graphite__hidden'><br /><br />Is this helpful? React 👍 or 👎 to let us know.</i>","created_at":"2026-01-21T06:09:39Z","updated_at":"2026-01-21T06:09:40Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/287#discussion_r2711106006","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/287","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2711106006"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/287#discussion_r2711106006"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/287"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2711106006/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":331,"start_side":"RIGHT","line":null,"original_line":333,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","original_position":333,"position":1,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2711117303","pull_request_review_id":3685511287,"id":2711117303,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs6hmF33","diff_hunk":"@@ -39,6 +47,8 @@ make gts-docs-test    # Run unit tests\n | `--exclude <PATTERN>` | Glob patterns to exclude (can be repeated) |\n | `--json` | Output results as JSON |\n | `--verbose` | Show file scanning progress |\n+| `--check-links` | Check for broken links in Markdown files |\n+| `--check-http` | Also validate HTTP/HTTPS URLs (requires `--check-links`) |","path":"apps/gts-docs-validator/README.md","commit_id":"b1ff420153eddfa3ad03be9f8e80520c81b20f5f","original_commit_id":"4e6fda46a32379f0662631fda0b4e6c73dc1ddfc","user":{"login":"coderabbitai[bot]","id":136622811,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOCCSy2w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/347564?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/coderabbitai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"_⚠️ Potential issue_ | _🟡 Minor_\n\n**Clarify `--check-http` status in the options table.**\n\nIf HTTP checks remain unimplemented, consider noting that here to avoid implying it’s active.\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nIn `@apps/gts-docs-validator/README.md` around lines 50 - 51, Update the options\ntable to clearly indicate the implementation status of the `--check-http` flag:\nif HTTP/HTTPS URL validation is not yet implemented, change the `--check-http`\ndescription to something like \"Also validate HTTP/HTTPS URLs (requires\n`--check-links`) — not yet implemented\" or add a parenthetical\n\"experimental/unimplemented\" note next to `--check-http`; ensure `--check-links`\nremains described as \"Check for broken links in Markdown files\" and that the two\nflags' relationship (`--check-http` requires `--check-links`) is still stated.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- fingerprinting:phantom:medusa:eagle -->\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment by CodeRabbit -->\n\n✅ Addressed in commit 5db68af","created_at":"2026-01-21T06:14:44Z","updated_at":"2026-01-21T06:28:12Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/287#discussion_r2711117303","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/287","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2711117303"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/287#discussion_r2711117303"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/287"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2711117303/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":50,"start_side":"RIGHT","line":null,"original_line":51,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","original_position":26,"position":1,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2711117306","pull_request_review_id":3685511287,"id":2711117306,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs6hmF36","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,451 @@\n+//! Link checking functionality for Markdown files\n+//!\n+//! Validates that links in Markdown files are not broken:\n+//! - Checks local file references exist\n+//! - Checks HTTP/HTTPS URLs are reachable\n+//! - Detects anchor references to headings\n+\n+use std::collections::{HashMap, HashSet};\n+use std::fs;\n+use std::path::{Path, PathBuf};\n+\n+use regex::Regex;\n+use serde::Serialize;\n+\n+/// Represents a link found in a Markdown file\n+#[derive(Debug, Clone)]\n+pub struct MarkdownLink {\n+    pub text: String,\n+    pub url: String,\n+    pub line: usize,\n+    pub column: usize,\n+}\n+\n+/// Types of links\n+#[derive(Debug, Clone, PartialEq, Eq)]\n+pub enum LinkType {\n+    LocalFile,\n+    LocalAnchor,\n+    Http,\n+    Https,\n+    Mailto,\n+    Other,\n+}\n+\n+/// Represents a broken link error\n+#[derive(Debug, Clone, Serialize)]\n+pub struct LinkError {\n+    pub file: PathBuf,\n+    pub line: usize,\n+    pub column: usize,\n+    pub link_text: String,\n+    pub link_url: String,\n+    pub error: String,\n+}\n+\n+/// Result of link checking\n+#[derive(Debug, Default)]\n+pub struct LinkCheckResult {\n+    pub errors: Vec<LinkError>,\n+    pub files_scanned: usize,\n+    pub links_checked: usize,\n+}\n+\n+impl LinkCheckResult {\n+    #[must_use]\n+    pub fn new(files_scanned: usize) -> Self {\n+        Self {\n+            errors: Vec::new(),\n+            files_scanned,\n+            links_checked: 0,\n+        }\n+    }\n+\n+    pub fn add_error(&mut self, error: LinkError) {\n+        self.errors.push(error);\n+    }\n+\n+    pub fn increment_links_checked(&mut self) {\n+        self.links_checked += 1;\n+    }\n+\n+    #[must_use]\n+    pub fn is_ok(&self) -> bool {\n+        self.errors.is_empty()\n+    }\n+}\n+\n+/// Extract all Markdown links from content\n+/// Supports:\n+/// - [text](url)\n+/// - [text](url \"title\")\n+/// - <url>\n+#[must_use]\n+pub fn extract_markdown_links(content: &str) -> Vec<MarkdownLink> {\n+    let mut links = Vec::new();\n+\n+    // Pattern for [text](url) or [text](url \"title\")\n+    let link_pattern = Regex::new(r\"\\[([^\\]]+)\\]\\(([^\\)]+)\\)\").expect(\"Invalid regex\");\n+\n+    // Pattern for <url>\n+    let autolink_pattern = Regex::new(r\"<(https?://[^>]+)>\").expect(\"Invalid regex\");\n+\n+    let lines: Vec<&str> = content.lines().collect();\n+\n+    for (line_idx, line) in lines.iter().enumerate() {\n+        let line_num = line_idx + 1;\n+\n+        // Extract [text](url) style links\n+        for cap in link_pattern.captures_iter(line) {\n+            if let (Some(text_match), Some(url_match)) = (cap.get(1), cap.get(2)) {\n+                let text = text_match.as_str().to_owned();\n+                let url_full = url_match.as_str();\n+\n+                // Remove optional title from URL (e.g., \"url \"title\"\" -> \"url\")\n+                let url = url_full\n+                    .split_whitespace()\n+                    .next()\n+                    .unwrap_or(url_full)\n+                    .trim_matches('\"')\n+                    .to_owned();\n+\n+                links.push(MarkdownLink {\n+                    text,\n+                    url,\n+                    line: line_num,\n+                    column: url_match.start() + 1,\n+                });\n+            }\n+        }\n+\n+        // Extract <url> style autolinks\n+        for cap in autolink_pattern.captures_iter(line) {\n+            if let Some(url_match) = cap.get(1) {\n+                let url = url_match.as_str().to_owned();\n+                links.push(MarkdownLink {\n+                    text: url.clone(),\n+                    url,\n+                    line: line_num,\n+                    column: url_match.start() + 1,\n+                });\n+            }\n+        }\n+    }\n+\n+    links\n+}\n+\n+/// Determine the type of a link\n+#[must_use]\n+pub fn classify_link(url: &str) -> LinkType {\n+    if url.starts_with(\"http://\") {\n+        LinkType::Http\n+    } else if url.starts_with(\"https://\") {\n+        LinkType::Https\n+    } else if url.starts_with(\"mailto:\") {\n+        LinkType::Mailto\n+    } else if url.starts_with('#') {\n+        LinkType::LocalAnchor\n+    } else if url.starts_with(\"ftp://\") || url.starts_with(\"file://\") {\n+        LinkType::Other\n+    } else {\n+        LinkType::LocalFile\n+    }\n+}\n+\n+/// Extract headings from Markdown content for anchor validation\n+#[must_use]\n+pub fn extract_headings(content: &str) -> HashSet<String> {\n+    let mut headings = HashSet::new();\n+    let heading_pattern = Regex::new(r\"^#{1,6}\\s+(.+)$\").expect(\"Invalid regex\");\n+\n+    for line in content.lines() {\n+        if let Some(cap) = heading_pattern.captures(line) {\n+            if let Some(heading_match) = cap.get(1) {\n+                let heading = heading_match.as_str().trim();\n+                // Convert to anchor format: lowercase, replace spaces with hyphens\n+                let anchor = heading\n+                    .to_lowercase()\n+                    .replace(' ', \"-\")\n+                    .chars()\n+                    .filter(|c| c.is_alphanumeric() || *c == '-' || *c == '_')\n+                    .collect::<String>();\n+                headings.insert(format!(\"#{anchor}\"));\n+            }\n+        }\n+    }\n+\n+    headings\n+}\n+\n+/// Check if a local file link is valid\n+pub fn check_local_file_link(\n+    base_path: &Path,\n+    link_url: &str,\n+) -> Result<(), String> {\n+    // Split anchor from path\n+    let (file_path, anchor) = if let Some(pos) = link_url.find('#') {\n+        (&link_url[..pos], Some(&link_url[pos..]))\n+    } else {\n+        (link_url, None)\n+    };\n+\n+    // Resolve relative path\n+    let full_path = if file_path.is_empty() {\n+        // Just an anchor reference to current file\n+        base_path.to_path_buf()\n+    } else {\n+        let parent = base_path.parent().unwrap_or(base_path);\n+        parent.join(file_path)\n+    };\n+\n+    // Check if path exists (file or directory)\n+    if !full_path.exists() {\n+        return Err(format!(\"Path not found: {}\", full_path.display()));\n+    }\n+\n+    // If it's a directory, that's valid (directory links are allowed)\n+    if full_path.is_dir() {\n+        // Optionally check if directory contains a README.md\n+        let readme_path = full_path.join(\"README.md\");\n+        if !readme_path.exists() {\n+            // Just a warning in verbose mode, not an error\n+            // Directory links without README are still valid\n+        }\n+        return Ok(());\n+    }\n+\n+    // If it's a file, validate it exists (already checked above)\n+    // If there's an anchor, validate it exists in the target file\n+    if let Some(anchor_ref) = anchor {\n+        if full_path.extension().and_then(|e| e.to_str()) == Some(\"md\") {\n+            if let Ok(content) = fs::read_to_string(&full_path) {\n+                let headings = extract_headings(&content);\n+                if !headings.contains(anchor_ref) {\n+                    return Err(format!(\n+                        \"Anchor '{}' not found in {}\",\n+                        anchor_ref,\n+                        full_path.display()\n+                    ));\n+                }\n+            }\n+        }\n+    }\n+\n+    Ok(())\n+}","path":"apps/gts-docs-validator/src/link_checker.rs","commit_id":"051bc84c058df86d1cff0737e79982e7daa27652","original_commit_id":"4e6fda46a32379f0662631fda0b4e6c73dc1ddfc","user":{"login":"coderabbitai[bot]","id":136622811,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOCCSy2w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/347564?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/coderabbitai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"_⚠️ Potential issue_ | _🟡 Minor_\n\n**Anchor validation skips unreadable files.**\n\nIf the file can’t be read, anchor checks silently pass, which can hide real failures. Consider surfacing a read error when an anchor is present.\n\n<details>\n<summary>Proposed fix</summary>\n\n```diff\n-        if full_path.extension().and_then(|e| e.to_str()) == Some(\"md\") {\n-            if let Ok(content) = fs::read_to_string(&full_path) {\n-                let headings = extract_headings(&content);\n-                if !headings.contains(anchor_ref) {\n-                    return Err(format!(\n-                        \"Anchor '{}' not found in {}\",\n-                        anchor_ref,\n-                        full_path.display()\n-                    ));\n-                }\n-            }\n-        }\n+        if full_path.extension().and_then(|e| e.to_str()) == Some(\"md\") {\n+            let content = fs::read_to_string(&full_path)\n+                .map_err(|e| format!(\"Failed to read {}: {e}\", full_path.display()))?;\n+            let headings = extract_headings(&content);\n+            if !headings.contains(anchor_ref) {\n+                return Err(format!(\n+                    \"Anchor '{}' not found in {}\",\n+                    anchor_ref,\n+                    full_path.display()\n+                ));\n+            }\n+        }\n```\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nIn `@apps/gts-docs-validator/src/link_checker.rs` around lines 181 - 236, The\nanchor validation in check_local_file_link currently ignores errors when reading\nthe target file (fs::read_to_string), letting anchor checks silently pass;\nupdate check_local_file_link so that when an anchor_ref is present and the\ntarget file is expected to be an .md, any error returned by\nfs::read_to_string(&full_path) is propagated as an Err with a clear message\n(include the anchor_ref and full_path.display()), rather than treating the read\nfailure as a successful anchor check; keep using extract_headings(&content) on\nsuccessful reads to validate the anchor.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- fingerprinting:phantom:medusa:eagle -->\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated reply by CodeRabbit -->","created_at":"2026-01-21T06:14:44Z","updated_at":"2026-01-22T17:49:28Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/287#discussion_r2711117306","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/287","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2711117306"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/287#discussion_r2711117306"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/287"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2711117306/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":181,"start_side":"RIGHT","line":null,"original_line":236,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","original_position":236,"position":1,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2711117314","pull_request_review_id":3685511287,"id":2711117314,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs6hmF4C","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,451 @@\n+//! Link checking functionality for Markdown files\n+//!\n+//! Validates that links in Markdown files are not broken:\n+//! - Checks local file references exist\n+//! - Checks HTTP/HTTPS URLs are reachable\n+//! - Detects anchor references to headings\n+\n+use std::collections::{HashMap, HashSet};\n+use std::fs;\n+use std::path::{Path, PathBuf};\n+\n+use regex::Regex;\n+use serde::Serialize;\n+\n+/// Represents a link found in a Markdown file\n+#[derive(Debug, Clone)]\n+pub struct MarkdownLink {\n+    pub text: String,\n+    pub url: String,\n+    pub line: usize,\n+    pub column: usize,\n+}\n+\n+/// Types of links\n+#[derive(Debug, Clone, PartialEq, Eq)]\n+pub enum LinkType {\n+    LocalFile,\n+    LocalAnchor,\n+    Http,\n+    Https,\n+    Mailto,\n+    Other,\n+}\n+\n+/// Represents a broken link error\n+#[derive(Debug, Clone, Serialize)]\n+pub struct LinkError {\n+    pub file: PathBuf,\n+    pub line: usize,\n+    pub column: usize,\n+    pub link_text: String,\n+    pub link_url: String,\n+    pub error: String,\n+}\n+\n+/// Result of link checking\n+#[derive(Debug, Default)]\n+pub struct LinkCheckResult {\n+    pub errors: Vec<LinkError>,\n+    pub files_scanned: usize,\n+    pub links_checked: usize,\n+}\n+\n+impl LinkCheckResult {\n+    #[must_use]\n+    pub fn new(files_scanned: usize) -> Self {\n+        Self {\n+            errors: Vec::new(),\n+            files_scanned,\n+            links_checked: 0,\n+        }\n+    }\n+\n+    pub fn add_error(&mut self, error: LinkError) {\n+        self.errors.push(error);\n+    }\n+\n+    pub fn increment_links_checked(&mut self) {\n+        self.links_checked += 1;\n+    }\n+\n+    #[must_use]\n+    pub fn is_ok(&self) -> bool {\n+        self.errors.is_empty()\n+    }\n+}\n+\n+/// Extract all Markdown links from content\n+/// Supports:\n+/// - [text](url)\n+/// - [text](url \"title\")\n+/// - <url>\n+#[must_use]\n+pub fn extract_markdown_links(content: &str) -> Vec<MarkdownLink> {\n+    let mut links = Vec::new();\n+\n+    // Pattern for [text](url) or [text](url \"title\")\n+    let link_pattern = Regex::new(r\"\\[([^\\]]+)\\]\\(([^\\)]+)\\)\").expect(\"Invalid regex\");\n+\n+    // Pattern for <url>\n+    let autolink_pattern = Regex::new(r\"<(https?://[^>]+)>\").expect(\"Invalid regex\");\n+\n+    let lines: Vec<&str> = content.lines().collect();\n+\n+    for (line_idx, line) in lines.iter().enumerate() {\n+        let line_num = line_idx + 1;\n+\n+        // Extract [text](url) style links\n+        for cap in link_pattern.captures_iter(line) {\n+            if let (Some(text_match), Some(url_match)) = (cap.get(1), cap.get(2)) {\n+                let text = text_match.as_str().to_owned();\n+                let url_full = url_match.as_str();\n+\n+                // Remove optional title from URL (e.g., \"url \"title\"\" -> \"url\")\n+                let url = url_full\n+                    .split_whitespace()\n+                    .next()\n+                    .unwrap_or(url_full)\n+                    .trim_matches('\"')\n+                    .to_owned();\n+\n+                links.push(MarkdownLink {\n+                    text,\n+                    url,\n+                    line: line_num,\n+                    column: url_match.start() + 1,\n+                });\n+            }\n+        }\n+\n+        // Extract <url> style autolinks\n+        for cap in autolink_pattern.captures_iter(line) {\n+            if let Some(url_match) = cap.get(1) {\n+                let url = url_match.as_str().to_owned();\n+                links.push(MarkdownLink {\n+                    text: url.clone(),\n+                    url,\n+                    line: line_num,\n+                    column: url_match.start() + 1,\n+                });\n+            }\n+        }\n+    }\n+\n+    links\n+}\n+\n+/// Determine the type of a link\n+#[must_use]\n+pub fn classify_link(url: &str) -> LinkType {\n+    if url.starts_with(\"http://\") {\n+        LinkType::Http\n+    } else if url.starts_with(\"https://\") {\n+        LinkType::Https\n+    } else if url.starts_with(\"mailto:\") {\n+        LinkType::Mailto\n+    } else if url.starts_with('#') {\n+        LinkType::LocalAnchor\n+    } else if url.starts_with(\"ftp://\") || url.starts_with(\"file://\") {\n+        LinkType::Other\n+    } else {\n+        LinkType::LocalFile\n+    }\n+}\n+\n+/// Extract headings from Markdown content for anchor validation\n+#[must_use]\n+pub fn extract_headings(content: &str) -> HashSet<String> {\n+    let mut headings = HashSet::new();\n+    let heading_pattern = Regex::new(r\"^#{1,6}\\s+(.+)$\").expect(\"Invalid regex\");\n+\n+    for line in content.lines() {\n+        if let Some(cap) = heading_pattern.captures(line) {\n+            if let Some(heading_match) = cap.get(1) {\n+                let heading = heading_match.as_str().trim();\n+                // Convert to anchor format: lowercase, replace spaces with hyphens\n+                let anchor = heading\n+                    .to_lowercase()\n+                    .replace(' ', \"-\")\n+                    .chars()\n+                    .filter(|c| c.is_alphanumeric() || *c == '-' || *c == '_')\n+                    .collect::<String>();\n+                headings.insert(format!(\"#{anchor}\"));\n+            }\n+        }\n+    }\n+\n+    headings\n+}\n+\n+/// Check if a local file link is valid\n+pub fn check_local_file_link(\n+    base_path: &Path,\n+    link_url: &str,\n+) -> Result<(), String> {\n+    // Split anchor from path\n+    let (file_path, anchor) = if let Some(pos) = link_url.find('#') {\n+        (&link_url[..pos], Some(&link_url[pos..]))\n+    } else {\n+        (link_url, None)\n+    };\n+\n+    // Resolve relative path\n+    let full_path = if file_path.is_empty() {\n+        // Just an anchor reference to current file\n+        base_path.to_path_buf()\n+    } else {\n+        let parent = base_path.parent().unwrap_or(base_path);\n+        parent.join(file_path)\n+    };\n+\n+    // Check if path exists (file or directory)\n+    if !full_path.exists() {\n+        return Err(format!(\"Path not found: {}\", full_path.display()));\n+    }\n+\n+    // If it's a directory, that's valid (directory links are allowed)\n+    if full_path.is_dir() {\n+        // Optionally check if directory contains a README.md\n+        let readme_path = full_path.join(\"README.md\");\n+        if !readme_path.exists() {\n+            // Just a warning in verbose mode, not an error\n+            // Directory links without README are still valid\n+        }\n+        return Ok(());\n+    }\n+\n+    // If it's a file, validate it exists (already checked above)\n+    // If there's an anchor, validate it exists in the target file\n+    if let Some(anchor_ref) = anchor {\n+        if full_path.extension().and_then(|e| e.to_str()) == Some(\"md\") {\n+            if let Ok(content) = fs::read_to_string(&full_path) {\n+                let headings = extract_headings(&content);\n+                if !headings.contains(anchor_ref) {\n+                    return Err(format!(\n+                        \"Anchor '{}' not found in {}\",\n+                        anchor_ref,\n+                        full_path.display()\n+                    ));\n+                }\n+            }\n+        }\n+    }\n+\n+    Ok(())\n+}\n+\n+/// Check if a local anchor exists in the given content\n+pub fn check_local_anchor(anchor: &str, headings: &HashSet<String>) -> Result<(), String> {\n+    if !headings.contains(anchor) {\n+        return Err(format!(\"Anchor '{anchor}' not found in current file\"));\n+    }\n+    Ok(())\n+}\n+\n+/// Check all links in a Markdown file\n+#[must_use]\n+pub fn check_links_in_file(\n+    file_path: &Path,\n+    check_http: bool,\n+    verbose: bool,\n+) -> Vec<LinkError> {\n+    let mut errors = Vec::new();\n+\n+    let content = match fs::read_to_string(file_path) {\n+        Ok(c) => c,\n+        Err(e) => {\n+            return vec![LinkError {\n+                file: file_path.to_path_buf(),\n+                line: 0,\n+                column: 0,\n+                link_text: String::new(),\n+                link_url: String::new(),\n+                error: format!(\"Failed to read file: {e}\"),\n+            }];\n+        }\n+    };\n+\n+    let links = extract_markdown_links(&content);\n+    let headings = extract_headings(&content);\n+\n+    for link in links {\n+        if verbose {\n+            eprintln!(\"    Checking link: {} -> {}\", link.text, link.url);\n+        }\n+\n+        let link_type = classify_link(&link.url);\n+\n+        let check_result = match link_type {\n+            LinkType::LocalFile => check_local_file_link(file_path, &link.url),\n+            LinkType::LocalAnchor => check_local_anchor(&link.url, &headings),\n+            LinkType::Http | LinkType::Https => {\n+                if check_http {\n+                    // HTTP checking would require async runtime\n+                    // For now, we'll skip HTTP checks in this implementation\n+                    // and focus on local file links\n+                    if verbose {\n+                        eprintln!(\"      Skipping HTTP check (not implemented yet)\");\n+                    }\n+                    Ok(())\n+                } else {\n+                    Ok(())\n+                }\n+            }\n+            LinkType::Mailto | LinkType::Other => {\n+                // Skip mailto and other special links\n+                Ok(())\n+            }\n+        };\n+\n+        if let Err(error_msg) = check_result {\n+            errors.push(LinkError {\n+                file: file_path.to_path_buf(),\n+                line: link.line,\n+                column: link.column,\n+                link_text: link.text,\n+                link_url: link.url,\n+                error: error_msg,\n+            });\n+        }\n+    }\n+\n+    errors\n+}","path":"apps/gts-docs-validator/src/link_checker.rs","commit_id":"051bc84c058df86d1cff0737e79982e7daa27652","original_commit_id":"4e6fda46a32379f0662631fda0b4e6c73dc1ddfc","user":{"login":"coderabbitai[bot]","id":136622811,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOCCSy2w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/347564?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/coderabbitai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"_⚠️ Potential issue_ | _🟠 Major_\n\n**`--check-http` currently does no validation.**\n\nWith `check_http = true`, HTTP/HTTPS links are accepted unconditionally, which can give a false sense of safety. Either implement the check or fail explicitly until it’s supported.\n\n<details>\n<summary>Proposed fix (fail fast when HTTP checks are requested)</summary>\n\n```diff\n             LinkType::Http | LinkType::Https => {\n                 if check_http {\n-                    // HTTP checking would require async runtime\n-                    // For now, we'll skip HTTP checks in this implementation\n-                    // and focus on local file links\n-                    if verbose {\n-                        eprintln!(\"      Skipping HTTP check (not implemented yet)\");\n-                    }\n-                    Ok(())\n+                    if verbose {\n+                        eprintln!(\"      HTTP check not implemented yet\");\n+                    }\n+                    Err(\"HTTP/HTTPS validation is not implemented yet\".to_string())\n                 } else {\n                     Ok(())\n                 }\n             }\n```\n</details>\n\n<!-- suggestion_start -->\n\n<details>\n<summary>📝 Committable suggestion</summary>\n\n> ‼️ **IMPORTANT**\n> Carefully review the code before committing. Ensure that it accurately replaces the highlighted code, contains no missing lines, and has no issues with indentation. Thoroughly test & benchmark the code to ensure it meets the requirements.\n\n```suggestion\n/// Check all links in a Markdown file\n#[must_use]\npub fn check_links_in_file(\n    file_path: &Path,\n    check_http: bool,\n    verbose: bool,\n) -> Vec<LinkError> {\n    let mut errors = Vec::new();\n\n    let content = match fs::read_to_string(file_path) {\n        Ok(c) => c,\n        Err(e) => {\n            return vec![LinkError {\n                file: file_path.to_path_buf(),\n                line: 0,\n                column: 0,\n                link_text: String::new(),\n                link_url: String::new(),\n                error: format!(\"Failed to read file: {e}\"),\n            }];\n        }\n    };\n\n    let links = extract_markdown_links(&content);\n    let headings = extract_headings(&content);\n\n    for link in links {\n        if verbose {\n            eprintln!(\"    Checking link: {} -> {}\", link.text, link.url);\n        }\n\n        let link_type = classify_link(&link.url);\n\n        let check_result = match link_type {\n            LinkType::LocalFile => check_local_file_link(file_path, &link.url),\n            LinkType::LocalAnchor => check_local_anchor(&link.url, &headings),\n            LinkType::Http | LinkType::Https => {\n                if check_http {\n                    if verbose {\n                        eprintln!(\"      HTTP check not implemented yet\");\n                    }\n                    Err(\"HTTP/HTTPS validation is not implemented yet\".to_string())\n                } else {\n                    Ok(())\n                }\n            }\n            LinkType::Mailto | LinkType::Other => {\n                // Skip mailto and other special links\n                Ok(())\n            }\n        };\n\n        if let Err(error_msg) = check_result {\n            errors.push(LinkError {\n                file: file_path.to_path_buf(),\n                line: link.line,\n                column: link.column,\n                link_text: link.text,\n                link_url: link.url,\n                error: error_msg,\n            });\n        }\n    }\n\n    errors\n}\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- suggestion_end -->\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nIn `@apps/gts-docs-validator/src/link_checker.rs` around lines 246 - 314, The\ncurrent check_links_in_file accepts HTTP/HTTPS links unconditionally when\ncheck_http is true; update the match arm for LinkType::Http and LinkType::Https\ninside check_links_in_file so that if check_http is true it returns an Err with\na clear message (e.g., \"HTTP checks not implemented\" or similar) instead of\nOk(), and only treat them as Ok() when check_http is false; reference the\nclassify_link/LinkType enum and the check_result handling to ensure the error\nbubbles into the LinkError vector rather than silently passing.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- fingerprinting:phantom:medusa:eagle -->\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment by CodeRabbit -->","created_at":"2026-01-21T06:14:45Z","updated_at":"2026-01-21T06:14:46Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/287#discussion_r2711117314","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/287","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2711117314"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/287#discussion_r2711117314"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/287"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2711117314/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":246,"start_side":"RIGHT","line":null,"original_line":314,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","original_position":314,"position":1,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2711117319","pull_request_review_id":3685511287,"id":2711117319,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs6hmF4H","diff_hunk":"@@ -70,6 +72,14 @@ struct Cli {\n     /// Show verbose output including file scanning progress\n     #[arg(long, short = 'v')]\n     verbose: bool,\n+\n+    /// Check for broken links in Markdown files\n+    #[arg(long)]\n+    check_links: bool,\n+\n+    /// Check HTTP/HTTPS links (slower, requires network)\n+    #[arg(long)]\n+    check_http: bool,","path":"apps/gts-docs-validator/src/main.rs","commit_id":"833f93f524ff9ed110378237feb54fbfff76e1d8","original_commit_id":"4e6fda46a32379f0662631fda0b4e6c73dc1ddfc","user":{"login":"coderabbitai[bot]","id":136622811,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOCCSy2w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/347564?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/coderabbitai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"_⚠️ Potential issue_ | _🟡 Minor_\n\n**Enforce `--check-links` as a prerequisite for `--check-http` in the CLI.**\n\nCurrently, `--check-http` is accepted but completely ignored unless `--check-links` is set, since the validator only uses the `check_http` flag within the `extract_links()` function, which is only called when `check_links` is true. Add the `requires` constraint to prevent confusing users who might enable HTTP checking without realizing it has no effect.\n\n<details>\n<summary>Proposed fix</summary>\n\n```diff\n     /// Check HTTP/HTTPS links (slower, requires network)\n-    #[arg(long)]\n+    #[arg(long, requires = \"check_links\")]\n     check_http: bool,\n```\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nIn `@apps/gts-docs-validator/src/main.rs` around lines 76 - 82, Add a CLI\nconstraint so --check-http cannot be used without --check-links: modify the\nargument attribute on the check_http field (the #[arg(long)] on check_http) to\ninclude a requires pointing at the check_links flag (e.g., #[arg(long, requires\n= \"check_links\")]) so the parser enforces that check_links is set; this ensures\nbehavior in extract_links() that reads check_http is not silently ignored.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- fingerprinting:phantom:medusa:eagle -->\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment by CodeRabbit -->","created_at":"2026-01-21T06:14:45Z","updated_at":"2026-01-21T06:14:46Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/287#discussion_r2711117319","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/287","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2711117319"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/287#discussion_r2711117319"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/287"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2711117319/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":76,"start_side":"RIGHT","line":null,"original_line":82,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","original_position":27,"position":1,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2711117321","pull_request_review_id":3685511287,"id":2711117321,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs6hmF4J","diff_hunk":"@@ -121,30 +131,75 @@ fn main() -> ExitCode {\n         return ExitCode::FAILURE;\n     }\n \n-    // Scan all files and collect errors\n-    let mut result = ValidationResult::new(files.len());\n+    // Determine what to check\n+    let check_gts = !cli.check_links; // Default behavior or explicit GTS check\n+    let check_links = cli.check_links;\n \n-    for file_path in &files {\n-        if cli.verbose {\n-            eprintln!(\"  Scanning: {}\", file_path.display());\n+    let mut exit_code = ExitCode::SUCCESS;\n+\n+    // Check GTS identifiers\n+    if check_gts {\n+        let mut result = ValidationResult::new(files.len());\n+\n+        for file_path in &files {\n+            if cli.verbose {\n+                eprintln!(\"  Scanning: {}\", file_path.display());\n+            }\n+\n+            let file_errors = scan_file(file_path, cli.vendor.as_deref(), cli.verbose);\n+            result.add_errors(file_errors);\n         }\n \n-        let file_errors = scan_file(file_path, cli.vendor.as_deref(), cli.verbose);\n-        result.add_errors(file_errors);\n-    }\n+        // Output results\n+        if cli.json {\n+            print_json_results(&result);\n+        } else {\n+            print_results(&result, cli.verbose);\n+        }\n \n-    // Output results\n-    if cli.json {\n-        print_json_results(&result);\n-    } else {\n-        print_results(&result, cli.verbose);\n+        if !result.is_ok() {\n+            exit_code = ExitCode::FAILURE;\n+        }\n     }\n \n-    if result.is_ok() {\n-        ExitCode::SUCCESS\n-    } else {\n-        ExitCode::FAILURE\n+    // Check links in Markdown files\n+    if check_links {\n+        // Filter to only .md files\n+        let md_files: Vec<PathBuf> = files\n+            .iter()\n+            .filter(|f| {\n+                f.extension()\n+                    .and_then(|e| e.to_str())\n+                    .map(|e| e.eq_ignore_ascii_case(\"md\"))\n+                    .unwrap_or(false)\n+            })\n+            .cloned()\n+            .collect();\n+\n+        if md_files.is_empty() {\n+            eprintln!(\"No Markdown files found to check links.\");\n+            return ExitCode::FAILURE;\n+        }\n+\n+        if cli.verbose {\n+            eprintln!(\"Checking links in {} Markdown files\", md_files.len());\n+        }\n+\n+        let link_result = check_links_in_files(&md_files, cli.check_http, cli.verbose);\n+\n+        // Output link check results\n+        if cli.json {\n+            print_link_json_results(&link_result);\n+        } else {\n+            print_link_results(&link_result, cli.verbose);\n+        }\n+\n+        if !link_result.is_ok() {\n+            exit_code = ExitCode::FAILURE;\n+        }","path":"apps/gts-docs-validator/src/main.rs","commit_id":"051bc84c058df86d1cff0737e79982e7daa27652","original_commit_id":"4e6fda46a32379f0662631fda0b4e6c73dc1ddfc","user":{"login":"coderabbitai[bot]","id":136622811,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOCCSy2w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/347564?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/coderabbitai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"_⚠️ Potential issue_ | _🟠 Major_\n\n**`--check-links` currently disables GTS validation.**\n\nGiven the docs present link checking as an additional capability, consider running GTS validation regardless and adding a separate “links-only” flag if you need that mode.\n\n<details>\n<summary>Proposed fix (additive link checking)</summary>\n\n```diff\n-    // Determine what to check\n-    let check_gts = !cli.check_links; // Default behavior or explicit GTS check\n-    let check_links = cli.check_links;\n+    // Determine what to check\n+    let check_gts = true; // Always run GTS validation\n+    let check_links = cli.check_links;\n```\n</details>\n\n<!-- suggestion_start -->\n\n<details>\n<summary>📝 Committable suggestion</summary>\n\n> ‼️ **IMPORTANT**\n> Carefully review the code before committing. Ensure that it accurately replaces the highlighted code, contains no missing lines, and has no issues with indentation. Thoroughly test & benchmark the code to ensure it meets the requirements.\n\n```suggestion\n    // Determine what to check\n    let check_gts = true; // Always run GTS validation\n    let check_links = cli.check_links;\n\n    let mut exit_code = ExitCode::SUCCESS;\n\n    // Check GTS identifiers\n    if check_gts {\n        let mut result = ValidationResult::new(files.len());\n\n        for file_path in &files {\n            if cli.verbose {\n                eprintln!(\"  Scanning: {}\", file_path.display());\n            }\n\n            let file_errors = scan_file(file_path, cli.vendor.as_deref(), cli.verbose);\n            result.add_errors(file_errors);\n        }\n\n        // Output results\n        if cli.json {\n            print_json_results(&result);\n        } else {\n            print_results(&result, cli.verbose);\n        }\n\n        if !result.is_ok() {\n            exit_code = ExitCode::FAILURE;\n        }\n    }\n\n    // Check links in Markdown files\n    if check_links {\n        // Filter to only .md files\n        let md_files: Vec<PathBuf> = files\n            .iter()\n            .filter(|f| {\n                f.extension()\n                    .and_then(|e| e.to_str())\n                    .map(|e| e.eq_ignore_ascii_case(\"md\"))\n                    .unwrap_or(false)\n            })\n            .cloned()\n            .collect();\n\n        if md_files.is_empty() {\n            eprintln!(\"No Markdown files found to check links.\");\n            return ExitCode::FAILURE;\n        }\n\n        if cli.verbose {\n            eprintln!(\"Checking links in {} Markdown files\", md_files.len());\n        }\n\n        let link_result = check_links_in_files(&md_files, cli.check_http, cli.verbose);\n\n        // Output link check results\n        if cli.json {\n            print_link_json_results(&link_result);\n        } else {\n            print_link_results(&link_result, cli.verbose);\n        }\n\n        if !link_result.is_ok() {\n            exit_code = ExitCode::FAILURE;\n        }\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- suggestion_end -->\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nIn `@apps/gts-docs-validator/src/main.rs` around lines 134 - 199, The current\nlogic disables GTS validation when cli.check_links is true; change it so GTS\nvalidation runs by default and introduce a new \"links-only\" flag (e.g.,\ncli.links_only) to opt out of GTS if needed. Concretely: stop setting check_gts\n= !cli.check_links and instead compute check_gts = !cli.links_only (or true by\ndefault), add the new CLI flag parsing for links-only, and keep the existing\ncheck_links = cli.check_links behavior; ensure both validation blocks (the GTS\nblock using ValidationResult and the Markdown link block using\ncheck_links_in_files) run independently and the exit_code logic still sets\nExitCode::FAILURE if either result.is_ok() is false.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- fingerprinting:phantom:medusa:eagle -->\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment by CodeRabbit -->\n\n✅ Addressed in commit 5db68af","created_at":"2026-01-21T06:14:45Z","updated_at":"2026-01-21T06:28:14Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/287#discussion_r2711117321","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/287","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2711117321"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/287#discussion_r2711117321"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/287"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2711117321/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":134,"start_side":"RIGHT","line":null,"original_line":199,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","original_position":117,"position":1,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2711175828","pull_request_review_id":3685578560,"id":2711175828,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs6hmUKU","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,432 @@\n+//! Link checking functionality for Markdown files\n+//!\n+//! Validates that links in Markdown files are not broken:\n+//! - Checks local file references exist\n+//! - Checks HTTP/HTTPS URLs are reachable\n+//! - Detects anchor references to headings\n+\n+use std::collections::{HashMap, HashSet};\n+use std::fs;\n+use std::path::{Path, PathBuf};\n+\n+use regex::Regex;\n+use serde::Serialize;\n+\n+/// Represents a link found in a Markdown file\n+#[derive(Debug, Clone)]\n+pub struct MarkdownLink {\n+    pub text: String,\n+    pub url: String,\n+    pub line: usize,\n+    pub column: usize,\n+}\n+\n+/// Types of links\n+#[derive(Debug, Clone, PartialEq, Eq)]\n+pub enum LinkType {\n+    LocalFile,\n+    LocalAnchor,\n+    Http,\n+    Https,\n+    Mailto,\n+    Other,\n+}\n+\n+/// Represents a broken link error\n+#[derive(Debug, Clone, Serialize)]\n+pub struct LinkError {\n+    pub file: PathBuf,\n+    pub line: usize,\n+    pub column: usize,\n+    pub link_text: String,\n+    pub link_url: String,\n+    pub error: String,\n+}\n+\n+/// Result of link checking\n+#[derive(Debug, Default)]\n+pub struct LinkCheckResult {\n+    pub errors: Vec<LinkError>,\n+    pub files_scanned: usize,\n+    pub links_checked: usize,\n+}\n+\n+impl LinkCheckResult {\n+    #[must_use]\n+    pub fn new(files_scanned: usize) -> Self {\n+        Self {\n+            errors: Vec::new(),\n+            files_scanned,\n+            links_checked: 0,\n+        }\n+    }\n+\n+    pub fn add_error(&mut self, error: LinkError) {\n+        self.errors.push(error);\n+    }\n+\n+    pub fn increment_links_checked(&mut self) {\n+        self.links_checked += 1;\n+    }\n+\n+    #[must_use]\n+    pub fn is_ok(&self) -> bool {\n+        self.errors.is_empty()\n+    }\n+}\n+\n+/// Extract all Markdown links from content\n+/// Supports:\n+/// - [text](url)\n+/// - [text](url \"title\")\n+/// - <url>\n+#[must_use]\n+pub fn extract_markdown_links(content: &str) -> Vec<MarkdownLink> {\n+    let mut links = Vec::new();\n+\n+    // Pattern for [text](url) or [text](url \"title\")\n+    let link_pattern = Regex::new(r\"\\[([^\\]]+)\\]\\(([^\\)]+)\\)\").expect(\"Invalid regex\");\n+\n+    // Pattern for <url>\n+    let autolink_pattern = Regex::new(r\"<(https?://[^>]+)>\").expect(\"Invalid regex\");\n+\n+    let lines: Vec<&str> = content.lines().collect();\n+\n+    for (line_idx, line) in lines.iter().enumerate() {\n+        let line_num = line_idx + 1;\n+\n+        // Extract [text](url) style links\n+        for cap in link_pattern.captures_iter(line) {\n+            if let (Some(text_match), Some(url_match)) = (cap.get(1), cap.get(2)) {\n+                let text = text_match.as_str().to_owned();\n+                let url_full = url_match.as_str();\n+\n+                // Remove optional title from URL (e.g., \"url \"title\"\" -> \"url\")\n+                let url = url_full\n+                    .split_whitespace()\n+                    .next()\n+                    .unwrap_or(url_full)\n+                    .trim_matches('\"')\n+                    .to_owned();\n+\n+                links.push(MarkdownLink {\n+                    text,\n+                    url,\n+                    line: line_num,\n+                    column: url_match.start() + 1,\n+                });\n+            }\n+        }\n+\n+        // Extract <url> style autolinks\n+        for cap in autolink_pattern.captures_iter(line) {\n+            if let Some(url_match) = cap.get(1) {\n+                let url = url_match.as_str().to_owned();\n+                links.push(MarkdownLink {\n+                    text: url.clone(),\n+                    url,\n+                    line: line_num,\n+                    column: url_match.start() + 1,\n+                });\n+            }\n+        }\n+    }\n+\n+    links\n+}\n+\n+/// Determine the type of a link\n+#[must_use]\n+pub fn classify_link(url: &str) -> LinkType {\n+    if url.starts_with(\"http://\") {\n+        LinkType::Http\n+    } else if url.starts_with(\"https://\") {\n+        LinkType::Https\n+    } else if url.starts_with(\"mailto:\") {\n+        LinkType::Mailto\n+    } else if url.starts_with('#') {\n+        LinkType::LocalAnchor\n+    } else if url.starts_with(\"ftp://\") || url.starts_with(\"file://\") {\n+        LinkType::Other\n+    } else {\n+        LinkType::LocalFile\n+    }\n+}\n+\n+/// Extract headings from Markdown content for anchor validation\n+#[must_use]\n+pub fn extract_headings(content: &str) -> HashSet<String> {\n+    let mut headings = HashSet::new();\n+    let heading_pattern = Regex::new(r\"^#{1,6}\\s+(.+)$\").expect(\"Invalid regex\");\n+\n+    for line in content.lines() {\n+        if let Some(cap) = heading_pattern.captures(line) {\n+            if let Some(heading_match) = cap.get(1) {\n+                let heading = heading_match.as_str().trim();\n+                // Convert to anchor format: lowercase, replace spaces with hyphens\n+                let anchor = heading\n+                    .to_lowercase()\n+                    .replace(' ', \"-\")\n+                    .chars()\n+                    .filter(|c| c.is_alphanumeric() || *c == '-' || *c == '_')\n+                    .collect::<String>();\n+                headings.insert(format!(\"#{anchor}\"));\n+            }\n+        }\n+    }\n+\n+    headings\n+}\n+\n+/// Check if a local file link is valid\n+pub fn check_local_file_link(base_path: &Path, link_url: &str) -> Result<(), String> {\n+    // Split anchor from path\n+    let (file_path, anchor) = if let Some(pos) = link_url.find('#') {\n+        (&link_url[..pos], Some(&link_url[pos..]))\n+    } else {\n+        (link_url, None)\n+    };\n+\n+    // Resolve relative path\n+    let full_path = if file_path.is_empty() {\n+        // Just an anchor reference to current file\n+        base_path.to_path_buf()\n+    } else {\n+        let parent = base_path.parent().unwrap_or(base_path);\n+        parent.join(file_path)\n+    };\n+\n+    // Check if path exists (file or directory)\n+    if !full_path.exists() {\n+        return Err(format!(\"Path not found: {}\", full_path.display()));\n+    }\n+\n+    // If it's a directory, that's valid (directory links are allowed)\n+    if full_path.is_dir() {\n+        // Optionally check if directory contains a README.md\n+        let readme_path = full_path.join(\"README.md\");\n+        if !readme_path.exists() {\n+            // Just a warning in verbose mode, not an error\n+            // Directory links without README are still valid\n+        }\n+        return Ok(());\n+    }\n+\n+    // If it's a file, validate it exists (already checked above)\n+    // If there's an anchor, validate it exists in the target file\n+    if let Some(anchor_ref) = anchor {\n+        if full_path.extension().and_then(|e| e.to_str()) == Some(\"md\") {\n+            if let Ok(content) = fs::read_to_string(&full_path) {\n+                let headings = extract_headings(&content);\n+                if !headings.contains(anchor_ref) {\n+                    return Err(format!(\n+                        \"Anchor '{}' not found in {}\",\n+                        anchor_ref,\n+                        full_path.display()\n+                    ));\n+                }\n+            }\n+        }\n+    }\n+\n+    Ok(())\n+}\n+\n+/// Check if a local anchor exists in the given content\n+pub fn check_local_anchor(anchor: &str, headings: &HashSet<String>) -> Result<(), String> {\n+    if !headings.contains(anchor) {\n+        return Err(format!(\"Anchor '{anchor}' not found in current file\"));\n+    }\n+    Ok(())\n+}\n+\n+/// Check all links in a Markdown file\n+#[must_use]\n+pub fn check_links_in_file(file_path: &Path, check_http: bool, verbose: bool) -> Vec<LinkError> {\n+    let mut errors = Vec::new();\n+\n+    let content = match fs::read_to_string(file_path) {\n+        Ok(c) => c,\n+        Err(e) => {\n+            return vec![LinkError {\n+                file: file_path.to_path_buf(),\n+                line: 0,\n+                column: 0,\n+                link_text: String::new(),\n+                link_url: String::new(),\n+                error: format!(\"Failed to read file: {e}\"),\n+            }];\n+        }\n+    };\n+\n+    let links = extract_markdown_links(&content);\n+    let headings = extract_headings(&content);\n+\n+    for link in links {\n+        if verbose {\n+            eprintln!(\"    Checking link: {} -> {}\", link.text, link.url);\n+        }\n+\n+        let link_type = classify_link(&link.url);\n+\n+        let check_result = match link_type {\n+            LinkType::LocalFile => check_local_file_link(file_path, &link.url),\n+            LinkType::LocalAnchor => check_local_anchor(&link.url, &headings),\n+            LinkType::Http | LinkType::Https => {\n+                if check_http {\n+                    // HTTP checking would require async runtime\n+                    // For now, we'll skip HTTP checks in this implementation\n+                    // and focus on local file links\n+                    if verbose {\n+                        eprintln!(\"      Skipping HTTP check (not implemented yet)\");\n+                    }\n+                    Ok(())\n+                } else {\n+                    Ok(())\n+                }\n+            }\n+            LinkType::Mailto | LinkType::Other => {\n+                // Skip mailto and other special links\n+                Ok(())\n+            }\n+        };\n+\n+        if let Err(error_msg) = check_result {\n+            errors.push(LinkError {\n+                file: file_path.to_path_buf(),\n+                line: link.line,\n+                column: link.column,\n+                link_text: link.text,\n+                link_url: link.url,\n+                error: error_msg,\n+            });\n+        }\n+    }\n+\n+    errors\n+}\n+\n+/// Check links in multiple files\n+#[must_use]\n+pub fn check_links_in_files(files: &[PathBuf], check_http: bool, verbose: bool) -> LinkCheckResult {\n+    let mut result = LinkCheckResult::new(files.len());\n+\n+    for file_path in files {\n+        if verbose {\n+            eprintln!(\"  Checking links in: {}\", file_path.display());\n+        }\n+\n+        let errors = check_likns_in_file(file_path, check_http, verbose);\n+        result.links_checked +=\n+            extract_markdown_links(&fs::read_to_string(file_path).unwrap_or_default()).len();","path":"apps/gts-docs-validator/src/link_checker.rs","commit_id":"051bc84c058df86d1cff0737e79982e7daa27652","original_commit_id":"6a3277bd9960ade001a7bb1219c25cb4295c389b","user":{"login":"coderabbitai[bot]","id":136622811,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOCCSy2w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/347564?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/coderabbitai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"_⚠️ Potential issue_ | _🔴 Critical_\n\n**Typo calls a non-existent function (compile error).**\n\n`check_likns_in_file` is misspelled and will fail to compile.\n\n<details>\n<summary>🛠️ Proposed fix</summary>\n\n```diff\n-        let errors = check_likns_in_file(file_path, check_http, verbose);\n+        let errors = check_links_in_file(file_path, check_http, verbose);\n```\n</details>\n\n<!-- suggestion_start -->\n\n<details>\n<summary>📝 Committable suggestion</summary>\n\n> ‼️ **IMPORTANT**\n> Carefully review the code before committing. Ensure that it accurately replaces the highlighted code, contains no missing lines, and has no issues with indentation. Thoroughly test & benchmark the code to ensure it meets the requirements.\n\n```suggestion\n/// Check links in multiple files\n#[must_use]\npub fn check_links_in_files(files: &[PathBuf], check_http: bool, verbose: bool) -> LinkCheckResult {\n    let mut result = LinkCheckResult::new(files.len());\n\n    for file_path in files {\n        if verbose {\n            eprintln!(\"  Checking links in: {}\", file_path.display());\n        }\n\n        let errors = check_links_in_file(file_path, check_http, verbose);\n        result.links_checked +=\n            extract_markdown_links(&fs::read_to_string(file_path).unwrap_or_default()).len();\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- suggestion_end -->\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nIn `@apps/gts-docs-validator/src/link_checker.rs` around lines 309 - 321, The code\nin check_links_in_files calls a misspelled function check_likns_in_file (causing\na compile error); update the call inside the loop to the correct function name\ncheck_links_in_file (or the actual intended function name if different) and\nensure the function definition matches that name so the reference in\ncheck_links_in_files resolves correctly.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- fingerprinting:phantom:medusa:eagle -->\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment by CodeRabbit -->\n\n✅ Addressed in commit 989c68e","created_at":"2026-01-21T06:39:26Z","updated_at":"2026-01-21T06:39:42Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/287#discussion_r2711175828","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/287","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2711175828"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/287#discussion_r2711175828"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/287"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2711175828/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":309,"start_side":"RIGHT","line":null,"original_line":321,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","original_position":321,"position":1,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2711223967","pull_request_review_id":3685634990,"id":2711223967,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs6hmf6f","diff_hunk":"@@ -245,29 +245,39 @@ A Dylint lint that prevents using `schemars::schema_for!()` on GTS-wrapped struc\n \n ### DE0903: Documentation Validator\n \n-A Rust CLI tool that validates GTS identifiers in documentation and configuration files.\n+A Rust CLI tool that validates GTS identifiers in documentation and configuration files, and checks for broken links in Markdown files.\n \n **What it checks:**\n+\n+*GTS Validation:*\n - All `.md`, `.json`, `.yaml`, `.yml` files in `docs/`, `modules/`, `libs/`, `examples/`\n - Skips intentionally invalid examples (marked with \"bad\", \"invalid\", \"❌\", etc.)\n - Allows wildcards in pattern/filter contexts\n - Optionally validates vendor consistency with `--vendor` flag\n - Tolerates example vendors: `acme`, `globex`, `example`, `demo`, `test`, `sample`, `tutorial`\n \n+*Link Checking:*\n+- Local file links in Markdown files (e.g., `[text](./file.md)`)\n+- Anchor links to headings (e.g., `[text](#heading)`)\n+- Relative path resolution from current file location\n+- Optional HTTP/HTTPS validation with `--check-http` flag\n+","path":"dylint_lints/README.md","commit_id":"5ce179f392fd6a0fddff12db719da1da08a0353c","original_commit_id":"acb7db7cab8facf7b0d0733d8212345a5b3f1fa1","user":{"login":"coderabbitai[bot]","id":136622811,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOCCSy2w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/347564?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/coderabbitai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"_⚠️ Potential issue_ | _🟡 Minor_\n\n**Clarify `--check-http` support in the DE0903 docs.**\n\nThe current implementation skips HTTP checks even when `--check-http` is provided, so this bullet reads as implemented when it’s not. Consider adding a “not implemented yet” note or removing the claim until it’s supported.  \n\n\n<details>\n<summary>📝 Suggested doc tweak</summary>\n\n```diff\n-* Optional HTTP/HTTPS validation with `--check-http` flag\n+* Optional HTTP/HTTPS validation with `--check-http` flag (not implemented yet)\n```\n</details>\n\n<!-- suggestion_start -->\n\n<details>\n<summary>📝 Committable suggestion</summary>\n\n> ‼️ **IMPORTANT**\n> Carefully review the code before committing. Ensure that it accurately replaces the highlighted code, contains no missing lines, and has no issues with indentation. Thoroughly test & benchmark the code to ensure it meets the requirements.\n\n```suggestion\nA Rust CLI tool that validates GTS identifiers in documentation and configuration files, and checks for broken links in Markdown files.\n\n**What it checks:**\n\n*GTS Validation:*\n- All `.md`, `.json`, `.yaml`, `.yml` files in `docs/`, `modules/`, `libs/`, `examples/`\n- Skips intentionally invalid examples (marked with \"bad\", \"invalid\", \"❌\", etc.)\n- Allows wildcards in pattern/filter contexts\n- Optionally validates vendor consistency with `--vendor` flag\n- Tolerates example vendors: `acme`, `globex`, `example`, `demo`, `test`, `sample`, `tutorial`\n\n*Link Checking:*\n- Local file links in Markdown files (e.g., `[text](./file.md)`)\n- Anchor links to headings (e.g., `[text](`#heading`)`)\n- Relative path resolution from current file location\n- Optional HTTP/HTTPS validation with `--check-http` flag (not implemented yet)\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- suggestion_end -->\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nIn `@dylint_lints/README.md` around lines 248 - 264, The Link Checking bullet\nincorrectly states HTTP/HTTPS validation with the --check-http flag is\nsupported; update the DE0903 docs/README to either mark HTTP/HTTPS validation as\n\"not implemented yet\" (or remove that claim) and add a short note about current\nbehavior (HTTP checks are skipped even if --check-http is passed) and, if\ndesired, add a TODO indicating where to implement support for --check-http in\nthe future; reference the --check-http flag and the Link Checking section so\nreviewers can verify the change.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- fingerprinting:phantom:medusa:eagle -->\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment by CodeRabbit -->\n\n✅ Addressed in commit 95a79df","created_at":"2026-01-21T06:59:16Z","updated_at":"2026-01-21T07:16:22Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/287#discussion_r2711223967","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/287","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2711223967"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/287#discussion_r2711223967"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/287"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2711223967/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":248,"start_side":"RIGHT","line":null,"original_line":264,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","original_position":21,"position":1,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2711238716","pull_request_review_id":3685654301,"id":2711238716,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs6hmjg8","diff_hunk":"@@ -71,10 +81,35 @@ gts.<vendor>.<org>.<package>.<type>.<version>~\n     └── Vendor identifier\n ```\n \n+## Link Checking\n+\n+The tool can also check for broken links in Markdown files:\n+\n+```bash\n+# Check local file links and anchors\n+gts-docs-validator --check-links docs\n+\n+# Also check HTTP/HTTPS URLs (slower, requires network)\n+gts-docs-validator --check-links --check-http docs\n+```\n+\n+### What Gets Checked\n+\n+- **Local file links**: `[text](./file.md)` - validates file exists\n+- **Anchor links**: `[text](#heading)` - validates heading exists in target file\n+- **Relative paths**: `[text](../other/file.md#section)` - resolves from current file location\n+- **HTTP/HTTPS**: Optional with `--check-http` flag (not implemented yet)\n+\n+### Link Types Skipped\n+\n+- `mailto:` links\n+- `ftp://` and other protocols\n+- External URLs (unless `--check-http` is specified)","path":"apps/gts-docs-validator/README.md","commit_id":"6eb4fff8ccb5cfa6a5460c809682ab976e7f50be","original_commit_id":"ea822cfcaf9ed4a2c80d8a6bab448599dda6b2d6","user":{"login":"coderabbitai[bot]","id":136622811,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOCCSy2w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/347564?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/coderabbitai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"_⚠️ Potential issue_ | _🟡 Minor_\n\n**Documentation inconsistency for HTTP/HTTPS link handling.**\n\nLine 101 correctly notes HTTP/HTTPS is \"not implemented yet\", but line 107 states external URLs are checked \"unless `--check-http` is specified\", implying the flag enables checking. Since HTTP validation isn't implemented, line 107 should clarify this.\n\n\n<details>\n<summary>Suggested clarification</summary>\n\n```diff\n ### Link Types Skipped\n \n - `mailto:` links\n - `ftp://` and other protocols\n-- External URLs (unless `--check-http` is specified)\n+- External HTTP/HTTPS URLs (validation not yet implemented, even with `--check-http`)\n```\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nIn `@apps/gts-docs-validator/README.md` around lines 101 - 107, The README\ncontains conflicting statements about HTTP/HTTPS handling: the header says\nHTTP/HTTPS is \"not implemented yet\" but later the bullet under \"Link Types\nSkipped\" implies external URLs are checked when the --check-http flag is used;\nupdate the latter text to clarify that external HTTP/HTTPS URLs are currently\nnot validated and the --check-http flag is not yet implemented, so external URLs\nremain skipped until HTTP validation is implemented (referencing the README\nmention of the --check-http flag).\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- fingerprinting:phantom:poseidon:ocelot -->\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment by CodeRabbit -->\n\n✅ Addressed in commit 95a79df","created_at":"2026-01-21T07:03:35Z","updated_at":"2026-01-21T07:16:27Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/287#discussion_r2711238716","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/287","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2711238716"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/287#discussion_r2711238716"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/287"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2711238716/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":101,"start_side":"RIGHT","line":null,"original_line":107,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","original_position":57,"position":1,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2711281382","pull_request_review_id":3685547700,"id":2711281382,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs6hmt7m","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,423 @@\n+//! Link checking functionality for Markdown files\n+//!\n+//! Validates that links in Markdown files are not broken:\n+//! - Checks local file references exist\n+//! - Checks HTTP/HTTPS URLs are reachable\n+//! - Detects anchor references to headings\n+\n+use std::collections::HashSet;\n+use std::fs;\n+use std::path::{Path, PathBuf};\n+\n+use regex::Regex;\n+use serde::Serialize;\n+\n+/// Represents a link found in a Markdown file\n+#[derive(Debug, Clone)]\n+pub struct MarkdownLink {\n+    pub text: String,\n+    pub url: String,\n+    pub line: usize,\n+    pub column: usize,\n+}\n+\n+/// Types of links\n+#[derive(Debug, Clone, PartialEq, Eq)]\n+pub enum LinkType {\n+    LocalFile,\n+    LocalAnchor,\n+    Http,\n+    Https,\n+    Mailto,\n+    Other,\n+}\n+\n+/// Represents a broken link error\n+#[derive(Debug, Clone, Serialize)]\n+pub struct LinkError {\n+    pub file: PathBuf,\n+    pub line: usize,\n+    pub column: usize,\n+    pub link_text: String,\n+    pub link_url: String,\n+    pub error: String,\n+}\n+\n+/// Result of link checking\n+#[derive(Debug, Default)]\n+pub struct LinkCheckResult {\n+    pub errors: Vec<LinkError>,\n+    pub files_scanned: usize,\n+    pub links_checked: usize,\n+}\n+\n+impl LinkCheckResult {\n+    #[must_use]\n+    pub fn new(files_scanned: usize) -> Self {\n+        Self {\n+            errors: Vec::new(),\n+            files_scanned,\n+            links_checked: 0,\n+        }\n+    }\n+\n+    pub fn add_error(&mut self, error: LinkError) {\n+        self.errors.push(error);\n+    }\n+\n+    #[must_use]\n+    pub fn is_ok(&self) -> bool {\n+        self.errors.is_empty()\n+    }\n+}\n+\n+/// Extract all Markdown links from content\n+/// Supports:\n+/// - [text](url)\n+/// - [text](url \"title\")\n+/// - <url>\n+#[must_use]\n+pub fn extract_markdown_links(content: &str) -> Vec<MarkdownLink> {\n+    let mut links = Vec::new();\n+\n+    // Pattern for [text](url) or [text](url \"title\")\n+    let link_pattern = Regex::new(r\"\\[([^\\]]+)\\]\\(([^\\)]+)\\)\").expect(\"Invalid regex\");\n+\n+    // Pattern for <url>\n+    let autolink_pattern = Regex::new(r\"<(https?://[^>]+)>\").expect(\"Invalid regex\");\n+\n+    let content_lines: Vec<&str> = content.lines().collect();\n+\n+    for (line_idx, line) in content_lines.iter().enumerate() {\n+        let line_num = line_idx + 1;\n+\n+        // Extract [text](url) style links\n+        for cap in link_pattern.captures_iter(line) {\n+            if let (Some(text_match), Some(url_match)) = (cap.get(1), cap.get(2)) {\n+                let text = text_match.as_str().to_owned();\n+                let url_full = url_match.as_str();\n+\n+                // Remove optional title from URL (e.g., \"url \"title\"\" -> \"url\")\n+                let url = url_full\n+                    .split_whitespace()\n+                    .next()\n+                    .unwrap_or(url_full)\n+                    .trim_matches('\"')\n+                    .to_owned();\n+\n+                links.push(MarkdownLink {\n+                    text,\n+                    url,\n+                    line: line_num,\n+                    column: url_match.start() + 1,\n+                });\n+            }\n+        }\n+\n+        // Extract <url> style autolinks\n+        for cap in autolink_pattern.captures_iter(line) {\n+            if let Some(url_match) = cap.get(1) {\n+                let url = url_match.as_str().to_owned();\n+                links.push(MarkdownLink {\n+                    text: url.clone(),\n+                    url,\n+                    line: line_num,\n+                    column: url_match.start() + 1,\n+                });\n+            }\n+        }\n+    }\n+\n+    links\n+}\n+\n+/// Determine the type of a link\n+#[must_use]\n+pub fn classify_link(url: &str) -> LinkType {\n+    if url.starts_with(\"http://\") {\n+        LinkType::Http\n+    } else if url.starts_with(\"https://\") {\n+        LinkType::Https\n+    } else if url.starts_with(\"mailto:\") {\n+        LinkType::Mailto\n+    } else if url.starts_with('#') {\n+        LinkType::LocalAnchor\n+    } else if url.starts_with(\"ftp://\") || url.starts_with(\"file://\") {\n+        LinkType::Other\n+    } else {\n+        LinkType::LocalFile\n+    }\n+}\n+\n+/// Extract headings from Markdown content for anchor validation\n+#[must_use]\n+pub fn extract_headings(content: &str) -> HashSet<String> {\n+    let mut headings = HashSet::new();\n+    let heading_pattern = Regex::new(r\"^#{1,6}\\s+(.+)$\").expect(\"Invalid regex\");\n+\n+    for line in content.lines() {\n+        if let Some(heading_match) = heading_pattern.captures(line).and_then(|cap| cap.get(1)) {\n+            let heading = heading_match.as_str().trim();\n+            // Convert to anchor format: lowercase, replace spaces with hyphens\n+            let anchor = heading\n+                .to_lowercase()\n+                .replace(' ', \"-\")\n+                .chars()\n+                .filter(|c| c.is_alphanumeric() || *c == '-' || *c == '_')\n+                .collect::<String>();\n+            headings.insert(format!(\"#{anchor}\"));\n+        }\n+    }\n+\n+    headings\n+}\n+\n+/// Check if a local file link is valid\n+pub fn check_local_file_link(base_path: &Path, link_url: &str) -> Result<(), String> {\n+    // Split anchor from path\n+    let (file_path, anchor) = if let Some(pos) = link_url.find('#') {\n+        (&link_url[..pos], Some(&link_url[pos..]))\n+    } else {\n+        (link_url, None)\n+    };\n+\n+    // Resolve relative path\n+    let full_path = if file_path.is_empty() {\n+        // Just an anchor reference to current file\n+        base_path.to_path_buf()\n+    } else {\n+        let parent = base_path.parent().unwrap_or(base_path);\n+        parent.join(file_path)\n+    };\n+\n+    // Check if path exists (file or directory)\n+    if !full_path.exists() {\n+        return Err(format!(\"Path not found: {}\", full_path.display()));\n+    }\n+\n+    // If it's a directory, that's valid (directory links are allowed)\n+    if full_path.is_dir() {\n+        // Optionally check if directory contains a README.md\n+        let readme_path = full_path.join(\"README.md\");\n+        if !readme_path.exists() {\n+            // Just a warning in verbose mode, not an error\n+            // Directory links without README are still valid\n+        }\n+        return Ok(());\n+    }\n+\n+    // If it's a file, validate it exists (already checked above)\n+    // If there's an anchor, validate it exists in the target file\n+    if let Some(anchor_ref) = anchor\n+        && full_path.extension().and_then(|e| e.to_str()) == Some(\"md\") {\n+        if let Ok(content) = fs::read_to_string(&full_path) {\n+            let headings = extract_headings(&content);\n+            if !headings.contains(anchor_ref) {\n+                return Err(format!(\n+                        \"Anchor '{}' not found in {}\",\n+                        anchor_ref,\n+                        full_path.display()\n+                    ));\n+                }\n+            }\n+        }\n+    }","path":"apps/gts-docs-validator/src/link_checker.rs","commit_id":"95a79df55c2f7ff4b31509dbae1b9c3f66fd5868","original_commit_id":"95a79df55c2f7ff4b31509dbae1b9c3f66fd5868","user":{"login":"graphite-app[bot]","id":96075541,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOBbn_FQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/158384?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/graphite-app%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/graphite-app","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/graphite-app%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/graphite-app%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/graphite-app%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/graphite-app%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/graphite-app%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/graphite-app%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/graphite-app%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/graphite-app%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/graphite-app%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"**Silent failure when target file cannot be read for anchor validation**\n\nIf a link contains an anchor (e.g., `./file.md#heading`), and the target file cannot be read due to permissions or I/O errors, the function silently returns `Ok(())` instead of reporting an error. This means broken links with anchors pointing to unreadable files will pass validation.\n\n```rust\n// Current code silently succeeds if file read fails:\nif let Some(anchor_ref) = anchor\n    && full_path.extension().and_then(|e| e.to_str()) == Some(\".md\") {\n    if let Ok(content) = fs::read_to_string(&full_path) {\n        // validation happens\n    } // if Err, silently continues to Ok(())\n}\n\n// Fix: Handle the error case\nif let Some(anchor_ref) = anchor\n    && full_path.extension().and_then(|e| e.to_str()) == Some(\"md\") {\n    let content = fs::read_to_string(&full_path)\n        .map_err(|e| format!(\"Failed to read file for anchor validation: {}\", e))?;\n    let headings = extract_headings(&content);\n    if !headings.contains(anchor_ref) {\n        return Err(format!(\"Anchor '{}' not found in {}\", anchor_ref, full_path.display()));\n    }\n}\n```\n```suggestion\n    if let Some(anchor_ref) = anchor\n        && full_path.extension().and_then(|e| e.to_str()) == Some(\"md\") {\n        let content = fs::read_to_string(&full_path)\n            .map_err(|e| format!(\"Failed to read file for anchor validation: {}\", e))?;\n        let headings = extract_headings(&content);\n        if !headings.contains(anchor_ref) {\n            return Err(format!(\n                \"Anchor '{}' not found in {}\",\n                anchor_ref,\n                full_path.display()\n            ));\n        }\n    }\n```\n  \n\n*Spotted by [Graphite Agent](https://app.graphite.com/diamond/?org=hypernetix&ref=ai-review-comment)*<i class='graphite__hidden'><br /><br /><a href=\"https://app.graphite.com/github/pr/hypernetix/hyperspot/287?chatWithGeneratedComment=efc9ab26-d20c-4f07-b0e2-51430fdf635e\"><picture><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\" srcset=\"https://static.graphite.dev/github-diamond-fix-in-graphite-dark.svg\"><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\" srcset=\"https://static.graphite.dev/github-diamond-fix-in-graphite-light.svg\"><img alt=\"Fix in Graphite\" src=\"https://static.graphite.dev/github-diamond-fix-in-graphite-dark.svg\"></picture></a></i><i class='graphite__hidden'><br /><br />Is this helpful? React 👍 or 👎 to let us know.</i>","created_at":"2026-01-21T07:20:40Z","updated_at":"2026-01-21T07:20:42Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/287#discussion_r2711281382","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/287","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2711281382"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/287#discussion_r2711281382"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/287"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2711281382/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":211,"start_side":"RIGHT","line":null,"original_line":224,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","original_position":224,"position":1,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2711304642","pull_request_review_id":3685723676,"id":2711304642,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs6hmznC","diff_hunk":"@@ -121,30 +132,74 @@ fn main() -> ExitCode {\n         return ExitCode::FAILURE;\n     }\n \n-    // Scan all files and collect errors\n-    let mut result = ValidationResult::new(files.len());\n+    // Determine what to check\n+    let check_gts = !cli.check_links; // Default behavior or explicit GTS check\n+    let check_links = cli.check_links;","path":"apps/gts-docs-validator/src/main.rs","commit_id":"6dd49d311d8015c53ce26886b3864b97036826f0","original_commit_id":"6dbe38d6f2def748d2d82d44807e088adf0e3aad","user":{"login":"graphite-app[bot]","id":96075541,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOBbn_FQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/158384?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/graphite-app%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/graphite-app","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/graphite-app%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/graphite-app%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/graphite-app%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/graphite-app%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/graphite-app%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/graphite-app%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/graphite-app%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/graphite-app%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/graphite-app%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"The logic makes GTS checking and link checking mutually exclusive. When `--check-links` is specified, `check_gts = !cli.check_links` becomes `false`, which skips all GTS validation. This means users cannot perform both checks in a single run, and the default GTS validation behavior is disabled when checking links.\n\nFix:\n```rust\n// Allow both checks to run (default to GTS check only)\nlet check_gts = !cli.check_links || cli.check_links; // Or simply: true\nlet check_links = cli.check_links;\n```\n\nOr if the intent is to make them mutually exclusive, this should be documented and the default behavior clarified.\n```suggestion\n    let check_gts = true; // Always perform GTS validation\n    let check_links = cli.check_links;\n```\n  \n\n*Spotted by [Graphite Agent](https://app.graphite.com/diamond/?org=hypernetix&ref=ai-review-comment)*<i class='graphite__hidden'><br /><br /><a href=\"https://app.graphite.com/github/pr/hypernetix/hyperspot/287?chatWithGeneratedComment=63473319-08f6-4450-ad90-3a401775fbcf\"><picture><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\" srcset=\"https://static.graphite.dev/github-diamond-fix-in-graphite-dark.svg\"><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\" srcset=\"https://static.graphite.dev/github-diamond-fix-in-graphite-light.svg\"><img alt=\"Fix in Graphite\" src=\"https://static.graphite.dev/github-diamond-fix-in-graphite-dark.svg\"></picture></a></i><i class='graphite__hidden'><br /><br />Is this helpful? React 👍 or 👎 to let us know.</i>","created_at":"2026-01-21T07:29:31Z","updated_at":"2026-01-21T07:29:34Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/287#discussion_r2711304642","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/287","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2711304642"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/287#discussion_r2711304642"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/287"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2711304642/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":136,"start_side":"RIGHT","line":null,"original_line":137,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","original_position":47,"position":1,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2711340128","pull_request_review_id":3685763608,"id":2711340128,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs6hm8Rg","diff_hunk":"@@ -128,6 +128,31 @@ gts-docs-vendor-release:\n gts-docs-test:\n \tcargo test -p gts-docs-validator\n \n+## Check for broken links in Markdown files\n+check-links:\n+\tcargo run -p gts-docs-validator -- \\\n+\t\t--check-links \\\n+\t\t--exclude \"target/*\" \\\n+\t\t--exclude \"docs/api/*\" \\\n+\t\tdocs modules libs examples\n+\n+## Check for broken links with HTTP/HTTPS validation (slower)\n+check-links-http:\n+\tcargo run -p gts-docs-validator -- \\\n+\t\t--check-links \\\n+\t\t--check-http \\\n+\t\t--exclude \"target/*\" \\\n+\t\t--exclude \"docs/api/*\" \\\n+\t\tdocs modules libs examples\n+","path":"Makefile","commit_id":"833f93f524ff9ed110378237feb54fbfff76e1d8","original_commit_id":"26b2dca93db9ca0badeeb9f423ce6b1115a7d293","user":{"login":"coderabbitai[bot]","id":136622811,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOCCSy2w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/347564?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/coderabbitai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"_⚠️ Potential issue_ | _🟡 Minor_\n\n**`check-links-http` target implies HTTP validation that doesn’t exist yet.**\n\nRight now `--check-http` doesn’t actually validate HTTP/HTTPS, so this target is misleading. Consider marking it as “not implemented yet” (or gating it until implemented).  \n\n\n<details>\n<summary>📝 Suggested Makefile comment update</summary>\n\n```diff\n-## Check for broken links with HTTP/HTTPS validation (slower)\n+## Check for broken links with HTTP/HTTPS validation (not implemented yet; slower once enabled)\n```\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nIn `@Makefile` around lines 139 - 147, The Makefile target check-links-http\nadvertises HTTP validation via the --check-http flag for the gts-docs-validator\ntool but that validation isn't implemented; update the check-links-http target\n(and its comment) to either mark it as \"not implemented yet\" or guard the target\nbehind a variable (e.g., ENABLE_HTTP_CHECK) so it is not advertised by\ndefault—adjust the target name/comment and/or add conditional gating around the\n--check-http flag invocation in the check-links-http recipe to prevent\nmisleading behavior until gts-docs-validator supports HTTP/HTTPS checking.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- fingerprinting:phantom:poseidon:eagle -->\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment by CodeRabbit -->\n\n✅ Addressed in commit 051bc84","created_at":"2026-01-21T07:42:31Z","updated_at":"2026-01-23T06:33:39Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/287#discussion_r2711340128","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/287","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2711340128"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/287#discussion_r2711340128"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/287"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2711340128/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":139,"start_side":"RIGHT","line":null,"original_line":147,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","original_position":29,"position":1,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2711383411","pull_request_review_id":3685744530,"id":2711383411,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs6hnG1z","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,425 @@\n+//! Link checking functionality for Markdown files\n+//!\n+//! Validates that links in Markdown files are not broken:\n+//! - Checks local file references exist\n+//! - Checks HTTP/HTTPS URLs are reachable\n+//! - Detects anchor references to headings\n+\n+use std::collections::HashSet;\n+use std::fs;\n+use std::path::{Path, PathBuf};\n+\n+use regex::Regex;\n+use serde::Serialize;\n+\n+/// Represents a link found in a Markdown file\n+#[derive(Debug, Clone)]\n+pub struct MarkdownLink {\n+    pub text: String,\n+    pub url: String,\n+    pub line: usize,\n+    pub column: usize,\n+}\n+\n+/// Types of links\n+#[derive(Debug, Clone, PartialEq, Eq)]\n+pub enum LinkType {\n+    LocalFile,\n+    LocalAnchor,\n+    Http,\n+    Https,\n+    Mailto,\n+    Other,\n+}\n+\n+/// Represents a broken link error\n+#[derive(Debug, Clone, Serialize)]\n+pub struct LinkError {\n+    pub file: PathBuf,\n+    pub line: usize,\n+    pub column: usize,\n+    pub link_text: String,\n+    pub link_url: String,\n+    pub error: String,\n+}\n+\n+/// Result of link checking\n+#[derive(Debug, Default)]\n+pub struct LinkCheckResult {\n+    pub errors: Vec<LinkError>,\n+    pub files_scanned: usize,\n+    pub links_checked: usize,\n+}\n+\n+impl LinkCheckResult {\n+    #[must_use]\n+    pub fn new(files_scanned: usize) -> Self {\n+        Self {\n+            errors: Vec::new(),\n+            files_scanned,\n+            links_checked: 0,\n+        }\n+    }\n+\n+    pub fn add_error(&mut self, error: LinkError) {\n+        self.errors.push(error);\n+    }\n+\n+    #[must_use]\n+    pub fn is_ok(&self) -> bool {\n+        self.errors.is_empty()\n+    }\n+}\n+\n+/// Extract all Markdown links from content\n+/// Supports:\n+/// - [text](url)\n+/// - [text](url \"title\")\n+/// - <url>\n+#[must_use]\n+pub fn extract_markdown_links(content: &str) -> Vec<MarkdownLink> {\n+    let mut links = Vec::new();\n+\n+    // Pattern for [text](url) or [text](url \"title\")\n+    let link_pattern = Regex::new(r\"\\[([^\\]]+)\\]\\(([^\\)]+)\\)\").expect(\"Invalid regex\");\n+\n+    // Pattern for <url>\n+    let autolink_pattern = Regex::new(r\"<(https?://[^>]+)>\").expect(\"Invalid regex\");\n+\n+    let content_lines: Vec<&str> = content.lines().collect();\n+\n+    for (line_idx, line) in content_lines.iter().enumerate() {\n+        let line_num = line_idx + 1;\n+\n+        // Extract [text](url) style links\n+        for cap in link_pattern.captures_iter(line) {\n+            if let (Some(text_match), Some(url_match)) = (cap.get(1), cap.get(2)) {\n+                let text = text_match.as_str().to_owned();\n+                let url_full = url_match.as_str();\n+\n+                // Remove optional title from URL (e.g., \"url \"title\"\" -> \"url\")\n+                let url = url_full\n+                    .split_whitespace()\n+                    .next()\n+                    .unwrap_or(url_full)\n+                    .trim_matches('\"')\n+                    .to_owned();\n+\n+                links.push(MarkdownLink {\n+                    text,\n+                    url,\n+                    line: line_num,\n+                    column: url_match.start() + 1,\n+                });\n+            }\n+        }\n+\n+        // Extract <url> style autolinks\n+        for cap in autolink_pattern.captures_iter(line) {\n+            if let Some(url_match) = cap.get(1) {\n+                let url = url_match.as_str().to_owned();\n+                links.push(MarkdownLink {\n+                    text: url.clone(),\n+                    url,\n+                    line: line_num,\n+                    column: url_match.start() + 1,\n+                });\n+            }\n+        }\n+    }\n+\n+    links\n+}\n+\n+/// Determine the type of a link\n+#[must_use]\n+pub fn classify_link(url: &str) -> LinkType {\n+    if url.starts_with(\"http://\") {\n+        LinkType::Http\n+    } else if url.starts_with(\"https://\") {\n+        LinkType::Https\n+    } else if url.starts_with(\"mailto:\") {\n+        LinkType::Mailto\n+    } else if url.starts_with('#') {\n+        LinkType::LocalAnchor\n+    } else if url.starts_with(\"ftp://\") || url.starts_with(\"file://\") {\n+        LinkType::Other\n+    } else {\n+        LinkType::LocalFile\n+    }\n+}\n+\n+/// Extract headings from Markdown content for anchor validation\n+#[must_use]\n+pub fn extract_headings(content: &str) -> HashSet<String> {\n+    let mut headings = HashSet::new();\n+    let heading_pattern = Regex::new(r\"^#{1,6}\\s+(.+)$\").expect(\"Invalid regex\");\n+\n+    for line in content.lines() {\n+        if let Some(heading_match) = heading_pattern.captures(line).and_then(|cap| cap.get(1)) {\n+            let heading = heading_match.as_str().trim();\n+            // Convert to anchor format: lowercase, replace spaces with hyphens\n+            let anchor = heading\n+                .to_lowercase()\n+                .replace(' ', \"-\")\n+                .chars()\n+                .filter(|c| c.is_alphanumeric() || *c == '-' || *c == '_')\n+                .collect::<String>();\n+            headings.insert(format!(\"#{anchor}\"));\n+        }\n+    }\n+\n+    headings\n+}\n+\n+/// Check if a local file link is valid\n+pub fn check_local_file_link(base_path: &Path, link_url: &str) -> Result<(), String> {\n+    // Split anchor from path\n+    let (file_path, anchor) = if let Some(pos) = link_url.find('#') {\n+        (&link_url[..pos], Some(&link_url[pos..]))\n+    } else {\n+        (link_url, None)\n+    };\n+\n+    // Resolve relative path\n+    let full_path = if file_path.is_empty() {\n+        // Just an anchor reference to current file\n+        base_path.to_path_buf()\n+    } else {\n+        let parent = base_path.parent().unwrap_or(base_path);\n+        parent.join(file_path)\n+    };","path":"apps/gts-docs-validator/src/link_checker.rs","commit_id":"051bc84c058df86d1cff0737e79982e7daa27652","original_commit_id":"be842d250b7a453e2aebb9f77be165a3bfebe01d","user":{"login":"graphite-app[bot]","id":96075541,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOBbn_FQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/158384?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/graphite-app%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/graphite-app","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/graphite-app%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/graphite-app%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/graphite-app%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/graphite-app%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/graphite-app%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/graphite-app%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/graphite-app%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/graphite-app%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/graphite-app%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Path construction bug when markdown file has no parent directory. If `base_path.parent()` returns `None` (e.g., file at root), the code falls back to `base_path` (the file itself) and then joins the relative path to it, creating an invalid path like `/file.md/relative/path.md`.\n\n```rust\nlet full_path = if file_path.is_empty() {\n    base_path.to_path_buf()\n} else {\n    let parent = base_path.parent()\n        .expect(\"Markdown file must have a parent directory\");\n    parent.join(file_path)\n};\n```\n\nAlternatively, handle the None case explicitly with proper error handling.\n```suggestion\n    let full_path = if file_path.is_empty() {\n        // Just an anchor reference to current file\n        base_path.to_path_buf()\n    } else {\n        let parent = if let Some(parent_dir) = base_path.parent() {\n            parent_dir\n        } else {\n            // If there's no parent, use the root directory\n            std::path::Path::new(\"/\")\n        };\n        parent.join(file_path)\n    };\n```\n  \n\n*Spotted by [Graphite Agent](https://app.graphite.com/diamond/?org=hypernetix&ref=ai-review-comment)*<i class='graphite__hidden'><br /><br /><a href=\"https://app.graphite.com/github/pr/hypernetix/hyperspot/287?chatWithGeneratedComment=e1b76a55-e0f4-4ff4-b754-28ab29d5bf27\"><picture><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\" srcset=\"https://static.graphite.dev/github-diamond-fix-in-graphite-dark.svg\"><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\" srcset=\"https://static.graphite.dev/github-diamond-fix-in-graphite-light.svg\"><img alt=\"Fix in Graphite\" src=\"https://static.graphite.dev/github-diamond-fix-in-graphite-dark.svg\"></picture></a></i><i class=