 say HTTP/HTTPS URLs are validated, but the current implementation skips them even when `--check-http` is set. Please align the docstring with behavior or implement the check.\n\n<details>\n<summary>📝 Suggested doc update</summary>\n\n```diff\n-//! - Checks HTTP/HTTPS URLs are reachable\n+//! - (Planned) Checks HTTP/HTTPS URLs are reachable (not implemented yet)\n```\n</details>\n\n<!-- suggestion_start -->\n\n<details>\n<summary>📝 Committable suggestion</summary>\n\n> ‼️ **IMPORTANT**\n> Carefully review the code before committing. Ensure that it accurately replaces the highlighted code, contains no missing lines, and has no issues with indentation. Thoroughly test & benchmark the code to ensure it meets the requirements.\n\n```suggestion\n//! Link checking functionality for Markdown files\n//!\n//! Validates that links in Markdown files are not broken:\n//! - Checks local file references exist\n//! - (Planned) Checks HTTP/HTTPS URLs are reachable (not implemented yet)\n//! - Detects anchor references to headings\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- suggestion_end -->\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nIn `@apps/gts-docs-validator/src/link_checker.rs` around lines 1 - 6, Docstring\nclaims HTTP/HTTPS URLs are validated but the implementation still skips them\neven when the CLI flag --check-http is set; either update the module docstring\nto reflect that HTTP checking is not performed or implement the missing HTTP\nvalidation. To fix, locate the link-processing flow (functions named\nparse_links, check_link, and the CLI flag variable check_http_flag or\nrun_link_checker) and: if you choose docs-only, change the module comment to\nstate HTTP/HTTPS links are currently ignored unless implemented; if you choose\nto implement, add an HTTP check branch in check_link/run_link_checker that, when\ncheck_http_flag is true, performs a HEAD/GET using the existing HTTP client (or\nadd reqwest) with sensible timeouts and treats non-2xx responses as failures,\nand ensure anchor handling and error reporting follow the same pattern as\nlocal-file checks.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- fingerprinting:phantom:medusa:eagle -->\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment by CodeRabbit -->","created_at":"2026-01-21T09:04:27Z","updated_at":"2026-01-21T09:04:28Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/287#discussion_r2711608524","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/287","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2711608524"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/287#discussion_r2711608524"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/287"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2711608524/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":1,"start_side":"RIGHT","line":null,"original_line":6,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","original_position":6,"position":1,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2716367807","pull_request_review_id":3691831544,"id":2716367807,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs6h6Hu_","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,422 @@\n+//! Link checking functionality for Markdown files","path":"apps/gts-docs-validator/src/link_checker.rs","commit_id":"051bc84c058df86d1cff0737e79982e7daa27652","original_commit_id":"833f93f524ff9ed110378237feb54fbfff76e1d8","user":{"login":"Artifizer","id":192502778,"node_id":"U_kgDOC3lb-g","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/192502778?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer","html_url":"https://github.com/Artifizer","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Let's implement it in https://github.com/GlobalTypeSystem/gts-rust/blob/main/gts-cli/src/cli.rs\nand then we can install it and use it in every project using GTS, not just HyperSpot / Cyber Fabric","created_at":"2026-01-22T10:51:40Z","updated_at":"2026-01-22T10:54:14Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/287#discussion_r2716367807","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/287","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2716367807"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/287#discussion_r2716367807"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/287"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2716367807/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":null,"original_line":1,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"MEMBER","original_position":1,"position":1,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2717977264","pull_request_review_id":3693775038,"id":2717977264,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs6iAQqw","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,451 @@\n+//! Link checking functionality for Markdown files\n+//!\n+//! Validates that links in Markdown files are not broken:\n+//! - Checks local file references exist\n+//! - Checks HTTP/HTTPS URLs are reachable\n+//! - Detects anchor references to headings\n+\n+use std::collections::{HashMap, HashSet};\n+use std::fs;\n+use std::path::{Path, PathBuf};\n+\n+use regex::Regex;\n+use serde::Serialize;\n+\n+/// Represents a link found in a Markdown file\n+#[derive(Debug, Clone)]\n+pub struct MarkdownLink {\n+    pub text: String,\n+    pub url: String,\n+    pub line: usize,\n+    pub column: usize,\n+}\n+\n+/// Types of links\n+#[derive(Debug, Clone, PartialEq, Eq)]\n+pub enum LinkType {\n+    LocalFile,\n+    LocalAnchor,\n+    Http,\n+    Https,\n+    Mailto,\n+    Other,\n+}\n+\n+/// Represents a broken link error\n+#[derive(Debug, Clone, Serialize)]\n+pub struct LinkError {\n+    pub file: PathBuf,\n+    pub line: usize,\n+    pub column: usize,\n+    pub link_text: String,\n+    pub link_url: String,\n+    pub error: String,\n+}\n+\n+/// Result of link checking\n+#[derive(Debug, Default)]\n+pub struct LinkCheckResult {\n+    pub errors: Vec<LinkError>,\n+    pub files_scanned: usize,\n+    pub links_checked: usize,\n+}\n+\n+impl LinkCheckResult {\n+    #[must_use]\n+    pub fn new(files_scanned: usize) -> Self {\n+        Self {\n+            errors: Vec::new(),\n+            files_scanned,\n+            links_checked: 0,\n+        }\n+    }\n+\n+    pub fn add_error(&mut self, error: LinkError) {\n+        self.errors.push(error);\n+    }\n+\n+    pub fn increment_links_checked(&mut self) {\n+        self.links_checked += 1;\n+    }\n+\n+    #[must_use]\n+    pub fn is_ok(&self) -> bool {\n+        self.errors.is_empty()\n+    }\n+}\n+\n+/// Extract all Markdown links from content\n+/// Supports:\n+/// - [text](url)\n+/// - [text](url \"title\")\n+/// - <url>\n+#[must_use]\n+pub fn extract_markdown_links(content: &str) -> Vec<MarkdownLink> {\n+    let mut links = Vec::new();\n+\n+    // Pattern for [text](url) or [text](url \"title\")\n+    let link_pattern = Regex::new(r\"\\[([^\\]]+)\\]\\(([^\\)]+)\\)\").expect(\"Invalid regex\");\n+\n+    // Pattern for <url>\n+    let autolink_pattern = Regex::new(r\"<(https?://[^>]+)>\").expect(\"Invalid regex\");\n+\n+    let lines: Vec<&str> = content.lines().collect();\n+\n+    for (line_idx, line) in lines.iter().enumerate() {\n+        let line_num = line_idx + 1;\n+\n+        // Extract [text](url) style links\n+        for cap in link_pattern.captures_iter(line) {\n+            if let (Some(text_match), Some(url_match)) = (cap.get(1), cap.get(2)) {\n+                let text = text_match.as_str().to_owned();\n+                let url_full = url_match.as_str();\n+\n+                // Remove optional title from URL (e.g., \"url \"title\"\" -> \"url\")\n+                let url = url_full\n+                    .split_whitespace()\n+                    .next()\n+                    .unwrap_or(url_full)\n+                    .trim_matches('\"')\n+                    .to_owned();\n+\n+                links.push(MarkdownLink {\n+                    text,\n+                    url,\n+                    line: line_num,\n+                    column: url_match.start() + 1,\n+                });\n+            }\n+        }\n+\n+        // Extract <url> style autolinks\n+        for cap in autolink_pattern.captures_iter(line) {\n+            if let Some(url_match) = cap.get(1) {\n+                let url = url_match.as_str().to_owned();\n+                links.push(MarkdownLink {\n+                    text: url.clone(),\n+                    url,\n+                    line: line_num,\n+                    column: url_match.start() + 1,\n+                });\n+            }\n+        }\n+    }\n+\n+    links\n+}\n+\n+/// Determine the type of a link\n+#[must_use]\n+pub fn classify_link(url: &str) -> LinkType {\n+    if url.starts_with(\"http://\") {\n+        LinkType::Http\n+    } else if url.starts_with(\"https://\") {\n+        LinkType::Https\n+    } else if url.starts_with(\"mailto:\") {\n+        LinkType::Mailto\n+    } else if url.starts_with('#') {\n+        LinkType::LocalAnchor\n+    } else if url.starts_with(\"ftp://\") || url.starts_with(\"file://\") {\n+        LinkType::Other\n+    } else {\n+        LinkType::LocalFile\n+    }\n+}\n+\n+/// Extract headings from Markdown content for anchor validation\n+#[must_use]\n+pub fn extract_headings(content: &str) -> HashSet<String> {\n+    let mut headings = HashSet::new();\n+    let heading_pattern = Regex::new(r\"^#{1,6}\\s+(.+)$\").expect(\"Invalid regex\");\n+\n+    for line in content.lines() {\n+        if let Some(cap) = heading_pattern.captures(line) {\n+            if let Some(heading_match) = cap.get(1) {\n+                let heading = heading_match.as_str().trim();\n+                // Convert to anchor format: lowercase, replace spaces with hyphens\n+                let anchor = heading\n+                    .to_lowercase()\n+                    .replace(' ', \"-\")\n+                    .chars()\n+                    .filter(|c| c.is_alphanumeric() || *c == '-' || *c == '_')\n+                    .collect::<String>();\n+                headings.insert(format!(\"#{anchor}\"));\n+            }\n+        }\n+    }\n+\n+    headings\n+}\n+\n+/// Check if a local file link is valid\n+pub fn check_local_file_link(\n+    base_path: &Path,\n+    link_url: &str,\n+) -> Result<(), String> {\n+    // Split anchor from path\n+    let (file_path, anchor) = if let Some(pos) = link_url.find('#') {\n+        (&link_url[..pos], Some(&link_url[pos..]))\n+    } else {\n+        (link_url, None)\n+    };\n+\n+    // Resolve relative path\n+    let full_path = if file_path.is_empty() {\n+        // Just an anchor reference to current file\n+        base_path.to_path_buf()\n+    } else {\n+        let parent = base_path.parent().unwrap_or(base_path);\n+        parent.join(file_path)\n+    };\n+\n+    // Check if path exists (file or directory)\n+    if !full_path.exists() {\n+        return Err(format!(\"Path not found: {}\", full_path.display()));\n+    }\n+\n+    // If it's a directory, that's valid (directory links are allowed)\n+    if full_path.is_dir() {\n+        // Optionally check if directory contains a README.md\n+        let readme_path = full_path.join(\"README.md\");\n+        if !readme_path.exists() {\n+            // Just a warning in verbose mode, not an error\n+            // Directory links without README are still valid\n+        }\n+        return Ok(());\n+    }\n+\n+    // If it's a file, validate it exists (already checked above)\n+    // If there's an anchor, validate it exists in the target file\n+    if let Some(anchor_ref) = anchor {\n+        if full_path.extension().and_then(|e| e.to_str()) == Some(\"md\") {\n+            if let Ok(content) = fs::read_to_string(&full_path) {\n+                let headings = extract_headings(&content);\n+                if !headings.contains(anchor_ref) {\n+                    return Err(format!(\n+                        \"Anchor '{}' not found in {}\",\n+                        anchor_ref,\n+                        full_path.display()\n+                    ));\n+                }\n+            }\n+        }\n+    }\n+\n+    Ok(())\n+}","path":"apps/gts-docs-validator/src/link_checker.rs","commit_id":"051bc84c058df86d1cff0737e79982e7daa27652","original_commit_id":"4e6fda46a32379f0662631fda0b4e6c73dc1ddfc","user":{"login":"MikeFalcon77","id":3686170,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM2ODYxNzA=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3686170?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/MikeFalcon77","html_url":"https://github.com/MikeFalcon77","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MikeFalcon77/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MikeFalcon77/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MikeFalcon77/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MikeFalcon77/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MikeFalcon77/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MikeFalcon77/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MikeFalcon77/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MikeFalcon77/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MikeFalcon77/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"please add error handling","created_at":"2026-01-22T17:49:22Z","updated_at":"2026-01-22T17:49:22Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/287#discussion_r2717977264","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/287","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2717977264"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/287#discussion_r2717977264"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/287"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2717977264/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":1},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":181,"start_side":"RIGHT","line":null,"original_line":236,"side":"RIGHT","in_reply_to_id":2711117306,"author_association":"MEMBER","original_position":236,"position":1,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2717978756","pull_request_review_id":3693776743,"id":2717978756,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs6iARCE","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,451 @@\n+//! Link checking functionality for Markdown files\n+//!\n+//! Validates that links in Markdown files are not broken:\n+//! - Checks local file references exist\n+//! - Checks HTTP/HTTPS URLs are reachable\n+//! - Detects anchor references to headings\n+\n+use std::collections::{HashMap, HashSet};\n+use std::fs;\n+use std::path::{Path, PathBuf};\n+\n+use regex::Regex;\n+use serde::Serialize;\n+\n+/// Represents a link found in a Markdown file\n+#[derive(Debug, Clone)]\n+pub struct MarkdownLink {\n+    pub text: String,\n+    pub url: String,\n+    pub line: usize,\n+    pub column: usize,\n+}\n+\n+/// Types of links\n+#[derive(Debug, Clone, PartialEq, Eq)]\n+pub enum LinkType {\n+    LocalFile,\n+    LocalAnchor,\n+    Http,\n+    Https,\n+    Mailto,\n+    Other,\n+}\n+\n+/// Represents a broken link error\n+#[derive(Debug, Clone, Serialize)]\n+pub struct LinkError {\n+    pub file: PathBuf,\n+    pub line: usize,\n+    pub column: usize,\n+    pub link_text: String,\n+    pub link_url: String,\n+    pub error: String,\n+}\n+\n+/// Result of link checking\n+#[derive(Debug, Default)]\n+pub struct LinkCheckResult {\n+    pub errors: Vec<LinkError>,\n+    pub files_scanned: usize,\n+    pub links_checked: usize,\n+}\n+\n+impl LinkCheckResult {\n+    #[must_use]\n+    pub fn new(files_scanned: usize) -> Self {\n+        Self {\n+            errors: Vec::new(),\n+            files_scanned,\n+            links_checked: 0,\n+        }\n+    }\n+\n+    pub fn add_error(&mut self, error: LinkError) {\n+        self.errors.push(error);\n+    }\n+\n+    pub fn increment_links_checked(&mut self) {\n+        self.links_checked += 1;\n+    }\n+\n+    #[must_use]\n+    pub fn is_ok(&self) -> bool {\n+        self.errors.is_empty()\n+    }\n+}\n+\n+/// Extract all Markdown links from content\n+/// Supports:\n+/// - [text](url)\n+/// - [text](url \"title\")\n+/// - <url>\n+#[must_use]\n+pub fn extract_markdown_links(content: &str) -> Vec<MarkdownLink> {\n+    let mut links = Vec::new();\n+\n+    // Pattern for [text](url) or [text](url \"title\")\n+    let link_pattern = Regex::new(r\"\\[([^\\]]+)\\]\\(([^\\)]+)\\)\").expect(\"Invalid regex\");\n+\n+    // Pattern for <url>\n+    let autolink_pattern = Regex::new(r\"<(https?://[^>]+)>\").expect(\"Invalid regex\");\n+\n+    let lines: Vec<&str> = content.lines().collect();\n+\n+    for (line_idx, line) in lines.iter().enumerate() {\n+        let line_num = line_idx + 1;\n+\n+        // Extract [text](url) style links\n+        for cap in link_pattern.captures_iter(line) {\n+            if let (Some(text_match), Some(url_match)) = (cap.get(1), cap.get(2)) {\n+                let text = text_match.as_str().to_owned();\n+                let url_full = url_match.as_str();\n+\n+                // Remove optional title from URL (e.g., \"url \"title\"\" -> \"url\")\n+                let url = url_full\n+                    .split_whitespace()\n+                    .next()\n+                    .unwrap_or(url_full)\n+                    .trim_matches('\"')\n+                    .to_owned();\n+\n+                links.push(MarkdownLink {\n+                    text,\n+                    url,\n+                    line: line_num,\n+                    column: url_match.start() + 1,\n+                });\n+            }\n+        }\n+\n+        // Extract <url> style autolinks\n+        for cap in autolink_pattern.captures_iter(line) {\n+            if let Some(url_match) = cap.get(1) {\n+                let url = url_match.as_str().to_owned();\n+                links.push(MarkdownLink {\n+                    text: url.clone(),\n+                    url,\n+                    line: line_num,\n+                    column: url_match.start() + 1,\n+                });\n+            }\n+        }\n+    }\n+\n+    links\n+}\n+\n+/// Determine the type of a link\n+#[must_use]\n+pub fn classify_link(url: &str) -> LinkType {\n+    if url.starts_with(\"http://\") {\n+        LinkType::Http\n+    } else if url.starts_with(\"https://\") {\n+        LinkType::Https\n+    } else if url.starts_with(\"mailto:\") {\n+        LinkType::Mailto\n+    } else if url.starts_with('#') {\n+        LinkType::LocalAnchor\n+    } else if url.starts_with(\"ftp://\") || url.starts_with(\"file://\") {\n+        LinkType::Other\n+    } else {\n+        LinkType::LocalFile\n+    }\n+}\n+\n+/// Extract headings from Markdown content for anchor validation\n+#[must_use]\n+pub fn extract_headings(content: &str) -> HashSet<String> {\n+    let mut headings = HashSet::new();\n+    let heading_pattern = Regex::new(r\"^#{1,6}\\s+(.+)$\").expect(\"Invalid regex\");\n+\n+    for line in content.lines() {\n+        if let Some(cap) = heading_pattern.captures(line) {\n+            if let Some(heading_match) = cap.get(1) {\n+                let heading = heading_match.as_str().trim();\n+                // Convert to anchor format: lowercase, replace spaces with hyphens\n+                let anchor = heading\n+                    .to_lowercase()\n+                    .replace(' ', \"-\")\n+                    .chars()\n+                    .filter(|c| c.is_alphanumeric() || *c == '-' || *c == '_')\n+                    .collect::<String>();\n+                headings.insert(format!(\"#{anchor}\"));\n+            }\n+        }\n+    }\n+\n+    headings\n+}\n+\n+/// Check if a local file link is valid\n+pub fn check_local_file_link(\n+    base_path: &Path,\n+    link_url: &str,\n+) -> Result<(), String> {\n+    // Split anchor from path\n+    let (file_path, anchor) = if let Some(pos) = link_url.find('#') {\n+        (&link_url[..pos], Some(&link_url[pos..]))\n+    } else {\n+        (link_url, None)\n+    };\n+\n+    // Resolve relative path\n+    let full_path = if file_path.is_empty() {\n+        // Just an anchor reference to current file\n+        base_path.to_path_buf()\n+    } else {\n+        let parent = base_path.parent().unwrap_or(base_path);\n+        parent.join(file_path)\n+    };\n+\n+    // Check if path exists (file or directory)\n+    if !full_path.exists() {\n+        return Err(format!(\"Path not found: {}\", full_path.display()));\n+    }\n+\n+    // If it's a directory, that's valid (directory links are allowed)\n+    if full_path.is_dir() {\n+        // Optionally check if directory contains a README.md\n+        let readme_path = full_path.join(\"README.md\");\n+        if !readme_path.exists() {\n+            // Just a warning in verbose mode, not an error\n+            // Directory links without README are still valid\n+        }\n+        return Ok(());\n+    }\n+\n+    // If it's a file, validate it exists (already checked above)\n+    // If there's an anchor, validate it exists in the target file\n+    if let Some(anchor_ref) = anchor {\n+        if full_path.extension().and_then(|e| e.to_str()) == Some(\"md\") {\n+            if let Ok(content) = fs::read_to_string(&full_path) {\n+                let headings = extract_headings(&content);\n+                if !headings.contains(anchor_ref) {\n+                    return Err(format!(\n+                        \"Anchor '{}' not found in {}\",\n+                        anchor_ref,\n+                        full_path.display()\n+                    ));\n+                }\n+            }\n+        }\n+    }\n+\n+    Ok(())\n+}","path":"apps/gts-docs-validator/src/link_checker.rs","commit_id":"051bc84c058df86d1cff0737e79982e7daa27652","original_commit_id":"4e6fda46a32379f0662631fda0b4e6c73dc1ddfc","user":{"login":"coderabbitai[bot]","id":136622811,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOCCSy2w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/347564?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/coderabbitai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"`@MikeFalcon77`, I'll add proper error handling for the anchor validation.\n\n\n\n## Task: Add error handling for file read operations in anchor validation\n- Update `check_local_file_link` to propagate file read errors when validating anchors\n- Ensure that read failures are reported instead of silently skipped\n\n<!-- <requirement>\n[requirement add_error_handling_1/1]\nUpdate the `check_local_file_link` function to propagate file read errors when an anchor is being validated. Replace the silent `if let Ok(content)` pattern with proper error handling using the `?` operator.\n\nFile: `apps/gts-docs-validator/src/link_checker.rs`\n\n```diff\n         if full_path.extension().and_then(|e| e.to_str()) == Some(\"md\") {\n-            if let Ok(content) = fs::read_to_string(&full_path) {\n-                let headings = extract_headings(&content);\n-                if !headings.contains(anchor_ref) {\n-                    return Err(format!(\n-                        \"Anchor '{}' not found in {}\",\n-                        anchor_ref,\n-                        full_path.display()\n-                    ));\n-                }\n-            }\n+            let content = fs::read_to_string(&full_path)\n+                .map_err(|e| format!(\"Failed to read {}: {e}\", full_path.display()))?;\n+            let headings = extract_headings(&content);\n+            if !headings.contains(anchor_ref) {\n+                return Err(format!(\n+                    \"Anchor '{}' not found in {}\",\n+                    anchor_ref,\n+                    full_path.display()\n+                ));\n+            }\n         }\n```\n</requirement> -->\n\n---\n\n<details>\n<summary>🧠 Learnings used</summary>\n\n```\nLearnt from: CR\nRepo: hypernetix/hyperspot PR: 0\nFile: dylint_lints/AGENTS.md:0-0\nTimestamp: 2026-01-14T17:18:31.912Z\nLearning: Applies to dylint_lints/**/src/lib.rs : Document lint behavior in doc comments within the lint implementation\n```\n\n---\n\n```\nLearnt from: CR\nRepo: hypernetix/hyperspot PR: 0\nFile: dylint_lints/AGENTS.md:0-0\nTimestamp: 2026-01-14T17:18:31.912Z\nLearning: Organize Rust lint crates with structure: `src/lib.rs` for implementation, `ui/` directory for UI test files with corresponding `.stderr` files\n```\n\n</details>\n\n---\n\n💡 For code changes across multiple files, use `@coderabbitai` plan in an issue comment\n\n\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated reply by CodeRabbit -->","created_at":"2026-01-22T17:49:49Z","updated_at":"2026-01-22T17:49:49Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/287#discussion_r2717978756","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/287","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2717978756"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/287#discussion_r2717978756"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/287"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2717978756/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":181,"start_side":"RIGHT","line":null,"original_line":236,"side":"RIGHT","in_reply_to_id":2711117306,"author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","original_position":236,"position":1,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2717980662","pull_request_review_id":3693778885,"id":2717980662,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs6iARf2","diff_hunk":"@@ -128,6 +128,31 @@ gts-docs-vendor-release:\n gts-docs-test:\n \tcargo test -p gts-docs-validator\n \n+## Check for broken links in Markdown files\n+check-links: