ers/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"_⚠️ Potential issue_ | _🟡 Minor_\n\n**Inconsistent directory lists between `check-links` and `check-links-release`.**\n\nThe `check-links` target scans `docs modules libs examples dylint_lints` (5 directories), but `check-links-release` only scans `docs modules libs examples` (4 directories). This inconsistency could lead to different results between debug and release builds.\n\n\n<details>\n<summary>🔧 Proposed fix</summary>\n\n```diff\n ## Check for broken links (release build)\n check-links-release:\n \tcargo run --release -p gts-docs-validator -- \\\n \t\t--check-links \\\n \t\t--exclude \"target/*\" \\\n \t\t--exclude \"docs/api/*\" \\\n-\t\tdocs modules libs examples\n+\t\tdocs modules libs examples dylint_lints\n```\n</details>\n\n<!-- suggestion_start -->\n\n<details>\n<summary>📝 Committable suggestion</summary>\n\n> ‼️ **IMPORTANT**\n> Carefully review the code before committing. Ensure that it accurately replaces the highlighted code, contains no missing lines, and has no issues with indentation. Thoroughly test & benchmark the code to ensure it meets the requirements.\n\n```suggestion\n## Check for broken links in Markdown files\ncheck-links:\n\tcargo run -p gts-docs-validator -- \\\n\t\t--check-links \\\n\t\t--exclude \"target/*\" \\\n\t\t--exclude \"docs/api/*\" \\\n\t\tdocs modules libs examples dylint_lints\n\n## Check for broken links (release build)\ncheck-links-release:\n\tcargo run --release -p gts-docs-validator -- \\\n\t\t--check-links \\\n\t\t--exclude \"target/*\" \\\n\t\t--exclude \"docs/api/*\" \\\n\t\tdocs modules libs examples dylint_lints\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- suggestion_end -->\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nIn `@Makefile` around lines 131 - 146, The two Makefile targets check-links and\ncheck-links-release have mismatched directory lists (check-links includes\n\"dylint_lints\" while check-links-release does not); update the\ncheck-links-release target to include \"dylint_lints\" so both targets scan the\nsame directories (or remove \"dylint_lints\" from check-links if you intend to\nexclude it everywhere) by editing the directory argument list in the\ncheck-links-release recipe to match check-links; confirm both targets\n(check-links and check-links-release) now use the identical directory sequence.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- fingerprinting:phantom:medusa:ocelot -->\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment by CodeRabbit -->","created_at":"2026-01-23T04:33:57Z","updated_at":"2026-01-23T04:33:58Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/287#discussion_r2719558282","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/287","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2719558282"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/287#discussion_r2719558282"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/287"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2719558282/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":131,"start_side":"RIGHT","line":null,"original_line":146,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","original_position":28,"position":1,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2719783517","pull_request_review_id":3695887171,"id":2719783517,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs6iHJpd","diff_hunk":"@@ -121,30 +128,76 @@ fn main() -> ExitCode {\n         return ExitCode::FAILURE;\n     }\n \n-    // Scan all files and collect errors\n-    let mut result = ValidationResult::new(files.len());\n+    // Determine what to check\n+    let check_gts = !cli.check_links;\n+    let check_links = cli.check_links;","path":"apps/gts-docs-validator/src/main.rs","commit_id":"051bc84c058df86d1cff0737e79982e7daa27652","original_commit_id":"51052193a6a8008edfbbb668cda2ef8be29e9082","user":{"login":"coderabbitai[bot]","id":136622811,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOCCSy2w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/347564?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/coderabbitai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"_⚠️ Potential issue_ | _🟠 Major_\n\n<details>\n<summary>🧩 Analysis chain</summary>\n\n🏁 Script executed:\n\n```shell\nwc -l apps/gts-docs-validator/src/main.rs\n```\n\nRepository: hypernetix/hyperspot\n\nLength of output: 103\n\n---\n\n🏁 Script executed:\n\n```shell\nsed -n '120,145p' apps/gts-docs-validator/src/main.rs\n```\n\nRepository: hypernetix/hyperspot\n\nLength of output: 769\n\n---\n\n🏁 Script executed:\n\n```shell\n# Search for CLI definition and help text\nrg -A 5 -B 5 \"check.links\\|check-links\" apps/gts-docs-validator/src/main.rs | head -80\n```\n\nRepository: hypernetix/hyperspot\n\nLength of output: 46\n\n---\n\n🏁 Script executed:\n\n```shell\n# Check how check_gts and check_links are used in the main logic\nrg -A 10 \"check_gts\\|check_links\" apps/gts-docs-validator/src/main.rs | head -100\n```\n\nRepository: hypernetix/hyperspot\n\nLength of output: 46\n\n---\n\n🌐 Web query:\n\n`CLI tools running multiple validation modes simultaneously vs mutually exclusive flags`\n\n💡 Result:\n\nWhen a CLI has multiple “validation modes” (e.g., schema, lint, security, formatting), you have two defensible designs—pick based on whether the modes are **orthogonal** or **competing**.\n\n## Prefer **simultaneous modes** when modes are additive (orthogonal)\nUse this when running more than one mode together is meaningful and has unambiguous semantics.\n\n**Good fit**\n- Each mode is an independent check; results can be merged (e.g., one combined report/exit code).\n- Users commonly want “run all selected checks”.\n- Order doesn’t matter, or you clearly define it.\n\n**Flag patterns**\n- Repeatable option: `--mode schema --mode lint` (POSIX synopsis often uses an ellipsis to denote repeatable options) ([pubs.opengroup.org](https://pubs.opengroup.org/onlinepubs/9699919799.orig/basedefs/V1_chap12.html?utm_source=openai))\n- List value: `--mode schema,lint`\n- Multiple booleans if there are only a few: `--schema --lint`\n- If modes have subtypes, allow repetition like ESLint does with `--fix-type` (multiple occurrences supported) ([archive.eslint.org](https://archive.eslint.org/docs/user-guide/command-line-interface?utm_source=openai))\n\n## Prefer **mutually exclusive flags** when modes conflict (competing)\nUse this when selecting more than one mode is ambiguous or unsafe.\n\n**Good fit**\n- Modes change *how* validation works in incompatible ways (different rule sets, different input interpretation, different output formats, different side effects like “fix in place” vs “check only”).\n- Combining would require arbitrary precedence (“last one wins”), which is easy to misuse.\n- You want the CLI to fail fast on invalid combinations.\n\n**Behavior**\n- Error on conflict (recommended). POSIX notes that “conflicting mutually-exclusive arguments” have undefined results unless the utility specifies otherwise—so don’t rely on implicit precedence. ([pubs.opengroup.org](https://pubs.opengroup.org/onlinepubs/9699919799.orig/basedefs/V1_chap12.html?utm_source=openai))\n- If you *do* implement precedence, document it explicitly (some utilities use “last one wins,” but that’s a choice, not a default expectation). ([qnx.com](https://www.qnx.com/developers/docs/7.0.0/com.qnx.doc.neutrino.utilities/topic/utilconv.html?utm_source=openai))\n\n**Implementation examples**\n- Python `argparse` has explicit mutually exclusive groups and shows the canonical help syntax `[--foo | --bar]`, erroring when both are present. ([docs.python.org](https://docs.python.org/3.9/library/argparse.html?utm_source=openai))\n- Rust `clap` supports explicit conflicts (`conflicts_with*`) and errors on conflicting args. ([docs.rs](https://docs.rs/clap/latest/clap/struct.Arg.html?utm_source=openai))\n\n## Practical rule of thumb\n- If modes are “**run these checks**” → allow **multiple simultaneously** (repeatable `--mode` is usually best).\n- If modes are “**choose one way to run**” → make them **mutually exclusive** (and error on conflicts).\n\nIf you tell me your concrete modes + what outputs/exit codes you want, I can suggest an exact flag schema and conflict matrix.\n\nCitations:\n\n- 1: https://pubs.opengroup.org/onlinepubs/9699919799.orig/basedefs/V1_chap12.html?utm_source=openai\n- 2: https://archive.eslint.org/docs/user-guide/command-line-interface?utm_source=openai\n- 3: https://pubs.opengroup.org/onlinepubs/9699919799.orig/basedefs/V1_chap12.html?utm_source=openai\n- 4: https://www.qnx.com/developers/docs/7.0.0/com.qnx.doc.neutrino.utilities/topic/utilconv.html?utm_source=openai\n- 5: https://docs.python.org/3.9/library/argparse.html?utm_source=openai\n- 6: https://docs.rs/clap/latest/clap/struct.Arg.html?utm_source=openai\n\n---\n\n🏁 Script executed:\n\n```shell\n# Find the CLI struct definition\nrg \"struct.*Cli\\|#\\[derive.*Clap\\|#\\[derive.*Parser\" apps/gts-docs-validator/src/main.rs -A 20 | head -80\n```\n\nRepository: hypernetix/hyperspot\n\nLength of output: 46\n\n---\n\n🏁 Script executed:\n\n```shell\n# Look for the field definitions for check_links and any related flags\nrg -B 5 -A 5 \"check.?link\\|check_gts\" apps/gts-docs-validator/src/main.rs\n```\n\nRepository: hypernetix/hyperspot\n\nLength of output: 46\n\n---\n\n🏁 Script executed:\n\n```shell\n# Look at the validation logic more comprehensively\nsed -n '130,200p' apps/gts-docs-validator/src/main.rs\n```\n\nRepository: hypernetix/hyperspot\n\nLength of output: 1944\n\n---\n\n🏁 Script executed:\n\n```shell\n# Search for help text or documentation of these flags\nrg \"help\\|doc\" apps/gts-docs-validator/src/main.rs | grep -i \"check\\|link\\|gts\"\n```\n\nRepository: hypernetix/hyperspot\n\nLength of output: 46\n\n---\n\n🏁 Script executed:\n\n```shell\n# Try to find the entire CLI struct - look at the beginning of the file\nhead -80 apps/gts-docs-validator/src/main.rs\n```\n\nRepository: hypernetix/hyperspot\n\nLength of output: 2412\n\n---\n\n🏁 Script executed:\n\n```shell\n# Search for where Cli struct is defined more broadly\nrg \"struct Cli\" apps/gts-docs-validator/src/main.rs -A 30\n```\n\nRepository: hypernetix/hyperspot\n\nLength of output: 1017\n\n---\n\n🏁 Script executed:\n\n```shell\n# Look for clap attributes and the full CLI struct\nast-grep --pattern 'struct Cli { $$$ }'\n```\n\nRepository: hypernetix/hyperspot\n\nLength of output: 5245\n\n---\n\n🏁 Script executed:\n\n```shell\n# Check if there are any comments or documentation explaining the mutual exclusivity design\nrg -B 5 -A 5 \"mutually\\|exclusive\\|only one\" apps/gts-docs-validator/\n```\n\nRepository: hypernetix/hyperspot\n\nLength of output: 46\n\n---\n\n🏁 Script executed:\n\n```shell\n# Look for any issues or ADRs that might explain this design\nfind apps/gts-docs-validator -name \"*.md\" -o -name \"*.txt\" -o -name \"*.doc*\" | xargs cat 2>/dev/null\n```\n\nRepository: hypernetix/hyperspot\n\nLength of output: 3366\n\n---\n\n🏁 Script executed:\n\n```shell\n# Check git history for this logic to see if there's context\ngit log --oneline -n 20 -- apps/gts-docs-validator/src/main.rs\n```\n\nRepository: hypernetix/hyperspot\n\nLength of output: 84\n\n---\n\n🏁 Script executed:\n\n```shell\n# Check the actual structure of the validation functions to ensure they truly can work together\nsed -n '148,200p' apps/gts-docs-validator/src/main.rs\n```\n\nRepository: hypernetix/hyperspot\n\nLength of output: 1404\n\n---\n\n\n\n</details>\n\n**The mutual exclusivity design appears incorrect; GTS and link checking are independent validations and should be combinable.**\n\nThe code enforces `check_gts = !cli.check_links` (lines 131–133), making these checks mutually exclusive without explicit clap conflict attributes or documented rationale. However, examining the validation logic reveals these are **independent, orthogonal operations**:\n\n- **GTS validation** scans `.md`, `.json`, `.yaml` files for identifier format and vendor compliance\n- **Link checking** scans only `.md` files for broken internal/anchor links\n\nThese validate different properties with non-overlapping semantics, and CLI best practices suggest simultaneous orthogonal modes should be combinable. Currently, the constraint is neither explicitly enforced in the CLI definition nor documented in help text or README.\n\n**Either redesign to allow both flags simultaneously (recommended), or if mutual exclusivity is intentional, use `conflicts_with()` in clap and add prominent documentation in `--help` explaining why.**\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nIn `@apps/gts-docs-validator/src/main.rs` around lines 131 - 133, The current\nlogic sets check_gts = !cli.check_links, wrongly making GTS checking mutually\nexclusive with link checking; update main.rs so GTS and link checks are\nindependent by assigning check_gts from the actual GTS flag (e.g., check_gts =\ncli.check_gts) or otherwise derive each from their own CLI options instead of\ninverting cli.check_links; alternatively, if mutual exclusion is intentional,\ndeclare the conflict in the clap CLI builder using conflicts_with(\"check_links\")\nfor the GTS flag and update help text—locate the assignment to check_gts and the\ncli struct usage to implement the chosen fix.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- fingerprinting:phantom:poseidon:ocelot -->\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment by CodeRabbit -->","created_at":"2026-01-23T06:26:52Z","updated_at":"2026-01-23T06:26:53Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/287#discussion_r2719783517","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/287","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2719783517"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/287#discussion_r2719783517"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/287"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2719783517/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":131,"start_side":"RIGHT","line":null,"original_line":133,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","original_position":43,"position":1,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2719795601","pull_request_review_id":3695900746,"id":2719795601,