.github/workflows/ci.yml\n```\n\nRepository: hypernetix/hyperspot\n\nLength of output: 92\n\n---\n\n🏁 Script executed:\n\n```shell\n# Now let's look at lines 533-557\nsed -n '533,557p' .github/workflows/ci.yml | cat -n\n```\n\nRepository: hypernetix/hyperspot\n\nLength of output: 1040\n\n---\n\n🏁 Script executed:\n\n```shell\n# Let's also check what's around that area\nsed -n '520,570p' .github/workflows/ci.yml | cat -n\n```\n\nRepository: hypernetix/hyperspot\n\nLength of output: 1577\n\n---\n\n\n\n</details>\n\n**Markdown link job won't run on docs-only changes.**  \nThe workflow's `paths-ignore` filters for `**/*.md` and `docs/**` prevent the entire workflow from triggering on documentation-only changes, so the markdown_links job never executes when it's most needed. Consider either removing those ignores to validate links on all changes, or moving markdown validation to a separate workflow that explicitly triggers on markdown files.\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nIn @.github/workflows/ci.yml around lines 533 - 557, The markdown_links job is\nnot executed for docs-only changes because the workflow-level paths-ignore\nfilters exclude \"**/*.md\" and \"docs/**\"; update the CI workflow so markdown\nvalidation runs on doc changes by either removing those paths-ignore entries or\nextracting the markdown_links job into its own workflow file that uses an on:\npush/pull_request trigger with paths: [\"**/*.md\",\"docs/**\"] (or both push and\npull_request) so the markdown_links job runs when only markdown/docs files\nchange.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- fingerprinting:phantom:poseidon:eagle -->\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment by CodeRabbit -->","created_at":"2026-01-26T09:23:02Z","updated_at":"2026-01-26T09:23:03Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/287#discussion_r2726871029","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/287","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.git