iers in documentation and configuration files, and checks for broken links in Markdown files.","path":"dylint_lints/README.md","commit_id":"5ce179f392fd6a0fddff12db719da1da08a0353c","original_commit_id":"5ce179f392fd6a0fddff12db719da1da08a0353c","user":{"login":"Artifizer","id":192502778,"node_id":"U_kgDOC3lb-g","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/192502778?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer","html_url":"https://github.com/Artifizer","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"I believe the tail of the statement is not correct, because 'dylint rule DE0903' doesn't check broken files","created_at":"2026-01-26T20:25:54Z","updated_at":"2026-01-26T20:31:35Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/287#discussion_r2729130445","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/287","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2729130445"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/287#discussion_r2729130445"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/287"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2729130445/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":null,"original_line":248,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"MEMBER","original_position":5,"position":1,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2729132632","pull_request_review_id":3707844319,"id":2729132632,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs6iq0JY","diff_hunk":"@@ -245,39 +245,42 @@ A Dylint lint that prevents using `schemars::schema_for!()` on GTS-wrapped struc\n \n ### DE0903: Documentation Validator\n \n-A Rust CLI tool that validates GTS identifiers in documentation and configuration files.\n+A Rust CLI tool that validates GTS identifiers in documentation and configuration files, and checks for broken links in Markdown files.\n \n **What it checks:**\n+\n+*GTS Validation:*\n - All `.md`, `.json`, `.yaml`, `.yml` files in `docs/`, `modules/`, `libs/`, `examples/`\n - Skips intentionally invalid examples (marked with \"bad\", \"invalid\", \"❌\", etc.)\n - Allows wildcards in pattern/filter contexts\n - Optionally validates vendor consistency with `--vendor` flag\n - Tolerates example vendors: `acme`, `globex`, `example`, `demo`, `test`, `sample`, `tutorial`\n \n+*Link Checking:*","path":"dylint_lints/README.md","commit_id":"5ce179f392fd6a0fddff12db719da1da08a0353c","original_commit_id":"5ce179f392fd6a0fddff12db719da1da08a0353c","user":{"login":"Artifizer","id":192502778,"node_id":"U_kgDOC3lb-g","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/192502778?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer","html_url":"https://github.com/Artifizer","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Is it true? Do you still check links in dylint DE0903? If no, please remove these lines","created_at":"2026-01-26T20:26:41Z","updated_at":"2026-01-26T20:31:35Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/287#discussion_r2729132632","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/287","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2729132632"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/287#discussion_r2729132632"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/287"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2729132632/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":null,"original_line":259,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"MEMBER","original_position":16,"position":1,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2729133821","pull_request_review_id":3707844319,"id":2729133821,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs6iq0b9","diff_hunk":"@@ -245,39 +245,42 @@ A Dylint lint that prevents using `schemars::schema_for!()` on GTS-wrapped struc\n \n ### DE0903: Documentation Validator\n \n-A Rust CLI tool that validates GTS identifiers in documentation and configuration files.\n+A Rust CLI tool that validates GTS identifiers in documentation and configuration files, and checks for broken links in Markdown files.\n \n **What it checks:**\n+\n+*GTS Validation:*\n - All `.md`, `.json`, `.yaml`, `.yml` files in `docs/`, `modules/`, `libs/`, `examples/`\n - Skips intentionally invalid examples (marked with \"bad\", \"invalid\", \"❌\", etc.)\n - Allows wildcards in pattern/filter contexts\n - Optionally validates vendor consistency with `--vendor` flag\n - Tolerates example vendors: `acme`, `globex`, `example`, `demo`, `test`, `sample`, `tutorial`\n \n+*Link Checking:*\n+- Local file links in Markdown files (e.g., `[text](./file.md)`)\n+- Anchor links to headings (e.g., `[text](#heading)`)\n+- Relative path resolution from current file location\n+- Optional HTTP/HTTPS validation with `--check-http` flag\n+\n **How to run:**\n ```bash\n-# Quick check (from workspace root)\n-make gts-docs\n-\n-# With vendor validation (ensures all IDs use vendor \"x\")\n-make gts-docs-vendor\n-\n-# Run tests\n-make gts-docs-test\n+# GTS validation (from workspace root)\n+make gts-docs                # Quick check\n+make gts-docs-vendor         # With vendor validation (ensures all IDs use vendor \"x\")\n+make gts-docs-test           # Run tests\n \n # Direct CLI with options\n cargo run -p gts-docs-validator -- docs modules libs examples\n cargo run -p gts-docs-validator -- --vendor x docs/              # Validate vendor\n-cargo run -p gts-docs-validator -- --exclude \"target/*\" .        # With exclusions\n cargo run -p gts-docs-validator -- --json docs                   # JSON output\n cargo run -p gts-docs-validator -- --verbose docs                # Verbose output\n ```\n \n **Location:** [`apps/gts-docs-validator/`](../apps/gts-docs-validator/)\n \n **Exit codes:**\n-- `0` - All GTS identifiers are valid\n-- `1` - Invalid GTS identifiers found (fails CI)\n+- `0` - All validations passed\n+- `1` - Validation errors found (GTS IDs or broken links, fails CI)","path":"dylint_lints/README.md","commit_id":"5ce179f392fd6a0fddff12db719da1da08a0353c","original_commit_id":"5ce179f392fd6a0fddff12db719da1da08a0353c","user":{"login":"Artifizer","id":192502778,"node_id":"U_kgDOC3lb-g","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/192502778?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer","html_url":"https://github.com/Artifizer","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Do we still check 'broken links'?","created_at":"2026-01-26T20:27:04Z","updated_at":"2026-01-26T20:31:35Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/287#discussion_r2729133821","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/287","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2729133821"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/287#discussion_r2729133821"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/287"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2729133821/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":null,"original_line":283,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"MEMBER","original_position":51,"position":1,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/re