ails>\n<summary>♻️ Duplicate comments (3)</summary><blockquote>\n\n<details>\n<summary>Makefile (1)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`287-293`: **Auto-install `broken-md-links` and align with other tool targets.**\n\nThis target currently assumes the binary is preinstalled; other tooling targets use `ensure_tool`. Also consider adding `markdown-check` to `.PHONY` and (if intended) the `check` dependencies to keep standard workflows consistent.  \n  \n\n<details>\n<summary>🛠️ Proposed fix (auto-install tool)</summary>\n\n```diff\n markdown-check:\n+\t$(call ensure_tool,broken-md-links)\n \tbroken-md-links docs\n \tbroken-md-links examples\n \tbroken-md-links dylint_lints\n \tbroken-md-links guidelines/README.md\n \tbroken-md-links guidelines/NEW_MODULE.md\n \tbroken-md-links guidelines/SECURITY.md\n```\n</details>\n\n</blockquote></details>\n<details>\n<summary>.github/workflows/ci.yml (1)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`533-563`: **Markdown link job won’t run on docs-only changes.**\n\nThe workflow `paths-ignore` excludes `**/*.md` and `docs/**`, so this job never triggers when only docs change. Consider removing those ignores or moving markdown validation into its own workflow with `paths` filters for Markdown.\n\n</blockquote></details>\n<details>\n<summary>dylint_lints/README.md (1)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`248-264`: **Docs still imply `--check-http`/link checks in `gts-docs-validator`.**\n\nThe CLI doesn’t expose link checking or `--check-http` today, so this section is misleading. Please attribute link checking to `broken-md-links` / `make markdown-check` and remove the HTTP claim (or mark it as not implemented). Also clarify exit codes to distinguish GTS validation vs link-check failures.  \n  \n\n<details>\n<summary>📝 Suggested doc update</summary>\n\n```diff\n-*Link Checking:*\n+*Link Checking (via `broken-md-links` / `make markdown-check`):*\n - Local file links in Markdown files (e.g., `[text](./file.md)`)\n - Anchor links to headings (e.g., `[text](`#heading`)`)\n - R