tions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"_⚠️ Potential issue_ | _🟡 Minor_\n\n**Fix the ADR date to the actual decision date.**\n\nThe date is set to **2025-01-21**, which is ~1 year before this PR (2026-01-20). If the decision is current, please update the date to the correct decision date.\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nIn `@docs/decisions/platform/0000-use-madr-for-architecture-decisions.md` around\nlines 1 - 4, The ADR front-matter has an incorrect date (currently \"date:\n2025-01-21\"); update the YAML \"date:\" field in\ndocs/decisions/platform/0000-use-madr-for-architecture-decisions.md to the\nactual decision date (e.g., \"date: 2026-01-20\") so the ADR reflects the correct\ndecision timestamp.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- fingerprinting:phantom:triton:eagle -->\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment by CodeRabbit -->\n\n✅ Addressed in commits 2a8d0c0 to 836c061","created_at":"2026-01-20T22:37:08Z","updated_at":"2026-01-22T13:26:52Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/286#discussion_r2710318431","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/286","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2710318431"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/286#discussion_r2710318431"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/286"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2710318431/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":1,"start_side":"RIGHT","line":null,"original_line":4,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","original_position":4,"position":1,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2710437959","pull_request_review_id":3684732068,"id":2710437959,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs6hjgBH","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,181 @@\n+# Architecture Decision Records (ADRs)\n+\n+This directory contains Architecture Decision Records (ADRs) for the HyperSpot platform, following the [MADR 4.0.0](https://adr.github.io/madr/) format.\n+\n+## What is an ADR?\n+\n+An Architecture Decision Record (ADR) captures an architecturally significant decision along with its context and consequences. ADRs help teams:\n+\n+- Document the reasoning behind important decisions\n+- Provide historical context for future maintainers\n+- Enable asynchronous review and approval across distributed teams\n+- Create a searchable knowledge base of architectural choices\n+\n+## MADR Format\n+\n+We use Markdown Architectural Decision Records (MADR) version 4.0.0. For detailed information:\n+\n+- [MADR Documentation](https://adr.github.io/madr/)\n+- [General ADR Information](https://adr.github.io/)\n+- [Templates](./templates/) - Local copy of MADR templates\n+\n+## Directory Structure\n+\n+ADRs are organized by category to make navigation easier:\n+\n+```text\n+docs/decisions/\n+├── README.md                    # This file\n+├── templates/                   # MADR templates\n+│   ├── adr-template.md          # Full template with explanations\n+│   ├── adr-template-minimal.md  # Minimal template\n+│   └── ...\n+├── api-design/                  # API design decisions\n+│   └── 0001-*.md\n+├── authorization/               # Authorization & access control\n+│   └── 0001-*.md\n+├── integration/                 # External integrations\n+│   └── 0001-*.md\n+├── platform/                    # Cross-cutting platform decisions\n+│   └── 0001-*.md\n+├── storage/                     # Storage & database decisions\n+│   └── 0001-*.md\n+└── workflow-engine/             # Workflow engine decisions\n+    └── 0001-*.md\n+```\n+\n+Each category maintains its own sequential numbering (0001, 0002, etc.).\n+\n+## Creating a New ADR\n+\n+1. **Choose the appropriate category** for your decision\n+2. **Copy the template**: `cp templates/adr-template.md <category>/NNNN-short-title.md`\n+3. **Fill in the template** with your decision details\n+4. **Submit a PR** for review (see approval process below)\n+\n+### File Naming Convention\n+\n+```text\n+NNNN-short-title-with-dashes.md\n+```\n+\n+- `NNNN`: Sequential number within the category (0001, 0002, ...)\n+- `short-title`: Lowercase, dash-separated description\n+- Example: `0001-use-jwt-for-authentication.md`\n+\n+## Multi-Stakeholder Approval Process\n+\n+HyperSpot is a platform used by multiple organizations. Each ADR must be reviewed and approved by representatives from all stakeholder companies before its status can change to `accepted`.\n+\n+### Current Stakeholders\n+\n+| Company | Required Approvers |\n+|---------|-------------------|\n+| **Acronis** | At least 1 designated reviewer |\n+| **Constructor** | At least 1 designated reviewer |\n+| **Virtuozzo** | At least 1 designated reviewer |\n+\n+### Approval Tracking\n+\n+Each ADR includes an `approvals` section in the YAML frontmatter:\n+\n+```yaml\n+---\n+status: proposed\n+date: 2025-01-21\n+approvals:\n+  acronis: false\n+  constructor: false\n+  virtuozzo: false\n+---\n+```\n+\n+When a stakeholder approves, update the frontmatter:\n+\n+```yaml\n+---\n+status: proposed\n+date: 2025-01-21\n+approvals:\n+  acronis: true   # @reviewer-name, 2025-01-21\n+  constructor: false\n+  virtuozzo: true  # @reviewer-name, 2025-01-20\n+---\n+```\n+\n+### Approval Workflow\n+\n+1. **Author creates ADR** with status `proposed` and opens a Pull Request\n+2. **PR can be merged** once basic review is complete (doesn't require all approvals)\n+3. **Stakeholders review** and approve via PR comments or follow-up PRs\n+4. **Update the checklist** when each stakeholder approves\n+5. **Status becomes `accepted`** only when all three stakeholders have approved (can be updated  in the PR with the last approval or by any stakeholder in a follow-up PR)\n+","path":"docs/decisions/README.md","commit_id":"7185b77a9308b3c404ecc1f6a0c2ac82e9a442b3","original_commit_id":"7185b77a9308b3c404ecc1f6a0c2ac82e9a442b3","user":{"login":"coderabbitai[bot]","id":136622811,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOCCSy2w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/347564?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/coderabbitai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"_⚠️ Potential issue_ | _🟡 Minor_\n\n**Fix minor typo in approval workflow text.**\n\nThere’s an extra space in “updated  in the PR”.\n\n<details>\n<summary>📝 Suggested fix</summary>\n\n```diff\n-5. **Status becomes `accepted`** only when all three stakeholders have approved (can be updated  in the PR with the last approval or by any stakeholder in a follow-up PR)\n+5. **Status becomes `accepted`** only when all three stakeholders have approved (can be updated in the PR with the last approval or by any stakeholder in a follow-up PR)\n```\n</details>\n\n<!-- suggestion_start -->\n\n<details>\n<summary>📝 Committable suggestion</summary>\n\n> ‼️ **IMPORTANT**\n> Carefully review the code before committing. Ensure that it accurately replaces the highlighted code, contains no missing lines, and has no issues with indentation. Thoroughly test & benchmark the code to ensure it meets the requirements.\n\n```suggestion\n1. **Author creates ADR** with status `proposed` and opens a Pull Request\n2. **PR can be merged** once basic review is complete (doesn't require all approvals)\n3. **Stakeholders review** and approve via PR comments or follow-up PRs\n4. **Update the checklist** when each stakeholder approves\n5. **Status becomes `accepted`** only when all three stakeholders have approved (can be updated in the PR with the last approval or by any stakeholder in a follow-up PR)\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- suggestion_end -->\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nIn `@docs/decisions/README.md` around lines 108 - 113, Fix the minor typo in the\nADR approval workflow by removing the double space in the phrase \"updated  in\nthe PR\" (found in the list item starting \"Status becomes `accepted`...\"); change\nit to \"updated in the PR\" so the sentence reads correctly and preserve\nsurrounding punctuation and backticks.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- fingerprinting:phantom:poseidon:eagle -->\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment by CodeRabbit -->","created_at":"2026-01-20T23:35:56Z","updated_at":"2026-01-20T23:35:57Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/286#discussion_r2710437959","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/286","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2710437959"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabri