5-01-21\n+  acronis: true   # `@reviewer-name`, YYYY-MM-DD\n   constructor: false\n-  virtuozzo: true  # `@reviewer-name`, 2025-01-20\n+  virtuozzo: true  # `@reviewer-name`, YYYY-MM-DD\n ---\n ```\n```\n</details>\n\n---\n\n`130-152`: **Minor: Consider varying sentence structure in category descriptions.**\n\nThe static analysis tool flagged that three successive sentences begin with \"Decisions about...\". While the parallel structure aids scannability, you could optionally vary the phrasing for better prose flow.\n\n</blockquote></details>\n<details>\n<summary>docs/decisions/templates/adr-template-bare.md (1)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`48-48`: **Add trailing newline at end of file.**\n\nThe file should end with a newline character for POSIX compliance and to avoid diff noise when content is appended.\n\n\n\n<details>\n<summary>Suggested fix</summary>\n\n```diff\n ## More Information\n+\n```\n</details>\n\n</blockquote></details>\n<details>\n<summary>docs/decisions/templates/adr-template-bare-minimal.md (1)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`24-27`: **Add trailing newline at end of file.**\n\nSame as the bare template - add a trailing newline for consistency and to avoid diff noise.\n\n\n\n<details>\n<summary>Suggested fix</summary>\n\n```diff\n ### Consequences\n \n \n+\n```\n</details>\n\n</blockquote></details>\n<details>\n<summary>docs/decisions/templates/adr-template.md (1)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`79-79`: **Add trailing newline at end of file.**\n\nAdd a trailing newline for POSIX compliance and consistency with other files.\n\n\n\n<details>\n<summary>Suggested fix</summary>\n\n```diff\n {You might want to provide additional evidence/confidence for the decision outcome here and/or document the team agreement on the decision and/or define when/how this decision the decision should be realized and if/when it should be re-visited. Links to other decisions and resources might appear here as well.}\n+\n```\n</details>\n\n</blockquote></details>\n\n</blockquote></details>\