berware-rust/pull/284#issuecomment-3774171332","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/issues/284","id":3774171332,"node_id":"IC_kwDOPaLyBs7g9UjE","user":{"login":"coderabbitai[bot]","id":136622811,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOCCSy2w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/347564?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/coderabbitai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-01-20T17:46:20Z","updated_at":"2026-01-22T18:10:35Z","body":"<!-- This is an auto-generated comment: summarize by coderabbit.ai -->\n<!-- other_code_reviewer_warning_start -->\n\n> [!NOTE]\n> ## Other AI code review bot(s) detected\n> \n> CodeRabbit has detected other AI code review bot(s) in this pull request and will avoid duplicating their findings in the review comments. This may lead to a less comprehensive review.\n\n<!-- other_code_reviewer_warning_end -->\n\n<!-- walkthrough_start -->\n\n<details>\n<summary>📝 Walkthrough</summary>\n\n## Walkthrough\n\nWorkspace-wide manifest and crate reorganization: many crates renamed with a `cf-` prefix and explicit versions; path dependencies converted to workspace resolution; DB layer migrated from `sqlx` to `sea_orm::sqlx`; new cf-system-sdks (directory SDK/protos/grpc) added; imports/re-exports updated to use the new SDK.\n\n## Changes\n\n| Cohort / File(s) | Summary |\n|---|---|\n| **Workspace root & membership** <br> `Cargo.toml` | Resolver bumped to \"3\"; `rust-version` and `readme` added; new workspace members added (`libs/system-sdks`, `libs/system-sdks/sdks/directory`, `modules/file_parser`); many workspace.dependencies added/expanded and features reformatted. |\n| **Library renames & metadata** <br> `libs/*/Cargo.toml` (e.g., `libs/modkit*/Cargo.toml`, `libs/modkit-db*/Cargo.toml`, `libs/modkit-errors*/Cargo.toml`, `libs/modkit-security/Cargo.toml`, `libs/modkit-transport-grpc/Cargo.toml`, `libs/modkit-utils/Cargo.toml`) | Multiple packages renamed to `cf-` prefix and given explicit versions (0.1.0), metadata (description, repository, rust-version, keywords) and explicit `[lib]` names added; lint blocks reorganized. |\n| **Workspace dependency migration** <br> `apps/*`, `examples/*`, `modules/*` (many Cargo.toml) | Numerous path-based local dependencies converted to `workspace = true` (examples, modules, apps), plus some feature adjustments and minor formatting changes. |\n| **DB layer: sqlx → sea_orm::sqlx** <br> `libs/modkit-db/Cargo.toml`, `libs/modkit-db/src/*.rs`, `libs/modkit-db/tests/**/*` | Replaced `sqlx` type/import/call paths with `sea_orm::sqlx` equivalents across types, errors, pool/transaction APIs and tests; reorganized and added sqlite-focused tests under `tests/sqlite/`. |\n| **System SDK — directory** <br> `libs/system-sdks/*`, `libs/system-sdks/sdks/directory/*`, `proto/directory` | Added `cf-system-sdks` crate and a `cf-system-sdk-directory` SDK: new Cargo.toml, build.rs (protobuf build), grpc module, API types, conditional exports and features (grpc/directory). |\n| **Module orchestrator → system-sdks migration** <br> `modules/system/module_orchestrator/*`, `modules/system/grpc_hub/src/module.rs`, `libs/modkit/src/*`, `examples/*/wiring.rs` | Replaced imports/re-exports previously pointing at `module_orchestrator_*` with `cf_system_sdks::directory` types/clients and adjusted re-export sites; removed an old proto build script. |\n| **ModKit core updates** <br> `libs/modkit/Cargo.toml`, `libs/modkit/src/bootstrap/*` | `modkit` package renamed to `cf-modkit`, features reformatted to multi-line arrays, some orchestrator deps replaced with `cf-system-sdks`, removed coverage cfg_attr. |\n| **CI & application cleanup** <br> `.github/workflows/ci.yml`, `apps/hyperspot-server/src/main.rs` | CI updated to use `cf-modkit-*` names and newer nightly; removed sqlx driver-linking boilerplate in hyperspot-server `main.rs`. |\n| **Build scripts & generated code** <br> `libs/system-sdks/sdks/directory/build.rs`, `modules/system/module_orchestrator/module_orchestrator-grpc/build.rs` | Added protobuf build script for new directory SDK; removed older module_orchestrator build.rs that compiled protos. |\n| **Tests & test scaffolding** <br> `libs/modkit-db/tests/**/*` | Tests updated to `sea_orm::sqlx` paths, many sqlite tests added/reorganized, some tests removed or re-gated by features. |\n\n## Sequence Diagram(s)\n\n*(skipped — changes are primarily manifests, dependency migrations and library refactors without a new multi-component runtime control flow to visualize)*\n\n## Estimated code review effort\n\n🎯 4 (Complex) | ⏱️ ~60 minutes\n\n## Possibly related PRs\n\n- hypernetix/hyperspot#256 — nodes_registry SDK and workspace manifest changes; overlaps SDK/workspace membership edits.  \n- hypernetix/hyperspot#249 — Directory client / Directory API import and re-export updates; overlaps cf-system-sdks migration.  \n- hypernetix/hyperspot#223 — simple-user-settings module and workspace entries; overlaps modules and workspace dependency changes.\n\n## Suggested reviewers\n\n- MikeFalcon77  \n- Artifizer\n\n## Poem\n\n> 🐰  \n> I hopped through Cargo fields at dawn,  \n> renamed crates until the lawn,  \n> sea_orm sang where sqlx slept,  \n> directory SDK gently lept,  \n> workspace snug — a tidy brawn.\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- walkthrough_end -->\n\n\n<!-- pre_merge_checks_walkthrough_start -->\n\n<details>\n<summary>🚥 Pre-merge checks | ✅ 3 | ❌ 2</summary>\n\n<details>\n<summary>❌ Failed checks (1 warning, 1 inconclusive)</summary>\n\n|      Check name     | Status         | Explanation                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                      | Resolution                                                                                                                                                                                          |\n| :-----------------: | :------------- | :------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | :-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| Linked Issues check | ⚠️ Warning     | The PR implements Phase 1 (Cargo hygiene), Phase 0.2 (package naming with cf- prefix), and Phase 3.2 (publish blockers via cf-system-sdks) from issue `#252`, including workspace dependency migration, package renaming, and new system SDK module creation. However, critical Phase 3.1 blockers (gts/gts-macros publishing) are not addressed, which the issue explicitly marks as required before publishing dependent crates. | Address the gts and gts-macros publish blockers mentioned in `#252` comments before publishing crates that depend on them, or document why the current approach resolves this concern differently.    |\n|     Title check     | ❓ Inconclusive | Title 'prepare lib for publishing' is vague and does not clearly describe the scope of changes. While related to the PR objectives, it lacks specificity about what is being prepared or which libraries are involved.                                                                                                                                                                                                           | Use a more descriptive title such as 'Rename framework crates to cf- prefix and migrate to workspace dependencies' or 'Prepare modkit crates for crates.io publishing with independent versioning'. |\n\n</details>\n<details>\n<summary>✅ Passed checks (3 passed)</summary>\n\n|         Check name         | Status   | Explanation                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                              |\n| :------------------------: | :------- | :--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n|      Description Check     | ✅ Passed | Check skipped - CodeRabbit’s high-level summary is enabled.                                                                                                                                                                                                                              |\n| Out of Scope Changes check | ✅ Passed | Changes are primarily focused on renaming crates to cf- prefix, migrating path dependencies to workspace, and creating cf-system-sdks module. These align with Phase 1 and Phase 0.2 objectives. No extraneous changes detected outside the scope of preparing for crates.io publishing. |\n|     Docstring Coverage     | ✅ Passed | Docstring coverage is 100.00% which is sufficient. The required threshold is 80.00%.                                                                                                                                                                                                     |\n\n</details>\n\n<sub>✏️ Tip: You can configure your own custom pre-merge checks in the settings.</sub>\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- pre_merge_checks_walkthrough_end -->\n\n<!-- tips_start -->\n\n---\n\n\n\n<sub>Comment `@coderabbitai help` to get the list of available commands and usage tips.</sub>\n\n<!-- tips_end -->\n\n<!-- internal state start -->\n\n\n<!--  -->\n\n<!-- internal state end -->","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/issues/comments/3774171332/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":{"id":347564,"client_id":"Iv1.6aaafe4fe882736b","slug":"coderabbitai","node_id":"A_kwHOB96YWc4ABU2s","owner":{"login":"coderabbitai","id":132028505,"node_id":"O_kgDOB96YWQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/132028505?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai","html_url":"https://github.com/coderabbitai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/received_events","type":"Organization","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"name":"coderabbitai","description":"# Transforming Code Reviews with AI\r\n\r\n## Features\r\n\r\n**Automated Reviews**: Continuous reviews of the pull requests including incremental commits. \r\n\r\n**Summarization**: Generates high-level summary and a technical walkthrough of the PR changes. \r\n\r\n**Line-by-line review**: Provides line-by-line suggestions committable with one click.\r\n\r\n**Codebase verification**:  Verifies the impact on the overall codebase and identifies missing changes.\r\n\r\n**Insights into your code**:  Ask any questions on your codebase within the pull request \r\n\r\n**Chat about your code** : Chat with the bot around your code. The more you chat, the smarter it gets.\r\n\r\n**Issue Validation**:  Validates the PR against the linked issues and identifies other related issues \r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n","external_url":"https://coderabbit.ai?utm_source=cr_app&utm_medium=github","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/coderabbitai","created_at":"2023-06-14T15:47:27Z","updated_at":"2026-03-14T07:58:44Z","permissions":{"actions":"read","checks":"write","contents":"write","discussions":"read","issues":"write","members":"read","metadata":"read","pull_requests":"write","statuses":"write"},"events":["issues","issue_comment","label","organization","pull_request","pull_request_review","pull_request_review_comment","pull_request_review_thread","release","repository"]}},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/issues/comments/3774174845","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberwa