"gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/coderabbitai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"_⚠️ Potential issue_ | _🟡 Minor_\n\n<details>\n<summary>🧩 Analysis chain</summary>\n\n🌐 Web query:\n\n`Rust edition 2024 minimum supported version MSRV`\n\n💡 Result:\n\nThe Rust 2024 edition requires Rust 1.85 (the Rust project recommends setting rust-version = \"1.85\" when switching to edition = \"2024\"). [1][2]\n\nSources:\n- Rust Blog: Rust 2024 in beta (migration instructions recommending rust-version = \"1.85\"). [1]\n- Rust Release Notes: Rust 1.85.0 — the 2024 Edition is now stable. [2]\n\n---\n\n🌐 Web query:\n\n`Cargo resolver 3 requirements Rust version`\n\n💡 Result:\n\nResolver = \"3\" requires Rust 1.84 or newer (it's the default for the Rust 2024 edition). [1][2]\n\nSources:\n[1] Cargo book — Resolver versions (notes \"requires Rust 1.84+\").  \n[2] Rust Edition Guide — \"edition = \\\"2024\\\" implies resolver = \\\"3\\\"\" and notes support since Rust 1.84.\n\n---\n\n🏁 Script executed:\n\n```shell\n# Verify the actual Cargo.toml content\nhead -10 Cargo.toml | cat -n\necho \"---\"\nsed -n '60,70p' Cargo.toml | cat -n\n```\n\nRepository: hypernetix/hyperspot\n\nLength of output: 845\n\n---\n\n🏁 Script executed:\n\n```shell\n# Check if there's a rust-version specification anywhere\nrg \"rust-version\" Cargo.toml\necho \"---\"\n# Check the entire workspace section to see full context\nsed -n '1,70p' Cargo.toml | cat -n\n```\n\nRepository: hypernetix/hyperspot\n\nLength of output: 2991\n\n---\n\n\n\n</details>\n\n**Add explicit `rust-version = \"1.85\"` to document the MSRV.**\n\nYour resolver = \"3\" and edition = \"2024\" combination is correct and tied together. However, you're missing an explicit `rust-version` declaration in the `[workspace.package]` section. Add `rust-version = \"1.85\"` to document the minimum supported Rust version, as recommended by the Rust toolchain documentation for edition 2024.\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nIn `@Cargo.toml` at line 65, Add an explicit rust-version = \"1.85\" entry to the\nCargo.toml under the [workspace.package] table to document the MSRV; keep the\nexisting resolver = \"3\" and edition = \"2024\" as-is and ensure the new\nrust-version key is placed alongside those fields in the [workspace.package]\nsection so tooling and readers know the minimum supported Rust version.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- fingerprinting:phantom:poseidon:ocelot -->\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment by CodeRabbit -->","created_at":"2026-01-20T17:55:09Z","updated_at":"2026-01-20T17:55:10Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/284#discussion_r2709466221","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/284","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2709466221"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/284#discussion_r2709466221"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/284"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-ru