et me verify the key issue: does the test_pragma_precedence actually pass?\n# If it does, then the DSN params ARE being handled somewhere\nrg \"test_pragma_precedence\" libs/modkit-db/tests/sqlite/sqlite_tests.rs -A 60 | grep -i \"dsn\\|params\\|synchronous\\|journal\"\n```\n\nRepository: hypernetix/hyperspot\n\nLength of output: 441\n\n---\n\n🏁 Script executed:\n\n```shell\n# Critical question: does SqliteConnectOptions support parsing from DSN?\n# Let me check if there's any usage pattern that would show this\nrg \"parse::<.*SqliteConnectOptions\" --type rust\n```\n\nRepository: hypernetix/hyperspot\n\nLength of output: 46\n\n---\n\n🏁 Script executed:\n\n```shell\n# Let me look at the complete test to see if the test actually validates that DSN params work\ncat -n libs/modkit-db/tests/sqlite/sqlite_tests.rs | sed -n '80,125p'\n```\n\nRepository: hypernetix/hyperspot\n\nLength of output: 2049\n\n---\n\n🏁 Script executed:\n\n```shell\n# Check if maybe there's a different code path that DOES extract DSN params\n# by looking at what DbManager.get actually does\ncat -n libs/modkit-db/src/manager.rs | grep -A 20 \"pub async fn get\"\n```\n\nRepository: hypernetix/hyperspot\n\nLength of output: 1160\n\n---\n\n🏁 Script executed:\n\n```shell\n# Let me definitively check: is SqliteConnectOptions::parse even possible?\n# Check sqlx-sqlite documentation or source patterns\nrg \"impl.*FromStr.*SqliteConnectOptions|fn parse.*SqliteConnectOptions\" --type rust -i\n```\n\nRepository: hypernetix/hyperspot\n\nLength of output: 46\n\n---\n\n🏁 Script executed:\n\n```shell\n# The critical question: what SHOULD be the correct fix?\n# Let me look at how mode=memory is actually handled\ncat -n libs/modkit-db/src/sqlite/dsn.rs | sed -n '56,77p'\n```\n\nRepository: hypernetix/hyperspot\n\nLength of output: 876\n\n---\n\n🏁 Script executed:\n\n```shell\n# Let me understand: the test passes a DSN with query params but ALSO passes params config\n# Does the test actually validate that the DSN query params are used?\ncat -n libs/modkit-db/tests/sqlite/sqlite_tests.rs | sed -n '80,123p'\n```\n\nRepository: hypernetix/hyperspot\n\nLength of output: 2002\n\n---\n\n\n\n</details>\n\n**SQLite DSN query parameters are lost in the configuration path.**\n\nWhen using `build_db_handle` with a SQLite DSN containing query parameters (e.g., `sqlite:file:memdb?mode=memory&cache=shared`), the function strips these parameters via `parse_sqlite_path_from_dsn`, which explicitly removes the query string and returns only the file path. This means connection options like `mode=memory` or `cache=shared` are discarded.\n\nNote: The alternative `DbHandle::connect()` path correctly preserves DSN parameters by extracting them with `extract_sqlite_pragmas()`, but `build_db_handle()` does not.\n\nThe proposed fix requires verification: `SqliteConnectOptions` does not appear to support parsing from a DSN string (unlike `PgConnectOptions` and `MySqlConnectOptions`), so the suggested approach may not work as written.\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nIn `@libs/modkit-db/src/options.rs` around lines 319 - 352, build_sqlite_options\ncurrently drops DSN query params by only using parse_sqlite_path_from_dsn;\nupdate it to also extract SQLite pragma/query params from the DSN and apply them\nto the SqliteConnectOptions. Specifically, inside build_sqlite_options when\ncfg.dsn is Some(dsn) call the existing extract_sqlite_pragmas(dsn) (or implement\nequivalent) to get a params map, then after creating opts with\n.filename(&db_path) and .create_if_missing(true) merge those extracted params\nwith cfg.params (choose explicit cfg.params to override DSN params) and pass the\ncombined map to sqlite_pragma::apply_pragmas(opts, &combined_params) so DSN\nquery parameters such as mode=memory and cache=shared are preserved; keep using\nparse_sqlite_path_from_dsn, sqlite_pragma::apply_pragmas, build_sqlite_options,\nand extract_sqlite_pragmas as the referenced symbols.\n```\n