derstand its publish configuration\ncat -n libs/modkit/Cargo.toml\n```\n\nRepository: hypernetix/hyperspot\n\nLength of output: 4490\n\n---\n\n🏁 Script executed:\n\n```shell\n# Check if there's a workspace root and if modkit is part of it\ncat -n Cargo.toml | head -50\n```\n\nRepository: hypernetix/hyperspot\n\nLength of output: 1855\n\n---\n\n🏁 Script executed:\n\n```shell\n# Verify that module_orchestrator-sdk is indeed a workspace member\ngrep -n \"module_orchestrator-sdk\" Cargo.toml\n```\n\nRepository: hypernetix/hyperspot\n\nLength of output: 132\n\n---\n\n🌐 Web query:\n\n`Cargo path dependency workspace member publish behavior`\n\n💡 Result:\n\nShort answer\n- Crates uploaded to crates.io cannot have dependencies that are only local path (or git) — non-dev path dependencies must include a registry version so Cargo can resolve them on crates.io. Locally you can use path = \"...\", but when publishing include version = \"x.y\" as well (Cargo uses the path locally and the registry version when published). [1]\n\n- In workspaces, path dependencies that live inside the workspace are treated as workspace members; that doesn’t automatically publish them for you. If your crate depends on another workspace member by path, you must either:\n  - publish the dependency to the registry first and change the dependency to include a version (or specify both path + version), or\n  - keep it as a workspace-only dependency and mark the consumer package as non-publishable (publish = false). [1][2]\n\n- Dev-dependencies that are path- or git-only are ignored/stripped when uploading, so they don’t block publish. Recent Cargo changes also relaxed some workspace publishing constraints (progress toward workspace publish workflows). [3]\n\nWhat to do in practice\n- For libraries you intend to publish: in Cargo.toml use both version and path for local development:\n  mydep = { path = \"../mydep\", version = \"1.2.3\" } — Cargo uses the path locally and the registry version when publishing. [1]\n- Or publish dependent crates first, then update the dependency to a registry-only dependency.\n- If you must keep it local-only, set publish = false on the consumer crate so you don’t attempt to upload it. [2]\n\nSources\n- Cargo dependency specification / path/git/version behavior. [1]\n- Cargo manifest & workspace rules (members, publish field). [2]\n- Cargo changelog notes about publishing/dev-dependency handling and workspace publishing changes. [3]\n\n---\n\n\n\n</details>\n\n**Path-only dependency will block `cargo publish`.**\n\nFor crates intended for crates.io, `module_orchestrator-sdk` needs either a published version or `{ version = \"...\", path = \"...\" }` (or a workspace dependency with an explicit version). Otherwise `cargo publish` fails.\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nIn `@libs/modkit/Cargo.toml` around lines 45 - 50, The Cargo.toml currently lists\na path-only dependency \"module_orchestrator-sdk\" which will prevent cargo\npublish; update the dependency declaration for module_orchestrator-sdk in\nlibs/modkit/Cargo.toml to use either a published version (e.g., add a version\nfield) or convert it into a workspace dependency with an explicit version (for\nexample change module_orchestrator-sdk = { path = \"...\", version = \"x.y.z\" } or\npoint to a crates.io version), ensuring the dependency line for\nmodule_orchestrator-sdk is no longer path-only.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- fingerprinting:phantom:medusa:eagle -->\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment by CodeRabbit -->\n\n✅ Addressed in commit 9e59909","created_at":"2026-01-20T23:26:14Z","updated_at":"2026-01-21T15:27:45Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/284#discussion_r2710420698","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/284","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2710420698"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/