hub.com/users/Artifizer","html_url":"https://github.com/Artifizer","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"> [@Artifizer](https://github.com/Artifizer) please check\r\n\r\nAgree. We can have 2 mandatory keywords:\r\ncyberfabric - always used\r\ncyberfabric-{CATEGORY} - depends on module\r\n\r\n@Bechma , @MikeFalcon77 , I'd even add a \"Dylint\" rule. This rule must allow you to use one of several predefined keywords (subsystems):\r\n\r\n**cyberfabric-modkit** - ...\r\n**cyberfabric-system** - API gateway, grpc, modules orchestrator, nodes registry ... - everything needed for Hyperspot itself to run a single binary\r\n**cyberfabric-genai** - llm_gateway, chat, agentic flow, etc - AI-specific\r\n**cyberfabric-data** - file parser, file storage .... -- everything that has access to customers' data\r\n**cyberfabric-core** - serverless runtime, settings service, event manager, tenant resolver, ... ,.. - everything that is needed for any SaaS\r\n\r\nWe can create a dedicated task for this, please do if agree\r\n","created_at":"2026-01-21T22:28:33Z","updated_at":"2026-01-22T11:03:35Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/284#discussion_r2714578237","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/284","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/