   run: cargo test --workspace --no-fail-fast --exclude cf-modkit-macros --exclude cf-modkit-db-macros\n> ```\n> </details>\n> \n> </blockquote></details>\n> \n> </blockquote></details>\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment by CodeRabbit for review status -->","state":"COMMENTED","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/284#pullrequestreview-3683566742","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/284","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","_links":{"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/284#pullrequestreview-3683566742"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/284"}},"submitted_at":"2026-01-20T18:00:01Z","commit_id":"452992567ddf38202565940e9920c2e1d0ac0d34"},{"id":3684362741,"node_id":"PRR_kwDOPaLyBs7bmun1","user":{"login":"coderabbitai[bot]","id":136622811,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOCCSy2w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/347564?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/coderabbitai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"**Actionable comments posted: 1**\n\n> [!CAUTION]\n> Some comments are outside the diff and can’t be posted inline due to platform limitations.\n> \n> \n> \n> <details>\n> <summary>⚠️ Outside diff range comments (1)</summary><blockquote>\n> \n> <details>\n> <summary>libs/modkit-db/tests/sqlite/sqlite_tests.rs (1)</summary><blockquote>\n> \n> `323-327`: **Guard shared-memory cleanup against missing file (Line 327).**\n> \n> `sqlite:file:memdb?mode=memory&cache=shared` usually does not create a real file; `remove_file(\"memdb\").unwrap()` can panic and fail the test. Handle `NotFound` (or ignore cleanup errors) instead.\n> \n> \n> <details>\n> <summary>💡 Proposed fix</summary>\n> \n> ```diff\n> -            std::fs::remove_file(\"memdb\").unwrap();\n> +            if let Err(err) = std::fs::remove_file(\"memdb\") {\n> +                if err.kind() != std::io::ErrorKind::NotFound {\n> +                    panic!(\"Failed to clean up memdb file: {err}\");\n> +                }\n> +            }\n> ```\n> </details>\n> \n> </blockquote></details>\n> \n> </blockquote></details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Fix all issues with AI agents</summary>\n\n```\nIn `@libs/modkit-db/Cargo.toml`:\n- Around line 2-10: Add a [package] section to this crate's Cargo.toml for the\n\"cf-modkit-db\" crate (lib name \"modkit_db\") and include crates.io metadata\nrequired for publishing: add a description (required), readme (path to\nREADME.md), keywords (array of relevant strings), and categories (array of\nappropriate crates.io categories); you can also add\nhomepage/documentation/edition fields if needed, but ensure description is\npresent because it is not inherited from workspace.package and will block\npublishing.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>🧹 Nitpick comments (2)</summary><blockquote>\n\n<details>\n<summary>libs/modkit-db/Cargo.toml (2)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`16-20`: **Confirm driver features are always enabled.**  \n`default = []` means every dependent must explicitly select `pg`, `mysql`, or `sqlite`. If any dependents rely on defaults today, they may now compile without a driver. Consider adding a safe default (e.g., `sqlite`) or audit all dependents.\n\n---\n\n`35-42`: **Watch for workspace feature overrides.**  \nSpecifying `features = [...]` on `workspace = true` deps can override the workspace feature list. Please confirm required features (e.g., sea‑orm runtime/macros, uuid serde, modkit-utils defaults) aren’t inadvertently dropped, or consolidate the full feature set in the workspace definition.\n\n</blockquote></details>\n\n</blockquote></details>\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment by CodeRabbit for review status -->","state":"COMMENTED","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/284#pullrequestreview-3684362741","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/284","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","_links":{"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/284#pullrequestreview-3684362741"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/284"}},"submitted_at":"2026-01-20T21:26:55Z","commit_id":"533c927555560ad6e6c3def834f8861c46d9db30"},{"id":3684481837,"node_id":"PRR_kwDOPaLyBs7bnLst","user":{"login":"coderabbitai[bot]","id":136622811,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOCCSy2w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/347564?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/coderabbitai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"**Actionable comments posted: 3**\n\n> [!CAUTION]\n> Some comments are outside the diff and can’t be posted inline due to platform limitations.\n> \n> \n> \n> <details>\n> <summary>⚠️ Outside diff range comments (1)</summary><blockquote>\n> \n> <details>\n> <summary>libs/modkit-db/tests/sqlite/pooling_tests.rs (1)</summary><blockquote>\n> \n> `227-235`: **Inconsistent migration: MySQL still uses `sqlx` instead of `sea_orm::sqlx`.**\n> \n> The SQLite and PostgreSQL sections have been updated to use `sea_orm::sqlx` types, but the MySQL section still references `sqlx::mysql::MySqlPoolOptions`. This should be updated for consistency with the rest of the migration.\n> \n> <details>\n> <summary>🔧 Proposed fix</summary>\n> \n> ```diff\n>      // Test MySQL helper\n>      #[cfg(feature = \"mysql\")]\n>      {\n> -        let mysql_opts = pool_cfg.apply_mysql(sqlx::mysql::MySqlPoolOptions::new());\n> +        let mysql_opts = pool_cfg.apply_mysql(sea_orm::sqlx::mysql::MySqlPoolOptions::new());\n>          assert_eq!(\n>              std::mem::size_of_val(&mysql_opts),\n> -            std::mem::size_of::<sqlx::mysql::MySqlPoolOptions>()\n> +            std::mem::size_of::<sea_orm::sqlx::mysql::MySqlPoolOptions>()\n>          );\n>      }\n> ```\n> </details>\n> \n> </blockquote></details>\n> \n> </blockquote></details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Fix all issues with AI agents</summary>\n\n```\nIn `@libs/modkit-db/tests/sqlite/manager.rs`:\n- Around line 113-118: The params HashMap in the SQLite test is using the\nincorrect pragma key \"WAL\" => \"true\"; update the parameter to use the standard\npragma key/value format (e.g. \"journal_mode\" => \"WAL\") while keeping other\npragmas like \"synchronous\" => \"NORMAL\"; locate the params construction in the\ntest (the params variable in libs/modkit-db/tests/sqlite/manager.rs) and replace\nthe \"WAL\" key with \"journal_mode\" and value \"WAL\" so the WAL journal mode is\nactually applied.\n\nIn `@libs/modkit-db/tests/sqlite/options.rs`:\n- Around line 68-99: Gate the SQLite-specific display tests so they only compile\nwhen the crate's \"sqlite\" feature is enabled: add #[cfg(feature = \"sqlite\")]\nabove each test (test_display_sqlite_memory, test_display_sqlite_file,\ntest_display_sqlite_relative_path) or wrap the whole file/module in\n#[cfg(feature = \"sqlite\")]; these tests reference\nsea_orm::sqlx::sqlite::SqliteConnectOptions and DbConnectOptions::Sqlite so\nensure the cfg covers those symbols to avoid compilation when the sqlite feature\nis absent.\n- Around line 26-43: The two SQLite-specific tests\ntest_build_db_handle_sqlite_memory and test_build_db_handle_sqlite_file need\nfeature gating; add the attribute #[cfg(feature = \"sqlite\")] above each test\nfunction (i.e., before the #[tokio::test] annotation) so they only compile/run\nwhen the \"sqlite\" feature is enabled, keeping the rest of the test bodies and\nfunction names unchanged.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>♻️ Duplicate comments (2)</summary><blockquote>\n\n<details>\n<summary>libs/modkit-db/Cargo.toml (1)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`1-10`: **Add crates.io metadata before publishing.**\n\nThis crate is missing required and recommended metadata for crates.io publishing:\n- `description` (required by crates.io)\n- `readme` (recommended)\n- `keywords` and `categories` (recommended for discoverability)\n\nThe `description` field is not inherited from `[workspace.package]` and must be added directly.\n\n</blockquote></details>\n<details>\n<summary>Cargo.toml (1)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`65-65`: **Add explicit `rust-version = \"1.85\"` to document the MSRV.**\n\nThe `resolver = \"3\"` and `edition = \"2024\"` combination requires Rust 1.85+. Add `rust-version = \"1.85\"` to the `[workspace.package]` section to document the minimum supported Rust version.\n\n</blockquote></details>\n\n</blockquote></details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>🧹 Nitpick comments (2)</summary><blockquote>\n\n<details>\n<summary>libs/modkit-db/tests/sqlite/options.rs (1)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`6-24`: **Consider adding feature gate and using `#[tokio::test]` for consistency.**\n\nThis test also tests SQLite functionality but lacks feature gating. Additionally, using `temp_env::with_var` with a manual runtime is valid but inconsistent with other tests. Consider if this could be restructured.\n\n<details>\n<summary>♻️ Alternative approach</summary>\n\n```diff\n+#[cfg(feature = \"sqlite\")]\n #[test]\n fn test_build_db_handle_env_expansion() {\n     temp_env::with_var(\"TEST_DB_PASSWORD\", Some(\"secret123\"), || {\n         let rt = tokio::runtime::Builder::new_current_thread()\n             .enable_all()\n             .build()\n             .unwrap();\n         rt.block_on(async {\n             // ...\n         });\n     });\n }\n```\n</details>\n\n</blockquote></details>\n<details>\n<summary>libs/modkit-db/tests/sqlite/manager.rs (1)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`8-66`: **Consider adding feature gates for consistency.**\n\nTests `test_dbmanager_sqlite_with_file` and `test_dbmanager_sqlite_with_path` lack the `#[cfg(feature = \"sqlite\")]` attribute that `test_dbmanager_caching` has. While the parent module is already feature-gated, adding explicit gates would maintain consistency within the file and make the feature requirements clear at the test level.\n\n</blockquote></details>\n\n</blockquote></details>\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment by CodeRabbit for review status -->","state":"COMMENTED","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/284#pullrequestreview-3684481837","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/284","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","_links":{"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/284#pullrequestreview-3684481837"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/284"}},"submitted_at":"2026-01-20T22:00:21Z","commit_id":"b7627ad4be35367dbb960657b15e754f25c6e771"},{"id":3684715026,"node_id":"PRR_kwDOPaLyBs7boEoS","user":{"login":"coderabbitai[bot]","id":136622811,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOCCSy2w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/347564?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/coderabbitai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"**Actionable comments posted: 3**\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Fix all issues with AI agents</summary>\n\n```\nIn `@libs/modkit-db/src/options.rs`:\n- Around line 319-352: build_sqlite_options currently drops DSN query params by\nonly using parse_sqlite_path_from_dsn; update it to also extract SQLite\npragma/query params from the DSN and apply them to the SqliteConnectOptions.\nSpecifically, inside build_sqlite_options when cfg.dsn is Some(dsn) call the\nexisting extract_sqlite_pragmas(dsn) (or implement equivalent) to get a params\nmap, then after creating opts with .filename(&db_path) and\n.create_if_missing(true) merge those extracted params with cfg.params (choose\nexplicit cfg.params to override DSN params) and pass the combined map to\nsqlite_pragma::apply_pragmas(opts, &combined_params) so DSN query parameters\nsuch as mode=memory and cache=shared are preserved; keep using\nparse_sqlite_path_from_dsn, sqlite_pragma::apply_pragmas, build_sqlite_options,\nand extract_sqlite_pragmas as the referenced symbols.\n\nIn `@libs/modkit-errors/Cargo.toml`:\n- Around line 2-12: The Cargo.toml for the cf-modkit-errors crate (package name\n\"cf-modkit-errors\", lib name \"modkit_errors\") is missing crate metadata required\nfor publishing; add at minimum readme and categories (and optionally keywords)\neither under [package] in this Cargo.toml or in [workspace.package] so they\napply workspace-wide; set readme to the README.md path, add a non-empty\ncategories array (at least one valid crates.io category), and consider adding a\nkeywords array to improve discoverability.\n\nIn `@libs/modkit/Cargo.toml`:\n- Around line 45-50: The Cargo.toml currently lists a path-only dependency\n\"module_orchestrator-sdk\" which will prevent cargo publish; update the\ndependency declaration for module_orchestrator-sdk in libs/modkit/Cargo.toml to\nuse either a published version (e.g., add a version field) or convert it into a\nworkspace dependency with an explicit version (for example change\nmodule_orchestrator-sdk = { path = \"...\", version = \"x.y.z\" } or point to a\ncrates.io version), ensuring the dependency line for module_orchestrator-sdk is\nno longer path-only.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>♻️ Duplicate comments (3)</summary><blockquote>\n\n<details>\n<summary>libs/modkit-db/Cargo.toml (1)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`1-12`: **Consider adding crates.io discoverability metadata (if not inherited).**  \nIf `readme`, `keywords`, and `categories` are not coming from `[workspace.package]`, add them here to align with the publishing objectives.  \n\n<details>\n<summary>➕ Possible metadata additions</summary>\n\n```diff\n [package]\n name = \"cf-modkit-db\"\n version = \"0.1.0\"\n edition.workspace = true\n license.workspace = true\n authors.workspace = true\n repository.workspace = true\n rust-version.workspace = true\n description = \"ModKit database library\"\n+readme = \"README.md\"\n+keywords = [\"database\", \"sqlx\", \"sea-orm\", \"sqlite\", \"postgres\"]\n+categories = [\"database\"]\n```\n</details>\n\n</blockquote></details>\n<details>\n<summary>libs/modkit-db/tests/sqlite/options.rs (1)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`1-24`: **LGTM - Imports and test structure are correct.**\n\nThe imports are properly declared and the `test_build_db_handle_env_expansion` test correctly validates environment variable expansion in password configuration.\n\nNote regarding past review comments about missing `#[cfg(feature = \"sqlite\")]` attributes: This file is located under `tests/sqlite/mod.rs` which already has `#![cfg(feature = \"sqlite\")]` at the module level (line 6 of mod.rs), so all tests in this file are already feature-gated by inheritance.\n\n</blockquote></details>\n<details>\n<summary>Cargo.toml (1)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`66-66`: **LGTM - Resolver 3 is correct for edition 2024.**\n\nThe resolver upgrade from \"2\" to \"3\" is the appropriate choice for edition 2024. Resolver 3 provides improved feature resolution semantics and is the default for the 2024 edition.\n\n</blockquote></details>\n\n</blockquote></details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>🧹 Nitpick comments (3)</summary><blockquote>\n\n<details>\n<summary>libs/modkit-db/tests/sqlite/transaction.rs (1)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`5-19`: **Consider extracting shared test setup into a helper function.**\n\nAll three tests share identical setup code for `ConnectOpts`, database connection, pool retrieval, and table creation. While acceptable for test clarity, a helper could reduce the ~14 lines of duplicated setup.\n\n\n\n<details>\n<summary>♻️ Optional helper extraction</summary>\n\n```rust\nasync fn setup_test_db() -> (DbHandle, &'static sqlx::SqlitePool) {\n    let opts = ConnectOpts {\n        max_conns: Some(1),\n        ..Default::default()\n    };\n    let db = DbHandle::connect(\"sqlite::memory:\", opts)\n        .await\n        .expect(\"Failed to connect to database\");\n    let pool = db.sqlx_sqlite().unwrap();\n\n    sea_orm::sqlx::query(\"CREATE TABLE tx_test (id INTEGER PRIMARY KEY, val TEXT NOT NULL)\")\n        .execute(pool)\n        .await\n        .expect(\"Failed to create table\");\n\n    (db, pool)\n}\n```\n\nNote: The lifetime handling for `pool` may require adjustments depending on the actual return type of `sqlx_sqlite()`.\n\n</details>\n\n</blockquote></details>\n<details>\n<summary>libs/modkit-db/tests/sqlite/options.rs (1)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`101-180`: **Redundant feature gates can be removed.**\n\nThe `#[cfg(feature = \"sqlite\")]` attributes on these tests (lines 101, 117, 137, 162) are redundant because the parent module `tests/sqlite/mod.rs` already has `#![cfg(feature = \"sqlite\")]` at the crate level, which gates all contents.\n\n\n<details>\n<summary>♻️ Optional cleanup</summary>\n\n```diff\n-#[cfg(feature = \"sqlite\")]\n #[tokio::test]\n async fn test_build_db_handle_invalid_env_var() {\n     // ...\n }\n\n-#[cfg(feature = \"sqlite\")]\n #[tokio::test]\n async fn test_build_db_handle_invalid_sqlite_pragma() {\n     // ...\n }\n\n-#[cfg(feature = \"sqlite\")]\n #[tokio::test]\n async fn test_build_db_handle_invalid_journal_mode() {\n     // ...\n }\n\n-#[cfg(feature = \"sqlite\")]\n #[tokio::test]\n async fn test_build_db_handle_pool_config() {\n     // ...\n }\n```\n</details>\n\n</blockquote></details>\n<details>\n<summary>Cargo.toml (1)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`422-423`: **Git dependencies will block crates.io publishing.**\n\nAs noted in Issue `#252`, `gts` and `gts-macros` are git-only dependencies that must be published to crates.io (or replaced) before any dependent crates can be published. This is a known blocker per the PR objectives.\n\nFor crates that depend on these (directly or transitively), you'll need to either:\n1. Publish `gts`/`gts-macros` to crates.io first, or\n2. Use `[patch]` sections for local development while ensuring the dependency is published before release\n\n\n\nDo you want me to help identify which workspace crates have transitive dependencies on `gts` or `gts-macros`?\n\n</blockquote></details>\n\n</blockquote></details>\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment by CodeRabbit for review status -->","state":"COMMENTED","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/284#pullrequestreview-3684715026","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/284","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","_links":{"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/284#pullrequestreview-3684715026"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/284"}},"submitted_at":"2026-01-20T23:26:14Z","commit_id":"f5351841f3e1a29a2776c10177a21a9edd87b04e"},{"id":3687385409,"node_id":"PRR_kwDOPaLyBs7byQlB","user":{"login":"coderabbitai[bot]","id":136622811,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOCCSy2w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/347564?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/coderabbitai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"**Actionable comments posted: 1**\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Fix all issues with AI agents</summary>\n\n```\nIn `@libs/modkit/Cargo.toml`:\n- Line 52: The dependency declaration for module_orchestrator-grpc in Cargo.toml\nis path-only which will prevent cargo publish; change the entry to use a\nversioned dependency (e.g. module_orchestrator-grpc = { version = \"x.y.z\",\noptional = true } ) or, if the crate should not be published yet, set the\ncrate's own Cargo.toml to publish = false; update the module_orchestrator-grpc\nline accordingly rather than leaving it as a path-only dependency.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>♻️ Duplicate comments (1)</summary><blockquote>\n\n<details>\n<summary>libs/modkit/Cargo.toml (1)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`51-51`: **Path-only dependency will block `cargo publish`.**\n\nThis issue was previously identified. The dependency needs `{ version = \"...\", path = \"...\" }` or workspace resolution with an explicit version.\n\n</blockquote></details>\n\n</blockquote></details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>🧹 Nitpick comments (1)</summary><blockquote>\n\n<details>\n<summary>apps/hyperspot-server/Cargo.toml (1)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`1-7`: **Consider adding `publish = false` for this application crate.**\n\nThis is an application binary (not a library), so it likely shouldn't be published to crates.io. Adding `publish = false` makes this intent explicit and prevents accidental publish attempts. Per issue `#252`: \"keep `publish = false` for internal-only crates.\"\n\n\n\n<details>\n<summary>🔧 Suggested addition</summary>\n\n```diff\n [package]\n name = \"hyperspot-server\"\n version.workspace = true\n edition.workspace = true\n license.workspace = true\n authors.workspace = true\n+publish = false\n```\n\n</details>\n\n</blockquote></details>\n\n</blockquote></details>\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment by CodeRabbit for review status -->","state":"COMMENTED","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/284#pullrequestreview-3687385409","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/284","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","_links":{"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/284#pullrequestreview-3687385409"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/284"}},"submitted_at":"2026-01-21T13:57:22Z","commit_id":"ff925ae94774bf6879b4b5305ebdb4eed58730e9"},{"id":3687885583,"node_id":"PRR_kwDOPaLyBs7b0KsP","user":{"login":"coderabbitai[bot]","id":136622811,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOCCSy2w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/347564?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/coderabbitai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"**Actionable comments posted: 2**\n\n> [!CAUTION]\n> Some comments are outside the diff and can’t be posted inline due to platform limitations.\n> \n> \n> \n> <details>\n> <summary>⚠️ Outside diff range comments (1)</summary><blockquote>\n> \n> <details>\n> <summary>modules/system/grpc_hub/Cargo.toml (1)</summary><blockquote>\n> \n> `3-3`: **Use explicit version or add `publish = false` for internal-only crates.**\n> \n> The crate currently uses `version.workspace = true` without a `publish = false` declaration. Per PR objectives, publishable crates should use explicit versions rather than workspace inheritance. Either set an explicit `version = \"0.1.0\"` or add `publish = false` if this is an internal-only crate.\n> \n> </blockquote></details>\n> \n> </blockquote></details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Fix all issues with AI agents</summary>\n\n```\nIn `@libs/system-sdks/directory-grpc/Cargo.toml`:\n- Around line 8-12: The Cargo.toml's include field is currently set to only\n\"proto\", which will exclude the src/ code when the crate is published; update\nCargo.toml to remove or broaden the include entry so that src/** (and other\nneeded files like Cargo.toml and build.rs which Cargo already includes) are\npackaged—specifically edit the include key referenced in the diff (the line\n`include = [\"proto\"]`) to either remove it entirely or change it to include\n\"src/**\" (and any other necessary files) so the library named by [lib] name =\n\"cf_system_directory_grpc\" is not excluded from the published crate.\n\nIn `@modules/system/module_orchestrator/src/module.rs`:\n- Around line 28-32: The module macro now declares name = \"directory\" (see\nmodkit::module entry), but the quickstart configuration files still use the old\ntop-level key \"module_orchestrator\"; update the quickstart YAML configs to\nreplace the module_orchestrator: key with directory: and set its value to\nconfig: {} so the runtime lookup matches the modkit::module name=\"directory\"\ndeclaration. Ensure both quickstart YAML variants use the exact key \"directory\"\n(not module_orchestrator) and include the config: {} block.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>🧹 Nitpick comments (6)</summary><blockquote>\n\n<details>\n<summary>apps/hyperspot-server/Cargo.toml (1)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`35-48`: **Consider workspace conversion for remaining system module dependencies (optional for WIP).**\n\nThe PR converts `modkit` and `modkit-db` to workspace dependencies, but other system modules (`api_gateway`, `grpc_hub`, `types-registry`, etc.) remain as path-only references. If these modules will also be published, they should follow the same pattern with `{ version = \"...\", path = \"...\" }` or workspace references per the PR objectives.\n\nSince this is a WIP PR, this may be intentional or planned for a follow-up. Just flagging for tracking.\n\n</blockquote></details>\n<details>\n<summary>libs/system-sdks/public/Cargo.toml (1)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`1-18`: **Consider adding crates.io metadata for publishability.**\n\nThe manifest structure is correct and ready for workspace-based publishing. However, per the PR objectives requiring \"crates.io metadata: description, repository, license, readme, keywords, categories\", consider adding:\n\n```diff\n repository.workspace = true\n description = \"Collection of system modules SDKs\"\n rust-version.workspace = true\n+readme = \"README.md\"\n+keywords = [\"sdk\", \"system\", \"hyperspot\"]\n+categories = [\"development-tools\"]\n```\n\nThis is optional if these fields are not enforced by your release workflow.\n\n</blockquote></details>\n<details>\n<summary>libs/system-sdks/sdks/directory/src/api.rs (1)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`19-31`: **Inconsistent format string style between `http()` and `https()`.**\n\nThe `#[must_use]` attributes are a good addition. However, there's an inconsistency: `https()` uses named format arguments while `http()` still uses positional arguments.\n\nConsider aligning both for consistency:\n\n<details>\n<summary>♻️ Suggested alignment</summary>\n\n```diff\n     #[must_use]\n     pub fn http(host: &str, port: u16) -> Self {\n         Self {\n-            uri: format!(\"{}://{}:{}\", \"http\", host, port),\n+            uri: format!(\"http://{host}:{port}\"),\n         }\n     }\n```\n</details>\n\n</blockquote></details>\n<details>\n<summary>libs/modkit/Cargo.toml (1)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`112-113`: **Consider workspace resolution for `nix` dependency.**\n\nFor consistency with other dependencies, consider defining `nix` in the workspace and using:\n\n```diff\n-nix = { version = \"0.29\", default-features = false, features = [\"signal\"] }\n+nix = { workspace = true, default-features = false, features = [\"signal\"] }\n```\n\nThis is optional if platform-specific dependencies are intentionally managed separately.\n\n</blockquote></details>\n<details>\n<summary>examples/oop-modules/calculator/calculator-sdk/Cargo.toml (1)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`1-30`: **Consider adding `publish = false` for example crate.**\n\nExample crates typically shouldn't be published to crates.io. The workspace migration looks correct, but consider adding:\n\n```diff\n [package]\n name = \"calculator-sdk\"\n version = \"0.1.0\"\n edition.workspace = true\n license.workspace = true\n authors.workspace = true\n description = \"SDK for calculator module: API trait, types, gRPC client, and wiring helpers\"\n build = \"build.rs\"\n+publish = false\n```\n\nThis prevents accidental publishing and aligns with the PR objective to \"keep `publish = false` for internal-only crates.\"\n\n</blockquote></details>\n<details>\n<summary>modules/system/grpc_hub/src/module.rs (1)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`465-478`: **Consider importing types for consistency.**\n\nThe code uses fully qualified `cf_system_sdks::directory::` paths for `RegisterInstanceInfo` and `ServiceEndpoint`, while `DirectoryClient` is imported via `modkit` at the top. For consistency and readability, consider adding these types to the imports.\n\n\n\n<details>\n<summary>♻️ Suggested import addition</summary>\n\nAdd to the imports at the top of the file:\n\n```rust\nuse cf_system_sdks::directory::{RegisterInstanceInfo, ServiceEndpoint};\n```\n\nThen simplify the usage:\n\n```diff\n-                let info = cf_system_sdks::directory::RegisterInstanceInfo {\n+                let info = RegisterInstanceInfo {\n                     module: module_data.module_name.clone(),\n                     instance_id: instance_id.clone(),\n                     grpc_services: service_names\n                         .iter()\n                         .map(|n| {\n                             (\n                                 n.clone(),\n-                                cf_system_sdks::directory::ServiceEndpoint::new(endpoint),\n+                                ServiceEndpoint::new(endpoint),\n                             )\n                         })\n                         .collect(),\n                     version: Some(env!(\"CARGO_PKG_VERSION\").to_owned()),\n                 };\n```\n</details>\n\n</blockquote></details>\n\n</blockquote></details>\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment by CodeRabbit for review status -->","state":"COMMENTED","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/284#pullrequestreview-3687885583","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/284","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","_links":{"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/284#pullrequestreview-3687885583"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/284"}},"submitted_at":"2026-01-21T15:32:42Z","commit_id":"9e5990928b7e0e8d6f271c7c806bbdce68e2d056"},{"id":3688302552,"node_id":"PRR_kwDOPaLyBs7b1wfY","user":{"login":"coderabbitai[bot]","id":136622811,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOCCSy2w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/347564?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/coderabbitai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"**Actionable comments posted: 1**\n\n> [!CAUTION]\n> Some comments are outside the diff and can’t be posted inline due to platform limitations.\n> \n> \n> \n> <details>\n> <summary>⚠️ Outside diff range comments (1)</summary><blockquote>\n> \n> <details>\n> <summary>Cargo.toml (1)</summary><blockquote>\n> \n> `426-427`: **Git-only `gts` dependencies block crates.io publishing if the containing crate is publishable.**\n> \n> Crates.io disallows git dependencies for published crates. `gts` and `gts-macros` are not currently published on crates.io, so publishing the containing crate will fail. Either publish `gts` and `gts-macros` to crates.io first and switch to versioned dependencies, or set `publish = false` on the containing crate if it should not be published.\n> \n> </blockquote></details>\n> \n> </blockquote></details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Fix all issues with AI agents</summary>\n\n```\nIn `@libs/system-sdks/Cargo.toml`:\n- Around line 1-9: Add the missing crates.io metadata fields to the package\ndefinition for \"cf-system-sdks\": in the [package] table add readme =\n\"README.md\", keywords = [\"sdk\", \"system\", \"directory\"], and categories =\n[\"development-tools\"] so the crate is publishable and discoverable on crates.io;\nensure you place these keys alongside the existing fields (name, version,\nedition.workspace, license.workspace, authors.workspace, repository.workspace,\ndescription, rust-version.workspace).\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>🧹 Nitpick comments (3)</summary><blockquote>\n\n<details>\n<summary>libs/system-sdks/src/lib.rs (1)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`1-2`: **Consider adding crate-level documentation.**\n\nThis umbrella crate would benefit from a crate-level doc comment explaining its purpose and available features:\n\n```rust\n//! Collection of system module SDKs for the hyperspot framework.\n//!\n//! # Features\n//! - `directory` - Enables the directory service SDK\n//! - `directory_grpc` - Enables gRPC transport for the directory service\n\n#[cfg(feature = \"directory\")]\npub use cf_system_sdk_directory as directory;\n```\n\n</blockquote></details>\n<details>\n<summary>libs/modkit/Cargo.toml (1)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`1-10`: **Add crates.io keywords/categories for cf-modkit.**\n\nYou now have the core metadata; adding `keywords` and `categories` will improve discoverability and aligns with the publish-hygiene objectives.\n\n</blockquote></details>\n<details>\n<summary>examples/oop-modules/calculator/calculator-sdk/Cargo.toml (1)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`1-8`: **Clarify publish intent and add metadata if this crate will be published.**\n\nThe package section has a `description` but lacks other crates.io metadata (`repository`, `readme`, `keywords`, `categories`). There is also no `publish = false`, so Cargo will attempt to publish this crate by default.\n\nPer the PR objectives:\n- If this crate is **internal-only** (example/test), add `publish = false` to prevent accidental publishing.\n- If this crate is **intended for crates.io**, add the missing metadata fields and consider whether the `workspace = true` dependencies should be converted to explicit versions with path fallbacks (e.g., `{ version = \"0.1\", path = \"...\" }`).\n\n\n\n<details>\n<summary>If internal-only, add publish = false</summary>\n\n```diff\n [package]\n name = \"calculator-sdk\"\n version = \"0.1.0\"\n edition.workspace = true\n license.workspace = true\n authors.workspace = true\n description = \"SDK for calculator module: API trait, types, gRPC client, and wiring helpers\"\n build = \"build.rs\"\n+publish = false\n```\n</details>\n\n</blockquote></details>\n\n</blockquote></details>\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment by CodeRabbit for review status -->","state":"COMMENTED","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/284#pullrequestreview-3688302552","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/284","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","_links":{"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/284#pullrequestreview-3688302552"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/284"}},"submitted_at":"2026-01-21T16:48:15Z","commit_id":"167a25457cab576cf505167a1c4dd396da29be9b"},{"id":3691582295,"node_id":"PRR_kwDOPaLyBs7cCRNX","user":{"login":"coderabbitai[bot]","id":136622811,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOCCSy2w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/347564?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/coderabbitai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"**Actionable comments posted: 2**\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Fix all issues with AI agents</summary>\n\n```\nIn `@libs/modkit-odata/Cargo.toml`:\n- Around line 2-10: The crate manifest for cf-modkit-odata is missing crates.io\nmetadata; add a readme and categories. In Cargo.toml for the cf-modkit-odata\ncrate add a readme = \"README.md\" entry and a categories = [ \"...\", \"...\" ] array\nusing valid crates.io category slugs that match the crate (pick appropriate\ncategories from the official list), ensure README.md exists at the repo root (or\nupdate the path), and run cargo publish --dry-run to validate the metadata\nbefore committing.\n\nIn `@libs/modkit-sdk/Cargo.toml`:\n- Around line 1-10: The Cargo.toml package metadata is missing the readme and\ncategories fields required for crates.io publishing; update the [package]\nsection for the cf-modkit-sdk crate to add readme = \"README.md\" (or the correct\nREADME file path) and a categories = [...] array with one or more appropriate\ncrates.io categories (e.g., \"development-tools\" or \"libraries\") and ensure the\nreferenced README file exists and is included in the package.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>♻️ Duplicate comments (4)</summary><blockquote>\n\n<details>\n<summary>libs/system-sdks/Cargo.toml (1)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`1-11`: **Missing `readme` and `categories` fields for crates.io publishing.**\n\nPer PR objectives, publishable crates should include `readme` and `categories` for crates.io discoverability. Keywords have been added (addressing past feedback), but these fields remain missing.\n\n```toml\nreadme = \"README.md\"\ncategories = [\"development-tools\"]\n```\n\n</blockquote></details>\n<details>\n<summary>libs/modkit-errors/Cargo.toml (1)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`1-13`: **Missing `readme` and `categories` for crates.io metadata.**\n\nKeywords have been added, but `readme` and `categories` are still missing per previous review feedback and PR objectives.\n\n</blockquote></details>\n<details>\n<summary>Cargo.toml (1)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`8-9`: **Confirm the declared MSRV (rust-version = 1.92.0) is intentional.**\n\nIf 1.92.0 isn’t released yet or isn’t your intended minimum, this will unnecessarily block older toolchains. Please verify it matches the intended MSRV and adjust if needed.  \n  \n\n```web\nLatest stable Rust version and release date for Rust 1.92.0\n```\n\n</blockquote></details>\n<details>\n<summary>libs/modkit-db/Cargo.toml (1)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`1-11`: **Add `readme` and `categories` for crates.io metadata completeness.**\n\nThe PR objectives require these for publishable crates.  \n \n\n<details>\n<summary>💡 Suggested manifest update</summary>\n\n```diff\n description = \"ModKit database library\"\n keywords = [\"cyberfabric\", \"cyberfabric-modkit\"]\n+readme = \"README.md\"\n+categories = [\"database\"]\n```\n</details>\n\n</blockquote></details>\n\n</blockquote></details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>🧹 Nitpick comments (2)</summary><blockquote>\n\n<details>\n<summary>libs/modkit-security/Cargo.toml (1)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`1-14`: **Good package restructuring; add `readme` and `categories` for publishing completeness.**\n\nThe rename to `cf-modkit-security` with unprefixed lib name `modkit_security` correctly implements the PR objective of keeping Rust import names stable while using crates.io-safe package names.\n\nConsider adding for full crates.io compliance:\n```toml\nreadme = \"README.md\"\ncategories = [\"development-tools\"]\n```\n\n</blockquote></details>\n<details>\n<summary>libs/modkit-errors/Cargo.toml (1)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`30-31`: **Inconsistent dev-dependency version specification.**\n\n`serde_json` uses an inline version `\"1\"` while all other dependencies use `workspace = true`. For consistency across the workspace:\n\n<details>\n<summary>Suggested fix</summary>\n\n```diff\n [dev-dependencies]\n-serde_json = \"1\"\n+serde_json = { workspace = true }\n```\n</details>\n\n</blockquote></details>\n\n</blockquote></details>\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment by CodeRabbit for review status -->","state":"COMMENTED","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/284#pullrequestreview-3691582295","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/284","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","_links":{"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/284#pullrequestreview-3691582295"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/284"}},"submitted_at":"2026-01-22T09:54:57Z","commit_id":"9b5340e8ca69a18239bcf483207399bbbe2a5565"},{"id":3693857657,"node_id":"PRR_kwDOPaLyBs7cK8t5","user":{"login":"coderabbitai[bot]","id":136622811,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOCCSy2w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/347564?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/coderabbitai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"**Actionable comments posted: 0**\n\n> [!CAUTION]\n> Some comments are outside the diff and can’t be posted inline due to platform limitations.\n> \n> \n> \n> <details>\n> <summary>⚠️ Outside diff range comments (1)</summary><blockquote>\n> \n> <details>\n> <summary>Cargo.toml (1)</summary><blockquote>\n> \n> `423-424`: **Git-only `gts` dependencies block crates.io publishing.**\n> \n> `cargo publish` rejects git dependencies for non-dev deps. `gts` and `gts-macros` are not published on crates.io, so any publishable crate depending on them (e.g., cf-modkit) cannot be published until: (1) these crates are published to crates.io, or (2) the dependent crate is marked `publish = false`.\n> \n> Consider requesting the upstream `globaltypesystem/gts-rust` maintainers to publish `gts` and `gts-macros` to crates.io, or temporarily marking cf-modkit and other affected crates as unpublishable.\n> \n> </blockquote></details>\n> \n> </blockquote></details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>🧹 Nitpick comments (2)</summary><blockquote>\n\n<details>\n<summary>apps/hyperspot-server/Cargo.toml (1)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`31-32`: **Confirm always enabling Postgres support is intended.**\n\nAdding `modkit-db`’s `pg` feature will pull in Postgres support for all builds. If this is not always required, consider feature-gating it to reduce deps.\n\n\n\n<details>\n<summary>♻️ Optional feature-gating example</summary>\n\n```diff\n [features]\n default = []\n+pg = [\"modkit-db/pg\"]\n\n [dependencies]\n-modkit-db = { workspace = true, features = [\"sqlite\", \"pg\"] }\n+modkit-db = { workspace = true, features = [\"sqlite\"] }\n```\n</details>\n\n</blockquote></details>\n<details>\n<summary>Cargo.toml (1)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`40-48`: **Ensure explicit `publish` flags for consistency across new workspace members.**\n\nResolver 3 is correctly set. However, publish flags are inconsistent: `modules/file_parser` and `modules/system/nodes_registry/nodes_registry` explicitly set `publish = false`, while `libs/system-sdks`, `libs/system-sdks/sdks/directory`, `modules/system/module_orchestrator`, and `modules/system/nodes_registry/nodes_registry-sdk` lack explicit flags and default to publishable. Add explicit `publish = true` or `publish = false` to all new members for clarity.\n\n</blockquote></details>\n\n</blockquote></details>\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment by CodeRabbit for review status -->","state":"COMMENTED","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/284#pullrequestreview-3693857657","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/284","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","_links":{"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/284#pullrequestreview-3693857657"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/284"}},"submitted_at":"2026-01-22T18:10:36Z","commit_id":"69748c6cb4794a442e7817368386788dadac45cb"}]},{"source_pr_number":283,"source_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/283","source_state":"closed","source_author":"Bechma","target_issue_number":null,"title":"[PR #283] [WIP] prepare naming for publishing","status":"exported","mirrored_at":null,"comments_status":"none","comments_mirrored":0,"pr_head_ref":"prepare-lib","pr_head_sha":"7c5dad3ac0fc9b766645629cee7507fa5a1ab586","pr_base_ref":"main","pr_head_owner":"Bechma","pr_from_fork":1,"source_data":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/283","id":3192006165,"node_id":"PR_kwDOPaLyBs6-QiYV","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/283","diff_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/283.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/283.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/issues/283","number":283,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"[WIP] prepare naming for publishing","user":{"login":"Bechma","id":19294519,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5Mjk0NTE5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.gi