/api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/received_events","type":"Organization","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"name":"coderabbitai","description":"# Transforming Code Reviews with AI\r\n\r\n## Features\r\n\r\n**Automated Reviews**: Continuous reviews of the pull requests including incremental commits. \r\n\r\n**Summarization**: Generates high-level summary and a technical walkthrough of the PR changes. \r\n\r\n**Line-by-line review**: Provides line-by-line suggestions committable with one click.\r\n\r\n**Codebase verification**:  Verifies the impact on the overall codebase and identifies missing changes.\r\n\r\n**Insights into your code**:  Ask any questions on your codebase within the pull request \r\n\r\n**Chat about your code** : Chat with the bot around your code. The more you chat, the smarter it gets.\r\n\r\n**Issue Validation**:  Validates the PR against the linked issues and identifies other related issues \r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n","external_url":"https://coderabbit.ai?utm_source=cr_app&utm_medium=github","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/coderabbitai","created_at":"2023-06-14T15:47:27Z","updated_at":"2026-03-14T07:58:44Z","permissions":{"actions":"read","checks":"write","contents":"write","discussions":"read","issues":"write","members":"read","metadata":"read","pull_requests":"write","statuses":"write"},"events":["issues","issue_comment","label","organization","pull_request","pull_request_review","pull_request_review_comment","pull_request_review_thread","release","repository"]}},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/issues/comments/3789197161","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/282#issuecomment-3789197161","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/issues/282","id":3789197161,"node_id":"IC_kwDOPaLyBs7h2o9p","user":{"login":"Artifizer","id":192502778,"node_id":"U_kgDOC3lb-g","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/192502778?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer","html_url":"https://github.com/Artifizer","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-01-23T09:12:23Z","updated_at":"2026-01-23T09:12:23Z","body":"The document seems to be rather AuthZEN-based authorization design, not an ADR.\r\nIf so, I'd expect it to be an AUTH_DESIGN.md doc with all the critical parts to be covered:\r\n\r\n1. somehow mention the API tokens and explain what role they play (e.g. why can't we encode all the rules inside token)\r\n2. Since authorization is about API processing, explain the typical API hander flow - when we do what. For example, are we going to have 'fail fast' role check on the middleware level? If yes, would it also call AuthZEN\r\n3. Explain the ideas regarding how the auth rules will appear in the PDP service\r\n\r\nAlso must be covered:\r\n4. Caching strategy need to be explained somehow - otherwise the whole idea can be just not affordable\r\n5. Empty filters semantics\r\n6. I did not get if PDP knows about PEP DB schema or it has own column? If PDP knows about 'custom DB fields':\r\n- how such rules will be stored?\r\n- How PDP would get 'custom DB fields schema update' (migrations)?\r\n- How to make PDP and PEP schemas to be consistent (especially if they upgraded separately)","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/issues/comments/3789197161/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/issues/comments/3798506337","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/282#issuecomment-3798506337","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/issues/282","id":3798506337,"node_id":"IC_kwDOPaLyBs7iaJth","user":{"login":"mergify[bot]","id":37929162,"node_id":"MDM6Qm90Mzc5MjkxNjI=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/10562?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mergify%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/mergify","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mergify%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mergify%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mergify%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mergify%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mergify%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mergify%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mergify%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mergify%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mergify%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-01-26T08:56:35Z","updated_at":"2026-02-05T10:42:10